window.MCD.DATA = [{"id":"rm-577820","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Use AI resources for your Copilot extensions","desc":"<p>Using the AI resources provides several benefits:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Reduced operational overhead</strong>: Avoid the need to handle infrastructure management, updates, monitoring, troubleshooting, or maintenance of custom Azure OpenAI subscriptions. This benefit frees up resources to focus on core business operations and provides value-adding intellectual property (IP) to customers.</li> <li><strong>Simplified onboarding</strong>: Quickly integrate AI capabilities into your solutions without having to navigate the complexities of setting up and managing your own Azure OpenAI subscription.</li> <li><strong>Improved reliability</strong>: Proactive scaling, throttling, load balancing, and fault tolerance measures ensure consistent performance during peak demand.</li> <li><strong>Enhanced security compliance</strong>: Built-in compliance measures and governance, including robust protection from malicious and harmful content, ensure compliance with data residency requirements. This benefit reduces the burden of ensuring regulatory compliance for ISVs.</li> <li><strong>Streamlined experience for customers</strong>: Customers get a seamless AI resource management process without maintaining different configurations for separate ISV solutions.</li> </ul> <p>This capability also provides a cohesive AI consumption tracking and billing experience for Business Central customers. Customers who use AI resources across multiple AI-enabled solutions built with Business Central customer developer tools for Copilot benefit from a unified approach to AI consumption monitoring and invoicing. They don't need to reconcile multiple invoices or metrics from separate ISVs.</p> <p>For details on billing costs, see AI tools at <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/requirements-messages-management#message-scenarios\">Message scenarios</a>.</p> <p>For most publishers, the default Business Central AI resources are enough. However, if you need specific models, including fine-tuned models, that the Business Central AI resources don't provide, you can bring your own subscription for customers. In this case, the publisher is responsible for deploying, maintaining, scaling, and securing the service. The publisher also handles billing AI resources to customers.</p> <p>We recommend using the developer toolkit AI resources when you extend Copilot in Business Central. You just need to authenticate with the <code>SetManagedResourceAuthorization</code> method in the <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/application/system-application/codeunit/system.ai.azure-openai\">AI Module AzureOpenAI</a> codeunit. You also provide your own Azure OpenAI subscription details, but the authentication process doesn't use them. (Update 2026 release wave 1: There's now a new method signature for SetManagedResources that doesn't require you to provide your subscription details anymore. You should use that going forward.)</p> <pre><code>// Example of using the default toolkit AI resources in AL AzureOpenAI.SetManagedResourceAuthorization(Enum::\"AOAI Model Type\"::\"Chat Completions\",AzureOpenAIAccountName,AzureOpenAIApiKey,AOAIDeployments.GetGPT4oLatest()); </code></pre> <p>To use your own subscription, authenticate it with the <code>SetAuthorization</code> method.</p> <pre><code>// Example of using your own Azure OpenAI subscription in AL AzureOpenAI.SetAuthorization(Enum::\"AOAI Model Type\"::\"Chat Completions\",GetEndpoint(),GetDeployment(),GetApiKey()); </code></pre> <p>This AI billing model isn't designed to replace the existing Marketplace monetization pathway for publishers who create Business Central apps. Instead, it offers another option that simplifies AI consumption for customers and partners. ISVs can use the Marketplace monetization option to monetize their IP.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>A key feature of the developer tools for Copilot in Business Central is that publishers in their Marketplace apps use large language models through Microsoft-managed Azure OpenAI resources when they extend Copilot in Business Central. This approach eliminates the need for customers to independently get and manage Azure OpenAI subscriptions. Using the Business Central AI resources is the default and recommended approach. However, some partners or customers might have special requirements that require them to use their own Azure OpenAI subscription when running the feature in production or when developing and testing in sandboxes, which is also supported in the developer tools for Copilot in Business Central.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577820","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"June CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/developer/ai-dev-tools-resources"},{"id":"rm-578074","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Enable enhanced screen recording controls for admins","desc":"<p>The enhanced screen recording capability offers greater flexibility and control, enabling organizations to manage recording behavior with more precision. Key enhancements include:</p> <ul> <li>Access all recording settings and configurations from <strong>Customer Service admin center</strong> &gt; <strong>Quality Management</strong>.</li> <li>Enable or disable screen recording using a dedicated toggle.</li> <li>Capture call audio alongside screen recordings.</li> <li>Turn off the red border displayed around representative screens during active window recording.</li> <li>Allow users with the screen recording supervisor role to play recordings within the Customer Service workspace.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You get more control over how your team captures and reviews screen activity. Role-based access makes it easy to decide who can view or download recordings, helping you stay compliant and maintain oversight. You can also play recordings directly in the Customer Service workspace, so investigations move faster. These updates cut rework, save time, and make coaching and performance reviews more effective.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578074","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704},{"id":"rm-577794","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Globalization Studio - Unified e‑invoicing integration framework","desc":"<p>The unified extensible e-invoicing integration framework extends the existing Electronic Invoicing service by introducing:</p> <ul> <li>A <strong>unified outbound and inbound document model</strong> (based on international standards such as UBL and PEPPOL).</li> <li>A <strong>standardized submission and response pipeline and API</strong> for e-invoicing documents and related statuses.</li> <li>A <strong>clear extensibility model</strong> that allows external ASPs, ISVs, Microsoft partners, and customers to implement their own integrations without requiring Microsoft to build or maintain provider specific connectors.</li> </ul> <p>With this framework, Microsoft defines the <strong>data (format) contract, integration pattern, and lifecycle handling</strong>, while <strong>external e-invoicing ASPs (for example, PDPs, PAs, or PACs) implement the required endpoints and data transformations on their side</strong>.</p> <p>This approach enables:</p> <ul> <li>Support for <strong>multiple service providers</strong> under a consistent integration model.</li> <li>Faster onboarding of new providers and markets.</li> <li>Reduced vendor lock-in for customers.</li> <li>Better alignment with country-specific regulatory requirements without Microsoft acting as an authorized e-invoicing service provider.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Important clarifications</strong> (out of scope):</p> <ul> <li>This feature <strong>does not make Microsoft an Authorized Service Provider</strong> (ASP / PDP / PA / PAC, PEPPOL access point).</li> <li>The feature <strong>does not include built‑in connectivity</strong> to e‑invoicing providers.</li> <li>Customers must <strong>continue to use third‑party e‑invoicing providers</strong> for “last‑mile” submission to tax authorities or clearance platforms.</li> <li>Integration with a specific ASP is <strong>the responsibility of the provider, customer, or ISV</strong>, using the established integration framework.</li> </ul> <p><strong>In the initial phase</strong>, Microsoft defines the data contract and API specification and supports these in Dynamics 365 ERP and Electronic invoicing service. Microsoft collaborates with a selected set of ASPs to build integrations using this standard data contract and API specification, and to validate the integrations for a subset of countries or regions. Customers will be able to choose from these providers based on their countries or regions of operation and configure the integrations within their ERP environments.</p> <p><strong>Moving forward</strong>, we will be:</p> <ul> <li>Extending the coverage by adding more countries or regions; and</li> <li>Engaging with more ASPs and ISVs to expand the ecosystem.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature introduces a unified, extensible integration framework for the Electronic invoicing service in Dynamics 365 Finance, Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, and Dynamics 365 Project Operations, enabling Authorized Service Providers (ASPs), Independent Software Vendors (ISVs), and Microsoft partners and customers to build and maintain their own integrations between the e-invoicing service and external e‑invoicing platforms using a Microsoft‑defined unified format (data contract) and integration pipeline / API.<br> The framework is designed to decouple ERP from any single e‑invoicing provider, giving customers more flexibility in ASP choice while reducing the need for Microsoft‑built, country‑specific formats and “last‑mile” connectors.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-578071","title":"Power Pages: Administration and governance - Configure site analytics and server logging","desc":"<p>Gain insights into your Power Pages site with integrated telemetry and analytics. Use Application Insights to monitor page views, form interactions, session details, and client-side analytics. Detect server-side errors, performance issues, and access logs to resolve problems and optimize your site.</p> <p>To configure site analytics, makers must open the setup workspace and add the analytics provider script to enable traffic analytics.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can monitor your Power Pages site traffic and user interactions with ease. Track page views, form interactions, and session details using client-side analytics. Gain insights into server-side errors and access detailed logs to quickly resolve issues and enhance site performance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578071","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577861","title":"Microsoft Edge: Extended Stable channel support for macOS","desc":"<p>Organizations managing macOS devices will be able to select the Microsoft Edge Extended Stable channel, providing a slower 8-week major release cycle, compared to the two-week major release cycle for Stable.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577861","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-578062","title":"Power Pages: Administration and governance - Manage external authentication providers with granular controls","desc":"<p>Power Pages now lets you manage external authentication providers with environment-level governance controls and optional site-level exceptions. You can centrally enforce which identity providers (IDPs) are allowed across all sites in an environment, while still enabling site-specific flexibility when needed. Makers will only see and select from the approved IDPs when setting up authentication, ensuring consistent governance and alignment with enterprise security policies.</p> <p>To enable this feature, go to the Power Platform admin center. Navigate to <strong>Manage</strong> &gt; <strong>Power Pages</strong> &gt; <strong>Governance settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Authentication providers</strong>. Here, you can configure allowed or restricted external IDPs, enable the control for environments, and manage exceptions for specific sites.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature gives you precise control over which external identity providers can be used on your Power Pages sites. It helps you enforce security, compliance, and privacy standards while maintaining flexibility for your team.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578062","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577543","title":"Microsoft Teams: Explicit consent for recording & transcription in one-to-one PSTN calls","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams will support explicit consent for participants connected through the public switched telephone network (PSTN) in one-to-one calls. When explicit consent is required, PSTN participants will hear an audio prompt when recording or transcription is started. They can use their phone keypad to consent or decline. Participants who decline can remain in the call but stay muted. This capability extends the existing Teams calling policy for explicit consent to one-to-one PSTN calls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577543","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Mobile"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-577401","title":"Microsoft Teams: Facilitator in GCC","desc":"<p>Facilitator is coming to Microsoft Teams meetings in GCC. The Facilitator agent can help capture notes in real time, answers questions about the meeting, and help keep the agenda and discussion on track. A Microsoft 365 Copilot license is required to use Facilitator.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577401","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576275","title":"Planner: Custom Views for plans","desc":"<p>Custom views lets users save a custom view of a plan and return to it later without re-applying filters, sorting, grouping, and other view customizations. A team can reuse saved views for triage, prioritization, work tracking, and more.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576275","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576281","title":"Power Apps: Form fill assistance using speech as input in model-driven apps","desc":"<p>We’re expanding form fill assistance in Power Apps to use speech as a source, providing users a more natural way to fill forms. Users select the microphone icon, record their content, and the transcript is used as a source for the form entry. Recordings are transient and not saved.</p> <p>Availability</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Monthly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2612.1</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Users (enabled by default)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576281","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576283","title":"Power Apps: Use Power Platform connectors in generative pages","desc":"<p>Makers can bring data from Power Platform connectors into generative pages. After creating and authenticating a connection and adding a connection reference to the environment, you select the connector data and describe how the generated page should use it. Connector data can be incorporated while working in the Maker Studio generative page designer or through the generative pages AI plugin.</p> <h2>Availability</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Not applicable</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>Gen page v302</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Admins or makers</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576283","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/model-driven-apps/generative-pages"},{"id":"rm-577878","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Payables Agent - Agent can process vendor credit notes","desc":"<p>Payables Agent can recognize a vendor credit note and produce a purchase credit memo and applies to the original invoice, using the same draft and task experience as invoices. Note: It does not have Return Order matching functionality.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577878","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-578069","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: IVR capabilities - Equip voice agents with custom voice","desc":"<p>Secure a voice talent that will represent the voice of your brand. After <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/responsible-ai/speech-service/text-to-speech/disclosure-voice-talent\">obtaining explicit consent</a>, gaining <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/responsible-ai/speech-service/text-to-speech/limited-access\">Limited Access</a> approval through Microsoft's Responsible AI practices, and <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/custom-neural-voice\">building a custom voice model</a>, it's time to integrate with Dynamics 365 Contact Center.</p> <p>In the Copilot Service admin center, create a connection between Dynamics 365 and Azure. Navigate to <strong>Channels</strong> &gt; <strong>Custom AI Voices</strong> &gt; <strong>Connect custom voice</strong>. You'll be prompted through a series of cascading dropdown boxes to select the speech resource and custom voice model to connect with. After the connection is established, you can create a voice channel for self-service and use the custom voice, like any portfolio voice.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Brand identity extends beyond visuals like logo, color, and typography, into voice. Custom neural voice enables enterprises to create a distinctive, natural sounding synthetic voice for contact centers. By training on approved human speech samples, organizations can deliver a natural sounding, one‑of‑a‑kind brand voice that preserves brand continuity, strengthens customer recognition, and elevates voice‑based experiences across AI‑powered agents and telephony interactions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578069","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576609","title":"Microsoft Teams: Default meeting templates","desc":"<p>Default meeting templates enable IT admins to automatically apply their organization’s preferred meeting settings whenever users schedule a Teams meeting through Outlook or Teams calendar. This helps organizations apply meeting settings (including protection settings) at scale, and reduce the need for organizers to manually configure meeting options. Only organizers with a Teams Premium (T-Pre) license assigned can use Default Meeting Templates.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576609","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577399","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced Copilot and AI controls for meetings","desc":"<p>Teams Meetings offer enhanced AI controls for Copilot and AI experiences. Organizers manage who can enable and access AI, while IT admins get a simpler policy model for governing AI across meetings and post-meeting experiences. These updates provide more predictable administration and greater flexibility for compliance and governance scenarios.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577399","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576285","title":"Power Apps: Expand model access and Maker Studio availability for generative pages via GitHub","desc":"<p>Connect your GitHub account to access additional model options for the built-in gen page coding agent directly in the generative page designer in Maker Studio. Makers can use the agent to create and refine generative pages without leaving the Power Apps authoring experience.</p> <p>This integration also brings Maker Studio generative page authoring to regions without dedicated Power Apps GPU capacity.</p> <p>Model availability through GitHub may evolve over time, and requests made through this connection consume the maker’s GitHub credits.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2611.1</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Admins or makers</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576285","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/model-driven-apps/generative-pages"},{"id":"rm-576279","title":"Power Apps: Model-driven apps - Use row summaries in US Government clouds","desc":"<p>Row summaries are expanding to supported US Government clouds, giving users in regulated environments access to AI-generated insights that help them understand model-driven app records at a glance. This release brings the row summary experience available to commercial customers to supported government environments while meeting their applicable compliance and data-boundary requirements.</p> <p>Admins and makers enable and configure row summaries for users in their model-driven apps.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2611.1</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Users (enabled by admins or makers)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576279","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577900","title":"Power Pages: Plugin support for GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code to create and edit traditional sites","desc":"<p>The Power Pages plugin for GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code now supports creating and editing traditional (non-SPA) Power Pages sites. Developers can use natural-language prompts in their AI coding agent to create a new traditional site or download, inspect, and update existing site metadata such as web pages, web templates, content snippets, basic and multistep forms, lists, table permissions, web roles, and site settings, then upload changes back to their environment using the Power Platform CLI.</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577900","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-578068","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Envision and design AI agents in Business Central","desc":"<h3>AI agents in Business Central</h3> <p>Business Central introduces AI agents to help users automate repetitive tasks and make business processes more intelligent and efficient. These agents act as specialized assistants that understand context, handle structured data, and collaborate with users to complete end-to-end workflows. For example, the Sales Order Agent simplifies order creation by transforming natural language or email instructions into complete sales documents, while the Payables Agent streamlines vendor invoice processing by extracting key details from incoming invoices and matching them to purchase orders—all reducing manual effort and freeing users to focus on higher-value work.</p> <p>The agent runtime that powers these built-in agents provides core capabilities that enable the use of agentic AI within Business Central. AI agents are defined, configured, activated, and run directly inside the familiar Business Central environment—leveraging the same security model, administration tools, and user experience as the rest of the product. Results are displayed in-context, with intuitive navigation to related data and entities, allowing users to control the agents through the interface they already know. This consistency dramatically reduces the learning curve, builds trust, and ensures efficiency when working with AI agents.</p> <p>The agent runtime ensures that every step taken by an agent is traceable and operates strictly within the access boundaries (permissions) assigned during configuration. It provides a timeline view of all agent activities, allowing users to review what happened and why—enabling a true human-in-the-loop experience. The runtime can also memorize relevant data during execution, use it in subsequent steps, and request additional instructions in natural language when user input is needed. It helps ensure that sensitive operations always require explicit user review and consent, supporting full transparency and control.</p> <p>Business Central business processes are inherently multistep, stateful, and financially consequential. The agent layer must be able to interact with a broad set of ERP capabilities and data, sequence operations with a high degree of accuracy across dependent steps, handle the data respecting permissions, company, environment, and tenant boundaries, provide a contextual audit trail, and keep humans in the loop.</p> <p>Business Central agentic strategy intentionally separates deep, well controlled, in-context and transparent execution within the product from cross-system orchestration. Business Central agents form the foundational layer inside the product, exposing well-defined agent capabilities that in the future will be possible to surface as MCP tools and consume by Declarative Agents in Microsoft Copilot Studio and Microsoft 365. This layered approach enables Business Central-tuned, transparent, managed execution at the ERP core processes, while allowing higher-level Declarative Agents to orchestrate end-to-end business processes across products.</p> <h3>Designing agents</h3> <p>The new in-product experience for designing agents that automate Business Central processes is made available with AI Development Toolkit for Business Central. The experience offers a low-risk environment for envisioning and prototyping new AI agents tailored to your own business scenarios—extending the same agent runtime capabilities used by built-in Business Central agents.</p> <p>Built for rapid iteration, the designing experience lets you create and refine custom agents using natural language instructions, define their behavior, test agent profiles and permissions, and safely experiment with Business Central data in a sandbox environment. This approach empowers partner personas like consultants, product owners, and domain experts, as well as developers and even power users, to explore new scenarios, validate ideas, and build confidence in their agents before moving to production. Whether you aim to automate repetitive business processes, streamline data processing, or deliver proactive insights, the agent design experience gives you the tools to bring your vision to life.</p> <h3>Agent instructions</h3> <p>At the core of every agent are its goals and instructions, defined in natural language. Writing agent instructions is similar to writing prompts for large language models, so you can apply general prompt-writing best practices—and even use tools like Copilot to optimize them. The agent design experience includes a simple editor to help you define, refine, and test these instructions efficiently.</p> <h3>Invoking your agent</h3> <p>You can invoke your agent by manually creating a task for it. When doing so, you can include an additional message that provides specific details or context to complement the agent’s core instructions. Although the ability to design your own agents is in public preview, there aren't yet any built-in integrations to automatically trigger these custom agents based on incoming emails, events, or scheduled recurrences (this can be done by professional developers using the APIs available in the AI Development Toolkit). However, you can simulate these scenarios by including the email header and body in the task message to mimic incoming emails, or by manually triggering the agent to emulate event, UI action, or time-based runs.</p> <h3>Troubleshooting</h3> <p>When running the agent tasks in the designing experience, you can access detailed diagnostic views to help you understand and tune the agent execution. Since an agent’s decisions depend on its instructions, available data, and language model reasoning, you can review execution logs to see its inputs, reasoning process, and outputs. This helps you identify where uncertainty occurred and why specific decisions were made to adjust your agent instructions.</p> <h3>Importing and exporting agents</h3> <p>To make it easy to back up or move custom agents across sandbox environments, the in-product experience allows you to import and export agent definitions. These definitions are stored as simple JSON files containing properties such as agent identity, instructions, assigned profiles, and permissions. We recommend storing these files in a source control system like GitHub to track changes and maintain version history.</p> <h3>Responsible AI</h3> <p>Agents built using the agent design experience adhere to Microsoft’s Responsible AI principles, helping you ensure agent compliance, fairness, and safety.</p> <h3>Billing</h3> <p>As with the built-in Sales Order and Payables agents, custom agents consume Copilot credits as they perform their steps. Credits can be provisioned through prepaid or pay-as-you-go models, providing flexible cost management as your AI usage scales.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Agents in Business Central are AI-powered team assistants that go beyond traditional automation. Unlike static workflows or hard-coded AL logic, agents can interpret high-level business goals expressed in natural language and translate them into actionable steps. They reason over Business Central data, make informed decisions within defined boundaries, and collaborate with users through human-in-the-loop approvals for critical operations.</p> <p>The benefits are substantial: agents reduce manual effort by automating repetitive or complex tasks, allowing users to focus on higher-value activities. They adapt to dynamic business scenarios that can't always be anticipated during development, offering flexibility that traditional automation lacks. Most importantly, agents operate transparently: every action is logged, permissions are rigorously enforced, and users remain in control at all times.</p> <p>This combination of intelligence, adaptability, and accountability makes agents a cornerstone of the next generation of ERP experiences. With the agent design experience, we're taking the first steps toward enabling you to build your own custom Business Central agents.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578068","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"February CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/ai/ai-development-toolkit-overview"},{"id":"rm-576607","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Use overflow actions to protect customer experience for direct inward calls","desc":"<p>Overflow for direct inward dialing leverages conversation orchestration to detect key direct inward dialing-related events—such as the representative being busy, offline, rejecting the call, or failing to answer—and apply administrator-defined fallback actions.</p> <p>Administrators configure natural language playbooks using conversation orchestration at the global or inbound profile level to specify the action to run when a direct inward dialed call can't be attended to or completed. The actions include offering a direct callback to the caller, sending them to voicemail, transferring the call to another queue or external number, or ending the call.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576607","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-578073","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Workforce engagement management - Manage overnight shifts as a single continuous schedule","desc":"<p>Supervisors can now create and manage overnight shifts that span across midnight while maintaining a single continuous shift experience. Shift plans support start and end times that extend into the next day, allowing organizations to accurately model overnight operations such as contact centers, support teams, healthcare services, and other 24x7 environments.<br> Activities, breaks, meals, and ad-hoc work can be scheduled anywhere within the overnight shift and remain part of a single continuous itinerary. Supervisors can view and manage the entire shift without manually splitting schedules across calendar days. Activities that cross midnight are preserved as a single record and are not divided into separate activities.<br> The system maintains a consistent ownership model where the shift belongs to the day on which it starts. Paid hours, schedule ownership, adherence calculations, and related scheduling behaviors continue to follow the shift-start day, providing predictable scheduling outcomes regardless of how the shift is displayed.<br> When viewing schedules across multiple shift plans, overnight shifts are displayed within the standard daily schedule view. When viewing an individual shift plan, supervisors can see the full overnight shift as a single continuous work session, making it easier to manage overnight operations and understand employee schedules.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Support 24×7 operations.<br> Eliminate workarounds that require splitting shifts across days.<br> Improve migration readiness from Verint, Genesys, NICE, UKG, and Calabrio.<br> Provide predictable overnight scheduling behavior.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578073","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569210","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): CSV and TSV references in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"<p>Copilot Notebooks now supports CSV and TSV files as knowledge sources, allowing users to bring structured lists and tables directly into their projects alongside traditional documents. This additional context helps Copilot generate more relevant presentations, reports, and briefs.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569210","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569211","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): JPG and PNG references in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"<p>Copilot Notebooks now supports JPG and PNG files as knowledge sources, allowing users to bring images directly into their projects alongside traditional documents. Copilot can use the content within these images, including text, charts, diagrams, and other visuals, as grounding context to help generate more relevant presentations, reports, and briefs.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569211","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-578066","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Digital commerce - Streamline multioutlet access for B2B web storefronts","desc":"<p>The multioutlet B2B web storefront introduces a unified sign-in system that allows buyers to access all their associated organizations and outlets using a single account. The storefront UI is updated to display an organization selector during sign-in and provides outlet-specific navigation and catalog views. Buyers can place, track, and manage orders for multiple outlets within a single session, with real-time visibility into order status, inventory, and account information.</p> <p>This feature supports role-based access, ensuring that users only see the organizations and outlets they are authorized to transact with. This experience is behind a feature flag that's available for administrators to update from Commerce headquarters. Administrators must configure organization and outlet relationships, assign users to their respective organizations, and activate the unified sign-in option in the storefront settings.</p> <p>The following features are available after enabling this feature:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Unified sign-in with organization selector</strong>: Enables buyers to select their organization during sign-in for multioutlet ordering and tracking.</li> <li><strong>On-account payments and credit limits</strong>: Provides real-time credit validation for organization accounts during checkout to ensure compliance and reduce payment friction.</li> <li><strong>Seller inventory visibility and Commerce Scale Unit (CSU) tools.</strong></li> <li><strong>Account header updates</strong>: Displays the organization name and linked accounts for clarity.</li> <li><strong>User management</strong>: Allows B2B organization administrators to use contacts to directly manage users from Commerce headquarters.</li> <li><strong>Multicart shopping</strong>: Enables individual contacts to manage separate carts for different outlets under one organization account.</li> <li><strong>CSU tools</strong>: Assist contact-based B2B sellers in the business partner employee role to implement real-time inventory data and efficiently accept or reject multioutlet orders.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature empowers business-to-business (B2B) buyers with a seamless, unified experience across multiple outlets. This feature simplifies account management by enabling a single sign-in for all organizations, reducing friction and improving efficiency. Buyers can place and track orders for multiple outlets from one storefront, thereby reducing errors. Buyers can use a single sign-in to access all their organizations, view outlet-specific catalogs, and manage orders for all their organizations in one place.</p> <p>By consolidating workflows and account management, businesses can increase productivity, reduce errors, and deliver a seamless experience that drives customer satisfaction and loyalty. The unified approach also supports faster onboarding for new outlets. For your business, this means stronger customer loyalty, higher order volumes, and streamlined operations, while delivering a modern, intuitive experience that differentiates your brand in a competitive market.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578066","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/commerce/b2b/b2b-multi-outlet"},{"id":"rm-578061","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Omnichannel commerce - Add support for multiple outlet B2B ordering via CSU","desc":"<p>Available for B2B scenarios in Dynamics 365 Commerce (including headless Commerce), this feature enables retailers to configure unified sign-in in Commerce headquarters and integrate third‑party storefronts using CSU APIs. The organization selector and related capabilities are exposed via CSU endpoints so that third-party sites can consume identities, organizational context, and ordering workflows without relying on native UI components.</p> <p>Functional enhancements</p> <ul> <li><strong>Contact model transition</strong>: Replaces the customer account type \"Person\" with type \"Contact\" to better manage B2B partners.</li> <li><strong>Single contact linking</strong>: Links one customer contact to multiple organizations within the hierarchy.</li> <li><strong>Customer hierarchy improvements</strong>: Links B2B buyer and seller contacts to organization accounts directly from the customer hierarchy.</li> <li><strong>Unified ordering</strong>: Enables buyers to purchase for multiple outlets using a single account.</li> <li><strong>Organization credit limits</strong>: Allows all authorized buyers to order against the credit limit for their organization.</li> <li><strong>Sales order invoices</strong>: Generates sales orders and invoices tied directly to the organization account.</li> <li><strong>Organization account-based experiences</strong>: Automatically populates buyer address and credit limits from the organization account.</li> <li><strong>Order taker identification</strong>: Captures the buyer's name as the order taker in the sales order.</li> <li><strong>Auditing</strong>: Enables easy auditing of user activity orders across multiple outlets.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature simplifies purchasing for business-to-business (B2B) buyers by enabling a single sign-in to manage multiple outlet orders. It reduces friction, improves operational efficiency, and ensures accurate credit and address data for every transaction, even when using third-party storefronts powered by a headless Commerce engine. By using Commerce Scale Unit (CSU) for contact identity and organizational context, businesses can unify sign-in, streamline workflows, and reduce operational complexity for B2B buyers who are managing multiple outlets. This flexibility enables retailers to extend multioutlet capabilities beyond native Dynamics 365 Commerce storefronts, accelerating innovation and improving buyer confidence across diverse channels.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578061","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/commerce/b2b/b2b-multi-outlet"},{"id":"rm-578064","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Copilot and AI innovation - Resolve customer emails autonomously with AI","desc":"<p>Autonomous email resolution delivers end-to-end handling of customer emails without manual intervention or default case creation. When an email arrives, the system analyzes the request, identifies the underlying intent, and determines whether the information and actions needed to resolve it are available.</p> <p>Using enterprise knowledge, configured business instructions, connectors, and custom agents, the system constructs a resolution dynamically. It generates a response that's context-aware, compliant with business rules, and tailored to the request, then delivers it directly by email—completing the interaction autonomously.</p> <p>If the customer isn't satisfied or the issue can't be resolved automatically, the system creates a case that carries the full conversation context, including customer intent, actions taken, and generated responses. A service representative can then step in without losing context or duplicating work.</p> <p>The capability is delivered through the Case Management Agent. An administrator enables the setting and sets the automation level for each line of business, from fully autonomous resolution to drafting a response for a service representative to review and send.</p> <p>This shifts email handling from a case-first workflow to an intent-driven resolution model, reducing manual effort, improving consistency, and accelerating time to resolution for high-volume customer interactions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Autonomous email resolution drives faster, consistent responses and frees service representatives to focus on complex, high-impact issues. It improves customer satisfaction and operational efficiency and scales support without increasing response times and costs by automatically resolving high-volume email inquiries.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578064","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-service/administer/configure-email-resolution"},{"id":"rm-578076","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Lead management - Deploy multiple Sales Qualification Agents in a single environment","desc":"<ul> <li><strong>Segment-specific qualification</strong>: Each agent operates with its own ideal customer profile, knowledge sources, templates, and consent settings, ensuring qualification conversations reflect the nuances of each product, region, or team.</li> <li><strong>Intelligent lead routing</strong>: The system evaluates incoming leads against agent selection criteria and assigns ownership based on configured priority, ensuring predictable and conflict-free lead management. A fallback agent handles leads that don't match any specialized criteria, ensuring no lead goes unprocessed.</li> <li><strong>Exclusive engagement with coordinated handoff</strong>: Only one agent engages a lead at any time. When a lead's interest shifts to another product or segment, the system hands off with full context to the appropriate agent.</li> <li><strong>Shared knowledge foundation</strong>: Agents can leverage common company-level knowledge while maintaining their own specialized sources, ensuring consistent answers across the organization.</li> <li><strong>Supervisor oversight and governance</strong>: A centralized dashboard enables supervisors to monitor agent activity, reassign leads, and track the full qualification journey across all agents.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Multi-agent configuration in Sales Qualification Agents enables sales organizations to deploy agents aligned to distinct product lines, regions, or sales teams, each with its own qualification criteria, knowledge sources, and engagement approach. Multi-agent configuration ensures exclusive lead ownership, coordinates handoffs when context shifts, and provides sales managers with visibility across agents. This targeted approach mirrors real-world sales structures, eliminates duplicate outreach, accelerates qualification, and scales coverage without additional seller headcount.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578076","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-578063","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Planning - Protect confirmed CTP dates with Planning Optimization","desc":"<p>Planning Optimization is the new high-performance planning engine for Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. With this feature, Planning Optimization now protects material and capacity allocated to sales order lines with delivery dates confirmed through capable to promise (CTP). You prevent reallocation of resources to newer orders, so your confirmed delivery dates stay reliable, and customer commitments are honored.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Protect your confirmed delivery dates with confidence. When you use capable to promise (CTP) for delivery date control with Planning Optimization, this feature ensures your commitments stay reliable, thereby preventing last-minute changes or manual fixes. You keep customer trust high and reduce the time spent adjusting orders or reallocating resources.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578063","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/master-planning/planning-optimization/keep-supply-for-confirmed-demand"},{"id":"rm-562351","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Get actionable suggestions from Copilot in your Copilot Page","desc":"<p>Request feedback from Copilot on your Page by selecting \"Suggested edits\" in the Copilot Shortcuts menu. Copilot will analyze the content on your page and provide actionable suggestions about what you can change to improve clarity and quality of your written content. You can then apply suggestions directly to the page. Updated October 23, 2026: We have decided not to move forward with this change at this time. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Cancelled","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562351","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-396575","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Decoupling of Policy tips and Email notifications while configuring rules on Data Loss Prevention for Sharepoint and Onedriv","desc":"<p>As of today, whenever the user wants to enable email notifications the policy tips also need to be enabled and vice versa, but with this decoupling the admin can configure the following: 1) None of policy tips or email notification 2) Only policy tips 3) Only Email Notifications 4) Both Email Notifications and Policy tips</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-05-14","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=396575","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-559482","title":"Microsoft Viva: Recent feed in Viva Engage","desc":"<p>Introducing a new “Recent” feed in Home to give users a more predictable view of followed and priority communications, while preserving the existing personalized “For you” experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-01","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559482","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566316","title":"OneDrive: Refreshed file browsing and filtering experience in OneDrive Web","desc":"<pre><code>OneDrive is making it easier to find and work with files across Microsoft 365. We're refreshing the filtering experience across OneDrive Web, updating existing filters in views like Home, Shared, People, Meetings, and Favorites to support multiple filters at once, and bringing those same filtering capabilities to folder-based experiences such as My files and shared folders. Users can also filter content by file type using both filter pills and the filter pane. </code></pre> <p>We're also bringing the modern SharePoint document library experience to OneDrive Web, with an updated layout, improved navigation, and familiar file management capabilities. Together, these updates make it easier to browse, filter, and manage content, while providing a more seamless experience across OneDrive and SharePoint.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566316","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-568368","title":"Outlook: Copilot Chat pop-out for Outlook for Mac and iPad","desc":"<p>Copilot Chat remains accessible within an Outlook app window but now can also be popped out to float over the main Outlook app window. Popping out Copilot Chat allows people to switch contexts or have more space for what they are working on in Outlook and control the space and form that Copilot Chat takes on screen. When you open Copilot chat and click the pop-out button, Copilot will open separately over the main Outlook window.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568368","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-578065","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Run multiple Sales Order Agents per company with smarter item matching, relevance filtering, and streamlined setup","desc":"<p>You can now configure and run multiple Sales Order Agent instances in a single company. Each instance operates independently with its own mailbox, folder settings, email signature, and processing rules.</p> <p>Each agent instance tracks its own KPI metrics, such as emails received, quotes created, orders created, and time saved. The setup page is restructured to support per-instance configuration, and an upgrade path migrates existing single-instance setups to the new architecture. This change allows organizations to set up separate agents for different sales teams, product lines, or customer segments, each monitoring their own personal or shared mailbox.</p> <h3>Improved items search:</h3> <p>When a customer requests items, the agent now uses a multi-layer matching strategy:</p> <ul> <li>Exact identifier match: direct lookup by item number, vendor item number, GTIN, or cross-reference.</li> <li>Semantic attribute matching: extracts attributes from the customer's message (color, material, size) and ranks candidates by relevance using AI.</li> <li>Broader fuzzy search: falls back to a global item search when direct and attribute-based searches produce no results.</li> </ul> <h3>Message and attachment relevance:</h3> <p>The agent now validates incoming messages and attachments against a detailed relevance model before processing. Messages that fall outside the agent's responsibilities (such as offers to sell, requests for discounts, or attempts to extract internal information) are identified and filtered.</p> <p>A separate relevance check runs on attachments, ensuring that non-sales-related documents don't trigger unnecessary processing. The validation considers the full conversation history and the agent's defined scope to make accurate relevance decisions.</p> <h3>Larger attachment files with diagnostics.</h3> <p>The maximum number of pages per PDF attachment has been raised from 10 to 50, addressing customer feedback about the agent not reading larger purchase orders. A new cumulative content length limit of 150,000 characters is also enforced across all attachments in a single email (approximately 50K tokens).</p> <p>When an attachment is skipped, Business Central now stores the specific reason directly on the attachment record (page count exceeded, cumulative content length exceeded, attachment count exceeded, unsupported format, or analyze-attachments not enabled). This information is visible on the <strong>Attachments</strong> page and logged in telemetry, making it straightforward to diagnose why a particular document wasn't processed.</p> <h3>Try it out.</h3> <p>You can now create tasks for the Sales Order Agent without sending an email. From the agent's setup page, a new <strong>Try it out</strong> section lets you compose a message by selecting a sender (from your contact or customer list), entering message text, and attaching files. The agent acts like it received a real email.</p> <p>To help you get started quickly, two sample messages are included. One is a text-only message that references items from your catalog, and the other is a message with a sample purchase order attachment. The sample order is generated based on your actual item data, so the agent has realistic content to work with.</p> <p>These samples are particularly useful for first-time setup, demos, and testing agent behavior with specific scenarios without needing to send an actual email.</p> <h3>Handling of unknown senders</h3> <p>When the agent receives an email from an unregistered email address, you now have three options instead of just one:</p> <ul> <li>Create a new contact: register the sender as a new contact (existing behavior)</li> <li>Use another contact once: pick an existing contact from the contact list and link them to this specific task only, without modifying any master data. The override is stored per task message and does not affect future emails.</li> <li>Update an existing contact's email: select an existing contact and update their email address to the sender's address</li> </ul> <h3>More control over email</h3> <p>New configuration options give administrators more control over how the agent interacts with the monitored mailbox:</p> <ul> <li>Mark email as read: a new toggle to mark processed emails as read in the mailbox. This works in addition to the custom <em>Processed by Sales Order Agent</em> category, giving users a visual signal in their inbox.</li> <li>Mandatory folder selection: the agent now requires you to select a specific mailbox folder before activation. Previously this was optional and could lead to the agent monitoring an unexpected folder. If in doubt, choose <em>Inbox</em>.</li> <li>Stricter activation validation: trying to activate the agent without a mailbox folder now shows a clear error message instead of allowing activation in an ambiguous state.</li> </ul> <h3>Prompts as embedded resources.</h3> <p>The agent's AI prompts (instructions, item search logic, mail template checks, irrelevance validation) are now shipped as embedded resource files within the app extension package. This change reduces latency on first task processing and makes the prompt structure more transparent for engineering iteration.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Sales Order Agent now handles more complex organizational structures and higher volumes with less manual intervention. You can run multiple agent instances in one company, each dedicated to a different team or shared mailbox with independent settings and performance tracking. The agent finds the right items more reliably by understanding product attributes, informal descriptions, and identifiers across multiple matching layers.<br> The agent now processes PDFs up to 50 pages (previously, the limit was 10) and clearly shows why any attachment was skipped. It also filters irrelevant messages before processing, so credits aren't consumed by marketing emails or out-of-scope inquiries. If a customer writes from an unregistered email address, you can link an existing contact to that single task without creating duplicates. You can test the agent directly from the setup page without sending a real email, reducing the time to validate your configuration.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578065","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-578075","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Enable enhanced screen recording controls for admins","desc":"<p>The enhanced screen recording capability offers greater flexibility and control, enabling organizations to manage recording behavior with more precision. Key enhancements include:</p> <ul> <li>Access all recording settings and configurations from <strong>Customer Service admin center</strong> &gt; <strong>Quality Management</strong>.</li> <li>Enable or disable screen recording using a dedicated toggle.</li> <li>Capture call audio alongside screen recordings.</li> <li>Turn off the red border displayed around representative screens during active window recording.</li> <li>Allow users with the screen recording supervisor role to play recordings within the Customer Service workspace.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You get more control over how your team captures and reviews screen activity. Role-based access makes it easy to decide who can view or download recordings, helping you stay compliant and maintain oversight. You can also play recordings directly in the Customer Service workspace, so investigations move faster. These updates cut rework, save time, and make coaching and performance reviews more effective.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578075","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577796","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Enforce governance policies on email attachments","desc":"<p>This feature extends governance capabilities to evaluate email attachments, closing a critical gap where sensitive or non-compliant information may exist outside the email body.</p> <p>When a user sends an email with attachments, the system automatically scans each document and applies configured governance policies. In the initial release, analysis is focused on plain text content within supported document types, such as Word and PDF files. Non-text elements, including images or embedded content, are excluded in this phase to ensure predictable and efficient processing.</p> <p>Every attachment included in an email is evaluated individually, and all applicable policies are enforced across each file. If multiple attachments are present, governance policies check all of them, ensuring that no document bypasses validation. If even a single attachment violates a configured policy, such as containing restricted content or failing compliance rules, the entire email is blocked from being sent.</p> <p>Administrators can configure policies to explicitly include attachment checks during policy setup. This allows organizations to apply governance selectively based on business needs, such as enforcing stricter controls for sensitive communications while maintaining flexibility for general scenarios. Existing policies can be updated to enable attachment analysis, while new policies can be configured to include attachments by default where required.</p> <p>To ensure transparency and accountability, all attachment evaluations are logged, including details such as which attachment triggered a violation and the reason for failure. Users are provided with clear feedback when an email is blocked, helping them quickly identify and correct issues before resending. This improves user experience while maintaining strong governance controls.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can now apply governance controls to email attachments, not just the message body. This helps you stop sensitive or non-compliant content from being sent externally. By scanning attachment text, you catch policy issues early and block risky emails before they go out. That means stronger compliance, less data leakage, and consistent protection across every outbound channel.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577796","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577798","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Manage policy strictness to enforce governance policies","desc":"<p>This feature introduces policy strictness control, enabling organizations to define how rigorously each governance policy evaluates and flags potential violations in outgoing emails. Governance policies serve as real-time guardrails, ensuring communications adhere to business, legal, and compliance standards before they are sent to customers.</p> <p>With this enhancement, supervisors can configure the strictness level for each policy. Lower strictness settings apply more lenient enforcement, reducing false positives and allowing borderline scenarios to pass, while higher settings perform more rigorous checks to identify subtle or potentially risky violations. This flexibility allows organizations to align policy enforcement with their compliance requirements and risk tolerance.</p> <p>All policies are set to medium strictness by default, providing a balanced level of enforcement. Organizations can then adjust strictness levels per policy depending on the nature of the rule. For example, highly sensitive policies, such as those related to data protection or regulatory compliance, can be configured with stricter enforcement, while policies focused on tone or content guidance can be set to be more lenient to avoid unnecessary disruptions.</p> <p>At runtime, the governance policies use the configured strictness level to determine how policy violations are flagged when outgoing emails are evaluated. This ensures that enforcement is consistent and adaptable across different policy types and business scenarios.</p> <p>By enabling strictness control at the policy level, organizations can fine-tune governance enforcement without modifying the underlying policy definitions, helping balance compliance protection, agent productivity, and a seamless customer communication experience.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Take control of how your governance policies handle outbound email violations. With adjustable strictness levels, you can cut down on false positives when flexibility matters or apply tighter controls for sensitive situations. This balance helps you build confidence in AI-driven enforcement while keeping your policies aligned with your risk tolerance, compliance requirements, and business goals.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577798","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-578070","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Modify and override submitted evaluations","desc":"<p>This feature enables Quality Managers to edit and override evaluation results even after they are marked as completed or expired. While completed evaluations remain read-only by default to preserve integrity, supervisors can initiate an <strong>Edit</strong> action when discrepancies are identified, such as incorrect AI predictions or errors in manual assessments.</p> <p>In edit mode, supervisors can update evaluation responses, adjust scores, and refine comments to reflect an accurate assessment. This ensures that evaluation records represent the final, validated view of agent performance and interaction quality. The capability is available across AI-assisted, AI agent-generated, and manual evaluations, providing a consistent correction experience.</p> <p>To maintain control and governance, only authorized users with supervisory permissions can perform overrides. All changes are tracked through audit signals, including who made the edit and when, and overridden evaluations are clearly flagged. This ensures full transparency for reporting, compliance, and downstream reviews.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enables Quality Managers or users with privileges to correct completed evaluations when inaccuracies arise from AI predictions or human review errors. This ensures evaluation outcomes accurately reflect real-world context and business standards. By introducing controlled human-in-the-loop oversight with full auditability, organizations can confidently scale automated and manual evaluations while maintaining trust, transparency, and governance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578070","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-578077","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Lead management - Personalize outreach emails generated by Sales Qualification Agent","desc":"<ul> <li>Define outreach scenario/goal in natural language.</li> <li>Choose desired call-to-action to drive next steps.</li> <li>Provide subject line guidance: fixed suggestion or style recommendation.</li> <li>Set message length and brevity targets.</li> <li>Specify tone rules, including name-usage limits and preferred terminology.</li> <li>Configure brand language and voice guardrails: approved phrases and banned words.</li> <li>Set formatting preferences: bullets, paragraph length, and maximum bullet count.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature expands the Sales Qualification Agent outreach by letting teams define the outreach purpose, brand-aligned tone (matching both company voice and seller style), the call-to-action, and key messaging preferences proven to resonate with prospects. The result is more relevant, consistent communication that drives higher response rates and, in turn, improves lead qualification rates.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578077","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-578072","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Boost productivity with flexible views and search in segments","desc":"<ul> <li>Customize your view: choose a Contact or Lead view from the new view picker to define which columns appear in the segment members table.</li> <li>Align export with your view: exported member data automatically reflects your selected columns, ensuring consistency and eliminating post-export cleanup.</li> <li>Quickly find specific members: use the built-in search to locate individuals within the segment membership list instantly.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Understanding and acting on your audience starts with having the right data at your fingertips. Until now, getting the full context for segment members often meant switching between views, exporting data, or manually piecing information together.<br> With flexible views and in-list search, you can quickly surface the information that matters most directly within the segment. Customize the fields you want to see, find specific members faster, and work more efficiently without extra steps. The result is a more streamlined experience that helps you stay focused and act with confidence.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578072","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-577805","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Set message expirations to keep communication relevant","desc":"<ul> <li>Set an expiration date on any message in your journeys (emails, text messages, push notifications, or custom).</li> <li>Choose from different expiration options (no expiry, expiration based on a date and time, or a trigger).</li> <li>Review analytics to understand which customers didn't receive messages due to expiration dates.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Contoso specializes in hosting virtual events and webinars for their customers. They have a customer journey designed to promote upcoming events, send reminders, and offer exclusive discounts to attendees.</p> <ul> <li>Contoso sets expiration dates on event reminder messages. This ensures that customers who register only a few days before the event don't receive the full series of reminders.</li> <li>They offer discounts for people registering four months prior to the event. To make sure customers receive only valid offers, Contoso sets these discount messages to expire four months before the webinar date.</li> </ul> <p>By setting expiration dates on message tiles, Contoso keeps its communications up to date and relevant. Customers who join the journey get timely information, which enhances their experience and engagement.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Customers may experience frustration when they receive outdated communications, such as expired coupons and irrelevant reminders. This creates confusion and diminishes their trust in your brand. You can now set expiration dates on your messages, ensuring that only current and relevant information reaches your audience. This keeps your customers engaged and satisfied with relevant communications in moments that matter.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577805","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/message-expiration"},{"id":"rm-578067","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Enforce governance policy","desc":"<p>Create and enforce policies that prevent risky or noncompliant customer communications.</p> <p>Governance policy checks serve as configurable safeguards that review AI‑generated and autonomous email responses before they are sent to customers. These checks enforce business, legal, and regulatory requirements by validating responses for relevance, prohibited content, and sensitive topics. If a response fails a policy check, delivery is blocked and the violation is clearly identified, enabling supervisors to review issues and take actions to improve outcomes.</p> <p>Governance policies are applied consistently across email engagement channels and seamlessly embedded within agent workflows, ensuring uniform enforcement of quality and compliance standards without requiring manual intervention. This approach empowers organizations to scale AI-assisted and autonomous customer engagement with confidence while upholding trust, safety, and governance.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Governance policies give you control over AI-driven customer interactions. By setting clear, configurable rules, you make sure every response meets your business, legal, and regulatory standards before it reaches customers. This reduces risk, protects your brand, and keeps communication consistent and trustworthy.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-23","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=578067","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-service/administer/configure-governance-policies"},{"id":"rm-488301","title":"Microsoft Teams: Speaker attribution now “On” by default in BYOD rooms with enhanced admin controls","desc":"<p>New PowerShell setting (SpeakerAttributionBYOD in csTeamsAIPolicy), enabled by default, gives IT admins more control over speaker attribution in BYOD (bring your own device) meeting rooms. This enhances the experience for users by enabling clear speaker labels and richer in-meeting and post-meeting insights with Microsoft 365 Copilot. Users just enroll profiles via Teams Settings to be recognized.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-08","modified":"2026-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488301","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-577787","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Improve contract management usability","desc":"<p>The enhanced Project Contract experience streamlines how you create, manage, and monitor contracts by significantly reducing the number of clicks and interactions required. This update transforms the contract into a central, intuitive workspace where all contract-related information is easier to access, understand, and act upon. The redesigned layout provides a clearer overview of contract status, financials, and performance, helping users work faster and with greater confidence.</p> <p>Core capabilities:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Modernized user experience</strong>: Aligns with improvements delivered in the Modern Quote feature and reduces unnecessary interactions across contract workflows.</li> <li><strong>Nested grids for better visibility</strong>: Quickly view detailed estimate breakdowns for each contract line directly within the grid—no need to open multiple forms.</li> <li><strong>Faster contract line management</strong>: Create and edit Contract Line Details from a single grid, including the ability to apply price overrides.</li> <li><strong>Improved financial clarity</strong>: Contract summary now includes key KPIs, total cost, gross margin, billing status, and tax information surfaced directly on the grid.</li> <li><strong>Streamlined contract lifecycle</strong>: Users can close a contract directly from the contract form, supported by improved visibility into contract health.</li> <li><strong>Contract performance dashboard</strong>: Enhanced insights to help users quickly understand contract progress and financial performance.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This enhancement significantly improves the efficiency and clarity of managing project contracts. By reducing clicks, consolidating key information, and modernizing the user experience, you can create, review, and update contracts much faster. Financial insights such as margins, costs, and billing status help users identify issues early and make confident decisions. Overall, the streamlined contract workspace reduces errors, accelerates project initiation, and improves productivity for project and billing teams.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577787","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577418","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Create journeys in minutes with Journey Creation Agent","desc":"<p>You simply describe in everyday words what you want to create and the Journey Creation Agent builds the journey for you.</p> <p>With Journey Creation Agent, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Use an AI-powered, guided experience for optimized outcomes.</li> <li>Build in minutes with no technical jargon, complex setup, or cold start. Use natural language to describe the journey you want to create.</li> <li>Drive results–the agent interprets your goal and asks relevant follow-up questions to refine your intent and ensure accuracy.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>A campaign manager wants to re-engage inactive customers but has no time to build a journey from scratch. The manager simply types, “Send a re-engagement email to customers who haven’t purchased in 90 days, follow up with a reminder with a discount.” The journey is instantly generated, with the right audience, content, and structure.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577418","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/journey-creation-agent"},{"id":"rm-577417","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Improve engagement and message timing with Outreach Optimization Agent","desc":"<p>Add the Outreach Optimization Agent to your journey, select the emails you want delivered, and let the agent handle timing and cadence automatically. With Outreach Optimization Agent, you can:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Start with an intelligent baseline</strong>: Outreach Optimization Agent automatically creates a baseline messaging plan for your audience by analyzing overall historical engagement patterns, producing a smart, generic plan that is designed to work well for most customers before any individual optimization kicks in.</li> <li><strong>Listen to incoming interactions and adapt the plan in real time</strong>: The agent continuously monitors incoming signals, including engagement and non-responsiveness, and adjusts follow-up timing and cadence, or exits the plan based on whether the goal is progressing or has been achieved.</li> <li><strong>Respect quiet times</strong>: The agent enforces quiet time settings as a hard constraint, ensuring that messages are never sent outside approved communication windows, even if engagement data suggests otherwise.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>A global retail brand uses Outreach Optimization Agent in a seasonal campaign to re-engage customers. Unlike previous efforts with fixed schedules and repeated reminders, the agent creates a smart baseline plan, then adjusts message timing for each customer based on their engagement. It slows or stops follow-ups when customers show interest and spaces out reminders for unresponsive customers, all while respecting quiet times and consent. This leads to better engagement and less message fatigue, with minimal manual intervention.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577417","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"July CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/outreach-optimization-agent"},{"id":"rm-577807","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - Optimize schedules with Scheduling Operations Agent","desc":"<p>Dispatchers often spend considerable time and energy reviewing and adjusting each technician's schedule as conditions change throughout the workday:</p> <ul> <li>A technician has one or more cancellations in the afternoon. To fill the open slots, what requirements optimally keep promise windows, prefer high-priority work, and locate work around the same neighborhoods that the technician is due to travel to?</li> <li>A technician is running over the planned time for the current booking. As a result, they're late for the next booking, and the delay might cascade to subsequent bookings. How do you best adjust the bookings for the remainder of the day?</li> <li>A technician recovers from illness sooner than expected and is now available for work earlier than planned. What's the best way to schedule work for them when they return?</li> <li>A technician’s schedule contains a lot of low-priority work that isn't due for weeks. How can you improve the schedule with work that better meets desired business goals?</li> <li>A technician’s schedule for the day is built manually or with the schedule assistant. How can you rearrange the schedule so that the resource’s travel time is reduced?</li> </ul> <p>In each case, the dispatcher needs to assess the situation, determine which business goals apply, and then update the schedule manually, one booking at a time.</p> <p>With this release of the Scheduling Operations Agent, dispatchers can ask Copilot to provide the best schedule for the affected technician. Within seconds, the dispatcher gets a suggested schedule for review and can apply the updates.</p> <p>You can direct Copilot to optimize for the business goal you want, such as maximizing technician usage or work order priority. Copilot intelligently chooses among existing bookings and new unfulfilled work orders based on factors like skillset match, territories, and customer promise windows. Users can access the feature from the Copilot side pane anywhere within the Dynamics 365 Field Service application.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Scheduling Operations Agent for Dynamics 365 Field Service enables dispatchers to quickly and easily optimize schedules for technicians as conditions change throughout the workday, so they can significantly improve their productivity. Dispatchers can ask Copilot to optimize schedules and address issues such as traffic delays, double bookings, or last-minute cancellations that often result in conflicts, gaps, or idle time in a technician's schedule. Instruct Copilot to achieve the desired business objective, such as maximizing technician usage or work order priority while considering factors like skillset match, territories, and promised time windows.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577807","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"June CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/soa-overview"},{"id":"rm-577424","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Extend price overrides to category and material","desc":"<p>Project Operations price lists support three price types — role, expense category, and product/material — but only role prices currently support date-effective overrides. This feature extends date-effective price overrides to expense category and material prices, so you can schedule a future or time-bound price change for a category or material the same way you do for a role, without creating a separate, context-specific price list. The system honors the override when it prices a transaction, so the effective price reflects the override in force on the transaction date. The feature also aligns other points where the three price types diverge where feasible, with date-effective overrides as the primary deliverable. Unit-group conversions for category and material, custom pricing dimensions for category and material, and full time-phasing of prices are not included in this release.</p> <p>How to enable: You configure overrides on the price list, the same way you set role-price overrides today, so pricing administrators and makers manage all three price types in one place. Overrides are stored in the existing Date-Effective Price Overrides table, so the feature is expected to reuse that mechanism; review any plug-ins or default pricing logic for category and material before you adopt it.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577424","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-577421","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: View resolved prices in a consolidated pricing view","desc":"<p>A new Pricing tab appears on the contract (and later the quote) and becomes the default pricing surface, replacing the Project Price List tab. Instead of listing only the price lists apply, it displays a consolidated grid of the prices that actually default for each pricing-dimension combination and date. You switch between price types, labor/role, category, and material, with a view picker, and role-price markups appear within the role view. A Date filter defaults to today and updates the grid to reflect date-effective overrides, and a Date effectivity column shows the date range each price is effective for. A Scope filter is set and locked automatically by the host record (Contract, Quote, Customer, Vendor purchase prices, or Org-unit cost prices). You can filter and sort across the pricing dimensions; grouping and frozen columns are not included in this release. Behind the grid, a unified query unions the Role Price and Date-Effective Price Overrides tables, de-duplicated and scoped to the price lists attached to the contract, and accounts for overrides at both the contract and associated customer levels.</p> <p>How to enable: The Pricing tab appears automatically on the contract form once the feature is deployed and enabled via the feature control menu. Because the new tab replaces the Project Price List tab as the primary surface, review any customizations or automation built against the existing tab before you adopt it. The price lists associated with the contract or quote will now be shown on the summary tab.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577421","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-576295","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Create pricing rules for attribute-based and volume-based pricing","desc":"<p>This feature will enable admins to define relevant pricing rules based on the following:<br> for the added list price based on product attributes<br> Discount on the list price based on tiered and absolute volume adjustment<br> This ensures the organization to associate the right pricing and discount policies to ensure profitability on their offered products and services.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576295","source":"roadmap","phases":["Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-576294","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Create product rules to guide sellers to valid product configurations","desc":"<p>This feature will allow admins to create the right set of compatibility, inclusion and exclusion rules, withing a single composite product to ensure the right set of products get bundled together. Based on the configured rules, the seller will receive relevant guidance while configuring a composite product for the customer to ensure an accurate product offering is provided to the customer. The scop of the rules will be at a single quote line relevant to a composite product.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576294","source":"roadmap","phases":["Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-565865","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Azure PST Import","desc":"<p>Azure PST Import is a migration method that enables PST files stored in Azure Blob Storage to be imported directly into Exchange Online mailboxes. It follows the standard two‑step Exchange Migration Service pattern: an initial analysis phase to validate and assess PST data, followed by execution of the actual migration. The process also involves creating a migration endpoint, running an analysis-only migration batch, using the analysis results to configure the final batch, and then starting the batch to import PST content into target mailboxes.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565865","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-577419","title":"Power Pages: SDK (Software Development Kit)","desc":"<p>Build native mobile applications or kioks using Power Pages as the backend foundation with support for authentication, authorization, APIs, data access, and reusable mobile capabilities.</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577419","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-577815","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Enable AI powered business workflows in Work IQ with Dataverse - Build Dataverse solutions with coding agents using Dataverse skills","desc":"<p>Build Dataverse solutions by using coding agents with natural language prompts. For example, \"I'm building a recruiting system for Zava Construction. I need tables for Positions, Candidates, Interviewers, Interviews, and Feedback - with lookups, a many-to-many relationship between Candidates and Positions, and a self-referential interview chain. Create everything in a Zava Recruiting solution, load sample data, and show me which candidates are currently interviewing.\"</p> <p>From this prompt, the agent autonomously:</p> <ol> <li>Discovers your Dataverse environment and configures MCP.</li> <li>Creates the solution by using the Microsoft Power Platform CLI.</li> <li>Builds five tables with choice columns, lookups, and a many-to-many relationship.</li> <li>Generates and runs a Python script to bulk-load realistic sample data.</li> <li>Queries across tables to answer your business question.</li> </ol> <p>No skill names. No tool flags. No context switching between docs, CLI, and scripts. The agent handles the orchestration end-to-end.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>By using coding agents, you can eliminate the need to manually create Microsoft Dataverse tables and solutions through the UI. Dataverse skills guide coding agents to connect to your environment and build solutions by using tables, relationships, forms, and views. This process also includes creating sample data.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577815","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/data-platform/data-platform-business-skills"},{"id":"rm-566324","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Adaptive Protection integration with Data Lifecycle Management","desc":"<p>Adaptive Protection in Microsoft Purview helps you protect your organization’s data by integrating dynamic insider risk levels, determined by data related activities, with various policy engines to automatically moving users in and out of policies as their risk levels change over time. The integration with Data Lifecycle Management will automatically apply retention labels to preserve deleted emails and files based on a user’s insider risk level.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566324","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-577817","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Copilot and AI innovation - Analyze demand using generative insights for better planning","desc":"<p>Generative insights for Demand planning in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management help you analyze sales history and forecast data across dimensions like product and location.</p> <p>With general availability, generative insights now include a new metric: <em>trends</em>. The system dynamically clusters data based on detected patterns, such as <em>high trending</em>, <em>medium trending</em>, <em>relative flat</em>, and <em>declining trend</em>.</p> <p>You can view aggregated values by selected dimensions or drill down into detailed values for each planning object.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Generative insights in Demand planning help you identify patterns like seasonality, trends, and signal correlations to improve forecast accuracy. By clustering data dynamically, you can make better decisions, optimize inventory, and reduce costs from overstocking or stockouts. These insights help you meet customer demand, improve service levels, and gain a competitive edge.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577817","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/demand-planning/generative-insights"},{"id":"rm-577542","title":"Microsoft Edge: Review your PDF notes and annotations in the Notes pane","desc":"<p>The built-in PDF viewer in Microsoft Edge will include a Notes pane that lists highlights, text notes, ink notes and comments in page order allowing users to quickly revisit them without finding them page by page. Users can search and filter their annotations, jump to each one in the document, and edit, delete or add comments from the pane. Available for Windows and macOS devices</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577542","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-181825","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Alert improvements","desc":"<p>This feature is about improving the alerting capabilities and customization in Communication Compliance.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-10-16","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=181825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-557559","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management- Azure PST Import","desc":"<p>Azure PST Import is a migration method that enables PST files stored in Azure Blob Storage to be imported directly into Exchange Online mailboxes. It follows the standard two‑step Exchange Migration Service pattern: an initial analysis phase to validate and assess PST data, followed by execution of the actual migration. The process also involves creating a migration endpoint, running an analysis-only migration batch, using the analysis results to configure the final batch, and then starting the batch to import PST content into target mailboxes.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557559","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576710","title":"Microsoft Purview: Introducing IRM Alert classification","desc":"<p>Insider risk management will be introducing the ability to classify alerts as True positive, Benign (operational), and False positive. This will be available on all alerts where authorized analysts with the appropriate permissions can choose from a list of predefined classification reasons. Alert classification will help tenants to better classify risk within alerts to support reporting and tuning needs. This will replace existing dismissal reasons.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576710","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577813","title":"Power Pages: Power Pages Copilot - Use Power Pages MCP server capabilities","desc":"<p>Power Pages MCP server enables makers to expose site data and operations through a secure, standardized interface compatible with AI clients.</p> <p>In the public preview release, makers can enable Create, Read, Update, Delete (CRUD) operations via the site’s Web API layer without writing custom code. Makers can provision the MCP server endpoint through site settings, allowing customers to securely interact with site data or perform operations using natural language queries through popular AI chat clients.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Power Pages MCP server empowers you to transform site data and operations into structured tools for AI assistants, enabling natural language interactions for updates and queries. This means faster workflows, less manual effort, and improved user experiences, helping your teams save time and stay productive.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577813","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"January CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/configure/mcp-overview"},{"id":"rm-577405","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Author Commerce receipt formats with Copilot Cowork","desc":"<p>Use natural language in Copilot Cowork to create, update, translate, and check Commerce receipt layouts using existing formats in headquarters.</p> <p>The Commerce receipt format designer skill lets authorized users work with receipt layouts through natural-language requests in Copilot Cowork, using receipt configuration in Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters. It applies to receipt formats used by Store Commerce point of sale (POS).</p> <p>Users can:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Create and adapt formats:</strong> Start from an existing format in the modern Receipt designer representation, create a new format, or request changes to an existing target.</li> <li><strong>Edit receipt sections:</strong> Modify header, line, and footer content, field positions, alignment, and supported formatting.</li> <li><strong>Translate and personalize content:</strong> Translate static labels and add user-supplied text while preserving dynamic fields. Missing business details are identified rather than invented.</li> <li><strong>Check layouts without changing them:</strong> Request structural or geometry checks that identify overlaps, width violations, and truncation risks, with findings and suggested remediation.</li> <li><strong>Verify saved changes:</strong> Review the resulting format and changes, with saved configuration re-read to confirm the requested update. Creating a format from a source preserves that source.</li> </ul> <p>The skill is available automatically to authorized Copilot Cowork users. Users describe the source format and desired outcome, resolve any source or target ambiguity, and review the results. A Commerce administrator ensures appropriate headquarters access and that the source format is available in the modern structured representation.</p> <p>Structural checks do not establish visual appearance, barcode scanability, runtime values, or legal and fiscal compliance. Users review the layout in the Receipt designer and perform appropriate test printing before operational use. Assigning formats to receipt profiles or printers and printing or reprinting transactions are separate setup and operational workflows.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577405","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576303","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Streamline pickup order workflows in Store Commerce","desc":"<p><strong>Business Value</strong><br> Trade counter pickups should be fast. When a business customer arrives to collect prepaid or pre-authorized orders, routing them through unnecessary screens and payment steps slows down the process. When customers want to add extra items during pickup, requiring a separate transaction introduces friction that can result in missed sales.</p> <p>This feature reshapes the pickup experience to better align with trade counter operations. Associates can collect multiple orders in a single action, add extra items within the same transaction, and capture the pickup person’s name and signature for audit purposes. For orders that aren't collected, the ability to unpick lines and release inventory helps prevent stock from being held unnecessarily. Together, these improvements save time per transaction, reduce payment friction, and provide B2B operations with the audit trail they require.</p> <p><strong>Feature Details</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Quick pickup operation</strong>: A new <strong>Quick pickup</strong> operation lets associates pick one or more orders or order lines for a single customer without navigating to the transaction screen. It is available when: <ul> <li>The customer is set up to pay on account.</li> <li>The order is fully paid or authorized.<br> ​</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Pickup dialog enhancements</strong>: The pickup dialog includes a <strong>Pickup all</strong> action to select all eligible lines in one step, along with barcode scanning to confirm quantities. Completing the pickup invoices the selected order lines and captures any open payment authorization.<br> ​</li> <li><strong>Adding carryout items during checkout pickup</strong>: During the checkout to pickup flow, associates can add additional carryout items to the transaction. A single payment covers both the new items and any remaining balance, so the customer isn't required to complete a separate transaction.<br> ​</li> <li><strong>Signature and name capture</strong>: For B2B scenarios where pickups often occur without a card payment, associates can capture the pickup person’s name and signature. This information is applied to all orders selected in the same pickup session and is stored for audit purposes.<br> ​</li> <li><strong>Unpicking order lines</strong>: When a customer doesn't collect goods, associates can unpick staged order lines. This action allows the order to be canceled and returns reserved inventory to available stock.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576303","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577789","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Boost customer confidence with branded content links","desc":"<p>With branded content links, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Set up your vanity link (or custom link) in the domain authenticator.</li> <li>Once authenticated, your vanity domain will be visible in: <ul> <li>All links in your emails.</li> <li>Hosted digital assets, forms, event registration pages, and your preference center.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>A retail brand launches a holiday campaign featuring special bundles and limited‑time offers. Instead of using long, generic tracking URLs, the team enables branded content links. Every email now displays clean, trustworthy links using the company’s own domain. Customers feel more confident clicking through, resulting in higher engagement and improved conversion rates across the campaign.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Links are the gateway to your landing pages, offers, and content. However, automatically generated URLs look unprofessional and suspicious, and they can lower your click rates and conversions. Now you can customize links to show your company name, increasing customers' trust and improving brand recognition and campaign performance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577789","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577810","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Update live segments without interrupting ongoing journeys","desc":"<p>For any segment, even those used in live journeys or other segments, marketers can edit and republish them to make changes. Changes won't take effect until the segments are published, giving marketers control over the timing of the changes. These changes are picked up at the next recurrence for recurring journeys and new additions are applied in real time for ongoing journeys.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Campaigns often require adjustments after launch, such as refining target audiences based on analytics or changing business needs. Now marketers can make quick updates to segments without having to remake or republish journeys, enabling more agile and responsive segment targeting.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577810","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-392839","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Automatic data preservation for high-risk users","desc":"<p>Adaptive Protection in Microsoft Purview helps you protect your organization’s data by integrating dynamic insider risk levels, determined by data related activities, with various policy engines to automatically moving users in and out of policies as their risk levels change over time. The integration with Data Lifecycle Management will automatically apply retention labels to preserve deleted emails and files based on a user’s insider risk level.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-06","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=392839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"June CY2024"},{"id":"rm-573701","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Graph API Support for Archive Mailboxes","desc":"<p>Access to Archive mailboxes (Main + Auxiliary) through Microsoft Graph. The goal is to give users a single, seamless Archive view, even though Archive data may physically reside across multiple auxiliary mailboxes with EWS Graph APIs being deprecated.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573701","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-574094","title":"Microsoft Teams: View files and conversations side by side","desc":"<p>Review shared files without losing conversation context. When you open a PDF, Markdown, or HTML file from a Teams chat or channel message, the conversation appears alongside the file and takes you directly to where it was shared, allowing you to catch up on the discussion and respond without closing the file preview or switching back to chat.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574094","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576271","title":"Microsoft Viva: Conversation Analytics","desc":"<p>Conversation analytics updates are coming to Microsoft Viva Engage, giving communicators richer signals to understand how audiences engage with posts and announcements.</p> <p>With this update, conversation analytics will include new engagement insights such as click-through rate, open rate, dwell time, and video performance signals. These enhancements help communicators better understand whether employees opened a conversation, spent time with the content, clicked through to linked resources, or engaged with video attachments. Click-through rate and open rate are expected to begin rolling out first with additional conversation analytics enhancements, including dwell time and video performance signals, expected to follow shortly after.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576271","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-577814","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data: Agents and Copilot - Increase AI accuracy by grounding agents in customer insights","desc":"<p>The Customer Insights MCP server allows AI agents and chat experiences to access and understand insights generated by Customer Insights - Data.<br> The Customer Insights MCP server uses the industry-standard MCP architecture to securely share unified profiles and insights with AI agents and chat experiences, providing the data context so AI agents can do their best work.</p> <p>AI tools can use the Customer Insights MCP server to:</p> <ul> <li>Resolve Dataverse contacts and leads to their unified customer profile.</li> <li>Access extended customer information unified by Customer Insights - Data from external sources not available to Dataverse.</li> <li>Understand calculated measures for a customer such as their purchase totals over the last 4 months, or the date of their most recent engagement.</li> <li>Quickly discover what segments the customer is a member of.</li> <li>See if a customer has multiple redundant contacts in your system, and which is considered authoritative for that customer.</li> <li>Get predictive insights for the customer such as Customer Lifetime Value (CLV) and Churn risk, giving you greater insights into the customer's current relationships with your company.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong><br> Sally is a seller who is evaluating a lead named Joe who recently attended a product launch webinar. Sally asks her AI embedded on their Contact and Lead forms if there are any insights about this lead and is delighted to find that the lead Joe is matched to a VIP customer Joseph who has existing paid licenses for several products. Because Customer Insights - Data unifies her company's external Purchase and Rewards data with Dataverse contact and lead data, the agent informs Sally that Joe is a valued Rewards and Loyalty points member, and it is able to provide other AI-generated insights such as the Customer Lifetime Value score, Churn Risk, and the segments Joe is a member of. Armed with a wealth of customer data, Sally is able to engage Joe and upsell Joe on their new product.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Agents give your marketing, sales, and service teams essential insights and can automate many business processes. But agents are only as good as the data they work with. When you give them access to customer insights that unify your customer data sources, you can get more valuable and actionable insights that enable organizational efficiencies that you couldn't achieve before.</p> <p>Now, more insights generated by Customer Insights - Data can be leveraged from within Microsoft Copilot Studio, allowing you to turn insights into a powerful business asset. Copilot Studio, and even your own custom copilots created in Microsoft Copilot Studio, can now simply and easily get access to more insights, allowing agents to understand, share, analyze, and act on these insights. Every team member gets tailored information and tools to reach their goals efficiently.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577814","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/data/mcp-server-tools"},{"id":"rm-577816","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data: Faster time to insights - Access unified profiles and insights in Fabric OneLake","desc":"<p>Unified profiles and insights are only useful when you can act on the data. If you use Microsoft Fabric, Customer Insights - Data makes it easier to share valuable unified profiles and insights directly in OneLake. You can add those insights to your core analytics and downstream processes.</p> <p><strong>Scenario:</strong></p> <p>Contoso has multiple departments with distinct systems and data requirements. After creating shortcuts in Fabric OneLake to all their Customer Insights - Data profiles and insights, the entire Contoso organization can leverage the unique advantage of customer 360-degree profiles across all the workloads of the organization.</p> <p>The enhanced visibility and collaboration from sharing unified customer profiles and insights in Fabric OneLake creates a cycle where several departments take steps to integrate their unique customer data into unified profiles. This process improves the fidelity and value of the profiles.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Customer Insights - Data makes it easy to access and use unified profiles and insights created in Customer Insights - Data directly in Microsoft Fabric OneLake. This capability powers your downstream workloads while saving time and reducing costs.</p> <p>Customer Insights - Data in Microsoft Fabric OneLake removes barriers to using your customer insights. It eliminates challenges that come from storing data in multiple fragmented data lakes. By using shortcuts to Customer Insights - Data managed data lake, you can access unified profiles and insights in OneLake. You can use all the insights Customer Insights - Data generates without copying any data. Microsoft Fabric OneLake and Customer Insights - Data improve collaboration and remove business barriers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577816","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577811","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Enable advanced personalization using simple formulas to modify text, dates, and numbers","desc":"<ul> <li>Apply a variety of PowerFx functions to text, numbers, and dates in messages.</li> <li>Text functions include concatenation, change case, trim, substitute, and replace.</li> <li>Number functions include arithmetic calculations, rounding, and formatting.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enhance personalization by transforming data directly within your messages using PowerFx expressions. Standardize customer names (for example, convert to proper case), format dates and numbers for different regions, and perform simple calculations such as days until expiration or suggested donation amounts based on prior activity. These capabilities help you deliver more accurate, relevant, and engaging communications, all without requiring changes to your data model.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577811","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"August CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/power-fx-dynamic-text"},{"id":"rm-577398","title":"Microsoft 365 Apps: Cloud Update - Export Improvements","desc":"<p>New export improvements are coming to Cloud Update, making it easier for organizations to access and analyze device data. These enhancements will expand export capabilities across Inventory and Cloud Update device views, include additional device and update information, and allow admins to export filtered results so they can focus on the devices most relevant to their needs.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577398","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577172","title":"Microsoft 365: [Education] Assign Study and Learn in Teams and LMS Assignments","desc":"<p>Educators can assign Study and Learn from Student AI Guidelines in Teams and LMS Assignments. Students open guided learning support grounded in the assignment's title, instructions, and supported files and resources, helping them work through concepts and practice their understanding.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577172","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577173","title":"Microsoft 365: [Education] Provide a Copilot starter prompt in Teams and LMS Assignments","desc":"<p>Educators can provide a Copilot starter prompt from Student AI Guidelines in Teams and LMS Assignments. Students open Copilot with the educator's prompt ready in their chat, helping them begin with instructions tailored to the assignment.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577173","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573294","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Enable semantic model in Sales agent","desc":"<p>Semantic model helps Sales Agent understand the structure and meaning of an organization’s CRM data. It creates a connected representation of CRM metadata, including tables or objects, fields, descriptions, data types, relationships, views, pick-list values, and glossary terms. Sales Agent can retrieve this context when responding to questions, improving its ability to interpret business language and answer complex questions that span related CRM records.</p> <p>Dynamics 365 admins can enable and turn on semantic model in Power Apps Maker Portal and configure the data coverage and signals that Sales Agent should use. Admins can configure the underlying data, views, metadata and relationships used in the model.</p> <p>For Salesforce customers, the semantic model will be based on existing Sales agent table and glossary configuration in Sales agent settings or Power Apps Maker Portal. In Power Apps Maker Portal, Salesforce admins will can configure additional Salesforce signals to use in semantic model such as relationships and views.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573294","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/data-platform/semantic-model-overview"},{"id":"rm-575289","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Sales Development Agent - Meeting scheduling","desc":"<p>Sales Development Agent can turn a prospect’s interest in meeting into a booked seller meeting. The agent asks the prospect to provide preferred dates and times, evaluates those options against the appropriate seller’s calendar, and books the first valid option in the prospect’s stated preference order. The seller and prospect receive the meeting invitation, while the seller receives additional conversation context to support a warm handoff. If scheduling cannot be completed, the agent transfers the request and relevant context to the seller for follow-up.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575289","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577546","title":"Outlook: Mark as read improvements","desc":"<p>Mark as read will be updated to better match user expectations. When using the Unread filter, items will also be marked as read in coherence with the existing \"Mark as read when using the reading pane\" setting. Additionally, opening an item in a popout will now mark it as read regardless of that setting.</p> <p>#newoutlookforwindows</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577546","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577809","title":"Power Pages: Design studio - Configure authentication with security agent","desc":"<p>The security agent is available directly within the security workspace in Power Pages design studio. Makers can open the security agent tab to access the embedded chat panel and security tools. From there, they can interact using natural language to review risks, understand configurations, and take guided actions.</p> <p>The agent assists with both authentication and authorization setup. It guides makers through configuring identity providers, reviewing authentication settings, and strengthening login protections. Based on the site’s setup, it can recommend improvements such as securing token configurations, validating redirect settings, or tightening session-related controls.</p> <p>For authorization, the security agent helps configure web roles and data access permissions. Using the site’s data schema and usage patterns, it suggests appropriate access levels, such as read-only, owner-only, or full administrative control aligned with least privilege best practices.</p> <p>All suggested changes require explicit user approval before being applied. After execution, the agent confirms what was updated, ensuring full transparency and control. By combining guided setup, continuous review, and contextual recommendations, the security agent helps keep Power Pages sites secure from initial configuration through ongoing maintenance.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Security agent empowers makers to set up secure access controls without needing deep security expertise. It uses AI to recommend the right roles and permissions for your data tables. It continuously monitors your site for misconfigurations, helping you reduce risk, ensure compliance, and build customer trust.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577809","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/security/security-agent"},{"id":"rm-573151","title":"PowerPoint: Present with confidence on a single screen in Slide Show","desc":"<p>When you present in Slide Show on just one display, like a laptop with no second monitor and no Presenter View, the on-screen presenting controls can be easy to miss. PowerPoint is making single-screen presenting easier: the controls you need to move through your slides and stay in command are more discoverable and useful, helping you present smoothly and confidently without a second screen.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573151","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577179","title":"PowerPoint: Present with ease using a modernized Presenter View","desc":"<p>When you present with Presenter View, the controls you need should be easy to find at a glance. Presenter View in PowerPoint for Mac has a refreshed design: presenter tools, slide navigation, and the timer now sit together in one control bar, with updated icons and slide thumbnails. You can also collapse the thumbnail pane and the Next Slide and Notes pane to focus on what matters most as you present.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577179","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-577178","title":"PowerPoint: Present with ease using a modernized Presenter View","desc":"<p>When you present with Presenter View, finding the right tool or slide shouldn't break your flow. Presenter View in PowerPoint for Windows has a refreshed design: presenter tools, slide navigation, and the timer now sit together in one control bar, and a new slide thumbnail strip lets you see what's coming and jump to any slide. You can also collapse or resize panes to focus on what matters most as you present.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577178","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1281505","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management- Azure PST Import","desc":"Updated October 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nAzure PST Import provides a structured, PowerShell-based way for administrators to import PST files stored in Azure Blob Storage into Exchange Online mailboxes, which are commonly used to store archived Outlook mailbox content. This capability helps organizations migrate historical email data in a controlled and auditable way by validating readiness before importing and by providing reports throughout the process. The process starts by creating an Azure PST Import endpoint to establish the connection between Azure storage and Exchange Online. Administrators then run a migration batch in Analyze mode to review readiness and validate the input before proceeding. Once the analysis results are reviewed, they use those results to create and start the import batch, which begins importing the PST files into the specified mailboxes.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557559.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out mid-October 2026 (previously mid-September) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late September).\n• Worldwide: We will begin rolling out late January 2027 (previously early December 2026) and expect to complete by late February 2027 (previously late December 2026).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Microsoft 365 administrators managing Exchange Online\n• Administrators using Microsoft Purview Data Lifecycle Management\n• Organizations that import PST files into user or archive mailboxes\n\nWhat will happen\n• Administrators complete the Azure PST Import process using PowerShell cmdlets only.\n• The workflow includes:• Creating an Azure PST Import migration endpoint\n• Running a migration batch in Analyze mode to validate readiness\n• Reviewing analysis results and reports\n• Creating and starting the import batch\n• Performing post-import cleanup\n\n• This experience is not available through a graphical user interface (GUI).\n• Existing mailbox prerequisites and quotas are validated before importing begins.\n• There is no direct user impact; the feature is admin-driven.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• Ensure your Azure storage account and container exist and are reachable; the endpoint creation cmdlet validates both during setup.\n• Grant the Storage Blob Data Reader role to the Office 365 Import Service app on the target storage account. Without this permission, creating the Azure PST Import endpoint will fail.\n• Prepare your batch input files (XML and/or CSV) and run the migration batch in Analyze mode first so the service can validate readiness before importing.\n• Confirm analysis prerequisites for target mailboxes:• Appropriate license assigned\n• Mailbox is not inactive or soft-deleted\n• Recipient type is UserMailbox\n• Archive is enabled if importing to archive\n• Quota validations (ArchiveQuota / RecoverableItemsQuota) occur during analysis\n\n• Validate PST files ahead of time:• Analysis verifies that all specified PST files exist\n• PST file size is validated during analysis\n\nFor detailed cmdlet usage and guidance, review the Azure PST Import documentation on Microsoft Learn.\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. The feature enables administrators to import existing customer email data contained in PST files into Exchange Online mailboxes, where the data is then stored and processed according to existing Exchange Online behaviors.\nDoes the change store customer data, and if so, where is it stored?Yes. PST file contents are imported into Exchange Online mailboxes within the customer’s Microsoft 365 tenant and are stored according to the tenant’s data residency and storage configuration.\nDoes the change modify retention policies, holds, or deletion workflows?Yes. Once imported, mailbox data becomes subject to any existing Microsoft Purview retention policies, retention labels, holds, and deletion workflows already configured for the target mailboxes.\nDoes the change affect audit logging capabilities?Yes. Administrative actions related to PST import and the resulting mailbox changes are logged using existing Exchange Online and Microsoft Purview audit logging mechanisms.\nDoes the change alter how admins can monitor or demonstrate compliance?Yes. Administrators can use existing Exchange Online and Microsoft Purview reporting and audit tools to monitor PST import activity and demonstrate compliance after the data is imported.\nDoes the change include an admin control?Yes. The feature is controlled through administrator access to PowerShell cmdlets and Azure role assignments, including permissions on the Azure storage account used for PST import.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-15","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1281505","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1309743","title":"(Updated) Viva Engage: Email updates for users without a routable mailbox","desc":"Updated September 30, 2026: We have updated the content timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nViva Engage will stop sending email notifications to users who do not have a valid mailbox or routable email destination. Previously, email notifications could still be attempted for these users, resulting in repeated delivery retries, increased load on email systems, and, in some cases, delays to important business communications.\nThis change reduces unnecessary email traffic, improves delivery efficiency, and helps ensure important communications are delivered reliably and on time.\nUsers with supported mailbox configurations, including cloud mailboxes, on-premises mailboxes, shared mailboxes, and other routable email destinations, will continue to receive Viva Engage email notifications as expected.\nNotifications delivered through supported channels such as Microsoft Teams remain unaffected.\n[When this will happen:]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins mid-October 2026 (previously end of September) and is expected to complete by end of December 2026 (previously end of October).\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n• Users who do not have a valid mailbox or routable email destination.\n• Microsoft 365 admins managing Viva Engage users and mailbox configurations.\n\nWhat will happen:\n• Viva Engage will no longer attempt to send email notifications to users who do not have a valid mailbox or routable email destination.\n• Users with cloud, on-premises, shared, or other supported mailbox configurations will continue to receive email notifications as expected.\n• This change does not affect the existing email notification experience for users with a valid mailbox or routable email destination.\n• Notifications delivered through Microsoft Teams or other supported channels are not impacted.\n• The change is enabled by default and applies automatically.\n• Organizations may see:• Reduced load on email systems and gateways.\n• Fewer retry attempts for undeliverable messages.\n• Improved email delivery efficiency and reliability.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• No action is required.\n• Review your Exchange Online licensing configuration to identify users without mailbox access.\n• Evaluate your notification strategy (e.g., Teams vs. Email) for frontline workers.\n• Inform helpdesk and user support teams of the expected behavior change.\n• Update internal documentation if email notifications are referenced for frontline users.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n• Alters how existing customer data is processed: Email notifications to users without mailboxes are no longer attempted, reducing unnecessary processing of undeliverable messages.\n• No other compliance impacts identified.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1309743","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-577788","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Orchestrate conversation distribution with natural language playbooks","desc":"<p>Conversation orchestration in Dynamics 365 Contact Center keeps every conversation actively managed throughout its lifecycle, from initiation through resolution. Instead of applying fixed rules at different stages of a conversation journey, conversation orchestration monitors each conversation as conditions evolve, like wait time increases, fast-filling queues, or service representatives going offline, and responds automatically with the right action. For example, administrators can define the intent using natural-language playbooks as follows: \"If a premium customer waits for more than three minutes and no senior agents are available, increase their priority and offer a callback.\" Conversation orchestration then handles how it's run in real time.</p> <p>You can configure playbooks per scenario through guided templates that keep instructions focused and reliable. Built-in validation catches conflicts before anything goes live, so that you confidently publish changes without needing to test every edge case manually.</p> <p>The key capabilities are as follows:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Dynamic priority escalation</strong>: In traditional systems, conversation priority is typically set once, at entry, and never revisited. This means a customer who has been waiting for 10 minutes competes for the same expert as another customer who has just arrived, and a conversation that’s transferred mid-journey resets to whatever the new queue's default priority is. Dynamic priority escalation fixes this by continuously re-evaluating priority as the conversation progresses. You define the conditions such as wait time thresholds, queue transfers, customer tier, or other context and conversation orchestration adjusts priority automatically throughout the conversation lifecycle. High-value or long-waiting customers move forward without anyone watching the queue manually.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Overflow handling across multiple conditions</strong>: Conversation orchestration supports a broader set of business triggered overflow conditions, allowing organizations to respond intelligently as queue conditions change. Administrators can define actions when a queue is outside operating hours, when all representatives in a queue are signed out or unavailable, when queue wait time exceeds a defined threshold, or when the number of waiting conversations surpasses a specified limit. Depending on the situation, orchestration can automatically offer callbacks, route conversations to alternate queues, expand assignment eligibility, notify supervisors, or deliver contextual customer messages. This ensures customers are never left waiting without a defined path forward. Admins can also configure overflow handling for direct inward dial calls now, when reps are not available or don't accept the calls.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Assign to a previously engaged or preferred representative</strong>: Customers often need to repeat information when they are connected to a new representative for every interaction. Conversation orchestration helps maintain continuity by reconnecting customers with previously engaged or preferred representatives whenever possible. Assignment decisions take into account historical interactions, queue membership alignment, representative availability, and workload capacity. For asynchronous conversations, organizations can choose to honor representative presence status and active conversation limits before reconnecting customers, ensuring returning conversations are assigned only when the preferred representative has capacity to engage. When the preferred or previously engaged representative is unavailable, conversations seamlessly fall back to the next best qualified representative. This reduces customer effort, improves resolution efficiency, and delivers a more personalized support experience.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Bullseye routing</strong>: Finding the right representative often requires balancing expertise with response times. Bullseye routing enables organizations to gradually expand the pool of eligible representatives when a conversation isn't assigned within a defined timeframe. Administrators can define progressive routing rings that begin with the most qualified representatives and then expand to broader groups based on skills, proficiency levels, teams, or other business criteria. This approach maximizes the likelihood of connecting customers with the best-qualified representative while ensuring conversations don't wait indefinitely for a specific resource.</p> </li> </ul> <p>These capabilities are the first in a broad and growing set of orchestration scenarios that conversation orchestration will support across the full conversation lifecycle, spanning overflow management, priority handling, assignment strategies, in-conversation messaging, and escalation. Each new capability builds on the same natural-language playbook foundation, so organizations can adopt new scenarios without rebuilding what they have already configured.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Traditional automatic conversation distribution systems rely on complex rules and static configuration that are difficult to maintain and can't adapt as conditions change throughout the conversation lifecycle. Unified routing with its new AI-powered conversation orchestration uses the power of agentic AI to continuously monitor events throughout the entire conversation lifecycle and responds with the right action when required.</p> <p>This is a shift from a static system to an orchestration layer that remains active and intelligent from the moment a conversation arrives in a queue until it's resolved. The new feature reduces administrative complexity and helps deliver more flexible customer experiences at scale, even under fluctuating demand.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577788","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/administer/configure-conversation-orchestration"},{"id":"rm-577423","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Notify users when approval sets finish processing","desc":"<p>When an approval set finishes processing, the person who started it receives an in-app notification built on the existing long-running-process (No More Wait) framework, and they see only notifications for the operations they triggered. On success, a brief pop-up reports that the approval set completed, shows the approval set name, and provides a deep link to the record, and the notification stays in the notifications pane until you clear it. When one or more approvals in the set fail, the notification reports that the set completed with failures, shows the failure reason, and links directly to the failing record; multiple failures appear as separate notifications. The feature covers completion notifications only: it does not add processing-started notifications, sends in-app notifications only (no email or Teams), and does not include a retry or remediation workflow.</p> <p>How to enable: This will be added to the existing list titled Select jobs for notification. Add approvals to that (or leave it entirely blank) to enable these notifications.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-568935","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Auto-labeling per-policy coverage report","desc":"<p>For each enforced auto-labeling policy, admins can view how files processed during enforcement correlate to the latest simulation run. The per-policy coverage report shows volumes of files that have been labeled or are not yet labeled, and whether those files were included in the last simulation snapshot. This helps admins understand enforcement progress for a specific policy against the data state captured during simulation, while also identifying files that were not found in the simulation snapshot but were processed during enforcement.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568935","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568078","title":"Microsoft Teams: Badges in Profile Card in Teams","desc":"<p>You can now see Awards and Certifications as badges on a user’s profile card, bringing a more consistent experience across Teams and Outlook.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-05","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568078","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-392328","title":"Microsoft Teams: Chat for organizers and presenters in structured meetings and webinars","desc":"<p>Organizers, co-organizers, and presenters can chat privately in a separate chat from attendees. This chat is available to access before, during, and after the event.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-04-08","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=392328","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570646","title":"Microsoft Teams: Organize important resources in chats and channels","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams is introducing a new way to organize and access important resources in chats and channels. Users will be able to pin key content, including links, files, and messages, directly beneath the chat or channel header for quick access. Resources can also be organized into folders, making it easier to keep important information visible and discoverable in active conversations. This update provides a more consistent experience across chats and channels, helping users stay organized, quickly find key resources, and remain aligned on important information. Existing pinned messages will continue to be available within the new experience, alongside other shared resources, on Teams desktop and web.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570646","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-567461","title":"Microsoft Teams: Updated header and dashboard for chats and channels on mobile","desc":"<p>You can now get oriented and take action faster when using Teams on mobile, with a redesigned header and lightweight dashboard that brings key channel details, people, and pinned content into one intuitive place. It creates a more predictable, familiar experience across desktop and mobile so you can move faster with less friction.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-03","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567461","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-577806","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Turbocharge your pipeline to drive growth - Transform customer journeys into action with record creation","desc":"<p>This feature gives you a single, flexible way to create downstream records and activities directly inside the journey builder.</p> <ul> <li>Create records or activities from a single tile, including tasks, phone calls, leads, opportunities, or custom entity records.</li> <li>Use required and optional fields, including custom attributes, to match your exact process requirements.</li> <li>Add dynamic content to any field, using real‑time attributes from contacts or leads.</li> <li>Eliminate the need for complex workflows or custom code, making automation more accessible and easier to maintain.</li> </ul> <p>This feature currently works when orchestrating journeys on contacts and leads. It doesn't support Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data profiles.</p> <p>Users can only create records that have a relationship to lead or contact and that they have access to. Records related to event planning aren't supported.</p> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>A contact clicks a \"Request Support\" link in an email. The journey automatically creates a case in Dynamics 365 Customer Service, prepopulated with the contact's details, so the service team can act immediately without waiting for a manual escalation.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Businesses need to automate processes across marketing, sales, and service, but they’re stuck with fragmented tools and manual steps. This slows execution, introduces errors, and makes it hard to scale personalized experiences.</p> <p>You can now create any record or activity directly from a journey with full control over fields and dynamic values. Instead of rigid workflows or manual data entry, you can automate actions for any scenario, including handing off high-value leads and opportunities or creating tasks for prompt follow-up, without leaving the journey builder. This means faster processes, fewer errors, and more flexibility to adapt customer journeys to your unique business needs without custom development.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577806","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/real-time-marketing-optimize-lead-management"},{"id":"rm-577792","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Automatic clearing of centralized bridged vendor payments during bank reconciliation","desc":"<p>This enhancement enables automatic clearing of bridge transactions generated by centralized vendor payments when bank statements are matched with records in Dynamics 365 Finance during the bank reconciliation process. The system posts the required clearing journals in the centralized legal entity, ensuring that general ledger balances are updated accurately.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Automatic clearing of centralized vendor payments streamlines the bank reconciliation process by eliminating manual clearing of bridge transactions, reducing reconciliation errors and ensuring general ledger balances are accurate and up to date. This improves operational efficiency, strengthens auditability in cross‑entity payment scenarios, and increases confidence in using automated bank reconciliation at scale.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577792","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/cash-bank-management/advanced-bank-reconciliation-overview"},{"id":"rm-577822","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Detect corruption in source document budget control tracking","desc":"<p>Budget control tracking data can become difficult to analyze when the underlying budget source is missing or when relieving relationships between commitments and relieving documents are broken. These conditions can make it harder for finance users to understand why budget control data does not reconcile as expected and where repair should begin. With this feature, Dynamics 365 Finance adds diagnostic capability to Budget control data maintenance. The diagnostic is designed to detect corrupted budget tracking data patterns before users run repair actions and highlight budget-controlled documents that are affected by orphaned budget tracking records, where the underlying budget source is missing. It also identifies broken relieving relationships between commitments and relieving documents, helping users understand where budget tracking data requires attention.<br> This capability complements source document reprocessing. Finance users can first run the diagnostic to detect corruption and understand the affected documents, then use the existing budget control data maintenance tool to repair the data.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature helps finance teams identify budget control tracking corruption before running repair activities. By highlighting budget-controlled documents affected by orphaned tracking records or broken relieving relationships, the diagnostic gives users a clearer starting point for analysis and remediation. Teams can validate the scope of impacted documents, reduce manual investigation, and use existing budget control data maintenance tools more confidently to repair the detected issues.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577822","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/budgeting/budget-control-tool"},{"id":"rm-577818","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Globalization Studio - Enhance Electronic Reporting with new capabilities","desc":"<p>Electronic Reporting (ER) is the configurable engine you use to author and run business documents—invoices, statutory reports, VAT declarations and payment files, and more. In 10.0.48 and 10.0.49 Microsoft delivered a set of general enhancements that respond directly to the most highly voted ideas on the Microsoft Idea portal and to recurring partner/customer requests. The enhancements remove long-standing workarounds, expand what ER formats can express out of the box, and modernize commonly used destinations.</p> <p>You can now:</p> <ul> <li>Send generated documents to silent (BCC) recipients straight from ER.</li> <li>Produce industry-standard GS1 barcodes directly in your ER labels.</li> <li>Write cleaner ER formulas using new integer-arithmetic functions.</li> <li>Print the exact number of copies you configured for ER-based documents.</li> <li>Run validation for multiple ER configurations at scale, with background execution and full traceability of validation results across configuration versions.</li> <li>Run ER with improved memory efficiency, enabling more reliable processing of large-volume reports and complex datasets.</li> </ul> <h3>New capabilities</h3> <p><strong>Send blind copies (BCC) from ER Email destinations</strong></p> <p>With this release wave, the ER <strong>Email</strong> destination is extended with support for blind carbon copy (BCC) recipients. In previous versions, only <strong>To</strong> and <strong>Cc</strong> recipients could be configured, which limited the ability to distribute generated documents to compliance, audit, or archival mailboxes without disclosing those addresses to the primary recipients.</p> <p>ER's <strong>Email</strong> destination now includes a <strong>Bcc</strong> field next to <strong>To</strong> and <strong>Cc</strong>.</p> <ul> <li>To enable, select <strong>Electronic reporting</strong> &gt; <strong>Electronic reporting destination</strong> &gt; <strong>File destination</strong> &gt; <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Email</strong>.</li> <li>The <strong>Bcc</strong> field accepts the same kinds of values as <strong>To</strong> and <strong>Cc</strong>: static addresses, ER expressions, or values bound to the data model.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: Confidential distribution of ER-generated documents to compliance, audit, and archival mailboxes is achieved entirely through configuration, eliminating the need for customization or post-processing.</p> <hr> <p><strong>Generate GS1 barcodes directly from ER</strong></p> <p>GS1 is the global standard for barcodes used in retail, warehousing, supply chain, transportation, and healthcare.</p> <p>ER now generates GS1 barcodes natively, with three new formats available in the barcode data source:</p> <ul> <li><strong>GS1-128</strong></li> <li><strong>GS1 DataMatrix</strong></li> <li><strong>GS1 QR Code</strong></li> </ul> <p>When you choose one of these formats, ER applies the correct GS1 encoding rules automatically. ER also warns you at design time when the configured barcode width is too small to scan reliably, so you catch problems before they reach the shop floor.</p> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: You can design GS1-compliant labels (warehouse, shipping, retail, healthcare) entirely inside ER, with no third-party barcode tools.</p> <hr> <p><strong>New ER formula functions: DIV and MOD</strong></p> <p>Integer division and remainder are common in reporting—for pagination, packaging quantities, currency splits, period bucketing, and check-digit calculations. Previously, ER report authors had to express these with combinations of <code>ROUND</code>, subtraction, and multiplication, which is verbose and easy to get wrong.</p> <p>Two new functions are now part of the ER formula language:</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>DIV(a, b)</code></strong> — integer division. Returns the integer (or Int64) quotient.</li> <li><strong><code>MOD(a, b)</code></strong> — the remainder of integer division. Returns the integer (or Int64) remainder.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: Cleaner, faster, and more readable ER formulas wherever whole-number arithmetic is needed.</p> <hr> <p><strong>ER destinations now apply the configured number of copies in Print management</strong></p> <p>When an ER-based document—for example, <em>Container content</em>—was configured in <strong>Print management</strong> with a number of copies greater than one, the printer still produced only a single copy. Warehouse, manufacturing, and logistics teams had to duplicate documents manually, slowing down pick, pack, and ship operations.</p> <p>ER destinations now correctly print the <strong>Number of copies</strong> configured in Print management, as well as the number requested in ad-hoc print dialogs. This applies across the standard entry points for ER documents driven by Print management.</p> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: The number of copies you configure is the number of copies you get—faster throughput, and fewer process errors.</p> <hr> <p><strong>Optimize memory consumption for large Electronic Reporting (ER) executions</strong></p> <p>This feature enhances memory efficiency during Electronic Reporting execution by introducing targeted optimizations in the reporting engine. These improvements reduce peak memory consumption by minimizing unnecessary object creation, avoiding redundant data duplication in memory, and reusing existing data structures more effectively.</p> <p>The optimization is broadly applicable across Electronic Reporting scenarios and is particularly beneficial for reports that process large volumes of data. Because the improvements are built into the engine, you benefit from them automatically, no configuration changes or report redesign are required.</p> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: Large ER reports run more reliably with reduced peak memory usage, lowering the risk of out-of-memory failures and helping high-volume reporting workloads complete consistently.</p> <hr> <p><strong>Enhanced validation management for Electronic Reporting configurations</strong></p> <p>This feature enables validation of multiple Electronic Reporting (ER) configuration versions in a single operation. When the feature is enabled, the <strong>Configuration repository</strong> page introduces a <strong>Validation</strong> experience that lets you:</p> <ul> <li>Select and validate multiple completed ER configurations at once, instead of validating one version at a time.</li> <li>Run validation as a batch job, so large validation workloads no longer block interactive sessions.</li> <li>Review validation results through a persistent <strong>Validation history</strong>, where results are retained for later review by configuration and version.</li> </ul> <p>This feature also introduces version-level validation tracking. Both users and system processes can identify which configuration versions have already been validated in the current environment, which helps you avoid redundant validation runs and focus on versions that still need attention.</p> <p><strong>Business outcome</strong>: Configuration quality can be governed at scale—teams validate many configuration versions in a single batch operation and rely on a persistent history and version-level tracking to confirm what has already been validated, reducing manual effort and rework.</p> <hr> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Capability</th> <th>Available from</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>BCC recipients on the ER Email destination</td> <td>10.0.48 (Platform update 72)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>GS1 barcode formats in ER</td> <td>10.0.49 (Platform update 73)</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>DIV</code> and <code>MOD</code> functions in ER formulas</td> <td>10.0.49 (Platform update 73)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Number of copies applied for ER destinations in Print management</td> <td>10.0.49 (Platform update 73)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Optimize memory consumption for large ER executions</td> <td>10.0.49 (Platform update 73)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Enhanced validation management for ER configurations</td> <td>10.0.49 (Platform update 73)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You’ll see ongoing improvements to Electronic Reporting in the current and upcoming releases. These updates make it easier for you to adapt to changing regulations by boosting flexibility, simplifying maintenance, and enabling greater reuse across configurations. This means less time spent on manual adjustments and more confidence in staying compliant as requirements evolve.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577818","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-577823","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Manufacturing and asset management - Enforce same-batch selection for raw materials in production and batch orders","desc":"<p>This feature ensures that raw materials consumed by production orders and batch orders all come from the same batch. Process and discrete manufacturers can use it together with related production-control capabilities that govern how raw materials are allocated to a production order.</p> <p>Product designers and production engineers can set the same-batch requirement at the released-product level so that it applies by default everywhere the item is consumed. They can optionally fine-tune it for individual bill of materials (BOM) or formula lines where a different rule is appropriate. Production planners and warehouse workers who reserve raw materials for a production or batch order see the system automatically restrict the available on-hand inventory to a single batch per line, instead of mixing quantities from several batches. The result is the consistent, traceable, single-batch consumption pattern that's needed for quality-controlled manufacturing scenarios—without requiring operators to remember and enforce the rule manually.</p> <h3>Key capabilities available in Supply Chain Management version 10.0.49</h3> <p>Version 10.0.49 of Supply Chain Management introduces the following capabilities to support same-batch selection for raw materials in production and batch orders:</p> <ul> <li>Configure same-batch selection at the product level as a default requirement to ensure consistent raw material consumption.</li> <li>Allow overrides on formula and BOM lines to support flexibility where batch consistency requirements differ.</li> <li>Enforce same-batch reservation by ensuring raw material reservation respects the same-batch requirement defined on formula and BOM lines.</li> <li>Support traceability and control by preventing mixed-batch consumption during raw material reservation.</li> </ul> <h3>Enhancements planned for future versions of Supply Chain Management</h3> <p>Future versions of Supply Chain Management are expected to introduce additional capabilities to further enhance same-batch selection for raw materials in production and batch orders, including:</p> <ul> <li>Same-batch enforcement during master planning allocation.</li> <li>Execution validation to ensure that same-batch requirements are validated during picking and consumption for production.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Same-batch selection helps ensure consistent product quality and traceability by preventing mixed-batch consumption, reducing compliance risk, and simplifying production control.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577823","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577825","title":"Power Pages: Administration and governance - Enable self-service site ownership transfer","desc":"<p>Power Pages now supports secure site ownership transfer for eligible sites. Existing site owners and global administrators can assign ownership to another valid user within the tenant without requiring manual intervention from support.</p> <p>The new owner must be a valid user with appropriate access to the environment. Every ownership transfer is recorded in an auditable history, including the previous owner, new owner, initiating user, and timestamp. Notifications are sent to the previous owner, the new owner, and administrators to ensure transparency and continuity and the changes get logged into Compliance Center.</p> <p>To help organizations maintain governance standards, Power Pages also identifies sites that no longer have a valid owner and surfaces this information on Power Advisor. Administrators can review these sites and take corrective action to ensure every production site has a designated accountable owner.</p> <p>This feature improves lifecycle management, reduces administrative overhead, and helps organizations maintain secure and compliant ownership practices across their Power Pages deployments.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Your organization needs a reliable way to transfer ownership of Power Pages sites when responsibilities change due to team reassignments, role changes, or employee departures. This feature helps maintain accountability, prevents orphaned sites, improves governance compliance, and ensures administrators always have visibility into who is responsible for managing a site. Built-in auditing and notifications provide traceability and help your organization meet operational and compliance requirements.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577821","title":"Power Pages: Professional developer experiences - Control Power Pages components using client APIs","desc":"<p>Developers often depend on custom JavaScript and fragile Document Object Model (DOM) manipulation to hide fields, update values, or trigger actions, an approach that easily breaks when page structures change, drives up maintenance costs, limits scalability, and leads to inconsistent experiences. Power Pages Client APIs address these challenges by offering stable, documented, and supported methods to interact with components, reducing risk, improving maintainability, and accelerating development.</p> <p>The Power Pages Client APIs (Preview) provide a JavaScript interface for controlling UI components and performing operations on your Power Pages site.</p> <p>Key features include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Form API</strong>: Retrieve forms by ID, manage their visibility, and interact with controls.</li> <li><strong>List API</strong>: Access lists, toggle their visibility, and retrieve HTML elements.</li> <li><strong>User API</strong>: Handle authentication actions like sign-in and sign-out.</li> <li><strong>Web API</strong>: Use OData-compliant methods to create, retrieve, and query records.</li> </ul> <p>These APIs allow you to dynamically update UI elements, manage data, and create tailored user experiences without reloading the page.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature empowers you to create richer, interactive Power Pages experiences without complex server-side logic. By using client-side APIs for forms, lists, and authentication, you’ll customize faster, control UI dynamically, and handle real-time data with ease. This means delivering tailored experiences, improving usability, and accelerating development, all while keeping your sites secure and consistent.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577821","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"November CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/configure/client-api"},{"id":"rm-577801","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Administrator experiences - Use enhanced customer-first direct callbacks","desc":"<ul> <li>Customer-first direct callback introduces a configurable, AI-powered experience managed through \"callback profiles\" in the Copilot Service admin center.</li> <li>Administrators define a callback profile—including greeting message, alternate number capture, callback offering window, retry logic, and AI agent selection—and associate it with queues under overflow handling.</li> <li>For each queue where direct callback is chosen as an overflow action, the administrator also must select a callback profile to ensure a customized callback experience for the queue.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Customer-first direct callback gives you a smarter way to manage customer calls. Instead of making customers wait on hold, the system initiates a callback the moment they reach the front of the line, so that they never lose their place. A prebuilt AI agent captures callback details. You can use your own AI agent to run custom workflows like customer verification. Your representatives join the call only when the customer is ready, saving time, reducing missed calls, and boosting productivity.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577801","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-577802","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Workforce engagement management - Automate shift rotations for consistent workforce coverage","desc":"<p><strong>What the feature does</strong></p> <p>Shift rotation policies help organizations distribute customer service representatives across recurring shifts on a configurable schedule. Supervisors can create rotation policies that define how representatives move between time slots over time and apply those policies to shift plans.</p> <p>Supervisors create policies by specifying a start date, time zone, rotation cadence, and a set of recurring time slots. Representatives are assigned to each time slot, and the scheduler automatically applies the rotation pattern when generating future schedules. This reduces the need for manual shift reassignment while supporting consistent workforce coverage across operating hours.</p> <p>Changes to a policy affect only future scheduling runs. Existing bookings remain unchanged. When additional staffing is needed, the scheduler can use available flexible workers or other eligible representatives who can cover the required time period.</p> <p><strong>How the feature is enabled</strong></p> <p>Administrators enable Workforce Management and shift scheduling capabilities in Customer Service. Supervisors then create and manage shift rotation policies, assign representatives to rotation groups, and associate policies with shift plans.</p> <p>After a policy is assigned to a shift plan, future automatic scheduling runs apply the configured rotation pattern. Supervisors can pause a policy or remove it from a shift plan at any time to stop rotation-based scheduling.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Organizations that operate 24/7 contact centers or use rotating shifts can reduce the time supervisors spend manually reassigning agents to schedules. With shift rotation policies, administrators define the rotation pattern once and the scheduler automatically applies it. This helps ensure fair and predictable shift distribution for customer service representatives, reduces administrative overhead for supervisors, and supports consistent staffing coverage across operating hours.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577802","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/use/workforce-management-shift-rotation-policies"},{"id":"rm-577804","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys: Elevate customer experiences - Automatically update emails with the latest content","desc":"<p>By automatically updating emails with latest content, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Easily create dynamic content blocks in Content gallery with new content or select existing content in email and save it as a dynamic content block.</li> <li>Have content only so it uses the layout of the email when inserted or have content with its layout preserved. You can mark the content block as “protected” to prevent content from being modified in the email.</li> <li>Allow personalized content (for example, dynamic text or conditional content).</li> <li>Easily see which emails will be updated when you update such content blocks.</li> </ul> <p>Dynamic content blocks can be enabled by going to the <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Feature switches</strong> area and turning on the feature switch <strong>Dynamic content block</strong>.</p> <p>Imagine a financial service company that includes a standard footer in each email that has legal disclaimer text along with a blurb about their company that includes assets under management and recent accolades and awards. Given the sensitivity of legal text, and the fact that key information about their company (assets under management) change every few months, they find it hard and inefficient to manually update all emails in use across multiple campaigns. Customer trust is eroded if the same customer receives two emails with different information about their company, or worse, an old legal disclaimer text.</p> <p>Such issues can now be avoided with dynamic content blocks. The marketing team can now put such regularly updated content in a dynamic content block included in the footer (you can do this as part of the email template itself). Now when this content block is updated, every email that includes the content block is automatically updated, ensuring customers receive the most recent content.</p> <p>Dynamic content blocks can include personalized content to make emails more engaging. For example, the content block can include conditional content and dynamic text to include only the most relevant awards for the customer’s industry or financial level.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>No business can afford to appear unprofessional or lower trust in their brand by sending emails with outdated or inaccurate information. Stakes are much higher with legal and disclaimer text routinely included in every email (usually via the footer). Updating such content in every email can be very time-consuming and error-prone.</p> <p>Dynamic content blocks eliminate such manual work and the risk of sending emails with outdated content. When a dynamic content block is updated, all emails using that block are automatically refreshed to ensure recipients always receive the most current content.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Journeys"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577804","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/content-blocks#static-vs-dynamic-content-blocks"},{"id":"rm-577819","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Copilot and AI innovation - View next best actions with Customer Intent Agent","desc":"<p>An administrator can enable this feature for the entire organization in the Customer Service admin center. Turning on next best actions populates the Copilot pane with actions that service representatives can use. Important case attributes are consolidated in one place as the representative gathers information through back-and-forth exchanges with the customer. Knowledge articles are suggested so representatives can dig deeper and understand the reasoning behind the recommendations.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Next Best Action (NBA) allows service representatives to perform a suite of Copilot-powered actions in one click. These actions include, but aren't limited to, drafting emails, updating knowledge articles, updating case notes, and more.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577819","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-577824","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Planning - Enhance demand forecasts with multiple data inputs","desc":"<p>Demand planning in Supply Chain Management helps you forecast demand using diverse data sources and signals. The latest updates enhance forecast accuracy, enabling you to optimize your supply chain and improve financial outcomes.</p> <p>New capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Support for multiple signals</strong>: Define multiple input signals such as inflation or weather-related measures and apply the <em>XGBoost</em> forecast algorithm. XGBoost assesses correlation, analyzes the impact of each signal against historical sales data, and incorporates these insights into the forecast result.</li> <li><strong>New forecast algorithms</strong>: Use algorithms like <em>Naive</em> and <em>Croston</em> for specific scenarios.</li> <li><strong>Preserve manual adjustment in rolling forecasts</strong>: The new <em>manual adjustment</em> principle extends time-freeze functionality to allow the system to preserve all manual adjustments when executing rolling forecasts.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The latest demand planning enhancements in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management allow you to create forecasts that consider the impacts of multiple inputs, including historical sales data, inflation, pricing, weather, and more. These tools help you optimize your supply chain and achieve better financial outcomes.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577824","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/demand-planning/forecasts-with-signals"},{"id":"rm-577826","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Export object-centric process mining data to Microsoft Fabric semantic model","desc":"<p>This feature allows seamless integration with Microsoft Fabric for enterprise-wide analytics. It enables direct publishing of object-centric process mining (OCPM) results into Microsoft Fabric semantic models, making process intelligence data available throughout the Microsoft analytics ecosystem.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Semantic model publishing: Export OCPM analysis results, including objects, events, relationships, and attributes, directly to Fabric as structured semantic models.</li> <li>Multi-object support: Preserve the rich, object-centric structure of your process data, maintaining relationships between different object types (orders, deliveries, invoices, and more) in the published model.</li> <li>Metric preservation: Transfer KPIs and metrics from your process analysis, making them available as measures within the Fabric semantic model.</li> <li>Power BI integration: Access published semantic models immediately in Power BI for report creation, dashboard development, and custom visualization.</li> <li>Data refresh synchronization: Configure publishing schedules to keep Fabric semantic models current with your process mining data updates.</li> <li>Enterprise connectivity: Combine process intelligence data with other Fabric data sources, enabling unified analytics across operational, financial, and customer domains.</li> </ul> <p>The published semantic models follow Fabric's standard architecture, ensuring compatibility with existing governance policies, security controls, and data management practices within your Microsoft environment.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Publishing to Microsoft Fabric breaks down data silos and amplifies the impact of your process insights across your organization. Instead of keeping process analytics isolated in a standalone tool, your teams can now blend object-centric process metrics with financial data, operational KPIs, customer information, and other enterprise data sources within Fabric's unified platform. This means business analysts can build comprehensive Power BI reports that combine process performance with business outcomes, data scientists can incorporate process patterns into predictive models, and executives can access process metrics alongside other strategic indicators in their existing dashboards. By meeting stakeholders where they already work, you accelerate adoption, enable richer cross-functional analysis, and ensure process intelligence becomes an integral part of enterprise decision-making rather than a disconnected specialty tool.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577826","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/object-centric-ingest-event-log"},{"id":"rm-577827","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Get support for normalized schema import for data ingestion","desc":"<p>Most systems of record have data stored in data structures that allow you to easily extract information about the analyzed entity (case-level data) and historical changes on those entities (event-level data). The attributes are also stored in a normalized form. The single-table approach to event log creation requires you to do inefficient transformations. With this feature, Power Automate Process Mining supports the case-event entity-based data structure plus a normalized form of attributes. This speeds up the ingestion process in both the transformation and import to process model phases and reduces the storage capacity needed.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Customers with existing data pipelines or data products in data mesh mostly want to stick to normalized, efficient forms such as star schema. Power Automate Process Mining currently requires you to transform the event log into a single-table form, where attributes with small cardinality are duplicated. Support for star schema reduces storage volumes and speeds up ingestion performance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577827","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/object-centric-semantic-model"},{"id":"rm-577812","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Administrator experiences - Manage users through Microsoft Entra security groups","desc":"<p>Administrators configure team-based access for representatives through Microsoft Entra ID security groups. They link an Entra security group to a Dataverse team of type <strong>Microsoft Entra ID Security Group</strong> and assign at the team level the required security roles such as:</p> <ul> <li>Basic user</li> <li>Customer Service Representative</li> <li>Omnichannel agent</li> </ul> <p>Every member of the linked group inherits the roles automatically with no per user role assignment, including:</p> <ul> <li>Queue participation</li> <li>Presence</li> <li>Conversation handling</li> </ul> <p>When a representative belongs to more than one team, they receive the combined privileges of their teams. Existing persona-based assignments continue to work, so current configurations continue to function without changes.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Large contact centers face major challenges when they onboard and offboard service representatives at scale. Administrators must assign multiple security roles to each user individually. This approach increases effort, delays readiness, and raises the risk of access errors.</p> <p>This feature simplifies access management through Microsoft Entra security groups. Administrators assign roles to a group once. They grant or revoke access instantly by adding or removing users from the groups.</p> <p>Organizations reduce administrative burden, strengthen access control, and speed up onboarding. New service representatives receive the access they need on day one. Administrators replace thousands of repetitive tasks with a centralized, scalable model that supports growth and improves operational efficiency.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577812","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577808","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Administrator experiences - Use Service Operations Agent to accelerate setup, onboard, and verify config changes","desc":"<p>Service Operations Agent in the Copilot Service admin center delivers a unified, conversational experience for configuring Dynamics 365 Contact Center.</p> <p>Administrators use conversational setup and orchestration in Service Operations Agent to streamline setup tasks—configure channels, voice settings, Teams Phone extensibility, and knowledge sources. Through the same single guided assistant, administrators also set up route-to-queue rules and assignment strategies for queues and AI agents—automating and optimizing queue management and agent assignments to drive operational efficiency.</p> <p>With Service Operations Agent, admins can:</p> <ul> <li>Generate and validate configurations in real time.</li> <li>Surface diagnostics and actionable insights.</li> <li>Receive clear explanations for recommendations and setup choices.</li> </ul> <p>By consolidating fragmented configuration workflows, Service Operations Agent reduces errors, shortens deployment timelines, and simplifies onboarding for customers and partners.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Service Operations Agent is an AI-powered assistant that empowers admins to simplify configuration, speed up onboarding, and ensure continuous validation of changes. By leveraging conversational setup and intelligent automation, the agent eliminates manual complexity, enabling faster deployments, reducing errors, and providing real-time feedback on every change. Designed for enterprise-scale reliability, Service Operations Agent supports seamless transitions, proactive monitoring, and compliance-ready operations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577808","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/administer/use-service-operations-agent"},{"id":"rm-577790","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Workforce engagement management - Enable evaluation retries and improve error handling","desc":"<p>Key features include:</p> <ul> <li>Added detailed error insights for failed AI evaluations, enabling supervisors and administrators to understand failure causes and take appropriate corrective actions.</li> <li>Improved bulk evaluation monitoring by introducing a Records Failed indicator in run history and displaying error details for failed records within evaluation runs.</li> <li>Enabled supervisors to retry failed evaluations directly from both the evaluation grid and bulk evaluation run lists.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature improves troubleshooting by providing supervisors with clear, actionable error messages that explain what went wrong and the recommended next steps. It also includes retry functionality, allowing supervisors to rerun failed evaluations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577790","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577800","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Automatically generate evaluation summary from final results","desc":"<p>This feature ensures that evaluation summaries and recommended actions always reflect the final, validated evaluation outcomes.</p> <p>When a reviewer or supervisor updates evaluation answers, either to correct AI misinterpretations or refine manual assessments, the system automatically regenerates the evaluation summary upon submission. This ensures that insights remain aligned with the finalized evaluation. If no changes are made, summary regeneration is skipped to optimize performance and cost.</p> <p>Administrators can control this behavior through a Customer Service admin center configuration setting. When enabled, summaries are automatically refreshed after edits to maintain accuracy. When disabled, the existing behavior is retained, and summaries remain unchanged after evaluation updates.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Ensures evaluation summaries accurately reflect final outcomes by regenerating them after corrections to AI predictions or human review are made. This helps you avoid mismatches between evaluation results and insights, improving trust, accuracy, and better decision-making. With flexible controls, you can scale AI-assisted and fully AI-driven evaluations while keeping reporting consistent and reliable.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577799","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Enable question-level weighting for quality evaluation scoring","desc":"<p>This feature enables supervisors to assign percentage-based weights at the individual question level, ensuring that evaluation scores reflect the relative importance of each question within a section.</p> <p>When scoring and question-level weight is enabled for an evaluation criterion, users can assign explicit weight percentages to each question. These weights directly influence score calculation, allowing higher-priority questions to have a greater impact on the final evaluation outcome. The system validates that the total weight of all questions within a section matches the section weight, ensuring consistency and preventing scoring errors.</p> <p>This enhancement extends the scoring model without disrupting existing workflows. Supervisors can enable and configure question-level weighting per criterion based on business needs. As a result, organizations can create more flexible and accurate evaluation frameworks that better align with operational goals and quality standards, while maintaining ease of use and system integrity.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enables organizations to move beyond equal scoring distribution by assigning custom weights to individual questions. This ensures evaluation scores better reflect business priorities, critical behaviors, and compliance requirements.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577799","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577791","title":"Power Automate: Desktop flows - Export work queue items to CSV","desc":"<p>You can now export work queue items directly from the Automation Center portal. A new option available in the Work Queues experience lets you download items as a CSV file.<br> This capability allows you to access work queue data in a portable format for further analysis, reporting, or integration with other tools, without needing to rely on external APIs or custom solutions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature lets you quickly export work queue data from Automation Center into a CSV file, so you can dig deeper into analysis, create custom reports, and share insights across your teams. It helps you boost visibility, streamline collaboration, and make smarter decisions faster.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-577793","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Automatic clearing of centralized bridged vendor payments during bank reconciliation","desc":"<p>This enhancement enables automatic clearing of bridge transactions generated by centralized vendor payments when bank statements are matched with records in Dynamics 365 Finance during the bank reconciliation process. The system posts the required clearing journals in the centralized legal entity, ensuring that general ledger balances are updated accurately.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Automatic clearing of centralized vendor payments streamlines the bank reconciliation process by eliminating manual clearing of bridge transactions, reducing reconciliation errors and ensuring general ledger balances are accurate and up to date. This improves operational efficiency, strengthens auditability in cross‑entity payment scenarios, and increases confidence in using automated bank reconciliation at scale.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577793","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/cash-bank-management/advanced-bank-reconciliation-overview"},{"id":"rm-555895","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"<p>You can now reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Copilot using Agent Mode in PowerPoint.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-02","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555895","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-577803","title":"Power Automate: Cloud flows - View property value expanded inline in new cloud flow designer","desc":"<p>When you add an action, you can view property values for multiple steps at design time, or output values for multiple steps at runtime. The inline view shows this information directly on the cards, so you can review and compare values across several steps at once.</p> <p>Without the inline view, you select each card individually to see its value in the side pane, and you can view only one step's value at a time. This makes it harder to compare values across steps.</p> <p>You can choose which experience you prefer. The current side pane experience remains the default. You can switch to the inline view whenever you want and switch back at any time.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can be more efficient when authoring or debugging flows by using the inline view to examine property values from multiple steps at once without needing to select each step separately.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-22","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577803","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/flows-designer"},{"id":"rm-555891","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation","desc":"<p>You can now reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555891","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-553592","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams shared display mode and peripheral detection available for GCC-H and DoD environments","desc":"<p>Shared display mode in Teams is now available in government CCC-H and DoD environments, enabling more seamless and private meeting hosting from your PC. Additionally, peripheral detection for bring-your-own-device spaces is available for inventory management and reporting through the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-10","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553592","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-482539","title":"Microsoft Teams: Standard and Basic licensed Teams rooms on Windows in the Pro Management portal","desc":"<p>The Teams Rooms Pro Management portal now supports and enforces licenses for devices in Teams Rooms on Windows with a Standard or Basic license. IT admins get a unified device management experience through the Pro Management portal where they can manage those devices with the same functionality found in Teams admin center for that license type.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-25","modified":"2026-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482539","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-576296","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Restrict task assignments to project team members","desc":"<p>This feature strengthens assignment governance by limiting the resources displayed in the Assigned to column to members of the current project team. Project managers can assign tasks only to resources who have already been added to the project, instead of selecting from the organization’s complete resource list.<br> If a resource isn’t part of the project team, the resource must first be added to the team before being assigned a task. This controlled workflow keeps task assignments aligned with the project’s defined staffing model and prevents resources from being assigned outside the established project team.<br> This is for both Project Operations core and Project Operations connected with ERP deployment types.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576296","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-573700","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Sales Development Agent is now available","desc":"<p>Autonomous agent that researches, qualifies, engages with leads, scaling sales capacity 24/7.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573700","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"aka.ms/SDA-Public-Docs"},{"id":"rm-568372","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - SLA Based Alert Reporting Dashboard","desc":"<p>Out-of-box MTTA/MTTD/MTTR SLA Alert Reporting dashboard showing past trends, Top SITs getting exposed via DLP alerts generated. Customers can define their custom SLAs for high, med and low severity alerts and get access to dashboard showing operational performance and SLA metrics.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568372","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577175","title":"Microsoft Viva: Glint - Teams notification customization","desc":"<p>Viva Glint admins can now customize the Microsoft Teams notifications sent for surveys. Admins can edit the title, message, and button label in each survey language and see their changes in a live preview. Teams and email messages stay consistent and match your organization's voice, which helps more employees see the survey and take part.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577175","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-573261","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Use Expense Manager role center","desc":"<p>The Expense Manager Role Center is updated to provide a more focused and efficient experience for managing vendor and expense-related activities. The enhancements align the workspace with typical expense management workflows, ensuring that key information and actions are readily accessible. Where relevant, other Role Centers are also updated to include access to expense management features.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573261","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573708","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Support Approver Comments for Expense Reports in Expense Management Mobile app","desc":"<p>Approvers using the Expense Management Mobile App currently have limited options to provide context when approving or rejecting expense reports. Approval decisions may require comments to provide justification, request clarification, document additional information, or communicate feedback to employees. Without this capability in the mobile experience, approvers may need to switch to the web application to complete the approval process.</p> <p>This enhancement will enable approvers to add and view approval or rejection comments directly within the Expense Mobile App, providing a more consistent experience across mobile and web.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573708","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573291","title":"Microsoft Edge: Simplified Energy Saver","desc":"<p>Energy saver, formerly known as efficiency mode, will have new defaults and different setting options. Edge will now support and recommend users to use the BatterySaverModeAvailability policy to manage the energy saver feature. The energy saver feature has been simplified to become enabled under two conditions: on low battery or when unplugged. The default will be for energy saver to be enabled on low battery. Energy saver will now have one mode. Users set to Balanced savings will be mapped to have energy saver enabled on low battery. Users set to Maximum savings will be mapped to have energy saver enabled when unplugged.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573291","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-559609","title":"Microsoft Teams: Audio announcement for recording and transcription","desc":"<p>Admins can enable a policy that<br> plays an audio announcement when recording or transcription starts. This can be<br> applied tenant-wide or to specific groups. The announcement helps ensure all<br> participants are informed and improves accessibility awareness.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559609","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-575295","title":"Power Apps: Form fill assistance in apps can provide suggestions for existing values","desc":"<p>We’re expanding form fill assistance in model-driven applications in Power Apps to suggest updates to fields that already contain values—not just empty fields. This helps users update existing information with ease using AI-powered skills in their apps.</p>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575295","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576282","title":"Power Apps: Monitor generative pages with out-of-the-box Application Insights telemetry","desc":"<p>Admins and developers can monitor published generative pages with Application Insights. When an administrator configures Application Insights data export for an environment, Power Apps automatically exports completed page loads, unhandled errors, supported Data API operations, and navigation initiated from generative pages without requiring telemetry code, the Application Insights JavaScript SDK, or a connection string on the page.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2608.5</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Admins or makers</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576282","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/model-driven-apps/generative-pages#monitor-a-generative-page-with-application-insights-preview"},{"id":"rm-576284","title":"Power Apps: Use Dataverse custom APIs in generative pages","desc":"<p>Makers can have a generative page call a Dataverse custom API to run server-side business logic, such as approving an order, recalculating a price, or validating a transaction. From either the Maker Studio generative page designer or the generative pages AI plugin, makers select a prepared API and describe when the page should call it, which input values to provide, and how to use the response.</p> <h2>Availability</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Not applicable</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>Gen page v307</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Admins or makers</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576284","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/model-driven-apps/generative-pages#run-server-side-business-logic-with-a-custom-api-preview"},{"id":"rm-573260","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Add an interim approver when you submit an expense report","desc":"<p>This feature introduces support for a simple interim approval scenario for expense reports. When someone submits an expense report, organizations can designate an interim approver to review and approve expenses before the final approver can review and approve. Interim approver must review expense reports to confirm whether they're complete and compliant before final approver.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573260","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573257","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Create expense reports per trip automatically","desc":"<p>Expense Agent can automatically create expense reports based on identified business trips. You just need to configure the feature on the <strong>Expense Agent Setup</strong> page. Instead of manually collecting and organizing individual expense entries, you can use the agent to group relevant expenses and generate a dedicated expense report for each trip. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Administrators can specify whether the company wants to group expenses by trip and not only by period.</li> <li>Automated expense report creation without requiring you to manually start and organize reports after a travel requisition is approved.</li> <li>Automatic trip-based expense grouping associates eligible expenses with the correct business trip based on information in the travel requisition. The agent automatically groups not only expenses based on the location, but uses intelligence to group all expenses based on the context.</li> <li>Non-trip related expenses keep existing period-based grouping in expense reports.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573257","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573263","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Finance - Use approvals with fixed asset journals","desc":"<p>Organizations can use approval workflows with <strong>Fixed Asset Journals</strong>, which gives them the same level of control and oversight for fixed assets that's available for other journals in Business Central.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573263","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573264","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Finance - Use batch totals for payment journals","desc":"<p>The <strong>Batch Total</strong> field on the <strong>Payment Journal</strong> page enhances payment processing by enabling you to work with and review a cumulative total for a payment journal batch. By surfacing batch-level totals directly in payment journals, organizations gain better control over outgoing payments and can streamline review and approval processes.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573264","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570864","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Keep Project Staffing and Field Service Scheduling Aligned","desc":"<p>Deliver consistent scheduling outcomes across Dynamics 365 Project Operations and Field Service, regardless of where scheduling begins. When a project task includes resource assignments and planned effort, that demand is represented on the related work order with the same role, resource, duration, and scheduling window. Users can therefore schedule the same demand from either application and receive consistent availability and booking results. When multiple assignments exist, dispatchers can select the specific requirement they want to schedule.</p> <p>When a project task does not provide assignment- or duration-based demand, the incident type on the work order continues to define the scheduling requirement. This flexibly supports an organization's scheduling needs, whether project-task-driven or incident-type-driven.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570864","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576711","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI Interpreter for Teams Events","desc":"<p>AI Interpreter for Events brings real-time, AI-powered audio interpretation to Teams Town Halls and Webinars, helping global audiences follow events in their preferred language. Organizers can configure supported languages for their event, giving attendees a more natural and engaging multilingual experience beyond translated captions.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576711","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576199","title":"Microsoft Teams: Expanded Markdown support in Microsoft Teams","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams is expanding Markdown support in the compose box, giving you more ways to structure and format messages using familiar Markdown syntax. Create richer, more readable messages while staying in the Markdown authoring experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576199","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-567315","title":"Planner: Capabilities in Microsoft Cowork","desc":"<p>You’ll soon be able to bring your Microsoft Planner into Microsoft Cowork. In Cowork, you can view, create, and update your plans, buckets, goals, and tasks without switching apps. Cowork goes a step further by helping you execute your Planner tasks across Microsoft 365, such as drafting and sending emails, scheduling meetings, posting updates to Teams, and working with files. It can then write progress back to Planner with your approval. You can move from planning your work to getting it done in one place.</p>","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567315","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575296","title":"Power Apps: Form fill assistance supports more field types","desc":"<p>We’re expanding form fill assistance in model-driven applications in Power Apps to support lookup, rich text, and multi-select choice fields, helping users complete more of their forms with AI-powered suggestions and less manual entry.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Monthly</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-21","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575296","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-560318","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI-powered notes for in-person meetings with Facilitator in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"<p>In addition to capturing real-time notes and meeting outcomes during scheduled or hybrid meetings, the Facilitator agent assists you with notes, decisions and actions for in-person meetings in Teams Rooms on Windows. Simply invite Facilitator with one tap of the room console. Meeting notes appear on the front of room display or touch board, are available via meeting recap when shared, and deleted if no one selected. Rest assured no data remains in the room. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-15","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560318","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-566528","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Extend Purview data security to the network layer via Entra GSA integration","desc":"<p>Extend Microsoft Purview data security controls to the network layer to detect and protect sensitive data in text and prompts by integrating with Entra Internet Access. This integration enables organizations to intercept and inspect text and AI interactions at the network layer, enforce restrictive actions based on DLP policies, and detect risky user activity through Insider Risk Management. It helps prevent sensitive data from being shared with untrusted cloud applications through browsers, apps, APIs, add-ins, and more - including generative AI platforms, social media, collaborative platforms - while managing alerts and incidents through Purview and Microsoft Defender.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566528","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-522096","title":"Microsoft Purview: Integration with Entra GSA Internet Access to enable sensitive file filtering at the network layer","desc":"<p>Extend Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies to filter sensitive files at the network layer by integrating with Entra Global Secure Access Internet Access. This integration enables organizations to intercept and inspect files at the network layer and enforce restrictive actions based on DLP policy conditions. It helps prevent sensitive data from being shared with untrusted cloud applications through browsers, apps, APIs, add-ins, and more - including generative AI platforms, cloud storage, and content-sharing services - while managing alerts and incidents through Purview and Microsoft Defender. Updated July 17, 2026: The GA release of this item has moved. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=522096","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-567302","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ability for IT admins to customize the user notification messages for recording and transcription in calls","desc":"<p>This feature enables IT admins to customize a portion of the user notification messages for recording and transcription during Teams calls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567302","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-570448","title":"OneDrive: Sync support for up to 1 million items on macOS","desc":"<p>OneDrive Sync supports syncing up to 1 million items on macOS devices, helping teams manage large document libraries and shared content at scale without compromising access across devices. This preview requires the Insiders ring and that devices meet minimum hardware and configuration requirements. Devices that don't meet these requirements continue to sync at the existing 300,000-item supported limit with no disruption.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570448","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-574126","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Data mirroring to Microsoft Fabric","desc":"<p>Connect Business Central to Microsoft Fabric to make business data available for analytics, reporting, and data integration.</p> <p>Choose the Business Central companies and tables to synchronise, and make the data available in OneLake for use with Fabric IQ, Power BI, Data Factory, and other analytics experiences.</p> <p>Get started quickly with ready-made sample Power BI apps, while built-in logging provides visibility into synchronisation health and helps troubleshoot issues.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574126","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577184","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Manage intraday operations with AI agent","desc":"<p>Intraday Agent is an autonomous AI agent that helps manage intraday operational scenarios. The following are its high‑level capabilities.</p> <p><strong>Intraday queue tracking</strong></p> <ul> <li>Continuously monitors queue volumes in real time.</li> <li>Detects anomalies when actual volume deviates significantly from forecasted demand.</li> <li>Automatically reforecasts in real time to assess current demand.</li> <li>Notifies supervisors with proactive alerts and recommendations.</li> <li>Automates corrective actions such as adjusting schedules, rescheduling breaks, or reallocating service representatives to maintain SLA performance.</li> <li>Supports customizable instructions to align mitigation actions with business needs.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Intraday adherence tracking</strong></p> <ul> <li>Monitors service representative adherence to scheduled shift activities in real time.</li> <li>Detects deviations such as late logins, extended breaks, or early logouts.</li> <li>Autonomously mitigates deviations through actions such as break rescheduling, shift extensions, overtime activation, or flexible channel reassignment.</li> <li>Supports customizable instructions to align mitigation actions with business needs.</li> </ul>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577184","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-577182","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Simplify the creation of recurring expenses","desc":"<p>This feature enables employees to automatically generate expense entries for predictable, repeatable business expenses (for example, monthly mobile bills, internet charges, parking, and subscriptions) without manual re-entry each period. It reduces repetitive effort, improves compliance, and ensures timely and accurate expense submission, while respecting organizational expense policies and approval workflows.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577182","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568936","title":"Microsoft Teams: Facilitator Can Join Channel Meetings","desc":"<p>Facilitator can now join meetings set up in Teams channels. Facilitator helps participants run more effective meetings through the ability to take live notes, manage the agenda, answer questions, and capture tasks.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-06","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568936","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-577186","title":"Microsoft Edge: Organize and merge PDF files in the built-in PDF reader","desc":"<p>Users can organize and merge PDF files in the Microsoft Edge built-in PDF reader. They can select pages to extract, delete, rotate, or reorder, and save the result as a new PDF file. They can also merge the open PDF file with other PDF files that are open in Microsoft Edge tabs or stored on their device, to create a single PDF file. Files are processed on the device, and the original files aren't modified. Admins can manage this feature using the PdfOrganizeAndMergeEnabled policy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577186","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-577187","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention-View-only access to device onboarding with the View-Only Device Management role","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention is introducing more granular, role-based access to the Devices page under Settings → Device Onboarding. Previously, viewing or managing device onboarding required broad administrative roles (such as Compliance Administrator, Global Administrator, or Security Administrator). With this update, organizations can grant access using least-privilege Purview role-based access control (RBAC) roles scoped specifically to device operations.</p> <p>A new View-Only Device Management role enables users, such as auditors or security analysts, to view device onboarding status, search for devices, review configuration details, and export device data, without granting permission to change onboarding configuration or other administrative settings. Existing administrative roles continue to have full access, so current workflows are unaffected. This change helps organizations follow the principle of least privilege and simplifies granting read-only visibility into device onboarding without over-provisioning permissions.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577187","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571387","title":"Microsoft Teams: Pop out sign language interpreter meeting video for continuous visibility","desc":"<p>Keep communication more accessible throughout your meeting. You can now pop out a sign language interpreter into a separate, resizable window that stays visible across monitors and apps. Designed to support Deaf and Hard of Hearing users, the sign language interpreter's popout video will persist while viewers are multitasking, sharing content, or changing meeting layouts.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571387","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-577185","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Enable semantic data understanding for agentic use","desc":"<p>Give AI agents and Copilot a true understanding of your business data — not just raw schema — so they can answer questions accurately with less manual configuration.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Learns from the systems you already run</strong> — Automatically extracts semantic knowledge from views, forms, and metadata already defined in your Dataverse environment, reducing agent deployment from days of manual setup to near-zero effort.</li> <li><strong>Full visibility for makers</strong> — View generated semantic knowledge per entity — including name, description, and sample questions — directly in the Power Apps maker portal. Search for understanding gaps and enrich missing context with a built-in glossary for domain-specific terms.</li> <li><strong>Governance and privacy built in</strong> — Enable or disable semantic signals at the org level, or at the individual signal-type or table level, giving makers and admins granular control to meet compliance and privacy requirements without sacrificing agent quality.</li> </ul> <p>No manual schema mapping. No custom query logic. No disambiguation between what your data is called and what your business actually means.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577185","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570157","title":"Microsoft Viva: Campaigns Hub in Engage and Engage in Teams mobile","desc":"<p>The Campaigns Hub in Viva Engage provides a centralized mobile destination where employees can discover and participate in organizational campaigns. Available in the Viva Engage app and Viva Engage in Teams mobile, the hub highlights top and sponsored campaigns, enables users to browse active and completed campaigns, and makes it easy to view campaign details and follow the campaigns that matter to them.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-27","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570157","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-560538","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Export metrics from Agent Dashboard","desc":"<p>Users can export de-identified, row-level agent metrics and attributes from the Agent Dashboard. Exported data provides detailed insights into agent usage and user-level agent interactions across the organization, with personal identifiers removed.<br> #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560538","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575293","title":"Outlook: Teams Meeting Options","desc":"<p>When you add a Teams meeting to an event in Outlook for Mac, the join link and dial-in details now appear in the invite while you're still writing it. A new Meeting Options button lets you change the Teams meeting settings right away, before you send.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575293","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1266912","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365 Copilot: Intelligent Summaries in Copilot Dashboard","desc":"Updated October 20, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nIntelligent summaries in Copilot Dashboard help you quickly understand what’s driving Copilot adoption in your organization. These AI‑generated insights highlight key usage trends, areas of success, and opportunities where focused attention can accelerate value. Suggested prompts guide deeper exploration of underlying drivers and adoption patterns.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557681.\n[When this will happen]\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout will begin in November 2026 (previously mid-August) and is expected to complete by end of November 2026 (previously late September).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Admins using the Microsoft 365 Copilot Dashboard in Microsoft Viva and Microsoft 365\n\nWhat will happen\n• Intelligent summaries will appear automatically in the Copilot Dashboard:\n•\n• Admins will see AI‑generated insights that highlight adoption trends and key usage patterns.\n• Suggested prompts will be available to help admins drill into specific drivers and areas of opportunity.\n• No configuration changes are required; the feature is on by default for eligible tenants.\n• Existing admin controls and permissions remain unchanged.\n• There is no user workflow impact.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required before rollout.\nIf helpful for your organization, you may:\n• Notify helpdesk or training teams about the new summaries.\n• Update internal documentation that references the Copilot Dashboard.\n• Review updated online documentation, which will be refreshed as rollout begins in late April.\n• If you choose not to use this feature, you can roll back by disabling intelligent summaries using available admin controls.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1266912","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1288531","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Viva - Copilot Analytics: Export agent data from the Agent Dashboard","desc":"Updated October 20, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo support deeper analysis of Copilot agent adoption and usage across your organization, Microsoft will introduce a new export capability in the Agent Dashboard. This feature will allow eligible users to download de‑identified Copilot agent usage data for analysis, helping organizations track adoption trends, optimize licensing, and support AI transformation strategies, while maintaining existing privacy and access controls. User identifiers are removed from the output.\nThis feature will require at least 50 Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses and will apply to the Viva Insights web app.\nThis message is related to Roadmap ID 560538.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out in late May 2026 and expect to complete rollout by early June 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in mid-November 2026 (previously late October) and expect to complete rollout by end of November 2026 (previously early November).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Agent Dashboard users with full company‑level data access, including:• Senior leaders (as identified in Microsoft Entra ID)\n• Admin‑assigned company‑level users\n• Delegates with company‑level access\n• Global analysts and admins\n\nNote: Group managers with data access limited to their own teams will not have access to this feature.\nWhat will happen\n• Eligible users will be able to export de‑identified, user‑level Copilot agent metrics and agent attributes aggregated by user and week, for up to the past six months. User identifiers are removed from the output.\n• The export will include multiple data tables, such as:• Copilot agent metadataincluding agent name, creator type, and publishing source\n• Copilot agent usage metrics, including the number of responses generated\n• Copilot agent credit usage and user retention metrics\n• People metadata, including organization and function type\n\n• By default, this feature will be ON for all eligible users.\n• Admins will be able to manage or disable the feature at the tenant or group level at any time using Viva Feature Access Management (VFAM):• Module: Viva Insights\n• Feature: Agent Metrics Export\n\n• There will be no impact to user workflows unless the feature is accessed by eligible users.\n\nScreenshot - View of the Agent Dashboard:\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No action is required to enable this feature.\n• If you do not want this feature enabled by default, you can disable it at the tenant or group level using Viva Feature Access Management (VFAM).\n• Review which users have full company‑level access to the Agent Dashboard.\n• Communicate the upcoming change to eligible users so they understand the new export capability and its intended use.\n\nLearn more:\n• Connect to the Agent Dashboard | Viva Insights | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n• Delegate access to the Copilot Dashboard, Agent Dashboard, and Copilot insights | Viva Insights | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n• Manage settings for the Microsoft Copilot Dashboard, Agent Dashboard, and Viva Insights web app | Viva Insights | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n• Using Entra ID data - Connect to the Microsoft Copilot Dashboard for Microsoft 365 customers | Viva Insights | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n• Viva features management - Control access to features in Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1288531","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-568790","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Review PDFs using the Copilot context menu on OneDrive iOS","desc":"<p>Microsoft 365 Copilot makes PDF reviews faster and easier on mobile. Select text in any PDF in OneDrive iOS and tap Ask Copilot to explain, summarize, translate, or ask a custom question about the selection — the same in-context Copilot experience already generally available on desktop, now on OneDrive iOS. Updated October 20, 2026: We have decided not to move forward with this change at this time. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Cancelled","created":"2026-08-10","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568790","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-577183","title":"Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration: Multi-grader comparison","desc":"<p>Multi-grader comparison enables makers to compare the results of multiple graders applied to the same evaluation.</p> <p>The experience highlights agreement, differences, and overall grading behavior.</p> <p><strong>Core capabilities</strong></p> <p>The core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Compare graders side-by-side.</li> <li>Compare scores.</li> <li>Review explanations from each grader.</li> <li>Analyze grading consistency.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Results experience</strong></p> <p>Results include:</p> <ul> <li>Comparative score view.</li> <li>Pass / fail comparison.</li> <li>Grader explanations.</li> <li>Evidence supporting each evaluation.</li> </ul>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-20","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=577183","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560820","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management – Increase in expansion limit for auto expanding archive beyond 1.5TB","desc":"<p>Previously, auto expanding archive mailbox expansion was supported only up to 1.5 TB, after which mailboxes would become inoperative. Archive mailboxes can now automatically expand beyond the 1.5 TB limit, ensuring uninterrupted retention and enabling scalable archive growth as storage thresholds are reached. This capability to expand archive beyond 1.5 TB will be available to customers with eligible E5 licenses.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560820","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571884","title":"Word: Legal plugins in Copilot","desc":"<p>Legal plugins in Copilot provide purpose-built skills to help legal professionals summarize, draft, review, and redline legal documents. Available in Word and Cowork, these plugins can use work context from Microsoft 365 and connect to supported third-party legal sources.</p>","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571884","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-572673","title":"Microsoft 365 Apps: Cloud Update - Extended rollback support for Monthly Enterprise Channel","desc":"<p>Cloud Update is expanding rollback options for devices on Monthly Enterprise Channel. Administrators will be able to roll back devices to a release from two versions prior, with the latest available security updates for that release, and keep devices in the rolled-back state across subsequent releases until they are ready to resume updates. This provides additional time to investigate and resolve compatibility issues while maintaining security coverage and centralized control through the Microsoft 365 Apps admin center.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=572673","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-365-apps/admin-center/cloud-update-pause-rollback"},{"id":"rm-503570","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Support permission sync missed in incremental crawl","desc":"<p>Earlier, permissions were synced only in the periodic full crawl which generally ha a default frequency of 1 day for most of the connectors. Now, we have support for doing permission syncs more frequently in an incremental way.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503570","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558251","title":"Microsoft 365 Apps: Cloud Update - Enhanced Rollout Waves","desc":"<p>New improvements are coming to the rollout wave functionality for Cloud Update. These enhancements will allow organizations to continue leveraging Microsoft Entra ID groups to set up rollout waves, with increased flexibility to configure more than the current limit of three waves. Additionally, admins will be able to assign custom delays between each wave, streamlining phased deployments and offering greater control over update distribution.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558251","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555894","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"<p>You can now reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Copilot using Agent Mode in PowerPoint.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555894","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-500019","title":"Microsoft 365: Backup Activity Logs","desc":"<p>In product monitoring logs to track all activities related to backup policy configuration &amp; restore related tasks. This will help admins with troubleshooting, monitoring, reporting and auditing capabilities.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-04","modified":"2026-10-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500019","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-574128","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - [US] Match Shopify tax lines to tax jurisdictions","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Reduce repetitive tax setup when you import Shopify orders that contain multiple United States tax jurisdictions. Shopify Tax Matching suggests how free-text tax lines map to configured tax jurisdictions and keeps you in control of exceptions before you create sales documents.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>The Shopify Tax Matching capability is available in public preview for organizations in the United States that use the Shopify connector. When standard tax-area mapping doesn't resolve an imported order, the capability uses AI to suggest tax jurisdictions based on Shopify tax-line titles and rates, configured tax jurisdictions, and limited ship-to location information.</p> <p>You can review each suggestion, confidence level, explanation, and rate before approving the final mapping. Configure which matches require review and whether the capability can create missing tax jurisdictions and tax areas. Unidentified jurisdictions and rate differences always require review.</p> <p>Shopify Tax Matching maps imported tax descriptions to tax setup. It doesn't calculate tax, determine tax liability, file tax returns, or replace professional tax advice.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574128","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"http://docs.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/shopify/shopify-tax-matching"},{"id":"rm-565866","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Retention capabilities based on files Last Accessed in OneDrive and SharePoint","desc":"<p>Ability to apply Retention labels and policies to items on OneDrive and SharePoint based on when the items were last accessed by an user.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565866","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-534609","title":"Microsoft Purview: Purview SDK embedded in Agent Framework SDK","desc":"<p>Purview SDK embedded in Agent Framework SDK enables developers to seamlessly integrate enterprise-grade security, compliance, and governance into the AI agents they build. This integration enables automatic classification and protection of sensitive data, prevents data leaks and oversharing, and provides visibility and control for regulatory compliance—empowering organizations to confidently and securely adopt AI agents in complex environments.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534609","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-576272","title":"Copilot Studio: Computer Use for web browsing on GitHub Copilot Harness","desc":"<p>Enable Microsoft Copilot Studio agents to browse and interact with websites as a native capability powered by the GitHub Copilot Harness. Using natural-language instructions, agents can navigate web pages, extract information, and download files. Agents can then use that information and those files alongside other tools to complete end-to-end workflows, extending their reach beyond configured knowledge sources and API-based integrations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576272","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-574121","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Add users without licenses to activity recipient fields","desc":"<p>Enable active Microsoft Entra users without Dataverse or Power Apps licenses as activity recipients. Created user records remain disabled and do not grant Dynamics 365 app access.</p> <p>Documentation: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/admin/add-unlicensed-users-activities</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Dynamics 365 Sales","Dynamics 365 Customer Service","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574121","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/admin/add-unlicensed-users-activities"},{"id":"rm-536576","title":"Microsoft Purview: Compliance Manager-Purview Compliance Manager integration with Microsoft Foundry for automated mapping of AI regulations and evaluation of Compliance controls for Foundry Agents","desc":"<p>This feature in Purview Compliance Manager shall enable customers to automatically access the compliance posture of Agents created in AI Foundry. Customers can map Agents being created in AI Foundry to compliance regulations and assessments in Purview Compliance Manager and get to know the compliance status and improvement actions to be innovative and compliant.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536576","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-570427","title":"Microsoft Teams: Meeting Shared Files","desc":"<p>The new Meeting Shared Files feature allows users to add relevant files and links to their meeting for easy access and to automatically share that content with all meeting participants. AI in the meeting, like the Facilitator agent, uses these files for targeted grounding to answer questions and enhance skill functionality.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570427","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-570652","title":"Work IQ: Agent Policy Governance","desc":"<p>Provide administrators with policy-based controls for governing agents and their capabilities at scale.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570652","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570672","title":"Work IQ: Human in the loop","desc":"<p>Allow agents and agent flows to pause for human input or approval before continuing.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570672","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562345","title":"Microsoft Purview: Archive SharePoint files under retention policies","desc":"<p>With the introduction of file archiving support in SharePoint Online, administrators are looking to seamlessly include archiving actions within their existing data retention policies. This means that, in addition to keeping or deleting data, admins want to now leverage Purview DLM to archive files according to organizational requirements, ensuring comprehensive governance across all stages of the content lifecycle in SPO. Retention based file archiving moves inactive content to low-cost storage, lowering costs with no compromise on Compliance, keeping data discoverable and making Copilot results highly relevant.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-18","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562345","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576278","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Complete zero-effort tasks","desc":"<p>Zero-effort task completion enables project managers and team members to mark tasks as complete even when no effort was planned or recorded. This capability supports milestones, administrative activities, checklists, and other tasks that track completion without requiring work hours.</p> <p>This is for both Project Operations core and Project Operations connected with ERP deployment types.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576278","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576286","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Inventory - Update Repair","desc":"<p>Update Repair helps admins identify Windows devices with Microsoft 365 Apps that are out of date or experiencing update issues. In the Microsoft 365 Apps admin center, admins can review device status and recommended actions, remotely start Online Repair for eligible devices, and follow manual remediation guidance for devices that need attention. Repair reinstalls Microsoft 365 Apps using the latest available build for the device’s configured update channel.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576286","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559605","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improved organization for muted and meeting chats","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams automatically organizes your chats with new built in sections that help reduce clutter and keep conversations easy to find. Muted chats (on by default) are grouped together in a dedicated area, while meeting chats (off by default) can be collected into a single section for quick access. You’re always in control, as each section can be turned on or off based on your preferences. The new Meeting chats section will replace the Meeting chats filter, that was previously available at the top of the chat and channel list. Updated July 20, 2026: We have temporarily rolled back this feature. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-01","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559605","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576709","title":"Microsoft Viva: Enhanced Microsoft Copilot in Viva Engage","desc":"<p>Introducing the <strong>Enhanced Microsoft 365 Copilot Experience in Viva Engage!</strong></p> <p>Powered by Engage MCP, this enhanced experience takes Copilot in Engage beyond catch-ups and summaries, helping users explore conversations more deeply, synthesize discussions, and uncover meaningful insights.</p> <p>It's also more deeply connected across Microsoft 365. For example, you can ask Copilot to analyze feedback on a leader's post, identify key themes, and turn those insights into a reusable PowerPoint deck.</p> <p>With Work IQ integration, Copilot also has a better understanding of you and your work context, connecting conversations in Engage to your broader work across Microsoft 365.</p> <p>Engage MCP expands both the breadth and depth of Engage scenarios Copilot can support, making it more useful for understanding conversations and insights across your Engage network.</p> <p>This update also brings Copilot in Engage closer to the broader Microsoft 365 Copilot experience, with your Microsoft 365 agents now accessible directly within Copilot in Engage.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576709","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573149","title":"PowerPoint: Set slide size in a modern PowerPoint pane","desc":"<p>Change slide size in PowerPoint from a modern task pane that keeps you in the flow of editing with real-time slide changes. Choose common slide sizes including new social media presets, or customize dimensions with a cleaner, more approachable experience.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573149","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573150","title":"PowerPoint: Set slide size in a modern task pane","desc":"<p>Change slide size in PowerPoint from a modern task pane that keeps you in the flow of editing with real-time slide changes. Choose common slide sizes including new social media presets, or customize dimensions with a cleaner, more approachable experience.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573150","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570651","title":"Work IQ: Real Time Transcripts","desc":"<p>Enable applications and agents to access Microsoft Teams meeting transcripts in real time for assistance and insights.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Work IQ"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570651","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1302905","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Purview SDK embedded in Agent Framework SDK","desc":"Updated October 19, 2026: We have paused rollout at this time. We will announce via Message center when we are ready to proceed. We apologize for any inconvenience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing integration of the Microsoft Purview SDK into the Microsoft Agent Framework SDK to help organizations build secure, enterprise-ready AI agents. This integration enables developers to apply Microsoft Purview compliance and data protection capabilities directly within agent runtimes. It extends existing security and governance controls to custom-built AI agents across Microsoft 365 workloads.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 534609.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will announce via Message center when we are ready to proceed.\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizations building or planning to build AI agents using the Microsoft Agent Framework SDK\n• Admins and developers responsible for security, compliance, and governance of custom AI agents\n• Tenants with Microsoft Purview licenses that enable SDK usage\n\nWhat will happen\n• Developers can embed Microsoft Purview SDK controls directly into AI agent runtimes built with the Agent Framework SDK.\n• AI agents can respect existing Microsoft Purview compliance configurations, such as data protection and policy enforcement, when accessing organizational data.\n• There is no change to user experiences in Microsoft 365 services.\n• The integration is not enabled automatically; it requires developer implementation within custom agents.\n• Existing Microsoft Purview policies and configurations remain unchanged unless explicitly used by the agent.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo immediate admin action is required if your organization is not developing AI agents.\nIf your organization builds AI agents:\n• Share this update with your development and security teams.\n• Review Microsoft Purview SDK documentation to understand supported compliance capabilities.\n• Validate how existing Purview policies should be applied within agent workflows.\n\nLearn more: Building Secure, Enterprise-Ready AI Agents with Purview SDK and Agent Framework | Microsoft Security Community Blog\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes this change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. When developers implement the Purview SDK, AI agents can access customer data under the governance of Microsoft Purview compliance policies, such as data protection and policy enforcement.\nDoes this change introduce or significantly modify AI or agent capabilities that interact with customer data?Yes. The change enables custom AI agents built with the Agent Framework SDK to respect customer's Microsoft Purview compliance controls while interacting with the customer data.\nDoes this change alter how admins can monitor, report on, or demonstrate compliance?Yes. When AI agents use the Purview SDK, compliance enforcement and related activities may be reflected through existing Microsoft Purview monitoring and reporting experiences.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1302905","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1307982","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams Town halls: Upload custom backgrounds in Manage what attendees see","desc":"Updated October 19, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo help organizations deliver more polished and branded town hall events, Microsoft Teams is introducing the ability for organizers and presenters to upload custom background images in the Manage what attendees see experience. This enhancement allows teams to replace default backgrounds with branded visuals—such as company logos or event-specific designs—so presenters and shared content appear consistently on brand for attendees. This feature is available for Teams events organizers with a Teams Enterprise license. This update applies to Teams for Windows desktop and Mac desktop.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 561493.\n[When this will happen]\n• Targeted Release: Rollout begins in early June 2026 (previously late May) and is expected to complete by early June 2026 (previously late May).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in early June 2026 and is expected to complete by early November 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizers and presenters of Teams town hall events\n• Users assigned a Teams Premium license\n• Tenants using Manage what attendees see in town halls\n\nWhat will happen\n• Organizers and presenters can upload custom background images directly within the Manage what attendees see experience.\n• Uploaded backgrounds appear behind presenters and shared content in supported town hall layouts.\n• JPEG and PNG image formats are supported, with recommended resolution guidance shown during upload.\n• Custom backgrounds appear alongside existing default background options in the background picker.\n• The feature is enabled by default for eligible users and applies only to town hall events where Manage what attendees see is enabled.\n• There is no change to standard Teams meetings or webinars.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No admin action is required before rollout.\n• Consider notifying users who organize or present town halls about this new capability.\n• Prepare branded background images that align with your organization’s visual identity guidelines.\n• Update internal documentation or event playbooks if you provide guidance on hosting town halls.\n• Optionally, run a test town hall event to familiarize presenters with the upload flow and attendee experience.\n\nLearn more: Customize the event screen - Manage what attendees see in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Support\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change store new customer data?Yes. Uploaded custom background images are stored as part of the Teams town hall event configuration.\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed or accessed?Yes. Background images are rendered behind presenters and shared content during the live event for attendees.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1307982","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1266027","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: New experience when users minimize the meeting window","desc":"Updated October 19, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are improving the Microsoft Teams meeting experience when the active meeting window is minimized. This update helps users stay engaged in meetings while multitasking across other apps. With this change, users can perform key in-meeting actions—such as raising their hand and sending reactions—without restoring the full Teams meeting window. Users can also choose between two different minimized views, depending on how much meeting context they want to keep visible while they work.\nThis change does not affect the experience when users are sharing their screen in a Teams meeting.\nThis message applies to Teams for Windows desktop and Teams for Mac desktop. It is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557179.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Targeted Release: Rollout begins mid-May 2026 (previously early May) and is expected to complete by late May 2026 (previously early May).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We expect to complete rollout by end of October, 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n• All users who join and participate in Microsoft Teams meetings.\n\nWhat will happen:\n• When users minimize a Teams meeting window, a new minimized meeting experience appears automatically.\n• Users can raise their hand and send reactions without restoring the full Microsoft Teams meeting window.\n• Users can choose between two minimized views:• Expanded view: Displays up to four participant videos.\n\n• • Compact view: Does not display participant video and takes up less screen space.\n\n•\n• The feature is enabled by default and does not require any admin configuration.\n• There is no change to the meeting experience while screen sharing.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• No action is required.\n• Consider notifying users and helpdesk staff about the new minimized meeting views in Microsoft Teams.\n• Update internal training or support documentation if it references Teams meeting window behavior.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1266027","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-561322","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot in PowerPoint for Government clouds","desc":"<p>Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot uses your files, meetings, emails, and more to help shape content and iterate quickly, and it connects to your brand kit so you can apply branded templates, insert brand approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot–licensed users.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561322","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-542181","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit with Copilot in Excel (Web, Win32, Mac) - GCC","desc":"<p>Edit with Copilot lets you build and edit workbooks side by side with Copilot. When you're updating budgets, creating financial models, or analyzing data, Copilot uses Excel's most powerful tools like tables, charts, PivotTables, and formulas to help you get the job done.</p>","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-17","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542181","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-566701","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit your document with Copilot in PowerPoint in Government Clouds","desc":"<p>Copilot in PowerPoint helps you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural language—right inside your deck. Start a new presentation or build on an existing one by asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design, all while preserving your formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot can also connect to your brand kit to apply branded templates, insert brand-approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) users.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-29","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566701","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571305","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Support for sensitive documents protected with Microsoft Purview Information Protection (MPIP)","desc":"<p>Unblock users from upload files with Microsoft Purview Information Protection (MPIP) sensitivity labels to Copilot Studio agents deployed on the M365 channel. With this support agents can process content based on the user's/agents account permissions, with label protections enforced end-to-end.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-19","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571305","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570845","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention for Microsoft Cowork","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) is expanding to Microsoft Cowork, enabling data security admins to use a single policy across Microsoft 365 Copilot and Cowork. The integration helps protect sensitive AI interactions by preventing the use of labeled knowledge sources, blocking prompts that contain supported sensitive information types, and restricting sensitive prompts from being sent to Bing for web search.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570845","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570666","title":"Outlook: Duplicate events in Outlook mobile apps","desc":"<p>We are adding the ability to duplicate an event. Simply go to the event details and select \"duplicate event\"</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570666","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570665","title":"Outlook: Send availability in Outlook mobile apps","desc":"<p>We are bringing back send availability on both iOS and Android. iOS users will now also be able to access more of this feature via keyboard and voiceover.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570665","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-567884","title":"Microsoft Teams: External phone call routing (GCC High, DoD)","desc":"<p>External call routing will provide users the ability to redirect all external phone calls to either voicemail or their unanswered settings.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-17","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567884","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-562412","title":"Microsoft Viva: Agent metrics for custom reporting in Insights analyst workbench","desc":"<p>Unlock deeper insights into Copilot agent adoption with flexible, self-serve analytics. Insights global and partition analysts can access and combine granular agent usage metrics with agent and organizational attributes to uncover agent adoption trends, export and customize reporting, and drive more informed decisions, without relying on predefined dashboards.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-14","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562412","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562353","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Session and Response Sharing in M365 Copilot","desc":"<p>Session and Response Sharing let Microsoft 365 Copilot users share Copilot chat content through a link. Session Sharing shares a full chat session, while Response Sharing shares a single Copilot response. The shared content opens as a read-only view, and recipients can continue from it in their own Copilot chat. This gives Copilot users an easier and more controlled way to share useful Copilot outputs with coworkers instead of copying and pasting. It helps teams reuse work, share context, and collaborate more efficiently while keeping sharing within organizational controls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-16","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562353","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-562534","title":"Microsoft Teams: Front-of-room view control for Town Hall in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>When a Teams Rooms on Android is invited as a meeting presenter, the front-of-room display defaults to the attendee view. Presenters always have full control from the console, including green room and off-stage management, and can switch the front-of-room display to presenter view without impacting attendees. Available in Teams Rooms Pro.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-30","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562534","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-559107","title":"Microsoft Viva: [Engage] Pinned resources & related communities in Teams for iOS","desc":"<p>Users will be able to see a community's pinned resources and related communities in Teams for iOS.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558922","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced media quality for Direct Guest Join","desc":"<p>You’ll notice&nbsp;media quality improvements including support for up to 16 participant videos (4×4 grid)&nbsp;available in May&nbsp;and simulcast streaming&nbsp;(June)&nbsp;when using Direct Guest Join.&nbsp;These updates make cross‑platform meetings more immersive and reliable when joining Teams meetings from Zoom, Google Meet, or Cisco devices.&nbsp;Direct Guest Join is not yet available for Google Meet on Teams Rooms for Android.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-26","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558922","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-500378","title":"Microsoft Teams: Front-of-room view control for Town Hall in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>When a Teams Rooms on Android is invited as a meeting presenter, the front-of-room display defaults to the attendee view. Presenters always have full control from the console, including green room and off-stage management, and can switch the front-of-room display to presenter view without impacting attendees. Available in Teams Rooms Pro. Note: An earlier listing incorrectly stated this feature applied to webinars as well. That experience is still in development and will be released later in 2026.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500378","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-502525","title":"Microsoft Teams: Simplified device settings for voice and face recognition on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>It's easier for admins to enable the benefits of intelligent audio and video and Copilot for users in Teams Rooms through a new user interface and admin settings. These new settings, on the device and in the Pro Management portal, simplify configuration and remove the requirement to use PowerShell, offering improved visibility across rooms.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-08","modified":"2026-10-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502525","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-576633","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Create multiple budget drafts for what-if analysis","desc":"<p><strong>How to enable the feature</strong></p> <p>This feature is applicable to Project Operations Core and Project Operations Integrated with ERP. In feature management, enable the feature <strong>Enable Multiple Project Budget Drafts.</strong></p> <p><strong>Problem</strong></p> <p>Project managers were limited to maintaining a single draft version of a budget that had to be submitted for approval.</p> <p>In real-world planning scenarios, project managers often need to evaluate multiple budget alternatives based on different assumptions such as resource mix, pricing, timelines, and cost structures. However, the absence of native support for multiple draft versions forced them to take the data outside Project Operations, perform offline analysis, and manually reconcile changes back into the system.</p> <p>This approach was not only time-consuming but also introduced risks of inconsistencies, version control issues, and manual errors, ultimately reducing productivity and confidence in budget accuracy.</p> <p><strong>Solution</strong></p> <p>This feature introduces support for multiple draft budgets, enabling project managers to create, maintain, and iterate on alternative budget versions directly within Project Operations. By allowing multiple drafts to coexist, project managers can now experiment with different planning scenarios without losing prior work or overriding existing drafts. This serves as a foundational capability for more advanced budget management scenarios.</p> <p>Additionally, the user interface has been enhanced to provide clear visibility into multiple draft versions, making it easier for project managers to navigate, review, and manage different budget iterations efficiently.</p> <p>This capability also sets the groundwork for upcoming enhancements, including in-product comparison across draft budgets, which will further streamline decision-making and scenario evaluation. We call that what-if analysis of a project budget.</p> <p><strong>Impact</strong></p> <ul> <li>Enables creation and management of multiple draft budget versions within the system.</li> <li>Eliminates the need for offline analysis and manual re-entry of budget changes.</li> <li>Reduces the risk of manual errors, inconsistencies, and version control challenges.</li> <li>Improves planning agility by allowing exploration of multiple budget scenarios.</li> <li>Enhances overall efficiency and productivity for project managers.</li> <li>Establishes a foundation for future capabilities such as draft comparison and advanced budget analytics.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Project managers creating project budgets, whether from estimates, contracts, quotes, or from scratch, were limited to a single draft version that had to be submitted for approval. When they needed to explore or compare alternative budget scenarios, the only option was to take Dynamics 365 Project Operations data, perform offline analysis, and manually update changes back into the system. This process was time-consuming, error-prone, and inefficient.</p> <p>This feature introduces support for multiple draft budgets, enabling project managers to create and manage alternative budget versions directly within Project Operations. This lays the foundation for in-product comparison of draft budgets, which will be introduced in a subsequent release.</p> <p>To support this capability, the user interface has been enhanced to allow project managers to easily view and manage multiple draft versions of a budget. As a result, this feature enables creation of multiple draft budget versions, eliminates the need for offline analysis and manual re-entry, reduces risk of manual errors, and improves efficiency and decision-making for project managers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576633","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576733","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable Change Order Management","desc":"<p>This capability provides a structured, auditable process for creating, evaluating, and approving change orders on active project contracts.</p> <p>You can capture updates to scope, pricing, resources, or timelines and apply those approved changes directly to the contract with full traceability. The system records the rationale, financial impact, and approval history for each change order, supports version comparison between original and updated contract details, and updates downstream elements such as billing schedules, budgets, and project schedule.</p> <p>This workflow ensures accuracy, visibility, and compliance across sales, delivery, and finance teams throughout the contract lifecycle.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Change Order Management provides organizations with a governed and transparent way to handle contract updates, eliminating the risks created by manual workarounds. By capturing all scope, pricing, resource, and timeline changes within a structured review and approval process, teams prevent billing leakage, margin erosion, and financial inaccuracies. Automated audit trails, version comparisons, and downstream updates strengthen compliance and contractual accountability while reducing rework and operational confusion. Cross-functional alignment improves as sales, delivery, and finance operate from a single, consistent source of truth. This capability enhances forecasting accuracy, reinforces customer trust, and ensures protection of project profitability throughout the lifecycle of the contract.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576733","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576737","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Support subscription billing for Project Operations","desc":"<p>Core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Recurring billing</strong>: Create and manage subscription contracts with flexible billing schedules (monthly, quarterly, annually).</li> <li><strong>Automated invoice generation</strong>: Automatically create invoices based on predefined schedules; supports batch processing.</li> <li><strong>Flexible pricing models</strong>: Standard, tiered-based pricing; consolidate multiple billing lines into one invoice.</li> <li><strong>Integration</strong>: Seamless flow between CE and finance and operations for invoicing and accounting; supports Dataverse-based configuration.</li> <li><strong>Advanced scenarios</strong>: Fee journal-based billing for project contracts, subscription hold or termination management, and refund handling.</li> </ul> <p>This feature is enabled using a feature flag.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Organizations increasingly adopt subscription-based models to create predictable revenue streams and improve customer experience. This feature drives efficiency by automating recurring invoicing and reducing manual intervention. It improves financial control, supports flexibility, and positions businesses to scale subscription offerings and forecast monthly recurring revenue (MRR) more accurately.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576737","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576883","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - View budget details in left navigation","desc":"<p>This feature enhances the Project Budget management experience by improving visibility, usability, and contextual clarity when working with project budgets and budget versions. It addresses limitations of the existing Project form Budget tab and reduces ambiguity around budget version actions.</p> <p>Since this is a navigation addition, the Budget section is available by default.</p> <p><strong>Improved budget visibility</strong></p> <ul> <li>Budget information is presented in a dedicated, optimized experience that overcomes space constraints of the Project form.</li> <li>Key budget attributes and financial details are clearly visible without excessive navigation.</li> <li>The layout helps project managers quickly understand the current state of the project budget.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Contextual budget version actions</strong></p> <ul> <li>Budget version actions are available directly within the budget context.</li> <li>The active or selected budget version is clearly indicated before any action is performed.</li> <li>This provides confidence that actions are applied to the intended budget version.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Simplified navigation and usability</strong></p> <ul> <li>Reduced dependency on the Project ribbon for budget-related tasks.</li> <li>Actions are aligned closely with the data being viewed.</li> <li>Improved usability lowers the learning curve and increases efficiency.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <ul> <li>Reduces confusion and errors when managing multiple budget versions.</li> <li>Improves productivity by minimizing unnecessary navigation.</li> <li>Enables more informed financial decision-making.</li> <li>Enhances overall user satisfaction and trust in the system.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Project managers can now view budget information in a more focused and intuitive experience, overcoming the space limitations of the Project form’s Budget tab. Key budget details are easier to access, improving visibility and understanding of project financials. Budget version actions are now clearly contextualized, reducing confusion about which version an action applies to. These improvements help minimize errors, improve usability, and enable more confident and efficient budget management.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576883","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576873","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable subcontractor vendor invoice matching to actuals","desc":"<p>When you enable the <strong>Enable subcontractor vendor invoice matching to actuals for Project Operations integrated with ERP</strong> setting, you activate this feature.</p> <p><strong>Key capabilities:</strong></p> <ul> <li><p>This feature enables procurement managers, project accountants, and accounts payable users in finance and operations apps to efficiently identify, review, and match project actuals generated from subcontracting activities against incoming vendor invoices. By providing visibility into the underlying actual cost transactions, users can validate that the invoice accurately represents the work performed and the costs incurred before approving vendor invoice.</p> </li> <li><p>The capability supports invoice validation and exception management by allowing users to compare vendor invoice amounts with received services, posted actuals, and project cost data, instead of to all product receipts.</p> </li> <li><p>By establishing a direct relationship between vendor invoices and subcontracting actuals, the feature significantly reduces the need for manual reconciliation activities.</p> </li> <li><p>The feature streamlines the end-to-end subcontracting procure-to-pay process by creating a more connected workflow between procurement, project operations, and finance teams. Organizations can achieve faster invoice review and approval cycles, improve financial controls, increase transparency into subcontracting costs, and ensure that vendor payments are aligned with actual project consumption and contractual commitments.</p> </li> <li><p>In addition, having actuals available during invoice matching improves auditability and traceability. Finance teams can easily demonstrate how vendor invoice amounts were derived, what project transactions they relate to, and whether they fall within approved project and procurement budgets, thereby strengthening compliance and governance controls.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enables subcontractor vendor invoice matching to actuals for Dynamics 365 Project Operations integrated with ERP and enhances financial accuracy and operational efficiency in subcontracting processes by enabling vendor invoice matching against actual costs. It reduces manual reconciliation, minimizes invoicing errors, and ensures compliance with cost tracking requirements. As a result, organizations can improve transparency, strengthen vendor relationships, and accelerate the procure-to-pay cycle.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576873","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2027","gaSort":202708,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/pro/subcontracting/subconpurchaseorders#three-way-matching-for-subcontract-vendor-invoice-lines"},{"id":"rm-576634","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Administrator experiences - Use industry templates to set up autonomous contact centers","desc":"<p>This release introduces industry-specific templates that simplify the creation and deployment of autonomous contact centers. Organizations can start with a preconfigured template in Copilot Service admin center &gt; <strong>Service Operations Agent</strong> and deploy an autonomous customer service experience in just a few clicks, significantly reducing the setup effort required to design agents, workflows, and service journeys from the ground up.</p> <p>The templates are built around common industry scenarios and best practices, helping organizations quickly establish operational autonomous contact centers while maintaining flexibility for customization as business needs evolve. Users can leverage these templates as a foundation and extend them to meet their specific customer service requirements.</p> <p>These templates enable organizations to rapidly launch autonomous contact centers, reduce implementation complexity, and begin delivering AI-powered customer support with minimal configuration effort.</p> <p>In this release, templates are available for the retail and telecom industries.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Accelerate the deployment of autonomous contact centers with prebuilt industry templates designed to help organizations get up and running in minutes rather than weeks. These ready-to-use templates reduce the complexity of designing autonomous customer service experiences from scratch, enabling businesses to quickly realize the benefits of AI-powered customer engagement, automated issue resolution, and around-the-clock service availability.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576634","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576636","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Copilot and AI innovation - Use agentic simulations to evaluate contact center setup","desc":"<p><strong>Agentic simulations</strong> are an AI-driven capability of Service Operations Agent that enable organizations to evaluate how their contact center behaves under realistic customer conditions before those conditions occur in production.</p> <p>Administrators define simulation scenarios using natural-language prompts. Agentic simulations then generate realistic synthetic conversations, runs them end-to-end through the configured contact center, and calculates the contact center KPIs.</p> <p><strong>What problems it helps solve</strong></p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Readiness of self-service experiences</strong>: Assess how AI agents handle real customer intents, variations in behavior, and edge cases.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Effectiveness of assisted service flows</strong>: Validate routing, assignment logic, and service representative experience in human-assisted scenarios.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Confidence in scale and load readiness</strong>: Understand how configurations and operations perform under realistic volume and fix any reliability and latency issues.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Preparedness of service representatives</strong>: Enable safe practice and evaluation using realistic customer interactions without impacting live customers.</p> </li> </ul> <p><strong>Key capabilities</strong></p> <ul> <li>Natural-language prompt interface for defining simulation scenarios</li> <li>Simulation of varied customer intents, personas, and behaviors</li> <li>End-to-end execution across AI agents, routing, and configurations</li> <li>Out-of-the-box KPI dashboards and scorecards</li> <li>Reusable and saved prompts, including canned scenarios</li> <li>Safe, pre-production execution with no impact on live customers</li> </ul> <p>Agentic simulations are currently available for the voice channel in the English language only. They support flows without Dual-Tone Multi-Frequency (DTMF)-based menu interactions and up to five conversations in a simulation.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Every contact center decision, such as deploying an AI agent, adjusting routing, onboarding new staff, or preparing for higher volumes, ultimately answers the same question:<br> “Will this work as expected when real customers arrive?”</p> <p>Agentic simulations provide a clear, data-backed answer before changes reach production.</p> <p>By generating realistic customer conversations and running them end-to-end through the contact center, organizations can see how their self-service, assisted service, and operational setup behave under real-world conditions. Instead of relying on assumptions, limited testing, or post-go-live corrections, teams gain measurable insight into experience quality, readiness, and scale.</p> <p>This feature transforms how contact centers operate:</p> <ul> <li>Experience quality improves because AI agents and service representatives are evaluated against realistic scenarios.</li> <li>Operational risk decreases because configuration and routing issues are identified early.</li> <li>Time to value accelerates because onboarding, training, and change validation happen faster.</li> <li>Scale becomes predictable because load behavior is understood before demand increases.</li> </ul> <p>Agentic simulations turn uncertainty into confidence, helping organizations ship changes faster, train teams better, and deliver consistent customer experiences at scale.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576636","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"July CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/administer/configure-simulation-agent"},{"id":"rm-576741","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Enable import of customer payment remittance advice for processing and settlement","desc":"<p>This feature includes the following functionalities:</p> <ul> <li>Automated customer payment and remittance advice import, scanning, and mapping using AI processing in the integrated Power Platform environment.</li> <li>Matching remittance advice data with data in Dynamics 365 Finance.</li> <li>Seamless integration of remittance advice details into Dynamics 365 Finance customer payment journals and the settlement process.</li> <li>Reports that provide insights into payment and settlement statuses, outstanding invoices, and overall cash flow.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The ability to import remittance advice streamlines the accounts receivable process by enabling businesses to efficiently manage and reconcile payments from customers. By automating the import, scanning, and consumption of remittance advice data, businesses save valuable time and resources. This capability improves cash flow management and financial reporting.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576741","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"March CY2027"},{"id":"rm-576738","title":"Dynamics 365 Sustainability: Use up‑to‑date regulatory templates","desc":"<p>This feature introduces updated regulatory standard and framework templates, refreshed on a bimonthly cadence. The updates include revised template structures, concepts, and mappings that reflect the latest changes, helping ensure assessments remain aligned with current disclosure expectations.</p> <p>After the updated regulatory templates are installed from the Power Platform admin center, customers can use these refreshed templates as a reliable starting point when configuring assessments and external disclosures. The updated mappings reduce the need for manual adjustments and reconfiguration as standards evolve, improving consistency across reports and reporting periods.</p> <p>By keeping regulatory structures and concepts current, customers can have more accurate, efficient, and dependable external reporting without tracking or implementing changes manually.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Sustainability standards and regulatory frameworks continue to evolve, creating ongoing maintenance challenges for external reporting teams. This release helps organizations stay current by providing refreshed regulatory templates that reflect the latest structural and conceptual changes. By starting from updated, standardized templates, customers can reduce manual rework, improve consistency across disclosures, and increase confidence in regulatory alignment.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sustainability"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576738","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-576638","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Enhancements to subscription billing","desc":"<p><strong>Performance improvements for subscription billing unbilled revenue</strong></p> <p>Performance is a common request within subscription billing, and we have focused on that request. This feature enhances the subscription billing unbilled revenue mass processing by introducing multithreaded execution. Multithreaded processing reduces batch execution time, minimizes system contention, and improves reliability during peak billing and close cycles. This enables customers to process large volumes of unbilled revenue records more efficiently, avoid operational bottlenecks, and confidently run concurrent batch jobs supporting scalability, performance, and overall customer satisfaction.</p> <p><strong>Performance improvements when generating sales order invoice with subscription billing</strong></p> <p>Changes are being made to improve sales order invoice generation performance, lower system load, and enhance scalability during high-volume billing runs. This leads to faster batch execution, reduced contention with parallel processes, and improved reliability of subscription billing operations for enterprise customers.</p> <p><strong>Multi-element revenue allocation logic correction during updates, termination</strong></p> <p>Correcting multi-element revenue allocation behavior during terminations prevents residual deferred revenue balances, ensures accurate financial reporting, and maintains alignment between billing events and revenue allocation logic. This reduces manual General ledger adjustments, minimizes audit risk, and improves confidence in subscription billing for customers using complex, multi-element arrangements at scale.</p> <p>This feature corrects multi-element revenue allocation behavior during billing schedule updates and terminations to ensure accurate General ledger distributions. When a billing schedule is terminated, with or without credit, the system will correctly apply multi-element revenue allocation logic to clear remaining deferred contract revenue account balances. Credit transactions generated during termination will be treated like standard invoices and allocated based on SSP, while non-credit terminations automatically generate adjustment entries to fully clear deferred balances in line with multi-element revenue allocation principles.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>These enhancements collectively strengthen subscription billing performance, scalability, and financial accuracy, addressing both operational efficiency and accounting integrity for enterprise-scale customers. The performance improvements to unbilled revenue mass processing and sales order invoice generation reduce batch execution times, lower system load, and minimize contention during high-volume billing and financial close cycles. By improving parallel processing and execution efficiency, customers can reliably process large subscription volumes, run concurrent batch jobs, and meet tight billing and close timelines with greater predictability and stability.</p> <p>In parallel, the correction to multi-element revenue allocation logic during billing schedule updates and terminations ensure accurate and compliant revenue recognition across the subscription lifecycle. Deferred contract revenue balances are now correctly cleared during terminations, with or without credit, and credit transactions are allocated consistently based on standalone selling price (SSP). This eliminates residual deferred balances, reduces manual General Ledger adjustments, and lowers audit and reconciliation risk.</p> <p>Together, these improvements deliver a faster, more reliable, and financially accurate subscription billing experience, reducing operational overhead, improving close efficiency, and increasing customer confidence in managing complex, high-volume subscription models.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576638","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/accounts-receivable/sub-bill-perf-improve"},{"id":"rm-576731","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable purchase orders with item requirements","desc":"<p>Activate this feature by turning on the <strong>Enable purchase orders and item reservations for stocked items in Project Operations integrated with ERP</strong> feature within the <strong>Feature management</strong> workspace on the finance and operations architecture. When you enable this feature, you get the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Purchase order creation</strong>: Project managers can create purchase orders directly from item requirements. This capability enables procurement of stocked materials that align with project needs.</li> <li><strong>Option to automatically create item requirements from purchase orders</strong>: Project managers who don't usually work with sales orders can get the benefits of item requirements while managing only purchase orders.</li> <li><strong>Cost recording at receipt</strong>: You can record project costs when you receive the product, instead of waiting for the vendor to invoice. This capability improves financial accuracy and timeliness.</li> <li><strong>Master planning integration</strong>: You can integrate with Dynamics 365 ERP master planning to autogenerate planned purchases or transfer orders based on project forecasts.</li> </ul> <p>This feature will initially be available as a preview starting with the 10.0.49 release.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The purchase orders using item requirements feature in Dynamics 365 Project Operations integrated with ERP enhances operational efficiency and financial accuracy by automating the procurement process for stocked materials tied to project needs.</p> <p>This feature reduces manual effort and procurement delays by automatically generating item requirements from purchase orders. It improves cost visibility and budget control by ensuring real-time material consumption and cost recognition during product receipt.</p> <p>Material usage synchronizes across Dynamics 365 Finance and Project Operations through seamless integration with Microsoft Dataverse through dual-write, which maintains data consistency. The system also supports three-way matching between purchase orders, receipts, and vendor invoices to ensure compliance and reduce financial discrepancies.</p> <p>You can reserve stock for project-specific usage in Dataverse to ensure material availability, which minimizes project delays and enhances delivery timelines.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576731","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576801","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable time phasing of quote and contract lines","desc":"<p>With this feature, the system automatically updates the correct sales and cost prices in quotes and contracts based on the effective date. The system calculates prices using weighted average prices for both quote line details and contract line details, so pricing calculations are precise and reliable. This automation greatly reduces the manual work needed to track and update prices. It also lowers the risk of errors and discrepancies in pricing.</p> <p>The feature also lets you keep a detailed audit trail of all changes you make to quotes and contracts. This audit trail provides full transparency and traceability, so you can trust the accuracy and integrity of your pricing information.</p> <p>You can view exact totals at any point in time, showing all current and historical pricing data. This real-time visibility into totals makes contract management easier and helps ensure that you accurately account for all financial aspects.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Managing time-phased price changes for labor, expenses, and materials within quotes and contracts can be challenging. This enhancement ensures that any price changes automatically take effect from their effective date. You get accurate and up-to-date pricing without manual intervention.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576801","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"March CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/pro/sales/create-estimate-quote-line-sales"},{"id":"rm-576642","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Improve the project quote experience","desc":"<p>The improvements to project quote provide usability enhancements designed to modernize and streamline the experience. The goal is to reduce unnecessary complexity, improve clarity, and enable users to work more efficiently when creating and managing quotes.</p> <p>The updated interface features an optimized layout and improved use of screen space, providing a cleaner, more efficient workspace for viewing and editing both project and product lines. You can access more relevant information at once with less visual clutter and fewer navigation steps, resulting in a more intuitive and productive workflow.</p> <p>In addition, context-based insights are now surfaced directly within the quote, highlighting important details such as pricing indicators, estimate breakdowns, and potential data inconsistencies. These insights guide you toward more accurate quoting decisions and reduce the time needed to validate contract and estimate information.</p> <p>Collectively, these enhancements deliver a smoother, more responsive, and more intuitive quoting experience, helping sales and project teams complete quotes with greater speed, accuracy, and confidence.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The enhanced project quote experience helps you work smarter and faster. By cutting unnecessary steps, simplifying the interface, and putting key insights right where you need them, you can make confident pricing decisions and finish quotes quickly. This means higher productivity, fewer mistakes, and faster turnaround for your business.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576642","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576730","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Speed up time phasing of estimates","desc":"<p>This update enhances the Time Phasing of Estimates experience by delivering significant performance improvements across loading, recalculation, and user interactions. You can now work more efficiently with large estimates, complex distributions, and multiline quotes without experiencing delays. These improvements ensure smoother navigation when adjusting phased values, faster response times when recalculating totals, and a more reliable experience when viewing historical and future estimate periods. The feature continues to support accurate time-phased cost and sales prices of the Quote Line and Contract Line estimates while offering a noticeably faster and more seamless workflow.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You’ll spend less time planning and adjusting estimates, even when you’re handling complex or high-volume project data. Faster recalculations and smoother interactions mean your team can move quickly and keep projects on track without wasting resources.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576730","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576878","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Use what-if analysis on estimates","desc":"<p>This feature introduces a robust what-if analysis capability for estimates that enables you to model scenarios and evaluate their impact on key financial goals.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Scenario modeling</strong>: Use existing quotes to simulate scenarios and assess their effects on goals like profitability and gross margins.</li> <li><strong>Goal-oriented analysis</strong>: Select specific goals and target values to model pricing changes effectively.</li> <li><strong>Dynamic pricing dimensions</strong>: Adjust key pricing dimensions to explore how changes influence the selected goals.</li> <li><strong>Informed decision-making</strong>: Review multiple what-if analysis models, compare outcomes, and apply the most suitable option to the quote.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature empowers you to simulate various estimation scenarios by adjusting key pricing dimensions, providing real-time insights into quote estimations. You can explore different strategies and quickly identify the most effective path to achieve your financial goals. By manipulating factors such as price, discount rates, and cost reductions, you can optimize profitability and align quotes with specific sales targets.</p> <p>Automated calculations save time, reduce errors, and enhance negotiation flexibility, enabling sales teams to confidently tailor proposals to client needs while safeguarding their bottom line. This ensures that every quote meets both customer satisfaction and business objectives.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576878","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"March CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/sales/quote-what-if-analysis"},{"id":"rm-576637","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Seller experiences - Clone and share Sales Development agent configuration across teams","desc":"<p>As a sales leader, you can configure a Sales Development agent once, then share or clone its configuration across your organization. Distribute the agent’s playbook, guidelines, guardrails, and settings to other business units to provide a consistent experience across sales teams.</p> <p>The feature supports these capabilities:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Export a configuration</strong>: In Teams, ask the source agent to package its configuration into a file. For example, enter Export your configuration.</li> <li><strong>Import a configuration</strong>: Attach the exported file to a new agent, then ask the agent to apply the configuration.</li> <li><strong>Create a one-time copy</strong>: The copied configuration is a snapshot, not a synchronized connection. Changes made later to the source agent aren’t automatically applied to the target agent.</li> </ul> <p>Knowledge sources, such as uploaded documents, FAQs, and URLs, aren’t included in the exported configuration. Add them directly to the target agent after importing the configuration.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Scaling your sales operations just got easier. Instead of manually configuring each Sales Development agent from scratch, you can now set up an agent once with your organization's best practices and guardrails, then share or clone it across your entire team. This means faster deployment, consistent outreach to prospects, and more time for your sellers to build relationships instead of repetitive work. Whether you're expanding to new markets or rolling out agents across multiple business units, you'll maintain quality and compliance while reducing the time it takes to get your agent up and running.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576637","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"August CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/sales/sales-dev-agent/copy-configuration"},{"id":"rm-576742","title":"Dynamics 365 Sustainability: Configure granular reporting‑period locking","desc":"<p>This feature provides granular and configurable reporting‑period locking within sustainability data management. Customers can independently lock data ingestion, calculations, and external reporting, enabling scenarios such as restatements or recalculations in closed periods without requiring a full unlock of all data and processes. The locking model allows organizations to define how locks apply across organizational units, facilities, scopes, and categories, including Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3, providing precise control over which data can be modified across complex organizational and reporting structures.</p> <p>The feature is automatically enabled and can be configured from the settings section of the product. Users can apply targeted locks with clearly defined boundaries to control when data can be modified across ingestion, calculation, and reporting workflows.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>As sustainability data volumes grow and reporting cycles become more regulated, organizations need stronger controls to protect reported results while still supporting corrections and restatements. This release provides greater precision over when and how data can change, reducing the risk of unintended modifications to closed reporting periods. By strengthening governance and auditability, customers can maintain trust in reported data while supporting controlled adjustments when required.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sustainability"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576742","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576756","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Omnichannel customer experiences - Use ML-based sensitive data redaction for human interactions","desc":"<p>Dynamics 365 Contact Center introduces large language model (LLM)‑based sensitive data redaction for human‑to‑human interactions, allowing administrators to automatically redact PCI data shared during live conversations between customers and customer service representatives.</p> <p>The system uses LLMs to identify sensitive data based on conversational context, not just patterns, across both voice and digital channels. When sensitive data such as a credit card number, PIN, or account number is detected, it is replaced with a standardized redaction token (for example, CreditCardNumber:Redacted) before the data is persisted.</p> <p>Redaction is applied consistently across:</p> <ul> <li>Conversation transcripts</li> <li>Call recordings</li> <li>Logs and diagnostic data</li> <li>Analytics outputs derived from conversations</li> </ul> <p>Administrators can configure which PCI data types are redacted, and the system enforces these policies automatically without requiring representatives to pause recordings or change their workflows. This capability helps ensure that sensitive customer data isn't stored while preserving the non‑sensitive conversation context needed for quality assurance, analytics, and operational insights.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Organizations in regulated industries must prevent sensitive payment data from being stored in call recordings, transcripts, logs, or analytics artifacts. Today, customers rely on manual processes or limited rule‑based masking, which increases compliance risk and operational overhead. This feature enables customers to safely use recording, transcription, and AI analytics by ensuring payment card information (PCI) data shared during live conversations between customers and customer service representatives is automatically redacted before storage. As a result, customers can reduce PCI scope, prevent compliance escalations, and confidently adopt advanced contact center capabilities without disrupting agent workflows or customer experience.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576756","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576884","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - Optimize multiple resources with Scheduling Operations Agent","desc":"<p>This release expands the optimization capabilities of the Scheduling Operations Agent to include multiple resources. The agent considers the availability of the resources, their current schedules, and unscheduled requirements. It suggests a schedule that honors configured constraints and optimizes it according to the selected goal. Dispatchers can review and compare the proposed schedules with the current schedules before applying changes.</p> <p>New capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Optimize schedules for up to 5 resources directly from the schedule board.</li> <li>Optimize schedules for up to 30 resources using an optimization plan.</li> <li>Create custom goals and weight objectives.</li> <li>Create custom optimization scopes to use with your optimization plans.</li> </ul> <p>These capabilities build on the existing public preview of the Scheduling Operations Agent and will be automatically enabled for all organizations that have the agent enabled. Learn more at <a href=\"https://aka.ms/soa\">Scheduling Operations Agent documentation</a>.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Optimize multiple resources with the Scheduling Operations Agent (SOA). Schedule up to five resources directly from the schedule board or Copilot or perform ad-hoc optimizations for up to 30 resources using an optimization plan. This feature streamlines scheduling, improves efficiency, and supports better resource management.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576884","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/soa-overview"},{"id":"rm-576740","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Delay settlement from journal posting","desc":"<p>The <strong>Delay settlement from journal posting</strong> feature addresses a critical pain point in payment processing. Traditionally, payment journal posting and settlement are tightly coupled, meaning any settlement error blocks the entire payment posting. This can cause operational delays, increased manual intervention, and business risk.</p> <p>With this feature:</p> <ul> <li>Payments are no longer blocked by settlement errors. Valid payments post successfully, even if settlement fails.</li> <li>Operational efficiency improves by reducing manual rework and bottlenecks.</li> <li>Cash flow visibility and reporting are enhanced: payments are reflected immediately, while settlements can be managed separately.</li> <li>Exception handling is streamlined: Failed settlements are isolated and can be retried or managed independently, reducing risk and improving auditability.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature ensures organizations process payments reliably and efficiently, reduces operational risk, and provides greater flexibility in managing settlements. It's especially valuable for businesses with high transaction volumes, complex payment scenarios, or a need for robust exception handling.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576740","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"August CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/cash-bank-management/delayed-settlements"},{"id":"rm-576732","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Enable support for KSeF UUID in vendor payment journals (Poland)","desc":"<p>This feature extends the vendor payment journal framework in Dynamics 365 Finance to capture, store, validate, and process KSeF UUIDs associated with vendor invoices issued through Poland’s National e-Invoicing System.</p> <p>It ensures that vendor payments can be linked explicitly to KSeF-registered invoices, supporting compliance, traceability, and downstream reconciliation processes.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enables organizations operating in Poland to capture and process KSeF UUIDs directly within vendor payment journals, ensuring alignment between payment transactions and invoices registered in the National e-Invoicing System (KSeF).</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576732","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576635","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Preview automatic bank reconciliation matching results","desc":"<p>This feature includes the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>Matching preview with an option to approve or reject bank reconciliation matching rule results.</li> <li>Ability to select matching rules for manual review before posting results during the reconciliation process.</li> <li>Pending review screen for users to investigate matching results.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Preview automatic bank reconciliation matching results feature enables users to preview matching results during an automatic bank reconciliation matching process. By allowing users to select rules that require review and user checks, the feature ensures accurate matching and minimizes errors.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576635","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"August CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/cash-bank-management/apply-cash-adv-bank-rec#preview-matching-results-before-posting"},{"id":"rm-576769","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Globalization Studio - Support customer prepayment invoices in e-invoicing","desc":"<p>In the current release wave, we are introducing the following e-invoicing capabilities.</p> <p><strong>Handling of customer prepayment invoices in E-invoicing</strong></p> <p>Global and local customers using <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/accounts-receivable/customer-prepayment-invoice\">Customer prepayment invoices</a> in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance can now process a dedicated electronic invoice type specifically for customer prepayments.</p> <p>For customer prepayment invoices created from sales orders, the system supports generation of electronic invoices as follows:</p> <ul> <li><strong>PEPPOL-based electronic invoices</strong> of type 386 are generated for original customer prepayment invoices.</li> <li>For <strong>Saudi Arabia</strong>: <ul> <li>Electronic invoices of type 386 are generated for original customer prepayment invoices.</li> <li>Reversal prepayment invoices are excluded from electronic invoice generation.</li> <li>Final electronic invoices take prepayment amounts into account and reference the original prepayment invoices.</li> <li>Generation of electronic invoices based on payment transactions is discontinued.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>In the current and upcoming release waves, we continue targeted investments in e‑invoicing to support evolving regulatory mandates and country‑specific requirements. Focus areas include extending coverage for additional clearance and post‑audit scenarios, improving interoperability with government platforms and service providers, and keeping formats and protocols aligned with regulatory changes.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576769","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-576297","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Import task - Assign generic resources to task","desc":"<p>This feature gives project managers control over how resource assignments are handled when importing tasks from one project to another. For each import, project managers can choose to:</p> <p>Not import the team members - Each imported task will lose the assignment information.<br> Use a generic placeholder: Create and assign a generic resource for each assignment in the imported task just like copy project functionality.</p> <p>Tasks without assignments continue to be imported without resources. This ensures that both the task structure and its staffing plan can be reused in the target project.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576297","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-576298","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Import task - Import at a given hierarchy in the task grid","desc":"<p>This feature gives project managers greater control over where imported tasks are placed within a project plan. From the task grid, a project manager can open the context menu for an existing task and select Insert task below. The standard Import Tasks pane then opens and confirms the selected insertion point.</p> <p>Imported tasks are placed immediately after the selected task and at the same level in the task hierarchy. If the selected task has subtasks, the imported tasks are inserted after the entire group of subtasks, preserving the existing hierarchy. When multiple tasks are imported, they remain together in their original order, and their internal structure and dependencies are maintained.</p> <p>The existing Import Tasks command remains unchanged and continues to add imported tasks to the end of the project plan.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576298","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-576743","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Cancel bookings partially from the schedule board","desc":"<p>This feature lets you:</p> <ul> <li>View continuous, multiday booking as blocks of booking for the daily/weekly/monthly view set on the schedule board.</li> <li>Select partial booking on the schedule board.</li> <li>Get cancel and delete options for complete booking and partial booking.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The partial booking modification feature lets resource managers cancel specific portions of a resource booking without deleting and recreating it. This reduces manual effort, improves scheduling accuracy, preserves audit history, and unlocks partially available capacity. The result is more flexible planning, higher usage, and better support for agile, real-world project delivery.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576743","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576763","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Create time entries from assignment and booking views","desc":"<p>Team members can now begin their time entry process from their assigned or booked projects and tasks, making their time entries more aligned with staffing and reducing manual effort overall. When you select time entry creation from the new <strong>Projects and Tasks</strong> view, you're redirected to the time entry grid where your entries are prepopulated based on assigned or booked hours.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature saves you time by eliminating manual entry. It prepopulates details with your current staffing, so you track time more accurately and focus on work that drives greater impact.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576763","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/enhanced-team-member-experience"},{"id":"rm-576735","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Define the accounting date at invoice level","desc":"<p>This feature:</p> <ul> <li>Introduces an accounting date field on the invoice that you can define.</li> <li>Sets a user-defined accounting date on the billed sales actuals, which is passed to finance and operations apps so the transaction is aligned to the same date.</li> <li>Lets the accounting date differ from the transaction or document date to give you control over period alignment.</li> <li>Lets the system fall back to the invoice confirmation date if the accounting date is not defined (existing default behavior).</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can set the accounting date on an invoice separately from the transaction and document dates, so your billed revenue posts to the right financial period. This keeps Project Operations and finance and operations apps in sync, with the same accounting date flowing through for consistent billed sales postings.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576735","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576734","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable on-account category in Dataverse","desc":"<p>This feature is applicable only for Project Operations integrated with ERP environments.</p> <p>Core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Expose Transaction Category field</strong>: Add the Transaction Category field to Retainer and Milestone entities in Microsoft Dataverse.</li> <li><strong>Data synchronization</strong>: <ul> <li>Sync selected categories from Dataverse to finance and operations apps via Data Integrator (DW maps).</li> <li>Align with project category in finance and operations apps for consistency.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p>This feature is enabled using a feature flag.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enables correct categorization of retainers, milestones, and advances for accurate revenue posting in Dynamics 365 Finance. This eliminates manual intervention in finance and operations apps for category management, helping to reduce errors and improve productivity.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576734","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576736","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Improve NTE reliability and validation coverage","desc":"<p>Core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Extends NTE validation beyond time entries to include expense, material, and fixed-price components.</li> <li>Enhances the Invoice Confirmation Service to block confirmation when Total Billed + Unbilled Committed &gt; NTE Amount.</li> <li>Fixes bugs where NTE status fails to update on approval records due to custom plugin conflicts, ensuring deterministic results.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You get consistent control over Not-To-Exceed (NTE) limits across every billable type, so you avoid over-billing and protect revenue. It flags issues before invoices go out, saving you from costly rework, disputes, and end-of-month headaches. Plus, you always see an accurate NTE status on approval records, even when your customers customize their setup.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576736","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576744","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Manage exchange rate variances on cash advances","desc":"<p>When employees receive cash advances in one currency and settle expenses in another (or on different dates), foreign exchange rate differences arise. This feature detects, calculates, and posts realized exchange rate variances between the advance issue rate and the settlement or report rate, ensuring accurate reimbursement amounts, GL impact, and auditability without manual adjustments.</p> <p>This feature ensures that:</p> <ul> <li>Cash advances are based on transaction currency, not just accounting currency.</li> <li>You can calculate and post realized foreign exchange (FX) gains or losses explicitly.</li> <li>Employee (vendor) accounts always net to zero after settlement.</li> <li>Finance teams gain clear visibility and auditability into exchange rate variances.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>With this feature, you can handle exchange rate differences with confidence. This capability makes settling cash advances easier by using the transaction currency instead of just the accounting currency. It also posts any realized foreign exchange gains or losses, so your books stay accurate.</p> <p>You'll see clear benefits: employee accounts always balance to zero after settlement, and your finance team gets full visibility into exchange rate variances. This means fewer reconciliation headaches and better audit readiness, saving time and reducing errors.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576744","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576767","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Perform bulk reconciliation of bookings from UI","desc":"<p>When enabled through feature control, this capability enables multiple selections on the Resource Reconciliation grid. This feature lets you:</p> <ul> <li>Select multiple time durations on the grid.</li> <li>Select multiple users on the grid.</li> <li>Extend the bookings for selections done on the grid.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Bulk reconciliation streamlines the process of aligning bookings and assignments in Dynamics 365 Project Operations by enabling users to reconcile multiple resources and date ranges in a single action. This eliminates repetitive, one-at-a-time reconciliation, significantly reducing administrative effort and time spent on project maintenance. By improving efficiency and accuracy at scale, the feature helps project teams keep plans aligned, reduce inconsistencies, and manage large or complex projects more effectively.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576767","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576768","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Set a default booking method for the schedule board","desc":"<p>When enabled through feature control, this feature lets you configure a default booking method in the Schedule Board settings. The selected default booking method is automatically applied during booking. You can override the default by changing the booking method at the time of booking.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Configurable booking method feature ensures consistent and predictable resource bookings by allowing organizations to set a default booking allocation method across the Schedule Board and Schedule Assistant. This reduces the risk of incorrect bookings caused by inconsistent defaults, minimizes rework and cancellations, and saves time for resource managers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576768","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576879","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Show accounting currency with the correct label","desc":"<p>This feature lets different currency units show the actual record for the accounting currency when the unit differs from the base currency. Today the correct value is shown, but the units are incorrectly shown as the base currency, regardless of the actual accounting currency unit. In this feature, accounting currency fields are stored in a child record with the correct currency unit and appears with the correct label on the actual form.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Currently in Project Operations, when an accounting currency differs from the company's base currency, it's shown with an incorrect currency label on the actual record in Microsoft Dataverse. The correct currencies are used when the data is sent to finance and operations apps, but this mismatch often creates confusion and leads to unnecessary double-checking and corrections. With this update, currency units are correctly shown in Dataverse.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576879","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576880","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Update correction journal usability","desc":"<p>Correcting transactions after they’ve been processed can be a complicated and difficult process. Currently in Project Operations, you must select all the transactions you want to correct at the same time to create the journal, and all transactions added to the journal must be corrected in the same way. This leads to significant repeat work, where you need to create multiple journals to be able to make different corrections on different transactions. This feature updates that process with the following changes:</p> <ul> <li>Transactions can be marked with <strong>Needs correction</strong> from the billing hub view, then once all required transactions have been marked, you can create the journal. This simplifies the journal creation process.</li> <li>Different transactions added to the same correction journal can be corrected in different ways, reducing the number of journals that need to be created.</li> <li>A wider set of fields is available for correction, limiting the number of transactions that need to be recalled to the draft entry state (a more complicated process) to complete the required changes.</li> <li>Time transactions can be split across multiple projects and tasks without recalling the draft entry state.</li> <li>A UI overhaul will be done to make the corrections process easier and simpler to follow.</li> </ul> <p>Overall, these changes make corrections easier, minimize mistakes that can lead to major problems, and reduce frustration with the interface.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Correcting previously processed transactions is a difficult process that’s made harder by UX limitations. The changes in this feature update let you make different corrections within the same journal, correct a wider range of fields, and easily select transactions that need correction. With the new experience, a larger volume of transactions can be corrected at once to reduce repetitive work while simultaneously making the process clearer and simpler. This reduces mistakes made during the corrections process, which in turn minimizes the more costly and problematic billing errors.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576880","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576757","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Use the new calendar interface for time entry","desc":"<p>The web experience for time entry in Dynamics 365 Project Operations is getting a series of improvements that make time entry faster and more accurate. The improvements give team members better tracking capabilities.</p> <p>These upgrades include:</p> <ul> <li>A new calendar interface to view, create, and change time entries.</li> <li>The ability to track time across different timelines, such as weekly or monthly.</li> <li>Tighter integration of the work breakdown structure for assigned tasks and projects within the time entry creation step (quick create forms).</li> <li>Improved tracking with benchmarking of actual versus target hours and visualizations that help team members track their progress on project tasks.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Every organization needs an efficient time entry experience for its consultants and team members. This experience gives you the flexibility to log time in different ways. It minimizes the number of clicks and effort required to enter time.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576757","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"May CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/time-entry-calendar"},{"id":"rm-576749","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Use the new Time Entry mobile app","desc":"<p>Project team members on Lite and resource-based and nonstocked deployments of Project Operations now have a new mobile application based on Microsoft Power Apps. The new mobile app helps them log time, keep track of submitted entries, and view the work assigned to them.</p> <p>The application provides users with the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>A view that summarizes all Microsoft Outlook meetings and Microsoft to-do items for the day. Use these meetings and to-do items to log time entries.</li> <li>The ability to view projects and tasks where the team member is currently assigned, and the duration of the staffed project.</li> <li>A section to view day-wise time entries across statuses (Draft, Submitted, and so on). Users can modify or delete editable entries, submit entries for approval, or recall already submitted entries.</li> <li>Users get access to a new mode of logging time with a timer. Use the timer to record how long you work on granular tasks. Later, tag the timer to a project or task to turn it into a time entry.</li> </ul> <p>When you make changes in the mobile app, the changes sync to the web app for Project Operations or Project Operations Team Member, and vice versa. We’ll soon update the steps to install or enable this mobile app.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Project consultants often travel for work and find it challenging to log weekly time entries while they're on the go. With the new mobile experience in Dynamics 365 Project Operations, users can view, create, and submit their time entries for approval.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576749","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"March CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/time-entry-mobile-app"},{"id":"rm-576764","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - View current and upcoming staffing in a timeline","desc":"<p>The new timeline view augments the experience for team members in Project Operations by giving them visibility into current and upcoming staffing (both task and project level).</p> <p>The feature includes:</p> <ul> <li>Weekly view of task-level assignments.</li> <li>Weekly view of project-level bookings.</li> <li>Clear highlighting of periods without staffing (bench time).</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>A lack of visibility into current and upcoming project staffing leads to suboptimal planning and inefficient onboarding. This also creates uncertainty around bench time (utilization). By providing team members with a clear view of task- and project-level staffing, this feature aims to eliminate these issues.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576764","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/enhanced-team-member-experience"},{"id":"rm-576758","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Procurement - Manage supplier relationships with Supplier Engagement","desc":"<p>The new Supplier Engagement application gives you a Microsoft Power Apps experience that integrates with Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management and Dynamics 365 Finance. With this app, you can manage both strategic and tactical areas of your supplier relationships. You can schedule appointments, track performance, schedule supplier reviews, and manage prospective suppliers who aren't registered yet.</p> <p>The experience also includes a supplier-facing portal based on Microsoft Power Pages. The new supplier portal supports many facets of the supplier relationship, ranging from tactical to operational and transactional aspects. It helps new suppliers onboard and enables existing suppliers to engage with your company through transactions such as requests for quotation (RFQs), managed bidding, purchase orders, and invoices. The supplier portal works with the existing vendor collaboration capabilities in Supply Chain Management.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>With the Supplier Engagement app, procurement professionals can manage supplier relationships for all legal entities from one workspace. Procurement professionals can view supplier performance, schedule appointments, and manage many other aspects of their supplier relationships. A new supplier portal gives suppliers a better experience when onboarding and engaging with procurement professionals. The portal supports collaboration throughout the relationship, including during requests for quotation, purchase ordering, and invoicing.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576758","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576760","title":"Dynamics 365 Sustainability: Capture snapshot‑based data trails","desc":"<p>This feature introduces snapshot‑based data trail support that captures a complete, point‑in‑time record for every calculated metric. Each snapshot includes source activity data, applied emission factors (including factor values and GWP versions), reference data, filters, and the calculation logic used. This ensures that aggregates can be reliably traced back to original inputs.</p> <p>A new visual data‑lineage view provides an end‑to‑end representation of how data flows from source records through calculations to final results, helping users understand how results roll up across organizational structures and how dimensional attributes influence calculated outcomes.</p> <p>These enhancements are available automatically without additional configuration, providing consistent and defensible traceability across all calculated metrics. Users can access snapshot details and the data‑lineage view directly from calculated metrics, providing consistent traceability and audit support across all emissions calculations.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>As sustainability data is increasingly scrutinized by auditors, regulators, and internal stakeholders, organizations need reliable point‑in‑time traceability for reported metrics. This release strengthens audit readiness by ensuring every calculated result can be traced back to its exact inputs, logic, and reference data at the time of calculation. By improving transparency and lineage, customers can respond to audits with greater confidence while reducing investigation time and reporting risk.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sustainability"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576760","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576751","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Country and regional - Start using the new non-deductible VAT framework in Belgium","desc":"<p>Belgian users will experience an improved non-deductible VAT process with the introduction of a new global feature. A preconfigured <strong>Non-deductible VAT Type</strong> field will be available specifically for Belgium. Previously, users selected a general ledger expense account in the <strong>Chart of Accounts</strong> and manually entered the partial deduction amount in the <strong>% Non-deductible VAT</strong> field. With the new approach, users will follow the standard global method, and setup will be managed through the <strong>VAT Posting Group Setup</strong>.</p> <p>When you enable the new feature in the <strong>VAT Setup</strong> page, the system automatically provides a data upgrade.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Users in Belgium will receive an upgraded version of non-deductible VAT using the new global feature.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576751","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"November CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/localfunctionality/belgium/how-to-set-up-non-deductible-vat"},{"id":"rm-576639","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Enhancements to Invoice capture","desc":"<p>This release consolidates multiple Invoice capture enhancements into a single, cohesive capability update with a public preview in 10.0.49. Updates include:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>AI‑based invoice header level derivation</strong>: Improves matching of invoice header level to purchase orders and procurement categories using vendor data. Continuous learning applies user corrections to future invoices, increasing touchless processing and reducing repeated manual effort.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Side‑by‑side invoice and purchase order view</strong>: Allows finance users to view invoice lines, the invoice PDF, and purchase order details simultaneously. This reduces context switching during manual matching, speeds up exception resolution, and lowers the risk of user error without changing existing purchase order structures.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Enhanced charge recognition and allocation</strong></p> </li> </ul> <p>This feature automatically identifies and classifies header‑level and line‑level charges on vendor invoices. Charges are allocated using defined rules during transfer to Dynamics 365 Finance, preventing invoice total mismatches and reducing downstream corrections.</p> <p>While the current release focuses on improving automation accuracy, exception‑handling efficiency, and usability for high‑volume invoice processing, future direction will be continued expansion of intelligent recognition, support for more complex invoice layouts such as line-level derivation, and ongoing scalability and usability improvements aligned with broader accounts payable automation investments.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Invoice capture is a critical capability for organizations processing high volumes of vendor invoices. Manual matching of invoice lines, limited visibility during exception handling, and incorrect handling of invoice charges increase operational effort and slow down invoice processing, especially during period‑end peaks.</p> <p>This release improves invoice processing efficiency by increasing automation accuracy while simplifying manual exception handling when required. Enhanced AI‑based derivation reduces repetitive corrections, improved usability accelerates manual validation, and better charge recognition prevents posting mismatches and downstream rework. Together, these improvements increase touchless processing rates, reduce operational cost, and strengthen confidence in automated invoice processing within Dynamics 365 Finance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576639","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/get-started/whats-new-invoice-capture"},{"id":"rm-576641","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Warehouse management - Integrate the Warehouse management module with external labor management systems","desc":"<p>This feature provides a standard framework for integrating the Warehouse management module in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management with external labor management systems. With this framework, you can connect warehouse execution data to a third-party LMS. This connection gives you advanced capabilities for labor planning, scheduling, and performance tracking. The integration supports warehouse execution with or without warehouse management processes. It also supports warehouse-only mode.</p> <p>Labor management systems typically provide features like:</p> <ul> <li>Real-time productivity monitoring and task tracking.</li> <li>Engineered labor standards and support for time studies to establish benchmarks for task durations.</li> <li>Predictive scheduling and dynamic labor forecasting.</li> <li>Customizable dashboards and ad-hoc reporting.</li> <li>Automated time and attendance tracking.</li> <li>Incentive program management.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Integrating external labor management systems (LMS) with your warehouse management system (WMS) enables smarter, data-driven workforce planning and execution by delivering value across multiple dimensions.</p> <p>This integration enhances operational efficiency by automating labor planning and reducing manual data entry through synchronized workforce schedules and warehouse task execution. It also provides performance visibility, offering real-time insights into labor productivity, cost-to-serve, and task-level performance to support continuous improvement.</p> <p>Centralizing labor data supports compliance and auditability, streamlining regulatory processes and reducing administrative overhead. Additionally, it fosters employee engagement by enabling transparent performance tracking and incentive programs that boost motivation and retention. Finally, cross-system coordination improves communication between warehouse operations and workforce management, ensuring labor resources are aligned with real-time operational needs.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576641","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560075","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management- IRM alerts in XDR","desc":"<p>With this feature, IRM alerts and other supporting data will be available in the following Microsoft Defender XDR experiences:</p> <ol> <li>IRM alerts will be surfaced in unified alert and Incident queue in Microsoft Defender XDR.</li> <li>IRM alerts, Indicators and enriched events will be available in Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting. Analysts can leverage KQL queries to identify potentially hidden risky patterns in data security related user activity.</li> <li>IRM alert, Indicators and enriched events will be exposed through Graph API.</li> </ol> <p>This feature can be enabled through “Share data with Microsoft Defender XDR” within Microsoft Insider Risk Management settings</p> <p>IRM data in Microsoft Defender XDR does not honor anonymization. This is to enable effective correlation of IRM alerts with alerts from other solutions in Microsoft Defender XDR platform (such as Defender for Endpoint, Defender for Cloud apps, etc.).</p> <p>Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-09","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560075","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-576770","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Omnichannel commerce - Support cross-legal entity order fulfillment for Dynamics 365 Commerce","desc":"<p>This feature includes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Cross-legal entity fulfillment groups</strong>: Define fulfillment groups that include warehouses and stores from multiple legal entities, enabling distributed order management (DOM) to select the best fulfillment location across the enterprise.</li> <li><strong>Inventory visibility</strong>: DOM can access inventory data from warehouses in different legal entities, ensuring accurate sourcing decisions.</li> <li><strong>Intercompany order automation</strong>: When you select a cross-legal entity warehouse, the system automatically creates intercompany orders and manages the fulfillment chain, including exception handling and reassignment scenarios.</li> <li><strong>Point of sale support</strong>: Orders assigned to stores in other legal entities are visible and can be fulfilled at those stores, with accurate customer details displayed.</li> <li><strong>Enhanced profiles and rules</strong>: DOM profiles and rules are updated to support cross-legal entity strategies, removing single-entity constraints and improving configuration flexibility.</li> <li><strong>Direct delivery</strong>: Supports direct delivery fulfillment method.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>By automating cross-legal entity order fulfillment, retailers can source, promise, and deliver orders from the most optimal location regardless of company boundaries. It reduces manual intervention, accelerates delivery, and enables true omnichannel experiences, directly addressing the needs of global and multiband retailers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576770","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576755","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Boost productivity with Copilot - Boost agent performance with optimal tool execution paths in Dynamics 365 ERP MCP","desc":"<p>With the dynamic tools of the Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server, large language models often have multiple options for tool-calling sequences to perform an operation or retrieve data. The orchestration can select the tool execution sequence and can include more tool calls than are required. This enhancement to the MCP server improves performance and accuracy of the server response by enabling the server to use optimal tool execution sequences to perform operations with a single point of entry for MCP tools and a semantic index of the available menu items, entities, and actions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server now uses a semantic index of target ERP menu items, entities, and actions to improve performance and accuracy of tool calls by optimizing the sequence of tool executions for agentic operations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576755","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/business-performance-analytics/erp-analytics-mcp-overview"},{"id":"rm-576762","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Business performance - MCP for ERP Analytics","desc":"<p>MCP for Analytics provides AI agents with structured access to ERP analytics data and tools. It ensures agents use the same definitions and models as users.</p> <p>Key benefits:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Data Access</strong>: Gives agents access to ERP analytics data for analysis and insights.</li> <li><strong>Metrics and Dimensions</strong>: Provides access to key metrics, dimensions, and relationships used in reporting.</li> <li><strong>Semantic Model</strong>: Exposes the full semantic model to support consistent interpretation of data.</li> <li><strong>Tool Access</strong>: Enables agents to connect with tools like Power BI and Business Performance Analytics.</li> </ul> <p>MCP makes ERP analytics data agent-ready, reliable, and explainable.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>MCP for Analytics allows agents to access ERP analytics data and tools with context. It ensures consistency across metrics, dimensions, and hierarchies so agents can reason reliably. This improves trust in insights, reduces duplication, and simplifies development of explainable agent experiences.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576762","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"January CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/build-agent-mcp"},{"id":"rm-576766","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Use time-zone-agnostic fields in project planning","desc":"<p>Project and project task start, and end times are saved in a date-time format. The system converts these times to GMT before saving them. When the product displays these times, it converts them back to the user's time zone. However, some integrations and customizations pull only the date from this field. This approach causes problems when the conversion to GMT changes the date. The problem happens when an integration pulls only that date from the field without converting it back to GMT.</p> <p>To prevent this problem, create new fields on the entity to store the start and end date and time values without converting them to GMT. With these fields, you can confidently pull only the date without worrying about time-zone conversion causing the date to change.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature helps you avoid time zone headaches when managing project schedules. Instead of converting times to GMT, which can shift dates and create confusion, it stores start and end dates exactly as you enter them. That means fewer errors, less rework, and more accurate timelines for your team.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576766","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"May CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/sales/tz-independent-date-fields"},{"id":"rm-576752","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Microsoft 365 collaboration - Discover, build, customize, and extend with management MCP server","desc":"<p>The management MCP server is a build surface and registry for agent-ready tools available within a customer's environment. It exposes an addressable endpoint where developers and agents can discover, assemble, and deploy MCP servers made from trusted components including connector actions, tools from other MCP servers, and custom APIs.</p> <h3>Discover available tools and servers</h3> <ul> <li>Find MCP servers authored, hosted, or certified by Microsoft</li> <li>Query and explore over 1,470 connectors and their individual actions</li> <li>Discover custom APIs available in your organization or from partner teams</li> </ul> <h3>Create and customize MCP servers</h3> <ul> <li>Build new MCP servers by selecting connector actions, APIs, and reusable tools</li> <li>Clone an existing MCP server, such as a Dataverse MCP, and tailor it by adding or removing tools to match your scenario</li> <li>Use MCP servers as modular, scenario-focused endpoints that can be reused across agents</li> </ul> <h3>Endpoint driven developer experience</h3> <ul> <li>Accessible as a simple environment scoped URL—no UI required</li> <li>Use in Visual Studio Code, Claude, or any agent or tool that supports HTTP</li> <li>Compose, publish, and maintain MCP servers entirely through API calls</li> </ul> <h3>Enterprise ready governance and control</h3> <ul> <li>Enforce data loss prevention (DLP) policies</li> <li>Apply access controls at both the MCP server and individual tool level</li> </ul> <p>The management MCP server gives you everything you need to build and scale agents using tools you already trust, no interface required, just secure, extensible control from the systems you already manage.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The management Model Context Protocol (MCP) server gives developers and system integrators a central API-based foundation to discover and build custom MCP servers. Through a single environment scoped endpoint, teams can find Microsoft certified or internal MCP servers, search across 1,470 connector actions and APIs, and create new or customized MCP servers with the exact tools their agents need. This capability reduces redundant development and enables a flexible, secure path from prototype to production across platforms like Visual Studio Code and Claude.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576752","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557561","title":"Microsoft Edge: Auto-open Copilot side pane for Outlook links","desc":"<p>When users open links from Outlook, Microsoft Edge can automatically open the Copilot side pane to provide contextual insights and actionable suggestion chips based on email and destination content - such as highlighting key points, and recommending next actions - without disrupting the browsing flow. This experience helps users quickly understand content, take action with fewer steps, and get more value from Copilot while extending productive browsing time in Edge. Admins can control availability to this feature using the M365LinksAutoOpenCopilotEnabled policy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557561","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-476488","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ability to separate out the Townhall attendee invites","desc":"<p>This backend change will now address the 'separation of attendee' invites from the events crew. This feature allows the organizers of Townhalls to maintain separate invites for attendees.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-23","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=476488","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-574110","title":"Microsoft Teams: Events now support up to 20,000 registrations, making it easier to reach and engage larger audiences at scale","desc":"<p>Connect with more attendees than ever before with Teams Events, now supporting up to 20,000 registrations for organizers with valid Attendee packs.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574110","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576858","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Configure minimum interval of time entry duration","desc":"<p>Customers can now configure the allowable increment for time entry durations to ensure that all logged time adheres to their organization’s time-tracking policies. When enabled, you can only create or modify time entries whose duration is a multiple of the configured value (for example, 15 minutes, or 1 hour), helping prevent erroneous or non-compliant time entries from being recorded.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Customers can now ensure that time entry duration is always a multiple of a value set by them, preventing erroneous time entries from being logged.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576745","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Seller experiences - Streamline Quick Campaigns for confident, one-time bulk email outreach","desc":"<p>Quick Campaigns support multiple bulk activity types (email, tasks, appointments, phone calls). This release focuses on improving the end-to-end experience for bulk email creation, with foundational improvements that benefit the overall Quick Campaigns flow.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Streamlined quick campaign flow</strong>: The existing multistep wizard is simplified for Quick Campaigns creation, including one-time bulk email sends. Sellers can create, review, and send bulk emails with fewer steps and clicks, staying in a single creation surface and focusing on execution rather than setup.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>In-flow template creation and editing</strong>: Sellers can create or edit email templates directly within the Quick Campaigns flow. Newly created or updated templates are easy to find and reuse without leaving the experience or restarting setup.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Enhanced template discovery with views</strong>: An improved template picker with a view selector helps sellers quickly find the right template, whether it’s one they created, one shared with them, or a marketing-approved one.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Send-specific edits and template-free bulk emails</strong>: Sellers can make send-specific edits such as adding a personalized greeting, dynamic text, or signature, without overwriting shared templates. For true one-off outreach, sellers can also compose bulk emails from scratch using rich text, dynamic text, and signatures without creating templates.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Inline template preview and test send</strong>: Sellers can preview the final rendered email inline and send a test email to themselves or a colleague to validate formatting and personalization. This removes the need for duplicate bulk email campaigns and rework, increasing confidence before sending.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Quick Campaigns are designed for fast, seller-led outreach such as post-meeting follow-ups, event or webinar recaps, policy updates, or one-time announcements to many customers at once. However, even simple bulk emails in Quick Campaigns were slow and error-prone. Sellers had to navigate a multistep wizard, rely on rigid templates, exit the flow to make changes, and use workarounds to gain confidence before sending. This breaks execution momentum and often pushes sellers to Outlook or custom solutions outside Dynamics 365.</p> <p>This release simplifies the Quick Campaigns experience, particularly for bulk email scenarios, by reducing unnecessary steps, keeping sellers in a single flow, supporting send-specific personalization, and improving confidence before sending, so sellers can act quickly without leaving the platform or compromising compliance.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576745","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-519571","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Usage reports – Microsoft 365 Copilot Connectors","desc":"<p>A new usage report will be available in the Microsoft 365 admin center for Copilot Connectors in Microsoft 365 Copilot, designed to give organizations a detailed view of how connectors are being used within Microsoft 365 Copilot. This report provides insights into overall connector activity, and connector powered response patterns over time, along with detailed user-level connectors adoption data. With these analytics, admins can monitor adoption, identify usage patterns, and optimize Copilot experiences to drive greater value across their organization. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-27","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=519571","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576194","title":"Microsoft Teams: Loop meeting notes stored in the meeting organizer's OneDrive","desc":"<p>For non-channel Microsoft Teams meetings, collaborative meeting notes, including Loop-powered meeting notes and Facilitator notes, will be stored in the meeting organizer's OneDrive for Business instead of the OneDrive of the person who starts the notes. This update provides more consistent ownership and management of meeting content while preserving the existing note-taking and collaboration experience for meeting participants.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576194","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576198","title":"Microsoft Teams: Near-real-time detection of malicious QR codes in messages","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams will introduce near-real-time detection of malicious QR codes shared in messages. By analyzing destinations embedded in QR codes, Teams can identify potential phishing and fraud threats and apply additional protections to malicious content, extending existing URL protection to QR-based attacks.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576198","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576193","title":"Microsoft Teams: Pinch to zoom in on shared screens","desc":"<p>Get a closer look at shared content in Teams calls and meetings with <strong>pinch-to-zoom using your touchpad</strong>. Quickly zoom in to make small text and detailed visuals easier to see, then zoom back out for the full view. Existing zoom controls remain available.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576193","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-567314","title":"Microsoft Teams: SharePoint app in Teams","desc":"<p>When a user who has access to the SharePoint app in Teams clicks a SharePoint page or news link in Teams chat or channels, the link will open inside the SharePoint app in Teams (if available) instead of the mobile browser</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567314","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-529851","title":"Outlook: Enriching profile cards with custom, organization-specific properties","desc":"<p>Customers can now customize their M365 profile cards by adding custom properties unique to their organization. These properties can be sourced from external systems like HR platforms, enriching user profiles with relevant organizational details. Tenant admins can configure these properties with a display name and icon, which will appear in the Contact Information section of the profile cards.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529851","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576750","title":"Power Pages: Design studio - Unify Power Pages authorization by merging web role with Dataverse security role","desc":"<p>This feature merges Power Pages web roles and site users with Dataverse security roles and system users, creating a unified authorization model.</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>User Mapping</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>Each Power Pages user is stored in both the <strong>System User</strong> table and the <strong>Contact</strong> table.</li> <li>The <strong>System Managed User Type</strong> column in the <strong>User</strong> table identifies Power Pages users as <code>C2 User</code>.</li> </ul> </li> <li><p><strong>Role Mapping</strong>: Each Power Pages web role is represented in both the <strong>Security Role</strong> table and the <strong>Web Role</strong> table.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>No Migration Required</strong>: Existing contact and web role records automatically sync with system user and security role tables.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Configuration</strong>: No changes required for makers; existing data security configurations remain intact.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You'll strengthen security and simplify user management by centralizing authorization in Dataverse. This means fewer redundant checks in Power Pages, reducing complexity and improving performance. Businesses gain consistent access control, enhanced auditing for compliance, and faster data operations, all without additional configuration or migration. The result is lower operational overhead, improved governance, and better scalability.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576750","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"July CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/security/unify-pages-security-with-dataverse"},{"id":"mc-MC1193692","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365: Enrich profile cards with custom properties from third-party systems","desc":"Updated October 16, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nWe’re introducing the ability for organizations to customize Microsoft 365 profile cards by adding up to 10 custom properties sourced from external systems such as HR platforms. This enhancement helps enrich user profiles with relevant organizational details, improving discoverability and context for collaboration.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 529851.\nWhen this will happen:\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in November 2026 (previously October) and expect to complete in November 2026 (previously October).\nHow this affects your organization\nWho is affected: Microsoft 365 tenant admins managing user profile cards\nWhat will happen:\n• You can add up to 10 custom properties to profile cards using Microsoft Graph People connectors.\n• Properties can be sourced from external systems (such as HR platforms).\n• This feature is OFF by default and requires admin configuration to enable.\n• Admins can configure visibility, display name, and icon for each property in Microsoft 365 admin center under: Settings > Org settings > People settings > Profile > Person info on profile cards\n•\n• Once enabled, properties appear in the Contact Information section of profile cards in Outlook Web:\n•\n• Changes may take up to 24 hours to propagate across profile cards.\n• Future updates will include direct ingestion from SAP SuccessFactors and Workday connectors.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\n• Review external systems for properties you want displayed on profile cards.\n• Ingest these properties using a Microsoft Graph People connector.\n• Configure visibility and enable properties in the Microsoft 365 admin center.\n• Communicate this change to helpdesk staff and update internal documentation if needed.\n\nLearn more: Microsoft 365 Copilot connectors for people data | Microsoft Learn\n•\n\nCompliance considerations\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-10","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1193692","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1009930","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Distinguish invites among Attendee, Presenter, and Co-organizer emails","desc":"Updated October 16, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nMicrosoft Teams Events invite emails will be separated based on the role of the participant. Event organizers will get an email explaining the specific roles of participants in the event. Similarly, each presenter will get a separate calendar invite, allowing the organizers of town halls to maintain separate invites for attendees.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 476488.\n[When this will happen:]\nTargeted Release: We will begin rolling out early December 2026 (previously early November) and expect to complete by mid-December 2026 (previously mid-November).\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCC High): We will begin rolling out mid-December 2026 (previously mid-November) and expect to complete by mid-January 2027 (previously mid-December)\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nThis feature update allows the organizers of town halls to maintain separate invites for attendees.\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nThis rollout will happen automatically with no admin action required. You may want to notify your users about this change and update any relevant documentation as appropriate.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1009930","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-576753","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Modernize customer detail page for assisted selling in Store Commerce","desc":"<p>The Customer Data Platform panel in Store Commerce has been rebuilt using React, replacing the legacy implementation with a modern, responsive layout optimized for both desktop and mobile form factors.</p> <p><strong>What's new in the modernized CDP panel</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Mobile-optimized layout</strong>: The panel uses a vertical scroll pattern that works naturally on tablets and handheld devices used by store associates on the floor.</li> <li><strong>Customer summary at a glance</strong>: Loyalty points, purchase frequency, average spend, and contact details are prominently displayed at the top of the panel.</li> <li><strong>Transaction history inline</strong>: Associates can view recent purchases, including items bought, channel, and location, without leaving the current context.</li> <li><strong>Buy-again workflow</strong>: Frequently purchased items are surfaced with a direct add-to-sale action, enabling associates to quickly rebuild a customer's basket.</li> <li><strong>Customer timeline</strong>: Chronological view of customer interactions, notes, and activities gives associates context for the current conversation.</li> <li><strong>Product recommendations</strong>: Curated or engine-driven recommendations are shown inline to support upsell and cross-sell during the interaction.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Streamlined customer creation and editing</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Single-save workflow</strong>: Associates can create a new customer record with both customer information and primary address captured in one form, saved in a single action. This reduces the number of clicks and screen transitions required compared to the legacy multistep flow.</li> <li><strong>Inline address validation</strong>: Mandatory address fields are validated at the point of entry before the record is saved to help ensure compliance with fiscal requirements for markets where a complete primary address is legally required on customer records. This validation is opt-in and configured at the channel level.</li> <li><strong>Unified edit experience</strong>: Editing an existing customer's details and address follows the same consolidated pattern to keep associates in a single context rather than navigating between separate management screens.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Custom attributes tab</strong></p> <p>Retailers who capture custom attribute data on customer records can now find that information directly within the CDP panel via a dedicated <strong>Custom information</strong> tab. The tab is displayed conditionally and appears only when custom attributes have been configured for the customer record to keep the panel clean and uncluttered for retailers who do not use custom attributes. This allows retailers to extend the clienteling experience with their own data, such as membership tiers, fit preferences, loyalty program details, or any other retailer-defined fields, without requiring associates to leave the panel or open a separate management screen.</p> <p><strong>How associates access the feature</strong></p> <p>The CDP panel is accessible from two entry points in Store Commerce:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Customer search</strong>: When an associate searches for and selects a customer, the modernized CDP panel opens directly.</li> <li><strong>Active transaction</strong>: Associates can open the CDP panel from within an in-progress transaction to view customer context without interrupting the sale.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Enabling the feature</strong></p> <p>This feature is enabled via <strong>Feature management</strong> in Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters. Once the feature flag is turned on, the modernized CDP panel is automatically available in Store Commerce for all users without additional configuration at the register or device level.</p> <p><strong>Applies to</strong>: Point of sale (Store Commerce)</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Store associates spend valuable selling time navigating a cluttered, legacy customer detail page that wasn't designed for mobile or fast-paced retail floors. Critical information, such as purchase history, loyalty points, preferences, and product recommendations, is buried across multiple tabs and screens, slowing assisted selling and reducing the quality of in-store customer interactions.</p> <p>The modernized Customer Data Platform (CDP) panel in Store Commerce delivers a lightweight, mobile-optimized clienteling experience designed for the way associates actually work. Key customer signals, such as spending summaries, recent transactions, buy-again suggestions, and a full customer timeline, are now surfaced inline without requiring associates to navigate away from the transaction. This means faster, more personalized customer conversations, higher basket value through timely product recommendations, and reduced training burden for new associates who can now act on customer context at a glance.</p> <p>Creating and editing customer records has also historically required associates to navigate multiple screens and save operations, increasing the risk of incomplete records and slowing down queue-sensitive moments on the shop floor. For retailers operating in regions with fiscal requirements, where a validated primary address is mandatory for customer records, the legacy workflow offered no inline guardrails, leading to compliance gaps and post-transaction corrections.</p> <p>The modernized CDP panel addresses this by consolidating customer creation and editing into a streamlined, single-save workflow. Associates can capture customer information and primary address in one form and save the complete record in a single action that reduces clicks and eliminates the back-and-forth between separate screens. Mandatory address field validation is enforced inline at the point of entry, ensuring compliance with fiscal requirements before the record is committed and removing the need for manual follow-up or administrative correction.</p> <p>For retailers investing in omnichannel clienteling, this feature provides a modern, compliant foundation to deliver consistent, data-informed customer engagement at the point of sale.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576753","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-576819","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Omnichannel customer experiences - Use data masking to protect customer data","desc":"<p>Customer service representative data masking is a new opt-in feature for Dynamics 365 Contact Center.</p> <p>When enabled, service representatives can select individual messages from the customer and redact them, so the customer's PII isn't stored in your repository. This feature complements the existing automatic data masking rules with both automatic and manual masking. You can be confident that your brand is protecting your customers' valuable information.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Protect your customers' sensitive data by enabling your customer service representatives to hide any personally identifiable information (PII) that customers inadvertently share.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576819","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-576746","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Assign conversation to expert who engaged with the customer previously","desc":"<p>Assign to a previously engaged or preferred expert leverages historical interaction context, queue membership alignment, and expert availability, to ensure customers are reconnected with experts who already understand their issue. When the previous or preferred expert is unavailable, assignments seamlessly fall back to the next best qualified expert, preserving service levels and reliability. This capability reduces repeat explanations, accelerates resolution times, and improves customer satisfaction, helping businesses lower cost to serve while delivering more consistent, personalized support experiences at scale. Administrators define assignment logic using natural language-based playbooks in conversation orchestration, with configurable lookback period to determine the time range until when the system should look for a previously engaged expert.</p> <p>For asynchronous conversations, administrators can also choose to reconnect customers with the same expert by checking the expert’s current presence status and honoring active conversation limits, ensuring returning conversations are assigned only when the expert has capacity to engage.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>By automatically assigning customers to a previous or preferred expert, you deliver faster, more personalized support. By routing repeat or follow up conversations to the most recent or preferred expert within configurable time windows, you reduce customer repetition, improve continuity, and accelerate resolution. When the previous expert is unavailable, the system intelligently falls back to the next best qualified expert, ensuring service levels are maintained. This leads to lower handling times, higher customer satisfaction, and improved expert efficiency.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576746","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576759","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Handle waiting conversations when queues close or become unstaffed","desc":"<p>This capability enhances queue handling by intelligently detecting two key scenarios where conversations would otherwise remain unserved:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Queue transitions to out-of-operating hours</strong>: The system continuously monitors active conversations that entered a queue before closing time. If the queue transitions to out-of-operating hours while conversations are still waiting, it automatically applies admin-defined overflow actions. Customers can be guided to leave a voicemail, request a callback, or be transferred to another available queue, ensuring a smooth end-of-day experience without manual intervention.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>No service representatives are signed in</strong>: The system evaluates real-time representative availability. If all representatives assigned to a queue are signed out, it immediately triggers the configured fallback action instead of waiting for in-queue overflow timers. This is especially valuable in scenarios such as mass logout events, unexpected breaks, or holidays not captured in operating hours.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Administrators configure both scenarios using natural language prompts in conversation orchestration, enabling fine-grained control over queue behavior. This ensures customers are always routed to the best possible outcome, even when direct support is unavailable.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This capability ensures customers are never left waiting when representatives aren't available. Whether a queue transitions to be out-of-operating hours or all support representatives are logged out, the system proactively routes conversations to configured fallback options such as voicemail, callback, or alternative queues.</p> <p>Organizations benefit from reduced wait times and lower abandonment, improved customer satisfaction during peak load or unexpected staffing gaps, and a more predictable service experience regardless of representative availability. At the same time, this eliminates the need for manual queue draining or extended shifts, helping protect service representative wellbeing while maintaining consistent service levels.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576759","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576761","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Detect intraday volume spikes with workforce alerts","desc":"<p>Supervisors can create volume spike alerts that compare real-time conversation volume with the forecast linked to a shift plan. When volume remains above forecast for the configured number of intervals, selected recipients receive an in-app notification.</p> <p>The capability includes the following features:</p> <ul> <li>Administrators can enable workforce alerts in Copilot Service admin center by going to <strong>Workforce management</strong> &gt; <strong>Intraday management</strong> &gt; <strong>Workforce alerts</strong>.</li> <li>Supervisors can create and manage alerts from Workforce alerts in the Copilot Service workspace site map.</li> <li>Each alert references a shift plan and monitors the queues associated with its linked capacity plan.</li> <li>Supervisors can specify the percentage by which actual volume must exceed forecast volume.</li> <li>Supervisors can specify the number of consecutive intervals during which the deviation must continue before an alert is raised. The forecast determines whether an interval is 15, 30, or 60 minutes.</li> <li>Supervisors can set an expiration date to limit an alert to a campaign, season, or known event.</li> <li>Supervisors can select one or more notification recipients for each alert.</li> <li>Active alerts are evaluated on a recurring schedule. Notifications are sent when the configured threshold and duration are met.</li> <li>Recipients can select a notification to open the alert details. The details include the queue and alert name, detection time, current and forecast volumes, spike percentage, and an interval-by-interval breakdown.</li> </ul> <h3>Access and prerequisites</h3> <ul> <li>An administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from Power Platform admin center.</li> <li>Forecasting and scheduling must be configured.</li> <li>The selected shift plan must have a linked capacity plan and forecast.</li> <li>Real-time conversation data must be available for the monitored queues.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Contact centers plan staffing based on forecasted demand, but actual demand can change quickly. When conversation volume rises significantly above forecast, queues can grow and service levels can decline before supervisors have time to respond.</p> <p>Workforce alerts help supervisors identify unusual intraday volume changes without continuously monitoring a dashboard. Supervisors define the deviation and duration that represent a volume spike and select who should be notified when those conditions are met.</p> <p>The notification provides information about the spike, including how far actual volume is above forecast and whether the deviation is continuing. Supervisors can use this information to decide whether to shift capacity, offer overtime, or defer offline work while these actions can still help protect the customer experience.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576761","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"August CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/use/workforce-management-use-volume-spike-alerts"},{"id":"rm-576748","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Monitor intraday performance against the forecast","desc":"<p>The intraday performance report provides supervisors with an interval-level view of performance against the forecast. In Copilot Service workspace, go to <strong>Workforce management</strong> to access the report.</p> <ul> <li>Compare forecast and actual contact volume and average handle time. Variances appear as values and percentages, making outliers easier to identify.</li> <li>Compare forecast, required, and scheduled staffing levels to identify understaffed and overstaffed intervals.</li> <li>Review service level, occupancy, and schedule adherence alongside volume and staffing data in a single report.</li> <li>View data in 15-, 30-, or 60-minute intervals to match how your organization manages intraday performance.</li> <li>Filter the report by planning group and shift plan to focus on the areas you manage.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Access and prerequisites</strong></p> <p>To use Workforce Management capabilities, an administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from the Power Platform admin center.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Contact center forecasts and schedules are built days or weeks in advance, but demand rarely arrives exactly as planned. When volume spikes, handle times run long, or agents are absent, supervisors often don't see the gap until service levels have already slipped and the interval is gone.</p> <p>The intraday performance report closes that gap by showing plan versus actual as the day unfolds. Supervisors can see which intervals are under- or over-staffed and act while there's still time by moving agents between queues, adjusting break and training schedules, or opening overtime only where it's genuinely needed. That protects service level and abandonment targets on the days that matter most, and it curbs the two costs that quietly compound in every contact center: paying for idle capacity in over-forecasted intervals and paying premium rates to recover from under-forecasted ones.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576748","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576747","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Business performance - Accelerate planning with quick-start templates","desc":"<p>Quick-start planning templates provide a guided, business-first experience for setting up planning in Business performance planning. Instead of selecting technical objects like fact tables, users simply choose a planning area—starting with OPEX, with Revenue, Workforce, and CAPEX to follow.</p> <p>When a planning area is selected, Business performance planning automatically generates the required data model, including cubes and dimensions, using recommended fact tables from Business performance analytics.</p> <p>A prebuilt Power BI app is then available to install and connect directly to the organization’s Business performance analytics environment. The app includes ready-to-use planning reports, allowing users to enter data, view results, and analyze scenarios with their own data immediately.</p> <p>This capability reduces proof-of-concept setup from weeks to minutes and provides a repeatable path for customers and partners to accelerate adoption across multiple planning domains.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Instead of configuring cubes, dimensions, and reports manually, finance teams can immediately experience planning by selecting a business planning area (starting with OPEX). The system automatically generates the required model and connects to a prebuilt Power BI app, allowing planning to begin in minutes. This reduces proof-of-concept setup from weeks to clicks, accelerating time to value and simplifying adoption.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576747","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/business-performance-planning/business-performance-planning-overview"},{"id":"rm-576754","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Copilot and AI innovation - Understand forecast accuracy with AI explanations","desc":"<p>By combining forecast results with contextual insights, planners can gain a detailed understanding of the key factors influencing each forecast rather than simply viewing the numbers. This increased transparency builds confidence and supports more informed planning decisions.</p> <p>Key benefits include:</p> <ul> <li>See symmetric mean absolute percentage error (SMAPE) values.</li> <li>View historical data and forecast results in one place.</li> <li>Understand forecast drivers through AI-generated explanations.</li> <li>Gain greater confidence in planning outcomes.</li> <li>Make faster and more informed business decisions.</li> </ul> <p>These capabilities help planners spend less time analyzing forecast changes and more time acting.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Get a clear view of historical data alongside a calculated forecast supported by AI-generated explanations. This feature enhances planners' understanding of each forecast, builds confidence in the results, and enables better planning decisions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576754","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575292","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Agent 365 reporting availability for Microsoft platform agents","desc":"<p>Customers can now view agent insights in the Agent 365 Dashboard in Microsoft Viva Insights (Copilot Analytics) without an Agent 365 license. Customers will be able to view reporting on their Microsoft platform-built agents in one consolidated picture, along with context on who built each agent and why.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575292","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-513275","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage Community feed improvements","desc":"<p>Align the community feeds default experience with expected user behaviors; support triage and content review for users who want to read every message in a community.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-14","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513275","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-576178","title":"Power Apps: Access updated visuals for row summaries across forms and views","desc":"<p>The row summaries experience has a refreshed layout that makes AI-generated insights more prominent and easier to consume. Improved visual hierarchy (including clearer spacing, background and border treatments, status indicators, and generation labels) helps summaries stand apart from surrounding form sections so users can quickly identify key information.</p> <p>The visual treatment takes inspiration from similar AI-powered experiences in Microsoft 365 apps, creating a more recognizable and consistent presentation for AI-generated content. It also establishes a foundation for bringing insights from multiple sources into a unified summary experience over time.</p> <p>Microsoft-provided summaries from Dynamics 365 applications, including Customer Service and Sales, are also available directly from model-driven app view pages. Users can access relevant insights while browsing records in a grid without opening each record individually.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2610.2</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Users (always enabled)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576178","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/release-plan/2026wave1/power-apps/enhance-row-summaries-model-driven-apps"},{"id":"rm-576765","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Enable Process Intelligence Studio in object-centric process mining","desc":"<p>Process Intelligence Studio is a modern, flexible workspace designed for comprehensive process analysis. It provides a fully customizable analysis environment that combines multiple visualization and analysis components into cohesive, purpose-built workspaces. The platform supports both traditional and object-centric process mining methodologies, enabling analysis across simple linear processes and complex, multi-object scenarios.</p> <p>Core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Tab-based navigation: Organize related analyses into separate tabs within a single workspace, maintaining context while exploring different perspectives or process segments.</li> <li>Flexible layouts: Arrange tiles in customizable grid layouts, allowing you to position process maps, charts, tables, and metrics exactly where you need them for optimal visibility and comparison.</li> <li>Powerful tiles: Choose from a comprehensive library of visualization and analysis components—process map, performance metrics, attribute breakdowns, case lists, and statistical views.</li> <li>Unified filtering: Apply filters once and have them cascade across all tiles in your workspace, ensuring consistency and enabling rapid scenario comparison without manual reconfiguration.</li> <li>Object-centric support: Extends full functionality to OCPM models, enabling multi-dimensional analysis of interconnected objects, relationships, and cross-object metrics within the same intuitive interface.</li> </ul> <p>Process Intelligence Studio saves your workspace configurations, allowing teams to create reusable analysis templates and share standardized views across the organization for consistent process monitoring and improvement tracking.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Process Intelligence Studio eliminates the friction between your questions and your answers. Instead of navigating rigid dashboards or switching between disconnected tools, your teams work in a fluid, customizable environment that adapts to their analysis needs in real-time. This means faster time-to-insight, reduced training overhead, and the ability to tackle complex process questions without constantly restarting your analysis. Business analysts, process owners, and improvement teams can now build comprehensive views that tell the complete story: compare scenarios side-by-side, drill from overview to detail without losing context, and share ready-made analyses with stakeholders. The result is more confident decision-making, shortened analysis cycles, and broader adoption of process intelligence across your organization. With object-centric process mining (OCPM) support, you now unlock these benefits even for your most complex, interconnected business processes.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576765","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576807","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Assign task level calendar for precise planning","desc":"<p>This feature provides an experience to change the task calendar on the <strong>Customizable task details pane</strong>. To enable this feature, from project parameters select <strong>Enable Customize Task Pane</strong>.</p> <p>When enabled through feature control, this functionality lets you:</p> <ul> <li>Set a task-level calendar on the <strong>Customizable task details</strong> pane.</li> <li>Manage task-level calendars.</li> <li>Schedule API support.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>With project-level calendars, every task follows the same schedule, even when timing needs differ. That often means extra work and inaccurate plans. Task-level calendars change that. You can assign a unique calendar to each task, giving you control over working hours and timelines. This flexibility helps you build accurate schedules, reduce manual changes, and keep projects moving even when tasks vary. Combined with task-level schedule mode, you decide what the system adjusts, effort, duration, or units, while still setting custom hours for each task.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576807","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-576808","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Assign task level schedule mode for precise planning","desc":"<p>This feature provides an experience to change the task schedule mode on the <strong>Customizable task details pane</strong>. To enable this feature, from project parameters select <strong>Enable Customize Task Pane</strong>.</p> <p>When enabled through feature control, this functionality lets you:</p> <ul> <li>Set a task level schedule mode on the <strong>Customizable task details</strong> pane.</li> <li>Manage the task level schedule modes.</li> <li>Schedule API support.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>With traditional scheduling, you’re stuck using one mode for the entire project, even when tasks have different needs. That limitation adds extra work and leads to plans that don’t match reality. Task-level schedule mode changes that. You can pick the right mode for each task, no matter what the project default is. This flexibility helps you create accurate timelines, cut down on manual effort, and keep projects on track when scheduling requirements vary.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576808","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-management/customize-task-details-pane"},{"id":"rm-576862","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Copy externally scheduled projects","desc":"<p>Project Operations supports <strong>Externally scheduled</strong> projects, where organizations use their own scheduling engine and manage project schedules outside of Project Operations. Previously, the <strong>Copy Project</strong> capability was available only for Project for the Web scheduled projects. Customers using externally scheduled projects had to manually recreate project structures, configurations, and related data when starting similar projects or creating project templates.</p> <p>With this feature, <strong>Copy Project</strong> is now supported for externally scheduled projects, bringing parity across project types through a unified copy experience. You can copy an externally scheduled project either to a new project or to an existing empty project, simplifying project creation and template-based planning. As part of the enhanced copy experience, you can also review and update key project attributes before completing the copy operation, including fields such as Contracting Unit, Owning Company, Calendar Template, and other project-specific settings. This provides greater flexibility and enables organizations to adapt copied projects to their target business context without requiring post-copy updates.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>If you work with external scheduling tools, you can now skip the hassle of starting over. This update lets you copy those projects directly into Microsoft Dataverse, so creating a new project is quick and simple. You save time, cut down on manual work, and keep your team focused on delivering results instead of repeating tasks.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576862","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"January CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-management/copy-project"},{"id":"rm-576877","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Customize the task details pane","desc":"<p>In the task grid, when you select the <strong>i</strong> icon next to a task name, the <strong>Task details pane</strong> opens so you can enter more information. This pane is part of Microsoft Project for the web and is embedded in an iframe that makes it non-customizable.</p> <p>With this feature, you get a customizable task form. The form shows essential task attributes and lets you bring customization to the task pane. You can manage and track project tasks more easily in one place. This feature is managed through a feature flag in Project Parameters. When enabled, clicking the <strong>i</strong> icon opens a customizable task pane that lets you manage tasks and trigger business flows directly from the task grid. You can still access the standard Project task pane via the overflow menu, giving you complete flexibility to choose between the custom Dataverse task pane and the Office task pane based on your requirements.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can customize tasks right in the details pane without leaving the grid. No more switching tabs or opening extra forms, just a smooth, in-context experience that keeps work moving. This flexibility lets you shape task views to fit your processes by adding, removing, or formatting fields. You also save time and reduce errors with custom validations and workflows triggered directly from the pane, helping your team work faster and more efficiently.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576877","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"January CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-management/customize-task-details-pane"},{"id":"rm-576809","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable the Investment project feature","desc":"<p>When you enable the <strong>Enable investment project for Project Operations integrated with ERP</strong> setting, you activate this feature.</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Project Classification</strong>: The project manager uses this classification to mark a project as an investment project. Use this classification for internal projects. Don't link investment projects to customer-facing contracts.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Transaction Estimates</strong>: The project manager adds estimates and budgets for each transaction type. This feature supports better planning and cost tracking.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Contract Restrictions</strong>: The system blocks investment projects from project contracts. This restriction keeps investment projects for internal use only.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Financial Treatment</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>The system records all costs as work in progress (WIP).</li> <li>When you complete the project, the system lets you choose between two options. You can eliminate the project to generate a fixed asset. Or, you can transfer WIP costs to another ledger account. The choice depends on your organization's accounting strategy.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Investment project feature in Dynamics 365 Project Operations, integrated with ERP, enables organizations to manage internal capital initiatives such as infrastructure development, research and development, and asset creation. It enhances financial governance, streamlines asset capitalization, and aligns project execution with strategic goals.</p> <p>Organizations can capitalize long-term project costs to support compliance with accounting standards and improve financial reporting accuracy. The feature tracks all costs for items, time, and expenses as work in progress (WIP), so you have complete visibility and control.</p> <p>When you complete the project, the system automates the conversion of WIP costs into fixed assets. This automation eliminates manual reconciliation and ensures accurate asset registration.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576809","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"February CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-accounting/project-operations-investment-project"},{"id":"rm-576803","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Support currency data type in custom columns","desc":"<p>As part of our commitment to continuously improve Project Operations, we plan to expand the Enterprise Task Custom Columns capability in an upcoming release. This enhancement builds on the existing functionality that allows you to add Date, Text, Number, and Choice fields to the task grid.</p> <p>With this enhancement, you gain the ability to add currency data type fields as enterprise task custom columns. This change makes it easier to surface financial data directly in the task grid, eliminating the need for task form customizations.</p> <p>The process for creating and adding custom columns remains unchanged, ensuring a consistent and familiar workflow while offering expanded options. This feature will be enabled by default for all customers and doesn't require any additional configuration or action to enable.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature lets you add Currency fields as custom columns in your task grid, so you can keep essential financial details where you need them. It saves you time by reducing extra navigation and eliminates the hassle of customizing task forms. With more data in one place, you make faster decisions and streamline your processes without added complexity.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576803","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-576800","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Support lookup data type in custom columns","desc":"<p>As part of our commitment to continuously improve Project Operations, we plan to expand the <strong>Enterprise Task Custom Columns</strong> capability. This enhancement builds on the existing functionality that allows you to add <strong>Date</strong>, <strong>Text</strong>, <strong>Number</strong>, and <strong>Choice</strong> fields to the task grid.</p> <p>With this enhancement, you gain the ability to add <strong>Lookup data type</strong> fields as enterprise task custom columns. This change makes it easier to surface relational data directly in the task grid, eliminating the need for task form customizations.</p> <p>The process for creating and adding custom columns remains unchanged, ensuring a consistent and familiar workflow while offering expanded options.</p> <p>This feature is enabled by default for all customers and doesn't require any additional configuration or action to enable.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature is designed for teams that manage complex projects and need quick access to key information. By adding Lookup fields directly to the task grid, you can keep critical data in one place without switching screens. This saves time, reduces manual customization, and helps your team stay focused on delivering results instead of managing forms.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-576861","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Update key project fields using Copy project","desc":"<p>Today, when you select <strong>Copy Project</strong>, the system creates a project and copies everything from the source project to the newly created project. In this flow, you aren't allowed to update fields like contracting unit, owning company, and other key fields for the new project.</p> <p>When this feature is enabled in the feature control settings, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Use the new unified copy project experience.</li> <li>Copy a project to a new project and to an existing empty project. Select the project as the target during the copy process.</li> <li>Specify important project attributes, including the Contracting Unit, Owning Company, Schedule Mode, and Calendar Template before creating a copy of a project.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>In Project Operations, copying a project has always been possible, but the current process limits your ability to change critical details. The new experience changes that. Now, you can update essential fields while duplicating a project, giving you greater control and flexibility to align with your business needs and save time managing project data.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576861","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"January CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-management/copy-project"},{"id":"rm-576640","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Lead management - Prioritize your hottest leads first with next best actions","desc":"<p>Get the next best actions for leads right on your Dynamics 365 leads grid, and navigate to see Sales Qualification Agent's research and pregenerated email suggestions. The actions show a preview of the lead, a summary of why it's a hot or high-intent lead, and the topic that the lead is interested in.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Sales Qualification Agent meticulously researches every lead and identifies which ones are hot, warm or cold. When configured to autonomously engage, it identifies the ones that explicitly state their purchase intent. Now, you can see hot and high-intent leads prominently on your leads grid in Dynamics 365 Sales so that you can immediately focus on the next best actions you need to take to build a pipeline. With Sales Qualification Agent, your best move is now right at your fingertips.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576640","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576739","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Opportunity acceleration - Enable custom source onboarding in Recommended Action","desc":"<p>This feature enables admins to register custom external insight sources through a step-by-step guided onboarding wizard. Once onboarded, the custom source appears alongside out-of-the-box agents in the Recommended Action Sources list and is governed by the same enable/disable controls. Actions from custom sources are normalized into action cards, ranked alongside built-in actions, and follow consistent UI patterns, execution flows, and prioritization models, ensuring a seamless and unified seller experience.</p> <p>The feature isn't enabled automatically. Admins must complete the guided registration flow by providing a source name and description, after which the system generates a unique source ID and registers the source for action ingestion and governance. Admins can enable or disable the custom source's participation in Recommended Action as needed, maintaining relevant governance and control.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You get a unified system that consolidates all seller actions from both built-in and custom sources, creating a single list of prioritized actions that the sellers need to focus on. This improves your sellers' productivity by prioritizing what to do next, saving time and reducing decision fatigue. It also enhances governance and visibility, helping your business operate more efficiently and with greater trust in the insights provided.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576739","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576783","title":"Dynamics 365 Sustainability: Streamline ESG internal data collection","desc":"<p>Under the streamlining data import, collection, and management product area, the data collection feature provides a structured and guided way for organizations to gather ESG information from internal teams and departments, ensuring that required data flows consistently from the people who own it. Practitioners can configure data owners, create targeted requests, assign reporting periods, set due dates, and optionally apply approval workflows to ensure data is validated before use.</p> <p>This feature is specifically designed for internal data providers, such as facility managers, HR teams, and business units, enabling organizations to capture operational inputs that are not available through automated ingestion or external systems and are often collected manually through asynchronous, hard‑to‑track communications. It ensures that internal data needed for calculations, metrics, and compliance reporting is collected accurately and securely. External value‑chain data is handled separately through the ESG Value Chain Portal, keeping internal and external processes cleanly segmented.</p> <p>Data managers can orchestrate collection at scale using data collection plans, enabling bulk requests, automated reminders, and clear tracking of submission status. Data owners receive an email link to a tailored MSM experience with the requests, allowing them to submit responses, add comments, and attach evidence or supporting documents. Approvers can review submitted data, evidence, and approval records in a unified workflow.</p> <p>This feature is automatically available in the solution and can be accessed from the left navigation under the Data collection section.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This data collection feature empowers teams to centralize and scale ESG data collection by gathering structured inputs from internal teams and departments. Customers benefit from improved data accuracy, reduced manual effort, and clearer accountability across contributors. By standardizing submissions and enabling governed workflows, organizations can accelerate preparation for CSRD, GRI, and other reporting frameworks while increasing confidence in the completeness and auditability of their data. It also supports downstream calculations and reporting processes by providing structured, validated inputs.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sustainability"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576783","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-576781","title":"PowerApps: Building modern apps - Modernize model-driven apps with the header and navigation refresh feature","desc":"<p>The header and navigation refresh feature delivers a modern, intuitive, and efficient model app experience across the app shell, form pages, and view pages. This update improves visual clarity, reduces vertical space usage, and aligns with modern Microsoft 365 design patterns.</p> <p>As the feature transitions to general availability (GA), the refreshed experience remains opt-in, allowing makers to control adoption and validate the experience at their own pace. Makers can switch between the classic and refreshed experience using the <strong>Header and navigation refresh</strong> app setting:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Auto (default)</strong>: The new experience is off for apps, except those apps created using Plans.</li> <li><strong>Yes</strong>: Turns on the new header and navigation experience.</li> <li><strong>No</strong>: Keeps the classic header and navigation experience.</li> </ul> <p>Key aspects include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Modern app header</strong>: A simplified header layout with improved spacing and icons that align with modern Microsoft 365 design patterns and enhance brand coherence across apps.</li> <li><strong>Streamlined sitemap</strong>: A cleaner, more readable sitemap structure that helps you find what you need faster.</li> <li><strong>More working space on forms</strong>: The command bar is now the only element fixed at the top of the page — the summary area and form header scroll off with the rest of the form, giving users more room to work. When the form header scrolls out of view, a <strong>condensed sticky header</strong> attaches below the command bar so the record is always identifiable.</li> <li><strong>More responsive form header</strong>: The form header adapts more gracefully across window sizes and content densities.</li> <li><strong>Tighter spacing and margins</strong>: Targeted adjustments across the app improve consistency, readability, and overall page density.</li> <li><strong>New command ordering</strong>: Injected system commands like <strong>Show As</strong> and <strong>Show Chart</strong> now appear in the third position, after <strong>New</strong> and <strong>Delete</strong>.</li> </ul> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2609.1</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Users (enabled by admins or makers)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The refreshed header and navigation experience provides a cleaner, more efficient layout across the app shell, forms, and views. These updates help you work efficiently by increasing your working area on forms and views, reducing the time you spend navigating pages, and aligning the experience with the latest Microsoft 365 design patterns.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576781","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"May CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/user/modern-fluent-design#header-and-navigation-refresh"},{"id":"rm-576777","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Speed up processing with Known Senders in Payables Agent","desc":"<p>This feature introduces email review policy and a <strong>Known Senders</strong> list page to give accounts payable teams more control over which incoming emails require human approval before the Payables Agent processes them.</p> <p>A new <strong>Email review</strong> field in the Payables Agent setup lets administrators choose when incoming emails require human approval. The following options are available:</p> <ul> <li>Always: Every email requires approval, regardless of the sender.</li> <li>Never: No emails require approval.</li> <li>Only if untrusted (recommended): Only emails from senders who aren't on the list of known senders require review. This is the recommended setting for most organizations.</li> </ul> <p>Administrators must explicitly select an option before they start to monitor the email inbox. To ensure that they make an active decision, a default isn't preselected for the field. Every known sender is subject to a setting that sets the review policy for the specific sender.</p> <p>When you set the email review policy to <strong>Manage per sender</strong>, the agent evaluates incoming emails in the following order:</p> <ul> <li>Invoice is uploaded and not received via email: No review required.</li> <li>Email subfolder is configured: All emails in the monitored subfolder are treated as trusted. No review required.</li> <li>Sender is on the Known Senders list: Action depends on the configured value (Ask, Approve, or Reject).</li> <li>Internal sender (same organization, not on the list): No review required. Internal detection uses email authentication headers (planned to be available in 2026 wave 2, version 29.0.).</li> </ul> <p>Administrators can maintain a list of known senders, each with a configured policy:</p> <ul> <li>Ask: The email requires human approval.</li> <li>Approve: The agent processes the invoice without review.</li> <li>Reject: The sender is blocked and the attachment isn't processed.</li> </ul> <p>To build the list organically, after you review an email and want to continue, the sender is added automatically to the list of known senders, provided that the <strong>Manage per sender</strong> policy is active. Security telemetry is logged for each auto-addition.</p> <p>This feature is available from the August minor release of 2026 release wave 1.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Payables Agent processes vendor invoices received by email, but today every incoming email requires supervisor approval before the agent can act on it, unless email review is disabled entirely. This creates friction for accounts payable teams who repeatedly receive invoices from the same vendors. They must manually approve each email, even from senders they already trust. The Known Senders feature lets businesses define which senders the agent can process automatically, reducing manual intervention while maintaining control over unknown or unverified sources. With this capability, organizations can safely default email review to off, moving closer to fully autonomous invoice processing.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576777","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576832","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Country and regional - Enable electronic invoicing in France","desc":"<p>Business Central adds support for e-invoicing and e‑reporting in France, following the DGFiP five‑corner model. Microsoft doesn't operate as a certified Partner Dematerialization Platform (PDP); instead, companies can use existing E‑Document connectors to exchange invoices and lifecycle messages through certified PDP providers. The localization app enables two compliant formats: <strong>Peppol BIS3</strong> (XML) and <strong>Factur‑X</strong> (PDF/A‑3 with embedded XML).</p> <p>The feature supports sending and receiving structured e‑invoices for sales and purchase processes, including all mandatory lifecycle statuses. Companies will use the standard <strong>E-Document</strong> module with the localization app for setup, where they can select one of the supported formats: Peppol BIS3 and Factur-X. Formats and integration services can be configured by running the <strong>E-Document Service</strong> page. Business Central also generates <strong>Transaction E‑Reporting</strong> for operations where structured invoices are not required but are required to be reported to French authorities in specific periods (monthly or quarterly).</p> <p>This functionality ensures that Business Central meets French e‑invoicing and CTC obligations effective September 2026, supporting invoice lifecycle traceability, and simplifying reporting obligations.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>French e-invoicing and e-reporting mandates will become mandatory for all VAT-registered businesses from September 2026. This feature helps your company maintain compliance with DGFiP regulations, avoid penalties, and streamline invoice exchange through certified PDPs. By supporting Peppol BIS3 and Factur-X formats, you can automate invoice processing, enhance interoperability, and reduce manual effort, all while fulfilling legal requirements for B2B transactions and real-time reporting.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576832","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/localfunctionality/france/enable-electronic-invoicing-france"},{"id":"rm-576813","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Electronic documents - Use payments with the E-Document framework","desc":"<p>You can mark an e-document as fully paid, partially paid, or unpaid. The system sends this information through accounts payable access points or receives it through accounts receivable access points, based on your e-document configuration. The payment tracking feature in e-documents includes details such as:</p> <ul> <li>Date of payment collection</li> <li>Amount collected, including VAT</li> <li>Base amount and VAT amount at the time of payment</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Boost productivity with enhanced tracking of e-documents by quickly identifying whether each document is fully paid, partially paid, or unpaid. This feature also helps businesses meet legal requirements in certain countries.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576813","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576772","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Omnichannel customer experiences - Handle duplicate callback requests in overflowing queues","desc":"<p>In the in-queue and pre-queue overflow settings within the Copilot Service admin center, administrators can define the following settings:</p> <ul> <li>Prevent duplicate callback requests from the same phone number.</li> <li>Define deduplication logic using combinations of caller phone number, channel phone number, and queue ID.</li> <li>Configure caller experiences when a duplicate is detected. An option to end the call or play a custom message in a loop is available. For example: “You are already in queue to receive a callback when a customer service representative is available. Your latest wait time is 12 minutes. You can choose to continue waiting on this call if needed or disconnect and receive the callback.”</li> <li>Specify the phone number to initiate the callback from.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature delivers significant benefits by enhancing customer experience, operational efficiency, and administrative control. It prevents redundant callback requests from the same phone number, reducing unnecessary loads on representatives and systems. Administrators gain flexibility to configure deduplication logic and tailor the caller experience, including custom messaging when duplicates are detected.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576772","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576779","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Use average wait-time diagnostics for wait-time predictions","desc":"<p>This feature introduces comprehensive event logging in Application Insights that captures exactly how average wait time is computed, evaluated, and shown to customers.</p> <p><strong>End-to-end average wait-time diagnostic events</strong></p> <p>The system logs detailed AWT diagnostic events in Application Insights at two key moments:</p> <ul> <li>When a conversation begins and the system evaluates whether average wait time should be shown.</li> <li>When the availability APIs return the average wait-time value (if applicable).</li> </ul> <p>Each event includes standard metadata (channel type, organization ID, conversation ID, scenario, and subscenario) and feature-specific fields such as calculated average wait time in seconds, whether average wait time was shared with customers, and reason. This allows administrators to pinpoint the exact cause when average wait time is missing or is an unexpected value.</p> <p><strong>Historical analytics for average wait-time accuracy</strong></p> <p>Supervisors can compare:</p> <ul> <li>Average wait-time values shown to customers.</li> <li>Actual wait times experienced by conversations.</li> </ul> <p>This helps teams validate prediction quality, identify discrepancies, and tune overflow thresholds.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Average wait time (AWT) is one of the most visible and impactful signals in a contact center, used to manage customer expectations and trigger overflow logic. But when average wait time doesn't appear or seems incorrect, supervisors often lack the visibility needed to understand why.</p> <p>Average wait-time diagnostics brings transparency and control to average wait-time calculation by giving administrators and supervisors detailed diagnostic logs, historical analytics, and real-time queue level average wait-time values that they can use to troubleshoot issues and validate system behavior without needing engineering or support.</p> <p>The feature dramatically reduces explainability gaps, increases trust in the system, and helps contact centers make data-driven staffing and overflow decisions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576779","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576837","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Unified routing - Use pick-based assignment method for work items","desc":"<p>Use the <strong>No auto assignment</strong> method for queues in Copilot Service admin center when you want routed conversations to remain unassigned after they enter a queue. Instead of being assigned automatically, conversations stay in the queue until a service representative picks them up from their Inbox or a supervisor assigns them manually.</p> <p>This assignment method supports a pick-based work distribution model, giving supervisors and service representatives greater control over how work is handled. Unlike the push-based model used by other out-of-the-box assignment methods, which automatically assign conversations based on representative availability and capacity, the no auto assignment method allows teams to review incoming work and decide who should handle it. This approach is well suited for organizations that prefer manual oversight, specialized work selection, or supervisor-managed assignments.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Improve operational control and consistency by enabling service representative-led work distribution. Conversations remain available in the queue until manually assigned by supervisors or picked by representatives, helping teams handle specialized, regulated, or sensitive interactions effectively.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576837","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576775","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Copilot and AI innovation - Classify emails by category and subcategory with Case Management Agent","desc":"<p>With email classification, administrators can define a custom taxonomy of categories and subcategories to automatically classify inbound emails in Dynamics 365 Customer Service. AI analyzes the email subject and body, then stores the assigned category or subcategory on the email activity record. Case Management Agent, automatic record creation rules, Power Automate flows, reporting, and other downstream processes can use this value to determine how to handle the email.</p> <p>Administrators can enable email classification and define category and subcategory names and descriptions. They can also set conditions that determine which emails are classified, such as specific mailboxes, sender domains, languages, and so forth. When the feature is enabled, the system qualifies inbound emails and automatically classifies them by using the Case Management Agent flow. Administrators can also manually update an assigned category or subcategory, or disable classification to stop processing new emails.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Email classification gives you control over how incoming emails are managed before any action is taken. It automatically sorts messages so you can ignore irrelevant ones, let the Case Management Agent handle routine issues, and focus on those that truly need human attention. This reduces clutter from non-support emails like thank-you notes, newsletters, and spam, allowing both AI and your team to concentrate on what matters most. The result is time saved, lower processing costs, and the ability to scale automated email handling confidently without adding operational risk.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576775","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576853","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Associate forecast scenarios with planning groups","desc":"<p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>When creating or editing a forecast scenario, forecasters can optionally select a planning group.</li> <li>When a planning group is selected, the <strong>Timezone</strong>, <strong>Channel</strong>, and <strong>Queue</strong> values are populated from the planning group definition and become read-only. This behavior keeps the scenario aligned with its planning group.</li> <li>When no planning group is selected, forecasters can manually edit the <strong>Timezone</strong>, <strong>Channel</strong>, and <strong>Queue</strong> values. Existing scenario creation workflows remain unchanged.</li> <li>The forecast scenario list includes a <strong>Planning group</strong> column that forecasters can use to sort and filter scenarios.</li> <li>Capacity plans created from a forecast scenario inherit the scenario’s planning group. For a capacity plan created from an uploaded file, forecasters can select the planning group manually.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Access and prerequisites</strong></p> <p>To use Workforce Management capabilities, an administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from the Power Platform admin center.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Contact center demand rarely aligns perfectly with a single queue. Most lines of business, sites, or skill pools rely on multiple queues and channels that share the same agents and service goals.</p> <p>Planning group support brings these queues and channels together so you can forecast them as one unit. Instead of juggling separate scenarios, you work with a single view where volume and average handle time reflect the actual demand pool your team staffs. This means you can pass accurate numbers straight to capacity planning and scheduling without extra steps. You save time, reduce errors, and measure performance at the level your business truly operates.</p> <p>If you manage dozens of queues across multiple lines of business, this feature shifts forecasting from a queue-by-queue task to planning at the scale of your entire operation.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576853","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576852","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Create capacity plans for planning groups","desc":"<p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>When creating or editing a capacity plan, planners can select a <strong>Planning group</strong>.</li> <li>A capacity plan created from a forecast scenario automatically inherits the scenario’s planning group. This behavior keeps the forecast scenario and capacity plan aligned without requiring additional input.</li> <li>For a capacity plan created from an uploaded forecast file, planners can select the planning group manually.</li> <li>The capacity plan calculates staffing requirements from the combined demand of the queues and channels in the planning group instead of providing separate results for each queue.</li> <li>The capacity plan list includes a <strong>Planning group</strong> column that planners can use to sort and filter plans.</li> <li>Capacity plans created without a planning group continue to work as before.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Access and prerequisites</strong><br> To use Workforce Management capabilities, an administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from the Power Platform admin center.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Staffing decisions should focus on the entire team, not individual queues. Typically, one pool of representatives supports multiple queues and channels, but traditional capacity planning treats each queue separately. This creates multiple FTE estimates that planners must manually combine, often inflating requirements because shared staffing efficiencies are ignored.</p> <p>With planning group support, you can manage capacity for the whole group as one unit. A single plan covers all queues, so FTE, shrinkage, and service goals are based on the combined demand your team actually handles. This approach gives you accurate staffing needs and real cost efficiency instead of overstated totals from isolated queue calculations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576854","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Filter adherence historical analytics by planning group","desc":"<p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>The adherence historical analytics report includes a planning group filter that workforce managers can use to scope results to one or more planning groups.</li> <li>The planning group filter works with the report’s existing filters, allowing managers to combine planning groups, date ranges, and other report parameters in a single view.</li> <li>The report recalculates adherence metrics for the filtered scope, providing a group-level view of adherence performance instead of a contact center-wide aggregate.</li> <li>The report associates representatives with planning groups through their scheduled shifts. This behavior keeps historical reporting aligned with the shift plans used to calculate adherence.</li> <li>Planning groups must be configured and have assigned representatives before the filter returns results.</li> <li>In Copilot Service workspace, go to <strong>Workforce management</strong>.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Access and prerequisites</strong></p> <ul> <li>To use Workforce Management capabilities, an administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from the Power Platform admin center.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Adherence only matters when it reflects how your work is organized. Until now, historical adherence reports didn’t account for planning groups, making it hard to see if performance dips came from a single under-supported queue or were spread across the operation.</p> <p>With planning group support, you can focus your analysis on the groups that matter and compare adherence across them for the same time period. This gives you clearer insights and helps you make smarter staffing decisions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576854","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576855","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Workforce engagement management - Filter the adherence tracker by planning group","desc":"<p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>The adherence tracker includes a planning group filter that supervisors can use to scope the view to a specific planning group.</li> <li>The planning group filter works with the existing shift plan and service representative filters, so supervisors can combine filters to refine a single view.</li> <li>The tracker displays representatives based on the planning groups associated with their scheduled shifts. This behavior keeps the tracker aligned with the shift plan used to calculate adherence.</li> <li>The tracker saves each supervisor’s filter selections across sessions and opens with their previous scope.</li> <li>The tracker recalculates adherence percentages and out-of-adherence counts for the filtered scope, providing a planning group-level view of intraday adherence.</li> <li>In Copilot Service workspace, go to <strong>Workforce management</strong> &gt; <strong>Adherence tracker</strong>.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Access and prerequisites</strong></p> <p>To use Workforce Management capabilities, an administrator must install the Workforce Management for Customer Service package from the Power Platform admin center.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Supervising large contact centers is tough when you have to scan endless lists to find your team. Now, with planning group support, you can filter the adherence tracker to just the groups you manage. That means you spot issues faster and act right away, keeping service levels on track in real time instead of fixing problems after the fact. This feature scales for enterprise operations with hundreds of representatives and aligns with the same planning group structure you already use for forecasting, staffing, and scheduling. It saves time, reduces complexity, and helps you stay focused on what matters most: delivering consistent service.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576840","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Boost technician productivity - Add simplified lookup control","desc":"<p>A new Power Apps component framework control, Drawer Lookup, is now available for lookup fields on forms. This control provides a streamlined mobile UI, reducing visible clutter and minimizing taps compared to the standard lookup. It's available exclusively for mobile experiences.</p> <p><strong>How to use</strong>:</p> <ol> <li>In Power Apps, open the table form containing the lookup field.</li> <li>Select the lookup field and choose <strong>+</strong> to add the new control.</li> <li>Select <strong>Drawer Lookup Control</strong> and set it for the phone and tablet client.</li> <li><strong>Save</strong> and publish the form. The mobile app will reflect the change after the next sync or refresh.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Enablement</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>This is a UI‑level control applied to the lookup field and doesn't require a platform feature flag.</li> <li>It is configured per form/lookup and applies only to mobile experiences. Web experiences will continue to use the standard lookup unless the control is also added for the web.</li> <li>To revert, remove the control and republish the form.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You’ll speed up mobile tasks and reduce friction by replacing the standard lookup with a simplified control designed for small screens. This control decreases clicks, lowers cognitive load, and helps your team complete work faster in the field.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576840","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/guidance/resources/field-service-mobile-add-lookup"},{"id":"rm-576790","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Boost technician productivity - Capture and review notes with mobile notes control","desc":"<p>The mobile notes control introduces a unified, mobile-first experience for creating and consuming notes directly within entity forms. Makers add this Power Apps component framework control to a form to replace the default note experience with a streamlined interface that supports:</p> <ul> <li>In-form note creation with text, images, and videos.</li> <li>Rich note consumption with optimized rendering for media and text.</li> <li>Clean, touch-friendly layout designed for fast interaction in field conditions.</li> </ul> <p>Notes created using this control are written to annotations for the related record. The control provides an enhanced viewing experience with rich previews and improved readability. It renders note-type activities only; other activity types do not appear in this view.</p> <p>This control is available for mobile use only and doesn't change the web experience.</p> <p><strong>How to use</strong></p> <ol> <li>In Power Apps, open the table form where you want to enable notes.</li> <li>Add the mobile notes control to the desired section of the form.</li> <li>Configure the control to show the capture experience, the consumption experience, or both.</li> <li>Save and publish the form.</li> </ol> <p>The mobile app shows the new experience after the next sync.</p> <p><strong>Enablement and scope</strong></p> <p>This is a UI-level framework control applied per form and is optimized for mobile. No feature flags are required. To revert, remove the control from the form and republish.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>If you manage field service teams, every minute your technicians spend switching between tools or digging through cluttered notes is time they're not completing jobs. With a mobile-optimized notes experience, frontline workers can quickly capture rich updates, including text, images, and video, and immediately access them in a clean, easy-to-scan format.</p> <p>This reduces task interruptions, improves documentation quality, and helps technicians find the right information faster on-site. The result is faster task completion, fewer return visits caused by missing details, and a more productive frontline workforce.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576790","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/guidance/resources/field-service-mobile-take-notes"},{"id":"rm-576825","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Boost productivity with Copilot - Open records in Dynamics 365 ERP applications with deep links from copilot responses","desc":"<p>The Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server enables copilots to respond to prompts related to data across the Dynamics 365 ERP suite of applications. Users expect visibility into how copilot responses relate to the underlying business data and system records. With this release, copilot responses generated from the Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server will include deep links to the data used to generate the response, improving transparency, traceability, and trust in the AI-generated responses.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Users receive transparency, traceability, and trust in copilot chat experiences with citations and deep links to ERP records in the copilot responses.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/mcp/mcp-deep-links"},{"id":"rm-576773","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: One Dynamics One Platform - Enable parallel processing for Archive long‑term retention job execution","desc":"<p>The parallel execution for Archive long‑term retention jobs feature delivers a major scalability upgrade to the archival framework by enabling parallel processing across job creation, marking, and scheduling. Each archive job remains aligned to the existing architectural principle of being defined per legal entity and per contract type (for example, General Ledger, Tax Transactions, or Sales Order), but the execution pipeline is now partitioned and processed concurrently to reduce total archive duration.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature introduces parallel execution for Archive long‑term retention jobs, enabling the system to execute multiple Archive long‑term retention jobs in parallel for a legal entity under the same archive scenario. By leveraging parallelism, long‑term retention throughput increases, dramatically reducing overall archive duration and minimizing impact on production systems.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576773","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/sysadmin/archive-data"},{"id":"rm-576797","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Business performance - Try the new financial planning and analysis planning experience in Power BI","desc":"<p>The financial planning and analysis planning experience is a downloadable Power BI app and report template that enables users to explore, analyze, and interact with financial planning and analysis plans directly in Power BI.</p> <p>The app is preconfigured to connect to Business performance planning cubes and dimensions deployed in Dataverse and provides a ready‑to‑use planning and analysis experience across core financial planning and analysis use cases, including:</p> <ul> <li>Driver-based revenue planning and scenario comparison.</li> <li>OPEX and workforce planning with assumption adjustments.</li> <li>CAPEX planning and financial impact analysis.</li> <li>Cost allocations and approvals visibility.</li> <li>Reporting, variance analysis, and management commentary (BVA).</li> </ul> <p>Users interact with the solution entirely from Power BI, using Business performance planning custom visuals to adjust planning values, test scenarios, and analyze outcomes. Planning inputs are written back to the underlying Business performance planning data model in Dataverse, keeping analysis and planning tightly connected.</p> <p>This Power BI app is designed to demonstrate how financial planning and analysis teams plan, analyze, and iterate inside Power BI, using a consistent and repeatable set of reports connected to prebuilt financial planning and analysis planning models. It focuses on illustrating planning workflows, decision-making, and cross‑domain impact, rather than report authoring or data model configuration.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature provides a hands-on, end-to-end demonstration of how Business performance planning enables integrated planning directly in a Power BI app.</p> <p>Customers, partners, and field teams can experience how strategic decisions, workforce plans, operating expenses, capital investments, and revenue forecasts connect into a single planning flow. This helps stakeholders visualize the value of planning in Power BI, supports customer evaluations, and enables consistent, repeatable demos without custom report development.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576797","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-576859","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Configure maximum daily time entry duration","desc":"<p>Project Operations sets a 24-hour limit on daily time entry hours that can be logged (including vacation hours). Administrators can modify this out-of-the-box validation in the Parameters section to meet their organization’s needs. Administrators can set a preferred maximum duration (in minutes) and provide a more realistic limit (for example, 9 hours) for time entry users. This configuration is checked each time a new time entry is created or modified.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can now set a limit on the number of hours logged in time entries, making it easier to keep reporting consistent and aligned with your organization’s policies.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/time-entry-configurations"},{"id":"rm-576804","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Implement access restrictions on the task grid","desc":"<p>This feature adds a security system that lets administrators restrict what users can access inside the Project for the web iFrame on projects they access but don't join as team members. Project managers can use the same system to set restrictions for team members on their projects.</p> <p>When this feature is enabled in the feature control settings, the following changes occur:</p> <ul> <li>Access restrictions are updated on user level and project team member levels.</li> <li>At user level, \"Read only\" and \"Full Access\" are supported.</li> <li>At project team member level, \"Read only\", \"Full Access\", and \"Custom\" are supported.</li> <li>\"Custom\" access can be configured for create, update, and delete tasks separately.</li> <li>The access control is applied at the task grid level.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Today, when you open a project record, you can make unlimited changes in the Microsoft Project for the web iFrame, including creating, editing, or deleting tasks, dependencies, and goals. This update gives you control over what actions users can take in that iFrame, helping you protect data integrity and manage permissions more effectively.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576804","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"May CY2025"},{"id":"rm-576805","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Import projects in MPP files into existing projects","desc":"<p>Previously, importing an .mpp file always created a new project. The import process copied the work breakdown structure from the .mpp file into the new project. You couldn't import a .mpp file into an existing project. This limitation made it difficult to manage projects when overall planning happens in Project Operations and individual planning happened offline in Microsoft Project for desktop.</p> <p>With this feature, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Choose to import the .mpp file into either a new project or an existing project.</li> <li>Update key project attributes, such as <strong>Contracting Unit</strong> and <strong>Owning Company</strong>, directly within the import experience.</li> <li>Know the project is imported based on the selected import option and configured settings.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Import Microsoft Project (.mpp) files directly into your empty projects to speed up setup. This helps you avoid starting from scratch and keeps your team focused on delivering results instead of managing project creation.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576805","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"August CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/expense/update-expense-mobile-app"},{"id":"rm-576806","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Seller experiences - Copy opportunities for repeat deals","desc":"<p>Administrators can control whether the Copy Opportunity feature is available. When enabled, sellers can duplicate an existing opportunity to quickly create a new one.</p> <p>The new opportunity retains key customer, deal, product, stakeholder, and custom-field information from the source opportunity, including hidden custom fields. Product line items are copied with their quantities and pricing; inactive products are excluded and recorded in the audit summary.</p> <p>To ensure the copied opportunity starts as a new sales deal, system-generated and outcome-related fields are reset. For example, the new opportunity is created with an Open status, and starts at the first stage of the sales process.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>If you manage repeat deals, you can start new opportunities by copying a proven one instead of rebuilding it every time. Dynamics 365 Sales carries forward the key details your team needs, including customer information, products, stakeholders, and ratings. You spend less time on setup, reduce data entry errors, and move deals into the pipeline faster with a more consistent sales process.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576806","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/sales/create-edit-opportunity-sales#copy-an-opportunity-preview"},{"id":"rm-576843","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Activate Enterprise Data in Copilot - Create Dataverse agent users with Microsoft Entra agent identity","desc":"<p>Organizations can securely deploy AI agents to access and interact with Dataverse data by using enterprise‑managed Microsoft Entra agent identities. This feature enables agents to be provisioned as Dataverse agent users with dedicated, least‑privileged security roles based on their intended capabilities. This feature ensures agents have only the access required to perform tasks autonomously or on behalf of users.</p> <p>By using identity‑based role assignment and full auditing of agent‑driven actions, organizations can enforce security and compliance policies across both human users and AI agents while maintaining traceability of data access and changes within Dataverse environments.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enables secure, compliant management of AI agents in Microsoft Dataverse, which reduces risk and improves governance for autonomous and interactive agents.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576843","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/admin/create-users#agent-users-preview"},{"id":"rm-576788","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Improved enterprise experiences in Power Platform - Enhance Dataverse record descriptions for Copilot /mention","desc":"<p>End users of Microsoft 365 Copilot will see improved Microsoft Dataverse, Dynamics 365, and Power Apps record references in Context IQ with richer, more descriptive labels that include environment, app, and table information. This makes it easier to identify and select the correct records during Copilot interactions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enables Microsoft 365 Copilot to surface business data with meaningful context, reducing confusion from generic labels and helping users quickly identify the right records to drive faster workflows and more reliable decision-making.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576788","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/admin/link-records-outlook-web"},{"id":"rm-576776","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Try Payables Agent for free without setting up email","desc":"<p>Payables Agent introduces a free trial mode that any user can start without help from an administrator or having paid credits.</p> <p>You can start the trial directly from the agent setup card or from the <strong>Purchase Invoices</strong> page. You don't need to have an administrator role or configure an email account. You upload invoice PDFs manually to start processing, bypassing the email-based sourcing flow entirely. The trial activates immediately the first time you upload an invoice. The trial includes 50 free invoice uploads. Each upload counts against the quota. You can track your remaining quota on the agent setup card throughout the trial. The full agent workflow is available during the trial:</p> <ul> <li>Extract invoice data</li> <li>Match vendors</li> <li>Suggest lines</li> <li>Create and finalize purchase invoice drafts</li> </ul> <p>You can experience the same capabilities that you would after subscribing. If you use up your quota of 50 invoices, continued use requires available credits.</p> <p>This feature is available from the May minor release of 2026 release wave 1.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Trying out the Payables Agent currently requires that you configure an email connection, which is a step that creates friction before a user has even seen what the agent does. Accounts payable clerks and accountants who want to explore the agent often can't do so on their own, because setting up email often requires help from an administrator.</p> <p>This feature lets any user start a Payables Agent free trial by uploading invoice files directly, with no email configuration required. Companies get a quota of 50 free invoices to experience the full agent workflow, including data extraction, vendor matching, line suggestion, and draft creation and finalization. By removing the technical barrier and the need to involve an administrator, more users can discover the agent's value firsthand and build the case for adoption within their organization.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576776","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-576836","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Sell to business customers on more Shopify plans with B2B company sync","desc":"<p>Shopify expanded its B2B capabilities to all plans, and the Shopify Connector for Business Central is updated accordingly. Core B2B features that previously required a Shopify Plus subscription now work on Basic, Grow, and Advanced plans.</p> <p>The following capabilities are available on all Shopify plans:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Company sync</strong>: Import Shopify B2B companies and company locations and map them to customers in Business Central.</li> <li><strong>B2B order processing</strong>: When a B2B order arrives, the connector identifies the company and resolves the correct bill-to and ship-to customer based on the company location.</li> <li><strong>Market catalogs</strong>: Assign catalogs to B2B markets for price synchronization. Basic, Grow, and Advanced plans support up to three active market catalog assignments (unlimited on Plus).</li> </ul> <p>The following features require Advanced or Plus plans:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Direct company catalogs</strong>: Assign catalogs to specific companies or company locations for customer-level pricing. The <strong>B2B Catalogs</strong> page and the <strong>Auto Create B2B Catalog</strong> toggle are only available in the Advanced and Plus plans.</li> <li><strong>Staff member mapping</strong>: Import Shopify staff members and map them to Business Central salespeople.</li> </ul> <p>If you're already using Shopify, to get the updated B2B availability, you must update the plan information for the connector. An easy way to do that is to turn off the Shopify connector and then turn it on again. To do that, open the <strong>Shopify Shop Card</strong> page, turn off the <strong>Enabled</strong> toggle, and then turn it back on.</p> <p>Learn more at <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/shopify/synchronize-customers\">Synchronize customers and companies</a>.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This change removes a key barrier for merchants who sell wholesale through Shopify but don't use the Plus plan. Market catalogs, payment terms, and B2B order processing are available on all plans, so more businesses can manage their wholesale and direct-to-consumer operations from a single connected platform.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576836","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-576844","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Financial Management - Calculate taxes for plastic and sugar","desc":"<p>Business Central introduces new capabilities in excise journals to calculate tax amounts for plastic and sugar based on legislation requirements that use weight, content, and transaction quantities as the basis for excise taxes. The new <strong>Excise Tax Type</strong>, <strong>Qty. for Excise Tax</strong>, and <strong>Excise UOM</strong> fields on the <strong>Item Card</strong> and <strong>Fixed Asset Card</strong> pages let you define material composition and the relevant quantity basis for each product or fixed asset.</p> <p>For tax on plastic, Business Central calculates excise quantities by aggregating item ledger entries from purchases, positive adjustments, production output, assembly output, and fixed asset ledger entries related to an acquisition. To determine the tax basis, it multiplies the calculated quantity by the defined excise quantity.</p> <p>For tax on sugar, Business Central uses Item ledger entries from sales and negative adjustments to determine the total sugar content for the reporting period. The tax basis is derived by multiplying the excise quantity per unit by the total quantity sold or consumed.</p> <p>These calculations generate the core data needed to report tax on plastics and sugar, while the specific country‑level tax declaration forms remain out of scope. This provides flexibility for partners and customers to adapt the output to local submission requirements while relying on standardized, accurate calculations in Business Central.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Many countries are introducing plastic and sugar‑related excise taxes, and companies must calculate these amounts based on material composition and quantities used or sold. Business Central provides a built‑in framework to calculate taxes on plastic and sugar without relying on manual spreadsheets or external tools. Support for these tax calculations helps organizations improve accuracy, reduce compliance risks, and prepare the core data needed for local tax declarations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576844","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-set-up-excise-tax#set-up-excise-tax-types"},{"id":"rm-576815","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Governance and administration - Upload, install, and manage PTEs in the admin center","desc":"<p>Business Central offers full management of per-tenant extensions (PTEs) in the admin center and through admin center API endpoints. In addition to viewing and uninstalling extensions, administrators can upload PTE packages, install them immediately or schedule installations, and view upcoming extension versions.</p> <p>The API accepts extension package uploads directly, making it easier to integrate with build pipelines and deployment automation. This removes previous limitations that required using the Automation API, which involved more complex configuration and constraints.</p> <p>All new endpoints are also exposed as tools through the admin center API MCP server, enabling developers to manage environments and extensions programmatically and through AI-assisted workflows in tools like VS Code. This provides a consistent, modern surface for extension lifecycle management across manual, automated, and AI-driven scenarios.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature gives administrators full lifecycle control over per-tenant extensions directly from the Business Central admin center and its APIs. It simplifies deployment workflows, enables reliable automation, and reduces operational overhead. Partners and customers can integrate extension management into CI/CD pipelines, improving governance, predictability, and release velocity.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576815","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-576872","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply chain management - Use subcontracting capabilities in production processes","desc":"<p>The standard Dynamics 365 Business Central solution already meets many global needs. We expand that solution to meet local needs by adding capabilities that include:</p> <ul> <li>Logistics flows that manage subcontractor transfers for raw materials and components, along with warehouse handling and item tracking.</li> <li>Flexible pricing that considers the work center, item, dates, and quantity.</li> <li>Finished goods receipts with item tracking and warehouse handling from purchase orders.</li> <li>Logistics flows that manage subcontractor transfers of finished goods.</li> <li>Enhanced usability and more transparency in production processes.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Special note for Italian localizations</strong></p> <p>The Italian localization currently supports logistics for both finished goods and raw materials/components. We deprecate the existing local functionality and provide upgrade logic to facilitate migration to a new W1 solution. You decide when to start the transition by activating a feature key on the <strong>Feature Management</strong> page.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>A complex industrial structure can include external vendors that handle specific tasks within the broader production process. Some companies outsource up to 75 percent of their production. Outsourcing can lead to significant cost savings or access to specialized skills and technologies that might not be available otherwise. A typical example is a company that handles research, design, quality control, and sales in-house but outsources all or large parts of the actual production.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576872","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/production-how-to-subcontract-manufacturing"},{"id":"rm-576835","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data: Elevate customer experiences - Use Microsoft Fabric OneLake as a data source","desc":"<p>Easily explore and select customer data stored in OneLake for processing in Customer Insights - Data. The OneLake connector reads directly from your OneLake data, eliminating the need to copy or stage data.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Integrate external sources quickly</strong>: Use Fabric shortcuts and mirroring to bring data from external systems into Customer Insights - Data.</li> <li><strong>Ingest data quickly</strong>: OneLake-managed tables use the Delta data format, which enables incremental data ingestion, reducing the time required to ingest large sets of data when only a small fraction changes each day.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>Contoso centralizes its customer data in Microsoft Fabric OneLake. Customer Insights - Data reads directly from OneLake. By creating shortcuts and mirrors to external sources such as Snowflake, Contoso can quickly and easily ingest all their customer data into Customer Insights - Data without having to build, run, and maintain complex data pipelines.</p> <p>With Fabric and Customer Insights - Data, Contoso replaces slow, costly ETL pipelines with a unified data foundation, streamlining operations, lowering overhead, and enabling faster, more responsive customer engagement.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data generates insights from your customer data, no matter where you store it. You can now bring customer data directly from Microsoft Fabric OneLake. This enhancement reduces the complexity, effort, cost, and time required to move, integrate, and transform customer data in Fabric, allowing you to focus on generating the insights you need.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576835","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/data/connect-fabric-onelake"},{"id":"rm-576827","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data: Turbocharge your pipeline to drive growth - Target right audience based on signals from earlier campaigns","desc":"<p>You can now access behavioral data captured by Customer Insights - Journeys, such as emails opened and links clicked, and use it in Customer Insights - Data. The behavioral data from Customer Insights - Journeys is now automatically available in Customer Insights - Data.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Get data quickly by eliminating the need to build and wait for special data flows to export behavioral data from Dataverse to Fabric, and then into Customer Insights - Data.</li> <li>Use the behavioral data to refine segments for precise targeting of customers that includes how they responded (or didn't respond) to previous campaigns.</li> <li>Combine Customer Insights - Journeys interaction data with other external data sources to create powerful customer measures for scoring and targeting customers with greater precision.</li> <li>Identify customers who weren't responsive to a campaign and retarget them using external systems like Google and Meta by exporting segments.</li> <li>Use unification to identify customers with multiple emails and see how they interact with your brand across different contact points, so you can see the customer and not just the email address.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Scenario</strong></p> <p>As a marketing manager at an online retail store, you send a monthly campaign that offers a 5 percent discount to customers. When you review the results, you see a high email open rate but a low click-through rate on the coupon. With Customer Insights - Data, you can see which contacts opened the email and interacted with your product. You create a new segment of customers who opened the email but didn't select the coupon, and you retarget them with a more compelling 10 percent offer. When you act on real engagement signals, you refine your audience, increase relevance, and boost sales.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>To refine your engagement strategy, you need to understand how customers respond to your communications efforts. When you create segments in Customer Insights - Data and use them in Customer Insights - Journeys campaigns, the interaction data captured by Customer Insights - Journeys can now be accessed and used in Customer Insights - Data segments to refine your segments based on how customers responded to your campaign. This capability enables customer experience teams to combine the power of unified profiles with insights from Customer Insights - Journeys.</p> <p>Create a segment of unified customer profiles where the predictive AI models show a high lifetime value score. Filter this segment of customers to only include those that engaged with your recent campaigns by opening emails and clicking links. To increase your engagement ratio, retarget customers by creating segments of nonresponsive customers. Use the export capabilities of Customer Insights - Data to target these refined segments on alternate platforms like social media and other external marketing channels.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Insights - Data"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576827","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/data/journeys-interaction-data-segments-measures"},{"id":"rm-576826","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Boost productivity with Copilot - Enable agents to work with attachments through Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server","desc":"<p>Document attachments provide valuable context and detail about ERP records. With this release, the Dynamics 365 ERP MCP server will provide access for agents to work with the attachments by creating, deleting, or reading and reasoning over the content of the attachments in agentic flows.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Document attachments provide valuable context and detail about ERP records. Enabling agents to access the attachments opens many opportunities for powerful agentic experiences.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576826","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/business-performance-analytics/erp-analytics-mcp-overview"},{"id":"rm-576857","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable time-zone-independent behavior in the time entry grid","desc":"<p>Administrators can now enable time-zone-independent behavior for the Time Entry Grid so that time entries appear on the same calendar date, regardless of a user's time zone. This helps organizations with globally distributed teams maintain a consistent view of reported time and eliminates issues where entries appear on different dates due to time zone conversions.</p> <p>The enhancement improves accuracy, simplifies reconciliation and approvals, and ensures users see and manage time entries based on the intended business date rather than their local time zone.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Make it easier for your global teams to stay aligned by showing time entries on the same date for everyone. This prevents unexpected date changes from time zone conversions, so you keep data consistent and avoid confusion.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/time/time-entry-configurations"},{"id":"rm-576798","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Track real project progress from field execution","desc":"<p>This feature enhances Dynamics 365 Project Operations by extending its native work breakdown structure effort tracking to include approved time captured in Field Service when the Field Service and Project Operations integration is enabled and time flows in at the project task level.</p> <p>Approved Field Service time now contributes directly to task-level WBS execution metrics in Project Operations when time is captured against a project task. Task metrics such as effort completed, effort remaining, percent complete, estimate at completion, and schedule variance are calculated using approved field labor under the same native project rules used for time entered directly in Project Operations.</p> <p>Because these calculations occur at the leaf task level, their impact rolls up automatically to summary tasks and the project root. Effort tracking views, reprojections, and project-level status indicators reflect real execution in the field, rather than inferred progress or manual reconciliation. Project managers can assess delivery health, forecast outcomes, and identify schedule risk using execution metrics grounded in approved field work.</p> <p>This enhancement doesn't introduce new execution logic or formulas. It enables existing Project Operations WBS effort tracking behavior to include Field Service execution when time is captured against project tasks.</p> <p>This feature is only available when the Field Service and Project Operations integration is enabled.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>When field technicians complete work tied to a project task, you see that progress reflected immediately in your project health metrics. Approved Field Service time flows directly into task-level work breakdown structure (WBS) tracking in Dynamics 365 Project Operations, so effort completed, percent complete, estimate at completion (EAC), and schedule variance stay accurate without manual reconciliation.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576798","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/field-service-integration/project-operations-integration-project-task"},{"id":"rm-576814","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Opportunity acceleration - Chat about sales opportunity agent insights from inside Sales agent","desc":"<p>As a seller, you can:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Ask questions in context</strong>: Ask about opportunity research from Sales agent.</li> <li><strong>Start concise, go deeper on demand</strong>: Begin with action-oriented insights, then request deeper analysis only when needed.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You need guidance that adapts to the moment you’re in a meeting preparation, a stage move, or a specific risk you want to validate. With the ability to ask about opportunity research from inside Sales agent, you get right-sized, action-first insights. You can quickly act on what matters now, then go deeper only when you choose. This reduces time spent hunting for answers, improves seller confidence at critical stages, and meet sellers where they are in their flow of work.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576814","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576824","title":"Power Automate: Cloud flows - Share Process license capacity across workflows","desc":"<p>With flow groups, you can share Process license capacity across up to 25 cloud flows, optimizing license allocation and reducing costs for organizations operating higher-volume workflows that don't need their own dedicated capacity.</p> <p>Prerequisites:</p> <ul> <li>Power Automate Process licenses available to the environment</li> <li>Cloud flows stored in solutions</li> <li>Power Automate maker permissions</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Save costs, reduce management effort, and improve resource utilization by efficiently sharing capacity across multiple flows.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576824","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/flow-groups"},{"id":"rm-576794","title":"Power Automate: Desktop flows - Configure notifications for desktop flow checker in admin portal","desc":"<p>The desktop flow checker in the Power Automate portal extends rule‑based static analysis to provide configurable notifications for violations detected across all desktop flows in an environment. Administrators can select the notification type (error, warning, or informational), adjust severity levels, and define parameters such as thresholds, recurrence, and scope. The checker uses the same rule engine that runs during initialization and analysis of flows, loading default and custom rules to evaluate quality, performance, and maintainability issues.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>As an administrator, you need a clear way to track quality issues across the desktop flows in your environment. But today you only discover problems when they cause run failures or support escalations. With configurable notifications in the admin portal, you choose which rule violations trigger alerts and what parameters apply to each notification type. You stay ahead of quality risks, enforce governance standards across makers, and reduce the time you spend reacting to issues across environments.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/desktop-flows/static-analysis"},{"id":"rm-576786","title":"Power Automate: Desktop flows - Encrypt and decrypt data with PGP","desc":"<p>This feature introduces PGP-specific encryption and decryption actions that use OpenPGP compatible public and private keys. You can encrypt files or data payloads using a recipient public key and decrypt incoming PGP-encrypted content using a corresponding private key and passphrase. The actions support standard PGP formats, making them suitable for interoperability with third-party systems that rely on PGP for secure data exchange. The actions appear in the action picker with no additional UI changes.</p> <p>The feature is not enabled automatically. To use it, you add a PGP encryption or PGP decryption action to your workflow and configure the required keys and passphrase. Encryption or decryption can be disabled by removing the action or controlling execution through conditions, allowing you to precisely manage when PGP cryptography is applied.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature is for organizations that exchange sensitive data with partners using Pretty Good Privacy (PGP) standards. You can automatically encrypt and decrypt data using PGP keys, reducing manual handling and human error. This helps you meet security and compliance requirements, speed up integrations with external systems, and avoid building and maintaining custom PGP solutions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576786","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/desktop-flows/actions-reference/pgp"},{"id":"rm-576785","title":"Power Automate: Desktop flows - Measure time and cost savings for desktop flows","desc":"<p>This feature introduces built-in rules that calculate time and cost savings for desktop flows based on successful runs. You can define how long a task previously took when performed manually and let the platform compute time saved using flow run data. Cost savings can be estimated by applying hourly rates or custom monetary baselines that scale with run volume. Savings accumulate automatically as flows run, making the impact of automation measurable over time.</p> <p>The feature is not enabled automatically. To use it, you configure time-saving and money-saving rules for a desktop flow by specifying manual run duration and cost baselines. Once configured, savings are calculated per successful run and aggregated automatically. The calculations can be disabled by turning off the configured rules, allowing you to control when savings are tracked.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature is designed for teams that want to demonstrate the business impact of desktop automation. It lets you automatically calculate time and cost savings compared to pre-automation processes, without relying on manual tracking or spreadsheets. These insights help you clearly show return on investment, justify automation initiatives, and communicate value to business stakeholders and Centers of Excellence.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576785","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-576868","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Create and visualize custom KPIs in the process intelligence experience","desc":"<p>The process intelligence experience allows flexible metric creation with seamless visualization integration. This feature enables you to define custom KPIs and metrics tailored to specific business requirements within the process intelligence experience. You can create custom metrics using configurable formulas that can incorporate existing process data, standard KPIs, and mathematical operations.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Custom metric creation: Build new KPIs using an intuitive formula editor that supports calculations based on case attributes, event data, timestamps, and existing metrics.</li> <li>Editing and management: Modify, refine, or delete custom metrics as business needs evolve, with changes automatically reflected across all visualizations using those metrics.</li> <li>Native visualization support: Integrate custom KPIs seamlessly into all process intelligence experience tiles and components. Display them in process maps, trend charts, statistical breakdowns, and comparative analyses just like standard metrics.</li> <li>Business-specific measurements: Define metrics that reflect your unique business context, such as weighted performance scores, custom cost calculations, compliance rates, or domain-specific efficiency ratios.</li> <li>Reusability: Reuse custom KPIs throughout the process intelligence experience, applying them to filters and analysis scenarios.</li> </ul> <p>Custom metrics are evaluated dynamically against your process data, ensuring calculations remain current with each data refresh and providing consistent measurement across your process intelligence environment.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Custom KPIs put your unique business priorities at the center of process analysis. While standard metrics provide valuable baseline insights, your competitive advantage often lies in tracking the specific measurements that drive your business, whether that's customer-specific SLAs, industry-specific compliance thresholds, or proprietary efficiency calculations. This feature enables your teams to define, calculate, and monitor the exact metrics that align with your strategic goals, without waiting for IT or vendor support. Business users gain autonomy to evolve their measurement framework as priorities shift, ensuring your process intelligence always reflects current objectives. The results are more relevant insights, stronger alignment between process performance and business outcomes, and the ability to demonstrate value in the language your stakeholders understand.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576868","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/process-mining-studio-kpi-card"},{"id":"rm-576793","title":"Power Pages: Design studio - Support Power BI embed token v2 for Power Pages","desc":"<p>Power Pages now supports <strong>Power BI Embed Token v2</strong>, unlocking modern Power BI embedding scenarios that weren't supported with Embed Token v1. This enhancement enables richer, more scalable analytics experiences within Power Pages sites.<br> With Embed Token v2, Power Pages can embed:</p> <ul> <li>Paginated (RDL) reports, including reports that use Power BI datasets as a data source or require multi-resource tokens.</li> <li>Reports backed by data lake–based semantic models, where v2 tokens are required to include dataset and identity permissions in the embed token.</li> <li>Multi‑artifact embedding scenarios, where a single token can grant access to multiple reports and datasets, enabling more app‑like analytics experiences inside Power Pages.</li> </ul> <p>To use these scenarios, makers must use Embed Token v2 when configuring Power BI embedding in their Power Pages sites. This support enables advanced enterprise reporting, complex analytics scenarios, and richer data experiences directly within Power Pages.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can unlock advanced Power BI scenarios in Power Pages by using Embed Token v2, including paginated reports and data lake–backed models. This lets you deliver richer analytics experiences, support enterprise reporting needs, and confidently use Power Pages for high‑value, data‑driven applications.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576793","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-576782","title":"PowerApps: Building modern apps - Use CLI to discover, create, and wire connectors in code apps","desc":"<h3>Power Apps CLI connector commands</h3> <p>The Power Apps CLI adds new commands that let developers discover available connectors and create connections directly from the command line. This enables developers to wire connectors into code apps as part of their normal development workflow, without switching tools or manually configuring connections in the maker portal.</p> <h3>Agent and how-to guidance for prompt-to-app workflows</h3> <p>New code app agent.md files and code app how-to documentation show how coding agents can handle connector discovery and connection creation as part of end-to-end prompt-to-app workflows. These examples demonstrate how agents can generate apps that are already connected to the required data and services, reducing manual setup during app creation.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can build richer, more complex code apps using manual development or coding agents, so your developers move faster from ideas to production. This shortens the path from ideation and prototyping to deployment, helping you deliver enterprise-ready apps sooner while saving development time and effort.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576782","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/developer/code-apps/how-to/npm-quickstart"},{"id":"rm-576789","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Unlock more Business Central data with MCP server enhancements","desc":"<p>With this update of the MCP server for Business Central, customers and developers can expose a broader set of Business Central APIs as tools, making it easier to build solutions that interact deeply and consistently with Business Central data and processes.</p> <p>Key improvements include:</p> <p><strong>Access to all Microsoft APIs</strong><br> The MCP server can now surface the full set of standard Microsoft APIs in Business Central. This enables agents and integrations to work with a wider range of entities and actions out of the box, reducing the need for custom extensions and ensuring more consistent access to business data.</p> <p><strong>Support for API queries</strong><br> In addition to standard APIs, API queries are now available through MCP configurations. This allows solutions to retrieve pre-aggregated and optimized datasets directly from Business Central, improving accuracy, consistency, and performance—especially for reporting and analytics scenarios.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This update to the MCP server in Business Central makes it easier to build powerful, reliable integrations and agents by expanding access to Business Central data and logic. By exposing all standard Microsoft APIs, customers can reduce the need for custom extensions and accelerate development of solutions that work consistently across their business data. Support for API queries further improves results by enabling access to pre-aggregated, optimized datasets, leading to better performance and more accurate insights in reporting and analytics scenarios. Together, these enhancements help organizations build more scalable solutions, improve data consistency, and unlock greater value from Business Central as a system of record and execution.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576789","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576802","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Country and regional - Comply with Australian Payment Times Reporting bill","desc":"<p>Every six months, Australian companies with more than AUD100 million in annual turnover must report how and when they pay small business suppliers (suppliers with annual turnover under AUD10 million).</p> <p>This feature organizes vendors by size or payment terms and creates reports that meet local authority requirements.</p> <ul> <li>The average agreed payment period.</li> <li>The average actual payment term.</li> <li>The proportion of invoices paid after the agreed payment period.</li> </ul> <p>Select the period for the calculation and choose a grouping for the details. For each grouping, you can view the sourced entries.</p> <p>Use this feature by opening the <strong>Payment Practices</strong> page and creating a new payment practice. To use different types of reporting for vendors, customers, or both, use the <strong>Header Type</strong> option. For payment time details and statistics, set up all parameters and select <strong>Generate</strong>.</p> <p>The report is in the required format. It categorizes details into ranges of time based on the timing after the invoice date:</p> <ul> <li>Less than 21 days</li> <li>21-30 days</li> <li>31-60 days</li> <li>61-90 days</li> <li>91-120 days</li> <li>More than 120 days</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The payment times reporting feature in the Australian localization helps large businesses with annual turnovers exceeding $100 million comply with Australian regulations. These regulations require businesses to report how and when they pay their small business suppliers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576802","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/localfunctionality/australia/payment-times-reporting"},{"id":"rm-576839","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Country and regional - Use Payment Practices in the UK localization","desc":"<p>Business Central extends UK localization to support the updated <em>Reporting on Payment Practices and Performance (Amendment) Regulations 2024</em>. The system introduces new data points to the existing <strong>Payment Practices</strong> page, including the total value of payments made during the period, late payments relative to agreed terms, and the percentage of late payments caused by disputes. A dispute mechanism is added to purchase invoices to link delayed payments directly to dispute status.</p> <p>The report can be exported in CSV format for submission or further processing.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>New legislation in the UK requires companies to report more detailed and accurate payment performance metrics. With this update, Business Central helps organizations stay compliant without manual data collection or spreadsheet work. By automatically tracking late payments, disputes, and other required rules, companies can improve reporting accuracy, strengthen supplier relationships, and reduce the administrative burden on finance teams.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576881","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Financial Management - Use self-billed invoices","desc":"<p>Business Central offers full support for self‑billed invoices in the purchase process. Buyers can now generate invoices on behalf of a vendor when a self‑billing agreement is in place. A new Boolean field on the <strong>Vendor Card</strong> page enables this agreement, and all <strong>Purchase Invoices</strong> created for that vendor, whether from <strong>Purchase Orders</strong> or directly, are automatically marked as self‑billed. Vendors can also be assigned a dedicated <strong>No. Series</strong> for self‑billed invoices, ensuring correct document sequencing.</p> <p>A new report layout, <strong>Posted Purchase Invoice – Self‑Billing Invoice</strong>, formats the invoice to align with the sales invoice style, showing buyer company information, vendor details, VAT information, and all essential invoice data.</p> <p>For Danish localizations, the posting process can automatically create <strong>Digital Vouchers</strong> when you enable self‑billing, ensuring compliance with local audit and documentation rules. To prevent conflicts between buyer‑issued and supplier‑issued documents, vendors with a self‑billing agreement can't receive inbound e‑documents for accounts payable. This guarantees data integrity and avoids duplicate or contradictory documents in the purchase flow.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Self‑billing reduces operational friction by allowing buyers to generate invoices on behalf of suppliers under a mutual agreement. This improves accuracy, accelerates processing, and eliminates delays caused by missing or inconsistent supplier‑issued invoices. With automated layouts, posting rules, and vendor configuration, you can streamline both compliance and internal controls while ensuring clean financial records.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576881","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576864","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Use new APIs for analyzing approval workflows for auditors and IT staff","desc":"<p>In this release wave, we're introducing read-only APIs on the (workflow) approval system. This allows for establishing security and auditing analytics and reporting outside Business Central—for example, creating reports with Power BI or agents with Microsoft Copilot Studio and MCP Server for Business Central.</p> <p>The APIs are read-only and allow querying for:</p> <ul> <li>Workflow</li> <li>Workflow and User mappings</li> <li>Workflow, User, and Action history</li> </ul> <p>We're also introducing a new permission set that allows a user to use approval APIs. This shouldn't be granted to standard users, but might be included in security-related permission sets.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enhances transparency and control by enabling secure, read-only access to approval workflows and user actions. Businesses can leverage these APIs to build advanced auditing and compliance reports in tools like Power BI, ensuring stronger governance and accountability. Additionally, integration with Microsoft Copilot Studio and MCP Server opens opportunities for intelligent automation and analytics, driving efficiency and insight. By isolating permissions for API access, organizations maintain robust security while empowering authorized teams to innovate confidently.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576864","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576841","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Use new APIs for analyzing permissions for auditors and IT staff","desc":"<p>In this release wave, we're introducing read-only APIs on the permission system. This allows for establishing security and auditing analytics and reporting outside Business Central—for example, creating reports with Power BI or agents with Microsoft Copilot Studio and MCP Server for Business Central.</p> <p>The APIs are read-only and allow querying for:</p> <ul> <li>Permission Set</li> <li>Object, Scope, Extension info, and Permission Set</li> <li>Permission Set and Security Group mappings</li> <li>Permission Set and User mappings</li> </ul> <p>We're also introducing a new permission set that allows you to use the new permission APIs. This shouldn't be granted to standard users, but might be included in security-related permission sets.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The new read-only permission APIs empower businesses to strengthen security and compliance by enabling external auditing and analytics without compromising system integrity. With seamless integration into tools like Power BI and Microsoft Copilot Studio, organizations can create advanced reports and intelligent agents for deeper insights. This capability enhances transparency, supports regulatory requirements, and accelerates decision-making by providing secure, real-time access to permission data. Ultimately, it helps businesses maintain robust governance while unlocking new opportunities for automation and analytics.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576841","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576792","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Use new APIs for getting the PDF of a document report","desc":"<p>We're introducing read-only APIs in the document report system. The APIs help establish automation on document reporting outside Business Central. For example, to create agents with Microsoft Copilot Studio and MCP Server for Business Central to automate business processes that involve document PDFs. The APIs are read-only and allow you to query the following types of documents:</p> <p><strong>Sales documents</strong></p> <ul> <li>Blanket sales orders</li> <li>Sales return orders</li> <li>Sales shipments</li> <li>Return receipts</li> <li>Sales archive quotes</li> <li>Sales archive orders</li> <li>Sales archive returns</li> <li>Sales archive blanket orders</li> </ul> <p><strong>Purchasing documents</strong></p> <ul> <li>Purchase quotes</li> <li>Blanket purchase orders</li> <li>Purchase receipts</li> <li>Purchase return orders</li> <li>Purch. Return Shipment</li> <li>Purchase Archive Quote</li> <li>Purchase Archive Order</li> <li>Purchase Archive Return</li> <li>Purchase Archive Blanket Order</li> </ul> <p><strong>Inventory documents</strong></p> <ul> <li>Phys. Inventory Order</li> <li>Posted Phys. Inventory Order</li> <li>Phys. Inventory Recording</li> <li>Posted Phys. Inventory Recording</li> <li>Inventory shipments</li> <li>Inventory receipts</li> <li>Posted inventory shipments</li> <li>Posted inventory receipts</li> <li>Transfer orders</li> <li>Transfer shipments</li> <li>Transfer receipts</li> <li>Posted direct transfers</li> </ul> <p><strong>Assembly documents</strong></p> <ul> <li>Assembly orders</li> <li>Posted assembly orders</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature enhances automation on processes that include document reports. Businesses can leverage these APIs to build integrations with Power Automate or Microsoft Copilot Studio and MCP Server, opening up opportunities for intelligent automation.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576792","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576874","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Use new APIs in Sustainability for better integration","desc":"<p>The feature introduces four new APIs in the Sustainability area to improve interoperability and enable automated data flows between Business Central and external applications.</p> <p>The new APIs are:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Goals</strong>: Provides read, insert, and modify operations for sustainability goals.</li> <li><strong>ESG Reporting Staging</strong>: Read-only API for accessing staged ESG reporting data.</li> <li><strong>Emission Value Entry</strong>: Read-only API for retrieving emission value entries calculated in Business Central.</li> <li><strong>Purchase Lines with Sustainability Detail</strong>: Enables read, insert, and modify operations on purchase lines, including sustainability-related fields.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>These new APIs make sustainability data easier to integrate with external systems and reporting tools. Businesses can automate ESG reporting, synchronize sustainability goals, and exchange emission details with procurement systems. This reduces manual data handling, improves accuracy, and supports compliance with sustainability regulations and corporate reporting standards.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576874","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/api-sustainability/sustainability-api"},{"id":"rm-576830","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Omnichannel commerce - Enable credit management support for Commerce orders","desc":"<p>This feature enhancement extends the standard credit management framework to all Commerce orders across channels, ensuring the consistent application of credit policies between Commerce and Supply Chain Management. During order fulfillment, Commerce channels including call center and POS adhere to defined credit management blocking rules to determine whether an order should be placed on credit hold for review. For order capture scenarios, POS and Commerce e-commerce continue to rely on the existing <strong>Check credit limit on sales order</strong> configuration in credit and collections parameters to evaluate whether a credit limit check should be performed at order placement.</p> <p>To use these capabilities, store administrators must enable a new <strong>Enable credit management for Commerce orders</strong> feature flag in the Commerce headquarters <strong>Feature management</strong> workspace.</p> <p>Two exceptions to standard credit limit validation remain in place:</p> <ul> <li>Cash-and-carry transactions paid on credit continue to be blocked when the customer’s available credit is insufficient, ensuring that on‑account purchases can't bypass credit policies.</li> <li>Customer orders using a carry-out mode of delivery continue to be marked as <strong>Exclude from credit management</strong>, because these orders are partially invoiced immediately when the customer pays for items they carry out at the point of sale.</li> </ul> <p>This feature enhancement ensures unified and predictable credit governance across all Commerce channels, while respecting scenarios that require operational exceptions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Credit limit management is essential for business-to-business (B2B) organizations because most transactions occur on accounts, often involving large orders, long fulfillment cycles, and repeat purchasing. By enforcing well‑defined credit limits and blocking rules, your organization can control financial risk, prevent bad debt, and maintain healthy cash flow, ensuring that open orders, uninvoiced orders, and outstanding balances are all factored into a buyer’s available credit.</p> <p>Before this feature enhancement, unlike Supply Chain Management orders, Commerce orders didn't follow the standard credit management capabilities. This resulted in different order processing flows that required customization to make order processing consistent.</p> <p>This feature ensures consistent credit policies for customers using both Supply Chain Management and Commerce orders, reducing operational complexity and eliminating costly customizations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576830","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/commerce/customer-orders-overview#use-credit-management-for-commerce-orders"},{"id":"rm-576834","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Omnichannel commerce - Streamline mass price updates using attribute-based pricing","desc":"<p>This feature enhancement introduces mass price update capabilities that use price attribute combinations and rule-based markups to provide an efficient way to manage large-scale pricing changes.</p> <p><strong>Create trade agreement prices using attribute combinations</strong></p> <p>Pricing managers can now define pricing updates based on price attribute combinations such as product attributes, customer segments, package types, and warranty types. This functionality allows a single rule to update pricing for a wide range of items and customers that share identical attribute characteristics.</p> <p><strong>Apply amount or percentage markups based on configurable pricing bases</strong></p> <p>Users can define new prices using:</p> <ul> <li>A fixed amount.</li> <li>A percentage markup applied on top of a selected pricing basis, such as: <ul> <li>Current price</li> <li>Base price</li> <li>Inventory cost</li> <li>Last purchase price</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p>This functionality provides a powerful extension of category pricing logic into attribute-based pricing updates.</p> <p><strong>Automatic expiration of matching legacy pricing rules</strong></p> <p>When a new pricing rule is created using attribute combinations, the system automatically identifies existing trade agreement records that match the same targeted segments. These legacy rules can then be automatically expired, eliminating the need for pricing managers to search for and manually retire outdated entries.</p> <p><strong>Mass-update capabilities</strong></p> <p>Mass-update capabilities do the following:</p> <ul> <li>Reduce repetitive data entry.</li> <li>Lower the chance of outdated or conflicting rules.</li> <li>Ensure cleaner pricing history and better governance.</li> </ul> <p>This functionality is especially valuable for organizations managing thousands of SKUs across multiple channels.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Mass price updates and expirations can often be time-consuming and labor-intensive activities. Pricing managers must manually create new trade agreement records, locate every previous version of the pricing rule across entities, and individually expire outdated entries. This creates significant operational overhead, especially for companies managing large product catalogs or complex pricing structures.</p> <p>With attribute-based mass pricing updates, unified pricing management now automates these processes and reduces manual effort. Pricing managers can update prices at scale using rule-driven logic, ensure consistent pricing across similar attribute combinations, and eliminate errors caused by manual expiration of legacy rules. This results in faster pricing updates, higher data accuracy, and improved responsiveness to market or cost changes.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576816","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Configure inline actions on transaction line items in Store Commerce","desc":"<p>Inline actions extensibility enables retailers and implementation partners to configure the set of actions displayed per line item in the modern transaction grid in Store Commerce, using Screen Layout Designer in Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters.</p> <p><strong>What retailers can configure</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Which actions appear</strong>: Select any eligible out-of-the-box POS operation or custom operation registered in headquarters to include as an inline action on transaction line items.</li> <li><strong>Display order</strong>: Control the sequence in which inline actions appear, so the most relevant operations for a given store format or associate role are surfaced first.</li> <li><strong>Custom operations</strong>: Operations built through the POS extension framework can be added as inline actions alongside out-of-the-box operations, giving retailers a unified configuration surface for both standard and customized workflows.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Default behavior and backward compatibility</strong></p> <p>No configuration is required to preserve the current experience. If no inline actions are configured for a layout, Store Commerce continues to display the existing default set of inline operations. There is no change in behavior for layouts that haven't been updated. Once a retailer configures inline actions for a specific layout, the configured list replaces the defaults for that layout only. Other layouts remain unaffected.</p> <p><strong>Localization</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Out-of-the-box operations</strong>: Display names are automatically localized using existing POS resource strings. No additional localization work is required.</li> <li><strong>Custom operations</strong>: Display names fall back to the operation name configured in headquarters. Retailers and partners who need localized display names can provide them with the POS extension framework using resource files and operation mappings in their extension code.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Security and permissions</strong></p> <p>Inline actions respect the same POS security roles and permission model as button grid operations. Retailers can use role-based access controls to restrict sensitive operations, such as price override or void line, to managers, while presenting a simplified action set to cashiers.</p> <p><strong>Requirements</strong></p> <p>This feature requires the modern React-based transaction grid. The following feature flags must be enabled in <strong>Feature management</strong> in Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters:</p> <ul> <li>Modern transaction grid (<code>RetailModernTransactionGridFeature</code>)</li> </ul> <p>The legacy transaction grid doesn't support inline actions extensibility.</p> <p><strong>How to configure inline actions</strong></p> <ol> <li>In Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters, go to <strong>Retail and Commerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Channel setup</strong> &gt; <strong>POS setup</strong> &gt; <strong>POS</strong> &gt; <strong>Screen layouts</strong>.</li> <li>Open the screen layout to configure and launch <strong>Screen layout designer</strong>.</li> <li>Select the transaction grid component and open the inline actions configuration.</li> <li>Add operations from the available list, remove operations that aren't needed, and set the display order.</li> <li>Save the layout and run the <strong>Channel configuration</strong> distribution schedule (<strong>1090</strong>) to push the changes to stores.</li> </ol> <p>Changes take effect in Store Commerce after the updated layout is downloaded at the register.</p> <p><strong>Applies to</strong>: Point of sale (Store Commerce)</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Retailers adopting the modern transaction grid in Store Commerce have had no control over the inline actions displayed per line item. Operations such as adding a serial number, changing a delivery method, applying a discount, or voiding a line were presented as a fixed, hard-coded set. This is the same for every store, every role, and every layout. There was no way to change this. The inline actions list was not extensible, even with developer involvement. This meant slower rollouts, unnecessary development cycles, and configuration changes that required code when they shouldn't have. For partners and ISVs, the gap was equally sharp. Custom operations they have built for retailers can't surface inline on line items at all, reducing discoverability and forcing associates to hunt through menus for operations that should be one tap away.</p> <p>Inline actions extensibility removes this cost. Retailers can now select which actions appear per line item, control their order, and include custom operations all through Screen Layout Designer in Dynamics 365 Commerce headquarters. No code, no deployment. Changes are pushed to stores through the standard distribution schedule.</p> <p>The feature is also risk-free to adopt. Existing deployments continue to show the current default inline actions unchanged. Retailers who configure inline actions for a layout replace the defaults only for that layout, giving them full control over the pace and scope of rollout.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576816","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576774","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Display distance in kilometers on the Store Commerce app","desc":"<p>Retailers operating across multiple regions often face challenges with distance unit consistency in Dynamics 365 Commerce. By default, distances in points of sale are hard-coded to miles, regardless of the store's locale. This limitation can cause confusion for customers in metric-based countries and lead to operational miscommunication across international teams.</p> <p>This feature introduces automatic distance unit display in Store Commerce, ensuring values are presented in the correct format for each legal entity. Distances are determined by the registered country address of the legal entity. For example, kilometers in metric countries and miles in non-metric countries.</p> <p>The setting is enabled by default and requires no per-entity configuration. Conversion is centrally managed in the Dynamics 365 Commerce runtime, providing a seamless and consistent experience across all regions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Automatic, locale-aware distance units in Store Commerce reduce customer confusion and prevent operational miscommunication by displaying distances in the correct format for each legal entity. By aligning point-of-sale distance values with regional standards, retailers can deliver a more intuitive customer experience and support smoother collaboration across global teams.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576774","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576811","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Enable associates to use the nearest store payment terminal","desc":"<p>Application: Point of sale (Store Commerce)</p> <p>When a sales associate selects a dedicated hardware station (HWS) from the POS, the system correctly pairs with the payment terminal physically attached to that hardware station and not the terminal attached to the register. While printer pairing from the selected HWS already works as expected, this change aligns payment terminal behavior to match.</p> <p>How to use the feature:</p> <ol> <li>The store administrator configures dedicated hardware stations in Headquarters, each with a payment terminal assigned.</li> <li>The sales associate enables shared shift on their register, except when the cash drawer isn't present, in which case they don't need a shared shift for this feature.</li> <li>From the POS, the associate selects the desired dedicated hardware station, typically the one nearest to where they're serving the customer.</li> <li>When the customer is ready to pay, the POS routes the payment request to the terminal on the selected hardware station.</li> <li>The associate completes the transaction at the customer's location without returning to the register.</li> </ol> <p>Setup and configuration:</p> <ul> <li>Dedicated hardware stations must be configured by an IT admin or store manager in Headquarters before use.</li> <li>Each hardware station requires an associated payment terminal.</li> <li>Shared shift must be enabled on the register.</li> </ul> <p>This feature is available by default in Store Commerce after you configure dedicated hardware stations. It doesn't require any additional feature flag.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Retailers operating large store formats increasingly rely on mobile associates who move throughout the floor to serve customers. Previously, even when a sales associate selected a dedicated hardware station away from the register, the POS system incorrectly routed payment to the terminal at the register, forcing the associate to walk back, breaking the customer interaction and slowing down checkout.</p> <p>With this capability, payment terminal selection correctly follows hardware station selection. Associates can complete end-to-end transactions from anywhere in the store from product discovery through payment without returning to a fixed register. It reduces customer wait times, increases sales floor efficiency, and enables high-touch service models where the associate stays with the customer throughout the entire journey.</p> <p>For global enterprises with complex store layouts or multiregion deployments, flexible payment terminal selection is foundational to delivering consistent, mobile payment acceptance regardless of where in the store the transaction takes place.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576811","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576845","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Enable contextual switching with external apps in POS","desc":"<p><strong>How it works</strong>:</p> <ol> <li><strong>POS to external application</strong>: A sales associate is working in POS and needs to use an external system (for example, a specialized parts-search tool). They trigger the <strong>Open URL</strong> POS operation, which opens the external application.</li> <li><strong>External application back to POS</strong>: After the associate completes their task in the external system (for example, selects a part), the external application calls POS back with the relevant context—for example, a product ID and quantity. POS receives this context and navigates to the correct screen with the information loaded.</li> <li><strong>Custom context handling</strong>: Businesses can add custom logic in POS to determine how incoming context from their external application is interpreted and handled.</li> </ol> <h3>Availability</h3> <p><strong>Application</strong>: Point of sale (POS)</p> <h3>Setup and configuration</h3> <p>No additional configuration is required in Commerce headquarters or POS. However, to use this feature, the business's <strong>IT team</strong> must:</p> <ul> <li>Customize the external application to call POS with the appropriate context parameters.</li> <li>Optionally, add custom logic within POS to interpret and act on the context passed by the external application.</li> </ul> <p>This is a developer-level customization, not an admin or store manager task.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Retailers and B2B commerce businesses often rely on specialized external systems such as parts-lookup tools, warranty platforms, or industry-specific catalogs alongside their point of sale (POS). Today, integrating these systems with POS requires significant development effort, and sales associates must manually re-enter information (such as product details or customer data) when moving between applications. This is time-consuming, error-prone, and costly.</p> <p>Contextual switching eliminates these friction points. By enabling external applications to pass context directly into POS, businesses can drastically reduce integration time and cost. Sales associates benefit from a streamlined workflow where product, customer, and transaction context flow automatically between systems to remove the need for manual data entry. This leads to faster transactions, fewer errors, and better experiences for store employees and customers.</p> <p>For businesses that depend on external tools as part of their sales process, this feature unlocks a flexible, low-friction way to extend POS without replacing existing investments in specialized systems.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576845","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/commerce/dev-itpro/store-commerce-contextual-switch"},{"id":"rm-576829","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Prevent the return of specific items in point of sale","desc":"<p>This feature enables merchandising managers to define specific products or entire product hierarchies as non-returnable. This can be done by enabling a new property on released products either individually, or in bulk via the category view. Once configured, POS blocks the return of such items to enforce compliance and reduce unauthorized returns. This capability also enhances operational efficiency by clearly signaling return restrictions to cashiers and customers during the original sale, reducing confusion and dispute rates at the counter.</p> <p>Implementation partners are also able to easily extend this functionality to support scenarios where one or more products or product components need to be classified as non-returnable—for example, floor models that are usually sold at heavy discounts. However, in cases of legitimate exceptions, store managers or workers with appropriate permissions are able to return such items with a manual override.</p> <p>The ability to automatically enforce restrictions while still allowing controlled manager overrides when legitimate exceptions arise creates a balanced governance workflow that protects the retailer’s financial interests without compromising customer service. Overall, the feature strengthens loss‑prevention strategy, supports regulatory adherence, and ensures consistent return handling across all stores and product hierarchies.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Retailers increasingly face operational, regulatory, and financial risks associated with return transactions, particularly for products that are hygiene‑sensitive, safety‑controlled, perishable, or otherwise unsuitable for resale. Enabling retailers to designate certain items as non‑returnable at the POS directly supports compliance with industry regulations and store policies, especially for categories such as personal use goods, medicines, health and beauty products, and end‑of‑life inventory. By preventing unauthorized or accidental returns, retailers can minimize revenue leakage, reduce fraud, and avoid unnecessary write‑offs that erode margins.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576829","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/commerce/pos-returns#block-specific-items-from-being-returned-in-pos"},{"id":"rm-576828","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Store Commerce - Set payment method display order and visibility in POS","desc":"<p>The feature introduces payment profiles that can be associated with POS registers. These payment profiles provide retailers with a flexible and centralized way to manage how payment methods appear across their POS registers. Store administrators can create reusable profiles and assign them to individual registers or groups of registers, ensuring that each station only displays relevant payment methods. Within each profile, administrators can control visibility by choosing which payment methods are displayed and hide previously used payment methods, eliminating the need for customization.</p> <p>Store administrators can also define the precise display order of payment methods to streamline checkout workflows and display commonly used payment methods above less commonly used methods.</p> <p>By enabling register grouping based on the register type (such as self‑checkout, service counters, or express lanes), payment profiles make it easy to enforce consistent and tailored payment experiences without custom development.</p> <p>This configuration model simplifies ongoing administration, prevents configuration drift across registers, and ensures that customers encounter the appropriate payment options for each payment scenario. The result is cleaner operations, reduced maintenance, and more adaptable, register‑specific payment management.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Allowing store administrators to easily show or hide payment methods and define their display order in POS eliminates the need for costly customizations to meet common store requirements. This flexibility improves operational efficiency and ensures a consistent, tailored checkout experience across locations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576828","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576780","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Administrator experiences - Support average wait time in messaging API channels","desc":"<ul> <li>Average wait time (AWT) is now supported for custom messaging channels built using the messaging APIs, apart from live chat and voice channels.</li> <li>The system computes the average wait time using an exponential moving average algorithm, giving more weight to recently connected conversations and automatically excluding abandoned ones.</li> <li>Administrators and supervisors can retrieve the wait-time metric through the representative availability APIs, enabling Copilot Studio agents or custom logic to decide whether to escalate, defer, or route conversations based on real‑time queue conditions.</li> <li>This enhancement ensures consistent wait‑time visibility across all supported channels, improving experience management and routing strategies.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Organizations using custom messaging channels built on messaging APIs can now provide customers with transparent and accurate wait‑time expectations. By surfacing estimated wait times directly through the availability APIs, contact centers can offer consistent experiences across voice, live chat, and custom channels. This helps reduce customer frustration, enables proactive decision‑making for AI agents and service representatives, and drives operational efficiency.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576780","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576875","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Service representative experiences - Use pinned contacts and queues during consult and transfer","desc":"<p>In the Copilot Service admin center, administrators configure and manage pinned contacts and queues for representatives as follows:</p> <ul> <li>Enable pins in the <strong>Customer settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Manage pins</strong> &gt; <strong>Admin pins</strong> page so that representatives pin their contacts and queues.</li> <li>Pin specific contacts and queues for representatives.</li> <li>Display pinned items to representatives based on business units.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature streamlines your team’s workflow by removing the hassle of tracking multiple consult and transfer targets, so that your service representatives focus on delivering faster, more reliable support.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576875","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-service/use/oc-conversation-control#use-pinned-contacts-and-queues-during-consult-and-transfer"},{"id":"rm-576842","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Supervisor experiences - Provide real-time coaching with Quality Assurance Agent","desc":"<p>The quality evaluation skill of the Quality Assurance Agent now includes real-time coaching, enabling organizations to shift from post-interaction monitoring to in-the-moment guidance during live conversations. Service representatives receive contextual coaching nudges during live conversations based on configured quality criteria and guardrails, allowing immediate course correction and improved interaction quality.</p> <p>Organizations can:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Define policy-driven coaching triggers</strong>: Configure which quality criteria (such as compliance, empathy, script adherence, or resolution steps) initiate real-time coaching.</li> <li><strong>Provide contextual, conversation-aware nudges</strong>: Deliver coaching suggestions based on the live conversation to ensure relevance.</li> <li><strong>Control coaching triggers</strong>: Specify when coaching is triggered, such as for missed behaviors, risk signals, or guideline violations.</li> <li><strong>Manage coaching frequency</strong>: Set frequency limits and suppression rules to prevent over-intervention.</li> <li><strong>Enforce boundaries for sensitive scenarios</strong>: Apply stricter or mandatory guidance for cases such as compliance requirements or escalations.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Shift your quality assurance approach from passive evaluation to real-time coaching that makes an immediate difference in customer interactions. With enhanced real-time guidance, you can move beyond monitoring and give your team the support they need to adjust on the spot, improve conversations, and maintain quality and compliance every time.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576842","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576771","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Supervisor experiences - Track segment‑level metrics across queues","desc":"<p>This capability directly impacts metric calculations, improving accuracy and delivering the following benefits:</p> <ul> <li>Tracks when interactions enter and exit queues, providing clearer operational visibility.</li> <li>Calculates wait time, service level, and abandonment for each queue segment, enabling more precise performance evaluation.</li> <li>Preserves metric accuracy during cross-queue transfers, minimizing errors and inconsistencies.</li> <li>Surfaces customer wait times after transfers, offering deeper insights than session-level metrics.</li> <li>Ensures consistent and reliable reporting by evaluating service adherence at every queue entry.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Tracking segment-level metrics across queues enables contact center leads to measure performance at each queue entry within a single customer interaction. Unlike conversation-level metrics, which mask post-transfer wait times, abandonment, and service level performance, segment-level metrics hold each queue accountable for its outcomes. This visibility helps supervisors pinpoint operational bottlenecks such as agent rejections, timeouts, or misrouted transfers, improving SLA accuracy, workforce planning, and routing decisions. The result is reduced abandonment, better post-transfer experiences, and more consistent service across complex interaction flows.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576771","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-576831","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Workforce engagement management - Analyze adherence history to optimize workforce planning","desc":"<p>The Adherence History Report provides a complete view of customer service representatives’ historical adherence to scheduled tasks and activities. It helps supervisors analyze patterns, identify gaps, and improve workforce efficiency.</p> <p><strong>Key capabilities</strong></p> <p><strong>Trend chart</strong>: Visualize adherence patterns for individual service representatives or the entire team over time.<br> <strong>Metrics dashboard</strong>: Track adherence percentage, total scheduled time, and time spent out of adherence.<br> <strong>Activity summary view</strong>: Access detailed activity records for each service representative, including precise durations for granular analysis.</p> <p>You can find the Adherence History Report in the Copilot Service workspace by navigating to <strong>Workforce Management</strong> in the site map and selecting <strong>Adherence Historical Analytics</strong>.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Organizations can gain actionable insights into customer service representative adherence behavior over time. By analyzing trends and deviations, supervisors can make informed decisions to optimize workforce planning, reduce inefficiencies, and improve service-level compliance. Using these insights helps lead to better resource allocation, higher productivity, and an enhanced customer experience.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576831","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/contact-center/use/workforce-management-use-adherence-history-report?context=/dynamics365/context/customer-service-use-context"},{"id":"rm-576818","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Copilot and AI innovation - Improve customer outcomes with Service Agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"<p>Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat is becoming a consistent way that users interact with AI across Microsoft experiences. With this update, that same chat experience is available in Dynamics 365 Customer Service, with service-aware grounding and workflows.</p> <p>Service users can start in Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat and then:</p> <ul> <li>See and prioritize work (for example, top cases and what needs attention).</li> <li>Draft customer communications and prepare next steps with Microsoft 365 context when relevant.</li> <li>Identify trends and operational signals across cases to help supervisors and leads intervene earlier.</li> <li>Discover answers from support knowledge.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Bring the familiar Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat experience directly into Dynamics 365 Customer Service, so supervisors, leads, and customer service representatives can get answers, summarize work, and take next steps using both Dynamics 365 data and Microsoft 365 context, without switching tools.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576818","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"March CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-service/administer/configure-service-agent"},{"id":"rm-576851","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Copilot and AI innovation - Use Copilot Cowork to orchestrate insights and actions for representatives","desc":"<p>The plugin in Copilot Cowork is available out of the box for service representatives. They can use the Customer Service skills after the administrator enables the plugin for them in Cowork settings. The key capabilities are as follows:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Prioritizes and enriches cases</strong>: Surfaces highest-attention cases with suggested next actions.</li> <li><strong>Reviews for criticality and severity</strong>: Flags cases where severity mismatches actual urgency signals.</li> <li><strong>Briefs case at intake</strong>: One-screen customer, history, prior cases, and SLA snapshot.</li> <li><strong>Summarizes root cause and resolution</strong>: Proposes likely cause and ranked next-step resolutions.</li> <li><strong>Matches knowledge articles</strong>: Matches top articles, flags gaps, updates stale content.</li> <li><strong>Drafts replies</strong>: Generates template-based customer email replies for CSR review.</li> <li><strong>Handles escalations and handoffs</strong>: Detects triggers and assembles escalation packet for next owner.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The Customer Service plugin in Copilot Cowork helps service teams boost productivity at scale by offloading complex, multi-step case workflows. It ensures every action is grounded in the right Dynamics 365 environment and enriched with Microsoft 365 context, eliminating manual lookup.<br> The custom skills allow teams to tailor Cowork to their workflows, knowledge sources, and triage rules for more precise assistance. The built-in checkpoints provide human-in-the-loop governance, ensuring accuracy, compliance, and trust before any changes are committed.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576851","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576886","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Boost technician productivity - Disable clickthrough on lookup values in forms","desc":"<p>A new option in the lookup control lets you disable clickthrough on the displayed lookup value. When disabled, the lookup value renders as plain text (not a hyperlink), preventing users from unintentionally opening the related record. This applies to forms across web and mobile.</p> <p><strong>How to use</strong></p> <ol> <li>In Power Apps, edit the table form containing the lookup.</li> <li>Select the lookup field, and then select <strong>Disable click-through of lookup value</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Save</strong> and publish the form. The mobile app reflects the change after the next sync.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Enablement and scope</strong></p> <ul> <li>This is a UI‑level control on the lookup field and doesn't require a platform feature flag.</li> <li>It's configured per form and applies to both mobile and web.</li> <li>To revert, reenable clickthrough or switch to the default display mode, and then republish the form.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You’ll reduce accidental taps and simplify forms by removing clickable lookup links. This helps frontline workers stay focused, lowers cognitive load, and cuts unnecessary navigation, saving time and improving task flow.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576886","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/guidance/resources/field-service-mobile-disable-click"},{"id":"rm-576820","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - Cancel segments of a booking in aggregate views","desc":"<p>Cancel booking actions in aggregate views give schedulers precise control over long-running or multiday bookings directly within their current view. Users can cancel bookings with the same time granularity as the selected view. For example, canceling a week in a weekly view, canceling a day in a daily view. To cancel a segment, open the <strong>Edit Details</strong> panel and set the desired interval's duration to 0 minutes.</p> <p>Instead of canceling an entire booking to address partial changes—such as a delayed week, scope adjustment, or unexpected time off—users can cancel only the portion that no longer applies. This capability preserves the remaining booking, maintains an accurate historical record, and reduces the need for re-creation or manual cleanup. The feature ensures schedules better reflect real-world changes while minimizing disruption, improving data integrity, and supporting clearer downstream reporting and planning.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Long‑running bookings often require partial changes due to delays, time off, or scope shifts. Partial cancellation minimizes unnecessary rework, preserves accurate history, and ensures schedules stay aligned with reality. This capability is particularly beneficial for Project Operations users.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576820","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/work-with-schedule-board"},{"id":"rm-576823","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - Move multiple bookings at once by a set offset","desc":"<p>Bulk move enables schedulers to shift multiple bookings forward or backward by a consistent time offset in a single action. Instead of adjusting each booking manually, users can select bookings across one or more resources and apply changes, such as moving all affected work by a day or a week. This feature is especially valuable when plans change due to factors like weather delays, customer reschedules, or operational disruptions. It is automatically enabled for users.</p> <p>By preserving each booking’s duration and details while updating its placement, bulk move ensures schedules remain accurate and aligned with the new timeline without introducing gaps, overlaps, or inconsistencies. This capability significantly reduces manual effort and helps teams to respond quickly and confidently to changing conditions.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Schedulers often need to adjust many bookings at once when timelines shift due to staffing changes, delays, or shifting priorities. Bulk move streamlines this process by eliminating repetitive edits, reducing errors, and enabling faster replanning during disruptions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576823","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/schedule-board-drag-drop"},{"id":"rm-576822","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - Move multiple bookings at once to new resource","desc":"<p>Bulk reassign simplifies large-scale staffing changes by allowing schedulers to move multiple bookings to a different resource in a single step. Instead of reassigning work one booking at a time, users can multi-select bookings and quickly redirect them to another qualified resource using a new feature in the right-click menu. This feature supports common scenarios such as covering for unexpected absences, rebalancing workloads, or shifting work between teams. It is automatically enabled for users.</p> <p>Booking timing and duration remain unchanged, ensuring continuity while ownership updates seamlessly. Bulk reassign helps maintain service continuity, reduce scheduling errors, and balance workloads without requiring time-consuming manual updates.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>When availability or ownership changes, reassigning bookings one by one is slow and error‑prone. Bulk reassignment helps schedulers rebalance workloads, maintain coverage, and respond quickly without disrupting schedules.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576822","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/schedule-board-drag-drop"},{"id":"rm-576821","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize resource scheduling - View full screen map mode on schedule board","desc":"<p>Full screen map mode allows dispatchers to expand the schedule board map to fill the entire workspace, removing visual constraints that limit situational awareness. With more space, users can easily analyze resource locations, view booking distribution, and evaluate geographic coverage without distractions from other panels. This capability is particularly useful for dispatchers who rely on spatial context when assigning or adjusting work, such as route planning, proximity-based scheduling, or identifying coverage gaps.</p> <p>By prioritizing geographic visibility while retaining essential scheduling context, the full screen map mode delivers clearer insights, faster decisions, and more effective route-based planning.</p> <p>This feature introduces an additional view type for the schedule board, complementing the existing List and Gantt views. It is automatically enabled for users and can be activated by selecting the Map view type.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>For dispatchers relying on spatial planning, limited map space makes it harder to see coverage gaps and hinders route optimization. Full screen map mode improves clarity, enabling faster and more confident scheduling decisions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576821","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/field-service/work-with-schedule-board"},{"id":"rm-576838","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Boost productivity with Copilot - Use Copilot Cowork to orchestrate insights and actions across Dynamics 365 ERP","desc":"<p>The Copilot Cowork plugin for finance and operations apps enables users to move from business intent to insight to execution in a single experience. Copilot orchestrates work across ERP data, emails, documents, spreadsheets, collaboration tools, and downstream business processes.</p> <h3>Key capabilities</h3> <ul> <li>Orchestrate workflows across ERP and Microsoft 365 data sources.</li> <li>Analyze business data and generate contextual insights.</li> <li>Reason across finance, operations, and supply chain domains.</li> <li>Generate recommendations and prepare next steps.</li> <li>Execute actions while keeping humans in the loop.</li> </ul> <h3>What this means for customers</h3> <p>The value is not just accessing ERP data through AI. Copilot Cowork enables agentic workflows where it can reason over business context, gather relevant information, evaluate options, and generate recommended actions.</p> <p>This reduces manual coordination across systems, accelerates decision-making, and improves consistency in how business processes are executed.</p> <h3>User experience shift</h3> <p>Users can interact with ERP through business intent rather than navigating complex application layers and disconnected tools. This creates a more natural way to work, where users focus on outcomes instead of system interactions.</p> <h3>Preview scope</h3> <ul> <li>Initial set of scenarios across finance and supply chain.</li> <li>Limited action coverage for transactional workflows.</li> <li>Available to selected preview customers.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enable users to move from business intent to insight to execution faster by orchestrating work across ERP data, emails, documents, and collaboration tools. Reduce manual coordination, accelerate decision-making, improve workflow consistency, and shift user time from information gathering to applying business judgment.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576838","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/enable-copilot-cowork-erp"},{"id":"rm-576778","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: One Dynamics One Platform - Build custom scenarios with Archive Framework","desc":"<p>This feature allows customers to implement and run custom archive scenarios that natively leverage the Archive Framework’s orchestration and data management capabilities.</p> <p>Custom scenarios integrate with existing archive job creation, scheduling, and execution flows, ensuring consistency with first-party archive behavior. Validation enforces framework standards for configuration, execution, and retention policies, while providing flexibility to model customer-specific data domains. As a result, customers gain a supported, extensible path to archive non-standard data sets using the same enterprise-grade architecture trusted for core Dynamics 365 archival scenarios.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This capability empowers customers to address unique regulatory, operational, and business-specific data retention needs without waiting for scenarios delivered by Microsoft. By using the Archive Framework, customers can build their own custom archive solutions that cover custom tables in Dynamics 365. This approach can reduce custom engineering effort, lower operational risk, and accelerate compliance with local or industry-specific requirements.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576778","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/sysadmin/archive-data"},{"id":"rm-576791","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Enable cash discounts for settling customer invoice matching rules for bank reconciliation","desc":"<p>Implement cash discounts on customer settlement when the payment is recorded through advanced bank reconciliation. The feature ensures that advanced bank reconciliation supports applying customer cash discounts when customer invoices are automatically settled through reconciliation matching rules. The process evaluates eligible cash discounts during automated settlement performed when running Settle customer invoices reconciliation rules, and applies them consistently, aligning behavior with manual settlement processes.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature improves financial accuracy and compliance by ensuring eligible cash discounts are consistently applied during automated customer invoice settlement, aligning Advanced bank reconciliation with manual settlement behavior. It reduces manual effort and corrections by eliminating the need for post‑reconciliation adjustments to apply cash discounts, streamlining month‑end close and daily reconciliation operations. It increases trust in automation by delivering predictable, consistent settlement outcomes through reconciliation matching rules, enabling organizations to scale automated bank reconciliation with confidence.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/cash-bank-management/apply-cash-adv-bank-rec#complete-cash-application-by-using-matching-rules"},{"id":"rm-576833","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Inquire about purchase orders processed during purchase order year-end","desc":"<p>The purchase order year-end process can update purchase order accounting dates and carry purchasing commitments into the next fiscal year. Finance users need a simple way to confirm which purchase orders were included in that process, understand how accounting dates changed, and see the resulting document status after year-end processing.</p> <p>With this feature, Dynamics 365 Finance adds a dedicated inquiry for purchase orders processed through Purchase order year-end. The inquiry is designed to help finance users review the year-end outcome without opening and investigating each purchase order individually.</p> <p>The inquiry shows the fiscal year that was closed, the original accounting date before year-end processing, the current accounting date after processing, and the resulting purchase order document status.<br> Finance teams can use the inquiry during year-end close, reconciliation, audit preparation, and period-close review to confirm that purchasing commitments moved as expected and to investigate exceptions more efficiently.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature helps finance teams validate the purchase orders carried forward during year-end close without manually tracing each document. A dedicated inquiry shows the closed fiscal year, original and current accounting dates, and resulting document status, giving teams a clearer audit trail for purchasing commitments as they move across fiscal years. Finance users can use the information to support reconciliation, audit evidence, and period-close reviews with less manual investigation.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/budgeting/purchase-order-year-end-process#select-purchase-orders-and-run-the-purchase-order-year-end-process"},{"id":"rm-576796","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core financials - Track branch-level registration IDs on invoices in a single legal entity","desc":"<p>This feature introduces the concept of an <em>Establishment</em> within a legal entity, allowing organizations to manage and apply establishment-specific registration identifiers such as branch IDs and local registration numbers across invoices.</p> <p>The feature provides the following key capabilities:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Establishment modeling</strong>: Establishments of the legal entity are modeled using <strong>Operating units</strong>, with a new organization hierarchy purpose called <strong>Enterprise establishment structure</strong>. Each establishment can be assigned unique registration identifiers through the <strong>Global address book</strong>.</p> <p>A new <strong>Establishment</strong> field is added to key transaction documents, including:</p> <ul> <li>Free text invoices</li> <li>Sales orders</li> <li>Purchase orders</li> <li>Vendor invoices</li> <li>Pending vendor invoices</li> <li>Project invoice proposals</li> <li>Intercompany customer invoices</li> <li>General journals</li> </ul> <p>The establishment can default based on context, such as site or financial dimension, or be selected manually. After a transaction is posted, the establishment reference is stored immutably for audit and compliance purposes.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Vendor ship-from address tracking</strong>: A new <strong>Ship-from address</strong> field is introduced on vendor-facing documents, allowing users to specify the originating establishment of goods or services. The associated registration identifiers are captured and stored on the invoice.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Registration ID validation rules</strong>: Administrators can configure validation rules to enforce the presence and format of registration IDs based on address purpose and role such as invoice or delivery. The system validates these rules during transaction posting, ensuring data completeness and consistency.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Post‑posting review of registration IDs</strong>: After an invoice is posted, the registration IDs that were applied and stored can be reviewed directly on:</p> <ul> <li>Customer invoice journals</li> <li>Vendor invoice journals</li> <li>Project invoice journals</li> </ul> </li> <li><p><strong>Use cases</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>Organizations with multiple branches or operational sites under a single legal entity.</li> <li>Businesses operating in jurisdictions that require branch-level registration data on invoices.</li> <li>Enterprises preparing for or complying with e-invoicing mandates or tax authority reporting requirements.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Many jurisdictions require that invoices and financial documents include not only the legal entity’s primary registration number but also identifiers for specific branches or establishments involved in the transaction. This feature introduces a standardized way to manage and apply establishment-level registration data across all relevant financial processes in Dynamics 365 Finance.</p> <p>By enabling organizations to define and associate multiple establishments within a single legal entity, this functionality ensures that the correct registration IDs are automatically applied to customer and vendor invoices, purchase and sales orders, and project transactions. This capability reduces manual data entry, improves audit readiness, and supports compliance with evolving global e-invoicing and tax reporting mandates.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576796","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/organization-administration/registration-ids"},{"id":"rm-576799","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Globalization Studio - Create faster XAF audit files for Netherlands","desc":"<p>In the current release wave, we are introducing the following regulatory reporting enhancements:</p> <p><strong>Performance improvements for Audit File Financial (XAF) – Netherlands</strong></p> <p>Dutch customers can generate the mandatory XAF export significantly faster, even for large data volumes.</p> <p>This enhancement uses optimized data storage and the latest XAF 4.0 format to reduce processing time and system load when producing audit files. It ensures compliance with the Dutch Tax Administration’s newest digital audit requirements by supporting XAF 4.0, which replaces the legacy XAF 3.2 standard.</p> <p>This performance enhancement is achieved through two key improvements:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Leveraging the new <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/general-ledger/financial-dimension-set-new\">General ledger dimension set balance calculation</a></strong>: The Audit File Financial report now takes advantage of the <strong>Performance enhancement for general ledger dimension set balance calculation</strong> feature in Dynamics 365 Finance. When this feature is enabled, the system precalculates and continuously updates ledger balances for defined financial dimension sets in the background (through a process automation job that runs every few minutes).</p> <p>Reports that use financial dimension sets (like the XAF report) can then pull data from these preaggregated balances instead of computing everything from scratch. This means the Audit File generation runs much more efficiently, data is stored in optimized tables using less space, and the trial balance figures are readily available for reporting. As a result, the XAF output can be produced quickly, even if the transactional data volume is very large, since calculations have been done ahead of time.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Adopting the latest Audit File implementation best practices</strong>: The feature updates the XAF generation to use the latest standard methods and format. It introduces a new Electronic Reporting (ER) model mapping configuration for XAF 4.0 optimized for that format. By using the ER framework, the solution follows Microsoft’s best practices for regulatory reporting, which improves maintainability and performance.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Together, these improvements mean that a Dutch legal entity can generate its XML Audit File Financial quickly and reliably. After setting up the feature (ensuring that financial dimension sets are defined and balance tracking is enabled for them) and importing the latest XAF 4.0 ER configurations, you run the Audit File Financial process as before. The report completes faster and the resulting XML complies with XAF 4.0 requirements (with fields like the RGS codes for each account as per the latest specification).</p> <p>By following the standard setup (such as associating main accounts with RGS codes in a consolidation account group per the documentation) and enabling this feature, organizations ensure that Audit File generation is not only compliant but also optimized for performance. This is especially beneficial at month-end or year-end, when time is critical–the audit file can be produced with minimal delay, allowing finance departments to confidently meet Dutch statutory obligations with improved efficiency and accuracy.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Dutch organizations can produce the Audit File Financial (XAF) export faster and more reliably with XAF 4.0 support. By preaggregating ledger balances in the background, the system reduces the time and load required at reporting time, helping your finance team stay compliant with Dutch Tax Administration requirements without delays.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576799","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/localizations/netherlands/emea-nl-audit-file"},{"id":"rm-576885","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable flexibility when determining financial dimension defaults","desc":"<p>Previously, you had limited options for how financial dimensions default. This feature adds functionality and flexibility to default financial dimension values. With this feature, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Create a configuration to determine how financial dimensions default based on criteria like contract, project, or cost and revenue profile.</li> <li>Set criteria to determine whether dimensions default from contract lines or projects.</li> <li>Improve reliability when you save financial dimensions and value defaults on the project.</li> <li>Add the ability to set dimensions on time and material contract lines.</li> <li>Add the ability to use contract lines for revenue recognition.</li> </ul> <p>For example, the system uses the following logic:</p> <ul> <li>The line at the end of the grid defaults all projects and contracts to use the project dimension unless an individual record overrides that behavior.</li> <li>The table line at the top of the grid is the next most specific record. It causes all projects associated with contract 00000017 to use the dimensions from the project line.</li> <li>The middle line is the most specific record. It's project-specific. It overrides previously defined behavior. All transactions for Project 000000004 use the contract line for the basis of default dimensions.</li> </ul> <p>The <strong>Enable contract line based revenue recognition with Project Operations for non-stocked/resource based scenarios</strong> feature modifies the <strong>Project default dimension rules</strong> form by adding a column to add rules based on specific contract line groups as the first filter.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature gives you more flexibility for resource-based and nonstocked scenarios. You can use financial dimensions for both cost and revenue to analyze financial performance. You don't need to manually reclassify costs or revenue.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576885","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2024","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-accounting/financial-dimension-defaults"},{"id":"rm-576882","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Enable project resources on general journal entries","desc":"<p>This feature expands the existing general journal functionality for modern projects.</p> <p>A new capability is added so general journal lines can have an associated <strong>project resource</strong>.</p> <ul> <li>Specifying the project resource on a journal line allows for increased tracking and auditability for where organizations want to track expense journals on a detailed per-resource basis instead of in a summary.</li> <li>Tracking expenses on a per-resource basis is especially helpful for scenarios around accruals where all expenses aren't approved and posted from the prior period and organizations want to track as per-resource accruals to reverse in the next month.</li> <li>Additional enhancements are being added for an improved user experience.</li> </ul> <p>This feature is specific to customers using the <strong>Project Operations Integrated with ERP</strong> deployment type.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance offers rich functionality with journals for many scenarios. It includes advanced capabilities such as workflow and reversals. When you use this functionality, you can create general journals in Finance for Microsoft Dataverse-based projects to post expenses.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576882","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/project-accounting/general-journals"},{"id":"rm-576860","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Post project invoice proposals using multithreaded batch tasks","desc":"<p>For organizations delivering complex projects, a single invoice proposal can include thousands of invoice lines. Similarly, thousands of customers might need to invoice every billing cycle. In both cases, the window is often short between the time users submit all transactions for the period, review them, and generate invoices. This feature significantly improves performance when posting the project invoice proposal and makes the final invoice document available.</p> <p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>New logic that splits the invoice posting process into multiple threads. This logic distributes the work instead of doing all the work sequentially in a single thread.</li> <li>A new project parameter where you configure the number of parallel threads.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>When you complete invoices on time, you meet billing deadlines and keep cash flowing into your business. This feature reduces the turnaround time for posting invoice proposals so you can quickly create the final invoice document to send to customers.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576860","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/invoicing/format-update-project-invoice-proposals#batch-posting-invoice-proposals-with-late-selection"},{"id":"rm-576812","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Resolve invoice proposal blocked in workflow","desc":"<p>For organizations using a structured and formal invoice workflow as part of their revenue collection, it's critical that invoices can be created and worked through to completion in a timely manner. When a configuration change causes an error, it's vital that these errors get resolved quickly so as not delay revenue generation. In support of timely invoicing, this new feature enables customers to unblock failed invoices on their own without complicated troubleshooting or the need to raise a support ticket.</p> <p>This feature provides the following capabilities:</p> <ul> <li>Use the new <strong>Reset invoice proposal workflow status</strong> form when invoicing workflow is enabled.</li> <li>View and reset failed workflows by users in the project accountant or project manager role without the need to involve IT or support.</li> <li>Preserve the existing workflow history for historical review and audit purposes.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Timely approval of customer invoices is critical to keeping your cash flow steady and your operations running smoothly. This feature helps you avoid delays by automatically correcting issues that could stop an invoicing workflow from being recalled or approved, so your business stays on track without extra effort.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576812","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/prod-pma/project-invoice-proposal-workflow"},{"id":"rm-576795","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize Project Operations - Use stocked products on projects","desc":"<p>The experiences for using inventoried products in Project Operations use the Inventory and Warehouse modules of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. To accurately estimate the availability of stocked items and their costs, the system uses Pricing and Inventory visibility services. Use the Inventory close process in Supply Chain Management to update the project cost and show accurate consumption of project budgets. Providing all the capabilities needed to manage stocked items on projects takes multiple release waves.</p> <p>This feature is specific to the Project Operations Integrated with ERP deployment type. It can be enabled in the <strong>Feature management</strong> workspace with the <strong>Enable stocked products usage for project operations integrated deployments</strong> feature. The same feature needs to be enabled in Dataverse under the feature control.</p> <p>This feature will leave preview and be generally available with the 10.0.49 release.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>If you manage projects that depend on inventoried products, this feature helps you stay in control. You can see real-time inventory levels across sites and warehouses, so you know exactly what’s available. With that insight, you can plan ahead, avoid delays, and keep your projects on track without overspending or running short on materials.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576795","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/project-operations/procurement/enable-stocked-products-integrated"},{"id":"rm-576850","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Copilot and AI innovation - Use Dynamics 365 Sales skills in Microsoft 365 Copilot Cowork","desc":"<p>As an admin, you can control who can access Copilot Cowork in your organization. The Dynamics 365 Sales plugin is installed by default in Copilot Cowork and available to all users who have access to Cowork.</p> <p>As a seller, you can use the sales skills in Copilot Cowork to:</p> <ul> <li>Understand customer, opportunity, and pipeline context without manually gathering information from multiple systems.</li> <li>Identify changes, risks, engagement patterns, and areas that require attention.</li> <li>Prioritize work across customers, opportunities, leads, and pipeline activities.</li> <li>Generate recommendations and next-best actions based on available business context.</li> <li>Analyze business performance, pipeline health, and sales execution trends.</li> <li>Support decision-making across individual, team, and organizational sales workflows.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>If you spend the day moving between CRM, email, meetings, calendars, and collaboration tools, Dynamics 365 Sales skills bring that context together in Microsoft 365 Copilot Cowork. By grounding Cowork in Dynamics 365 Sales data and Microsoft 365 signals, you get more relevant insights, recommendations, and actions in the flow of work. This helps you quickly understand customer relationships, opportunity health, pipeline changes, and next steps, so you spend less time gathering information and more time moving deals forward.</p> <p>By combining customer, opportunity, account, lead, activity, and pipeline information with emails, meetings, calendars, and collaboration signals, Cowork can help users understand what has changed, identify what requires attention, and determine appropriate next actions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576850","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/sales/use-copilot-cowork-sales-skills"},{"id":"rm-576787","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Opportunity acceleration - Accelerate Sales Opportunity Agent deployment with simplified admin configuration","desc":"<p>As an admin, you gain access to:</p> <ul> <li><p><strong>Simple configuration experience</strong>: Navigate an intuitive, guided setup interface designed for the Sales Opportunity Agent, eliminating complexity and reducing configuration time significantly.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Smart defaults</strong>: Leverage preoptimized settings for advanced configurations that are automatically applied, enabling rapid testing and deployment while maintaining best-practice standards.</p> </li> <li><p><strong>Segregation of basic and advanced settings</strong>: Enable the agent quickly with essential settings, then progressively unlock and configure advanced options as your team's expertise grows and business requirements evolve.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>As an admin, you get an easy setup experience to start testing and configuring the Sales Opportunity Agent right away. Basic settings and smart defaults let you enable the agent quickly, so you can see results fast. As adoption grows, you can fine-tune advanced options to fit your business needs without slowing your progress.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576787","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/sales/configure-opportunity-research-agent"},{"id":"rm-576871","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Sales and marketing - Calculate prices for external systems through API","desc":"<p>The new pricing calculation API allows external systems to programmatically retrieve active prices or price quotes directly from Supply Chain Management. Based on key input data provided by the external system—such as product and customer details—Supply Chain Management provides real-time pricing and discount calculation results.</p> <p>The API returns a product’s calculated price, including simple discounts. It doesn't calculate multiline discounts and assumes that each product in a request has a quantity of one.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Empower external applications to retrieve accurate, real-time pricing and discount calculation results directly from Supply Chain Management. Seamlessly integrate pricing logic into your sales channels to enhance quoting and pricing consistency.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576871","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/unified-pricing-management/upm-pricing-calculation-api"},{"id":"rm-576865","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Warehouse management - Automate dynamic work classification with Power FX","desc":"<p>Dynamic work classification powered by Power FX formulas lets you evaluate warehouse queries in real time, so you can prioritize work based on load priority or any operational data. This removes the need for multiple location directives or work templates, reducing configuration complexity and making your warehouse more responsive. You use familiar Power FX capabilities from Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance and the Power Platform to define and adjust operational logic with a flexible, low-code approach. This leads to faster decisions, better resource allocation, and more autonomy for your warehouse teams. You can classify work dynamically by carrier, load, or other criteria to optimize throughput and reduce overhead.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Boost warehouse efficiency and agility with real-time work classification using Power FX formulas. You can prioritize tasks based on load priority or any operational data, reducing configuration complexity, and responding quickly to changing conditions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576865","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/warehousing/dynamic-work-classification"},{"id":"rm-576867","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Warehouse management - Enable precise serial and batch capture in cluster picking","desc":"<p>This feature lets you control how serial and batch numbers are captured during cluster picking for items tracked below the location level in the reservation hierarchy. You get two new strategies in the cluster setup: capture serial and batch numbers once before distributing items or capture them separately for each cluster position. The new Enum in the cluster setup UI makes it easy to choose your preferred mode, so you can ensure every serial or batch number is matched to the right order.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Boost shipment accuracy and reduce picking errors with precise serial and batch capture for every order in cluster picking. You control how items are tracked, ensuring each serial or batch number is matched to the correct order, so your warehouse runs smoother and your customers get exactly what they expect.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576867","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/warehousing/set-up-cluster-picking#cluster-picking-strategy"},{"id":"rm-576866","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Warehouse management - Streamline transfer order receiving in WOM with ASNs","desc":"<p>Receive transfer orders in warehouse-only mode with a single license plate scan. This feature uses ASN-based packing structures to speed up inbound shipment processing and improve accuracy. The packing structure is defined within the ASN, so you can streamline your receiving workflow and reduce manual steps.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Streamline your warehouse receiving process in warehouse-only mode (WOM). With advance shipping notice (ASN) packing structures, you can process transfer orders using a single license plate scan, saving time and minimizing manual work.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p> <p><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/release-plan/2026wave1/enterprise-resource-planning/dynamics365-supply-chain-management/streamline-transfer-order-receiving-wom-asns\">Documentation</a></p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576866","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576876","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Build your low code hyperscale backend on Dataverse - Build your agentic flows with Dataverse SDK for Python","desc":"<p>The Microsoft Dataverse SDK for Python empowers data scientists and developers to build intelligent, compliant, and scalable agentic flows that integrate seamlessly with Dataverse. In the agentic age, where autonomous agents orchestrate workflows and act on behalf of users, the SDK provides the essential tools to interact programmatically with enterprise data platforms. The SDK supports structured data access, composable APIs, and governance features that are critical for building trustworthy and efficient agents.</p> <p>Key capabilities can include:</p> <ul> <li>Autonomous data agents that can query, update, and evaluate data quality</li> <li>Form prediction and autofill</li> <li>Support for agentic primitives like Model Context Protocol (MCP) and Agent-to-Agent (A2A) collaboration</li> </ul> <p>The SDK for Python offers a streamlined developer experience with support for common Create, Retrieve, Update, and Delete (CRUD) operations, bulk data processing, metadata access, and observability tools. SDK Python packages are to be published on PyPI.org with open-source support. The SDK is strategically positioned to enable agent-native development with semantic modeling, secure impersonation, and compliance built-in.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Enables data scientists and developers to create, access, and manage Dataverse business data using Python programming. The Dataverse SDK for Python implements common Python programming paradigms and best practices, provides a more natural Python interface to Dataverse, and supports community contributions.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576876","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"November CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/developer/data-platform/sdk-python/"},{"id":"rm-576817","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Finance and operations cross application integration - Monitor data management framework with Azure Monitor Application Insights","desc":"<p>By integrating data management framework telemetry for Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps, organizations can gain deeper visibility into data management executions, such as import and export jobs. This integration streams telemetry directly into the customer's own Azure Application Insights instance.</p> <p>By using this integration, customers can:</p> <ul> <li>Monitor import and export data management functions with start and end times.</li> <li>Monitor job status from source to staging and staging to target.</li> <li>Monitor failures with error messages at a granular level.</li> <li>Set up alerts and dashboards for proactive monitoring.</li> <li>Accelerate issue resolution.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Data management framework telemetry gives customers real‑time visibility into data import and export jobs. It provides progress tracking, detailed error insights, and proactive alerts through Azure Application Insights, helping teams troubleshoot faster, reduce operational effort, and run data management more reliably.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576817","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/monitoring-telemetry/monitoring-available-telemetry#dmf-telemetry-preview"},{"id":"rm-576810","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Improved enterprise experiences in Power Platform - Improve bulk delete user experience","desc":"<p>As you scale your data management operations, bulk delete must be predictable, transparent, and safe to operate across environments. In this release, Microsoft enhances bulk delete with an improved error handling experience and solution aware configuration support, delivering a more consistent, reliable, and enterprise‑ready data cleanup workflow.</p> <p>This release focuses on two core improvements that directly address admin pain points around visibility, consistency, and operational risk when managing bulk delete jobs at scale.</p> <p>Key improvements:</p> <ul> <li>Actionable error handling with an intuitive UI. Bulk delete now provides clear, job‑ and record‑level error details through an intuitive user interface. Instead of generic failures, admins can quickly understand what went wrong and why, enabling faster troubleshooting, fewer reruns, and more efficient resolution of large‑scale deletion jobs.</li> <li>Solution aware bulk delete for consistent multi‑environment operations. Bulk delete configurations are now solution aware, allowing deletion jobs to be safely transported across environments. This feature ensures consistent behavior from development to production, reduces manual reconfiguration, and significantly lowers the risk of misconfiguration in higher environments, delivering a more reliable and governed operational experience.</li> </ul> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This release significantly improves the reliability and operational safety of bulk delete jobs in Microsoft Dataverse. By making failures easy to understand and configurations portable across environments, admins can execute large‑scale data cleanup with confidence, reducing troubleshooting time, lowering support dependency, and minimizing the risk of costly misconfigurations in higher environments.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576810","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-576863","title":"Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration: Security and compliance - Prevent sending sensitive data to Purview audit logs","desc":"<p>To help prevent leaking sensitive customer data from Dataverse audit logs, all customer data is removed before these audit events are sent to Purview activity logging. Examples of sensitive customer data include financial information, medical and health data, and personally identifiable information.</p> <p>In Dataverse audit logs, create and update events—including a column’s before-and-after values—are captured. These values remain in Dataverse audit logs, but aren’t sent to Purview activity logging.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature restricts customer business data in Dataverse audit logs from being sent to Purview auditing streams. This helps ensure compliance and reduces the risk of leaking sensitive customer data.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled by admins/makers/marketers for end users</p>","products":["Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576863","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/important-changes-coming#removal-of-before-and-after-field-change-values-in-audit-events-sent-to-microsoft-purview"},{"id":"rm-576784","title":"Power Automate: Desktop flows - Debug flows using variable default values","desc":"<p>This feature introduces advanced debugging support by allowing you to assign default values to variables directly within the desktop flow designer. During debugging sessions, when you are starting the execution from a specific step of the automation, the assigned default values are automatically applied, enabling you to test specific scenarios without modifying actions or rerunning the flow from the beginning. This is especially useful when working with complex logic, conditions, or branches that depend on variable state.</p> <p>The feature is enabled automatically. To use it, edit a variable in the designer and define a default value for debugging. The value is applied only during debug runs and does not affect production executions. You can disable the behavior at any time by clearing the default value, restoring standard variable handling.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>This feature is for makers who build and maintain complex desktop flows. You can test and troubleshoot flows faster by setting variable default values directly in the designer, instead of restarting runs or manually preparing inputs each time. This reduces debugging time, lowers frustration, and helps you iterate more confidently when working with conditional logic and complex scenarios.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576784","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/desktop-flows/manage-variables"},{"id":"rm-576870","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Analyze processes using object-centric process mining","desc":"<p>Real business processes rarely flow as a single, linear <em>instance</em>. Events routinely touch <em>several objects of different types at the same time</em> (for example, creating an invoice for a specific order, or shipping a package that contains items from multiple orders). Object-centric process mining captures that reality by recording events that relate to <em>many objects and object types</em> in one process, preserving their relationships end‑to‑end.</p> <p>Here's the key idea: Instead of “one case → one sequence of activities,” object-centric process mining lets <em>one event</em> belong to <em>multiple objects</em> (and object types), keeping the full context intact.</p> <p>Object-centric process mining support in Power Automate Process Mining allows you to:</p> <ul> <li>Easily ingest your object-centric event logs from Azure Data Lake or OneLake.</li> <li>Map object and event-level attributes to unlock detailed analytical opportunities.</li> <li>Visualize your object-centric process in an understandable, customizable, and easy-to-read process map.</li> <li>Visualize key metrics in a comprehensive process overview.</li> <li>Analyze your process from process execution and throughput time viewpoint.</li> <li>Focus on specific process areas by using filters or by specifying a particular path in the Process Analysis widget.</li> </ul> <p>This premium feature is automatically enabled for all Power Automate Process Mining customers.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>Object-centric process mining delivers transformative insights that traditional process analysis simply can't capture. By analyzing how multiple object types, such as orders, items, deliveries, and invoices interact throughout your processes, you gain a complete, realistic view of your operations as they actually function.</p> <p>This comprehensive visibility enables you to identify hidden inefficiencies, such as bottlenecks that only appear when certain object combinations occur, or resource constraints that emerge from complex object interactions. You can pinpoint exactly where delays cascade across related objects, causing ripple effects that impact customer satisfaction and operational costs. The ability to analyze multiple dimensions simultaneously means faster root cause analysis and more accurate process optimization. Instead of piecing together fragmented views from separate analyses, you see the full picture immediately, reducing investigation time from weeks to hours and enabling data-driven decisions with confidence.</p> <p>Ultimately, object-centric process mining helps you reduce cycle times, lower operational costs, improve resource utilization, and enhance customer experience by addressing the real complexity of your business processes rather than oversimplified approximations.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576870","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"November CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/object-centric-overview"},{"id":"rm-576869","title":"Power Automate: Process mining - Analyze your processes in the process intelligence experience","desc":"<p>The process intelligence experience is a modern, flexible workspace designed for comprehensive process analysis. It provides a fully customizable analysis environment that combines multiple visualization and analysis components into cohesive, purpose-built workspaces. The platform empowers users to construct exactly the analytical view they need without technical complexity.</p> <p>Core capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Tab-based navigation: Organize related analyses into separate tabs within a single workspace, maintaining context while exploring different perspectives or process segments.</li> <li>Flexible layouts: Arrange tiles in customizable grid layouts, allowing you to position process maps, charts, tables, and metrics exactly where you need them for optimal visibility and comparison.</li> <li>Powerful tiles: Choose from a comprehensive library of visualization and analysis components—process maps, variant analysis, performance metrics, attribute breakdowns, case lists, and statistical views.</li> <li>Unified filtering: Apply filters once and have them cascade across all tiles in your workspace, ensuring consistency and enabling rapid scenario comparison without manual reconfiguration.</li> </ul> <p>The process intelligence experience saves your workspace configurations, allowing teams to create reusable analysis templates and share standardized views across the organization for consistent process monitoring and improvement tracking.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>The process intelligence experience eliminates the friction between your questions and your answers. Instead of navigating rigid dashboards or using a desktop application, your teams work in a fluid, customizable environment that adapts to their analysis needs in real-time. This means faster time-to-insight, reduced training overhead, and the ability to tackle complex process questions without constantly restarting your analysis. Business analysts, process owners, and improvement teams can now build comprehensive views that tell the complete story by comparing scenarios side-by-side, drilling from overview to detail without losing context, and sharing ready-made analyses with stakeholders. The result is more confident decision-making, shortened analysis cycles, and broader adoption of process intelligence across your organization.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for admins/makers/marketers automatically</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-16","modified":"2026-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576869","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"March CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/process-mining-studio-tab-management"},{"id":"rm-573450","title":"Microsoft Teams: Facilitator's enhanced protection skill can alert you to potential scams","desc":"<p>Facilitator can help you spot suspected attempts by people outside your organization to trick you into sharing sensitive information during a meeting. When Facilitator is in your meeting, its Protection skill uses AI to check the meeting transcript for signs of possible social engineering. If it detects a suspected attempt, you'll see a warning in the meeting, with options to end or to temporarily restrict information sharing.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573450","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2027","gaSort":202711},{"id":"rm-571663","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Microsoft Copilot in Field Service Mobile app","desc":"<p>Microsoft Copilot in the Dynamics 365 Field Service mobile app brings conversational AI chat capabilities directly to frontline workers. Once enabled, technicians can ask natural-language questions about Dynamics 365 Field Service data and receive contextual answers based on the app experience and their organization’s Dataverse data. With standard capabilities, Dataverse Q&amp;A supports questions such as “What is the work history of this asset?” or “Who worked on this job last?” Organizations can also extend the with custom experiences and agents available to frontline and back-office users.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571663","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-566700","title":"Microsoft Teams: IntelliFrame people labels in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"<p>Remote meeting participants know who is in the room and better follow the conversation with new IntelliFrame people labels that identify in-room participants and provide a hover-over contact card using voice and face profiles on intelligent cameras and in the cloud. Available with Teams Rooms on Windows licensed for Teams Rooms Pro.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-29","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566700","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-576276","title":"OneDrive: PDF annotation for sensitivity-label protected PDFs in OneDrive/SharePoint web viewer","desc":"<p>We're enabling PDF annotation for sensitivity-label protected PDFs in OneDrive and SharePoint on the web. With this update, users who have the appropriate usage rights can annotate these protected PDFs in place in their browser while preserving the file's sensitivity label, encryption, and usage rights when changes are saved.</p>","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576276","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-573696","title":"SharePoint: Copilot Search in SharePoint and OneDrive","desc":"<p>Copilot Search brings AI-powered, natural-language search to SharePoint and OneDrive, combining relevant results, AI-generated summaries with source references, intuitive filters, and a seamless handoff to Copilot.</p>","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573696","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-547827","title":"Microsoft Edge: Watermarking Protection","desc":"<p>Watermarking Protection in Microsoft Edge helps organizations visibly reinforce data protection policies by overlaying a persistent watermark on sensitive content viewed in the browser. This feature is designed to deter unauthorized sharing, support compliance efforts, and increase user awareness when handling confidential information.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-17","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547827","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-management-watermark-protection"},{"id":"rm-558341","title":"Microsoft Teams: Facilitator detects and answers questions","desc":"<p>Facilitator now automatically detects open questions raised during a Teams meeting and offers to help answer them using web search. When a participant asks a question (e.g., “What is an LLM?”) and no one answers, Facilitator posts a prompt offering to find an answer. Participants can select “Yes” to have the agent retrieve and share the information.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-01","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558341","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-575291","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Full-screen mode on task grid","desc":"<p>Task grid full-screen mode enables project managers and team members to expand the task grid to use the available screen space. By minimizing surrounding page elements, users gain a larger workspace for viewing and managing task hierarchies, schedules, assignments, dependencies, and other task details.</p> <p>Users can enter full-screen mode when they need a focused planning experience and return to the standard project view when they need access to other project information.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575291","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-500872","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Export Copilot metrics in the Copilot Dashboard","desc":"<p>This enables users to export row-level Copilot metrics from the Copilot Dashboard for reporting and deeper analysis.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500872","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570865","title":"Microsoft Dataverse: Prompt column values in bulk for existing records (backfill)","desc":"<p>Prompt columns can now generate AI values for records that already exist in your table, not just new or updated ones. Makers can choose to apply a prompt to existing records in bulk, optionally filtered to just the rows they need, so historical data gets the same AI-generated insights as incoming data, without touching each record one at a time.</p>","products":["Power Apps","Microsoft Dataverse","Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570865","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-574108","title":"Microsoft Teams: Admin center - Intelligent insights for meeting quality","desc":"<p>Gain proactive visibility into meeting quality across your organization with AI-powered insights in the Teams admin center that identify emerging patterns, highlight impacted users and locations, and surface likely causes with recommended actions. This helps IT administrators detect and address issues earlier, improve meeting quality, and stay ahead of potential disruptions.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574108","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573279","title":"Power Apps: Prompt Columns - multiple lines of text output","desc":"<p>Prompt columns can now store multilple lines of text as prompt output, enabling longer and detailed AI-generated insights to be stored in your tables.</p>","products":["Power Apps","Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-15","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573279","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1173208","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Copilot Analytics: Data export public preview for Copilot metrics in the Copilot dashboard","desc":"Updated October 15, 2026: We have updated the timeline. This post has also been updated to remind customers that this feature is default-on for Copilot Dashboard users with full company-level data access. The export output remains de-identified, with each user represented by a hashed ID. Please review and take any actions as appropriate for your organization. Thank you for your patience.\nThis MC post is associated with Roadmap ID 500872.\n[Introduction:]\nTo support deeper analysis of Copilot adoption, Microsoft is introducing a new export capability in the Copilot Dashboard. This feature allows dashboard users with company-level access to download de-identified Copilot usage metrics, aggregated by user and week, from the past six months. Organizations can use this data to track adoption trends, optimize licensing, and support AI transformation strategies.\nThis feature requires at least 50 Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses and applies to the Viva Insights web app.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Public Preview: Begins in early October 2026 (previously early December 2025), completes by late October 2026 (previously late December 2025).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Begins in mid-November 2026 (previously mid-October), completes by end of November 2026 (previously end of October).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\nCopilot Dashboard users with full company-level data access, including senior leaders (as identified in Entra ID), admin-assigned company-level users, delegates with company-level access, as well as global analysts and admins.\nNote: Group managers with data access limited to their own teams will not have access to this feature.\nWhat will happen:\n• Users will be able to export de-identified, row-level Copilot usage metrics from the dashboard.\n• The dataset includes weekly, user-level metrics from the past six months.\n• The export supports Copilot usage analysis across apps (such as Word, Excel, Teams), and includes two attributes: Organization, and Job function.\n• Organizations can use the data to track usage patterns, generate insights to inform adoption strategies, optimize licensing, and measure ROI.\n• The feature is enabled by default for eligible users.\n• Admins can manage access via Viva Feature Access Management (VFAM) settings, under Module: Viva Insights; Feature: Copilot Metrics Export.\n• No impact to user workflow unless accessed by eligible users.\n\nScreenshot 1 - View of the new Microsoft Copilot dashboard:\n\nScreenshot 2 - Example of output:\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• Review the assignment of the Copilot dashboard users with full company-wide data access and adjust VFAM policies as needed.\n• Communicate the upcoming feature to eligible users so they know what to expect.\n• No admin setup is required to start using the export.\n• Admins can disable the feature at the tenant or group level at any time using VFAM settings.\n\nLearn more:\nMicrosoft Viva Feature access management | Microsoft Learn\nConnect to the Microsoft Copilot Dashboard for Microsoft 365 customers | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1173208","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1269864","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: New chat sections for muted and meeting chats","desc":"Updated October 15, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft Teams is introducing two new system chat sections called Muted chats and Meeting chats. These sections allow users to organize their chat and channels list by grouping muted conversations and meeting chats into dedicated sections that users can turn on or off. The new Meeting chats section will replace the Meeting chats filter, that was previously available at the top of the chat and channel list.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 559605.\n[When this will happen]\n• General Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCC High, DoD): Rollout begins in early November 2026 (previously mid-October) and is expected to complete by mid-November 2026 (previously end of October).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All Microsoft Teams users in Microsoft 365 tenants, including Worldwide, GCC, GCC High, and DoD\n\nWhat will happen\nUsers may see up to two new system sections in their Teams chat and channels list:\n• Muted chats section• Enabled by default.\n• Muted chats that are not in Favorites or user‑created sections automatically move to this section.\n• The section appears at the bottom of the chat list.\n• Unread chats continue to appear bold.\n\n• Meeting chats section• Disabled by default.\n• When enabled by the user, meeting chats that are not in Favorites or user‑created sections automatically move to this section.\n• The section appears below the main chats list.\n• Unread chats continue to appear bold and contribute to badge counts.\n\n• Chats in Favorites or user‑created sections are not moved.\n• Users can drag and drop these sections to reorder them.\n• There are no admin controls for these sections.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo admin action is required.\nYou may want to:\n• Inform users that new chat sections are available and that they can turn them on or off.\n• Notify helpdesk staff that muted chats may appear in a separate section by default.\n• Direct users to Settings > Chats and channels to manage these sections.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-03","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1269864","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1155311","title":"(Updated) Viva Engage: Agents in Viva Engage communities Public Preview","desc":"Updated October 15, 2026: We have refreshed the public preview details, knowledge-source configuration, and analytics information. The general availability date will be announced in a future update. We apologize for any inconvenience.\n[Introduction]\nAgent in Viva Engage communities are now available in Public Preview. Community admins can add agents to communities to help draft answers to questions without best or verified answers based on community content and add context to posts by answering follow up questions using the community's conversations and SharePoint site and library.\n\nWe’re now adding the option for community admins to specify additional SharePoint sites outside the community as grounding sources. The agent will only use sites that community admins select, and it drafts answers from items that community members can view (Read).\nWe are also adding a new capability: tagging by community members. Tagging by community members enables Microsoft 365 copilot-licensed users to @-mention the community agent in the comments and replies of threads with follow up questions and requests to add context to posts. When tagged, the community agent will reply in the post. Tagging by community members will be enabled by default, but can be disabled by community admins in the agent settings.\n\nPublic preview updates\nCommunity Agent public preview now includes:\n• Community and network analytics: Community admins can view question coverage, answers generated and posted, review time, people helped, and estimated time saved. Network admins can view agent activity across communities, including agent status and posting mode. Time-period filters help admins understand activity over time.\n• Additional knowledge sources: Community admins can add public websites and enable content from other public communities in their Engage network. Admins can also turn on Only use expert and verified content to limit the community conversations used to best answers, verified answers, and content written or created by community admins and experts.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n• Community Agent remains available in public preview. The general availability date will be announced in a future update.\n• At general availability, a new network-wide Community Agent setting will replace the public preview toggle. We’ll provide at least 30 days’ notice and make the new setting available at the start of that notice period, so admins can set their network’s preference before general availability.\n• Before general availability, review the new network-wide Community Agent setting when it becomes available and set your network’s preference.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]Who is affected: Viva Engage community admins and members with Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses; Global and Engage admins managing Viva Engage networks\nWhat will happen:\n• During Public Preview:• Admins can opt their network into the preview via the Engage admin center: Engage admin center > Tenant Settings > Enable Community Agent Public Preview.\n\nOnce enabled, admins can add agents to any community they manage.\nFigure i. Add agent to community​\n\nThe agent will proactively draft answers to unanswered questions using past conversations.\nBy default, the agent posts answers automatically.\nAdmins can configure whether the agent posts answers automatically or only after approval and if tagging by community members is enabled.\nFigure ii. Configure the agent's capabilities and knowledge sources\n\n[Grounding on SharePoint sites outside the community]\n• Community admins can add SharePoint sites and libraries outside the community as additional grounding sources (for sites/libraries they administer).\n• When an admin adds a site or library, they’ll be prompted to grant the community’s Microsoft 365 group Read access if it doesn’t already have permission.\n• The agent only drafts answers using content that all community members can view (Read).\n• By default, the agent uses the community’s SharePoint site and library. Any sites outside the community are optional and add to (not replace) the default grounding.\n\nIf Require review is enabled, admins and designated experts will be notified when the agent drafts an answer. They can approve, edit, or dismiss the response.\nFigure iii. Community admins and experts can review agent suggestions​\n\nIf tagging by community members is enabled, then community members can @-mention the agent in messages.\nComing soon (General Availability):\n\nThe agent will only use content that all community members can access.\nAdmins must be owners of the SharePoint sites they wish to configure.\nAdmins can add additional SharePoint sites to expand the agent’s grounding knowledge.\nThe agent will be grounded by default on the community’s SharePoint site.\nCommunity members can tag the community agent in community posts.\nAll Microsoft 365 Copilot licensed users will have access to the Community Agent by default.\nThe Community Agent Public Preview toggle will be retired.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• If participating in preview:\n• Opt your network into the preview via the Engage admin center\n• Communicate this change to helpdesk staff.\n• Update internal documentation that references Viva Engage Community Agent behavior or setup.\n• No action is required at GA; the feature will be on by default.\n\nLearn more: Set up and manage agents in Viva Engage communities | Microsoft Learn\n[Compliance considerations:]\nConsiderationExplanation\nUses customer dataThe agent accesses SharePoint content to generate answers. Only content accessible to all community members is used.\nIntroduces AI/ML agent capabilitiesThe agent uses generative AI to draft responses based on SharePoint content.\nAdmin control available(Optional) Community admins can configure which SharePoint sites are used for grounding. Admin must be site owner.\nUser interaction with generative AIEnd users receive AI-generated answers grounded in community conversations and SharePoint content\nCan be controlled through Entra ID group membershipAdmin access and site ownership can be managed via Entra ID group membership.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1155311","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1187781","title":"(Updated) Viva Engage: Community feeds improvements","desc":"Updated October 15, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction:]\nWe’re introducing a simpler way to view conversations in Viva Engage communities, organized by recent posts rather than recent activity. This new view is designed to make it easier for users to follow discussions and will be available as an option, alongside the current system, for those who prefer sorting by recent activity and filtering to new conversations only.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 513275.\n[When this will happen:]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in October 2026 and expect to complete by the end of October 2026.\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nThis change should align better with how people expect to browse and engage with content in their communities, while still preserving the triage flow for those who prefer it.\nWho is affected: All Viva Engage users in your organization.\nCurrent experience:\n• Communities default to “new” and “recent activity” if there’s any new content (posts or replies).\n• If there’s no new content, the feed falls back to “all.”\n• Unread indicators on content only exist in the “new” feed.\n\nNew experience:\n• The feature will be ON by default.\n• Communities will default to “all” and “recent posts”:\n\n• Unread indicators will exist in both the “new” and “all” feeds.\n• A sticky user preference will be introduced:• If someone changes the feed (new/all) or sort order (recent posts/recent activity), we will maintain that setting across their communities.\n• If someone picks “new” and there’s no new content in the next community, we will fall back to “all” for that community visit, but “new” will remain the preference for that user.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\nNo action is required.\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1187781","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-561854","title":"Access: Rounded corners on Access form controls","desc":"<p>We’re making it easier to give your Access apps a polished, up-to-date feel. With the new CornerRadius property, you can add rounded corners to form controls—bringing a softer, more modern look to your designs.</p>","products":["Access"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561854","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1261587","title":"Microsoft Purview | Data Lifecycle Management - Hard delete OneDrive and SharePoint files with priority cleanup workflow","desc":"Updated October 15, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are introducing a new priority cleanup workflow in Microsoft Purview Data Lifecycle Management that allows administrators to permanently delete (hard delete) specific OneDrive and SharePoint content types, even when retention policies or holds are in place. This capability helps reduce data exposure risk from rapidly growing Copilot-related content while maintaining compliance through required eDiscovery admin review and approval.\nThis change is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558343.\n[When this will happen:]\nPublic Preview: We will begin rolling out mid-August 2026 (previously mid-July) and expect to complete by mid-September 2026 (previously late July).\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide) Rollout begins mid-October 2026 and is expected to complete by end of November 2026 (previously mid-November).\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n• Microsoft 365 administrators managing Microsoft Purview Data Lifecycle Management\n• Organizations using OneDrive for Business and SharePoint Online with retention policies or holds\n\nWhat will happen:\n• Admins can create a priority cleanup policy targeting specific content types in OneDrive and SharePoint.\n• A new Delete data permanently option enables hard deletion of targeted items.\n•\n• Content deleted through this workflow is fully removed and is no longer discoverable in:• SharePoint search\n• Copilot experiences\n• eDiscovery (after required approval)\n\n• For content under hold, eDiscovery admin review and approval is required before deletion.\n• This capability is not enabled by default and requires explicit admin configuration.\n• There is no change to user workflows unless an admin configures and applies a priority cleanup policy.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• Review your organization’s data risk and retention strategy, especially for Copilot-generated content such as Teams transcripts.\n• In Microsoft Purview, plan and configure a priority cleanup policy if permanent deletion is required for specific content types:• Navigate to Microsoft Purview portal > Data Lifecycle Management > Priority cleanup.\n• Create a new policy and select Delete data permanently in the policy settings.\n\n• Ensure appropriate eDiscovery admin roles and approval processes are in place for content under hold.\n• Update internal governance or compliance documentation to reflect this new deletion capability.\n\nLearn more: Compare types of groups in Microsoft 365 - Microsoft 365 admin | Microsoft Learn\n[Compliance considerations:]\nCompliance areaExplanation\nAlteration of existing customer data processingThis change introduces a priority cleanup workflow that allows permanent deletion of specific OneDrive and SharePoint content types, even when retention policies or holds exist, subject to required approval.\neDiscovery or Content SearchContent deleted through the priority cleanup workflow is fully removed and no longer discoverable in eDiscovery or Content Search after eDiscovery admin review and approval for items under hold.\nRetention policies, holds, or deletion workflowsAdds a new admin-controlled deletion workflow that can override standard retention outcomes through an approved hard-delete process.\nAdmin controls and compliance monitoringThe feature is managed by administrators in Microsoft Purview and includes review and approval steps that support compliance oversight and auditing.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1261587","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569424","title":"Excel: Excel canvas","desc":"<p>A Copilot-generated canvas that turns workbook data into a polished, interactive view of key visualizations, metrics, and insights. As workbook data changes, it automatically updates to reflect the latest information. Users can modify the canvas by chatting with Copilot.</p>","products":["Excel"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569424","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-565860","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.154 - Sign in to Edge with a Google account","desc":"<p>Users can now sign in to Microsoft Edge using a Google account in addition to the Microsoft account from the profile menu and Edge sign-in screen. Available for Windows and macOS devices. Admins can control availability to this feature using the NonMicrosoftAccountSignInEnabled policy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-16","modified":"2026-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565860","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-573245","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Out of the box real time translation on digital channels","desc":"<p>With this feature, users get an out-of-the-box solution for translation services, so they don't need to bring their own web resources. Service representatives get updated feature usage with more configurations. They can tailor their conversations more accurately based on their existing skills and preferences. The feature is transparent yet modernized with new settings, making conversations easier to consume in a language of the representative's choice.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573245","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-572676","title":"Microsoft Purview: Adaptive Scope evaluation control with recipient and site owner lifecycle status","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Adaptive Scopes will provide administrators with explicit control over lifecycle-state evaluation for recipients and site owners, helping ensure policy targeting and scope membership remain aligned with organizational requirements.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=572676","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-570846","title":"Microsoft Teams: Express face enrollment","desc":"<p>Express face enrollment makes it easier for users to create a face profile in Teams by using their camera during eligible meetings, after they opt in. Once enrolled, users can be recognized in supported Teams Rooms experiences, helping identify who is in the room and improving downstream meeting experiences such as Copilot and recap. Admins can enable or disable the feature for their organization.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570846","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-576395","title":"Power Pages: Design studio - Enhance OpenID Connect with encrypted token support","desc":"<p>This feature adds support for token-level encryption during authentication, allowing Power Pages to accept encrypted ID tokens in addition to signed tokens. It ensures secure claim transmission, improves compatibility with advanced identity providers, and strengthens overall authentication security without changing existing sign-in flows.</p> <p>Business Value:</p> <p>You can integrate with more secure identity providers to meet stricter security and compliance requirements. This helps you expand into high-trust scenarios and allows your organization to confidently use Power Pages for sensitive, external-facing applications.</p> <p>Enabled for:</p> <p>Enabled for end users automatically</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576395","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575288","title":"Microsoft Teams: Phishing Detection in Teams Messaging","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams is introducing AI-powered phishing detection that uses conversation context to identify phishing and social engineering in higher-risk messaging scenarios, primarily external first-contact chats. Additional protection may apply in certain regions or scenarios. The capability is used only for security protection, and users may see warnings when suspicious activity is detected.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575288","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-576195","title":"Microsoft Teams: PowerPoint Live support for webinars and structured meetings on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>Participants joining webinars and structured meetings from Teams Rooms on Android can view and interact with PowerPoint Live presentations. This provides greater flexibility and accessibility while keeping room participants aligned with the active presentation.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=576195","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573266","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Quality evaluation - One-Time Evaluation Frequency","desc":"<p>Quality evaluation plans now support a Once frequency type for both case evaluations and conversation evaluations. When creating an evaluation plan, users can select Once from the Frequency type dropdown to run the evaluation a single time instead of on a recurring schedule or trigger-based cadence.</p> <p>This option is useful for one-time evaluation runs where ongoing recurrence is not needed. Once selected, the plan is configured to execute only one time based on the specified plan start date.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573266","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574111","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot response personalization - Memory citations","desc":"<p>When Copilot Chat uses memory to personalize a response, users can now see what informed the answer. Select Sources beneath the response, then open the Personalization tab to view the custom instructions, saved memories, memories learned from conversations, and past chats that shaped the response. From there, users can return to a cited chat to pick up where they left off or review and delete saved memories. Memory citations appear only when memory is turned on.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574111","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-561032","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – New Guided Experience to Diagnose and Resolve DLP Issues","desc":"<p>We’re introducing a new guided diagnostics experience to help users understand why their DLP policies may not be behaving as expected. This experience provides a clear summary of why a DLP action was taken on a document, including which policies were triggered, the order of evaluation, and detailed insights into which conditions evaluated as true or false.<br> For Microsoft 365 E5 customers, the experience also includes Copilot-powered insights and tailored recommendations to accelerate troubleshooting and policy optimization.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561032","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569934","title":"Microsoft Teams: Events in Meet app in Teams in GCC","desc":"<p>Users can now use the Teams Meet app to discover events across their organization, track what important events are upcoming, and plan and organize their own professional events. With this release, Meet app will be renamed to Events app.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-26","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569934","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569206","title":"Microsoft Teams: Pop out calls into a new browser window","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams browser app users will be able to pop out calls into a simplified call window that stays available while they navigate away from, hide, or minimize the tab or progressive web app (PWA) hosting the call. This helps users multitask and collaborate more easily during calls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-13","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569206","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573168","title":"Planner: Planner Agent in Copilot V2 Improvements","desc":"<p>Planner Agent brings Planner’s intelligent work management directly into Copilot Chat, enabling users to create, update, and manage personal tasks and shared basic plans without switching context. Integrated across Microsoft 365, it provides insights into priorities, deadlines, and at-risk work, along with interactive task cards to help users stay organized and keep work moving.</p> <p>Building on the initial launch, planned improvements include:</p> <ul> <li>Improved context handling and support for larger plans.</li> <li>Higher-quality responses through model upgrades, refined prompts, and better grounding.</li> <li>Greater reliability and reduced latency for more consistent, responsive interactions.</li> <li>Expanded task management capabilities, including broader task assignment support.</li> <li>User experience enhancements to make managing tasks and plans in Copilot Chat more intuitive.</li> <li>New capabilities, including scheduled task catch-ups.</li> </ul>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-14","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573168","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-532720","title":"Microsoft Teams: Organization Evaluation Score for Apps and Agents","desc":"<p>Today, IT admins manually review trust data for Teams apps and agents in the Teams admin center to ensure they meet organizational security, privacy, and compliance standards. This feature introduces a scalable, automated evaluation process. Admins can define their organization’s trust requirements once, and the system will automatically assess each app and agent—generating an evaluation score and detailed evaluation report tailored to those requirements. This enables faster, more consistent decision-making by clearly identifying which apps and agents meet the organization’s standards and where further review is needed.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532720","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-168524","title":"Microsoft Teams: Co-organizer updates in Webinars","desc":"<div><span>Co-organizers can edit webinar details, publish the event, and cancel the event, similar to the organizer.</span> </div>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-10-20","modified":"2026-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=168524","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release (Entire Organization)","Targeted Release (Select People)"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-574125","title":"Visio: Desktop Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server","desc":"<p>The Microsoft Visio Desktop MCP Server enables compatible AI clients to connect with the Visio Desktop application to create, read, and update Visio diagrams using natural language. It runs locally on Windows and requires a licensed Visio Desktop application.</p>","products":["Visio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574125","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-574124","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Enable MCP tools for POS returns","desc":"<p>This feature provides reusable MCP tools for Store Commerce POS returns. These tools expose Commerce return capabilities as structured actions that customers, partners, and agent developers can use to build conversational or agentic return experiences.</p> <p>The tools enable agentic experiences to look up the original purchase using supported identifiers such as receipt, order, invoice, or confirmation number; retrieve matching transactions and returnable lines; identify items that are returnable, partially returnable, already returned, or not returnable; create a return using selected lines, quantities, and reason codes; determine eligible refund options for original-tender refund scenarios; and execute eligible original-tender refunds through existing Commerce return and payment logic.</p> <p>The tools can also explain return eligibility, policy restrictions, and why specific lines may or may not be returnable. They can analyze prior returns and refunds to surface duplicate-refund risk, frequent-return patterns, cross-store return history, or other return-risk indicators. Tool responses provide structured data that host experiences can use to present return details, choices, summaries, and next steps in the experience they build.<br> Customers can use these tools from POS-embedded agents, chat-based copilots, workflow orchestrators, or other agentic surfaces.</p> <p>Setup is performed by an administrator, IT owner, or implementation partner. Customers configure the host surface, authorize the agent or integration to call the tools, and maintain existing Commerce return policies, reason codes, tender rules, and payment configuration.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574124","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-472030","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Retention based on Last Accessed for files in OneDrive and SharePoint","desc":"<p>This creates the ability to apply Retention to each SharePoint or OneDrive item based on when it was last accessed by a user. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-11","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=472030","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-564617","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Rights Management connector – Certificate-based authentication","desc":"<p>The Microsoft Rights Management (RMS) connector is moving from shared-secret authentication to certificate-based authentication, improving its security posture. With this update, administrators configure their own Microsoft Entra app registration and certificate, then use the new PowerShell module to configure the certificate for each workload (Connector, Exchange, SharePoint, and FCI). New PowerShell cmdlets handle certificate import, registry configuration, private-key permissions, and validation. As part of this change, the connector setup no longer provisions an Entra service principal or issues a shared secret on the customer's behalf. Customers should plan to register an Entra ID application and upload a certificate before installing or upgrading the connector.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-03","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564617","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561327","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection- File Labeler and File Viewer for MacOS","desc":"<p>This feature is bringing the Information Protection Filer Labeler and Viewer applications to the MacOS platform. Enabling customers to have the same capabilities available on Mac. Core functionality will be available with the exception of the Advanced label-based protection feature.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-07","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561327","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575298","title":"SharePoint: Agent chat web part","desc":"<p>This is a new web part available for modern page editors in SharePoint. The web part can be configured to use any M365 Copilot agent.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575298","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570870","title":"Work IQ: Microsoft IQ","desc":"<p>Provide a unified intelligence layer that helps agents discover, reason over, and use organizational knowledge.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570870","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573705","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Procurement Agent - Define custom scenarios for agent-generated supplier emails","desc":"<p>Business end-users and buyers can define and maintain their own outbound follow-up scenarios and use them wherever built-in scenarios are used today:</p> <ol> <li>Scenario maintenance — a dedicated setup page where users create, edit, and maintain custom follow-up scenarios. Each scenario carries its own name, the instructions that shape the email the agent writes, and the business entity it applies to.</li> <li>Scenario-driven configuration — follow-up configurations are built around the chosen scenario, so criteria, email content, and agent behavior all follow the scenario the user selected.</li> <li>Scenario-driven runtime — when the agent runs, it generates and sends messages according to the selected scenario's intent and instructions.</li> <li>Self-describing configuration history — scenario details are captured with each saved configuration, so the audit history of an agent configuration remains readable even if the underlying scenario definition is later changed or removed.</li> </ol>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573705","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-568067","title":"Microsoft Teams: See more messages on mobile","desc":"<p>We are introducing a more streamlined messaging experience that displays more content on screen while improving readability when using Teams on mobile. These updates make it easier to scan conversations and follow the discussion flow, helping users stay productive and engaged wherever they work.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-03","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568067","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-566703","title":"Microsoft Edge: Upgraded Copilot new tab page","desc":"<p>Search, chat, and explore the web from one search box with Copilot-suggested actions and curated work content to help your users get things done faster on the Copilot new tab page. Users will see upgraded Copilot new tab page functionality and features.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-26","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566703","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575287","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-Admin Units Support for Copilot & Cowork DLP","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention is extending Administrative Units support to Microsoft 365 Copilot, Copilot Chat, and Cowork. This enables organizations to delegate management of supported Copilot DLP policies to administrators within their assigned Administrative Units, supporting regional, departmental, and regulatory boundaries without granting tenant-wide policy-management permissions. Existing tenant-wide policies continue to apply, and configuration is optional for organizations choosing to use Administrative Unit (AU)-scoped management.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562016","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Policy Sync & Device Health AI-Powered Investigation","desc":"<p>AI agent skill to detect and alert unhealthy policy sync and device configuration.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562016","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-574363","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Auto-labeling for legacy Office files","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview server-side auto-labeling will support legacy Microsoft Office file formats, including Word (.doc), Excel (.xls), and PowerPoint (.ppt). Organizations can automatically evaluate and apply sensitivity labels to these files in SharePoint and OneDrive.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574363","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558933","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI-generated meeting memory for knowledge retention (formerly AI-generated meeting archive)","desc":"<p>Teams will store AI-generated meeting memory files for meetings where Intelligent Recap was turned on, allowing Copilot (and Facilitator) to retain key insights from meetings beyond transcript retention periods and when a transcript was not saved. This enables Copilot to continue answering questions about past meetings even after the transcript expires or the meeting is over. Admins can also configure how long this AI-generated meeting memory file is stored.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-08","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558933","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573625","title":"Microsoft Teams: Event Chat now available for Events optimized for a large audience in GCC, GCC High and DoD","desc":"<p>All users in Events larger than 1,000 users or in any Event optimized for a large audience can now chat with one another in a public event chat in GCC, GCC High and DoD.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573625","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-562340","title":"Microsoft Teams: Preloaded video for Teams Events and Meetings","desc":"<p>Users can now upload videos directly into a Teams event or meeting from OneDrive from the \"Manage view\" options when an organizer has turned on Manage What Attendees See mode. This ensures a smoother high quality video playback with a more consistent experience for attendees.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-14","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562340","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573698","title":"Outlook: Copilot Chat available in shared and delegate mailboxes","desc":"<p>Shared mailbox users and delegates with read and manage (full access) and/or mail folder-level permission will now be able to access Copilot Chat directly from their shared and delegate mailboxes in classic Outlook, when added as a <a href=\"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/sharing/open-and-use-a-shared-mailbox-in-outlook\">resource</a>.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573698","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-572682","title":"Power Apps: Control information density in model-driven apps","desc":"<p>Model-driven apps now support configurable display density settings that let users choose how information is spaced throughout the application. Users can select from three density options:</p> <ul> <li>Comfortable (default)</li> <li>Cozy</li> <li>Compact<br> ​</li> </ul> <p>Each density setting adjusts layout spacing while maintaining accessibility target-size requirements. Administrators and makers can configure default density settings at the environment and app level, while individual users can personalize the experience by selecting their preferred density. User preferences take precedence over administrator-configured defaults.<br> ​<br> Display density requires the Header and Navigation Refresh experience to be enabled, and will be enabled by default for apps that have Header and Navigation Refresh enabled. Makers can disable display density for their apps using the app setting if needed.<br> ​<br> Some controls and components may not yet support display density. These controls will continue to render using their standard spacing regardless of the selected density setting. Custom component developers can add support for display density by adopting Fluent design spacing tokens. Learn more in the documentation.<br> ​<br> Availability</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Release channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2609.1</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Dependencies</td> <td>Header and navigation refresh enabled</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature scope</td> <td>Users (enabled by default)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=572682","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/user/appearance-settings"},{"id":"rm-573277","title":"Power Pages: Create Power Pages SPA site from the Power Pages studio","desc":"<p>Quickly get started with modern single-page application (SPA) development by creating a site directly from Power Pages Studio. Continue building and customizing your experience using your preferred development tools and frameworks.</p>","products":["Power Pages"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570852","title":"Work IQ: A2A and MCP elicitation","desc":"<p>Enable A2A and MCP tasks to request missing information or authorization and then resume.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570851","title":"Work IQ: A2A and MCP long running tasks","desc":"<p>Enable durable long-running A2A and MCP tasks with progress tracking, later result retrieval, and cancellation.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570851","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570868","title":"Work IQ: REST endpoint tools","desc":"<p>Enable agents to use supported REST endpoints as tools through governed Work IQ integrations.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570868","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570673","title":"Work IQ: Retrieve","desc":"<p>Enable agents to retrieve relevant Microsoft 365 content and context through Work IQ.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570673","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-574116","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Collaborative comments for planning cubes and dimensions","desc":"<p>Create and manage contextual discussion threads directly on planning cubes and dimensions. Users can comment on dimension cells, detailed or aggregate cube cells, and reporting rows; reply to and mention colleagues; receive email notifications; and resolve or reactivate discussions. Public and private visibility options, together with an All Comments view, filters, export, and role-based management actions, support collaboration throughout the planning cycle.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574116","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574118","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Improved planning writeback performance and flexibility","desc":"<p>Business performance planning improves the performance and flexibility of writeback from the Matrix visual.<br> Writeback processing has been optimized to improve performance for planning adjustments, particularly for larger splash and multi-update operations. The improvements also optimize writeback for users with dimension security, where additional security validation is required.<br> In addition, report designers no longer need to include a field from every cube dimension in the Matrix visual to enable writeback. The Matrix can now be designed using only the dimensions relevant to the planning experience while still supporting writeback to the underlying cube.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574118","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574117","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Manage dimension security with Microsoft Entra groups","desc":"<p>Administrators can now assign Microsoft Dataverse group teams backed by Microsoft Entra groups to Business performance planning dimension security groups. Previously, dimension security assignments were limited to individual users. The updated experience allows administrators to view and add eligible Entra group-backed teams alongside users, with separate membership information for each assignment type.</p> <p>To use this capability, the Dataverse group team must first be configured correctly and assigned an appropriate Business performance planning security role.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574117","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/business-performance-planning/bpp-security"},{"id":"rm-558435","title":"Microsoft Edge: Security Update Alerts in the Edge management service","desc":"<p>Administrators can choose a severity threshold and receive alerts when a new Edge update includes security fixes that meet or exceed that level, including zero day fixes. This helps organizations quickly identify updates that may require attention, while avoiding unnecessary notifications for routine releases.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-18","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558435","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558286","title":"Microsoft Teams: Intelligent meeting recap available without saving transcript","desc":"<p>Intelligent recap can now be generated without retaining a transcript after the meeting. Meeting organizers can choose this setting from the meeting options before the meeting, or organizers and eligible participants can enable it during the meeting. After the meeting, the AI Summary will be available, but other elements of the recap may not be available (Chapters, Topics, Mentions, Audio recap).</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558286","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574104","title":"Power Apps: Manage model-driven app AI features from consolidated settings","desc":"<p>Consolidated AI settings make it easier for makers and admins to find and manage AI capabilities for model-driven apps across two complementary surfaces.</p> <p>In Maker Studio, the <strong>Settings</strong> dialog in the model app form designer adds a new top-level <strong>Copilot and AI</strong> tab. Makers can see and adjust all available AI options for the app in one place instead of finding them scattered among all the other settings.</p> <p>In the Power Platform admin center, model-driven app AI settings are consolidated from <strong>Environment &gt; Settings</strong> into <strong>Copilot Hub &gt; Power Apps</strong>. This provides a central location for settings such as Generative pages, Copilot in apps, and the in-app AI skills. The in-app skill settings are organized into these groups:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Data entry:</strong> Form fill assistance.</li> <li><strong>Summary:</strong> Row summaries.</li> <li><strong>Data analysis:</strong> AI-generated charts and natural-language search and filtering.</li> </ul> <p>Labels and descriptions are aligned across Maker Studio and Copilot Hub so makers and admins can understand how the controls relate.</p> <p>As part of this consolidation, the old model-driven app AI switches under <strong>Environment &gt; Settings</strong> will also be retired and removed.</p> <h3>Availability</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Weekly</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2610.3</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Admins or makers</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-13","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574104","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571682","title":"Power Apps: Modern, refreshed look for embedded model-driven apps","desc":"<p>Extends the modern, refreshed look to embedded app experiences so model-driven app content retains consistent Fluent styling and interaction patterns when it appears inside another host. This was previously enabled for the monthly channel with the 2602.1 release and is now being enabled for the semiannual channel with the 2609.3 release.</p> <p>Availability</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Release Channel</td> <td>Semiannual</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2609.3</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature Scope</td> <td>Users (always enabled)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571682","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/user/modern-fluent-design"},{"id":"rm-571681","title":"Power Apps: Modern, refreshed look for the mail app","desc":"<p>Extends the Fluent-based modern, refreshed look for model-driven apps to the mail app, providing consistent controls, spacing, colors, and visual treatment when users work in that app. This was previously enabled for the monthly channel with the 2602.1 release and is now being enabled for the semiannual channel with the 2609.3 release.</p> <p>Availability</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Value</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Applies to</td> <td>Model-driven apps</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Release channel</td> <td>Semiannual</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Version</td> <td>2609.3</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature scope</td> <td>Users (always enabled)</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571681","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/user/modern-fluent-design"},{"id":"rm-569209","title":"Microsoft Teams: Add multiple steps when building a workflow from scratch","desc":"<p>You will now be able to add multiple steps to your workflow when building one from scratch.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569209","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-570429","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Survey taking experience refinements","desc":"<p>This feature is a collection of improvements including updates to the auto-save experience for comments, simplifying survey navigation through buttons by consolidating the \"Skip\" and \"Done\" buttons into a single \"Next\" button, and to give the survey taker greater control over question progression by refining the auto-scroll behavior when updating answers to questions.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570429","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-501292","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): User can use Hubspot Connector in Researcher","desc":"<p>The HubSpot connector allows users using the Researcher agent to be able to leverage 3rd party information from HubSpot to enrich generated responses with relevant information.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-10-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501292","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-560601","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Reduce temporary file noise for Endpoint activities in IRM","desc":"<p>When files are opened in Windows, the operating system, and applications (for example, Microsoft Office and browsers) can create, rename, and delete temporary files as part of normal behavior. The Endpoint client audits these activities, resulting in high-volume, low-signal events that appear as “noise” for Insider Risk Management (IRM) customers. While global exclusions exist (file type, keyword, file path, etc.), some temporary file naming patterns are not easily captured with the current exclusions, leaving customers without a practical way to reduce noise without over-excluding. This feature introduces built-in filtering for well-known temporary file name patterns so that Endpoint file operations are excluded from IRM activity explorer and scoring reducing noise allowing customers to focus on the most relevant alerts. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-07","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560601","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2027","gaSort":202705,"preview":"March CY2027"},{"id":"rm-574123","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Unify product receipt and item requirement posting","desc":"<p>This feature posts a purchase order product receipt and the consumption of its linked project item requirement in one transaction. It applies when automatic item consumption is enabled or when you select Consume immediately while posting the product receipt. Both updates succeed together, or the system rolls them both back when an error occurs. The posting flow prevents duplicate project posting and preserves existing behavior for batch posting and cancellation or correction flows. This combined posting can only be triggered from product receipt posting. The feature is available for public preview in version 10.0.49 and is off by default. It applies to Project Operations connected with ERP and Project Operations for manufacturing deployment types.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574123","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568371","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Rule-based tagging and auto-resolution of alerts based on business needs of the customer.","desc":"<p>Alert auto-resolution &amp; tagging rules let you tell DLP, in advance, how to handle predictable alerts. You define a rule once, and from then on DLP applies it automatically to every new alert:<br> ● Resolve alerts you don't need to see - e.g., Low-severity alerts for mail sent only to your trusted partner domains, so they never reach your triage queue.<br> ● Tag alerts so you can find and route them - e.g., label every alert from your Legal department as a “Business Process”.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568371","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-528978","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-Priority content support for Risky AI usage","desc":"<p>With this update, Risky AI usage policy template will support priority content. Customers can define Sensitive Info Types (SITs), Trainable Classifiers, Sensitivity Labels as priority content, and get alerted only when the activity matches the selected priority content. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=528978","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-570871","title":"Work IQ: Updating documents in Office","desc":"<p>Work IQ enables agents to create and edit Microsoft Office documents using organizational context, helping users produce and update content more efficiently.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Work IQ"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570871","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575285","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-Apply Purview network data security DLP policies to all websites, or all websites except specific cloud apps, through Entra GSA Internet Access integration","desc":"<p>With this feature, admins can scope their network data security data loss prevention policies, integrated with Entra GSA Internet Access, to apply to all websites (<em>.</em>) or all websites except specific cloud apps, allowing them to apply protection to cloud apps and websites that are not in the Defender Cloud App Catalog.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575285","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-518289","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint and Viva Insights Integration - Continuous employee engagement for leaders and managers with workplace metrics","desc":"<p>Stay connected to your team’s engagement with Viva Insights Workplace Metrics, available alongside your survey results in Viva Glint. Between survey cycles, leaders and managers can use these continuous, real-time metrics to see how their team is working and evaluate whether actions they are taking to improve engagement are having the desired impact. This feature currently supports work-life balance and collaboration metrics, with more areas planned in the future.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518289","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-570469","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft M365): Copilot Chat can now better match search results from text that appears inside images embedded in Word and PowerPoint files","desc":"<p>Copilot Chat can now better match search results from text that appears inside images embedded in Word and PowerPoint files is user's working files — such as scanned contracts in Word, text from tables, text from images — content that was previously difficult to search and find.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-10","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570469","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-561208","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management – Archive SharePoint files under retention","desc":"<p>We are introducing file archiving support in SharePoint Online, utilizing this feature administrators can seamlessly include archiving actions within their existing data retention policies. This means that, in addition to keeping or deleting data, admins can now leverage Purview DLM to archive files according to organizational requirements, ensuring comprehensive governance across all stages of the content lifecycle in SharePoint Online. Retention based file archiving moves inactive content to low-cost storage, lowering costs with no compromise on Compliance, keeping data discoverable and making Copilot results highly relevant.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561208","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-575283","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Apply default SharePoint library labels to data at rest","desc":"<p>Enables auto‑labeling of existing SharePoint files to match the default sensitivity label configured on their document library. This helps organizations close labeling gaps for data at rest and ensure consistent, secure‑by‑default protection across SharePoint libraries—without relying on manual user labeling.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=575283","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568072","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Dashboard - Targeted Audience Surveys","desc":"<p>Targeted Audience Surveys let change leaders launch a Copilot Pulse survey directly from the Copilot Dashboard to all licensed or active users. Audiences update automatically using Insights data and respect existing dashboard filters like organization and job function, with privacy protected through population-level reporting only. Pair adoption metrics with employee sentiment in just a few clicks.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-29","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568072","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571888","title":"Power Apps: Model-driven applications in Business Apps in Work IQ","desc":"<p>Power Apps model-driven apps are now available as Business Apps in Work IQ. They can be accessed through the Work IQ (Preview) tool in Copilot Studio or through a natural-language chat experience powered by Work IQ MCP. In either experience, natural-language prompts let users list and read records or create, update, and delete them. For create and update, Work IQ maps supplied values to the appropriate app fields. Before a change is submitted, the proposed values require explicit user confirmation.</p>","products":["Power Apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571888","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573692","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Import tasks into a project from other projects","desc":"<p>Currently, to bring tasks from another project into a new project, you must manually enter the task details in the task grid or use schedule APIs. You can also use the <strong>Copy project</strong> feature to create a new project with the same tasks, but this feature has limitations:<br> ​</p> <ul> <li>You copy the entire project, including unwanted tasks and extra information.</li> <li>You can't combine tasks from multiple projects into a new project.<br> ​<br> With this feature, you can select and import tasks from one or more existing projects into a new project, saving time and effort. You can choose the project and tasks to import while adhering to the task limits per project as specified in the public documentation.<br> ​<br> When this feature is enabled in the feature control settings, you can:<br> ​</li> <li>Select the <strong>Import Tasks</strong> button from the project ribbon.</li> <li>Use the project picker to select the source project in the side pane.</li> <li>See the grid populate with the tasks associated with that project after a project is selected.</li> <li>Choose the tasks to be imported into the target project, and then select <strong>Add</strong>.</li> <li>Know that imported tasks are automatically appended to the target project's Work Breakdown Structure (WBS).</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573692","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-574105","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Integrate the Sales Development agent with Salesforce","desc":"<p><strong>Sales Development Agent now integrates with Salesforce, enabling organizations to use SDA with their existing Salesforce CRM.</strong> SDA can access leads, manage prospect records, log sales activities, and keep engagement actions—including qualification, disqualification, and ownership changes—connected to the CRM workflow. The integration uses Microsoft’s Salesforce Model Context Protocol (MCP) server to connect SDA with Salesforce.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574105","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570443","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.155 - Tab organization enhancements","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is expanding tab and Workspace organization capabilities to suggest groupings, names, visuals, and labels. Users can manage these experiences through the proposed “Let Microsoft Edge help keep your tabs organized” setting under Privacy, search, and services &gt; Search and connected experiences; administrators can control them using the TabServicesEnabled policy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-03","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570443","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570850","title":"Work IQ: Upload","desc":"<p>Enable agents to upload files and content to supported Microsoft 365 destinations.</p>","products":["Work IQ"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-12","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570850","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561485","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot in Forms - US Government clouds","desc":"<p>Copilot in Forms is being enabled for Microsoft Forms in Government Cloud environments, bringing end-to-end AI assistance to forms, from creating a form, to refining and sending to analyzing results. This rollout includes key Copilot features such as: - Draft with Copilot - Distribution and monitoring - Copilot Insights - On-canvas Copilot features such as Rewrite question, Continue writing, Answer explanations, and more.</p>","products":["Forms","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561485","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-498640","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Capture voice notes in the Microsoft 365 Copilot mobile app","desc":"<p>With a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, transform offline discussions into structured, actionable, and searchable content with voice notes in Copilot.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-23","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498640","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568364","title":"Microsoft Viva: Rolling out Custom branding in Engage","desc":"<p>Engage is rolling out Custom Branding, a new admin-led capability that lets organizations define a customized, tenant-wide visual identity across the Engage web and mobile apps. Engage-level admins can configure a brand name, add large and small logos, and a theme color that is applied consistently for all users in the tenant. Branding is managed from the new Brand Center in the Viva Engage admin center and helps organizations reinforce their identity throughout the Engage experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-29","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-480725","title":"SharePoint: AI citations analytics for documents and pages","desc":"<p>AI citations analytics will help you track the usage of SP documents, news and pages through copilot and AI agents. You will be able to see how often a page or a file is referenced in a copilot response. You can also get insights into SharePoint site content getting referenced in copilot responses aggregated at the site level.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-14","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480725","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-547732","title":"SharePoint: New SharePoint Experience","desc":"<p>We are introducing a reimagined SharePoint experience designed to be simple and intuitive, centered on the core jobs of discovering knowledge, publishing content, and building solutions. This update establishes the foundation for AI-assisted creation across the product. This includes an updated information architecture and cohesive design language, delivering a clean and consistent experience across surfaces. Updated August 14, 2026: We are still rolling out to some gov tenants and expect to complete by mid to late September, 2026. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547732","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-485731","title":"Microsoft 365: Use Copilot in your search tab in the Microsoft 365 Copilot mobile app","desc":"<p>Quickly find your files and leverage Copilot to get a better understanding within the search tab on the go. This item is no longer accurate and is being removed from the roadmap. We apologize for the inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Cancelled","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2026-10-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485731","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-160008","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Optical character recognition (OCR) support for endpoint","desc":"<div>Optical character recognition (OCR) support will detect sensitive content in images and subsequently apply data loss prevention (DLP) policies to prevent exfiltration of that sensitive data on your Windows endpoint devices. This release supports key file types like JPG, JPEG, PNG, TIFF, BMP and PDF (image only PDF). </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-08-04","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=160008","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-573704","title":"Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Procurement Agent - Customize the Procurement Agent supplier follow-up criteria","desc":"<p>Organizations often use business-specific data and criteria to determine when suppliers require follow-up on purchase orders. The Procurement Agent will enable buyers to extend supplier follow-up criteria using related standard, extended, and custom table data. Buyers can add table joins and use fields from those tables as filter conditions, providing greater flexibility to determine which purchase order lines qualify for supplier follow-up based on their organization’s processes and data.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573704","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-574362","title":"Microsoft Teams: Pro Management portal Analytics & Reports Design Refresh","desc":"<p>We are refreshing the way we organize the Analytics &amp; Reports area in the Pro Management portal to make it more user-friendly.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574362","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-499898","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Viva Engage - Community Agent","desc":"<p>Community Agent helps members get answers to questions in Viva Engage communities using community knowledge and connected sources. Community admins can choose to require human review before answers are posted or allow automatic posting.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499898","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/viva/engage/community-agent"},{"id":"rm-570669","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Discover and use shared plugins in Copilot Studio","desc":"<p>Copilot Studio now connects to Microsoft's shared plugin registry, making it easier for makers to discover and use plugins, connectors, and other available capabilities. This integration provides a more consistent way to extend agents with capabilities across Microsoft's AI ecosystem.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570669","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-536577","title":"Microsoft Edge: Enterprise New Tab Page experience","desc":"<p>A modern experience for the New Tab Page (NTP) on Microsoft Edge for Business.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536577","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-574107","title":"Microsoft Teams: Chat for organizers and presenters in structured meetings and webinars on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>When a Teams Rooms on Android device acts as an organizer, co-organizer, or presenter in a structured meeting or webinar, you have access to the private chat for event management known as the Event Group. You can also switch to a separate chat with attendees, enabling smooth event experiences for all. Available in Teams Rooms Pro-licensed rooms.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573706","title":"Microsoft Teams: External presenter support for event group chat","desc":"<p>Event group chat, the private chat for organizers, co-organizers, and presenters in an event or structured meeting, will support external presenters.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573706","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573250","title":"Microsoft Teams: Invite attendees to register","desc":"<p>For an event that needs registration, send email invites to the selected people and groups who will be invited to register to the event</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573250","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-560541","title":"SharePoint: Governance Reviews Dashboard for Site Owners","desc":"<p>Site owners have a critical role to play in ensuring accuracy of site information, including the site's necessity, its owners, members, permissions, and sharing settings. We’re introducing the Governance Reviews Dashboard in Private Preview, a centralized view where site owners can see all pending site governance reviews (inactivity, ownership, attestation) across the sites they own.<br> The dashboard shows required actions, due timelines, and site enforcement status and allows site owners to take action directly from one place. Combined with consolidated policy notifications, it replaces multiple emails with a single, actionable governance surface.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560541","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-574119","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Improved Matrix visual performance for large table","desc":"<p>Business Performance Planning introduce Virtualization to optimizes how the Matrix visual renders large planning datasets. Rather than loading and displaying the entire dataset at once, the visual progressively renders the rows and columns needed as users scroll, expand, collapse, and navigate through the Matrix. This reduces the amount of data processed by the browser at any one time and helps maintain visual responsiveness at scale.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574119","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574365","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Import task - Public API support","desc":"<p>Public APIs for the Import tasks capability enable customers and partners to programmatically import tasks from one project into another. Organizations can call these APIs from custom applications, integrations, or automated workflows instead of requiring a user to initiate each import manually.</p> <p>The APIs support repeatable project-creation and planning scenarios, such as populating new projects with tasks from templates or previously completed projects. Customers can incorporate task imports into their existing project provisioning and automation processes.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574365","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-574364","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Choose the data sources AI-powered Data Enrichment uses, including CRM notes","desc":"<p>AI-powered Data Enrichment now lets admins choose which data sources the agent uses to enrich records. Outlook emails, Teams meetings, and the new CRM notes source each have their own control toggle, and the agent keeps running as long as at least one source is toggled on. Admins no longer need to connect every permission before they create the agent. With CRM notes, the agent extracts insights from manual notes added to supported records and uses them to enrich those records, with no tenant admin consent needed to use CRM notes. Only notes added by users with a Dynamics 365 Sales Premium license are used, and Dataverse search is needed only for emails and Teams meetings, since notes are already linked to their records.</p> <p>These control toggles are available automatically. Admins can turn each source on or off in the Agent behavior section of the Data Enrichment settings. Outlook emails and Teams meetings stay off until their permissions are connected, and connecting a permission never turns a source on by itself. For organizations already using the agent, CRM notes is off by default and a banner lets admins know it's available. For new organizations, CRM notes is on by default.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573220","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Scheduling with Copilot","desc":"<p>Users can now schedule appointments and meetings directly from chat. Simply ask Copilot to create an appointment or schedule a meeting with colleagues, and it will find available times, book rooms, draft agendas, and send invites—all within the chat experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573220","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570467","title":"Microsoft Teams: Admins can control profanity filtering in meeting transcripts","desc":"<p>Teams administrators will be able to use a meeting policy to control whether profane words are masked in live transcription and saved meeting transcripts. Filtering remains on by default. When an organizer is assigned a policy that turns filtering off, profane words can appear without masking in both the live and saved transcript, while live captions continue to follow each participant's existing profanity setting.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-02","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570467","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570439","title":"Microsoft Teams: QR code protection in Teams messaging","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams will provide additional protection for QR codes shared by external users in messages. Images containing QR codes from external senders will be obscured by default and require users to reveal them before viewing or scanning. This helps reduce the risk of phishing and fraud by encouraging more deliberate interaction with QR code content.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-03","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570439","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570442","title":"Outlook: Improved SharePoint file experience in file picker in Outlook mobile apps","desc":"<p>Users can more easily work with SharePoint files in Outlook by saving email attachments directly to SharePoint and searching across SharePoint sites for files from the file picker.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-09","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570442","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569930","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Conversational configuration of connectors in Copilot Studio","desc":"<p>Configure the connectors your agent needs, with a simple in-chat sign-in instead of a full settings experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-26","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569930","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561922","title":"Universal Print: Universal Print Portal","desc":"<p>You can release your secure print jobs by scanning a QR code at any printer and access your print workflows from a browser on any device, all signed in with your Microsoft 365 account.</p>","products":["Universal Print"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561922","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562018","title":"SharePoint: AI overview for SharePoint News posts in the SharePoint app for Teams","desc":"<p>Users will be able access an AI generated audio summary of SharePoint News posts in the SharePoint app for Teams (Viva Connections).</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562018","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-552592","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Simplifying Content in the Input Box","desc":"<p>When users insert content in a prompt using 'Add Work Content' under the Plus menu, the content will only appear as a pill in the Input Box UI and will not be repeated as part of the user's prompt. This helps to simplify the Input Box and reserve it for prompt creation. Updated April 22, 2026: We are moving this item back to In Development and will be relaunching after further updates. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-28","modified":"2026-10-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552592","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-561036","title":"Microsoft Purview: DSPM – New Microsoft Purview Data Security Posture Management Experience","desc":"<p>At Ignite, Microsoft is introducing a major evolution of Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM) to help organizations strengthen data security and confidently embrace AI. The new DSPM experience unifies visibility and control across traditional data and AI-driven environments, delivering outcome-based guided workflows that turn insights into actionable steps—so teams can prioritize risks and remediate faster. It brings AI observability, enhanced posture reporting, and intelligent Security Copilot agents to automate tasks like triage and policy management. Plus, Purview now extends coverage beyond Microsoft data with third-party signals from partners like BigID, Cyera, OneTrust, and Varonis, giving security teams a single, streamlined view of sensitive data across clouds and platforms. Together, these innovations make DSPM the central hub for managing data security posture in the era of AI. We are also extending Data Risk Assessments to Fabric and to item-level analysis with new remediation actions like bulk disabling of overshared SharePoint links.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561036","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-573252","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Cancel packing slips for stocked item requirements","desc":"<p>This feature supports controlled returns and packing slip cancellations for stocked item requirements originating in Finance and Supply Chain Management. You can open the Packing slip journal from the Item requirements page and cancel packing slips for eligible independent item requirements. Packing slip posting performs the physical inventory update while deferring the financial update, allowing cancellation before invoicing or finalization. Cancellation reverses the project cost, returns the item requirement to open order, and creates negative material usage and sales transactions through dual-write. Negative quantities remain blocked when entered directly in Dataverse.</p> <p>This feature also enables the ability to create new item requirements for both positive consumption and negative return scenarios with product dimensions such as serial number to support returns or warranty scenarios.</p> <p>The feature is off by default. To enable it, in Feature management, enable Enable packing slip cancellation for integrated deployments. It requires Enable packing slip cancellation for item requirements and Enable stocked products usage for resource/non-stock scenarios features to also be enabled.</p> <p>To see the project cost posting, be sure to enable Post packing slip in ledger in Accounts receivable parameters to create the physical inventory voucher and display project cost. Fixed-price projects also require the feature Finalize uninvoiced stocked items before inventory can be financially finalized.</p> <p>Turning off the integrated cancellation feature restores the previous posting behavior and removes cancellation availability.</p> <p>This feature applies to the Project Operations connected with ERP deployment type.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573252","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573709","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Review financial dimensions when approving expenses on mobile","desc":"<p>Approvers need access to the financial information behind an expense to make accurate approval decisions without leaving the approval experience. Dynamics 365 expense management mobile app will surface relevant financial dimensions directly within expense report approvals in the mobile app. Approvers can review financial coding in context before making a decision, helping reduce unnecessary navigation and keep expense approvals moving.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573709","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573707","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Track mileage expenses using kilometers","desc":"<p>Organizations operating across different regions need to record mileage expenses using the units of measure appropriate for their employees and local requirements. Dynamics 365 Project Operations will support kilometers (km) as a configurable unit of measure for mileage expenses, in addition to miles. Organizations can configure the appropriate mileage unit for their business, helping employees record mileage expenses accurately using the measurement standard relevant to their regional requirements.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573707","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573446","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat in OneNote can create, edit, and refine content","desc":"<p>Copilot in OneNote can generate new content and directly edit when in edit mode. In this mode you can create, rename, and delete pages, sections, or notebooks as well as add or edit content in pages. Copilot can bring content from across WorkIQ as well as complete actions across other workflows such as creating Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573446","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573453","title":"Microsoft Teams: Streaming switchboard for Network Device Interface (NDI) Sources","desc":"<p>For Teams meetings and events, a new streaming switchboard will soon be available to easily manage and send NDI sources out to production software.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573453","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-565217","title":"Microsoft Teams: Tenant-level dashboard for Interpreter","desc":"<p>We have decided not to move forward with this change at this time. We apologize for any inconvenience. Admins now have a dedicated dashboard in the Teams Admin Center to view Interpreter usage across their organization. Track adoption and usage trends in one place to better understand how Interpreter is being used.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Cancelled","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565217","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-574115","title":"Outlook: Upcoming visual improvements and a more consistent Outlook experience","desc":"<p>The first updates will focus on visual details, such as icons, spacing and alignment. Users of classic Outlook for Windows will begin seeing refinements to familiar mail and calendar surfaces. The initial visual updates are intended to improve clarity and consistency without changing how users perform their tasks.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574115","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573274","title":"Planner: Refreshed experience and new capabilities","desc":"<p>Microsoft Planner will be updated with a cleaner, more modern interface, improved navigation, responsive layouts, and a more consistent experience across Planner in Teams and Planner for the web.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573274","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-574106","title":"SharePoint: AI input widget and content preview in Copilot","desc":"<p>With this new capability, users of Copilot in SharePoint will be able to view saved and unsaved preview content side by side with chat. Users will also be able to interact with created HTML forms and confirm responses to send to chat.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=574106","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570966","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Audio Overview updates in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"<p>We're rolling out new capabilities for Copilot Notebook audio overview that make it easier to navigate longer content with topic-based episodes, new audio formats such as Critique and Debate, support enterprise information protection with sensitivity labels, and expand audio overview context to more content types.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570966","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557970","title":"Microsoft Teams: Centralized notification settings for channels","desc":"<p>Centralized notification settings streamline channel notification setup and management. Available in Teams settings, users have a single place to review and adjust notifications for all visible channels, instead of managing each individually.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557970","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573169","title":"Microsoft Viva: Expanded agent coverage in Agent Dashboard","desc":"<p>Customers can now view reporting for agents from third-party platforms in the Agent 365 Dashboard in Microsoft Viva Insights (Copilot Analytics). This expanded coverage provides a more comprehensive view of agent activity across their organization.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-08","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573169","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557170","title":"Microsoft Teams: Delete meeting generated content in recap","desc":"<p>Meeting organizers can now easily delete meeting generated content including recording, transcript, AI summary, and notes through the new delete button in recap page. Shared files in the meeting won't be deleted.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557170","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-555886","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation","desc":"<p>You can now reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555886","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-486696","title":"Outlook: Agents for Microsoft 365 Copilot available in Copilot Chat in Outlook for Mac","desc":"<p>We will be adding declarative agents support in Copilot Chat in Outlook. This roadmap item tracks availability in Outlook for Mac.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-24","modified":"2026-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486696","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-570847","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Agent value insights in Agent 365 Dashboard","desc":"<p>Customers can now view value insights in the Agent 365 Dashboard in Microsoft Viva Insights (Copilot Analytics). These insights help business leaders and change and adoption specialists understand not only whether agents are being used, but also the estimated assisted hours agents provide and the types of work contributing to that value.</p> <p>This update builds on the existing Agent 365 Dashboard adoption experience by connecting agent activity with a clearer view of the work agents support across the organization.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570847","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-515145","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Workforce Insights Agent","desc":"<p>Workforce Insights (WFI) Agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot is an agent designed to help leaders, managers, and their delegates quickly understand their organization by turning complex workforce data into clear, actionable insights. With WFI Agent, leaders can quickly explore their organization’s structure, team composition, skills inventories, and flexible work patterns to move from insight to action in a single, unified experience directly in Copilot or Teams.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515145","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-537284","title":"Microsoft Edge: Adding contextual nudges to the Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat icon","desc":"<p>Edge for Business will soon help users quickly take contextual action on their open pages using contextual nudges attached to the Copilot icon in the toolbar</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-16","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537284","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568786","title":"Microsoft Edge: Inline Switching for Workspaces","desc":"<p>Workspaces Inline Switching manages multiple Workspaces in a single window. Selecting a Workspace swaps in its tabs, theme, and context, with an easy return to the default space.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-26","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568786","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568217","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Sensitivity Labels for Microsoft Entra Security Groups","desc":"<p>Apply sensitivity labels to Microsoft Entra cloud security groups to extend the classification and governance you already use for Microsoft 365 groups. The same labels you publish in the Microsoft Purview portal and configure for groups and sites apply automatically to cloud security groups, with no separate label configuration required.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568217","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573157","title":"Microsoft Teams: Impersonation Protection for Teams meetings","desc":"<p>Impersonation Protection for Teams meetings helps users identify potentially deceptive participants and meeting organizers. When Teams detects a potential impersonation attempt, it surfaces warnings and risk indicators to help users recognize suspicious identities and make more informed decisions when joining or participating in a meeting.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573157","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573451","title":"Microsoft Teams: Third-party synthetic audio and video detection in Microsoft Teams","desc":"<p>Organizations can enhance meeting security with synthetic audio and video detection solutions provided by certified third-party providers. Third-party detection solutions analyze meeting media for signs of synthetic or manipulated audio and video and send detection signals to Teams, enabling integrated in-meeting experiences and controls. Important: Synthetic media detection is performed by the third-party provider. Microsoft Teams provides the platform integration and experiences for surfacing and acting on detection signals from supported providers.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573451","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1227622","title":"(Updated) Transitioning Teams Android Device Management from Teams admin Center to the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal","desc":"Updated October 7, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nAs part of our ongoing mission to deliver a modern, secure, and scalable one-stop management portal for admins, we are transitioning Teams Android device management from the Teams admin center (TAC) to the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal (PMP).\nThis move consolidates management of all Teams devices, including Teams Rooms on Windows, Teams Rooms on Android, Teams phones, and Teams panels, into a single unified portal, providing IT admins a consistent and seamless experience for managing devices at scale.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 555235.\n[When this will happen:]\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Effective July 2, 2026, the rollout is 100% complete across all regions in the Public cloud.\n• General Availability (GCC High): We expect to start the rollout by mid-August 2026 and complete by late-August 2026 (previously late-July).\n• General Availability (GCC and DoD): We expect to complete the rollout by mid-October 2026 (previously late-August).\n• Device management deprecation in TAC: The deprecation of Teams device management capabilities in TAC will begin in October 2026 and will roll out in phases based on device type and feature readiness.• For public cloud, we will begin the phased deprecation of SIP device management this week. The rollout will occur in stages and is expected to be fully completed by next week.\n• The current planned sequence is: SIP devices → Teams Phones → Teams Rooms on Android & Teams Panels\n• For government clouds, the deprecation rollout will follow the readiness of the respective environments. GCCH will follow the public cloud rollout, while GCC and DoD customers will have a migration period after the required convergence features become available.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\nAdmins who manage Teams Rooms on Android, Teams phones, Teams panels, and SIP Phones.\nWhat will happen:\n• By end of June 2026, Android device management capabilities, including inventory, updates, health monitoring, and settings will transition from TAC to PMP for the device types, Teams Rooms on Android, Teams phones, Teams panels and SIP Phones.\n• The following capabilities will be available and enhanced in PMP:• Device inventories for Android-based Teams Rooms, phones, and panels, including metadata and app information\n• Remote device actions (restart, log collection, sign-in/out, provisioning, and more)\n• Update management\n• Device settings management\n• Device health monitoring\n• SIP device management\n\n• PMP will become the primary portal for all Teams device management. By November 2026, overlapping TAC capabilities (updates, settings, restart, sign-in/out, log collection, provisioning) will be deprecated in TAC.\n• The article below serves as the main information source for this transition. It has been updated with the latest timelines, milestones, migration guidance, and readiness steps. We will keep updating it as the rollout progresses.• Transitioning Teams Android Device Management from Teams Admin Center to the Teams Rooms Pro Management Portal - Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\n• Monitor the below article for any feature specific updates and timelines. This article also provides migration guidance and pre-requisites for successful transition to PMP.• Transitioning Teams Android Device Management from Teams Admin Center to the Teams Rooms Pro Management Portal - Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n\n• Learn more about Pro Management portal features with these Teams Rooms Pro Management short YouTube videos.\n• Update internal helpdesk and IT documentation to reference PMP as the new management portal.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft 365 for the web"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1227622","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-492622","title":"Microsoft 365: The Next Generation of File & Folder Sharing","desc":"<p>We're now introducing the third generation of the Microsoft 365 sharing experience designed to make collaboration simpler, smarter, and more secure by default. At the heart of this update is the new hero link, a single, powerful link that controls access to your files. Whether you copy a link, share via email, or send the URL from your browser, you now have a seamless and consistent way to share and stay in control of your files.</p>","products":["Excel","Microsoft 365","OneDrive","PowerPoint","SharePoint","Word"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-08","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492622","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-502541","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Improved discovery of Copilot connector sources in Microsoft 365 Copilot (optionally add chat) with Content Source filter(s)","desc":"<p>Improved discovery of Copilot connector sources in Microsoft 365 Copilot (optionally add chat) with Content Source filter(s).</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-22","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502541","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-489825","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Overview of recent comments and changes in Word","desc":"<p>Use Copilot to see a summary of the latest comments and changes made to your Word files using the Copilot chat pane.</p>","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489825","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568793","title":"Microsoft Edge: Updated horizontal tab appearance","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is introducing an updated horizontal tab-strip appearance on Windows and macOS. The treatment uses rounded tabs with revised spacing and aligns related tab-strip controls with the refreshed browser-frame design. Tab behavior and enterprise data handling remain unchanged. Note: We have made the decision to cancel this planned release. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Cancelled","created":"2026-08-10","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568793","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566699","title":"Microsoft Viva: Discussion Post Previews","desc":"<p>Discussion post previews allow users to review how their discussion posts will appear before publishing, helping them catch formatting issues, validate content, and post with greater confidence.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-26","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566699","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568074","title":"SharePoint: Cross-post SharePoint News to Engage","desc":"<p>This feature allows SharePoint News authors to distribute posts to an Engage community or storyline while preserving full fidelity rendering and a unified conversation experience. SharePoint News post will appear consistently in Engage across feeds, digests, Outlook, Teams, desktop, web and mobile apps. When distributed, the SharePoint News comments module is replaced with the richer Engage conversation module, ensuring a single, shared discussion thread across surfaces.</p>","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-22","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568074","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566321","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Export DLP and Label Policy Configurations","desc":"<p>A new export functionality will be introduced in two locations: the Data Loss Prevention &gt; Policies page and the Information Protection &gt; Label publishing policies page. This feature will allow users to export their existing DLP configurations and label policies, including schema, as a downloadable ZIP file. The exported file can be attached to support tickets to accelerate troubleshooting.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566321","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-560338","title":"Excel: Plan Mode for Copilot in Excel","desc":"<p>Plan Mode for Copilot in Excel helps users make complex changes with confidence by outlining a clear, step by step approach before anything in the workbook is updated. Users can review how Copilot intends to complete the task, see which data or capabilities may be used, and adjust the plan as needed—ensuring edits are intentional, transparent, and aligned with their goals before they’re applied. This makes it easier to tackle multi step or high impact tasks while staying in control of every change.</p>","products":["Excel"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560338","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-160010","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Optical character recognition (OCR) support for SharePoint Online and OneDrive for Business","desc":"<p>Optical character recognition (OCR) support will detect sensitive content in images and subsequently apply data loss prevention (DLP) policies to prevent exfiltration of that sensitive data in SharePoint Online and OneDrive. This release supports key file types like JPG, JPEG, PNG, TIFF, BMP, and PDF (image-only PDF).</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-08-16","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=160010","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704},{"id":"rm-571397","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-Upgraded inline protection for Microsoft Entra-managed apps in Edge for Business","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview is upgrading inline data protection for Microsoft Entra-managed apps in Edge for Business. The experience integrates with a Microsoft Entra Conditional Access grant control and simplifies configuration while removing current Purview policy restrictions. Admins can now use expanded conditions and condition combinations, multiple activities per rule, simulation mode, configurable alerts and notifications, and rule match activities are visible in activity explorer.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571397","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703,"preview":"February CY2027"},{"id":"rm-567311","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Collection and DLP Policies for Intune-Policy Managed Apps","desc":"<p>We are introducing a new integrated Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) capability for Intune Mobile Application Management (MAM)-protected mobile apps, enabling organizations to apply content‑aware protection policies to sensitive data on mobile devices. This integration ensures that clipboard actions in managed mobile apps are evaluated against Purview DLP policies before sharing is allowed, helping reduce data leakage, insider risk, and exposure to advanced threats across mobile workflows. Additionally, Microsoft Purview Collection policies can be used to govern how sensitive data is being handled in mobile apps.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567311","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-571301","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Quality evaluation supports custom Case-like records evaluation","desc":"<p>Quality evaluation now supports on-demand evaluations for case-like custom entities in public preview. Organizations can extend evaluation capabilities beyond the standard case entity to supported custom Dataverse entities that follow a case-like service workflow. This enables teams to evaluate additional business records using the quality evaluation framework, while giving admins flexibility to configure evaluation entry points for their custom scenarios.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571301","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573242","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Improve mobile offline reliability across network conditions","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Field service work often happens in environments where network quality changes throughout the day. Technicians may move between connected, low-connectivity, intermittent, and offline conditions while still needing the mobile app to remain dependable.</p> <p>Mobile offline is being improved to better detect and respond to changing network conditions. More adaptive sync behavior can help reduce disruptions, avoid unnecessary retries, and improve reliability when users move across different connectivity states.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>This update improves how mobile offline detects and responds to weak, intermittent, or limited connectivity. Sync behavior will become more adaptive so the app can better determine when to sync, when to pause, and when to reduce unnecessary work.</p> <p>The capability is intended to help Field Service Mobile provide a more dependable offline experience in real-world field environments. It focuses on sync behavior and connectivity response, while administrators and makers remain responsible for designing offline profiles that match field usage, data volume, and business requirements.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573242","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-570856","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Capture project expenses directly from Field Service Work Orders","desc":"<p>Technicians can create, update, and submit project-related expenses directly from a Work Order in Field Service web and mobile when the Field Service and Project Operations integration is enabled. Expenses remain connected to the related project and follow the standard Project Operations approval process, helping teams capture field costs with less context switching and better financial traceability.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573241","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Enhance mobile offline up-sync","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Technicians often complete work in the field while connectivity is limited or intermittent. When offline changes still need to sync, users and back-office teams can be uncertain whether work details, status updates, and other field changes have reached business systems.</p> <p>Mobile offline up-sync is being enhanced so changes captured in the field can continue syncing more reliably. This helps frontline users gain confidence that completed work will be submitted without repeatedly checking the app or following up manually.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>This update improves mobile offline up-sync for changes created while technicians work in Field Service Mobile. It includes support for background up-sync and user notifications when pending changes still need to sync.</p> <p>When changes remain pending, the mobile experience can help users understand that additional sync work is still required. The capability is intended to reduce uncertainty around offline changes and help field updates reach Dataverse more reliably as connectivity becomes available.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573241","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573240","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Modernize the mobile offline foundation","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Field service organizations often depend on mobile offline so technicians can keep working when connectivity is limited or unavailable. As offline profiles grow larger and apps include more related data, first sync, resource loading, and repeated sync work can affect technician productivity and confidence in the mobile experience.</p> <p>Power Apps mobile offline is being updated with a more native foundation for data access and sync orchestration. This foundation is intended to improve responsiveness, reduce repeated sync work, and better support complex Field Service Mobile apps that use larger offline profiles and richer related data.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>This update modernizes the mobile offline foundation used by Power Apps mobile and Field Service Mobile. It includes native sync processing, improved handling of related rows during first sync, and optimizations for app resource and custom file loading.</p> <p>The updated foundation is designed to strengthen offline data access and sync orchestration while preserving the mobile offline app experience customers already use. Administrators and makers should continue to review offline profile design, table relationships, data volume, and file usage to align mobile offline configuration with field usage patterns.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573240","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-562352","title":"Microsoft 365: Pay-as-you-go storage for OneDrive","desc":"<p>New pay-as-you-go, consumption-based meter for additional OneDrive storage. Control which OneDrive accounts can grow beyond their licensed storage limits and give selected users more space as needed.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-26","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562352","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573702","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Increase in expansion limit for auto-expanding archive beyond 1.5 TB","desc":"<p>Previously, auto-expanding archive mailbox expansion was supported only up to 1.5 TB, after which mailboxes would become inoperative. Archive mailboxes can now automatically expand beyond the 1.5 TB limit, ensuring uninterrupted retention and enabling scalable archive growth as storage thresholds are reached. This capability to expand archives beyond 1.5 TB will be available to customers with eligible E5 licenses.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573702","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573292","title":"Power Automate: Build and visualize desktop flows using Flowchart mode","desc":"<p>Flowchart mode introduces a new visual authoring experience in Power Automate for desktop that allows makers to create, view, and edit desktop flows using a flowchart representation. Actions are displayed as connected nodes and execution paths are represented visually, making it easier to understand, build, and maintain complex automations that include conditions, loops, and branching logic. Makers can create new flows directly in Flowchart mode or switch existing flows between Sequence mode and Flowchart mode.</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573292","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-545896","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Structured Document Generation with Forms","desc":"<p>Structured Document Generation with Forms enables organizations to create, manage, and generate standardized documents at scale with built-in governance and compliance in SharePoint. Business process owners can centrally build and maintain form-driven templates -- such as contracts, agreements, proposals, and HR documents -- ensuring content stays accurate and up to date. Users can then generate the right document every time by just filling out the form, without manual formatting, versioning issues, or compliance risk, simplifying high-volume, structured document workflows across the organization.</p>","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-01-09","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545896","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-567890","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Auto-labeling scale increase for SharePoint and OneDrive","desc":"<p>We are increasing the maximum auto-labeling capacity for SharePoint and OneDrive from 100,000 up to 500,000 files per tenant per day. This helps organizations label and protect more of their data at rest, faster, closing labeling gaps across existing content. With sensitivity labels and protection settings applied to more files sooner, organizations can better prepare their data estate for Microsoft 365 Copilot with greater confidence.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-17","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567890","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564619","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Enhanced user profile in IRM alerts","desc":"<p>We’re enhancing the User section within Insider Risk Management alerts to provide investigators with more contextual user profile and risk attributes directly within their workflow. With this update, analysts can now view key user details such as employee type, office location, start date, policy inclusion, priority user group status, and last working day—helping them build a more complete understanding of the user during investigations without navigating away from the alert experience. This feature will be available as part of the new alert workflow through the Alert Details panel. Additional user attributes will continue to be introduced over time, with pseudo‑anonymization honored to support privacy‑by‑design investigation practices. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564619","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564620","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Expanding note capabilities across alerts & cases","desc":"<p>We’re introducing a new collaboration capability in Insider Risk Management that enables analysts and investigators to add notes directly within alerts. With this feature, users can document investigation progress, share findings, and capture key context throughout the triage process. In addition to manually added notes, system‑generated notes will automatically record updates such as alert status changes or user assignments — helping teams maintain a clear and auditable investigation timeline. By centralizing investigation history directly within alerts, this update helps improve collaboration and ensures all stakeholders stay aligned throughout the investigation lifecycle. These note enhancements will also be made available in Cases. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564620","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573447","title":"Microsoft Purview: Permissions audit log improvements","desc":"<p>Improving permission checks when users access the Microsoft Purview portal. Enhanced audit logs will provide clearer visibility into role and scoped-role access decisions, helping administrators troubleshoot access issues and monitor authorization outcomes.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573447","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-565132","title":"Microsoft Teams: Granular channel notification controls","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams introduces flexible presets for channel notifications, allowing you to choose between All new messages, @mentions and replies, or Mute. You can further customize alerts for unfollowed threads, tags, and channel or team mentions, as well as control banner notifications for the channel. This added flexibility enables you to set notifications to match to your work style and reduce unnecessary distractions.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565132","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-563807","title":"Outlook: Choose to Show Unread or Total Count for Each Folder","desc":"<p>You can now pick whether each folder in your folder pane shows the unread count or the total item count. Until now, Outlook only displayed unread counts, but sometimes you need to see how many items are in a folder overall. Just right-click any folder and choose whether to show the total or unread count. It gives you more control over how you keep track of your email without changing how anything else works. #newoutlookforwindows</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-21","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=563807","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570664","title":"Outlook: Right-click to customize the classic ribbon","desc":"<p>You can now customize the classic ribbon in New Outlook for Windows and Outlook on the Web by right-clicking the ribbon and choosing which commands and groups appear on the Home and View tabs. #newoutlookforwindows</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-11","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570664","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-508524","title":"Outlook: User-initiated Copilot insights in classic Outlook","desc":"<p>Users can manually select text and ask Copilot to help provide relevant information.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508524","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567886","title":"Planner: AI-generated Status Reports in Planner Agent","desc":"<p>AI-powered Status Report in Planner Agent turns your plan data into a polished, stakeholder-ready update in minutes. Just ask Planner Agent for a status report and it pulls your task data and transforms it into a clear narrative covering overall status, progress, risks, and what's next. You can easily customize the report to your needs by specifying the audience, tone, length, and sections you want.</p>","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567886","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573278","title":"Power Automate: Schedule desktop flows directly with Scheduled Triggers","desc":"<p>Scheduled triggers enable makers to run desktop flows on a recurring schedule directly from the Power Automate automation center, eliminating the need to create and manage intermediary scheduled cloud flows. Users can configure daily, weekly, monthly, hourly, or custom recurrence patterns, select the execution machine or machine group, and monitor upcoming scheduled runs from a centralized experience. Scheduled Triggers simplify desktop automation management and provide a more intuitive scheduling experience for attended and unattended desktop flows.</p>","products":["Power Automate"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-06","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573278","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566318","title":"Microsoft 365 app: New Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot App (iOS)","desc":"<p>Copilot Notebooks in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app (iOS) now lets users organize related chats, output creations, and references into a persistent AI workspace. Copilot uses the Notebook's accumulated context to ground responses, so work continues across sessions instead of starting over each time.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566318","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-560539","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Dataverse data connected to Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"<p>Let people search and query Dataverse business data from Microsoft 365 Copilot.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560539","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569019","title":"Microsoft Teams: Identify custom apps that need updates for Teams private and shared channels","desc":"<p>Admins will be able to view in Teams Admin Center a list of custom apps in their tenant that need to be updated to work in private and shared channels. This experience will help admins identify impacted apps, understand which apps require developer action, and coordinate updates so users can continue using custom apps across all supported channel types.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569019","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567300","title":"Microsoft Teams: Prevent presence transition to \"Do not disturb\" setting when screen sharing (GCC High, DoD)","desc":"<p>We're introducing a setting that allows users to opt-out of transitioning presence automatically to Do Not Disturb when presenting or screen sharing. This ensures that they can continue to receive calls, keeping them connected and responsive without manual presence adjustments.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567300","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-564613","title":"Microsoft Teams: New layout when sharing content for Teams events","desc":"<p>Organizers and presenters who have access to production tools will see updated layout options when sharing content in the \"Manage what attendees see\" experience for Teams events. The available layouts are \"Speaker focused\", \"Content focused\", and \"Content only\". The new Speaker focused layout prioritizes presenter video alongside shared content for greater visibility. This feature is available for Teams events organizers with a Teams Enterprise license. This feature is available on Teams for Windows desktop and Mac desktop.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-02","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564613","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561320","title":"Microsoft Purview: Use sensitivity labels to block all connected experiences that analyze content in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint","desc":"<p>In Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, the ‘Prevent some connected experiences that analyze content’ label setting now prevents files in these apps from being sent to all Microsoft connected experiences for analysis, rather than a subset of these connected experiences.</p>","products":["Excel","PowerPoint","Word","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561320","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558689","title":"Outlook: Data Loss Prevention (DLP) Policy Tips & Override in Outlook for Mac","desc":"<p>Outlook for Mac now supports Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policy tips, helping users avoid accidental data leaks. When sensitive content is detected, users are alerted with inline tips or pop-ups, based on admin-configured rules.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-07","modified":"2026-10-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558689","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-493752","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Cloud Attachments preservation for users on hold","desc":"<p>Enables cloud attachment preservation for users put on infinite hold so that file versions shared are preserved across any OneDrive or SharePoint site. This is a new capability which is different from the existing capability of applying label to cloud attachments and links present in OneDrive and SharePoint and shared in Exchange, Teams, Viva Engage and Copilot</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-27","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493752","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2027","gaSort":202705,"preview":"March CY2027"},{"id":"rm-506749","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Agent Dashboard.","desc":"<p>Viva Insights is creating an Agent Dashboard, designed to be a central place for leaders, delegates and analysts to understand how your organization is adopting agents. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506749","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-503771","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users in GCC-H will be able to use custom engine agents","desc":"<p>Users in GCC-H will be able to use custom engine agents.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503771","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-561490","title":"Microsoft Teams: Connect Teams meeting to existing Planner Plans","desc":"<p>Teams meetings automatically create a corresponding Planner plan to capture meeting tasks. However, when teams use meetings as their primary collaboration surface for long-running initiatives, tasks from the same project can become scattered across multiple auto-generated plans. With this capability, users can now connect Teams meetings to existing Planner plans, so all related tasks across meetings can be tracked in one place.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561490","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573697","title":"OneDrive: Presentation mode for PDFs in the iOS app on iPad","desc":"<p>Microsoft OneDrive is introducing presentation mode in the OneDrive iOS app for users on iPad devices. Users select a new Presentation button in the PDF viewer to enter a focused, view-only experience that prevents free gesture scrolling between pages, reducing accidental page changes while presenting without moving the file to another app. The feature is not available on iPhone.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-05","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573697","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-573699","title":"SharePoint: Advanced Management - Inactive files policy","desc":"<p>SharePoint administrators can use the Inactive files policy in SharePoint Advanced Management to automatically archive files based on when they were last accessed. The public preview is available through PowerShell only. Admins can set an inactivity threshold from 6 to 48 months, scope policies to all SharePoint sites or selected sites, include or exclude file types and sites, and use What-If mode to review impact before activation. Eligible files move to the Microsoft 365 Archive cold-storage tier while remaining in place and retaining their metadata, permissions, compliance, and searchability. Microsoft 365 Archive and pay-as-you-go billing must be enabled.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-05","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573699","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.online.sharepoint.powershell/new-spofilearchivepolicy?view=sharepoint-ps#-lastaccessdatecriteria"},{"id":"rm-489232","title":"Microsoft Edge: Adding support for viewing Sensitivity labels applied to a Microsoft Information Protection (MIP) Protected PDF","desc":"<p>Enterprise customers can view sensitivity labels applied to MIP protected PDF to be well informed of the data classification to enable them to handle such sensitive documents. This change will be available in the new PDF viewer on Microsoft Edge.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489232","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-516043","title":"Microsoft Edge: PDF Viewer Performance Improvement and Minor Visual Updates","desc":"<p>The PDF Viewer in Microsoft Edge is enhancing responsiveness and introducing a series of subtle visual upgrades aimed at improving overall usability and utility. This migration ensures UI coherence with the rest of the browser while maintaining the same user experience.<br> The update focuses on improving underlying performance, consistency in design elements, and a smoother interaction without altering any existing workflows for users.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516043","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571687","title":"Microsoft Teams: Add alternate text to images shared from OneDrive and SharePoint","desc":"<p>Improve accessibility by adding alternate text to images shared in Teams from OneDrive and SharePoint, helping users better understand visual content</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571687","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-565216","title":"Microsoft Teams: Intelligent call delegation","desc":"<p>Incoming Teams calls don't wait for a break in your day. Intelligent call delegation provides AI-powered calling assistance so you can focus on the conversations that matter most. It answers calls and gathers context, helping you decide whether to pick up and engage the caller. It can also schedule follow-up appointments through an integration with Microsoft Bookings so you can reconnect with callers at a more convenient time.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565216","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573267","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Quality evaluation - Recurring conversation evaluations","desc":"<p>Quality Evaluation now supports recurring frequency for conversation evaluations. Previously, only event-based trigger evaluations were supported, meaning evaluations were created only when a conversation closed.<br> With recurring evaluations, users can run bulk evaluations over previously closed conversations, evaluate future closed conversations, and sample selected conversations that match configured conditions. This enables ongoing quality monitoring, retrospective analysis, and targeted evaluation programs without relying solely on conversation-close events.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-05","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573267","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-565868","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Protect sensitive data over FTP and SFTP with Endpoint DLP","desc":"<p>Endpoint DLP support for FTP and SFTP enables organizations to monitor and protect sensitive data transferred from managed endpoints using FTP and SFTP, helping prevent unauthorized data exfiltration while maintaining visibility and control.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565868","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559105","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Apply default SharePoint library labels to data at rest","desc":"<p>Enables auto‑labeling of existing SharePoint files to match the default sensitivity label configured on their document library. This helps organizations close labeling gaps for data at rest and ensure consistent, secure‑by‑default protection across SharePoint libraries—without relying on manual user labeling.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559105","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573275","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Add multiple items to a transaction using bulk entry","desc":"<p>Associates can trigger the <strong>Bulk add</strong> operation from the button grid on the transaction screen in Store Commerce. A drawer-based dialog opens where associates can paste or enter multiple item number and quantity pairs, with one pair specified per line.</p> <ul> <li>Supported formats include SKU x quantity, quantity x SKU, SKU quantity, quantity SKU, or SKU only (which defaults the quantity to 1).</li> <li>Multiple item number and quantity pairs can also be entered on a single line and separated by spaces or commas.</li> <li>Supported delimiters between item numbers and quantities include x, spaces, commas, and tab characters for Microsoft Excel paste scenarios. Input can also follow a CSV structure.</li> </ul> <p>Select <strong>Add to sale</strong> to process all items in a single operation.</p> <p>The system parses the input, resolves each item, and adds the items to the transaction. If an item requires variant selection, such as size or color, the variant selection dialog is displayed inline.</p> <h2>Feedback and error handling</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Success</strong>: The dialog closes and a confirmation message indicates that all items were added successfully.</li> <li><strong>Partial success</strong>: A warning message shows the number of items that were added and the number that failed. Failed items remain in the dialog so they can be corrected and resubmitted.</li> <li><strong>Failure</strong>: An error message is displayed. The dialog remains open and includes a collapsible error list that identifies the items that failed and the reason for each failure.</li> <li>Duplicate item numbers aren't merged and remain as separate transaction lines.</li> </ul> <h2>Entry point</h2> <p>The operation is accessed through the button grid, allowing merchants to add it to any button grid layout by using the existing screen layout designer.</p> <h2>Configuration</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Application</strong>: Store Commerce (Point of Sale)</li> <li><strong>Enabled by</strong>: Adding the <strong>Bulk add</strong> operation to a button grid through the screen layout designer in Commerce headquarters.</li> <li><strong>Setup</strong>: A store administrator or IT administrator configures a button grid layout to include the <strong>Bulk add</strong> operation. After the configuration is published, associates can access the operation from the transaction screen.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-10-05","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573275","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564913","title":"Outlook: New Outlook for Windows for GCC-H and DoD","desc":"<p>The new Microsoft Outlook for Windows will be available for US Government clouds (GCC-H and DoD sovereign environments).</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-04","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564913","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555852","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Branded footer in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app","desc":"<p>This update introduces a co-branding experience in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app that helps organizations present an admin approved visual identifier directly within the Chat screen. Specifically, the experience enables administrators to leverage the organization-supported logo already managed in the Microsoft Admin Center theming settings and display it in the footer of the Chat screen, paired with a fixed label: “Approved by”.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-24","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566323","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - File Testing Against Sensitive Information Classifiers","desc":"<p>A new feature will be introduced on the main Classification page, allowing users to test files against all available classifiers to identify the presence of sensitive information. Users will have the option to select a single classifier or run tests across all classifiers. This capability is designed to help users identify sensitive content within files and troubleshoot classification issues more efficiently.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-548648","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ad-hoc room reservation from Teams Rooms on Windows console","desc":"<p>With Teams Rooms on Windows consoles, you can quickly book a meeting room for immediate use, helping to avoid scheduling conflicts and ensure uninterrupted spontaneous meetings. Available in Teams Rooms Pro-licensed rooms.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-22","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548648","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-564970","title":"Outlook: Improved PDF Preview on iOS","desc":"<p>MIP-label protected PDFs are now supported in the PDF previewer along with a built-in control's toolbar for easier navigation.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-02","modified":"2026-10-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564970","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-571675","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Automate optimizations with Scheduling Operations Agent","desc":"<p>This release expands the optimization capabilities of the Scheduling Operations Agent to include the ability to create recurring optimizations on a schedule. The agent considers the availability of the resources, their current schedules, and unscheduled requirements. It suggests a schedule that honors configured constraints and optimizes it according to the selected goal. The agent automatically runs optimizations and applies the results on the configured schedule.</p> <p>New capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Configure optimization plans to run on a recurrence schedule.</li> <li>Add and weight additional objectives to optimization goals.</li> </ul> <p>These capabilities build on the existing public preview of the Scheduling Operations Agent and are automatically enabled for all organizations that have the agent enabled. Learn more at <a href=\"https://aka.ms/soa\">Scheduling Operations Agent overview</a>.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571675","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/field-service/soa-overview"},{"id":"rm-561040","title":"Microsoft Edge: Commercial Journeys - AI-powered task completion for Microsoft 365 Copilot users","desc":"<p>Commercial Journeys helps information workers stay on top of their most important work when browsing in Microsoft Edge. Powered by AI, it proactively surfaces unfinished, new, and recurring tasks on the Copilot new tab page- with context-rich cards that explain why each task matters now. One click opens a guided execution flow that delivers ready-to-use outputs (emails, documents, presentations, and more), so users can complete their unfinished work faster with higher quality. This feature will be available to users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot Premium license in Edge.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561040","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573276","title":"Dynamics 365 Commerce: Add items to a transaction from the numpad","desc":"<h2>How it works</h2> <p>​<br> Quick add reuses the existing numpad on the transaction screen, so there is no new input control to learn and no additional space consumed in the transaction grid.<br> ​</p> <ol> <li>The associate enters a full or partial item number on the numpad.</li> <li>On an exact match, the item is added directly to the transaction.</li> <li>On a partial match, instead of navigating to the search results page, an inline dialog opens on the transaction screen listing the matching products.</li> <li>The associate adds an item directly from that inline list using Add to sale.<br> ​<br> If a selected product requires variant selection such as size or color, the variant selection dialog is invoked inline before the item is added. Quick add is optimized for fast, SKU-based matching and is intentionally distinct from global search, which remains the tool for exploration and rich product discovery.<br> ​</li> </ol> <h2>Inline result experience</h2> <p>​</p> <ul> <li>Partial matches are shown as a list on the transaction screen, each row offering an Add to sale action.</li> <li>Results do not navigate to the product page by default, keeping the associate in context.</li> </ul> <p>​</p> <h2>Platform behavior</h2> <p>​</p> <ul> <li>Desktop and mobile behave consistently: exact matches add directly, partial matches show inline results.</li> <li>On mobile, the full-screen numpad follows the same logic.<br> ​</li> </ul> <h2>Entry point</h2> <p>​<br> Quick add is triggered from the existing numpad on the transaction screen. There is no separate text input field, avoiding redundancy with global search and preserving screen space.<br> ​</p> <h2>Enabling the feature</h2> <p>​</p> <ul> <li>Application: Store Commerce (Point of Sale).</li> <li>Quick add builds on the numpad entry experience already present on the transaction screen.<br> ​</li> </ul> <h2>Dependencies</h2> <p>​</p> <ul> <li>Reuses the inline variant selector common control, shared with the Bulk add experience.</li> <li>Quick add and Bulk add are companion features; Bulk add covers pasting a full list of items, while Quick add covers fast single-item entry from the numpad.<br> ​</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Commerce"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573276","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571394","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Dataverse Business Skills in Sales Agent","desc":"<p>Business Skills are natural language instructions authored and stored in Microsoft Dataverse that teach Sales Agent how work gets done within a specific organization. Business Skills enable organizations to create natural language instructions for Sales Agent to follow, which represent their business processes, policies, and business knowledge. Business skills can represent common sales workflows such as lead qualification, pipeline reviews, account planning, opportunity scoring, account brief creation, or organization-specific sales methodologies. Sales Agent uses the instructions in Business Skills to deliver responses that align with the customer's business processes and guidance.</p> <p>Sellers can interact with Sales agent using natural language and receive responses that are guided by their organization's Business Skills, following admin defined sales processes, applying company specific guidance, and surface insights that reflect how the organization operations.</p> <p>Administrators enable the required Dataverse capabilities, create and manage Business skills within Dataverse, and control Business skill access. Business skills can be authored using natural language instructions and associated with the organization's CRM environment.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571394","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573452","title":"Microsoft Teams: Onboarding workflow for new team members","desc":"<p>Help people get started faster by automatically connecting new team members to relevant channels when they join a team. Improve engagement, accelerate onboarding, and make it easier to discover important information from day one.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573452","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573156","title":"Microsoft Teams: Start side conversations during meetings","desc":"<p>Keep collaboration moving without disrupting the main discussion. Start and continue one-to-one or small-group conversations directly from a meeting to ask questions, coordinate next steps, share information, and collaborate in parallel while staying engaged in the conversation, reducing context switching and helping teams stay focused and productive.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-01","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573156","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573280","title":"Outlook: Draft, edit and format emails conversationally with Copilot in Outlook","desc":"<p>In Outlook, Copilot now works side by side with users to draft, refine, and format emails conversationally, powered by the same agentic capabilities available in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573280","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1279093","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Enhancing how we handle promotional mail","desc":"Updated October 2, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are enhancing how Microsoft Defender for Office 365 identifies and manages promotional email. Promotional messages will be tagged as “promotions” (previously “Bulk” in preview) and can be moved automatically to a new Promotions folder. The system learns from user actions, such as moving messages into or out of the Promotions folder and applies those preferences to future messages. These improvements reduce inbox clutter and help users stay focused while still receiving promotional content they want.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview (Limited): We will begin rolling out in mid-April 2026 and expect to complete by mid-May 2026 (previously end of April). To be included in the public preview program, send an email to BulkMailPreviews@microsoft.com indicating: Organization name, Tenant ID and your onmicrosoft.com domain (e.g contoso.onmicrosoft.com). Slots are limited and will close on May 15th, 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in late July 2026 (previously early July) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late August).\n• General Availability (DoD, GCC, GCC High): We will begin rolling out in late July 2026 (previously early July) and expect to complete by late November 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All organizations that use Microsoft Defender for Office 365 across Worldwide, GCC, GCC High, and DoD clouds\n\nWhat will happen\n• Incoming promotional messages will be tagged as “promotions.” (previously “Bulk” in private and public preview)\n• If the Bulk Moves Enabled setting is turned on, tagged messages will automatically move to a Promotions folder created in user mailboxes.\n• The system will learn from user actions when they move messages into or out of the Promotions folder. Future messages will follow the learned behavior.\n• Users will be able to create inbox rules that reference the promotions tag.• During the Public Preview: Tagging will be opt-in and configured using Exchange transport rules.\n• Folder routing will be enabled through anti-spam policy settings (“Bulk moves enabled”).\n• Both features will be able to be scoped to pilot security groups for a staged rollout.\n\n• At Worldwide General Availability, tagging will be enabled by default for all tenants and will always remain that way.\n• For the tagging experience, supported outlooks clients are Outlook on the web and outlook for Windows. Other client such as Outlook for IOS/Android and classic outlook will follow subsequently\n• For the promotions folder experiences, Outlook on the web, outlook for Windows, Outlook for IOS/Android and classic outlook are all supported.\n\nFigure one - Admin configuration for tagging using exchange transport rule (required for public preview opt-In):\n\nFigure two - Admin configuration for Bulk moves enabled to provision the promotions folder:\n\nFigure three - System tagging of “Promotions” in outlook client and promotions folder (previously tagged as “Bulk” in private and public preview):\n\nFigure four - User inbox rules using the promotions” tag:\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• To be included in the public preview program, send an email to BulkMailPreviews@microsoft.com indicating: Organization name, Tenant ID and your onmicrosoft.com domain (e.g contoso.onmicrosoft.com). Slots are limited and will close on April 30th, 2026.\n• Review your internal mailbox and message handling guidance and update training materials if needed.\n• If you plan to participate in the Public Preview, review your Exchange transport rule and anti-spam policy configurations to determine if you want to opt-in.\n• Monitor the product documentation. You can review the following: Bulk email detection and bulk complaint level (BCL) in cloud organizations\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. Incoming email will receive the promotions classification and may be moved automatically to the Promotions folder depending on admin configuration.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI or ML that interacts with customer data?Yes. The system learns from user actions when they move messages and applies that learning to future similar messages.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Yes. Admins can enable or disable Bulk Moves Enabled and can opt in to tagging during Public Preview. These controls can be scoped using existing admin delegation models.\nDoes the change allow a user to enable or disable the feature themselves?Yes. Users can override tagging behavior by moving messages in or out of the Promotions folder, which trains the ML model and adjusts future message handling.","products":["Microsoft Defender XDR"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1279093","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1166852","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Viva Copilot Analytics launches new agent dashboard","desc":"Updated October 2, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing the Agent Dashboard, a new dashboard available as part of Copilot Analytics in Microsoft Viva. This dashboard provides visibility into key agent adoption trends and associated Copilot credit usage. It supports insights into agents used within Microsoft 365 Copilot, which may be:\n• Built using Microsoft Copilot Studio, SharePoint, or the Microsoft 365 Agents Toolkit\n• Built by employees, your organization, Microsoft, or Microsoft partners\n\nThis release also enhances the Adoption tab of the Copilot Dashboard, allowing users to view agent insights directly and access the Agent Dashboard for deeper analysis.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Public Preview (Worldwide): Begins rolling out in early February 2026 (previously January), expected to complete by mid-February 2026 (previously end of January).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Begins rolling out in February 2026 (previously late October), expected to complete February 2026 (previously early November).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n• Leaders, delegates, adoption specialists, and administrators using Microsoft Viva Insights\n• Tenants with at least 50 Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses assigned\n\nWhat will happen:\n• A new Agent Dashboard will be available in Viva Insights under Copilot Analytics\n• Users will find:• Key adoption metrics with historical trends (up to 6 months):• Number of active agents\n• Number of active agent users\n• Number of agent responses\n• Copilot credits used\n• Number of users using Copilot credits\n• Percentage of Copilot users using agents\n\n• Screenshot 1: Key adoption metrics with historical trends, including active agents, active users, agent responses, and Copilot credit usage.\n•\n• Monthly and weekly user retention trends, with comparison across groups\n\n• Screenshot 2: Monthly and weekly user retention trends, with comparison across groups.• Top agents based on the following, with the ability to dive deeper into specific agents:• Active user count\n• Agent responses\n• Copilot credits consumed\n\n• Screenshot 3: Agent highlights along with a table of top agents, each with active usage metrics and the ability to dive deeper.\n•\n•\n• Screenshot 4: Individual agent deep dive page with key adoption metrics and trends over time.\n•\n\n• Minimum group size threshold must be met for agent activity insights.\n• Learn more: Configure manager settings\n• The Adoption tab of the Copilot Dashboard will also include:• Contextual insights on how Copilot users are leveraging agents and credits\n• Direct entry points to the Agent Dashboard\n\n• Screenshot 5: Entry points to the Agent Dashboard from the Copilot Dashboard Adoption tab, including agent usage and Copilot credit usage insights.\n•\n• [What you can do to prepare:]• Review and assess the impact for your organization\n• Manage access to the Agent Dashboard using VFAM controls at user, group, and tenant levels (nested under Viva Insights Web app VFAM controls)\n• Consider reviewing with your works council\n• Update training and documentation as needed\n• Additional details will be available on MS Learn once this functionality is released, in a separate Agent Dashboard section: Copilot Analytics introduction\n\n•\n• [Compliance considerations:]\n• No compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.\n•\n•","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1166852","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571400","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Chat: Access to UBB models via the model selector","desc":"<p>Users will be able to access models that require usage-based billing (UBB) from the model selector in Chat. Tenant admins will need to allocate credits so that users can interact with these models. If users consume their allotted credits, they will be able to request credits from their tenant admins.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-02","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571400","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-552598","title":"Microsoft Edge: Improvements to site permissions user interfaces","desc":"<p>To better align with user expectations, site permissions are changing to look and work both in context on a website that is requesting permissions and when navigating to permissions from Settings. On a website that is requesting permissions, there are changes to the Omnibox and the Page Info dialog and permissions will be easier to see and modify in Settings.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-10-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552598","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573244","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Migrate finance and operations environments from Lifecycle Services to Power Platform admin center","desc":"<p>The self-service environment migration feature moves management of an existing finance and operations apps environment from Microsoft Dynamics Lifecycle Services to the Microsoft Power Platform admin center.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance","Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management","Dynamics 365 Project Operations","Dynamics 365 Commerce","Microsoft Dataverse","Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app","Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-01","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573244","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"September CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/lifecycle-services/migrate-lifecycle-services-environments-power-platform-admin-center"},{"id":"rm-569721","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management – Ensure regulatory compliance by deleting inactive OneDrives and mailboxes for departing employees","desc":"<p>Enables admins to delete both content and containers for departed users at scale thereby keeping your tenant compliant without any manual effort.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-01","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569721","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571692","title":"Microsoft Edge: Updated performance information in tab hover cards","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is updating tab hover cards to provide clearer information about tab memory usage and memory savings when inactive tabs are discarded. Users will also have separate settings for tab-preview images and memory-usage information.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571692","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"mc-MC1243549","title":"(Updated) Retirement of SharePoint One-Time Passcode (SPO OTP) and transition to Microsoft Entra B2B","desc":"Updated October 1, 2026: Phase 1, which enables Entra B2B for new external sharing, is now fully rolled out for Production environments. To ensure a smooth transition, Phase 2, the retirement of SharePoint Online OTP, has been rescheduled to begin in mid-October 2026 and is expected to complete by end of November 2026 for Production environments.\n\nBoth Phase 1 and Phase 2 roll outs exclude GCC, GCCH & DoD. New dates for these environments will be communicated via Message center when we are ready to proceed. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are retiring SharePoint One‑Time Passcode (SPO OTP) authentication in OneDrive and SharePoint starting mid-October 2026. Beginning in May 2026, new external sharing invitations and authentication will start using Microsoft Entra B2B instead of SPO OTP. This transition simplifies external collaboration, aligns authentication with Microsoft identity standards, and enables consistent guest lifecycle management, governance, and Conditional Access coverage across Microsoft 365.\n[When this will happen]\n• May & June 2026: Invitation and authentication for new external sharing transitions to Microsoft Entra B2B. Users who previously authenticated via SPO OTP will continue to have access to specific people links even without a B2B guest account yet.\n• Mid-October 2026: Retirement of SPO OTP authentication begins. External users without a guest account get access denied on previously shared specific people links. To restore access, a guest account must be created in Entra B2B, or an allowed user must share/re-share at least one file/folder/site.\n• Retirement is expected to complete by end of November 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All Microsoft 365 tenants (commercial, government, sovereign).\n• All external users who access OneDrive or SharePoint files, folders, or sites.\n\nWhat will happen\n• The EnableAzureADB2BIntegration setting will no longer control external sharing behavior beginning May 2026.\n• SPO OTP authentication will retire beginning mid-October 2026.\n• The option to disable Entra B2B integration will be removed.\n\nImpact on external users\n• External users who already have an Entra B2B guest account in your directory:• No change in behavior.\n\n• External users without a B2B guest account:• Specific people links shared after changes rolled out to your tenant: A guest account will be automatically created via the Entra B2B Invitation Manager and authentication will use Entra B2B. The email one-time passcode feature is now turned on by default for all new tenants and for any existing tenants where you haven’t explicitly turned it off. Please refer to this article to learn more.\n• Specific people links shared before changes rolled out to your tenant: SPO OTP authentication continues until the retirement reaches the tenant. After the retirement, these users will receive access denied until a matching B2B guest account exists.\n\nRestoring access after retirement\n• Admins can manually create a guest account for the external user at any time. Alternatively, an internal user with permissions needs to share or re-share at least one file, folder, or site, which will automatically create the guest account and restore access to all previously shared content.\n\n[What you need to do to prepare]\nTo ensure a smooth transition:\n• Review external sharing policies and conditional access settings for guests in SharePoint and Entra admin centers.\n• Ensure that Microsoft Entra is configured to allow guest invitations for the appropriate users. For example, assign the Guest Inviter role to users who need external sharing or are responsible for creating guest accounts.\n• Inform users that, beginning in mid-October 2026, some external collaborators may see an access denied message when opening older links that were previously authenticated with SharePoint Online OTP. This can occur if a matching B2B guest account was not created for the email address used with the original sharing link.• To restore access, users can share or reshare at least one file with the external collaborator. This creates the required B2B guest account, after which the collaborator can continue accessing previously shared links.\n\n• If your organization relies on email OTP authentication via Entra, ensure it is not disabled in Entra External ID settings. See Email OTP for B2B guests.\n• Optionally, identify external collaborators without guest accounts via external sharing reports. Proactively create guest accounts to retain access.\n• Update internal documentation.\n\nLearn more:\n• Add and manage B2B collaboration users in the Microsoft Entra admin center | External ID | Microsoft Entra | Microsoft Learn\n• Email one-time passcode authentication for B2B guest users | External ID | Microsoft Entra | Microsoft Learn\n• Frequently Asked Questions: Improvements to external sharing in OneDrive & SharePoint | SharePoint in Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n• Overview: B2B collaboration with external guests for your workforce | External ID | Microsoft Entra | Microsoft Learn\n• Quickstart: Add a guest user and send an invitation | External ID | Microsoft Entra | Microsoft Learn\n• SharePoint and OneDrive integration with Microsoft Entra B2B | SharePoint in Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n• Configure external collaboration - Microsoft Entra External ID | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nCompliance QuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is accessed, processed, or stored?Yes. This change retires SPO OTP authentication and requires all external users to authenticate using Microsoft Entra B2B guest accounts, which alters the authentication method used to access existing SharePoint and OneDrive content.\nDoes the change modify Conditional Access policies or enforcement?Yes. After retirement, all external users will authenticate through Entra B2B and become fully subject to Microsoft Entra Conditional Access, Identity Protection, and guest governance policies.\nDoes the change provide a new way of communicating between users, tenants, or subscriptions?Yes. External sharing invitations will be routed through Microsoft Entra B2B Invitation Manager instead of SharePoint’s OTP invitation flow.\nDoes the change alter how admins monitor, report on, or demonstrate compliance activities?Yes. Authentication events and guest lifecycle actions will be logged through Entra audit logs rather than SPO OTP logs, changing where admins review authentication and guest access activity.","products":["SharePoint Online","Microsoft OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1243549","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-559613","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat can now better match search results from Scanned PDFs","desc":"<p>Copilot Chat can now better match search results from Scanned PDFs on Copilot users' files they are working on — content that was previously difficult to search and find.</p> <p>This feature will work for new/updated user's working files on a go-forward basis.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559613","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569432","title":"Microsoft Entra ID: Passkey support for B2B users","desc":"<p>B2B users, including internal guest users and external users, will be able to register and sign in with passkeys issued by a resource tenant to meet that tenant's multifactor authentication (MFA) requirements. Today, passkeys are supported for member users in their home tenant. With this update, B2B users can register a resource tenant passkey from the resource tenant's My Security Info page, or in-line during a proof-up prompt or passkey registration campaign, and then use it to satisfy the resource tenant's MFA requirements. This change is on by default. B2B users already in scope for passkeys in your Authentication methods policy will be enabled automatically. No action is required to turn it on. If you want to review or adjust who's affected, update your Authentication methods policy, passkey registration campaign, Conditional Access policies, and user scoping before rollout.</p>","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-10-01","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569432","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-515465","title":"Microsoft Teams: Adaptive card-based app & copilot agent link unfurling in Teams","desc":"<p>Discover and add SharePoint agents in chats and channels from in-context store. Users can click on 'Add agents and bots' from the roster drop down. This will open the in-context store, where users can discover SharePoint agents and add them directly to the conversation and collaborate in the group. Updated January 29, 2026: Due to a blocker we have paused rollout until March for this feature. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515465","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569421","title":"Microsoft Teams: Malicious URL Protection for Teams Chat and Channels for Gov clouds","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams can now detect and warn users on malicious URLs sent in Teams chat and channels in Gov clouds, increasing protection against malware attacks for Gov clouds customers.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-14","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569421","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-568369","title":"Microsoft 365: [Education] Assign Different Content to Learning Groups in a Single Assignment","desc":"<p>Enable educators to assign different content (attachments, resources, instructions) to different Individual Groups within a single Assignment. Today teachers must create separate assignments to differentiate — one for advanced readers, another for struggling students, etc. This feature collapses that into one assignment with group-specific content mapping.<br> Key capabilities:<br> Map different content to different Individual Groups within one Assignment<br> Students only see content assigned to their group<br> Clear group-to-content mapping visible to the educator before publishing<br> Differentiated content does not change submission or grading behavior<br> Content created using existing Assignment resource workflows (no new content surfaces)</p> <p>#education</p>","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-31","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568369","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568762","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Agent Readiness in Microsoft Copilot Studio","desc":"<p>Agent Readiness gives makers a real-time, always-visible health check for their Copilot Studio agents. A single \"Review\" indicator in the build experience surfaces anything blocking or at risk — from policy restrictions to missing evaluations — before it derails a publish. Blocked capabilities are grayed out up front with a clear reason, so makers never waste time configuring something that was never going to work.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-06","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568762","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-560548","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Configure user and survey data retention for deleted users in Viva Glint","desc":"<p>With the new control in Viva Glint, service administrators can now configure whether to retain or delete survey and relevant indefinable user data for users who are manually deleted from Glint or deleted via the signals received via Microsoft Entra. This will ensure that the consistency of previously generate Glint survey reports is retained and user data is handled in accordance with the relevant organizational policies. We will also process the delete signals received via Microsoft Entra and handle the corresponding user data retention or deletion as per our terms of service.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560548","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566865","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Admin assignment time limit","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview is introducing the ability to set a limit in days when assigning users and security groups to role groups. This allows admins to define a fixed duration when providing admin permission on a temporary basis.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566865","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-566529","title":"Microsoft Purview: View only Role management enhancements","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview is introducing a new view-only role management role to give admins permissions to see all the member assignments in Purview and Defender portal. This addition will be added to Global Reader and Security Reader in Purview and Entra.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-23","modified":"2026-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566529","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-573305","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: E-Documents - Exchange EDI documents","desc":"<p>This feature extends the <strong>E-Documents</strong> framework to support Electronic Data Interchange (EDI), which enables organizations to exchange business documents electronically with vendors and partners using widely adopted industry standards. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Leverage the existing E-Documents framework as a unified platform for managing electronic document exchange.</li> <li>Enable organizations to send and receive structured business documents without relying on paper-based or manual processes.</li> <li>Exchange documents using Peppol BIS 3, which is an often used for electronic procurement and invoicing, but also opened for adding new formats based on local or customer standards.</li> <li>Support order exchange, and sending remitannce advices, and is open for additional document types.</li> <li>Facilitate standardized document exchange between organizations and vendors.</li> <li>Automate the generation, transmission, and processing of electronic business documents.</li> <li>Align with regulatory, industry, and partner requirements for electronic document exchange.</li> </ul> <p>By bringing EDI capabilities into e-documents, organizations can modernize their supply chain and procurement processes while using a consistent, scalable approach to electronic business communication.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573305","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573304","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Calculate withholding tax automatically in expense reports","desc":"<p>Organizations can automatically calculate employee withholding taxes (WHT) as part of the expense report process. When employees submit expenses that are subject to withholding tax requirements, the system applies the appropriate tax calculations directly within the expense report workflow. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Automatic withholding tax calculation for employee expense transactions that require tax deductions.</li> <li>Calculate single or multiple withholding taxes for each category, based on you setup. Calculations can also be simple or compound.</li> <li>Calculate thresholds based on different periods for records, documents, categories (period accumulation), and total (period accumulation).</li> <li>Base calculations on gross or net amounts.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573304","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2027","gaSort":202704,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571666","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Generate maintenance work orders within a configurable lead window","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Organizations can turn upcoming maintenance requirements into executable Field Service work without requiring planners to monitor every asset and create each work order manually. Generating work at a controlled point before it is due gives dispatchers time to secure technicians, skills, parts, and customer access while avoiding an unnecessarily large backlog of work created too far in advance.</p> <p>This connects long-range maintenance planning with day-to-day service execution and helps ensure that a valid maintenance requirement becomes actionable at the right time.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>Configure a lead window that determines how far in advance an upcoming maintenance event should create a work order. When a scheduled or predicted event enters that window, generate the corresponding Field Service work order for the customer asset.</p> <p>Carry the relevant maintenance context into the generated work, including the maintenance activity and the information required to prepare and schedule service. Depending on the configured maintenance definition, this can include tasks, products, services, required skills, and expected duration.</p> <p>Work-order generation can operate from maintenance due through calendar recurrence, actual meter usage, or a projected usage date. The generated work remains connected to the originating maintenance event so planners can understand why it was created and prevent duplicate demand.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571666","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573239","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Preserve actual booking End Time when completion is recorded later","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Technicians do not always record booking completion at the moment work ends. They may update the booking later because of connectivity, customer-facing responsibilities, or end-of-day administration. When the later administrative action replaces the booking End Time, the recorded duration can extend beyond the work that was actually performed and affect downstream journals, time entries, labor costs, actuals, and work-order completion reporting.</p> <p>Field Service administrators can choose whether completion by the booked resource automatically changes the booking End Time. Organizations whose technicians complete bookings later can preserve the existing or explicitly supplied work end, helping booking duration and downstream time and cost records remain aligned with when the work occurred.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>Use the organization-level <strong>Set End Time on booked resource completion</strong> setting in Field Service settings to control the automatic End Time update.</p> <ul> <li>With the setting set to <strong>Yes</strong>, which is the default, current behavior is preserved. When the booked resource completes a booking without supplying End Time, Field Service sets End Time to the completion time and recalculates Duration.</li> <li>With the setting set to <strong>No</strong>, Field Service preserves End Time and Duration when the booked resource completes the booking unless the completion request explicitly supplies a different End Time.</li> <li>Completion by another user or an integration continues to preserve End Time for either setting value.</li> </ul> <p>When the setting is No and the booked resource completes the booking, Field Service uses the retained or supplied End Time as the effective Completed booking timestamp. This keeps timestamp-derived booking journals and automatic time entries aligned with the recorded work end. Dataverse audit fields continue to show when the completion was submitted.</p> <p>The setting applies to future completion transitions and does not rewrite historical bookings. It does not change the booking-status lifecycle, invoice generation, or the existing Work Order Completed On calculation, which continues to use the latest eligible booking End Time.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573239","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-523223","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Deep citations in Copilot","desc":"<p>Deep citations let users quickly verify Copilot's results by linking directly to the relevant part of the reference, boosting trust. We're starting with Word and PPT files, then adding Meetings, Web, and PDF references.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-18","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523223","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573306","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Finance - Calculate multiple excise duties per item","desc":"<p>This feature enhances excise tax management by allowing multiple excise duty definitions to be associated with a single item and calculated during transactions.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Assign multiple excise duty configurations to the same inventory item (i.e, item is liable for both plastic and sugar tax).</li> <li>Automatically calculate all applicable excise duties during purchasing and vendor-related transactions.</li> <li>Support complex tax scenarios where products are subject to more than one excise levy.</li> <li>Reduce the need for manual workarounds, customizations, or separate item records to represent different tax obligations.</li> <li>Improve tax accuracy and consistency across purchasing, inventory valuation, and financial reporting processes.</li> </ul> <p>With this enhancement, businesses can model real-world excise tax structures more effectively while maintaining compliance with local regulatory requirements. The system aggregates and applies all configured excise duties for an item, ensuring that tax amounts are calculated consistently and transparently throughout the transaction lifecycle.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573306","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573308","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Finance - Use withholding taxes (WHT) with employee transactions","desc":"<p>This feature extends withholding tax capabilities to include employee transactions. The feature supports scenarios where employee-related payments or reimbursements are subject to withholding tax requirements and ensures that you accurately process the transactions in the financial system. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Apply withholding tax rules to employee transactions.</li> <li>Automatically calculate withholding tax amounts based on configured tax setups.</li> <li>Maintain consistent tax treatment across vendor and employee transaction processing.</li> </ul> <p>When someone creates an employee transaction, the system finds the applicable withholding tax configuration and applies the relevant withholding tax treatment. This capabililty enables organizations to meet local tax requirements for employee-related payments while keeping financial records accurate and compliant.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573308","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573307","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Finance - Vendor specific number series for Self-billing Invoices","desc":"<p>Organizations that use self-billing often need to follow supplier-specific invoicing requirements, including unique numbering conventions. With this enhancement, users can define and assign dedicated number series for self-billed purchase invoices on a per-vendor basis.</p> <p>Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Set up a unique number series for individual vendors that participate in self-billing arrangements.</li> <li>Automatically apply the vendor-specific number series when creating self-billed purchase invoices.</li> <li>Maintain separate invoice numbering sequences across different suppliers.</li> <li>Improve compliance with vendor agreements and local business requirements that mandate specific invoice numbering practices.</li> <li>Reduce manual intervention and the risk of numbering errors during invoice generation.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573307","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573255","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - AI-Driven Approvals","desc":"<p>Expense Agent can validate submitted expense reports against approval policies written in natural language and provide approvers with guidance during the review process. After an employee submits an expense report, the system evaluates both the overall report and the individual expense lines to detect potential policy violations, suspicious patterns, or situations that might require closer attention. This process supports policies that aren't limited to exact thresholds or fixed numeric conditions, such as when business class travel is allowed, what qualifies as an appropriate business meal, or when exceptions to preferred hotel standards might be acceptable. The result is additional review context that helps approvers make better-informed decisions without replacing the final human approval step.</p> <p>By running policy validation after submission, the feature can apply controls at the level of a single expense line in the first release. The feature complements existing approval workflows by highlighting issues, providing context, and helping organizations enforce policy consistently while keeping approvers in control of the final decision.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573255","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573262","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Calculate and report VAT based on expense reports","desc":"<p>Expense Agent supports automated VAT handling for expense reports, which can help simplify tax management and improve reporting accuracy. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Automatic VAT Calculation</strong>: Expense Agent identifies VAT-relevant expense transactions and calculates applicable VAT amounts based on the information in submitted expense reports.</li> <li><strong>VAT-Aware Expense Processing</strong>: VAT values are incorporated into the expense review and processing workflow, reducing the need for manual tax calculations.</li> <li><strong>Enhanced VAT Reporting</strong>: VAT amounts captured from employee expenses are aggregated and reported, supporting financial reporting and tax recovery processes.</li> <li><strong>Improved Compliance</strong>: Standardized VAT handling helps ensure that expense-related tax calculations apply consistently across the organization.</li> <li><strong>Human in the loop</strong>: If the VAT calculation is enabled for expense reports, accountants must review VAT calculation and confirm that everything is correct before posting it.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573262","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573258","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Improve duplicates prevention","desc":"<p>Expense Agent can identify and handle duplicated expense submissions. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Enhanced duplicate detection that identifies expenses with matching or highly similar details, such as amount, date, merchant, receipt, or transaction information.</li> <li>Proactive guidance that alerts employees when it detects a potential duplicate expense in the current expense report, or one that is already posted.</li> <li>Reduced manual review effort by helping prevent duplicate claims from entering approval and reimbursement workflows.</li> <li>Improved expense data integrity through more intelligent validation and comparison of submitted expenses.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573258","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573259","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Use assigned projects only in the web app","desc":"<p>Expense Agent web app now uses dedicated resource assignments for projects to determine which projects are available to each user when they create or manage expense entries. Key capabilities include:</p> <ul> <li>You can assign dedicated resources (employees) to the whole project or to the specific task.</li> <li>Display only projects or/and tasks where the user is assigned as a resource.</li> <li>Automatically filter project lists based on project-resource relationships.</li> <li>Reduce the risk of users selecting projects that aren't relevant to their role or assignments.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573259","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571677","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app: Role-based access controls for ERP agents","desc":"<p>Dynamics 365 ERP security administrators can apply additional, agent-specific security restrictions that take effect when a user accesses the ERP through an agent. Administrators define these restrictions using the existing security model — assigning roles, duties, and privileges that apply only to agent-initiated requests, scoped by legal entity — so that a user's agent session can operate with narrower permissions than the same user holds when working directly in the ERP.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations cross-app"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571677","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570430","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Persistent identity for Copilot Studio Agents","desc":"<p>Makers can now give their Copilot Studio agents their own accounts, making it a governed Microsoft 365 identity for shared, collaborative business processes that spans across teams. With its own mailbox, Teams presence &amp; Office access, the agent can collaborate where work happens while admins can control and govern its access, policies and use as its own first-class entity.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570430","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568366","title":"Microsoft Edge: Automatically unsubscribe users from notifications sent by scam and malicious sites","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge now helps further protect users from malicious web notifications. When a notification leads users to a site that Microsoft Defender SmartScreen blocks as a scam, phishing, or malware page, Edge automatically stops that source from sending users further notifications and lets users know. Users can review and restore any of these sites anytime under edge://settings/privacy/sitePermissions/allPermissions/notifications.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-03","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568366","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569434","title":"Microsoft Teams: App centric management in Teams Admin Center to manage the Apps access for tenants, end-users, and groups in DoD","desc":"<p>App centric management introduces new admin settings to control who in the tenant can install Teams apps. First, admins can set a default value for new apps that are published to Teams app store. Second, admins can edit the availability of an app to “All users can install,” “Specific users and groups can install,” or “No user can install.” This feature evolves the existing app permission policies and provides admins with the ability to manage access to the app individually. The app permission policies for existing customers are migrated to maintain existing app availability in the tenant.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-14","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569434","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569433","title":"Microsoft Teams: App centric management in Teams Admin Center to manage the Apps access for tenants, end-users, and groups in GCC High","desc":"<p>App centric management introduces new admin settings to control who in the tenant can install Teams apps. First, admins can set a default value for new apps that are published to Teams app store. Second, admins can edit the availability of an app to “All users can install,” “Specific users and groups can install,” or “No user can install.” This feature evolves the existing app permission policies and provides admins with the ability to manage access to the app individually. The app permission policies for existing customers are migrated to maintain existing app availability in the tenant.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-14","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569433","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-557165","title":"Microsoft Teams: Chat for organizers and presenters in structured meetings and webinars on Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"<p>When a Teams Rooms on Windows acts as an organizer, co-organizer or presenter in a structured meeting or webinar, you have access to the private chat for event management known as the Event Group. You can also switch to a separate chat with attendees enabling smooth event experiences for all. Available in Teams Rooms Pro-licensed rooms.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557165","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569609","title":"Microsoft Teams: Report a Message or an External User for Security Concern in Gov Clouds","desc":"<p>Users in Gov clouds can now report suspicious messages and external users within Teams. Reports are surfaced in the Teams admin center, giving admins greater visibility into potentially malicious activity and enabling them to investigate and take appropriate action. By incorporating end-user reports as an additional security signal, this capability helps organizations identify and respond more quickly to phishing, impersonation, spam, and other messaging threats.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569609","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-573365","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Adapt faster with Power Platform - Map new Dataverse fields in Business Central","desc":"<p>This feature simplifies how administrators keep Business Central and Dataverse aligned as Dataverse schemas evolve. Previously, exposing new or existing custom Dataverse fields required creating or updating a table extension (PTE) in the integration layer. Based on partner and customer feedback, this update removes that dependency.</p> <p>When a new field is added in Dataverse—such as a custom field in Dynamics 365 Sales—you can now map the field directly from the <strong>Integration Table Mappings</strong> page. You can refresh the Dataverse field list, add the field to an existing mapping, select the corresponding Business Central field, define the synchronization direction, and enable it for data synchronization. Once enabled, the field participates in sync without modifying extensions or recreating mappings.</p> <p><img src=\"media/dataverse-mappings.png\" alt=\"Shows the new integration mappings page in Business Central\" title=\"Shows the new integration mappings page in Business Central\"></p> <p>This enhancement reduces configuration overhead and supports faster adoption of custom Dataverse fields, especially for organizations that frequently customize their Dataverse environments.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> As an administrator, you can map newly added Dataverse fields without recreating table extensions or writing code, reducing configuration effort and supporting faster adoption of custom fields and solutions. This improvement makes it easier to keep Business Central and Dataverse aligned as Dataverse schemas change.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573365","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573362","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Enable Microsoft Copilot chat experience","desc":"<p>The updated Microsoft Copilot chat experience introduces a modern, consistent, and intuitive interface that aligns Business Central with the broader Microsoft Copilot ecosystem. The enhancement modernizes the chat panel, streamlines navigation, and improves user workflows by adopting familiar interaction patterns from Microsoft Copilot.</p> <p>This update benefits users who regularly interact with Copilot to accelerate daily tasks - especially operations managers, accountants, sales representatives, and administrators who rely on conversational assistance to navigate and analyse data. It also provides a more predictable experience across Microsoft 365 applications, reducing onboarding time and helping organizations adopt AI capabilities more systematically.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> The updated Copilot chat experience provides a familiar and consistent AI experience across Business Central and Microsoft applications. You get started faster, switch more easily between applications, and interact with AI more confidently, helping improve productivity and accelerate adoption.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573362","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com//dynamics365/business-central/chat-with-copilot"},{"id":"rm-573380","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Improve purchase order matching in Payables Agent","desc":"<p>This feature improves PO matching quality in Payables Agent and aligns draft finalization behavior with existing posting controls.</p> <p>The agent uses an enriched <strong>PO Lines</strong> list page during matching that includes these fields:</p> <ul> <li>Line Amount — enables matching on value, not just description and quantity. This field is especially valuable for service lines where quantity (often just 1) isn't a meaningful discriminator.</li> <li>Expected Receipt Date — helps the agent factor in timing when multiple PO lines could match.</li> </ul> <p>By using these fields, the agent can more reliably distinguish between similar-looking PO lines, which improves accuracy in first-pass matches.</p> <p>The agent now respects the app's <em>Never block draft finalization</em> setting in the <strong>Receipt on Invoice</strong> field on purchase orders. This change means the agent doesn't block draft finalization because a matched PO line isn't yet marked as received. Whether goods are received is a posting time control, not a draft time control. The \"Receipt on Invoice\" setting on the order governs this behavior at posting.</p> <p>The \"Receipt on Invoice\" field is already available on purchase orders. With this release, we're expanding this setting to more entities:</p> <ul> <li>A new vendor-level \"Receipt on Invoice\" setting is introduced and automatically applied to new purchase orders created for a vendor.</li> <li>A new PO-line-level \"Receipt on Invoice\" setting allows per-line override. The inheritance chain for the setting is vendor, then purchase order, and then purchase order line, but each level can override the parent.</li> </ul> <p>We've also improved draft warnings. When the agent creates a purchase invoice draft matched to a PO, the draft surfaces warnings based not just on quantity, but also on amount. The draft warnings are for information only and don't block finalization. For example, they warn about the discrepancies in the draft and you can decide how to proceed.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573380","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573370","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Manage agent permissions easier","desc":"<p>Assign additional permissions to agents when they request them.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573370","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573363","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Manage tasks from all agents in dedicated task pane","desc":"<p>This feature introduces a dedicated task pane in Business Central that displays all tasks generated by the agents.</p> <p>The task pane appears as an additional panel in the user interface and can be opened from anywhere in Business Central. Tasks include suggestions, validations, follow‑ups access to draft documents, and other agent‑initiated actions. Users can review task details, navigate directly to the affected record, complete tasks, or dismiss them.</p> <p>This improvement primarily benefits roles that rely heavily on AI‑driven workflows—such as accountants, sales people, and managers—who often engage with multiple agents throughout the day. The task pane reduces friction by collecting all insights in a single location, minimizing missed tasks and improving throughput.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> The Show all agent tasks on a separate task pane feature help organizations get more value from Microsoft Copilot in Business Central by giving users a single, structured place to review and act on AI‑generated tasks. Instead of relying on notifications scattered across different pages, users gain a clear, consolidated overview of all tasks created by agents working in finance, purchasing, sales, and operations.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573363","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573366","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Review content generated by agents directly on pages","desc":"<p>This improvement introduces the ability for Business Central users to review and approve content generated by agents directly on the pages where they work. You no longer need to navigate to separate task pane to understand that a given document was created by an agent. Instead, agent‑generated suggestions—such as descriptions, text proposals, or field‑specific updates—appear inline where they can be evaluated and modified before being applied.</p> <p>By keeping the review process within the page context, users maintain flow, reduce clicks, and ensure content quality with minimal disruption. The feature builds on existing Business Central autofill user interface patterns ensuring admins and users can adopt it as part of existing agent‑powered daily workflows.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> The ability to review agent‑generated content directly on pages helps organizations streamline their daily work while maintaining accuracy and control. You can evaluate suggestions in the context of the task you are performing, reducing interruptions and improving the quality of the final output.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573366","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573312","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Run data queries with MCP Server","desc":"<p>Use new MCP tools to define, validate, and run custom data queries. Your MCP application can then query data for which no existing APIs exist.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573312","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573364","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Show avatars for record creators and modifiers in list","desc":"<p>This feature introduces visual avatars in Business Central list pages to indicate which user or agent created or last modified a record. The capability enhances traceability and supports collaborative work by making identity information immediately visible without opening the record.</p> <p>The avatars reflect either a named Business Central user, a system user or an AI agent, following the existing identity model. Users can hover over the avatar to see a tooltip with the full display name and record update timestamp (if available).</p> <p>This improvement benefits roles that frequently work with shared data—including accountants, order processors, warehouse staff, service teams, and administrators—by reducing time spent verifying ownership or responsibility for items, documents, or configuration entries. It also helps organizations adopting AI‑generated records understand when an automated agent has contributed.</p> <p>The feature surfaces existing <strong>Created By</strong> and <strong>Modified By</strong> fields more intuitively while respecting Business Central’s data privacy and permissions model.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> Supporting avatars for the users or agents who created and last modified entries makes record ownership clearer and easier to understand across Business Central. By surfacing identity information directly in list pages, you can quickly determine responsibility, follow up with the right person, and work with shared data more confidently.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573372","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Copilot and agents - Updates to Agent UI experience","desc":"<p>Manage agents more easily by grouping avatars and using a dedicated action to start new tasks.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573372","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573354","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Access application links through ModuleInfo","desc":"<p>\"Read help, EULA, privacy statement, and locale-aware context-sensitive help links from an app manifest at runtime through additional ModuleInfo properties.</p> <p>Business value: Extensions can surface application-specific help, legal, and privacy resources dynamically instead of duplicating links in code. Context-sensitive help can also respect the current user's locale, improving support experiences for multilingual deployments.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573354","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573313","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Actions on reports and pages can now inherit tooltips","desc":"<p>Tooltips on page or report objects are now inherited into actions that run those pages.</p> <p>This means you only need to write descriptive tooltips in one place and have it propagated out to all usage of the object.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573313","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573314","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - AL developers can turn indexes on/off in AL code.","desc":"<p>AL developers can now turn indexes off/on from AL code.</p> <p>This allows app publishers to ship index management to match their features.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573314","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573336","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Audit AL app accessibility and debugging boundaries","desc":"<p>\"Build and query static AL call graphs to trace public-to-internal calls, debugging boundaries, elevated code, and cross-app relationships, with visual exports.</p> <p>Business value: Extension developers can understand how public APIs expose internal implementation details and where execution crosses debugging boundaries. This visibility helps teams review extension architecture, reduce unintended API exposure, and identify cases where sensitive values could become inspectable in the debugger. The analysis can run across an app and its dependencies, making it useful for architecture reviews, security assessments, and automated governance in larger extension portfolios.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573336","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573333","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Build extensible and data-driven AL test suites","desc":"<p>\"Create parameterized AL tests from reusable data sources, and attach lifecycle handlers for shared setup, cleanup, logging, measurement, and test reporting.</p> <p>Business value: Developers can build more maintainable AL test suites by separating reusable test data and lifecycle behavior from individual test procedures. Data-driven tests reduce duplicated test code, while test handlers provide a consistent way to implement logging, cleanup, performance measurement, and custom reporting across many test codeunits. These capabilities make it easier to expand test coverage, standardize test execution, and understand failures without adding the same setup and instrumentation code to every test.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573333","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573360","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Check records for uncommitted changes","desc":"<p>\"Use the Record API IsDirty property to determine whether a record instance contains unsaved changes before deciding to validate, save, or otherwise process it.</p> <p>Business value: AL developers can determine whether a record instance has been changed before deciding to save it, validate it, or prompt the user. This can simplify conditional persistence and reduce unnecessary database operations.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573360","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573348","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Configure AL MCP workspaces dynamically","desc":"<p>\"Start the AL MCP server without a predefined project, add AL projects at runtime, and use configured connection details in headless scenarios without authentication prompts.</p> <p>Business value: AI-agent hosts can start a reusable AL MCP server before the target project is known, then load projects as work begins. This supports flexible agent sessions, shared tooling configurations, and headless automation without requiring a separate server process for every preconfigured workspace.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573348","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573361","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Debug recorded Business Central failures with an AI agent","desc":"<p>\"Describe a failing scenario to an AI agent, record the next matching Business Central session or a known session, and collect its snapshot for offline AL debugging.</p> <p>Business value: Developers can investigate intermittent or production-only AL failures by describing the problem to an AI agent and reproducing the scenario, without manually configuring and operating the snapshot debugger. The agent arms the recording, monitors its status, and collects the completed snapshot for offline debugging. This guided workflow makes snapshot debugging more accessible and helps support teams capture the execution that caused an error even when the affected session doesn't yet exist.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573361","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573315","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Developers can define indexes that span fields from a base table and its table extensions","desc":"<p>The new data model for storing fields from table extensions allows developers to define keys across fields from the base table and table extensions.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573315","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573349","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Diagnose AL MCP server activity with file logging","desc":"<p>\"Write AL MCP server diagnostics to a configurable file, select the appropriate detail level for troubleshooting, or turn file logging off when it isn't required.</p> <p>Business value: Developers and administrators can retain AL MCP server diagnostics for troubleshooting intermittent failures and reviewing agent activity. Configurable verbosity helps capture detailed information during investigation without permanently producing excessive logs.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573349","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573339","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Discover objects in connected Business Central environments","desc":"<p>\"Search objects installed in a connected Business Central environment, including owning-app metadata needed to add dependencies and download the correct symbols.</p> <p>Business value: Developers and coding agents can discover AL objects that are installed in the target Business Central environment even when the corresponding symbols haven't yet been downloaded into the workspace. This reduces failed searches and helps agents add the correct app dependency before generating code that uses an object.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573339","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573352","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Evolve AL interfaces with default implementations","desc":"<p>\"Add default method bodies to AL interfaces so existing implementors continue working, then use RequiredPending and analyzer rules to introduce required methods safely.</p> <p>Business value: Extension publishers can add behavior to an interface without immediately requiring every implementing extension to change. Default methods provide a compatible implementation, while the new transition attribute and AppSourceCop rules support a managed path toward making a method mandatory in a future version. This reduces disruptive interface upgrades and gives dependent developers time to adopt new contracts.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573352","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573337","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Get clearer guidance for AL object structure","desc":"<p>\"Use compiler diagnostic AL0926 to identify AL object sections declared in the wrong order instead of interpreting multiple secondary and less specific parser errors.</p> <p>Business value: Developers and coding agents receive a direct explanation when sections of an AL object are declared in the wrong order. The clearer diagnostic reduces time spent interpreting secondary parser errors and makes automated code generation easier to correct.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573337","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573346","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Let agents allocate free AL object IDs","desc":"<p>\"Let coding agents find available IDs for AL objects and extension objects within project ranges, reducing manual range checks and collisions with existing project objects. Note that only IDs in connected environment are considered.</p> <p>Business value: Coding agents can scaffold AL objects without manually reading ID ranges or risking collisions with objects already declared in the project. This makes generated code more reliable and reduces the corrections needed before it compiles.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573346","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573384","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Page Scripting enters General Availability","desc":"<p>The page scripting tool that can be used to record and replay user actions directly in the Business Central web client is moving out of preview to general availability. Thus the tool is fully localized and includes accessibility, usability, and visual improvements. We have also added new capabilitites to select multiple rows in grids and validate text displayed in message and error dialogs.</p> <p>Business value: Customers, consultants, and testers can create repeatable user acceptance tests for real business processes without writing AL code. The new support for multi-selection captures bulk workflows accurately, while dialog-text validation turns recordings into meaningful checks of expected messages and errors.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573384","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573335","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Profile slow Business Central sessions with AI agents","desc":"<p>\"Let an AI agent schedule profiling for a Business Central session, collect CPU and memory data, identify costly AL paths, and summarize SQL and HTTP activity.</p> <p>Business value: Developers and administrators can investigate slow Business Central sessions with help from an AI agent instead of manually collecting and interpreting performance profiles. The agent can capture the affected session, identify expensive AL call paths, and summarize whether CPU or managed-memory usage contributes to the problem. This guided workflow shortens the time from a reported performance problem to actionable code-level findings, even when the user isn't already debugging the session.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573335","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573357","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Restrict global symbol resolution to a minor version","desc":"<p>\"Configure global symbol downloads to remain within the major and minor version in app.json while still selecting the newest available patch for all dependencies.</p> <p>Business value: Development teams can make symbol restoration more predictable by preventing dependencies from moving to a newer minor release unexpectedly. This helps reproduce builds and test extensions against the intended Business Central minor version while still receiving compatible patch updates.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573357","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573334","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Run AL tests from command-line and CI/CD workflows","desc":"<p>\"Use ALTool to compile, deploy, and run AL test projects from scripts or pipelines, with structured JSON results for test methods and pass, fail, and skip counts.</p> <p>Business value: Development teams can run AL tests directly from automated build and release pipelines without depending on the MCP server or a manually operated test client. Machine-readable output makes it easier to publish test results, enforce quality gates, and diagnose failures in continuous integration environments. The same command can also be used locally, giving developers and build systems a consistent test-execution workflow.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573334","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573356","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Simplify AL extension setup and authentication in Visual Studio Code","desc":"<p>\"Automatically acquire the required .NET runtime and use Visual Studio Code authentication by default, reducing manual setup across local and browser-hosted environments.</p> <p>Business value: AL developers spend less time installing runtimes and managing separate authentication prompts when setting up Visual Studio Code. The AL extension is also smaller because it no longer includes separate runtime copies for each supported operating system. The streamlined configuration provides a more consistent setup across Windows, macOS, and Linux.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573356","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573351","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Track AL compiler diagnostics in automated builds","desc":"<p>\"Have ALTool workspace builds write structured, project-specific compiler error logs that automated systems can retain, analyze, and use for code-quality tracking.</p> <p>Business value: Development teams can retain structured compiler and analyzer results from workspace builds, making it easier to track code-quality regressions and integrate AL diagnostics with automated alerting and reporting systems.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573351","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573359","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Translate objects with the same name in different namespaces","desc":"<p>\"Generate namespace-aware translation identifiers so identically named AL objects can be translated independently while existing non-namespaced translations remain valid.</p> <p>Business value: Extension developers can translate objects independently when those objects have the same name but belong to different namespaces. This avoids translation identifier collisions and supports broader adoption of namespaces in existing apps.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573359","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573338","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Development - Use AL language intelligence from AI agents and other editors","desc":"<p>\"Run the standalone AL language server to provide completion, navigation, references, rename, formatting, and other project-aware LSP features outside Visual Studio Code.</p> <p>Business value: Teams can use full AL language intelligence in AI coding agents and development environments that support the Language Server Protocol (LSP), without requiring Visual Studio Code as the client. This opens AL development to additional editors and agentic workflows while retaining accurate project-aware navigation and refactoring.\"</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573338","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573340","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Control sales document creation for Shopify orders and returns","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Set Use Shopify Order No. and Process Returns as on the Shopify Shop Card, then review contacts before you choose Create Sales Document.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>The Shopify connector gives you more control before it creates sales documents.</p> <p>Although the connector already stores the Shopify order number in dedicated fields on sales documents, using the same document number in Shopify and Business Central can improve traceability across both systems even more.</p> <ul> <li>Turn on <strong>Use Shopify Order No.</strong> on the Shopify Shop Card to use the Shopify order number as the Business Central sales document number.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>[!NOTE]<br> Configure a number series that permits manual numbers. A number conflict can prevent the Shopify order number from being used.</p> </blockquote> <p>You can also review the contacts that the connector selects for billing, shipping, and order communication before you create the sales document.</p> <ul> <li>Review and edit sell-to, ship-to, and bill-to contact numbers on the Shopify Order. If the connector doesn't find the right contact, use the lookup to select a different contact for the corresponding customer. The contact fields are hidden by default and can be added through personalization.</li> </ul> <p>Both Shopify and Business Central support advanced return processes, but the original connector implementation represented refunds only as sales credit memos, which doesn't support warehouse return processing. You can now choose which sales document type the connector creates for refunds.</p> <ul> <li>Use <strong>Process Returns as</strong> to choose whether Shopify refunds create sales credit memos or sales return orders.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>[!NOTE]<br> Processing Shopify returns remains unsupported.</p> </blockquote>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573340","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573341","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Keep Shopify connections current","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Shopify regularly retires API versions. Staying current helps prevent avoidable connection interruptions and keeps synchronization compatible with Shopify platform changes. Better operational cues and clearer timestamps help administrators find failures faster and understand whether a value came from Shopify or Business Central.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>Shopify releases a new API version every three months at the beginning of the quarter, and supports each version for 12 months. The updated versions might contain important changes, so it's important to uptake Shopify API versions in major releases of Business Central. Typically, new versions of APIs increase stability and security, and enable additional capabilities. Starting with this release, Shopify Connector uses the Shopify API that was released in July 2026. This update keeps the integration on a supported API version and includes security changes such as support for expiring offline access tokens for public apps, as well as functional changes, like market-driven shipping methods.</p> <blockquote> <p>[!IMPORTANT]</p> <p>The Shopify Connector released in 2026 release wave 1 (April 2026) relies on API 2026-01, which is supported until December 31, 2026. To continue to use your integration, upgrade to the latest version of Business Central before this date.</p> </blockquote> <h3>The connector now supports Shopify's expiring offline access tokens</h3> <ul> <li>Access tokens refresh automatically before their one-hour lifetime expires.</li> <li>Refresh tokens rotate and remain valid for up to 90 days.</li> <li>Existing non-expiring tokens migrate when the connector needs next authentication.</li> <li>If the refresh-token window expires, an administrator must reconnect the shop from the Shopify Shop Card.</li> </ul> <h3>Operational improvements make synchronization easier to supervise</h3> <ul> <li>A <strong>With errors</strong> view filters the Shopify Log to entries that contain errors.</li> <li>The Shopify Activities page shows <strong>Skipped Records</strong> and <strong>API Errors</strong> cues and highlights them when action is needed.</li> <li>Product and price synchronization skips invalid item unit-of-measure combinations and records the reason instead of stopping the complete synchronization. Enable logging to retain skipped-record details.</li> <li>Suffixes help you to distinguish <strong>Created At (Shopify)</strong> and <strong>Updated At (Shopify)</strong> imported from Shopify from standard audit fields present in Business Central.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573341","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573342","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Manage Shopify B2B companies, catalogs, and pricing","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Shopify expanded core B2B capabilities to all plans, and the Shopify connector supports company synchronization, B2B order processing, and market catalogs across those plans. The latest improvements make tax identifiers, company records, and catalog pricing easier to configure and help prevent conflicting price synchronization.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>The following capabilities are available on all Shopify plans:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Company synchronization</strong>: Import Shopify B2B companies and company locations and map them to customers in Business Central.</li> <li><strong>B2B order processing</strong>: When a B2B order arrives, the connector identifies the company and resolves the correct bill-to and ship-to customer based on the company location.</li> <li><strong>Market catalogs</strong>: Assign catalogs to B2B markets for price synchronization. Basic, Grow, and Advanced plans support up to three active market catalog assignments. The Plus plan supports unlimited assignments.</li> </ul> <p>Customer and company synchronization includes these improvements:</p> <ul> <li>Open <strong>Companies</strong> directly from the Shopify navigation group on supported role centers.</li> <li>Map Shopify company tax registration IDs to the appropriate customer registration or VAT registration field. In Belgium, the localized mapping uses <strong>Enterprise No.</strong> and avoids conflicting VAT Registration No. validation.</li> <li>Use the Country/Region <strong>ISO Code</strong> when the connector selects a Shopify Tax Area for customer or company export. Shopify Tax Area mappings must use the applicable Shopify ISO codes.</li> <li>Use updated province data for the Italian provinces formerly named Olbia-Tempio and Carbonia-Iglesias.</li> <li>When the same direct company catalog appears for multiple companies, the connector prevents you from synchronizing its prices more than once. If you enable <strong>Sync Prices</strong> on another entry, the connector explains that only one pricing configuration per catalog is used, offers to disable synchronization on the other entries, and recommends market catalogs when you want to link one catalog to multiple B2B companies.</li> <li>Use the clearer <strong>B2B Catalog</strong> terminology in company-related captions and tooltips, including <strong>Auto Create B2B Catalog</strong>. The <strong>Get Catalogs</strong> tooltip now explains that companies must be imported before company catalogs can be retrieved.</li> </ul> <p>The following features require an Advanced or Plus plan:</p> <ul> <li>Direct company catalogs</li> <li>Staff member mapping</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573342","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573343","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Process Shopify order changes, exchanges, and refunds","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Keep edited and exchanged Shopify orders aligned when you create sales documents and process refunds.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>When a Shopify return includes a replacement item, the connector imports the returned item and the exchange item together and adds them to a sales credit memo or sales return order. You can keep both items on the same document or move the exchange item to a new sales document.</p> <h3>Example: Process an exchange</h3> <p>A customer orders, pays for, and receives an item. You import and process the Shopify order in Business Central, where it becomes a posted sales invoice. Later, the customer decides that the item doesn't fit and returns it in exchange for a replacement item.</p> <p>The connector imports the updated Shopify order and its linked refund. When you choose <strong>Create Sales Document</strong>, the connector creates the document type selected in <strong>Process Returns as</strong>: a sales credit memo or sales return order. The returned item has a positive quantity on the new document, and the exchange item has a negative quantity.</p> <p>You can post the document with both lines, or you can keep the returned item on the credit memo or return order and move the exchange item to a separate sales document. To split the lines before posting:</p> <ol> <li>If the credit memo or return order has the <strong>Released</strong> status, choose <strong>Reopen</strong>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Move Negative Lines</strong>. From a sales credit memo, this action creates a sales invoice by default. From a sales return order, it creates a sales order by default.</li> </ol> <p>The new invoice or order for the replacement remains linked to the originating Shopify order and appears in the <strong>Linked Documents</strong> FactBox.</p> <p>For exchanges where the replacement costs more, the connector doesn't add an unnecessary balancing refund-account G/L line. A G/L line can still be added for cash rounding.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573343","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573344","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Ecommerce - Synchronize tariff numbers and origin values with Shopify","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Accurate tariff numbers and country/region of origin values support international shipping and customs reporting. Synchronizing these values with Shopify reduces duplicate data entry and helps keep product trade data consistent across both systems</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>Turn on <strong>Sync HS Code and Country/Region of Origin</strong> on the Shopify Shop Card to synchronize tariff numbers and country or region of origin values between Business Central and Shopify. On import, the connector updates values only when the Shopify value resolves to an existing Tariff Number or Country/Region record.</p> <p>Other product information management improvements provide more control over matching, product status, and variant information:</p> <ul> <li>Use <strong>Find Mapping by Barcode</strong> to control whether the connector tries barcode matching after the selected SKU mapping strategy fails. The setting is on by default for compatibility and can be disabled when barcodes aren't unique.</li> <li>Set <strong>Status for Created Products</strong> now includes new <strong>Unlisted</strong> status. The selected status applies when the connector creates a product in Shopify.</li> <li>Add <strong>Compare-at Price</strong> to the Shopify Variants page through personalization to inspect the comparison price used for a variant.</li> <li>From an Item Card or Item List, the <strong>Show Product in Shopify</strong> action is also enabled for items exported as variants to Shopify.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573344","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573254","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - Add date ranges and vehicle types in your mileage calculation","desc":"<p>Expense Agent now supports advanced mileage rate configuration based on both effective date ranges and vehicle types, enabling more flexible and accurate mileage reimbursement calculations. This enhancement combines mileage rate scheduling with support for differentiated vehicle categories. Key capabilities include additions on the Mileage Rate Setup page:</p> <ul> <li>Define mileage rates that are valid only within specific date ranges, allowing organizations to accommodate rate changes over time.</li> <li>Configure separate mileage reimbursement rates for different vehicle types, such as cars, motorcycles, electric vehicles, or other organization-defined vehicle categories.</li> <li>Automatically apply the correct reimbursement rate based on the travel date and selected vehicle type during mileage expense calculation.</li> <li>Support evolving regulatory requirements, company policies, and regional reimbursement standards without requiring manual recalculation of submitted mileage claims.</li> </ul> <p>Administrators can maintain a set of mileage rate records that include both an effective date range and an associated vehicle type. When someone creates a mileage expense, Expense Agent evaluates the trip date and the type of vehicle, and then applies the matching reimbursement rate automatically. This evaluation ensures that mileage claims are calculated using the appropriate rate in effect for the specific travel period and mode of transportation.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573254","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573253","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Expense Agent - More countries and languages","desc":"<p>Expense Agent supports more languages and regions, enabling an experience for users in <strong>all countries/regions</strong> where Business Central is available, and adding the following languages: Czech, Dutch, Finnish, Icelandic, Italian, Norwegian, and Swedish.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573253","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-573316","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Governance and administration - Administrators can turn SIFT indexes on/off","desc":"<p>Administrators can now turn SIFT indexes on/off directly in the Business Central application.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573316","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573317","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Governance and administration - Monitor usage of Open in Excel with telemetry","desc":"<p>Logging Open in Excel actions to telemetry makes data export events auditable, which can be critical for compliance, security investigations, and understanding how customers use Business Central.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573317","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573318","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Automate report outputs","desc":"<p>Use new APIs on the report inbox to extend automation with Power Automate or MCP to reports.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573318","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573319","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Bookmark list views and analysis tabs","desc":"<p>Bookmark analysis tabs and list views to your role center and/or incorporate them into profiles.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573319","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573327","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Brand document reports with report themes","desc":"<p>With the new composable layouts feature, you can apply a report theme on layouts to get consistent look and feel on the PDF output.</p> <p>It is possible to set defaults on a global level, per company, per report, or per layout, giving the administrator full flexibility of theming.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573327","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573320","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Control the lifecycle of all report layouts","desc":"<p>Set status on all types of layouts (including layouts shipped with Business Central, per-tenant extensions, and AppSource apps) to control which layouts are available to end users.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573320","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573330","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Design document report themes with the updated Word add-in","desc":"<p>Design document report themes using the new document samples controls in the Word add-in.</p> <p>We have added samples that look like common document types, such as</p> <ul> <li>invoice</li> <li>pick list</li> <li>outstanding orders.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573330","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573328","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Design document reports with the updated Word add-in","desc":"<p>Use new design components in the Word add-in to layout your document report layouts.</p> <p>We have added design controls for common document report parts, such as</p> <ul> <li>Addresses</li> <li>Field groups</li> <li>Amounts</li> <li>Signature lines</li> <li>Notes</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573328","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573331","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Design header/footer layouts for document reports with the updated Word add-in","desc":"<p>Design document report header/footer layouts using the new header and/or footer document samples controls in the Word add-in.</p> <p>We have addes samples that can be used for internal or external reports.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573331","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573325","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Financial report changes are now always logged","desc":"<p>Changes to financial row, column, and report definitions are automatically recorded in the change log for easier auditing.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573325","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573321","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Reduce complexity of report datasets","desc":"<p>Word layouts now include a company information dataitem that is shared across all report datasets.</p> <p>This reduces the work needed for a report developer and standardizes how company information is used across report layouts.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573321","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573326","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Reuse header/footer layouts across document reports","desc":"<p>With the new composable layouts feature, you can apply a header/footer on layouts to get consistent look and feel on the PDF output.</p> <p>It is possible to set defaults on a global level, per company, per report, or per layout, giving the administrator full flexibility of theming.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573326","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573323","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Run multiple financial reports and get a single PDF output","desc":"<p>Define report packs that contain multiple financial reports, and then run them immediately or schedule delivery to report inboxes or by email.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573324","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Trace G/L account usage in finance reports","desc":"<p>Financial report authors can now identify uncategorized accounts, trace account usage and calculations, and preview definitions before publishing.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573324","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573329","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Use conditional visibility in the updated Word add-in","desc":"<p>Design document reports layouts with conditional visibility using the new HideIf logic control in the Word add-in.</p> <p>The control can use boolean fields in the dataset to handle visibility of the content inside.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573329","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573322","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Reporting and data analysis - Use system audit fields in analysis mode and in profiles","desc":"<p>Use system audit fields in analysis tabs and add them directly to pages in profiles.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573322","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573332","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Service and platform - Faster data loading with improved data model for table extensions","desc":"<p>With the new data model for table extensions, all fields on an AL table are stored in the same table in the database.</p> <p>This gives faster performance on all database operations that involve table extensions.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573332","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573345","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Carry subcontracting instructions into purchase orders","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Subcontractors need clear instructions about the work they must perform. Reentering that information on purchase orders takes time and can introduce differences between the routing, production order, and purchasing documents.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>Subcontracting comments and attachments now follow the operation into the purchase order. The purchasing document keeps the production context needed by the vendor while allowing you to review and adjust the information before sending the order.</p> <p>The <strong>Subcontracting Comments</strong> action is available from standard tasks, routing lines, routing version lines, and production order routing operations. Comments follow the production flow:</p> <ol> <li>Add subcontracting comments to a standard task or routing operation.</li> <li>When you assign the standard task, its comments copy to the routing operation.</li> <li>When you create or refresh a production order, routing comments copy to the production order routing operation.</li> <li>When you create a subcontracting purchase order directly or from the Subcontracting Worksheet, the comments become descriptive purchase lines attached to the related subcontracting line.</li> </ol> <p>Both <strong>Description</strong> and <strong>Description 2</strong> flow through the process. If you change the vendor or recalculate the work center on the Subcontracting Worksheet, the worksheet preserves routing-specific descriptions when the work center still matches the production order routing operation.</p> <p>You can also carry supporting documents from the routing into the purchase order. On a routing header attachment, turn on both <strong>Production Trx</strong> and <strong>Purchase Trx</strong>. The attachment copies first to the production order and then to each related subcontracting purchase line. Attachments added manually to a production order line don't offer the <strong>Purchase Trx</strong> setting and don't copy automatically. Purchase-line attachments also aren't included automatically in vendor email messages. Use the <strong>Add file from source document</strong> action on the <strong>Email Editor</strong> page.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573345","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573347","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Post direct transfer orders from warehouse-enabled locations","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Direct transfers move inventory between locations without using an in-transit location. You can use this simpler transfer method when the source location requires outbound warehouse handling, while preserving the picking and shipment controls configured for that location.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>Previously, one setting on the <strong>Inventory Setup</strong> page controlled how Business Central posted all direct transfers. You can now choose a posting method for each transfer route, so different routes can post separate transfer shipment and receipt documents together or create one posted direct transfer document.</p> <p>Set <strong>Default Direct Transfer Posting</strong> on the <strong>Inventory Setup</strong> page to define the company-wide default. On the <strong>Transfer Routes</strong> page, set <strong>Direct Transfer Posting</strong> for routes that need a different method. The transfer order uses the route setting when one is specified and otherwise uses the Inventory Setup default. You can change <strong>Direct Transfer Posting</strong> on an open <strong>Transfer Order</strong> when needed.</p> <p>The posting methods work as follows:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Shipment and Receipt</strong> posts a transfer shipment and transfer receipt together. <strong>Qty. to Ship</strong> must equal <strong>Qty. to Receive</strong>. When you post from a warehouse shipment, partial posting is supported.</li> <li><strong>Direct Transfer</strong> posts one <strong>Posted Direct Transfer</strong> document. Business Central posts the full transfer-line quantity without creating separate transfer shipment and receipt documents.</li> </ul> <p>Direct transfers support the following outbound warehouse scenarios:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Transfer-from location setup</th> <th>How you complete the transfer</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>No warehouse requirements</td> <td>Post from the <strong>Transfer Order</strong>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Require Pick</strong> without <strong>Require Shipment</strong></td> <td>Create and post an <strong>Inventory Pick</strong>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Require Shipment</strong> without <strong>Require Pick</strong></td> <td>Create and post a <strong>Warehouse Shipment</strong>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Require Pick</strong> and <strong>Require Shipment</strong></td> <td>Register the <strong>Warehouse Pick</strong>, and then post the <strong>Warehouse Shipment</strong>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Bin Mandatory</strong></td> <td>Enter valid source and destination bins, and post from the document required by the other warehouse settings.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Directed Put-away and Pick</strong> at the source</td> <td>Register the warehouse pick and post the warehouse shipment by using the advanced warehouse process.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>With <strong>Shipment and Receipt</strong>, the destination can't require warehouse receipt or put-away. A destination that uses bins requires a valid <strong>Transfer-To Bin Code</strong>.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573347","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573350","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Reduce manual work in quality tests and inspections","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>The Quality Management extension helps you include quality checks in receiving, production, assembly, and inventory processes. We improved several parts of the experience so that inspectors and quality managers can complete routine tasks with fewer interruptions. These improvements reduce manual work when you record inspection outcomes, make inventory disposition easier to complete, and provide clearer guidance when a quality inspection blocks a transaction.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <h3>Choose whether to assign an inspection to yourself</h3> <p>When you edit an eligible unassigned quality inspection, Business Central asks whether you want to take ownership of it. The notification provides the following choices:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Assign to myself</strong> assigns the inspection to you.</li> <li><strong>Ignore</strong> leaves the inspection unassigned.</li> </ul> <h3>Calculate passed and failed quantities automatically</h3> <p>When you finish an inspection, Quality Management automatically records the inspected quantity as <strong>Passed Quantity</strong> when the result is acceptable, or as <strong>Failed Quantity</strong> for another result. The calculation uses <strong>Sample Size</strong>, or <strong>Quantity (Base)</strong> when no sample size is specified.</p> <h3>Select destination bins when moving inspected inventory</h3> <p>Quality Management workflows provide more control when a disposition moves inspected inventory. You can specify the movement method, quantity basis, destination location, and destination bin. Assisted bin selection helps you choose a valid destination for the movement.</p> <h3>Resolve blocked transactions from the responsible inspection</h3> <p>When a quality inspection prevents a transaction, such as sale or consumption, the error includes details about the inspection that caused the block. You can open the responsible inspection directly from the error and review or complete it before trying the transaction again.</p> <h3>Apply quality rules and permissions consistently</h3> <p>Quality Management validates inspection assignments and enforces quality rules consistently, including operations performed through indirect or implicit access. These checks help preserve the intended inspection and transaction controls without requiring broader permissions than the task needs.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573350","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573353","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Set up and explore subcontracting more easily","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Subcontracting requires coordinated setup across work centers, vendors, locations, prices, and production BOMs. A guided starting point and actionable warnings help administrators find the required setup and correct missing information before it interrupts production work.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>Clearer demonstration data also makes it easier to evaluate intermediate and final subcontracting operations and compare more than one subcontractor.</p> <p>The <strong>Subcontracting Setup</strong> assisted setup guide, available after the Subcontracting app is installed, organizes initial configuration into three steps:</p> <ol> <li>Review an introduction to subcontracting.</li> <li>Review company defaults such as the worksheet template and batch, production-order information lines, component costs, and transfer lead time.</li> <li>Open the related pages to set up work centers, vendors, locations, subcontractor prices, component supply methods, and supporting documentation.</li> </ol> <p>Additional improvements make setup and discovery clearer:</p> <ul> <li>From the <strong>Work Center Card</strong>, open <strong>Subcontractor Prices</strong>, <strong>Subcontracting WIP Entries</strong>, and <strong>Subcontractor - Dispatch List</strong> for configured subcontractor work centers.</li> <li>From routing lines and production order pages, review subcontracting comments, prices, work-in-process entries, related purchase documents, transfer orders and entries, return transfers, and linked components. You can also create subcontracting orders and adjust WIP from supported released production order pages.</li> <li>When you open the obsolete Subcontracting Worksheet in an online environment without the app installed, a notification explains that the app replaces the worksheet. Choose <strong>Install</strong> to get the new experience or <strong>Don't show me again</strong> to dismiss future notifications.</li> <li>When you assign a subcontractor vendor to a work center and the vendor has no <strong>Subc. Location Code</strong>, a notification explains why the location is needed for components and WIP items.</li> <li>Contoso Coffee demonstration data includes <strong>Bulk Assembly</strong> and <strong>Local Assembly</strong> subcontractors, locations, and work centers. The <strong>Airpot - Subc. Mid-Routing</strong> and <strong>Airpot - Subc. Final Op</strong> routings demonstrate intermediate and final subcontracting operations.</li> <li>Standard tasks and detailed work instructions provide more realistic manufacturing examples. Routing operations use different direct costs so that you can compare scenarios without relying on preconfigured subcontractor price records.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573353","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573355","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Use inventory put-aways and picks for subcontracting","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Companies that use basic warehouse configurations can include subcontracting in the same inventory activities they use for other inbound and outbound work. Warehouse employees can process subcontracted output without switching to warehouse receipts, and production teams can move work-in-process items (WIP items) between locations without treating them as physical inventory.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>The activities respect the different accounting and inventory effects of final and intermediate routing operations. They also preserve unit-of-measure conversions, bin information, and item tracking where the subcontracting flow supports those details.</p> <p>You can use inventory put-aways for subcontracting purchase lines at locations that require put-away processing but don't require warehouse receipts. You can also use inventory picks and return put-aways for WIP transfer orders.</p> <p>The posting behavior depends on the source line:</p> <ul> <li>For the final subcontracting operation, posting the inventory put-away records physical production output and the related capacity. Serial and lot tracking assigned to the production order flows to the subcontracting documents and resulting item ledger entries.</li> <li>For an intermediate subcontracting operation, the activity records outside processing without creating physical item or warehouse ledger entries.</li> <li>For a WIP transfer, the inventory activity keeps the displayed transfer quantity while the base quantity remains zero. The transfer therefore represents production progress rather than stocked inventory.</li> </ul> <p>To use an inventory put-away for subcontracted output:</p> <ol> <li>Set up a basic warehouse location that requires put-away processing but doesn't require receive processing.</li> <li>Create and release the production order, calculate subcontracts, and create the subcontracting purchase order.</li> <li>Assign serial or lot numbers from the production or subcontracting document when item tracking is required.</li> <li>On the released purchase order, choose the <strong>Create Inventory Put-away/Pick</strong> action.</li> <li>Open and post the inventory put-away after you record the quantities and bins that warehouse employees handled.</li> </ol> <p>The activities handle partial processing, repeated processing, unit conversions, and split put-away lines across bins. Item tracking isn't supported for WIP item transfers. Some follow-up processes, including receiving subcontracting invoices through <strong>Get Receipt Lines</strong> and specific undo-receipt scenarios, remain restricted.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573355","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573358","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Supply Chain Management - Work more efficiently with manufacturing documents and capacity calendars","desc":"<h2>Business Value</h2> <p>Planners and production managers often move between planning worksheets, production orders, work and machine centers, production BOMs, and routings to complete routine work. Small gaps in page actions, fields, filtering, and error navigation add unnecessary steps and can delay production scheduling.</p> <h2>Details</h2> <p>These improvements place manufacturing information and actions closer to the records where you work. You can create released production orders directly from planning suggestions, monitor and calculate capacity calendars, correct uncertified production definitions from actionable errors, and find relevant manufacturing details with less navigation.</p> <h3>Create released production orders from planning suggestions</h3> <p>On the <strong>Planning Worksheet</strong>, run <strong>Carry Out Action Message</strong> and choose one of the new production order options:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Released</strong> creates released production orders directly from the accepted planning lines.</li> <li><strong>Released &amp; Print</strong> creates released production orders and includes them in production order printing.</li> </ul> <h3>Calculate and monitor capacity calendars</h3> <p>You can run <strong>Calculate Work Center Calendar</strong> from the <strong>Work Center Card</strong> and <strong>Calculate Machine Center Calendar</strong> from the <strong>Machine Center Card</strong>. The reports open for the current center, so you don't need to return to the list page.</p> <p>The <strong>Calendar Entries Available Until</strong> field on Work Center and Machine Center cards and lists shows the latest date for which calendar entries exist. A date earlier than the work date appears in the warning style so that you can identify calendars that need recalculation before scheduling fails.</p> <h3>Resolve uncertified BOM and routing errors</h3> <p>When a production order references a production BOM or routing that isn't certified, the validation error provides a navigation action:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Show Production BOM [number]</strong> opens the affected Production BOM.</li> <li><strong>Show Routing [number]</strong> opens the affected Routing.</li> </ul> <p>Certify the document and retry the operation.</p> <h3>Find and maintain manufacturing information more easily</h3> <p>The following page improvements reduce extra navigation and prevent avoidable errors:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Copy Production Order Document</strong> excludes the current production order from the <strong>Document No.</strong> lookup when the source and destination statuses match.</li> <li><strong>Routing Link Code</strong> is available on <strong>Planning Routing</strong>, <strong>Prod. Order Components</strong>, and <strong>Prod. Order Comp. Line List</strong>.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573358","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573376","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Reverse Sustainability Ledger entries transaction","desc":"<p>Keep your sustainability data accurate by reversing sustainability ledger entries that contain mistakes.</p> <p>If you post sustainability transactions that contain a mistake, you can’t delete the entries. However, if you posted the entries from a sustainability journal or a general journal, what you can do is use the <strong>Reverse Transaction</strong> action on the <strong>Sustainability Ledger Entries</strong> page to reverse them. The reversal creates a new sustainability ledger entry that has the document number and posting date from the original entry. It also records the user who ran the reversal. The original posting date makes the values net to zero in the same period.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573376","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573377","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Track your carbon footprint for fixed assets","desc":"<p>This feature extends sustainability tracking to fixed assets by introducing fields and logic that capture emissions during acquisition, reclassification, and disposal. Emission data flows into the sustainability ledger and integrates with existing sustainability reporting. Validation ensures you can enter emissions only for acquisition transactions. Posting rules maintain data integrity across your fixed asset and sustainability ledgers.</p> <p>Sustainability fields are available only if you enable sustainability features in setup.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573377","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573378","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Track your carbon footprint with item journals and item reclassification journals","desc":"<p>This feature introduces carbon footprint tracking to <strong>Item Journals</strong> and <strong>Item Reclassification Journals</strong>. It adds fields for CO₂e per unit and total CO₂e, and calculates emissions to ensure that emissions follow the same lifecycle logic as item costs.</p> <p>Emissions are calculated based on <strong>Sustainability Value Entries</strong> by using the <strong>Average</strong> or the new <strong>Specific</strong> method. Posting results are recorded in <strong>Sustainability Value Entries</strong> only. There are no changes to item cost entries.</p> <p>For <strong>Item Reclassification Journals</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>Emissions transfer between items without adding new values.</li> <li>Maintains a chain for updates after adjustments.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573378","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573374","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Use formulas to calculate emissions in purchase documents","desc":"<p>This feature introduces formula-based emission calculations on purchase documents and uses the same calculation logic as sustainability journals. It applies emission factors to inputs such as fuel, electricity, distance, or custom amounts.</p> <p>Set up this feature on the <strong>Sustainability Setup</strong> page:</p> <ul> <li>First, turn on the <strong>Use Emissions in Purchase Documents</strong> toggle.</li> <li>Then, turn on the <strong>Use Formulas in Purchase Documents</strong> toggle.</li> <li>When both options are active, additional fields become available on purchase lines.</li> </ul> <p>When you fill in a formula field, Business Central calculates values for <strong>Emission CO₂</strong>, <strong>Emission CH₄</strong>, and <strong>Emission N₂O</strong> using <strong>Emission Factors</strong>.</p> <p>Input validation follows the same rules as sustainability journals, and is based on <strong>Sustainability Account Categories</strong>. If formula fields contain values, manual entry of emissions is blocked. If you enter emissions manually, you can't use formula fields.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573374","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573379","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainability Management - Use specific method for carbon footprint calculation when enabling item tracking","desc":"<p>This feature introduces a new calculation method for carbon footprint tracking in sustainability value entries. In addition to the current <strong>Average</strong> method, you can enable a <strong>Specific</strong> method for items that you track with serial or lot numbers. On the <strong>Item Card</strong> page, on the <strong>Sustainability</strong> FastTab, you can choose one of the following options in the <strong>Carbon Tracking Method</strong> field:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Average</strong> (default) – Use the current behavior for all postings.</li> <li><strong>Specific</strong> – Use the exact emission value for the unit received, similar to specific costing, when you track items by using serial or lot numbers.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573379","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573375","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Sustainabilty Management - Estimate your carbon footprint in Service Management","desc":"<p>This feature extends sustainability tracking to cover <strong>Service Management</strong> features by displaying carbon footprint values on service documents. Emission data comes from sustainability value entries for items and from resource cards for resource-related emissions.</p> <p>When you consume or ship items or resources as part of a service order, the system retrieves their associated CO₂e values from sustainability data.</p> <p>The system shows emission details on service invoices and posted documents for reporting and customer communication. Resource emissions are based on values defined on the resource card. Item emissions come from sustainability setup and item configuration.</p> <p>Calculations follow the same logic as in other sustainability features, ensuring consistency across modules.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573375","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573367","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: User experience - Preview images directly in web client","desc":"<p>You can open image attachments in the Business Central web client without downloading the images first. Files display in preview mode with an easy to use viewer experience that's similar to the print preview or PDF preview features. If you want to save a copy, you can download the image file from the viewer.</p> <p>This feature works across all areas of Business Central, including agents, email, and code from extensions. However, extension developers must add support for this feature using <em>File.ViewFromStream</em> for Business Central online, or <em>File.View</em> for Business Central on-premises. These methods follow the pattern of the <em>File.Download</em> method.</p> <p>Preview images directly supports the following types of image files: JPEG, JPG, PNG, BMP, SVG, WEBP, ICO, plus GIF and AVIF (both include animated versions). On the Safari browser, this feature also supports TIFF and TIF.</p> <p>The following are a couple of additional benefits:</p> <ul> <li>There is suport for GIF files as FactBox thumbnails, including animation for GIFs up to 48 frames.</li> <li>Thumbnail previews are clickable for images and the first page of PDFs, which open the previewer window.</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573367","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573369","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: User experiences - Agent actions review notifications on lists","desc":"<p>Show and manage documents where agents require human interaction by using a new review bar on documents and lists.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573369","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573371","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: User experiences - Show recently searched in Tell Me","desc":"<p>Find pages and reports faster by accessing recent searches in Tell Me (Alt+Q).</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573371","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-573368","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: User experiences - Show recently used in lookups","desc":"<p>Business Central now highlights recently used records directly in lookup dialogs. When users open a lookup, the system surfaces records they have recently accessed or worked with, making it easier to select the correct value without performing a search.</p> <p>The suggestions are personalized to each user and are based on usage signals already collected by the platform. The feature reuses the same server-side intelligence that supports Autofill and recent-record scenarios, ensuring consistent recommendations across Business Central experiences.</p> <p>The feature makes Business Central feel more responsive and personalized by adapting lookup suggestions to each user's working patterns. It reduces repetitive data entry, speeds up transaction processing, and helps users stay focused on their work. By reusing existing server intelligence already powering Autofill experiences, the feature delivers a consistent and efficient way to surface the most relevant records across the application.</p> <p>Business Value:<br> Finding the right record in a lookup is a common task throughout Business Central, but users often select the same customers, vendors, items, projects, or dimensions repeatedly during the day. By showing recently used records at the top of lookup dialogs, users can find and select frequently accessed data faster, with fewer searches and less navigation.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Business Central"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573368","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570641","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Streamline mobile work with an optimized Subgrid control","desc":"<p><strong>Business Value</strong></p> <p>With a Subgrid optimized for mobile, frontline workers will experience click reduction and faster field workflows. Enhancements to the Subgrid control include top‑level Add New and Use/Complete all action buttons, bulk‑add functionality, barcode scanning, and inline editing to speed record management on the go.</p> <p><strong>Feature Details</strong></p> <p>Field Service Mobile is improving the existing Service Task View, Service View, and Product View Subgrid controls to provide a faster, touch-first way for technicians to work with common Field Service scenarios such as Work Order Products, Services, and Service Tasks.</p> <ul> <li>Users can add multiple records in fewer steps using bulk add mutli-select functionality.</li> <li>Users can mark all records as complete/used in one go, saving repetitive, individual clicks per record.</li> <li>Frequently used fields for Subgrid records can be edited inline, reducing the need to open the full record form for common updates.</li> <li>Barcode scanning helps users quickly find and select products instead of scrolling through a long list.</li> </ul> <p>This experience keeps frontline workers in context by returning them directly to the grid after save, reducing navigation, scrolling, and form transitions — allowing them stay focused on their customer work.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-09-10","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570641","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570432","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Self-learning for Copilot Studio Agents","desc":"<p>Soon agents can help makers improve agents using lessons from completed runs. It will identify repeated tool sequences that can be handled by workflows to standardize agent behavior, minimize errors, and most importantly control costs. Makers will be presented with recommendations and supporting evidence, expected impact, and the related instruction and tool changes. Makers accept recommendations, configure, test, and publish a refined copy of the agent. This helps improve agent output quality and controls costs while preserving work that requires model judgment and keeping makers in control.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570432","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-572683","title":"OneDrive: Updated placement of the Create or upload button for Web","desc":"<p>OneDrive for the web is updating the placement of the Create or upload button to provide a more consistent file experience across OneDrive and SharePoint. The button will move from the left navigation pane to the right side of the page, bringing familiar navigation from SharePoint document libraries to OneDrive.</p> <p>The available options for creating files and folders or uploading content will remain unchanged.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=572683","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-422323","title":"OneNote: Summary and Q&A in OneNote Mobile with Copilot (Android)","desc":"<p>With this new Summary feature in OneNote mobile, you can create a short and fluent summary of your longer pages which will help to consume relevant information faster. With the Question and Answer at your fingertips, you can get real-time answers to your queries directly within your notes, enhancing your ability to access and utilize information quickly and effectively.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneNote"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-22","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-422324","title":"OneNote: Summary and Q&A in OneNote Mobile with Copilot (Iphone)","desc":"<p>With this new Summary feature in OneNote mobile, you can create a short and fluent summary of your longer pages which will help to consume relevant information faster. With the Question and Answer at your fingertips, you can get real-time answers to your queries directly within your notes, enhancing your ability to access and utilize information quickly and effectively. We inadvertently marked this item as rolling out and now have updated it to be accurate. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneNote"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-22","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422324","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1309746","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365 Copilot: Copilot chat pane and Summary feature in OneNote Mobile (Android)","desc":"Updated September 30, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft is introducing a new Copilot chat pane in OneNote Mobile (Android) for users licensed with Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium). This update adds a new Summary feature that allows users to generate concise summaries of longer OneNote pages, as well as ask questions about their notes, directly within the OneNote mobile app. This helps users review and interact with note content more efficiently while on the go.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 422323.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out end of October 2026 (previously late September) and expect to complete end of October 2026 (previously mid-October).\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Users with Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) licenses\n• Users accessing OneNote on Android\n• All Microsoft 365 tenants\n\nWhat will happen\n• Users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license will see a Copilot chat pane in the OneNote mobile app on Android:\n•\n• The Copilot chat pane allows users to generate concise summaries of longer OneNote pages and ask questions about their notes:\n•\n• Existing Microsoft 365 Copilot controls, permissions, and policies continue to apply.\n• Users without a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license are not impacted.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No admin action is required before rollout.\n• Ensure that users who should access this feature are assigned a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license.\n• Consider informing helpdesk staff and users about the availability of Copilot chat and the Summary feature in OneNote mobile.\n• Review existing Microsoft 365 Copilot governance, compliance, and usage policies to ensure they align with your organization’s requirements.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. Copilot chat processes OneNote content that users already have access to in order to generate summaries and answer questions, in accordance with existing Microsoft 365 Copilot data handling, permissions, and security controls.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI or ML capabilities that interact with customer data?Yes. This update introduces Copilot chat capabilities within OneNote Mobile, allowing generative AI to analyze note content that the user has permission to access.\nDoes the change provide end users a new way of interacting with generative AI?Yes. Users can interact with generative AI through the Copilot chat pane in OneNote Mobile to summarize content and ask questions about their notes.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1309746","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1307979","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365 Copilot: Copilot chat pane and Summary feature in OneNote Mobile (iPhone)","desc":"Updated September 30, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft is introducing a new Copilot chat pane in OneNote Mobile (iPhone) for users licensed with Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium). This update adds a new Summary feature that allows users to generate concise summaries of longer OneNote pages, as well as ask questions about their notes, directly within the OneNote mobile app. This helps users review and interact with note content more efficiently while on the go.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 422324.\n\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out end of October 2026 (previously late September) and expect to complete end of October 2026 (previously mid-October).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Users with Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) licenses\n• Users accessing OneNote on iPhone\n• All Microsoft 365 tenants\n\nWhat will happen\n• Users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license will see a Copilot chat pane in the OneNote mobile app on iPhone:\n•\n• The Copilot chat pane allows users to generate concise summaries of longer OneNote pages and ask questions about their notes:\n•\n• Existing Microsoft 365 Copilot controls, permissions, and policies continue to apply.\n• Users without a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license are not impacted.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No admin action is required before rollout.\n• Ensure that users who should access this feature are assigned a Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license.\n• Consider informing helpdesk staff and users about the availability of Copilot chat and the Summary feature in OneNote mobile.\n• Review existing Microsoft 365 Copilot governance, compliance, and usage policies to ensure they align with your organization’s requirements.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nQuestion Answer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. Copilot chat processes OneNote content that users already have access to in order to generate summaries and answer questions, in accordance with existing Microsoft 365 Copilot data handling, permissions, and security controls.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI or ML capabilities that interact with customer data? Yes. This update introduces Copilot chat capabilities within OneNote Mobile, allowing generative AI to analyze note content that the user has permission to access.\nDoes the change provide end users a new way of interacting with generative AI? Yes. Users can interact with generative AI through the Copilot chat pane in OneNote Mobile to summarize content and ask questions about their notes.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1307979","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-573311","title":"Dynamics 365 Business Central: Apply line discounts and fees on contract lines","desc":"<p>This feature lets you define discount and fee percentages on a quotation or contract line. When a transaction is generated and approved, the system applies the discount or fee, updates actuals, and applies the amounts during invoicing. A discount reduces the line total, while a fee increases it. Quotation values carry over to contract lines.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573311","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-573383","title":"Dynamics 365 Contact Center: Quality evaluation - Specify who to evaluate in conversations","desc":"<p>Participant evaluated\" lets users choose who to evaluate within a conversation transcript for quality evaluation.Users can select Participant evaluated to choose the scope of the evaluation: Entire record, Current owner, or IVR/Bot.</p> <p>By default, \"Entire record\" evaluates the full conversation transcript, including all participants. Current owner evaluates the current conversation owner, defined as the last conversation owner. IVR/Bot evaluates only the automated IVR or bot portion of the conversation.</p> <p>This option is available when running an on-demand evaluation from both the conversation list view and from the evaluation plan.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573383","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-573381","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Service tools, skills and plugins are now available for Code","desc":"<p>The updated Service application brings Dynamics 365 Customer Service context, actions, and guided workflows into Code. Customer service teams can work with service information and take supported actions in the flow of work, reducing the need to switch to Dynamics 365.</p> <p>First-party tools delivered through the Service package on Dynamics 365 MCP respect Dynamics 365 business logic and the user's existing permissions on each call. The package provides a governed foundation for the supported tools and skills in Code.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573381","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571678","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Service tools, skills and plugins are now available for Cowork, Code and Scout","desc":"<p>The updated Service application brings Dynamics 365 Customer Service context, actions, and guided workflows into supported Copilot experiences, including Chat, Cowork, Code, and Scout. Customer service teams can work with service information and take supported actions in the flow of work, reducing the need to switch to Dynamics 365.</p> <p>First-party tools delivered through the Service package on Dynamics 365 MCP respect Dynamics 365 business logic and the user's existing permissions on each call. The package provides a governed foundation for the supported tools and skills. Availability is tracked separately for each experience.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571678","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-573382","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Service tools, skills and plugins are now available for Scout","desc":"<p>The updated Service application brings Dynamics 365 Customer Service context, actions, and guided workflows into Scout. Customer service teams can work with service information and take supported actions in the flow of work, reducing the need to switch to Dynamics 365.</p> <p>First-party tools delivered through the Service package on Dynamics 365 MCP respect Dynamics 365 business logic and the user's existing permissions on each call. The package provides a governed foundation for the supported tools and skills in Scout.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573382","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-573373","title":"Dynamics 365 Sales: Sales tools, skills and plugin are now available in Copilot Cowork","desc":"<p>The updated Sales plugin brings expanded Dynamics 365 Sales context, actions, and guided workflows to Copilot Cowork, building on the native Sales skills already available in Cowork. Sellers can work with sales data and take supported actions directly in the flow of work, reducing the need to switch to Dynamics 365 Sales.</p> <p>The native Sales skills invoke tools published through the Dynamics 365 MCP server to retrieve sales context and perform supported actions in Dynamics 365 Sales. These native Sales skills are included in the Sales plugin, which will be delivered through the updated MOS package for the Sales app, providing administrators with a governed way to deploy and manage the capabilities.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Sales"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-09-30","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=573373","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568933","title":"Microsoft Teams: Use Copilot Chat after a call in Queues app","desc":"<p>After a recorded call is completed, use Copilot in the Queues app to quickly catch up on key details, uncover insights, and resolve customer issues faster without having to manually search through a transcript or listen back to a recording. Navigate to the unified call history in the Queues app, select the recorded call record, and launch the Copilot Chat sidecar from within the Recap tab. You can then ask Copilot to generate a summary or answer questions about specific details related to the call.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-06","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568933","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568367","title":"Outlook: Drag and Drop","desc":"<p>You can now reschedule events by dragging them to a new time slot in your calendar. This feature is available in day and multi day views.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568367","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-568760","title":"Outlook: Filter Messages by Events","desc":"<p>You can now filter your messages for calendar invitations. Simply go to the filter and select Events from the drop down.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568760","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-557347","title":"Outlook: Follow meetings in Outlook mobile","desc":"<p>If you're unable to attend a meeting, you can select Follow as your response to help you stay informed of the meeting events. Following a meeting reminds the organizer to record the meeting and alert you to any follow-up items.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557347","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559794","title":"Outlook: Keep Invitations After Responding in Outlook Mobile","desc":"<p>You can now control whether meeting invitations are automatically removed from your inbox after you RSVP. Simply to go to settings, calendar, and turn off or on \"Delete Invite After RSVP.\"</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-559795","title":"Outlook: Work week view for Outlook iOS and iPad","desc":"<p>You can now use a work week calendar view on iOS and iPad to focus on the days you work. On iPad, you can select \"work week\" directly from the view picker. On iOS, you can select work week from the view picker when you rotate your device to landscape. You can choose which days are included in your work week by syncing from your default account or by customizing the days just for your device.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559795","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-543427","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Auto-Archive for Exchange Online","desc":"<p>A new capability called Auto-Archiving for Exchange Online will enter public preview in November 2025 (currently under private preview for selected customers). When a user's mailbox utilization exceeds 95% of its quota and archive mailbox is present, this feature automatically moves the oldest items excluding those tagged with “Never Move to Archive” from the primary mailbox to the archive mailbox to prevent mail flow disruptions by keeping usage below the safe threshold of 95% of mailbox quota.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-23","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543427","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-491017","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: DLP Policy Tip Support in Outlook Mobile","desc":"<p>DLP policy tip support for Outlook Mobile enhances data loss prevention measures on mobile devices by providing real-time alerts to help users avoid accidentally sharing sensitive information, ensuring compliance with organizational policies.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-28","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491017","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526791","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Show remote machine information on File Copy to Remote Desktop","desc":"<p>Admin should be able to see destination machine information when end-user copy a sensitive file to a remote machine through RDP.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-560600","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Policy Recommendation Panel in IRM","desc":"<p>Today, Insider Risk Management (IRM) provides policy-driven protection for data leaks, data theft, and risky AI usage. However, while policy-driven protections are powerful, customers may not always have clear visibility into where coverage can be optimized or expanded to address latent insider risk.</p> <p>IRM now provides guidance on what protections are missing or which policy configurations deliver the most incremental value, providing customers with more comprehensive coverage to mitigate their most critical insider risk.</p> <p>Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-28","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560600","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-565869","title":"Microsoft Teams: Personal message reminders for chat and channels","desc":"<p>Teams now lets you set and manage reminders directly on chat and channel messages, helping you keep track of important items. Create, update, complete, and delete reminders, track them in a dedicated Reminders view, and receive timely notifications when they become due. Reminders are private to each user and include message context, making them easy to revisit and act on when needed.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565869","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570853","title":"Work IQ: Custom agents + 3P calls","desc":"<p>Enable Work IQ to invoke custom agents and agents that call supported third-party tools.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-29","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570853","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570854","title":"Work IQ: ExpandedContextIQ","desc":"<p>Expand Context IQ so users can discover and select additional agents, skills, and content sources while composing prompts.</p>","products":["Work IQ","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-29","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570854","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569425","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft M365): Delegated prompt publishing for organization prompts","desc":"<p>This release follows the availability of organization prompts, providing admins the ability to upload custom prompts for their organization in the Copilot app home screen. Now, admins can delegate organization prompt publishing to users, AAD security groups, and distribution groups. These delegated users and groups will be able to create, edit and delete organization prompts at the tenant level through the Prompt Lab, without having to access the Microsoft 365 Admin Center. Admins can continue to monitor and provide oversight through the current experience in the Microsoft 365 Admin Center.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-18","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569425","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571880","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Discover & Add Skills from the skill catalog","desc":"<p>With the Skills catalog in Copilot Studio, makers can discover, reuse and selectively share approved organizational skills instead of recreating the same instructions and workflows for every agent. The shared catalog powered by Microsoft 365 App Store enables shared skills to extend across experiences such as Copilot Studio M365 copilot, and Cowork, helping organizations standardize proven ways of working while maintaining centralized governance.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-29","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571880","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568075","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Data Security for non-Microsoft connected apps","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention and Information Protection Auto-labeling capabilities now extend to non-Microsoft connected apps (e.g., Google Workspace, Box, Dropbox, Salesforce, ServiceNow, Amazon Web Services, and Cisco Webex). The conditions and actions supported for each of these applications vary.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-21","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568075","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567121","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 admin center - Usage reports - Copilot Chat for GCC, GCC High and DoD","desc":"<p>We will be introducing a new Usage report covering Copilot Chat. This report will include total active users, Copilot Chat usage with a breakout per Microsoft 365 app, and user-level activity insights (anonymized by default). #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-06","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567121","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-554937","title":"Microsoft 365: Change Meeting Organizer via PowerShell Cmdlet in Exchange Online","desc":"<p>Allows the administrator of an Exchange Online tenant to change the organizer of an existing meeting or meeting series via a PowerShell cmdlet. This can be used, for example, to maintain continuity and history of a long-running meeting series in cases where the meeting organizer has a new role, is on leave, or during the offboarding process. Once the meeting is transferred, the new organizer will be able to maintain all properties of the event including meeting time and recurrence, attendees, and description. Meeting attendees within the Exchange Online tenant will not need to re-RSVP and the existing event on their calendar will be silently updated with the new meeting organizer information.</p> <p>A subsequent feature will enable users to to change the organizer via Modern Calendar in OWA, New Outlook, and Teams. For user-initiated transfers the new organizer must accept the meeting before the transfer completes.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554937","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-543422","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Excel Agent","desc":"<p>Excel Agent helps you turn data into clear charts, summaries, and insights using built‑in formulas and logic. It streamlines data preparation, formulas, and visualization so you can stay focused on the story behind the numbers. Use multi‑turn chat to refine your output or open it in Excel for full editing and collaboration. Ideal for financial forecasts, project plans, and decision‑making tools. Available to Microsoft 365 users with or without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.</p>","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543422","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-502858","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Live subtitles on voice chat in Copilot when using the quick composer","desc":"<p>Live subtitles for voice chats in Copilot will be available for users to help them follow the conversation when using the quick composer.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-30","modified":"2026-09-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-499076","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Information Protection- Scan existing files in SharePoint and OneDrive for business for sensitive information","desc":"<p>This new capability will enable admins to scan existing files at rest in SharePoint or OneDrive for business for sensitive data.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-24","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499076","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-570963","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Copilot video creation updates","desc":"<p>Copilot brings agentic video creation to Clipchamp Video Hub. Users can generate, edit, and refine videos from prompts—grounded in explicit documents or implicit WorkIQ knowledge. Preview and playback video directly in chat, then continue iterating towards a finished video.</p>","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570963","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570857","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Track costs for non-billable field work","desc":"<p>Organizations often use the same field teams for both customer work and internal operational work, such as maintenance, inspections, or asset-related activities that are not billed to an external customer. These scenarios still require scheduling, technician execution, and accurate tracking of the labor, materials, and other costs associated with the work.</p> <p>With this capability, Field Service Work Orders can be connected to a project that serves as the financial container for the work. Technicians continue to plan and execute through Field Service, while supported labor, material, expense, and other costs are captured against that project for centralized cost tracking.</p> <p>This gives organizations a consistent way to manage non-billable field work and understand its total cost without requiring a customer contract simply to connect the Work Order to a project.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-386901","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Sensitivity label grouping modernization","desc":"<p>To help improve label usability and configuration, the sensitivity labeling scheme will be simplified to only consist of labels and label groupings. These new label groupings allow admins to better organize and categorize their labels (previously done via parent labels).</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-03-14","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=386901","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571309","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Auto-labeling scale increase for SharePoint and OneDrive","desc":"<p>We are increasing the maximum auto-labeling capacity for SharePoint and OneDrive from 100,000 up to 500,000 files per tenant per day. This helps organizations label and protect more of their data at rest, faster, closing labeling gaps across existing content. With sensitivity labels and protection settings applied to more files sooner, organizations can better prepare their data estate for Microsoft 365 Copilot with greater confidence.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571309","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569608","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enable agents for existing applications in your organization","desc":"<p>For third-party applications already being used in your organization, admins can now discover and enable the corresponding Teams agents from within the Teams Admin Center. Admins receive recommendations for high-value agents and gain visibility into any required configuration changes during the enablement workflow. These agents increase employee productivity by bringing their everyday applications into the flow of work in Teams. This helps organizations get more value from their existing software investments and unlocks more surfaces for the tools their users already rely on.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-28","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569608","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571879","title":"Microsoft Teams: Granular Conditional Access for Teams meetings","desc":"<p>Granular Conditional Access for Teams meetings gives organizations greater control over access to sensitive meetings. Administrators can apply Conditional Access policies to selected meetings, helping ensure participants meet organizational security requirements before joining.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571879","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570962","title":"Microsoft Teams: Multi-line call history tabs in the Calls app","desc":"<p>Multi-line users get a redesigned call history experience that organizes activity by phone line. Call activity is organized into dedicated tabs for each line, so history, voicemails, and recordings appear under the line they belong to, making navigation and call management simpler and more intuitive.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570962","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-498923","title":"Viva Glint - Action Taking Report (Public Preview)","desc":"<p>Introduction of a new report that provides transparency into platform activity by dashboard users. Metrics such as report views, Team Conversations completed, and Focus Areas created will be visible and filterable with this report.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-24","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498923","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571308","title":"OneDrive: Prompt gallery for Copilot","desc":"<p>Discover easier ways to use Copilot in OneDrive<br> The new Prompt Gallery offers ready-to-use prompts for common file tasks, helping you get started quickly, discover what Copilot can do, and customize prompts to fit your needs.</p> <p>Access the Prompt Gallery from:</p> <p>The Copilot button in the bottom-right corner of OneDrive<br> The + button in the Copilot chat pane<br> Select Open Prompt Gallery to explore prompts across categories such as Create, Analyze, Find, and Collaborate.</p>","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-28","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571308","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567007","title":"Outlook: New Copilot entry point in Classic Outlook","desc":"<p>We've introduced a new experience for Copilot in the apps—a consistent entry point across apps that sits above your work and understands the context beneath it. Rather than scattering touchpoints across the interface, it anchors Copilot as one connected system across Microsoft 365, surfacing relevant actions that help you stay in flow. With this release, we are rolling out this new experience - already available across other Outlook endpoints, as well as in Word, Excel and PowerPoint - to classic Outlook.</p>","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-22","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567007","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569363","title":"Microsoft Purview: Permissions audit log improvements","desc":"<p>Improving permission checks when users access the Microsoft Purview portal. Enhanced audit logs will provide clearer visibility into role and scoped-role access decisions, helping administrators troubleshoot access issues and monitor authorization outcomes.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569363","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-565425","title":"Microsoft Teams: Language selection by users in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>Users can now choose their preferred meeting language in Teams Rooms on Android. Select from up to 69 languages using the language button on the console. The room system must restart after a language is selected.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565425","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-409534","title":"Microsoft Teams: Local PTZ for Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows will provide native Pan-Tilt-Zoom (PTZ) controls for connected cameras that support this capability, whether the camera moves a physical lens or adjusts the image digitally. Controls are available when Teams Rooms can confirm the camera isn't independently framing the room.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-07-26","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=409534","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567895","title":"OneNote: Multimodal capture in Copilot Notebooks (Android)","desc":"<p>Multimodal capture enables users to transcribe audio, take images, and type notes in a single session. Copilot then creates a structured Copilot Page with insights and user-captured content, saved to a user-selected Copilot Notebook. Designed for capturing offline work moments—including in-person conversations, whiteboard sessions, and personal notes. This capability is already generally available on OneNote for iPhone and iPad.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-20","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567895","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568792","title":"Planner: Refreshed experience and new capabilities","desc":"<p>Microsoft Planner will be updated with a cleaner, more modern interface, improved navigation, responsive layouts, and a more consistent experience across Planner in Teams and Planner for the web. This update also introduces Goals in basic plans.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-05","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568792","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568791","title":"Planner: Refreshed experience and new capabilities","desc":"<p>Microsoft Planner will be updated with a cleaner, more modern interface, improved navigation, responsive layouts, and a more consistent experience across Planner in Teams and Planner for the web. This update also introduces Goals in basic plans.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571672","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Expand your service offering through subcontractors without the onboarding overhead","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Subcontractors commonly communicate completion through an emailed service report or a message describing the work performed. Dispatchers then have to find the correct assignment, interpret the report, update the booking and work order, and copy important closeout details into Field Service. This manual process delays operational visibility, creates inconsistent service history, and can leave completed bookings or work orders open.</p> <p>Service teams can setup an agent to process subcontractor service reports to prepare a coordinated booking and work-order closeout. This supports faster reconciliation of external work and helps keep scheduling status, operational records, and service history consistent.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>An agent in Dynamics 365 Field Service processes supported emails and service reports, identifies the applicable Field Service work order and active booking, and prepares a coordinated closeout proposal.</p> <p>The proposal can include supported booking and work-order status changes together with completion details extracted from the submission, such as the completion summary, work performed, notes, recommendations, requirements, requested follow-up, actual completion information, and supported labor-duration values.</p> <p>An internal dispatcher or service coordinator reviews the source submission and the proposed values, corrects or selects the supported changes as allowed, and applies them to Field Service. Coordinating the booking and work-order changes keeps scheduling records, operational status, and service history aligned.</p> <p>If the sender is not authorized, the work cannot be matched confidently, multiple bookings could apply, required information is missing, or the message contains no actionable closeout information, the submission is routed for human resolution rather than being silently applied.</p> <p>This feature closes out existing supported bookings and work orders. It does not create new follow-up work, process payroll or invoices, or automatically create parts and product-consumption records unless those capabilities are delivered separately.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571672","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564969","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced IntelliFrame with AI data channel for intelligent cameras","desc":"<p>Teams Rooms on Windows users can now benefit from next generation IntelliFrame features on certified AI-capable cameras with on-device video processing. With IntelliFrame’s expanded AI data channel, participants experience faster active speaker framing, people recognition and labels, and more responsive meeting views—even when network conditions are limited. These capabilities are available with Teams Rooms Pro.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-17","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564969","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-570862","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Support multiple payers across Work Order lines","desc":"<p>Field work does not always have a single payer. A customer may be responsible for the primary service while another party, such as a warranty provider, manufacturer, partner, or other eligible billing customer, is responsible for specific products or services performed during the same visit.</p> <p>This capability gives service teams more flexibility during execution by allowing the billing responsibility to be determined at the individual Work Order line level rather than just requiring every transaction on the Work Order to follow the same payer.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-25","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570862","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570858","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Support multiple warehouse assignments for field technicians","desc":"<p>Field technicians often source parts from more than one warehouse. Limiting a technician to a single warehouse can make it harder to reflect how materials are actually sourced across field operations.</p> <p>With this capability, administrators can assign multiple warehouses to a Bookable Resource and designate a preferred/default warehouse for the applicable legal entity. When a technician records material consumption, the warehouse can be automatically populated based on the Work Order legal entity and the technician’s configured default warehouse for that legal entity, while still allowing the technician to select another applicable warehouse when needed.</p> <p>This reduces manual selection for technicians, helps ensure materials are recorded against the correct warehouse and legal entity, and gives organizations more flexibility to reflect how inventory is actually managed across field operations.</p> <p>This capability is supported in the Integrated deployment type with Project Operations, where Field Service works with Finance and Supply Chain Management through Dual-write.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570967","title":"Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration: Maker Guidelines","desc":"<p>The Maker guidelines feature gives organizations a direct way to share guidance with Copilot Studio makers in the flow of work. Administrators can explain which tools, models, connectors, and channels are approved for an environment and point makers to the right policy, request process, or support contact.</p> <p>The message appears in the Review pane alongside the agent's blockers and warnings and remains available when the agent has no issues. This gives makers a consistent place to understand organizational expectations and find help without leaving Copilot Studio.</p>","products":["Microsoft Power Platform governance and administration"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-25","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570967","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-502520","title":"Microsoft Teams: New sharing panel in meetings - improved content discovery and ease of sharing","desc":"<p>The sharing panel in today’s meetings is the default place for content discoverability and sharing. New sharing panel UI is crafted with intent of modernising and simplifying default tasks such as window sharing, but also for easier discovery of sharing options and more discoverable file sharing.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-29","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502520","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568781","title":"Microsoft Teams: Proximity join support for attendees in Teams events from Teams Rooms on Windows and Android","desc":"<p>Attendees can take advantage of proximity join with Teams Rooms on Windows and/or Android for fast, effortless connection to nearby room systems during Teams events, such as town halls, webinars, and structured meetings.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568781","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-554934","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat in Outlook expands to reason over inbox, calendar, and enterprise data","desc":"<p>Copilot Chat in Outlook expanding to support reasoning over a user's entire inbox, calendar and other enterprise data for Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat users (without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license) .</p>","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554934","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-499423","title":"Microsoft Edge: Ground Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in Edge for Business in your open OneDrive and SharePoint documents","desc":"<p>Get relevant answers and insights about your open cloud documents in Copilot Chat in Edge.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-01","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570436","title":"PowerPoint: Async Notifications for Copilot in PowerPoint","desc":"<p>Enable users to leave PowerPoint, switch devices, go offline, or end their workday while remaining confident that Copilot will notify them when work is complete or requires attention.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-25","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570436","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1187682","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Edge: Microsoft 365 Copilot will support summarization and contextual grounding","desc":"Updated September 25, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction:]\nMicrosoft Edge for Business will soon support summarization and contextual grounding with Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat. This enhancement enables users to ask Copilot questions about multiple open browser tabs, Microsoft 365 documents (such as Word, Excel, PowerPoint), and YouTube videos directly from the Edge side pane.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 496364, 499423, and 499424.\n[When this will happen:]\n• General Availability (Multiple browser tabs and YouTube videos): Currently Available\n• General Availability (Microsoft 365 documents): Rollout is expected to begin mid-October 2026 (previously mid-September)\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected: Users signed in to Microsoft Edge for Business with their Entra ID and who have access to Microsoft 365 Copilot.\nWhat will happen:\n• Users will be able to ask Copilot questions about open browser tabs, Microsoft 365 documents, and YouTube videos.\n• The feature will be off by default.\n• If Copilot is restricted from accessing page content via Data Loss Prevention (DLP) or the EdgeEntraCopilotPageContext policy, it will be suppressed to maintain DLP integrity.\n• Existing DLP and policy configurations will be respected.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• This rollout will happen automatically by the specified date; no admin action is required before rollout.\n• Ensure users who need this capability have access to Microsoft 365 Copilot.\n• Ensure your tenant is configured to support Microsoft 365 Copilot and that eligible users meet all licensing prerequisites, including Entra ID sign-in and applicable Microsoft 365 service plans.\n• Review your current DLP and Edge policy configurations to determine potential impact.\n• Notify users about this upcoming capability.\n• Update internal documentation if needed.\n\nLearn more:\n• Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in Edge and Access to Page Content | Microsoft Edge | Microsoft Learn\n• Microsoft Edge - Policies | Microsoft Edge | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. Microsoft 365 Copilot introduces contextual grounding and summarization using generative AI across browser tabs, Microsoft 365 documents, and YouTube videos.\nDoes the change provide end users any new way of interacting with generative AI?Yes. Users can now ask Copilot questions about open browser tabs and documents directly from the Edge sidepane, enabling real-time summarization and contextual responses.\nDoes the change modify Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies or enforcement?Yes. If DLP or the EdgeEntraCopilotPageContext policy restricts access, Copilot will be suppressed from accessing page content to maintain DLP integrity.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Yes. Admins can manage access to Copilot’s contextual grounding capabilities via DLP settings and Edge policy configurations, which can be scoped using Entra ID group membership.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1187682","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-501451","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot in SharePoint","desc":"<p>Simplifies SharePoint content management and ensures content is Copilot-ready by automating metadata, fixing stale content, enabling fast page creation, improving compliance, and enriching content so Copilot can deliver more accurate, grounded answers. Updated April 16: We are still in development for GA and have launched to Preview only.</p>","products":["SharePoint","SharePoint Syntex","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501451","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-516577","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Planner capabilities in Copilot chat (M365 Copilot)","desc":"<p>We will support creating Planner tasks and plans querying Planner information in M365 Copilot chat, allowing users to manage their tasks and plans between Copilot and Planner seamlessly.</p>","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-09-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516577","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571673","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Close out bookings and work orders from subcontractor service reports","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Subcontractors commonly communicate completion through an emailed service report or a message describing the work performed. Dispatchers then have to find the correct assignment, interpret the report, update the booking and work order, and copy important closeout details into Field Service. This manual process delays operational visibility, creates inconsistent service history, and can leave completed bookings or work orders open.</p> <p>Using the subcontractor's service report to prepare the complete closeout gives service teams a faster and more consistent way to reconcile external work. Booking state, work-order status, and the details of the completed visit can be reviewed together before the internal records are updated.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>The Subcontractor Agent processes a supported email and service report, identifies the applicable Field Service work order and active booking, and prepares a coordinated closeout proposal.</p> <p>The proposal can include supported booking and work-order status changes together with completion details extracted from the submission, such as the completion summary, work performed, notes, recommendations, requirements, requested follow-up, actual completion information, and supported labor-duration values.</p> <p>An internal dispatcher or service coordinator reviews the source submission and the proposed values, corrects or selects the supported changes as allowed, and deliberately applies them to Field Service. Coordinating the booking and work-order changes keeps scheduling records, operational status, and service history aligned.</p> <p>If the sender is not authorized, the work cannot be matched confidently, multiple bookings could apply, required information is missing, or the message contains no actionable closeout information, the submission is routed for human resolution rather than being silently applied.</p> <p>This feature closes out existing supported bookings and work orders. It does not create new follow-up work, process payroll or invoices, or automatically create parts and product-consumption records unless those capabilities are delivered separately.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571673","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571664","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Create and apply reusable maintenance plans to assets","desc":"<p><strong>Business value</strong></p> <p>Organizations can define a consistent maintenance strategy once and use it across groups of similar assets instead of designing a separate plan for every asset. This reduces setup effort, limits configuration differences across locations and teams, and provides a repeatable way to bring growing asset populations under managed maintenance.</p> <p>Reusable templates also make maintenance standards easier to govern. Asset and service leaders can establish the expected maintenance program for an equipment type while allowing each asset to have the plan it needs for ongoing execution.</p> <p><strong>Feature detail</strong></p> <p>Create maintenance plan templates that describe the maintenance program for an asset model, manufacturer, product, SKU, or asset category. A template brings together the maintenance activities and scheduling rules that should apply to that type of equipment.</p> <p>Use a template to establish a maintenance plan for one or more eligible customer assets. The resulting asset maintenance plan provides the asset-specific context used to schedule activities, forecast maintenance, and generate future work.</p> <p>The template and assignment experience helps users identify the appropriate standard for an asset and consistently establish maintenance coverage without rebuilding the complete maintenance definition each time.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571664","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571671","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Onboard mid-lifecycle assets into maintenance plans","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Organizations often introduce maintenance management after equipment is already operating or acquire used assets with established age, usage, and service histories. Starting those assets at the beginning of a new maintenance plan produces irrelevant past activities and inaccurate future dates, while manually reconstructing every historical event requires significant effort.</p> <p>Mid-lifecycle onboarding allows existing assets to enter a standardized maintenance program at an appropriate point, helping organizations expand maintenance coverage without treating every asset as newly commissioned.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>Apply a reusable maintenance plan template to an existing or used asset and initialize the resulting plan using the asset's current lifecycle information. Relevant inputs can include commissioning or installation date, current meter usage, known maintenance history, and the appropriate position in a sequential maintenance program.</p> <p>Advance through earlier template activities that no longer apply so the asset begins with the next relevant maintenance requirement. Preserve the context used during initialization so planners can understand how the starting position was determined.</p> <p>After initialization, the asset participates in the same scheduling, forecasting, work-order generation, completion feedback, and coverage experiences as other assets using the maintenance plan.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571671","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571674","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Process subcontractor photos, completion documents, and inspection results","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Subcontractors often document completed work through photos, service reports, inspection forms, certificates, and other files. When those documents remain only in a shared mailbox, service teams must manually download, interpret, organize, and reconnect them with the work they support. Important completion evidence and inspection findings can be difficult to find when a customer, dispatcher, auditor, or future technician needs them.</p> <p>Processing subcontractor completion documents as part of the closeout keeps evidence and supported findings connected to the Field Service work. This improves traceability, reduces document-handling effort, and preserves a more complete operational history.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>The Subcontractor Agent processes supported attachments received with a subcontractor submission, including photos, PDFs, service reports, inspection documents, and other supported completion files. It associates those files with the relevant Field Service work so authorized users can find the evidence from the operational record rather than searching the mailbox.</p> <p>The agent can use supported document content when preparing the closeout proposal. For an inspection or task-completion document, this can include extracting supported inspection findings, outcomes, observations, deficiencies, or task results for the internal reviewer to validate and apply to the appropriate Field Service record.</p> <p>The review experience keeps the original document available alongside the proposed structured information so the dispatcher, service coordinator, or other authorized reviewer can compare the extraction with the source. Unsupported, unreadable, encrypted, oversized, or potentially unsafe files are surfaced for appropriate handling instead of being represented as successfully processed.</p> <p>Processing an invoice, parts list, or other financial or consumption document does not by itself create, match, approve, or post a financial transaction or product-consumption record unless that behavior is separately supported.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571674","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571670","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Review and visualize an asset's maintenance schedules","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>An asset can have several lines of service, each with its own maintenance schedule, recurrence pattern, and future events. When those schedules are reviewed separately, planners have difficulty understanding the asset's complete maintenance plan and how the different service requirements will play out together.</p> <p>A consolidated list and visual timeline give maintenance teams one place to understand the asset's planned service, investigate individual events, and identify schedules or timing that should be adjusted. This visibility supports faster, more informed planning without requiring teams to reconstruct the plan from separate records.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>From an asset's maintenance plan, view all maintenance schedules for that asset in one place. Review each line of service and the schedule that controls when its maintenance activities become due, including calendar-based, usage-based, combined time-and-usage, and sequential criteria.</p> <p>Visualize how those schedules are expected to play out over time. The visualization brings the projected maintenance events from the asset's schedules into a chronological view so users can see how the different service lines relate to one another and when maintenance is expected.</p> <p>Users can select and investigate an individual maintenance event to understand the service activity, schedule, trigger, and expected timing behind it. They can then return to the relevant schedule when its criteria, recurrence, sequence, or timing needs to be changed.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571670","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571157","title":"Microsoft Purview: DSPM-Copilot Readiness and Data Explorer","desc":"<p>We’re introducing the new readiness for Microsoft Copilot and data explorer experiences in Microsoft Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM). These new capabilities provide data security teams with greater visibility into their organization’s data security posture and help them assess risks, investigate findings, and prioritize remediation.</p> <p>The readiness for Microsoft Copilot experience in Purview DSPM helps organizations assess and improve their data readiness for Microsoft Copilot. It brings together insights into sensitive data exposure, oversharing, and protection coverage, helping security teams identify risks and assess progress toward a more secure Microsoft Copilot deployment.</p> <p>The new data explorer experience in Purview DSPM provides a centralized investigation experience that helps organizations understand where sensitive data exists across sites, review site-level access, and explore relevant data through preset views. It brings together sites, sensitive data, and preset views, to support more efficient investigations and reduce context switching.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571157","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570859","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Enhanced visibility into work order financial performance","desc":"<p>The new Work Order Cost Summary gives field teams a clearer view of how project-related work is performing by bringing estimated and actual costs, sales, and project task progress together in one place. Teams can quickly compare what was planned with what was actually delivered across products, services, and expenses.</p> <p>When the Work Order is associated with a Project Task, the summary also shows planned and completed task effort, allowing users to review financial performance and execution progress together.</p> <p>The summary recalculates automatically as the Work Order moves through key execution statuses, including Scheduled, In Progress, and Completed. Users can also select Refresh Totals at any time to recalculate the summary and review the latest Work Order and project values.</p> <p>By bringing Field Service execution data together with Project Operations financial and task information directly on the Work Order, teams can identify cost and execution variances earlier, make more informed decisions while work is in progress, and reduce the need to manually reconcile information across applications.</p> <p>This feature is available when the Field Service and Project Operations integration is enabled.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-560700","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI-powered notes for in-person meetings with Facilitator in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>In addition to capturing real-time notes and meeting outcomes during scheduled or hybrid meetings, the Facilitator agent assists you with notes, decisions and actions for in-person meetings in Teams Rooms on Android. Simply invite Facilitator with one tap of the room console. Meeting notes appear on the front of room display or touch board, are available via meeting recap when shared, and deleted if no one selected. Rest assured no data remains in the room. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560700","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571388","title":"Microsoft Teams: Schedule Channel Meetings from Outlook Calendar","desc":"<p>Users will be able to schedule Microsoft Teams channel meetings directly from Outlook Calendar. This streamlines meeting creation and helps keep discussions and meeting content connected in the appropriate channel.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-17","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571388","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571389","title":"Microsoft Teams: Schedule Teams Channel Meeting from Win32","desc":"<p>Users can now schedule Teams Channel Meetings from Win32 (Outlook classic client)</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-16","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571389","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-566322","title":"OneNote: Multimodal capture in Copilot Notebooks (Windows)","desc":"<p>Capture on Windows helps you bring conversations and ideas from meetings, brainstorming sessions, and everyday work into Copilot Notebooks. Capture audio, images, and notes in one experience, then let Copilot turn them into structured notes with key insights, decisions, and action items, in a Copilot Notebook of your choice</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566322","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571683","title":"Outlook: Insert Symbol","desc":"<p>You can insert a variety of symbols into an email message while composing it. To add a symbol, go to the Insert tab and select Symbols.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-24","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571683","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1307888","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: AI-powered notes for in-person meetings with Facilitator in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"Updated September 24, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo support more effective in-person collaboration, Microsoft Teams is expanding AI-powered meeting notes with the Facilitator agent to Teams Rooms on Android. This enhancement allows teams meeting in a physical room to capture real-time notes, decisions, and action items—without requiring a scheduled or hybrid meeting. The experience is designed to ensure notes are securely stored in your tenant while no data remains on the room device after the meeting ends.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 56700.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability\n• Worldwide and GCC: We will begin rolling out in early November 2026 (previously late October) expect to complete by early December 2026 (previously mid-November).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizations using Teams Rooms on Android\n• Rooms licensed with Teams Rooms Pro\n\nWhat will happen\n• During an in-person meeting, users can start AI-powered notes by selecting the Take notes button on the Teams Rooms console.\n• Notes appear on the front-of-room display or touch board during the meeting:\n•\n• Notes are stored in tenant-owned SharePoint embedded storage.\n• Access to notes requires adding your work account using the Access notes button on the Teams Rooms console.\n•\n• After the meeting, notes can be viewed and edited by participants with access via the meeting recap in the meeting chat on the Teams desktop client.\n•\n• If no participant was added during the note-taking session via Access notes, notes are deleted automatically.\n\nDefault state:\n• The feature is available automatically once licensing and prerequisite configurations are met.\n• No additional admin enablement is required beyond existing settings.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo immediate action is required if your organization already meets the prerequisites.\nTo prepare:\n• Confirm Teams Rooms Pro licenses are assigned to applicable rooms.\n• Ensure Facilitator is enabled in your tenant.\n• Verify Loop components are enabled:• IsLoopEnabled\n• IsCollabMeetingNotesFluidEnabled\n\n• Ensure meeting transcription is enabled in Teams meeting policies.\n• Consider notifying helpdesk staff and users about:• How to start notes in an in-person meeting\n• Where notes are stored and accessed after the meeting\n\nLearn more:\n• Allow Facilitator in the Teams admin center - Set up Facilitator in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n• Meetings - Admins- Manage transcription and captions for Teams meetings | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n• Settings management for Loop functionality in Teams - Admin policies for Loop components and Loop workspaces | Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change store new customer data, and if so, where, and is the data cached or permanently stored?Yes. Meeting notes generated by Facilitator are stored in tenant‑owned SharePoint Embedded storage. No meeting data is stored or cached on the Teams Rooms device after the meeting ends.\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed (for example, documents, emails, or chats)?Yes. Meeting audio and transcription data are processed to generate AI‑powered meeting notes, including summaries, decisions, and action items. Access to the notes occurs through the meeting recap in the meeting chat on Teams desktop client.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. The Facilitator agent uses AI to generate real‑time meeting notes, summaries, decisions, and action items based on in‑person meeting content.\nDoes the change provide users a new way of interacting with generative AI, and if so, how?Yes. Users can initiate AI‑generated meeting notes during an in‑person meeting by selecting “Take notes” on the Teams Rooms console.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through tenant configuration?Yes. Availability of the feature depends on existing tenant settings, including Teams Rooms Pro licensing, Facilitator enablement, Loop component settings, and meeting transcription policies.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1307888","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-558547","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – analyze files tied to endpoint DLP alerts","desc":"<p>Speed up analysis of exfiltrated content by launching Data Security Investigations (DSI) from endpoint Data Loss Prevention (DLP) alerts. In DSI, define your endpoint DLP query (for example, time range, users, and endpoints). DSI then automatically gathers the related files that triggered the alerts for review (for example, UserA downloaded a file on 3/1/2026).</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558547","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571667","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Forecast asset usage to predict maintenance due dates","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Usage-based maintenance aligns service with the work an asset has actually performed, but a current meter reading alone does not tell the organization when the next threshold will be reached. Forecasting the asset's expected usage rate converts meter-based maintenance from a reactive trigger into a forward-looking planning signal.</p> <p>Maintenance and reliability teams can use the projected due date to plan labor, parts, capacity, and customer downtime before the threshold is reached. Because the estimate is derived from the individual asset's recent operating history, it reflects real utilization more closely than a generic calendar assumption while remaining explainable and reviewable by planners.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>Calculate a projected usage rate for each asset from the trailing 30-day mean of its historical meter-usage logs. This rate represents the asset's recent pace of operation and drives all projected due dates for usage-based maintenance activities on that asset.</p> <p>For each usage-based maintenance requirement, use the calculated rate to translate the remaining usage before the next threshold into an estimated calendar due date. The configured meter threshold remains the maintenance requirement; the projected date provides the advance planning signal used by maintenance forecasts and lead-window work-order generation.</p> <p>Store the calculated usage rate and the date and time when it was last calculated. Exposing both values lets planners assess how fresh the estimate is and whether the available history is sufficient to rely on the projection.</p> <p>Apply outlier protection when calculating the trailing mean so isolated meter spikes, incorrect readings, or other anomalous input data do not disproportionately change the projected usage rate. Recalculate the rate as additional meter history becomes available so future maintenance predictions continue to reflect the asset's recent usage.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571667","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571668","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Forecast planned maintenance demand","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Maintenance demand often becomes visible to service operations only after work orders are created, leaving limited time to prepare capacity and materials. A forward-looking maintenance forecast gives organizations earlier visibility into expected work so they can anticipate labor, skills, parts, and scheduling demand across the asset population.</p> <p>This supports more proactive operational planning and helps teams identify periods of concentrated demand before they result in resource conflicts, parts shortages, or delayed maintenance.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>Provide a forecast of maintenance events expected within a selected future planning horizon. Bring together events calculated from calendar schedules, actual meter usage, sequential maintenance plans, and projected usage based on meter history.</p> <p>Allow planners to understand when maintenance is expected and which assets, plans, and activities contribute to the forecast. Expected activity duration and other planning information from the maintenance definition can be used to represent the likely operational demand.</p> <p>The forecast provides visibility before work orders are generated. As schedules, meter readings, and usage predictions change, the expected maintenance demand can be refreshed to reflect the latest plan.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571668","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571669","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Optimize asset maintenance schedules using completed service","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Asset maintenance is most effective when service intervals reflect how equipment is actually used and maintained. Static schedules that continue from an assumed date or meter value can cause an organization to service an asset more often than necessary after early maintenance or wait too long after late, partial, or usage-intensive service.</p> <p>Feeding completed maintenance activities, actual completion dates, and meter readings back into the maintenance plan recalibrates future requirements around the asset's real operating and service history. This closed-loop approach helps organizations avoid both over-maintenance and under-maintenance, balancing asset reliability and availability with labor, parts, and service costs.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>Completed maintenance is used as a planning input, not only recorded as service history. When maintenance work is completed, the system evaluates which planned maintenance activities were fulfilled and feeds the actual completion date and relevant meter readings back into the asset's maintenance plan. The plan uses those results as the new basis for calculating the next applicable maintenance requirement.</p> <p>For calendar-based maintenance, the next event is recalculated from the completed service and the plan's recurrence rules. For usage-based maintenance, the next threshold is calculated from the asset's meter value when the activity was completed. For criteria that combine time and usage, the plan continues to evaluate both conditions from the updated maintenance baseline. Sequential plans advance according to the activities that were actually completed.</p> <p>The optimized plan then supplies updated due dates and activities to maintenance coverage views, demand forecasts, and future work-order generation. As additional maintenance is completed, the feedback loop keeps the schedule aligned with the asset's evolving usage and service history.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571669","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571665","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Plan asset maintenance using time, actual usage, and service sequences","desc":"<p>Business value</p> <p>Organizations can maintain assets according to how the equipment ages, how much it is actually used, and which service activities have already been completed. A flexible maintenance schedule helps avoid servicing lightly used equipment too often while reducing the risk that heavily used equipment operates beyond its required maintenance interval.</p> <p>Usage-based schedules connect maintenance directly to meter readings recorded for the individual asset. This allows work to be driven by actual operating hours, mileage, cycles, production counts, or another tracked measure rather than by an estimated calendar interval alone. Combining scheduling methods in one plan supports more consistent execution of manufacturer guidance, internal reliability standards, and contractual maintenance commitments.</p> <p>Feature detail</p> <p>Define maintenance activities against the actual usage of an asset by specifying recurring service intervals on its meter. For example, require an oil change after every 150 operating hours or an inspection after every configured number of miles, cycles, or units produced. As new readings are recorded, the asset's accumulated usage determines when the next maintenance interval is reached.</p> <p>Define other activities using calendar recurrence or combine calendar and usage criteria in one rule. For combined criteria, the plan initiates maintenance when either the elapsed-time threshold or the actual-usage threshold occurs first.</p> <p>Create sequential maintenance programs in which different activities become due at different points in the maintenance cycle. For example, a plan can progress through inspections, minor services, major services, and overhauls rather than repeating the same activity at every interval.</p> <p>The maintenance plan continuously evaluates its configured intervals against the asset's dates, recorded meter usage, and completed maintenance sequence to determine which activity is due next. When the applicable threshold is reached, the plan produces the maintenance requirement that drives downstream work-order generation. This gives planners one place to manage calendar-based, actual-usage-based, whichever-comes-first, and multi-step maintenance strategies.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571665","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571886","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Local inferencing","desc":"<p>Local inferencing expands Microsoft Copilot’s sovereign controls by enabling AI inferencing for supported Copilot interactions to occur within the applicable local geography.</p> <p>Launching in Australia, India, the United Arab Emirates, the United Kingdom, and the United States, this capability gives organizations greater control over where AI inferencing occurs, helping them address sovereignty and regional requirements. Inferencing is the processing step when an AI model executes a prompt to produce an output or response.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571886","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-572677","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Auto-labeling per-policy coverage report","desc":"<p>For each enforced auto-labeling policy, admins can view how files processed during enforcement correlate to the latest simulation run. The per-policy coverage report shows volumes of files that have been labeled or are not yet labeled, and whether those files were included in the last simulation snapshot. This helps admins understand enforcement progress for a specific policy against the data state captured during simulation, while also identifying files that were not found in the simulation snapshot but were processed during enforcement.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=572677","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-566856","title":"Microsoft Teams: Additional health signals available for Teams Rooms on Android on Pro Management Portal","desc":"<p>Expanded Pro Management Portal (PMP) health monitoring for Teams Rooms on Android by surfacing device health signals including storage health, Teams meeting app, calendar sync, secondary display health and network. When issues are detected, PMP will automatically generate actionable alerts and support ticket creation workflows, enabling IT administrators to proactively identify and triage room health issues before they impact meeting experiences.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569018","title":"PowerPoint: Skills in Brand Kit","desc":"<p>Upload skill (.md file) in Brand Kit and use within PPT Copilot</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-23","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569018","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1317197","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: A refreshed in-meeting experience with simpler controls and a smarter share panel","desc":"Updated September 23, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[What and Why]\nAs Microsoft Teams has added meeting capabilities over time, the meeting controls and share panel have grown crowded, contributing to mis-clicks between high‑impact actions like Share, Leave, and Raise hand, and to accidental shares of unintended content. Drawing on extensive customer feedback and telemetry, we’re introducing two coordinated updates: redesigned meeting and sharing controls. Together, they make core actions easier to find, reduce accidental clicks, and give users more confidence when sharing content.\nThis update supports personal and team productivity by reducing friction in everyday meetings and improving confidence when presenting or sharing content.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560321 and 502520. It applies to Teams for Windows desktop, Teams for Mac desktop, and Teams for the web.\n[Rollout Schedule]\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out redesigned meeting controls in late July 2026 (previously early July) and expect to complete by mid-August 2026 (previously late July). Redesigned Sharing controls will begin rolling out in September 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in mid-October 2026 (previously late September) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late September).\n• General Availability (GCC, GCC High): We will begin rolling out in late October 2026 (previously late September) and expect to complete by mid-December 2026 (previously late November).\n• General Availability (DoD): We will begin rolling out in mid-December 2026 (previously late November) and expect to complete by early January 2027 (previously late December 2026).\n\n[Impact on Your Organization]\nWho is affected:\n• All Teams work and school users joining meetings\n\nPlatforms:\n• Teams for Windows desktop\n• Teams for Mac desktop\n• Teams for the web\n• Not in scope: Teams (consumer), iOS, Android, Teams Rooms, Linux\n\nWhat will happen:\n• Meeting controls will be center‑aligned, with microphone, camera, and share grouped together.\n• The Leave button will be separated to reduce accidental exits.\n• Less‑used actions will move into a reorganized More menu.\n• Users can personalize meeting controls by pinning, unpinning, and rearranging controls using drag and drop.\n\nScreenshot: New More options menu\n\n• Users can personalize meeting controls by pinning, unpinning, and rearranging controls using drag and drop.\n• The redesigned share panel may include:• Live previews of screens and windows.\n• A tabbed layout\n• A two‑step share confirmation to reduce accidental sharing.\n\nScreenshot: Reorganized share panel - not final UI\n\n• The new experience is enabled by default and cannot be disabled at the tenant level.\n• During rollout, users may opt in early and can temporarily return to the previous experience from Teams settings.\n• Existing meeting app pinning policies will continue to be honored.\n• New meeting app pinning policies will support up to two apps pinned to the main meeting controls, with additional apps available in the More menu.\n\nKnown limitations:\n• Meeting controls customization preferences (such as pinned controls) do not sync across devices at launch. Preferences persist across meetings on the same client. Cross‑device sync is planned for a future release.\n• The opt‑out toggle for the new meeting experience is controlled by individual users and cannot be managed at the tenant level. This opt‑out is a temporary adoption aid and will be retired in a future release. Microsoft will provide advance notice via a separate Message Center post before removal.\n\n[Action Required / Recommendations]\n•\n\nNo immediate action is required.\nWe recommend that you:\n• Review existing Teams meeting app pinning policies and plan future policies around the two‑app limit.\n• Communicate ​the redesiged meeting control changes to users, helpdesk, and internal support teams ahead of the July 2026 rollout. Detailed change management guidance for IT Pros/admins, along with an end user visual guide will be published on July 9th 2026: https://adoption.microsoft.com/microsoft-teams/new-meeting-controls-experience.\n• Update internal documentation and training materials to reflect:• The new meeting controls layout.\n• User customization options.\n• The updated share panel experience.\n\n[Compliance Considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-20","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1317197","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568763","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage: New left navigation controls — collapse, resize, increased favorites cap, and reorder favorites capabilities","desc":"<p>We're introducing a set of left-navigation improvements in Viva Engage on the web that give people more control over their navigation pane. These are additive, user-driven changes — users can collapse the left nav, resize its width, favorite up to 50 communities, and drag to reorder their favorited communities. None of these changes alter which destinations appear in the navigation. These enhancements are applicable to all surfaces that have the Engage left navigation menu - Web, and the Engage app in Teams and Outlook.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568763","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-555897","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"<p>You can now reference files saved in SharePoint libraries and OneDrive folders when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-02","modified":"2026-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555897","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-571303","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Transaction Journals","desc":"<p>Transaction journals let users author complete time, expense, and material transactions—including different transaction classes within the same journal. Users enter transactions through a dedicated Transactions tab and select Preview to generate and review the journal lines and relationships that will be created.</p> <p>When the journal is confirmed, Project Operations creates the applicable cost, unbilled-sales, and inter-organizational actuals, along with the required relationships between them, without creating an approval record or initiating an approval workflow. The confirmed journal is then locked using the existing journal behavior, and resulting actuals can be corrected through the existing correction-journal process.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-22","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571303","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-570861","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Choose how work order services flow into project financials","desc":"<p>Organizations can now control how work order services contribute to project financials when using Dynamics 365 Field Service and Project Operations together. A new administrator-level setting lets organizations choose whether work order services flow as time or material transactions based on how they manage field execution and technician labor.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-22","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570861","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570648","title":"Microsoft Teams: Analytics for desk utilization on Teams Pro Management portal","desc":"<p>Teams admins can access utilization analytics for Teams bookable desks on Teams Pro Management portal, similar to analytics provided for meeting rooms on the portal today. For utilization analytics to be enabled, a desk needs to have one or more peripheral device associated, and the desk needs to be licensed with Teams Shared Space license or Teams Shared Space - Single Space license.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570648","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570843","title":"Microsoft Teams: Upgraded call history in Teams Calls app","desc":"<p>Call history in the Teams Calls app is being upgraded to make it easier to find and act on past call activity. Missed calls and associated voicemails will be consolidated into a single call history entry, reducing clutter and simplifying follow-up. Call history will also expand from 100 records to up to 3,000 records or 6 months of history, whichever limit is reached first, giving users more context when they need it.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570843","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570964","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Federated Copilot Connectors will support write, update and delete actions","desc":"<p>Federated Copilot connectors (MCP type) currently let Microsoft 365 Copilot read data from third-party services in real time. With this update, the connector tools that create, update, and delete content in those services are unblocked in Copilot Chat, so users can complete work without leaving Copilot. Copilot acts with the user's own account and permissions at the third-party service, and every create, update, or delete action requires the user's explicit confirmation before it runs. Admins can view each connector's read and write/delete tools in the Microsoft 365 admin center and disable connectors that don't meet their organization's policies.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-22","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570964","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1261595","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams town halls now support backup Real-Time Messaging Protocol (RTMP) streams","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nTo improve reliability for large-scale live events, Microsoft Teams town halls will soon support a backup Real-Time Messaging Protocol (RTMP) stream. RTMP is a standard live‑streaming protocol used by event organizers to send live video and audio to a streaming service, such as Microsoft Teams. This enhancement helps ensure uninterrupted broadcasts by automatically failing over to a secondary RTMP stream if the primary stream experiences an interruption. This change increases resiliency for high-visibility events without adding complexity for organizers.\nThis message applies to Teams for Windows desktop, Teams for Mac desktop, and Teams for the web. It is associated with Roadmap ID 554932.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide, GCC): Rollout begins late April 2026 and completes by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September)\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizers and producers hosting Microsoft Teams town halls using RTMP-based production workflows\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Organizers can configure a backup RTMP stream during event setup using Teams Meeting options in Production tools.\n\n• If the primary RTMP stream fails, Teams will automatically fail over to the backup stream with no manual intervention.\n• There's no change to the attendee experience.\n\n• The feature is available by default; no admin configuration is required.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required.\n\n• Optionally, update internal event-production documentation and notify event producers of this new resiliency option.\n\nLearn more: Use RTMP-In in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Support (will be updated before rollout)\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1261595","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1257308","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Building‑level insights on the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal recommended actions page","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re adding new building‑level insights to the recommended actions page in the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal. This update helps IT admins identify buildings with high Microsoft Teams Rooms (MTR) utilization that still have bring-your-own-device (BYOD) rooms in them, creating an inconsistent user experience from room to room. These insights support more consistent meeting experiences across buildings and help organizations optimize room‑technology investments. Available with a Teams Rooms Pro or Shared Space license.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 553591.\n[When this will happen]\n• General availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out mid-June 2026 (previously early June) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizations using the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal with Teams Rooms Pro or Shared Device licenses\n\nWhat will happen\n• A new building‑level insights view will appear on the portal’s Recommended actions page:\n•\n• Insights will highlight buildings with high MTR usage and remaining BYOD meeting rooms:\n•\n• These insights are designed to help IT create more consistent room to room experiences for users within a building.\n• No changes will occur to existing configurations, policies, or settings.\n• The feature will be enabled by default for tenants with eligible licenses.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required.\nIf relevant to your organization’s deployment planning, you may:\n• Review your current MTR and BYOD room distribution in the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal.\n• Update internal documentation or planning guidance as needed.\n• Share this update with teams responsible for meeting room technology decisions.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1257308","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1316231","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Front-of-room view control for Webinars and structured meetings in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe're introducing an update to how front-of-room (FoR) displays behave in Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android during webinars and structured meetings. This change ensures that when a Teams Room joins as a presenter, the in-room display defaults to the attendee view—creating a clearer and more professional experience for in-room participants, especially in hybrid scenarios where presenters and attendees are co-located.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 559602.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in mid-June 2026 (previously early June) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n• General Availability (GCC, GCC High, DoD): We will begin rolling out in mid-June 2026 and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n• Organizations using Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android\n• Meeting organizers and presenters running webinars or structured meetings\n• In-room participants viewing front-of-room displays\n• A Teams Rooms Pro license is needed to use this feature\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• The front-of-room display will default to attendee view when joining webinars or structured meetings.\n• In-room audiences will not see presenter tools such as Green Room or backstage controls.\n\n• Presenters will retain full control from the Teams Rooms console, including:\n\n• Managing Green Room and off-stage participants.\n\n• Switching display modes (e.g., to presenter view when needed).\n\n• The feature is enabled by default and requires no configuration.\n\n• There is no impact to remote attendees or their experience.\n\n• Existing Teams Rooms functionality and policies remain unchanged.\n\nScreenshot 1: Front-of-room webinar experience with Manage screen mode on and the user in presenter view:\n\nScreenshot 2: Console view in presenter view:\n\nScreenshot 3: Front-of-room webinar experience with the user in attendee view:\n\nScreenshot 4: Console view with the user in attendee view:\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required to enable this feature.\n\n• Verify device readiness: Ensure Teams Rooms on Android devices are updated.\n\n• Validate meeting room setup: Confirm displays and consoles function as expected.\n\n• Educate organizers and presenters on the updated experience.\n\n• Update internal documentation.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-19","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1316231","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1251206","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Identify external bots joining your Teams meetings","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nAI‑powered meeting assistant bots—such as transcription and summarization services—are increasingly used to enhance productivity in online meetings. While these tools can be valuable, some bots may access meetings without the knowledge or consent of the meeting organizer or the hosting tenant, which can create data security, privacy, and compliance risks.\nTo help organizations protect meeting content and increase visibility into automated participants, Microsoft Teams is introducing a new capability that detects external meeting assistant bots as they attempt to join meetings. This update gives organizers greater awareness and control and provides administrators with clear controls to manage how detected bots are handled in meetings hosted across the organization.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558107.\n[When this will happen]\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out in mid-May 2026 and expect to complete by early June 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in early June 2026 and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n• General Availability (GCC): We will begin rolling out in early June 2026 and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All organizations using Microsoft Teams meetings, including GCC tenants\n• Meeting organizers and Teams administrators\n\nWhat will happen\n• Teams will detect external meeting bots as they attempt to join meetings hosted by your organization.\n• When detected, bots will be clearly labeled in the meeting lobby experience.\n•\n\n• Note: There might still be bots that are undetected by the system due to their intrinsic behavior. Please inform your users to report them out directly from the app/meeting. This will help us improve our detection system.\n• Organizers will be able to:\n• approve or deny detected bots from the meeting lobby.\n• see clearly which participants have been identified as bots.\n• remove detected bots during the meeting if necessary.\n• These organizer controls are designed to help ensure that bot participation in meetings is an intentional and informed decision.\n• A new meeting policy will be available in the Teams admin center that allows admins to configure how detected bots are handled (do not detect bots, require approval). In the future, we intend to provide more granular controls to admins, as appropriate.\n• Bot detection will be enabled by default for all tenants.\n• Teams will continue improving detection accuracy; however, some bots may not be detected in all scenarios.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required at this time.\nHowever, we recommend that Teams admins:\n• Review the new meeting policy in the Teams admin center once it becomes available.\n• Keep the default setting, which requires organizers to approve detected bots before they join meetings (recommended).\n• Choose a stricter or more permissive option based on your organization’s collaboration and compliance requirements.\n• Inform meeting organizers that they may see new indicators and approval prompts when detected bots attempt to join meetings.\n• Update internal helpdesk or governance documentation if your organization documents meeting join or lobby controls behavior.\n• Monitor future Message center updates for expanded administrative controls.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to your data?Yes. This change introduces detection logic that analyzes meeting join metadata to identify external automated bots attempting to join meetings.\nDoes the change provide a new way of communicating between users, tenants, or subscriptions?No. The feature only changes how external meeting assistant bots are surfaced to organizers during the meeting join process, increasing visibility of automated external participants. There is no change in the way participants can communicate with these bots or vice versa.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Yes. The change introduces a new meeting policy in the Teams admin center that allows admins to define how detected bots are handled. It cannot be controlled through Entra ID group membership at this time.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-13","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1251206","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1045221","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: New user setting to view incoming calls in a small window","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nComing soon for Microsoft Teams: A new setting that allows users to view incoming calls in a small window in Teams to prevent disruptions. Users will be able to take a call in the small window and continue to see what they were working on before the call.\nThis message applies to Teams on Windows desktop, Teams on Mac desktop, Teams for the web, and Teams for iOS/Android.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 482747.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out early May 2025 and expect to complete by mid-May 2025.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out mid-March 2026 (previously mid-January) and expect to complete by late March 2026 (previously late January).\n• General Availability (GCC): We will begin rolling out early April 2026 (previously early February) and expect to complete by mid-April 2026 (previously mid-February).\n• General Availability: (GCC High, DoD): We will begin rolling out early May 2026 (previously early February) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this will affect your organization:]\n• Before this rollout: Teams users are disrupted by the larger Teams screen when viewing an incoming call.\n• After this rollout: Teams users can turn on this setting to view calls in a small window. Note that both large and small windows are resizable:\n\nThis feature will be on by default.\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nThis rollout will happen automatically by the specified dates with no admin action required before the rollout. You may want to notify your users about this change and update any relevant documentation.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-31","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1045221","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1256307","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Recently used emojis sync across devices","desc":"Updated September 22, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re releasing an improvement to Microsoft Teams that syncs your recently used emojis and reactions across devices. With this update, users will see the same set of “recently used” emojis when using Teams on Android, iOS, Mac, Windows desktop, and Teams for the web, creating a more consistent and seamless experience when communicating across chats and channels. This enhancement aligns with customer feedback requesting a unified emoji experience across platforms.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 554927.\n[When this will happen]\n• Targeted Release: We expect to complete rollout by mid-July 2026 (previously mid-June).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in mid-July 2026 (previously mid-June) and expect to complete in late July 2026 (previously late June).\n• General Availability (GCC and GCCH): We will begin rolling out in mid-July 2026 (previously mid-June) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n• General Availability (DoD): We will begin rolling out in mid-August 2026 (previously mid-July) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All Microsoft Teams users across supported clients.\n\nWhat will happen\n• Recently used emojis and reactions will sync across devices.\n• Users will see the same “recently used” list regardless of which Teams client they use.\n• The feature will be enabled by default; no configuration is required for rollout.\n• Existing Teams admin settings and messaging policies will continue to apply.\n• There is no impact to message flow, data storage, compliance boundaries, or customer data pathways.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required. This update will roll out automatically.\nAdmins may optionally:\n• Inform helpdesk or support teams about this user experience update.\n• Update internal documentation if you reference emoji behavior or Teams UI details.\n• Review your Messaging settings and Messaging policies if you manage custom emoji usage.\n\nLearn more about emoji and reaction usage in Microsoft Teams: Send an emoji, GIF, or sticker in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Support\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.\nThis feature does not introduce new data storage, processing changes, AI/ML capabilities, communication pathways, admin reporting changes, or modifications to Purview‑governed workflows.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1256307","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-522616","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Ask Copilot about highlighted response content","desc":"<p>Highlight a sentence, paragraph, or table from the response and ask Copilot to work only on that selection. Get focused explanations, concise summaries, quick translations, or next steps for the exact passage you’re reviewing—no more over broad answers. Your selection is previewed in the prompt so you can edit before you send. It’s a faster, more controlled way to get help right where you’re working.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=522616","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-555881","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Attach and reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","desc":"<p>You can now attach and reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot using Agent Mode in PowerPoint.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555881","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-558254","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improved copy and paste support for @mentions and shared contacts","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams preserves @mentions and shared contacts when you copy and paste messages in chats and channels. Instead of defaulting to plain text, Teams intelligently displays an @mention, shared contact, or plain text based on where the content is pasted, reducing manual rework.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558254","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-555890","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Attach and reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","desc":"<p>You can now reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot using Agent Mode in PowerPoint.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555890","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558437","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention– Unmanaged cloud app discovery and protection with Microsoft Purview and the Island Enterprise Browser","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview network data security now integrates with Island, extending protection to Island’s browser-based workflows at the point of user interaction. With this integration, new and existing Island customers can configure Microsoft Purview collection and data loss prevention policies to detect and protect data shared with unmanaged cloud apps through the Island Enterprise Browser, the Island Extension, and browser add ins via HTTP and HTTPS, using the same classifiers, sensitive information types, and sensitivity labels used in other Purview policies. Island provides visibility and control at the presentation layer, including typed and pasted input, file transfers, and extension activity, so data can be inspected before it ever leaves the browser. This integration further enriches Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM), Insider Risk Management (IRM) risk score, enables data security and compliance for AI interactions, and more.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558437","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562343","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Insights and policy recommendations on sensitive M365 data for better Data Security and Compliance posture","desc":"<p>Insights on sensitive M365 data (OneDrive and SharePoint) and recommendations on retention policies for customers to better govern their sensitive data.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-18","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562343","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"January CY2027"},{"id":"rm-571302","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Quality evaluation supports knowledge source in criteria","desc":"<p>Criteria questions can now use knowledge sources to help evaluate customer interactions. This allows organizations to ground evaluation criteria in approved knowledge content, policies, or guidance so quality checks can better reflect expected handling standards. This preview capability is scoped to case and on-demand evaluations.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571302","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566527","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Ensure regulatory compliance by deleting inactive OneDrives and mailboxes for departing employees","desc":"<p>Enables admins to delete both content and containers for departed users at scale thereby keeping your tenant compliant without any manual effort.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-25","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566527","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-565222","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - In-product diagnostics to troubleshoot common challenges","desc":"<p>Self-service diagnostics help identify common issues with case permissions, security filters, and policy status. The experience highlights potential misconfigurations and provides simple guidance to help customers understand and resolve them. This brings basic troubleshooting into the product and helps eDiscovery admins overcome common challenges.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-05","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565222","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560822","title":"SharePoint: eSignature for Microsoft 365 - Recipient groups","desc":"<p>Recipient groups in eSignature allow a recipient slot to be assigned to multiple people, such that any one of those people can fulfil the signing requirement on behalf of the group.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560822","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-571390","title":"Microsoft Teams: Events in Meet app in Teams in GCC High and DoD","desc":"<p>Users can now use the Teams Meet app to discover events across their organization, track what important events are upcoming, and plan and organize their own professional events. With this release, Meet app will be renamed to Events app.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571390","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570446","title":"Microsoft Viva: Ability for leaders to publish Power BI reports","desc":"<p>Microsoft Viva Insights is extending its report publishing capabilities from analysts to leader personas such as Chief Officers, Managers and their delegates. This enhancement enables leaders to directly distribute curated reports within their organizations through a lightweight publishing experience, complementing the existing report customization features.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570446","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-557563","title":"OneDrive: Improved max path error experience on desktop","desc":"<p>OneDrive desktop sync users now get clearer, more actionable guidance when file paths exceed the supported 520-character limit. The updated experience shows exactly how many characters a path is over the limit and offers a guided flow to rename or move the affected items so they can sync.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557563","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1290821","title":"(Updated) eSignature for Microsoft 365 - Recipient groups","desc":"Updated September 21, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are introducing recipient groups for eSignature in Microsoft 365. Recipient groups allow a single recipient slot to be assigned to multiple people, where the first person to sign fulfills the signing requirement. This update helps make signature workflows more reliable by reducing delays when a specific signer is unavailable, without changing existing tenant policies.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560822.\n[When this will happen]\nPublic Preview: Rollout is expected to complete by late September 2026General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout will begin in early December 2026 (previously early September) and is expected to complete by mid-December 2026 (previously late October).\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Users who create eSignature requests in Microsoft Word\n• Microsoft 365 tenants that use eSignature for Microsoft 365\n\nWhat will happen\n• Users can assign up to 10 people to a single recipient slot:\n\n• The first person in the recipient group to sign fulfills the signing requirement for the group.\n• Signature workflows are less likely to stall due to individual signer availability.\n• The feature is enabled by default and respects existing tenant policies.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No action is required from admins.\n• Consider informing users who rely on eSignature workflows about this improvement.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed or accessed?Yes. Signature completion logic is updated so that one signer in a recipient group can fulfill the signing requirement for the group.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite","SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1290821","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571191","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Detailed quality evaluation score breakdown","desc":"<p>Evaluation details now include a scoring breakdown at the overall, section, and question level. Users can see how the final evaluation score was calculated, including how individual question outcomes contribute to section scores and the overall score. This improves transparency, helps quality teams validate results, and makes it easier to identify areas for coaching, calibration, and process improvement.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571191","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571193","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Inactivate quality evaluation records","desc":"<p>Quality managers can now inactivate evaluation records that should no longer contribute to scoring or reporting. Inactive evaluations are preserved for traceability but excluded from overall score calculations and analytics. This helps teams correct reporting outcomes when evaluations were created in error, used the wrong criteria, were duplicates, or should otherwise be removed from active quality results.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571193","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571192","title":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service: Support Not Applicable answer option for quality evaluation criteria","desc":"<p>Criteria questions now support a Not Applicable answer option. When a question is marked as not applicable, it is excluded from scoring instead of negatively affecting the evaluation score. This helps ensure evaluations remain accurate when a specific criterion does not apply to the case, interaction, or business scenario being reviewed.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Contact Center","Dynamics 365 Customer Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-21","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571192","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-503553","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: Authoritative content management for Microsoft 365 Copilot Search","desc":"<p>Specify and manage SharePoint sites deemed as authoritative content to enhance their relevance and ranking in Microsoft 365 Copilot Search. In the Microsoft 365 admin center, under Copilot &gt; Search &gt; Authoritative content, add and manage up to 100 SharePoint sites. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-25","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503553","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569207","title":"Microsoft Teams: Report a Security Concern in Meetings","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams will enable meeting organizers and attendees to report suspicious, malicious, or potentially fraudulent activity directly from meetings. Users can submit reports during or after a meeting, helping organizations identify potential threats such as impersonation, phishing, scams, and other suspicious behavior. Reports are integrated with Microsoft security and administrative workflows to support investigation, remediation, and ongoing improvements to security protections.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-18","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569207","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568782","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Admin Center - Single pane for monitoring & troubleshooting for meetings and calls across the organisation","desc":"<p>Administrators can monitor meeting and call health across the organization, uncover recurring patterns, and proactively troubleshoot issues impacting users in both active and completed meetings and calls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568782","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-562017","title":"Microsoft Viva: Fresh Copilot Metrics in Custom Person Queries & Reports- Viva Advanced Analysis","desc":"<p>Key Microsoft 365 Copilot metrics in custom person queries and reports will have values up to 2-3 days old from the current date. This will provide fresher copilot usage analysis to analysts in Viva Advanced analysis.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562017","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-559017","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work IQ APIs: Pay‑As‑You‑Go usage","desc":"<p>Enables metered, pay‑as‑you‑go access to Work IQ endpoints, allowing developers to invoke agents and capabilities without requiring pre‑assigned licenses, with usage billed based on the agents and models invoked per request.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559017","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Linux","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560076","title":"SharePoint: Create charts on pages with AI","desc":"<p>This feature empowers authors to create rich, interactive charts with AI in SharePoint when editing SharePoint pages. Authors can describe the chart they want to create in plain language within a chat on a SharePoint page.</p>","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-09","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560076","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-503772","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users in DoD will be able to use custom engine agents","desc":"<p>Users in DoD will be able to use custom engine agents.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-09-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503772","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-571847","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Core finance - Improve financial journal processing and control","desc":"<p>Finance teams rely on journals for high-volume accounting processes, where performance, accuracy, and visibility are critical to keeping financial operations moving. The new financial journal capabilities in Dynamics 365 Finance will provide a more scalable approach to creating, importing, reviewing, and posting journals, helping finance teams reduce manual steps and identify issues earlier in the process.</p> <p>Finance teams can work with customer and ledger account types, import journals and review errors without navigating to the Data management workspace, and preview intercompany and intracompany accounting, accruals, and allocations before posting. Related documents make it easier to trace transactions, while integration with advanced tax calculations supports applicable tax scenarios. Future-period accruals no longer post automatically, reducing the need to keep future periods open.</p> <p>Optimized financial dimensions and the Ledger posting rules framework are prerequisites for using these capabilities.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571847","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2027","gaSort":202712,"preview":"March CY2027"},{"id":"rm-562993","title":"Endpoint Data Loss Prevention — Endpoint DLP now supports a pre curated list of file extensions for the file extension condition","desc":"<p>Endpoint DLP now includes a pre curated list of file extensions for the file extension condition. Previously, file extensions were entered as free form text, which could result in unsupported or non-scannable extensions being used. This could lead to gaps in protection and increase processing overhead on endpoints. With the pre curated list, you can select only supported file extensions. This helps improve policy reliability and reduces unnecessary processing on endpoints.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562993","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-571637","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Cowork for Government Clouds","desc":"<p>Copilot Cowork makes it easy to delegate work. Describe the outcome you want and Cowork automatically grounds the work in your emails, meetings, messages, files, and data.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571637","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571307","title":"Microsoft Edge: Autolaunch opt-in experience for managed devices","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge will introduce an opt-in experience that allows users on managed devices to choose whether Edge launches automatically when Windows starts. Administrators can also manage this behavior through the LaunchEdgeOnWindowsStartupEnabled policy with opt-in, opt-out, and user-choice configurations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571307","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570844","title":"Microsoft Purview: Unified Classification Management Experience","desc":"<p>The Unified Classification Management Experience unifies every classifier in Microsoft Purview—Sensitive Information Types (SITs), Exact Data Match (EDM), fingerprint SITs, and trainable classifiers—into one place to discover, create, validate, and manage classifiers.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570844","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-500242","title":"Microsoft Teams: Intelligent recap for DoD","desc":"<p>Intelligent meeting recap uses AI to provide a quick summary of your meeting, highlighting key discussion points, identifying follow-up actions, and offering quick access to significant points such as name mentions, when a screen was shared, individualized speaker markers, topics, and chapters.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-08","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500242","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-566702","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit your document with Copilot in PowerPoint in Government Clouds","desc":"<p>Copilot in PowerPoint helps you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural language—right inside your deck. Start a new presentation or build on an existing one by asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design, all while preserving your formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot can also connect to your brand kit to apply branded templates, insert brand-approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) users.</p>","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-29","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566702","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-487852","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Realtime voice interactions in Word and PowerPoint","desc":"<p>Use your voice to talk with Copilot, interact in-real time, and understand the content within your document or presentation. Updated September 9, 2026: We will be re-releasing this feature with updates in October. Thank you for your patience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","PowerPoint","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571306","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Legacy Teams retention policies covering Copilot will be treated as Teams-only","desc":"<p>Some existing retention policies scoped to Microsoft Teams may currently also apply to Microsoft 365 Copilot interactions. As part of an upcoming change, these legacy Teams retention policies will be converted to—and treated as—Teams-only policies. They will no longer implicitly govern Copilot workloads.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571306","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571392","title":"Planner: Expiration of plans from meetings due to inactivity","desc":"<p>Planner plans created from Teams meetings (via Meeting Notes or Loop) often remain unused long after the meeting ends. These inactive plans accumulate and clutter over time. This feature automatically expires and deletes meeting-created plans that have had no task activity for 180 days. Only the Planner plan is removed whereas the tasks in Loop and meeting notes stay intact.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-18","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571392","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1249424","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview DLP: Unmanaged cloud app protection with Microsoft Purview and the Island Enterprise Browser","desc":"Updated September 18, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nMicrosoft Purview network data security now integrates with Island, extending protection to Island’s browser-based workflows at the point of user interaction. With this integration, new and existing Island customers can configure Microsoft Purview collection and data loss prevention policies to detect and protect data shared with unmanaged cloud apps through the Island Enterprise Browser, the Island Extension, and browser add ins via HTTP and HTTPS, using the same classifiers, sensitive information types, and sensitivity labels used in other Purview policies. Island provides visibility and control at the presentation layer, including typed and pasted input, file transfers, and extension activity, so data can be inspected before it ever leaves the browser.\nThis integration further enriches Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM), Insider Risk Management (IRM) risk score, enables data security and compliance for AI interactions, and more.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558437.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: Rollout will begin in late March 2026 and is expected to complete by late April 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout will begin in June 2027 (previously late June 2026) and is expected to complete June 2027 (previoulsy late July 2026).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft Purview\n\n• Customers using or planning to use the Island Enterprise Browser, Island Extension, or supported browser add-ins.\n\n• Microsoft 365 administrators managing Purview collection and DLP policies.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• The Island integration will automatically appear in the Purview DLP Security Store as the feature rolls out.\n\n• The integration is not enabled by default. Administrators must explicitly enable it before it can be used in policies.\n\n• Once enabled, admins can use existing or new Purview collection and DLP policies to inspect and protect data shared through Island-managed browser activity.\n\n• There is no impact to end users unless administrators enable the integration and configure network data security policies in Purview.\n• Existing network data security collection and DLP policies will automatically apply if the integration is enabled.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Confirm that Purview pay-as-you-go is enabled and configured for your tenant, as it is required to use this integration. Learn more: Enable pay-as-you-go billing for Microsoft Purview.\n\n• Review your existing Purview collection and DLP policies to determine where network-based data inspection may be appropriate.\n\n• Inform other data security and compliance administrators in your organization about this upcoming capability.\n\n• After rollout, enable the Island integration from the Purview DLP Security Store when you are ready to use it.\n\nLearn more:\n\n• Microsoft Purview collection policies\n\n• Microsoft Purview data loss prevention\n\n• Microsoft Purview network data security\n\n• Purview Security Store\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nExplanation\n\nNew customer data processed\nWhen the integration is enabled, browser-based activity metadata and inspection results may be processed as part of Microsoft Purview network data security.\n\nChanges to existing customer data processing\nExisting Purview classifiers, sensitive information types, and sensitivity labels are applied to data shared through Island-managed browser workflows.\n\nAI and ML interaction with customer data\nThe integration supports data security and compliance for AI interactions occurring within browser-based workflows.\n\nPurview DLP and information protection capabilities\nPurview collection and DLP policies are extended to inspect and protect data at the browser presentation layer when configured by an administrator.\n\nAdmin monitoring and compliance reporting\nSignals from browser-based inspections can contribute to Purview Data Security Posture Management and Insider Risk Management insights.\n\nThird-party integration\nThis change introduces an integration between Microsoft Purview and Island browser technologies.\n\nAdmin control\nThe integration is admin-controlled and must be explicitly enabled from the Purview DLP Security Store.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1249424","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566351","title":"PowerPoint: Create on brand presentations with additional brand assets","desc":"<p>Seamlessly access your brand colors, images, icons, logos and more right within PowerPoint to create on-brand presentations.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-25","modified":"2026-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566351","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-571300","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Manage rental service demand with work order requests","desc":"<p>Rental organizations need to coordinate commercial rental activity, equipment availability, asset condition, and service execution across multiple teams and applications. Service needs can arise while equipment is in stock, in transit, at a customer site, or being returned, but those needs don’t always require an immediate work order.</p> <p>This feature connects rental operations in Dynamics 365 Finance and Supply Chain Management with Dynamics 365 Field Service by introducing fleet items and work order requests for rental service scenarios. Field Service users can view relevant fleet, rental contract, location, movement, and asset information while service needs can be captured and reviewed before a work order is created.</p> <p>Work order requests provide a controlled intake and approval process, allowing teams to validate service needs before committing technicians, inventory, or scheduling resources. When approved, a request can create a Field Service work order while preserving the relevant fleet item, asset, and rental context as the work progresses.</p> <p>This connected experience gives rental, service, and operations teams better visibility and coordination across the rental service lifecycle while giving organizations greater control over when service work is initiated. The capability can be used with Field Service alone or with the combined Field Service and Project Operations solution.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-17","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571300","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2027","gaSort":202712,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570863","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Book Work Orders with Multiple Requirements","desc":"<p>Dispatchers can now select which resource requirement to schedule when booking a work order that has multiple requirements. The new <strong>Book</strong> experience is available from both the work order form and list view, and shows relevant details such as requirement duration, time windows, resource preferences, booking status, and links to active bookings.</p> <p>Work orders with a single resource requirement continue directly to the configured Schedule Assistant or Quick Book experience. The requirement picker is accessible, responsive, localized, and supports right-to-left languages.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-17","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570863","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571298","title":"Microsoft Teams: Customize blocked file extensions for Weaponizable File Protection","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams is expanding admin controls for Weaponizable File Protection. Administrators will be able to customize which file types are blocked in Teams to align with their organization's security requirements or continue using the Microsoft-recommended default list. This added flexibility helps organizations tailor file protection policies while maintaining a secure collaboration environment.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-16","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571298","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571391","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Optional Public CDN Support in Brand Center Setup","desc":"<p>We are updating the Brand Center setup experience so that administrators can set up Brand Center without enabling Public CDN.</p> <p>Today, Public CDN is enabled as part of Brand Center setup, even when an organization only wants to use branding governance capabilities that do not require it. With this update, organizations can begin using Brand Center while deferring Public CDN until they need capabilities that depend on it, such as organizational fonts.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-17","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571391","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sharepoint/brand-center-overview#setting-up-the-brand-center"},{"id":"rm-566864","title":"Microsoft Edge: Ask Copilot about an image","desc":"<p>Ask Copilot about an image in Edge enables users to instantly analyze images from the web by sending them directly to Copilot from the Edge context menu, making it easy to ask questions, gain insights, and understand visual content without leaving their browsing experience. Admins can control availability to this feature using the EdgeEntraCopilotPageContext and Microsoft365CopilotChatIconEnabled policies.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566864","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-554938","title":"Microsoft Edge: Enhanced Autofill","desc":"<p>For desktop users, Microsoft Edge can now autofill additional document types—including passports, driver’s licenses, and other specialized forms—on top of your saved addresses.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554938","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570441","title":"Outlook: Multi Account Search","desc":"<p>Users will be able to see results from multiple mailboxes interweaved in a single ranked list and will be able to do standard mail actions.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-17","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570441","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1238432","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365 Copilot app: Branded footer customization","desc":"Updated September 17, 2026: We have updated the content. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing a new co-branding capability that will allow organizations to display a branded footer at the bottom of the Chat screen in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app. This update will enable admins to add their organization’s logo to their users’ Microsoft 365 Copilot app, helping users confirm they are using their trusted, work-managed Copilot experience.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 555852.\n[When this will happen]\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out August 2026 (previously mid-July) and is expected to complete by mid-September 2026 (previously end of July).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All Microsoft 365 tenants using the Microsoft 365 Copilot app.\n\nWhat will happen\n• Admins will be able to upload a logo in the Microsoft 365 admin center to customize the footer in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app.\n• The footer will use the same logo configured in your organization’s theme for other Microsoft 365 apps. Only the logo will be used; other theme settings will not apply in this release.\n\n• Admins can choose a footer label: Approved by, Provided by, or Managed by. Selecting No label will display the logo without a label.\n• This feature will be off by default and will require admin configuration.\n• There will be no user impact unless an admin enables the footer.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action will be required unless you want to enable the branded footer.\nAdmins who want to configure this feature should:\n• In the Microsoft 365 admin center, go to Org settings > Custom theme and open your default theme.\n• Confirm that your organization’s logo is configured in the Logos tab. This is the same logo used for your organization’s branding in other Microsoft 365 apps.\n• Open the Copilot Chat tab and select Add your brand to Copilot Chat footer area.\n• In the Footer style dropdown, choose No label, Approved by, Provided by, or Managed by.\n• Save your changes to display your logo in the branded footer in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app.\n\nPlease note: The footer currently uses your organization's default theme and applies to all users. Targeting different logos to specific user groups will be supported in a later update.\nFor configuration guidance: Customize the theme for your organization | Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1238432","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567304","title":"Microsoft Teams: Explicit recording and transcription consent for PSTN participants now available in GCC High and DoD","desc":"<p>We are introducing explicit recording and transcription consent support for PSTN participants joining Microsoft Teams meetings in GCC High and DoD environments. This feature is already available in Public and GCC clouds and is now being extended to sovereign environments. After this rollout, when a meeting is being recorded or transcribed, PSTN participants will be prompted to provide explicit consent before they can unmute and participate. If consent is not provided, participants will remain muted for the duration of the meeting. This update aligns PSTN behavior with the existing consent experience in Teams clients and enhances compliance by ensuring all participants actively acknowledge recording and transcription. This rollout may impact PSTN users joining meetings where recording or transcription is enabled. We recommend informing users about this change so they are prepared to provide consent when prompted.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-16","modified":"2026-09-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567304","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-501781","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management: Data Security Investigations integration","desc":"<p>Launch a pre-scoped Data Security Investigation (DSI) from an IRM case. When a data security admin identifies a risky user who needs deeper investigation, they can launch a pre-scoped investigation directly from an IRM case, allowing them to view content analysis related to that user and better assess post-incident data impact. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-05","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501781","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2027","gaSort":202712},{"id":"rm-567010","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - User Based Aggregation of DLP Alerts","desc":"<p>Enable aggregation of DLP alerts based on common entities user even when multiple rules are matched. This feature should consolidate related alert events into a single alert object to: Reduce alert noise, simplify investigation workflows, enhance contextual understanding of violations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567010","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-571396","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-Expanded inline protection for unmanaged apps in Edge for Business","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview collection and data loss prevention (DLP) policies will support browser inline protection for a significantly broader set of unmanaged generative AI apps in Edge for Business. Admins can use existing Purview policy experiences to detect and protect sensitive data shared through supported browser activities, helping extend consistent data security controls across more destinations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571396","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570860","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Automatically complete Project Tasks when field work is finished","desc":"<p>Keep project plans aligned with field execution by automatically completing a linked Project Task when its Work Order is completed.</p> <p>When project work is carried out through Field Service, the Work Order often represents the execution of a specific Project Task. With this capability, organizations can configure Work Order Types so that completing the Work Order also completes the associated Project Task.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-16","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570860","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570855","title":"Dynamics 365 Field Service: Bring project material plans into field execution","desc":"<p>When the Field Service and Project Operations integration is enabled, material estimates created in a project plan can now create connected Work Order Products on the related Field Service work order. This allows project-planned materials to flow into Field Service without requiring project and field teams to recreate material lines, keeping both teams aligned on the same material plan.</p> <p>As before, Work Order Products can create material estimates when materials are added from Field Service during execution. Supported changes remain synchronized across the project task, work order, and material line, allowing material planning to begin from either Project Operations or Field Service while keeping planning and execution aligned.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Field Service"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-16","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-561486","title":"Microsoft Edge: Improved website compatibility with site troubleshooting controls","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is introducing improvements to help users quickly resolve website issues directly from the browser. When a site is not functioning as expected, users may be guided to relevant troubleshooting options such as adjusting tracking prevention settings (e.g., Strict mode) and reviewing site-specific configurations. This experience surfaces relevant actions in-context to help users restore site functionality without navigating deep into settings.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-04","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561486","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571299","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ask Copilot from Search on Mobile","desc":"<p>Get answers without leaving search. As you type in the Teams search bar, you'll see an option to ask Copilot alongside search results. You can also select Ask Copilot from the search results page to turn your query into a Copilot conversation, helping you quickly find information, get answers, and ask follow-up questions in context.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571299","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571297","title":"Microsoft Teams: Report suspicious guest invitations","desc":"<p>Microsoft Teams will enable users to report suspicious guest invitations directly from Teams. When users receive an unexpected or potentially malicious guest invitation, they can report it to their IT admin for review, helping identify and mitigate phishing and other abuse through guest invitations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-14","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571297","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569928","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Power BI reports as references in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"<p>Copilot Notebooks now lets users add Power BI reports as references, bringing report data directly into their notebooks alongside files. Copilot uses this information to help generate more relevant summaries, presentations, and briefs grounded in the organization's data.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-25","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569928","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-571200","title":"SharePoint: New Mobile Experience on iOS and Android","desc":"<p>The SharePoint mobile app for iOS and Android is redesigned around the personalized SharePoint Discover experience, bringing your most relevant files, sites, people, and news together in one place, with improved site browsing, in-app file previews, refreshed news and search, dark mode, and better performance.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-16","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571200","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569205","title":"Microsoft Teams: Temporarily pause all notifications","desc":"<p>Users can now temporarily pause all notifications to minimize interruptions and stay focused on important work, meetings, or other priorities, without changing their existing notification settings.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569205","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-560705","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Power user insights in Copilot dashboard","desc":"<p>Understand who is building a habit using Copilot with the new power user insights in Copilot dashboard</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560705","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-500396","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Expanding access to Diagnostics to Compliance Administrator, Security Administrator and Organization Management","desc":"<p>We are expanding the access to Diagnostics beyond Global Admin to: Compliance Administrator, Security Administrator and Organization Management</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-11","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500396","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-510099","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Add references to your Copilot Notebooks from the Quick Access section in Search on the M365 Copilot app","desc":"<p>Users can quickly add references to a Copilot Notebook through the Quick Access section in Search on the M365 Copilot app.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=510099","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-516044","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Metadata understanding support for queries scoped to SharePoint document libraries or folders","desc":"<p>We’re introducing column metadata support for queries in Microsoft 365 Copilot when a SharePoint library or folder is attached or its URL is provided. This enhancement improves contextual relevance by enabling Copilot to leverage additional metadata from the selected library, delivering more accurate and meaningful results.</p>","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516044","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-491918","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Information Protection - Sensitivity Label support in Engage","desc":"<p>Your organization can now manually apply Information Protection sensitivity labels in Engage. Sensitivity label support in this new application will allow admins to create labels and configure label publishing policies to determine which users and groups can manually label content in Engage. End users will be able to manually apply labels to Engage communities and in turn classify and protect their sensitive data via privacy and external user access controls.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-02","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491918","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-501582","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Collection policies impact on IRM","desc":"<p>With this update, Microsoft Purview will start supporting collection policies. Collection policies allow customers to scope classification (SITs - Sensitive Information Types) and activities for scoped users. We recommend reviewing collection policies as they can be created by different Purview solution admins to ensure they are setup to detect the activities required by Insider Risk Management policies Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501582","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-480734","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Endpoint DLP shows full path of target domain","desc":"<p>Endpoint DLP should show full path of target domain and not just the domain name in Activity Explorer.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-11","modified":"2026-09-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480734","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-571304","title":"Dynamics 365 Project Operations: Optimize, discover and manage features from one place","desc":"<p>A single place in Project Operations where administrators and end users can discover the core features relevant to them <strong>in lite or resource/non-stocked deployments</strong>.</p> <p>**For administrators: **</p> <ul> <li>Browse features by status: New, Available, Enabled, or Coming soon.</li> <li>Filter and search by product area.</li> <li>Review benefits, impact, dependencies, availability timing, and guidance.</li> <li>Check whether a feature is optional or automatically enabled and whether it can be reversed.</li> <li>Receive advance notice of upcoming features through notifications and a banner.</li> </ul> <p>**For end users: **</p> <ul> <li>View newly available and enabled features.</li> <li>Access task-level guidance through Learn more.</li> <li>Receive notifications on features newly available in the product</li> </ul>","products":["Dynamics 365 Project Operations"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571304","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2027","gaSort":202705,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-80239","title":"Microsoft Teams: Two presenters can share their screens or windows simultaneously in meetings","desc":"<p>Two presenters can share a screen or window at the same time in a Teams meeting. Participants can see both shared content streams simultaneously, making it easier to compare and discuss content from different presenters.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=80239","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-571310","title":"Outlook: Spell check before sending emails in new Outlook","desc":"<p>If you don’t want to check spelling manually for every message—or you’re worried you might forget!—you can set Outlook to check spelling for you every time before sending emails.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571310","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570438","title":"PowerPoint: Async Notifications for PowerPoint Agent (Web)","desc":"<p>Enable users to leave PowerPoint, switch devices, go offline, or end their workday while remaining confident that Copilot will notify them when work is complete or requires attention.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570438","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570437","title":"PowerPoint: Async Notifications for PowerPoint Agent (Windows Desktop)","desc":"<p>Enable users to leave PowerPoint, switch devices, go offline, or end their workday while remaining confident that Copilot will notify them when work is complete or requires attention.</p>","products":["PowerPoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570437","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-502533","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility]​​[Search UX] Rich entity representation for connectors in Search results","desc":"<p>Rich entity representation for connectors in Search results.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502533","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571195","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Cost visibility in Agent Evaluations","desc":"<p>Now makers will have clear visibility into their consumption costs directly associated with their evaluations, including a breakdown of usage for eval generation, test runs and model grading/judgement. Makers can see the costs as they test, iterate, and review conversations, making usage transparent throughout the development lifecycle.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571195","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571196","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Cost visibility in Monitor tab","desc":"<p>Now makers will have clear visibility into their consumption costs directly within Monitor tab at both a per-agent level and an estimated breakdown of those costs across the agents lifecylce. This will allow makers to see costs distributed across activities such as authoring, testing, evaluations, and production usage, helping connect overall consumption to specific actions and experiences.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571196","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-571194","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Cost visibility in Preview Chat and History","desc":"<p>Now makers will have clear visibility into their consumption costs directly within preview tab and agent history for their preview/testing usage as well as all every historical run. Makers can see the costs as they test, iterate, and review conversations, making usage costs transparent throughout the development experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-15","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571194","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568787","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.153 - Changes to local IP address detection for proxy auto-config (PAC) scripts","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is changing how it selects the local network address reported to proxy auto-config (PAC) scripts and is adding administrator control over it. The default IPv4 and IPv6 probe destinations now match Chromium’s defaults. Administrators can override these defaults using the PacMyIpAddressIPv4ProbeAddress and PacMyIpAddressIPv6ProbeAddress policies when required by their network routing.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-08-05","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568787","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-530578","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.153 - Tracking prevention when browsing InPrivate","desc":"<p>Microsoft Edge is unifying the tracking prevention experience for non-InPrivate and InPrivate browsing windows. Microsoft Edge will use the same tracking prevention setting as a normal browsing window when in InPrivate mode.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-03","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=530578","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561325","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics: Copilot usage snapshot PBI at day level with fresh data","desc":"<p>A day level Copilot adoption Power BI report reflecting the most recent copilot activity &amp; freshest insights.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561325","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567301","title":"Microsoft Teams: New controls for quick views in the chat list","desc":"<p>The new chats and channels experience introduced quick views at the top of the chat and channels list. These are views into mentions, followed threads and more. This update allows users to choose when and how these quick views are shown. Users will have options such as always show, always hide and show only when unread. Users will also be able to collapse the quick views section.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567301","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567470","title":"OneDrive: Exclude specific folders from syncing","desc":"<p>OneDrive for Windows and Mac will let users exclude specific folders from syncing, so folders that do not belong in the cloud, such as developer tooling folders like PowerShell modules, Visual Studio configuration, and node modules, stay local on the device instead of uploading to OneDrive. Administrators can define folder exclusion rules for their organization.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567470","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-537269","title":"Microsoft Teams: Express voice enrollment in Microsoft Teams","desc":"<p>Express voice enrollment makes registering your voice in Teams fast and easy. Your profile enables features like voice isolation, speaker recognition, identification in a meeting room and transcripts, and enhanced meeting recaps and insights from Microsoft 365 Copilot. If you don’t yet have a voice profile, just go to the recognition tab in Teams settings and opt-in to enroll your voice simply by speaking during a meeting.&nbsp; Admins can enable or disable this feature.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537269","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560396","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Expand protection to Copilot + PC devices for Recall snapshots through custom policies","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview Endpoint data loss prevention is expanding coverage to Copilot + PCs initially to support Recall snapshots and determining whether policies exist to prevent capture of windows containing restricted sensitivity labels and Sensitive information types (SITs). Purview admins will author Endpoint DLP custom policies to integrate with Windows Copilot + PC Recall setup by Intune admins for Copilot + PC devices exclusively.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560396","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-529864","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Semantic Goodbye word for voice in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"<p>Now users can close a voice session on Windows by simply saying bye or goodbye when they want to close voice session. This, paired with \"Hey Copilot\" wake word, provides them with complete hands-free experience for voice in Microsoft 365 Copilot on Windows devices.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-09-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529864","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-562991","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Allow customer to scope JIT Audit to specific user or user group","desc":"<p>Enable customers to include or exclude users/user groups from Just‑In‑Time (JIT) Audit, ensuring audits are generated only for the selected users or groups.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-26","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562991","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-562992","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention – Ability to protect files stored in the excluded folders in Windows","desc":"<p>Endpoint DLP now extends protection to files stored in commonly excluded Windows folders, including Temp and AppData. This helps improve coverage by detecting and protecting sensitive data in these locations.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-26","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562992","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-569423","title":"Microsoft Teams: Hide Organizer name in Calendar View on Teams Panels","desc":"<p>Admins can now choose whether the organizer name will show up in the Calendar View on Teams panels. Admins can toggle the \"Show organizer name\" setting ON or OFF in the Pro Management portal or on the panel device. Based on the selection, the organizer name will or will not be shown in the calendar view on the panel device. Available with Teams Rooms Pro and Teams Shared Space licenses.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-26","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-571199","title":"Outlook: New Cloud Policy controls","desc":"<p>We’re introducing Cloud Policy service support for Outlook on the web and new Outlook for Windows. Admins can set default values for supported Outlook settings and choose whether users can change them, providing consistent cloud-based control across their organization</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-14","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=571199","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1282567","title":"(Updated) Create charts on pages with AI in SharePoint","desc":"Updated September 14, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nIntroduction\n\nWe’re introducing a new Charts web part with AI assistance in SharePoint, designed to help page authors quickly create rich, interactive charts using plain-language prompts. This update reduces the time and effort needed to visualize data on SharePoint pages and enables more intuitive, AI-powered authoring experiences directly within SharePoint.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560076.\n\nWhen this will happen:\n\n• Targeted Release: Rollout begins in late May 2026 (previously early May) and is expected to complete by mid-June 2026 (previously mid-May).\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in mid-June 2026 (previously mid-May) and is expected to complete by end of September 2026 (previously end of August).\n\nHow this affects your organization:\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• SharePoint page authors\n• Tenants using SharePoint Online\n\n• A Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license is required to use this feature\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• While editing a SharePoint page, a Chart web part can be added in one of the following ways:• Open the AI agent chat pane from the Agents coin icon in the upper-right navigation or the AI sparkle icon on the page toolbar.\n• Open the web part toolbox, search for Chart under the AI category, and add it to the page (this automatically opens the chat pane).\nScreenshot 1: Entry point if adding a chart from the web part toolbox:\n\n• Describe the chart to create using plain language, such as the data to visualize and the chart type. Relevant files can be attached to provide additional context.\nScreenshot 2: Prompt to add a chart through the chat pane:\n\n• After the chart is created, follow-up prompts can be used to:• Add, edit, or remove data\n• Adjust the look and feel of the chart\n\n• Changes can be reverted at any time using the Undo button in the command bar.\n• The feature is enabled by default for users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, and existing SharePoint permissions and Microsoft 365 policies continue to apply.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n\nNo action is required.\n\n• Optionally inform SharePoint authors of the new capability.\n\n• Update internal documentation if you provide SharePoint or Copilot guidance.\n• Review Copilot licensing assignments to confirm which users will have access.\n\nLearn more: Create a chart on pages with AI in SharePoint | Microsoft Support\nCompliance considerations:\n\nThis change introduces a new way for users to interact with generative AI by using natural language prompts to create and edit charts in SharePoint pages.","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1282567","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1093912","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Outlook for iOS/Android: Improved Contacts with profile enrichment and duplicate management","desc":"Updated September 14, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n\nWe’re enhancing the contact experience in Microsoft Outlook Mobile (iOS and Android) by introducing profile-enriched contacts and automatic duplicate contact management. These improvements aim to streamline contact views and provide richer organizational context.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 493753.\nThis feature has previously been released to the People Hub in new Outlook for Windows. More details in MC927963 (Updated) New Microsoft Outlook for Windows: People Hub improvements (published November 2024, updated April 2025).\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out mid-July 2025 (previously late June) and expect to complete by mid-November 2026 (previously end of September).\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nBefore this rollout, Outlook Mobile may have displayed multiple entries for the same contact and lacked organizational profile context.\nAfter this rollout:\n• Contacts will be unified into a single enriched view, displaying additional profile information from your organization’s directory (where available).\n\n• Identical duplicate contacts will be automatically hidden.\n\n• These enhancements will be on by default and apply to both iOS and Android versions of Outlook Mobile. No admin controls exist.\n• Users can access their contact list by selecting Contacts from the Apps section in the Outlook Mobile app.\n\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nThis rollout will happen automatically by the specified dates with no admin action required before the rollout. You may want to notify your users about this change and update internal documentation.\n\nAfter the feature is rolled out, please ensure that users have updated to the latest version of Outlook for iOS or Outlook for Android.\nLearn more: Manage Outlook contacts in your organization - Microsoft Support","products":["Exchange Online","Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-13","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1093912","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561856","title":"Access: Zooming for Continuous Forms and Multiple-Items Forms","desc":"<p>Access extends zoom capabilities to continuous forms and pop-up forms, building on zoom support already available in tables and queries. Adjust magnification from 10 percent to 500 percent using the slider in the lower-right corner or controls on the ribbon. Keyboard shortcuts are also available, making it easy to quickly change your view and focus on the details that matter most.</p>","products":["Access"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561330","title":"Microsoft 365: Introducing Exchange Online Cross-tenant Message Recall","desc":"<p>We're enhancing the Exchange Online Message Recall feature to add support for cross-tenant recalls. Today, you can recall messages only within your organization. Cross-tenant recall will let you recall messages sent to other organizations that add your tenant to their recall allow list.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561330","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-501111","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users in GCC-M will able to use custom engine agents","desc":"<p>Users in GCC-M will be able to use custom engine agents.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501111","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566697","title":"OneDrive: PDF annotation for sensitivity-label protected PDFs in the OneDrive apps (iOS and Android)","desc":"<p>The Microsoft OneDrive apps for iOS and Android will let users annotate PDFs protected by a Microsoft Purview Information Protection sensitivity label that applies encryption — without removing or weakening the label. Users with edit/annotate rights can add a full set of annotations — including ink, highlight, free text, notes, signatures, image/shape/date stamps, bookmarks, and form fields — directly in the OneDrive mobile PDF viewer; the file's encryption and usage rights are preserved end to end. This applies to the OneDrive apps for iOS and Android only (not OneDrive or SharePoint on the web). The feature is enabled by default for eligible users and requires no new admin action.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566697","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561491","title":"Outlook: Copilot Settings in classic Outlook for Windows","desc":"<p>You will now be able to access different Copilot settings directly in classic Outlook for Windows.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561491","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-489227","title":"Access: Enable zoom magnification to Microsoft Access for Forms, Tables, Queries","desc":"<p>Access will add magnification slider (10% to 500%) in lower right of the application, similar to the feature in Word, PowerPoint, and Excel. It will also be keyboard accessible and available on the ribbon in Access forms, tables, and queries.</p>","products":["Access"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-10","modified":"2026-09-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489227","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-569420","title":"Microsoft Teams: Coordinated meetings support on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>Teams Rooms on Android now supports coordinated meetings, enabling paired Teams Rooms on Android devices and Android-based touch boards to work together in the same hybrid meeting experience. This feature enables coordinated join and leave, and collaboration across front-of-room displays and touch boards. This creates more immersive and flexible meeting spaces for both in-room and remote participants.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-21","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569420","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-567466","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams events attendance and engagement report policy","desc":"<p>Teams events will soon have a separate attendance and engagement report policy from the \"CsTeamsMeetingPolicy\" attendance and engagement report policy. This will permit admins to allow Teams events organizers to access attendance and engagement reports, while restricting access to Teams meeting attendance and engagement reports.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567466","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570277","title":"Word: Copilot edit mode is available to users in Office 365 GCC","desc":"<p>Edit with Copilot in Word is now available to users in Office 365 GCC, enabling government customers to work with Copilot as a co-creator directly in your document to create, refine, and transform documents more efficiently.</p>","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-11","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-561328","title":"Access: Cascading combo and list boxes with LinkMasterFields/LinkChildFields","desc":"<p>Combo boxes and list boxes now support LinkMasterFields/LinkChildFields properties, enabling cascading dropdowns (e.g., Country filters City) without writing VBA code.</p>","products":["Access"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561328","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1181769","title":"Microsoft Purview: Integration with Entra GSA Internet Access to enable sensitive file filtering at the network layer","desc":"Updated September 11, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nTo help organizations better protect sensitive files in transit, we're introducing a public preview for extending Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies to the network through integration with Entra Global Secure Access Internet Access. Through this integration, organizations can intercept and inspect file traffic at the network layer and enforce actions based on DLP policy conditions. It helps prevent sensitive files from being shared with untrusted cloud applications through browsers, apps, APIs, add-ins, and more—including generative AI platforms, cloud storage, and content-sharing services—while managing alerts and incidents through Purview and Microsoft Defender.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 522096.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public preview: Rollout begins mid-November 2025 and completes by mid-December 2025.\n\n• General availability: Rollout begins end of September and completes by end of October 2026 (previously end of September).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\n• Who is affected: Microsoft 365 tenants with E3 or E5 licenses; Admins managing Microsoft Purview DLP and Entra Global Secure Access.\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• A new “Inline Web Traffic” scenario will be available in Purview DLP policy creation.\n\n• Admins can configure granular policies and rules to detect and protect sensitive files transmitted to over 35,000 unmanaged cloud applications.\n\n• Policy matches, alerts, and incidents will be managed centrally in Microsoft Purview and Microsoft Defender.\n\n• The feature will be available by default but requires configuration to activate.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Ensure your GSA administrator configures the following in Entra Global Secure Access:\n\n• Enabled the internet access traffic profile and ensure the correct user assignments apply.\n\n• Configure TLS inspection and configure a TLS inspection policy.\n• Create a file policy and add a rule that specifies the action \"Scan with Purview\".\n• Configure a security profile with the above policies and link it to a conditional access policy.\n\n• Your global admin must activate Purview pay-as-you-go to enable this capability. No charges will apply during public preview.\n\n• Review your current DLP and network configurations to assess impact.\n\n• Communicate this change to helpdesk and security teams.\n\n• Update internal documentation to reflect new policy options.\n\n• For more details, refer to: Learn about data loss prevention\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance Area\nExplanation\n\nAlters how existing customer data is processed\nSensitive file traffic is inspected at the network layer before reaching unmanaged cloud apps.\n\nIntroduces AI/ML capabilitiesDLP policies may interact with generative AI platforms to prevent data leakage.\n\nModifies DLP enforcementAdds network-layer enforcement to existing Purview DLP capabilities.\n\nAdds integration to extend Purview DLP controls\nIntegrates with Entra Global Secure Access Internet Access.\n\nIncludes admin controlControlled via Purview and Entra admin portals.\n\nCan be controlled through Entra ID group membership\nPolicy scoping can leverage Entra ID groups.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1181769","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566870","title":"OneNote: Suggested Artifact Creation in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"<p>Copilot Notebooks in OneNote now suggests artifacts to create, such as Word documents, Excel workbooks, and PowerPoint presentations, based on Microsoft 365 knowledge and the content in your notebook. Select the suggestion and Copilot will generate the artifact.</p>","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-30","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566870","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567005","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Insights: Copilot Analytics - Cowork adoption and impact","desc":"<p>Deeper insights into Cowork adoption and impact accessible from the new AI Cost dashboard and Copilot dashboard. Includes export capability. All metrics can be queried by analysts with the new AI cost query in advanced insights.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-30","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567005","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-566313","title":"OneDrive: Document library views now available in OneDrive","desc":"<p>Users can now work with SharePoint document library views directly from OneDrive. In addition to switching between existing views, users can create and manage views to customize how library content is organized and displayed. This helps teams surface the information that matters most while staying within the OneDrive experience.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566313","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-566315","title":"OneDrive: Refreshed Libraries View in OneDrive Web","desc":"<p>We're replacing the existing More places experience in OneDrive Web with a refreshed Libraries view. Users can see more recently accessed libraries, navigate to default document libraries for Teams and favorite SharePoint sites, and use new filtering, sorting, and view options.</p>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566315","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-564605","title":"Outlook: Co-Authoring Highlight and Rewrite","desc":"<p>Users can now collaborate with Copilot to make improvements to email drafts. Select a section of the draft and ask Copilot to make changes, like changing its length, tone, or structure.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-26","modified":"2026-09-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564605","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-570965","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention-Archive File Classification Behavior Change for Windows Endpoints","desc":"<p>We are updating archive file classification behavior on Windows endpoints to align with cloud workloads. This change improves consistency, reduces noise in event reporting, and enhances performance when processing archive files.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570965","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1282683","title":"(Updated) Create and edit SharePoint pages with Copilot-powered AI","desc":"Updated September 10, 2026: We have have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are introducing Create and edit SharePoint pages with Copilot-powered AI, a new authoring experience that helps page editors plan, create, and refine SharePoint pages using natural language prompts. This feature reduces the time and effort required to build high-quality pages by allowing authors to generate and edit content, layouts, and web parts directly through an AI-assisted editing panel, grounded in their organization’s existing Microsoft 365 content.\n[When this will happen]\n• Targeted Release: We began rolling out in early April 2026 and expect to complete by mid-April 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We have begun rollout and expect to complete by late September 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• SharePoint page editors in Microsoft 365 tenants\n• Only users assigned a Microsoft 365 Copilot license\n• Production tenants (not GCC or Gallatin)\n\nWhat will happen\n• Page editors with a Copilot license will see a new AI authoring panel automatically open when editing SharePoint pages:\n\n• Users can:• Generate new page sections using natural language prompts:\n\n• Edit existing text, layouts, and web parts through chat-based instructions.\n• Attach Microsoft 365 files as grounding context for better AI-generated results:\n\n• AI-generated changes are inserted directly into the page and visually highlighted:\n\n• Users can switch between AI-assisted editing and standard manual editing at any time:\n\n• Chat history persists for the duration of the editing session unless manually cleared:\n\n• This feature is enabled by default for eligible users with Copilot licenses.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required to prepare for this change.\nRecommended actions:\n• Inform SharePoint page authors about the new AI-assisted editing experience.\n• Update internal documentation or training materials if you provide guidance on SharePoint authoring.\n• Ensure Copilot license assignments align with who should have access to AI-powered page creation.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed (for example, documents or page content)?Yes. Copilot uses existing SharePoint page content and user-selected Microsoft 365 files (such as documents) as grounding context to generate or edit page sections. Content is processed at the time of generation to produce suggestions and changes directly in the page editor.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI or agent capabilities that interact with customer data?Yes. This change introduces a Copilot-powered AI authoring experience in SharePoint. The AI assists users by generating and editing page content, layouts, and web parts based on prompts and selected Microsoft 365 content.\nDoes the change provide users a new way of interacting with generative AI?Yes. Page editors with a Copilot license can interact with generative AI directly within the SharePoint page editing experience using natural language chat prompts to plan, create, and modify content.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Yes. Access to the feature is governed by Microsoft Copilot license assignment. Only users assigned a Copilot license can access the AI authoring panel. There is no additional tenant-level toggle specific to this feature.\nDoes the change allow users to enable or disable the feature themselves?Yes. While the feature is available by default for Copilot-licensed users, users can choose when to use AI during page editing and can switch between AI-assisted editing and standard manual editing at any time.","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1282683","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567008","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): New Rich Answer Cards","desc":"<p>Surface new model-driven, dynamically placed Answer Cards across top 7 segments: weather, sports, finance, images, video, places and news for Entra &amp; MSA users across all surfaces.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-28","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567008","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-488142","title":"Microsoft Excel: Extending support for Insights Services to GCC-H and DoD sovereign clouds","desc":"<p>GCC-H and DoD sovereign cloud customers will be able to use features in Excel run by Insights Services, including Analyze Data found on the Data tab.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Excel"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-02","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488142","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566858","title":"Microsoft Teams: Clearer text highlighting in dark mode and high contrast mode","desc":"<p>We've improved how highlighted text looks when composing messages in dark mode and high contrast mode, giving you a more consistent editing experience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-03","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-553224","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Enhanced Topic Assignment","desc":"<p>We're upgrading our topic assignment pipeline to be powered by Copilot, delivering significantly improved accuracy in categorizing survey comments into relevant topics. Updated August 18, 2026: Rollout timing of this feature is now planned for end of August through early September. We apologize for any inconvenience.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553224","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-472031","title":"Data Loss Prevention- DLP Policy Change Insights with Security Copilot","desc":"<p>Copilot for Security in DLP can summarize DLP policies. This enhancement enables DLP admins to gain insights on coverage of policies viz. location, classifiers and notifications, and more.</p> <p>DLP admins can get these insights on all the policies or on few selected policies. They will be able to use prompts to gain deeper level view of how a policy is configured for their digital landscape. This helps them align their data posture on a regular basis and make corrections to policy posture as needed. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-20","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=472031","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2027","gaSort":202709},{"id":"rm-493742","title":"Microsoft Teams: Advanced Collaboration Analytics for GCC","desc":"<p>Advanced Collaboration Analytics for GGC provides Teams admins with insights into external collaboration patterns - covering teams, federated domains, channels, guests, and internal users - along with recommended actions to enhance security for external collaboration.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-28","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493742","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-569447","title":"Microsoft Teams: Breakout room support on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>With breakout room support, Teams Rooms on Android can be added to a breakout room and moved in and out of the main room making it easy for breakout session coordination.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569447","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-543713","title":"Microsoft Teams: Call quality feedback surveys for Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"<p>Users can now rate the quality of their calls and meetings and provide additional feedback on calling, video, and screen-sharing experiences to help organizations ensure consistent, high-quality experiences.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-08","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543713","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570440","title":"Outlook: Inline chat for email drafting","desc":"<p>Instead of opening Copilot Chat every time you want to use Copilot to draft a message, this change introduces an inline chat component that streamlines the process and lets you interact with Copilot without opening the sidebar.</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570440","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570647","title":"SharePoint: Changes to the FAQ web part authoring experience","desc":"<p>The SharePoint FAQ web part will provide a standard, non-AI experience for manually creating, editing, and managing FAQs. The AI-assisted FAQ creation and import will move to the Copilot in SharePoint authoring experience, where authors can use natural-language prompts and selected grounding sources to generate FAQ content that is saved to the compatible FAQ web part. Existing FAQ web parts and their content will continue to render without migration.</p>","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-09","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570647","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1146821","title":"(Updated) Rewrite with Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat coming soon to Edge for Business users","desc":"Updated September 9, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nIntroduction\nMicrosoft Edge for Business will soon support Rewrite, a new feature powered by Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat. This capability helps users draft and rephrase editable text directly within Edge, enhancing productivity and writing quality. Users can access Rewrite by highlighting editable text and right-clicking to open the context menu.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 420335.\nWhen this will happen\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling end of September 2026 (previously late August) and expect to complete rollout by late October 2026.\nHow this affects your organization\n• Rewrite will be enabled by default for Edge for Business users.\n• Users can access Rewrite by highlighting editable text and right-clicking to open the context menu.\n\n• If Microsoft 365 Copilot is restricted from accessing page content due to Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies, Rewrite will not function on that content.\n• Admins can manage this feature using the InlineComposeEnabled policy setting.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\nNo admin action is required before rollout.\nWe recommend:\n• Reviewing your current DLP configurations to understand how they may impact Rewrite functionality.\n• Notifying users about this new capability.\n• Updating internal documentation to reflect this change.\n\nLearn more about how DLP affects Copilot access to page content: Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in Edge and Access to Page Content | Microsoft Edge | Microsoft Learn\nCompliance considerations\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. This change introduces a new generative AI capability through Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat, allowing users to rewrite or draft text directly in Edge for Business.\nDoes the change provide end users any new way of interacting with generative AI?Yes. Users can interact with Copilot Chat by highlighting editable text and using the right-click context menu to access Rewrite, enabling AI-assisted drafting and rephrasing.\nDoes the change modify Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies or enforcement?Yes. If DLP policies restrict Copilot from accessing page content, the Rewrite feature will not function on that content.\nDoes the change include an admin control and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Yes. Admins can manage the availability of this feature using the InlineComposeEnabled policy setting.\nDoes the change allow a user to enable and disable the feature themselves?Yes. Users can choose to use the Rewrite feature by manually invoking it through the right-click context menu in Edge.","products":["Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-02","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1146821","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561204","title":"Planner: My Tasks redesign","desc":"<p>A redesigned My Tasks experience that brings your tasks into one place, making it easier to capture work, prioritize what matters, and stay focused.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561204","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567671","title":"Planner: Planner Agent chat in Basic Plans","desc":"<p>Introducing built-in Planner Agent chat with natural language Q&amp;A, smart task discovery, and in-plan task management.</p>","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567671","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-486828","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Apply a retention policy to Microsoft Planner content","desc":"<p>Introducing Data lifecycle management capabilities for Microsoft Planner. Compliance admins can now create a retention policy to manage content located in Microsoft Planner such as tasks for plans associated with an Microsoft 365 Group.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-01","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486828","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561857","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Topic Assignments Included in Comment Report Export","desc":"<p>When exporting comments to spreadsheet from the Comments report, the topic(s) assigned to each comment will be included in the export.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-499153","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Enhanced personalization with memory in Copilot","desc":"<p>Microsoft 365 Copilot will improve memory in Copilot by increasing the relevance and quality of Copilot responses based on previous communications. This AI-powered capability improves the relevance and quality of Copilot responses by learning from previous communications. These memories are private to the user.</p>","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2026-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499153","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Linux","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-570668","title":"Microsoft 365: Teams Channel Backup","desc":"<p>A backup and recovery feature that lets you recover team &amp; channel data (like files, messages exchanged over channels) in Microsoft Teams to a previously known good state after accidental changes or security compromises. Supported items include Team, Channels (Standard, Private, Public) and underlying data. Retention period supported is 30 days.</p>","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570668","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-560324","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - DLM Meter Change","desc":"<p>Data Lifecycle Management (DLM) billing will be based on the volume of data retained. For example, any number of non‑Microsoft 365 generative AI prompts and responses that collectively amount to 1 GB of retained data will be billed at $0.25 per GB per month (equivalent to ~$0.0082 per GB per day). In the updated model, DLM is billed based on the total volume of text messages managed by a DLM policy. Each non‑Microsoft 365 generative AI prompt and response is treated as an individual text message and is retained and deleted according to the configured Microsoft Purview retention settings. Billing is calculated on the managed text messages in storage, at a rate equivalent to $6 per one million text messages per month. Customer impact Customers will need to migrate from the legacy meter to the new meter. Based on current analysis, the overall cost impact is expected to be cost‑neutral or lower for customers under the new billing model.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560324","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-570842","title":"Dynamics 365 Finance: Support requirements of tax reform in Brazil in 2027","desc":"<p>Microsoft plans to introduce additional Globalization Studio capabilities to help support Brazil tax reform requirements, including the new IS tax type, tax assessment capabilities for reformed taxes, expanded fiscal note functionality for additional business scenarios, enhanced tax posting processes, and further updates to CNPJ-related processes. Additional capabilities will continue to be introduced as future phases of Brazil's tax reform are implemented.</p>","products":["Dynamics 365 Finance"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570842","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-561035","title":"Microsoft Edge: Allow M365 authentication popups in work profiles","desc":"<p>When users are signed in with a work account, some Microsoft 365 sites (for example, microsoft.com, cloud.microsoft, and microsoft365.com) may open authentication pop-up windows to Microsoft sign-in endpoints such as login.microsoftonline.com, login.live.com, or login.microsoft.com. These pop-ups are required to complete sign-in. Microsoft Edge now allows authentication pop-up windows from Microsoft first party services by default. Admins can control availability to this feature using the M365AuthPopupsInWorkEnabled policy.</p>","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561035","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-547749","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Export metrics in the Copilot Dashboard at Day Level","desc":"<p>This feature enables users to export fresher row-level Copilot metrics from the Copilot Dashboard for reporting and deeper analysis at day level. #copilotcontrolsystem</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-14","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547749","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570153","title":"Planner: Add times to task start, finish, and due dates","desc":"<p>Add specific times to task start, finish, and due dates. Define a plan’s time zone and working hours to automatically provide default task times and choose whether to view times in the plan’s time zone or your local time zone. This helps distributed teams coordinate effectively across time zones and keep deadlines clear.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570153","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-392838","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Introduction of secure workflow to bypass legal holds and retention policies","desc":"<p>The first release of Priority cleanup enables admins to create a recurring exception to delete items under a broader retention policy and/or legal hold on Exchange workload. Creating a Priority cleanup will require a separate security role, multiple approvers, and will have a complete audit trail.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-22","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=392838","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"February CY2025"},{"id":"rm-567319","title":"Outlook: Categorize Emails by Dragging Them onto a Favorite Category","desc":"<p>You can now add a category to your Favorites and then drag emails right onto it to apply that category. No need to open menus or right-click each message. Just pin the category you use most to Favorites, then drop your emails on it to tag them in one quick motion. It's a faster, more visual way to keep your inbox sorted the way you like. #newoutlookforwindows</p>","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567319","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569933","title":"Planner: Task History","desc":"<p>Task History helps keep teams up to date on changes made to a task. View recent activity to see what changed, when it changed, and track progress over time.</p>","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-08","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569933","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-568932","title":"Microsoft Teams: Collect information with list form in Workflows","desc":"<p>Starts a workflow with a form to collect the information you need to run the rest of your workflow.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568932","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-550513","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Upgraded music selection for Copilot AI Videos","desc":"<p>With a Microsoft365 Copilot license, Copilot AI-generated video projects have improved audio with realistic AI voiceover, professional sound effects, and enhanced audio mixing.</p>","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=550513","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557560","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): AI Generated video drafts include text animations and new layout options","desc":"<p>Users will find updated layouts and text animations on video projects generated with Copilot.</p>","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557560","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-566317","title":"Microsoft Viva: Create and customize PBI reports","desc":"<p>We are introducing a new feature for leaders and analysts of Viva Insights, where they can view a Power BI report, and edit time range, filters, attributes and change visuals as per their organizations' needs. They can then save the report for viewing later.</p>","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-19","modified":"2026-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566317","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-558928","title":"Planner: Microsoft Planner tab support for shared and private channels in Microsoft Teams","desc":"<p>Now you can add Microsoft Planner as a tab in shared and private channels in Microsoft Teams, which allows to create and manage tasks directly within the channel.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams","Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558928","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-564968","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: New text and shape animations in the video editor","desc":"<p>Clipchamp Editor will support simple animations for text layers. Users can apply preset in/out animations, adjust how long the animation lasts, choose its direction, and preview the animated text in the editor prior to exporting. This capability will be available across web and native desktop versions of Clipchamp.</p>","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-03","modified":"2026-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564968","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561033","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention – Device Health Reporting Dashboard","desc":"<p>This dashboard will allow admins to view the device health across all their devices to ensure the system is healthy and ready to receive policy updates and quickly identify devices that are not ready.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561033","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-553215","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create Videos in the Clipchamp Start Page","desc":"<p>Users can use Copilot to create videos directly from the Clipchamp Start page. Turn a simple prompt or existing document into a polished video in minutes. Copilot will automatically draft a script, selects visuals, add narration, and assembles the video for you—no video editing experience required. Review, refine, and export your video quickly, all in one flow.</p>","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553215","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"more":"https://m365.cloud.microsoft/launch/Clipchamp/"},{"id":"rm-570468","title":"Microsoft Teams: Automatic recording and transcription choices align with admin policies","desc":"<p>Meeting organizers will only see automatic recording and transcription choices in Meeting Options that are allowed by their organization's existing meeting policies. A new Record only choice lets organizers automatically start recording without starting transcription. Depending on the organizer's policies, available choices can include Record and transcribe, Transcribe only, Record only, and Off. When both recording and transcription are disabled by policy, the automatic setting is not shown.</p>","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-02","modified":"2026-09-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570468","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-570445","title":"Microsoft Purview: Auto-labeling scalability, policy management, and reporting enhancements","desc":"<p>Microsoft Purview is improving auto-labeling capabilities to help organizations manage and validate labeling policies at enterprise scale. These enhancements expand support for larger SharePoint scopes, improve policy management flexibility, and provide richer visibility into auto-labeling activity.</p>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-03","modified":"2026-09-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570445","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570433","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Deliver rich interactive app experiences in Copilot Studio agents","desc":"Copilot Studio agents can now render rich, interactive UI inline using MCP Apps, an extension of the Model Context Protocol. When an agent calls a UI-enabled tool from a compatible MCP server, interactive experiences like sortable tables and drilldowns render directly in the conversation. Users can now explore and act on data without leaving the chat or switching tools. A plain-text fallback keeps the agent working on surfaces that can't render the UI, and makers get this simply by connecting a compliant MCP server.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-02","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570433","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-494839","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Scanner data export for custom reporting","desc":"Learn about the state of your scanned repositories and create custom reports with the information protection scanner. Labeling, classification and protection actions on scanned files are stored in SQL tables that form a foundation to feed into custom reports.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-22","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569474","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Introducing an App- and Intent-First Agent Creation Experience","desc":"Copilot Studio is evolving to an app-first agent creation experience. Makers start with the application their agent will work with and configure the capabilities it needs. This update brings tools and knowledge into a more unified experience, simplifying how agents are created and configured.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-02","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569474","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569214","title":"Microsoft Teams: Copilot Chat for chats, channels, calls, and meetings in GCC, GCC High, and DoD","desc":"Copilot Chat will soon be available across chats, channels, calls, and meetings, helping users stay informed and catch up quickly.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569214","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1247902","title":"(Updated) SharePoint: AI citations analytics for documents and pages","desc":"Updated September 2, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are adding copilot citations to SharePoint to help site owners understand how their SharePoint documents, news posts, and pages are referenced by Microsoft 365 Copilot. These insights will help organizations track content value, identify high‑impact information, and understand how AI‑powered workflows use SharePoint content. Tenants must have Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses, and these insights become available only for tenants with more than 50 Copilot licenses (seats).\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 480725.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): Rollout will begin end of August 2026 (previously start of August) and will complete by end of September 2026 (previously early September).\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected:\n• SharePoint Online site owners, content authors, and admins.\n• Tenants with more than 50 Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses (seats).\n\nWhat will happen:\nThe following updates will appear in SharePoint:\n• SharePoint Popular content in Site Usage will display documents, news posts, and pages ranked by how often they are cited by Copilot chat.\n• SharePoint page analytics will include a new Total citations card showing the number of times a page or news post is referenced in Copilot chat responses.\n• SharePoint file statistics will include a new AI citations metric displayed alongside existing metrics such as views and viewers.\n• A new Copilot citations analytics page will appear under Site Usage. It will provide:• The number of users who consume site content through Copilot chat citations.\n• The total number of citations for the site.\n• The most frequently cited documents, news posts, and pages.\n\nIn this release, citations are counted only from Microsoft 365 Copilot chat on desktop and web (Microsoft 365 Copilot chat at m365.cloud.microsoft/chat and the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on desktop). All other Copilot experiences and agents are out of scope, including Copilot in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Cowork, Copilot in SharePoint, SharePoint custom agents, Copilot Studio agents accessed outside Copilot, custom engine agents, and agents that use a custom orchestrator. This scope may expand in future releases.\nThis feature will be on by default and will not require admin action to enable.\n\nScreenshot 1 - AI citations aggregated across site content in the Site analytics view:\n\nScreenshot 2 - AI citations shown for an individual SharePoint page or news post in Page analytics:\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo admin action is required before the rollout.\nYou may want to:\n• Inform site owners and content authors about the new analytics.\n• Review your SharePoint usage and analytics processes to understand how the new AI citation metrics may support governance, content lifecycle planning, and content strategy.\n• Update internal documentation or training materials.\n• Provide guidance to users on Copilot licensing requirements if your organization centrally manages those licenses.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-09","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1247902","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561648","title":"Microsoft Teams: Town hall media optimization for VDI attendees","desc":"What’s new Teams now supports audio and video offloading for Town hall attendees in VDI environments that are using the new optimization. Media streams are offloaded directly to the user’s local device, improving performance and delivering a high definition viewing experience while reducing virtual desktop resource usage. Who it applies to • Windows endpoints only using the new VDI optimization • Supported VDI platforms: o Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365 o Citrix o Omnissa o Amazon WorkSpaces What stays the same All attendee interactivity features remain supported, including captions, DVR, reactions, streaming chat, and Q&A. Additional details First party and third party eCDNs are supported. When enabled, the attendee’s endpoint establishes a direct peer to peer connection using the local device network, avoiding virtual desktop double hop traffic. Action required No action is required if the new optimization for Microsoft Teams is already enabled.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561648","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-565215","title":"Microsoft Teams: Automatic recording and transcription for Teams Call Queues","desc":"Administrators can enable automatic recording and transcription for Teams call queues. When enabled, calls answered by calling representatives are automatically recorded without manual action. Admins configure the feature per queue via Teams admin center or PowerShell, with controls for recording, transcription and agent access to recordings. Recordings are stored in SharePoint and available through the Queues app call history. Note: Queues app requires a Teams Premium license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565215","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-558852","title":"Microsoft Teams: Digital signage support for Teams panels","desc":"Digital signage can now be displayed on idle Teams panel devices, similar to digital signage support for Microsoft Teams Rooms front of room displays. Signage source and settings can be configured in the Pro Management portal. Available with Teams Rooms Pro or Shared space-licensed spaces.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561031","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced bookable desk experience with Teams panel-based desk dock devices","desc":"Users have better experiences in flexible work environments with Microsoft Teams panel-based desk dock devices coming later this year. The Teams panel app now enables devices, such as the Yealink Linkhub, to enhance bookable desk experiences by indicating at-a-glance availability and letting visitors book directly on the device. Each device requires a Teams Shared Space license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561031","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-564912","title":"Microsoft Teams: New room optimization mode user experience in Teams desktop","desc":"Users can more easily use their laptop for meetings and collaboration in spaces like focus or huddle rooms that don’t yet have a Teams Rooms system. The new room optimization mode replaces shared display mode, has a new location, and enables or disables room-specific features. When room peripherals are connected, Teams can automatically select audio and video devices, enable speaker recognition and shared display, and disable voice isolation.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-10","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564912","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-495002","title":"Microsoft Teams: Slash commands for apps","desc":"You can now interact with your favorite apps directly from Teams chat and channels compose box using slash commands. Type / and start interacting with Apps and Agents, invoke workflows and more.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-02","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495002","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-564614","title":"Microsoft Teams: Meeting recap app","desc":"The meeting recap app brings all your meeting recaps into one place, making it easier to find, filter, and catch up. Quick filters help you surface the right meetings instantly, while audio recap lets you efficiently review multiple meetings at once. You can also browse and revisit any recap from the past 30 days.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-05","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564614","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-565131","title":"Microsoft Teams: Multi-line Calling on Teams Mobile","desc":"Make and receive calls using multiple assigned phone numbers directly from your mobile device - choose the right line for every call, with unified call history and seamless switching across all your lines.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-04","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565131","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-562050","title":"Microsoft Teams: Support human interpreter listening mode in Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows now supports human interpreter listening mode in meetings where organizers enable language interpretation in Meeting options, allowing room participants to select a language and hear interpreter audio.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-18","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562050","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561604","title":"Microsoft Teams: Chat panel open by default in the gallery view on Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"The chat panel will open by default in gallery view, allowing participants in Teams Room on Android to quickly see ongoing meeting chat when they join. Admins can configure this default device behavior, and users can close the panel in one tap during meetings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-07","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561604","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-555235","title":"Microsoft Teams: One-stop admin portal for Teams devices with Teams Rooms Pro Management","desc":"Admins now have a one-stop portal for inventory, health monitoring, management, and analytics for both Windows and Android devices with the Pro Management portal. Management of all Android Teams rooms, panels, and phone devices are transitioning to this portal from the Teams admin center, enabling easy, consistent, and secure management of Teams devices across all operating systems and manufacturers.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555235","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560323","title":"Microsoft Teams: Profanity filter is disabled by default for captions","desc":"We are updating the default profanity filter setting for live captions from On to Off across Teams meetings, calls, events, and Microsoft Teams Rooms (MTR) devices to improve accessibility and align with EU requirements. This change will only affect users who have never configured their live captions profanity filter preference. Users who have already set their preference will keep their current setting. As a result, some users may begin seeing unfiltered profanity in live captions by default after this rollout. Users can update this preference in settings at any time.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558679","title":"Microsoft Teams: Standardized preview experience for Word, PowerPoint, and Excel files","desc":"Microsoft Word, Microsoft PowerPoint, and Microsoft Excel files now open in a standardized preview in Teams on Android and iOS, delivering faster performance, improved reliability, and a more consistent viewing experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558679","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559608","title":"Microsoft Teams: Quick access to read items from unread-only view","desc":"Teams chat and channel lists can be filtered to show unread items only. When this filter is applied, hovering over a section reveals an eye icon next to the section name. Selecting the eye icon opens a list of read chats or channels within that section, allowing you to open them without leaving the unread-only view.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559608","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-501120","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Federated Copilot Connectors","desc":"Microsoft is announcing the General Availability (GA) of federated Copilot connectors for Microsoft 365 Copilot. Federated Copilot connectors enable users to securely connect Copilot to popular third‑party sources and retrieve data in real time using the Model Context Protocol (MCP). These connectors do not store or index customer data in Microsoft services; access occurs in real time using the user’s identity, while administrators retain full governance and control through the Microsoft 365 admin center. With GA, federated Copilot connectors will be supported in Researcher agent, Microsoft 365 Chat, and Agent Mode in Excel, enabling users to bring external data directly into their workflows.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501120","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-529850","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Meeting Prepare from Up Next","desc":"Get timely reminders in Outlook mobile to prepare for your meetings with Copilot. The Up Next card now offers a Prepare option so you can get ready with one tap.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529850","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-567885","title":"Microsoft 365: Entra ID Backup & Recovery","desc":"Enable extended 30-day backup and recovery for a tenant's Entra objects via the Microsoft 365 Backup native app or M365 Backup Storage platform APIs. This capability allows customers and ISV apps to do a point in time restore of Entra objects to a last known good state to a rolling historical 30-day point. Advanced recovery features are currently limited to the Entra admin portal, but some user recovery actions will be possible via the M365 Backup native app UX in the M365 Admin center. Note that the existing 7-day recovery that comes with a customer's P1 & P2 licenses is already generally available and is independent of this roadmap item.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567885","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-569446","title":"Microsoft Entra: Enhanced Security Accounts Manager (sAM) Account Name support for Microsoft Entra Domain Services","desc":"Enhanced support for synchronizing the Security Accounts Manager account name (sAMAccountName) with Microsoft Entra Domain Services is now in Public Preview. This feature allows sAMAccountName to be populated from the onPremisesSamAccountName attribute in Microsoft Entra ID. Existing managed domains can enable the new synchronization behavior, while it is enabled by default for new managed domains. When enabled, existing hybrid users are updated during synchronization; cloud-only users without an onPremisesSamAccountName value continue to use mailNickname-based generation. The feature is available for Enterprise and Premium SKUs.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569446","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557675","title":"Outlook: Share Word, Excel, and PowerPoint local files via the new Outlook for Windows","desc":"When working in an open Word, Excel, or PowerPoint file, users will now be able to send a copy of the locally stored file by email through the new Outlook for Windows. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557675","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-561026","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Generate documents using forms in SharePoint with Power Automate","desc":"We are introducing a new Power Automate action that enables automated document generation using document generation (DocGen) forms in SharePoint. Generate document from form (Preview) allows customers to create documents from a template by mapping data inputs to predefined template fields. Documents are generated as part of an automated flow and stored in SharePoint. This capability supports scenarios such as creating contracts, invoices, letters, or reports using structured templates and form-driven inputs. The action works by mapping input data to template fields and returns the generated document along with file metadata such as location and status.","products":["Power Automate","SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-30","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561026","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-495465","title":"Microsoft Places: Microsoft Places Support to GCC cloud","desc":"Microsoft Places features will now be available in GCC cloud","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-23","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495465","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-570444","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - New Survey Owner role provides access to survey results","desc":"When a new program is being set up in Glint, there is now an option to designate Survey Owners. Those added as Survey Owners will be able to view and manage certain aspects of the program, as well as see the results when a survey in the program closes.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570444","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1311978","title":"(Updated) Classic Outlook for Windows: User-initiated insights with Copilot","desc":"Updated September 1, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe're introducing User Initiated Insights in Copilot for classic Outlook for Windows, enabling users to manually select text within an email and prompt Copilot to provide contextual insights. This enhancement gives users greater control over when and how Copilot assists them, improving productivity, clarity, and decision-making directly within their workflow.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 508524.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview (Worldwide): We began rolling out in early May 2026 and expect to complete by late May 2026.\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in early October 2026 (previously early September) and expect to complete by end of October 2026 (previously end of September).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Users with Microsoft 365 Copilot capabilities\n\n• Organizations using classic Outlook for Windows\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Users will be able to highlight text in emails and invoke Copilot to generate insights.\nScreenshot: When text is highlighted in an email, an Explain This button appears to provide additional context:\n\n• Functionality is built into the Outlook experience and does not require a separate add-in.\n\n• The feature will be on by default for eligible users.\n\n• Existing Microsoft 365 security, compliance, and data protection policies continue to apply.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• If you do not want users to access this feature, remove or restrict Copilot capabilities.\n• Verify users are running the latest version of classic Outlook for Windows.\n• Inform helpdesk and support staff about this new Copilot interaction model.\n• Communicate to users how to select text and invoke Copilot for contextual insights.\n\nLearn more:\n• How do I enable or disable Microsoft Copilot on MS 365 Premium | Microsoft Learn\n• Instructions to turn off Copilot | Microsoft Support\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nCompliance areaExplanation\nIntroduces AI/ML capabilities interacting with customer data.The feature enables Copilot to process user-selected email content to generate insights.\nProvides a new way for users to interact with generative AI.Users can invoke Copilot directly by selecting text within emails.\nAllows users to enable or disable the feature at use time.Users control invocation by choosing when to select text and engage Copilot.","products":["Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1311978","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1158329","title":"(Updated) Microsoft 365 Copilot: Updates to memory and personalization","desc":"Updated September 1, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction:]\nWe’re updating Memory in Microsoft 365 Copilot to improve personalization and enhance the user experience. With this update, Copilot will personalize responses using chat history, helping users receive more relevant and contextual replies. We’re also introducing refreshed user controls in Copilot settings to make it easier to view and manage Saved Memory. This will be available to all Copilot Chat users.\n\nControl over personalization using chat history is also available, with details for users via the settings screen.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Public Preview (Frontier): Begins rolling out mid-November 2025.\n• General Availability: Begins mid-September 2026 (previously early January) and is expected to complete by late October 2026 (previously late July).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nAll users of Microsoft 365 Copilot in tenants where Memory is enabled.\nWhat will happen:\n• Copilot will use chat history to personalize responses, making interactions more tailored and helpful:\n\n• Users will see a redesigned Memory settings page that improves visibility and control over what Copilot remembers.\n• Existing admin and user-level Memory settings are respected. If Memory is toggled off, it will remain off.\n• No changes to admin controls or policy enforcement.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• Review the updated Memory settings experience with your users once available.\n• No admin action is required unless you wish to update internal documentation or training materials.\n\nLearn more:\n• Enhanced personalization control overview | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\n• enhancedPersonalizationSetting resource type | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed (e.g. documents, emails, chats, etc.)?Yes. Copilot will now use chat history to personalize responses, which changes how existing customer data is processed to generate contextual replies.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. This update enhances Copilot’s personalization model by incorporating chat history, allowing it to generate more tailored responses.\nDoes the change provide end users any new way of interacting with generative AI?Yes. Users will receive more personalized and contextual responses from Copilot based on their prior chat interactions.\nDoes the change allow a user to enable and disable the feature themselves?Yes. Users can manage what Copilot remembers through the updated Memory settings page in Copilot settings.","products":["Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-23","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1158329","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1188222","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Private chat for organizers and presenters in structured meetings, webinars, and town halls","desc":"Updated September 1, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe’re introducing a private chat feature for organizers, co-organizers, and presenters in structured meetings and webinars in Microsoft Teams. This separate chat enhances collaboration by allowing key participants to communicate privately before, during, and after the event, without involving attendees. Additionally, we are unifying backroom chat behavior in town halls to ensure consistent functionality across all structured meetings. Currently, backroom chat behavior varies depending on whether streaming chat is enabled for town halls and whether the organizer has a Teams Premium license. This update removes that inconsistency.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 392328 and applies to Teams for Windows desktop, Teams for Mac desktop, Teams for the web, Teams for iOS/Android, MTR-W and MTR-A devices.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Targeted Release: Rollout begins in mid-October 2026 (previously late September) and is expected to complete by late October 2026 (previously late August).\n• General Availability (Worldwide and GCC): Rollout begins in late October 2026 (previously mid-September) and is expected to complete by late November 2026 (previously early November).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected: Admins managing Microsoft Teams meetings, webinars, and town halls.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• New private chat for organizers, co-organizers, and presenters: This chat is separate from attendee chat and is available before, during, and after the event.\n\n• Unified backroom chat policy for town halls: The default setting will be ON for all town halls, regardless of streaming chat availability or license type.\n\n• Existing town halls will adopt the new policy once meeting options are updated.\n\n• If admins turn the backroom chat policy OFF, previously enabled town halls will lose access after update.\n\n• Non-TPre town halls (those without a Teams Premium license) will have backroom chat ON by default after rollout and update.\n\nTwo potential impacts:\n\n• If an admin explicitly turns the new backroom chat policy OFF, any already-scheduled town hall that previously had backroom chat ON will lose access once the meeting options are updated.\n\n• For non-TPre town halls where backroom chat was previously OFF, it will switch to ON by default after the rollout and a meeting options update.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Review your Teams meeting policies and decide whether to enable private chat for organizers and presenters.\n\n• Communicate this change to helpdesk staff and event organizers.\n\n• Update internal documentation to reflect the new backroom chat behavior.\n\n• If you want to disable backroom chat, adjust the policy in the Teams admin center.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1188222","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1245222","title":"(Updated) Outlook: Share Word, Excel and PowerPoint local files via the new Outlook for Windows","desc":"Updated September 1, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re adding support for sending locally stored Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files as email attachments directly through the new Outlook for Windows. This update streamlines the sharing experience and aligns with ongoing efforts to bring feature parity between classic Outlook for Windows and the new Outlook.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557675.\n[When this will happen]\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in early November 2026 (previously early September) and expect to complete by early December 2026 (previously late September).\n• General Availability (GCC): We will begin rolling out in mid-January 2027 (previously early October 2026) and expect to complete by mid-February 2027 (previously late October 2026).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Users working with locally stored Word, Excel, or PowerPoint files (not stored in OneDrive).\n• Organizations adopting or transitioning to the new Outlook for Windows.\n\nWhat will happen\n• Users can now share local Office files as email attachments directly through the new Outlook for Windows.\n• Users will no longer need to rely on the classic Outlook for Windows to send local file attachments.\n• This feature is ON by default.\n• There is no change to existing admin controls or policies, and all existing Outlook/Exchange policies continue to apply.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo admin action is required.\nTo prepare your organization, you may:\n• Inform help desk staff about this update to reduce support inquiries.\n• Update your internal documentation if it references classic Outlook workflows.\n• Encourage users to adopt the new Outlook for Windows if your organization is transitioning away from classic Outlook.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1245222","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1069563","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Usage reports to manage metered consumption costs for Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat (preview)","desc":"Updated September 1, 2026: We have updated the timeline below. Thank you for your patience.\n\nTo help you manage metered consumption costs for Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat, we will introduce a new Message consumption usage report in the Microsoft 365 admin center. The new report will give you visibility into billed messages associated with your Microsoft 365 Copilot pay-as-you-go billing policies and includes total messages consumed, cumulative and daily time series, and messages per user, per billing policy, per agent, and per agent-user pair. The new report will roll out in preview. During the preview stage, the report will display a maximum of 30 days of message consumption history. Usage information from prior to May 3, 2025, will not be available in the report.\nThis message refers to Microsoft Copilot in a pay-as-you-go model. A Microsoft Copilot license is not required.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 490738.\n[When this will happen:]\n\nPublic Preview: Available now.\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in early January 2027 (previously September 2026) and expect to complete by end of January 2027 (previously end of September 2026).\n[How this will affect your organization:]\n\nAfter you have set up pay-as-you-go billing for Microsoft 365 Copilot, either in the Microsoft 365 admin center or the Microsoft Power Platform admin center, and you have enabled agent usage in your organization, you will see a new report including metrics for messages consumed at the levels of tenant, users, agents, and agent-user. To help you mitigate overspending, you will see alerts when users have consumed more than 2000 billed messages.\n\nThis new report will be on by default and will be available in the Microsoft admin center at Reporting > Usage > Microsoft 365 Copilot > Message consumption:\n\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\n\nThis rollout will happen automatically by the specified date with no admin action required before the rollout. You may want to notify any admins that manage agents on the integrated apps page about this feature.\n\nLearn more: Microsoft 365 reports in the admin center - Message consumption","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-07","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1069563","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-570431","title":"Microsoft 365: Organizational Data Service is now available in GCC-High","desc":"We’re excited to announce that Microsoft 365 Organizational Data Service is now available in the GCC-High (GCC-H) environment! Microsoft 365 Organizational Data Service enables rapid ingestion of organizational/HR data through connectors from multiple HRIS systems using a single unified ingestion point. This service also provides organizational data for use across Microsoft Copilot and Microsoft 365 apps to power various features with robust data quality framework that detects, communicates, and provides solutions for data quality issues before data is used.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570431","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-503144","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Domain exclusion for web grounding","desc":"This feature will allow admins to specify a limited set of sites to exclude from web grounding in M365 Copilot and Copilot Chat #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503144","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-570434","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Enabling makers to require human approval for tool calls","desc":"Copilot Studio now let’s makers require human approval before an agent runs specific tools. With a per-tool, per-agent toggle, any gated tool call pauses and shows an approval request describing what the agent intends to do, so a person can approve, approve for the session, or deny before the action runs. This gives organizations a deterministic guardrail for high-stakes or sensitive operations like sending emails, closing tickets, or processing payments, independent of the agent's instructions. Approval requests appear inline in the channel where the agent is deployed, including Microsoft Teams and Microsoft 365 Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570434","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-570435","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Streamlining experiences from Copilot Studio Agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"This update is meant to bridge the experience of using Copilot Studio agents in M365 Copilot with the Copilot Chat experience. With these updates, agent responses in Copilot Chat will look (similar formatting, compressed chain of thought), feel (smoother streaming, resume/retry and voice dictation) and behave (deliver clickable citations and tool execution traces) very similarly to Copilot Chat responses themselves.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570435","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568784","title":"Microsoft Defender for Identity: Unified identity timeline on the Identity page","desc":"The updated identity timeline provides security teams with a single chronological view of activity and alerts associated with an identity and its linked accounts. It normalizes activity from integrated Microsoft security products, including Microsoft Entra sign-ins, Microsoft Graph audit events, SaaS and cloud activity, and device logons. New fields and filters include Source table, Session ID, and Unique token identifier, with expanded Conditional Access and event context.","products":["Microsoft 365 Defender","Microsoft Defender"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568784","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569477","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Default Protection Controls for Exchange Online in the event of classification failure","desc":"Default protection controls for Exchange Online is available in public preview. This release gives administrators fine-grained control to create DLP policies based on specific classification or text extraction failure types — such as timeout, throttling and other scan errors — rather than one blanket policy for all failure conditions.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569477","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-566201","title":"Microsoft Teams: Block all identified external bots automatically from joining your meetings","desc":"Extending the admin controls provided for managing external AI bots and regulating their access to your meetings, we are adding the option to automatically block all identified bots.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-22","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566201","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569017","title":"Microsoft Teams: Intelligent call recaps in Queues app","desc":"Spend less time catching up on call recordings to resolve customer issues faster. For recorded call queue calls, the Queues app now supports intelligent call recaps for recorded calls that includes AI-generated summary notes, key discussion points, and follow-up actions. Navigate to the call record in the Queues app and select the Recap tab to access.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569017","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-561914","title":"Microsoft Teams: Mandatory pre-meeting consent","desc":"We are providing a new configuration experience in Teams Admin Center where tenant admins can enable and customize an explicit consent message before joining any meeting hosted in their organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561914","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567469","title":"Microsoft Teams: PowerPoint Live Light theme support","desc":"Presenting PowerPoint slides in Teams just got better. PowerPoint Live now supports light mode, giving presenters the option to present in light, dark, classic, or high contrast mode based on their preferences and system settings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567469","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-570428","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Insights and Copilot Analytics in GCC-High","desc":"Microsoft Viva Insights and Copilot Analytics are coming to Microsoft 365 Government Community Cloud High (GCC High), providing eligible organizations with privacy-protected, role-based analytics experiences to help them understand Microsoft 365 Copilot adoption, usage, and impact. Viva Insights also provides data-driven behavioral insights into how employees collaborate, helping organizations improve productivity and wellbeing within the GCC High environment.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570428","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569720","title":"SharePoint: PowerShell support for brand fonts deletion","desc":"Microsoft SharePoint is introducing PowerShell support for deleting brand font files from the Brand Fonts library used by the SharePoint Brand Center. With the new Remove-SPOFontFile cmdlet, SharePoint administrators can remove brand font files that are no longer approved, licensed, or needed across their organization in SharePoint.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-09-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569720","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567891","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Power BI integration in M365 Copilot","desc":"This release enables M365 Copilot to reason over Power BI enterprise data and returns grounded answers directly from Power BI reports and semantic models. Users can ask natural‑language questions and receive accurate answers.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-20","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567891","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564765","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - User Based Aggregation of DLP Alerts","desc":"Enable aggregation of DLP alerts based on common entities user even when multiple rules are matched. This feature should consolidate related alert events into a single alert object to: Reduce alert noise, simplify investigation workflows, enhance contextual understanding of violations.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564765","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560702","title":"Microsoft Teams: Security Detection Report in Teams Admin Center","desc":"A new Security Detection Report in the Teams admin center provides a centralized view of messaging security detections, including impersonation, malicious URLs, and weaponizable file types. Admins can review detection activity in one place and export detailed data to support investigation and response. This capability helps consolidate security signals for Teams messaging scenarios.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560702","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561038","title":"SharePoint: Admin Center - detailed report on Everyone except external user permissions","desc":"The new report provides SharePoint Advanced Management admins complete item level details of permissions granted to Everyone except external user and Everyone special SharePoint groups.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561038","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566866","title":"Planner: Task Details Side Pane experience","desc":"The Task Details Side Pane lets you view and edit task details in a side pane while keeping your Board, Grid, or My Tasks view visible. Update tasks without losing context or switching back and forth from modal dialogs.","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-02","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566866","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-558539","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced cross-platform join via SIP for Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"Enable Teams Rooms on Android to join third-party meetings via SIP, delivering seamless cross-platform interoperability. This capability ensures users can connect to external meeting services directly from Teams Rooms, maintaining a consistent and reliable meeting experience across diverse environments. Available on Teams Rooms Pro license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558539","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-503955","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updates to Memory and Personalization in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"Copilot now uses chat history to provide more relevant, contextual responses. Updated settings make it easier to view and manage what Copilot remembers and your personalization preferences.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-23","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503955","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-487836","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Employee Self-Service Agent in M365 Copilot","desc":"The Employee Self-Service Agent in M365 Copilot expedites answers for the most common workplace policy-related questions and takes action on key HR and IT related tasks, connecting employees to authorized knowledge bases and HR/IT systems of record for faster resolution time and a streamlined employee experience.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-08","modified":"2026-09-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487836","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mobile","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-570155","title":"SharePoint: Site Skills in Copilot in SharePoint","desc":"The feature introduces enhanced Site Skills management capabilities, including skill editing, version control, publishing, restoration, and cross-site duplication, enabling organizations to govern and reuse skills more effectively across SharePoint sites.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-31","modified":"2026-08-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570155","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-519573","title":"Universal Print: audit logging","desc":"I can access Universal Print audit records of key administrator and user activities, such as print job submissions, configuration changes, and printer registrations. Audit records will be available in Microsoft Purview’s Unified Audit Log for compliance and long-term record-keeping.","products":["Universal Print"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=519573","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-396782","title":"Universal Print: Logs and alerts","desc":"With a new Azure Monitor integration, Universal Print customers can send detailed diagnostic logs to a Log Analytics workspace to conduct troubleshooting and configure custom alerts.","products":["Universal Print"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-20","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=396782","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569475","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Agent Sharing amongst makers","desc":"Enables sharing of agents with other makers in the new GHCP harness. Makers can grant other makers Agent Viewer (view analytics/evaluations only) or Editor (view, edit, configure, share, publish) access to an agent, with auto-assigned security roles.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-27","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569475","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567320","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Copilot admin configuration assistance","desc":"A Copilot-powered conversational assistant embedded in the Viva Glint admin experience that answers configuration and how-to questions and provides step-by-step guidance. Responses will include deep links to configuration pages streamlining navigation and discoverability. Only available for Viva Glint users with Admin permissions.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-08-03","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567320","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1230889","title":"(Updated) Outlook for Windows report retirement in the Exchange admin center","desc":"Updated August 28, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo streamline and modernize reporting experiences across Microsoft 365, we are retiring the Outlook for Windows Usage Report in the Exchange admin center (EAC). Admins can continue accessing Outlook usage information in the Microsoft 365 admin center (MAC), which offers a more complete and up‑to‑date reporting experience across Microsoft 365 apps.\n[When this will happen]\n• Retirement will begin in early November 2026 (previously mid-August).\n• Retirement will complete in late November 2026 (previously mid-September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Admins who use the Exchange admin center (EAC) to view Outlook for Windows usage data.\n\nWhat will happen\n• The Outlook for Windows Usage Report will be removed from the EAC.\n• No replacement Outlook usage reporting will remain in the EAC after this retirement.\n• Admins can continue accessing Outlook for Windows usage insights through the Microsoft 365 admin center (MAC): Reports > Usage > M365 Apps > Usage > Outlook for Windows\n• MAC provides consolidated usage reporting with charts and tables to help admins understand usage patterns across Outlook and other Microsoft 365 apps.\n• No impact to Outlook for Windows functionality for users.\n• This report retirement will occur automatically; no opt‑out or admin toggle will be available.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• No admin action is required.\n• If your organization references the EAC usage report in documentation or internal processes, update those materials before the retirement is complete.\n\nLearn more: Microsoft 365 Reports in the admin center - Microsoft 365 Apps usage | Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1230889","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1268933","title":"(Updated) Viva Engage: Pinned resources and related communities in Teams for iOS","desc":"Updated August 28, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe're improving the Viva Engage experience in Microsoft Teams for iOS by bringing pinned resources and related communities into the Teams mobile app. Pinned resources highlight important links and files within a community, while related communities help users discover other relevant Viva Engage communities. These are two separate features that work together to improve information access and community discovery.\nThis update aligns the iOS experience with Engage on the web, the Engage mobile app, and Teams for Android, helping users discover important content and related communities more easily—especially those who rely on Teams on iOS as their primary communication tool.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 559107.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in mid-June 2026 (previously late May) and is expected to complete by end of September 2026 (previously mid-August).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Users who access Viva Engage communities in Microsoft Teams on iOS\n\n• Community admins who manage Viva Engage communities\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Users will see pinned resources for a community directly within Teams on iOS.\n\n• Users will see related communities surfaced within the community experience.\n\n• The experience will match what is already available in the Viva Engage mobile app, Viva Engage on the web, and Teams for Android.\n\n• The feature is enabled by default.\n\n• There are no changes to existing admin policies or configurations.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\nNo admin action is required.\n\n• Communicate this update to end users who use Teams on iOS.\n\n• Encourage Viva Engage community admins to review pinned resources and related communities.\n\n• Update internal documentation or helpdesk guidance, if applicable.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-02","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1268933","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567883","title":"Microsoft Teams: Unified Agent and App Installation Management Across Microsoft 365 and Teams Admin Center","desc":"Administrators using the Microsoft 365 admin center and Teams admin center will be able to apply app and agent installation changes once and have them consistently enforced across Teams, Outlook, and Microsoft 365 Copilot. Previously, installation changes made in the Microsoft 365 admin center only applied to Outlook and Microsoft 365, while changes made in the Teams admin center only applied to Teams. With this update, app and agent installation is unified across all supported surfaces, enabling a more consistent and streamlined admin experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-20","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567883","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567317","title":"Minecraft Education: Learning Cubed Update with Cross-Tenant Multiplayer and Latest Bedrock Features","desc":"The Learning Cubed Update introduces cross-tenant multiplayer for dedicated servers and key features from the latest Bedrock updates.","products":["Minecraft Education"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567317","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557189","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Ability to preview content in Insider Risk Management Alerts","desc":"Insider Risk Management is excited to announce the ability to preview content directly within an IRM alert without having to create a case. Users with appropriate permissions will be able to preview relevant files referenced directly within activity explorer in each alert. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557189","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558448","title":"Microsoft Agent 365: the control plane for agents","desc":"Agent 365 is the control plane for AI agents. It empowers IT and security administrators to observe, govern, and secure agents across Microsoft 365 and connected platforms at scale.","products":["Microsoft Agent 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-24","modified":"2026-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558448","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-549288","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Adaptive Scopes for DLP for SharePoint","desc":"Adaptive Scope for SharePoint is a dynamic scoping capability in Microsoft Purview DLP that allows administrators to automatically target DLP policies to the right sites based on attributes such as site URL, site name, or custom site metadata. Unlike static scoping, which requires manually listing sites and maintaining them over time, adaptive scopes continuously evaluate site properties and auto‑include or exclude locations as they evolve. This enables scalable policy deployment, eliminates the 100‑site static policy limit, and delivers granular, and automated targeting.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-21","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=549288","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-570069","title":"Outlook: Offline settings \"Days of email to save\" admin policy","desc":"Tenant admins will be able to define the default value for \"Days of email to save\" in Offline settings and designate whether end users can change the setting. This policy will set and enforce the \"Days of email to save\" setting found under Settings > General > Offline. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-27","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=570069","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568937","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Data Quality Report for Profile Data","desc":"Microsoft 365 Organizational Data Services is introducing a new data quality report that helps administrators assess the coverage and health of people data used across Microsoft 365 experiences. High-quality people data enables users to more effectively discover and learn about colleagues through experiences such as the People Card, Org Explorer, Microsoft 365 Copilot, and Microsoft 365 Cowork. The new report provides organizational data administrators, People Administrators, and AI Administrators with visibility into the completeness and quality of people attributes available in Microsoft 365. Administrators can use these insights to identify data gaps, improve attribute coverage, and help ensure users and AI-powered experiences have access to accurate organizational information. Key benefits: - Monitor the health and completeness of people profile attributes across the organization. - Identify missing or incomplete organizational data that may impact user and AI experiences. - Improve discoverability and organizational understanding in People Card and Org Explorer. - Help increase the effectiveness of Microsoft 365 Copilot and Microsoft 365 Cowork by improving the quality of underlying people data. This feature is available to Organizational Data Administrators, People Administrators, and AI Administrators through Microsoft 365 Organizational Data Services.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-27","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568937","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569476","title":"Planner: Conditional Coloring","desc":"Conditional Coloring highlight tasks based on selected criteria, making priorities, status, and important task details easier to spot.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-27","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569476","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1234571","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | Data Loss Prevention – Adaptive scopes for DLP for SharePoint","desc":"Updated August 27, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nAdaptive scopes for SharePoint DLP policies in Microsoft Purview enable you to target SharePoint sites based on site attributes instead of manually maintaining static site lists. As sites are created or updated, adaptive scopes automatically adjust membership, ensuring that DLP policies remain aligned to your environment without ongoing manual updates.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 549288.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: We began rollout in early February 2026 and expect to complete by late‑February 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rollout in early January 2027 (previously late August 2026) and expect to complete by late January 2027 (previously late September).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\nWho is affected: Admins who manage Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies for SharePoint in Microsoft Purview.\nWhat will happen:\nWith adaptive scopes for SharePoint, your organization will -\n• Apply DLP policies more efficiently and at scale.\n• Automatically target the correct SharePoint sites based on attributes such as URL, name, or metadata.\n• Ensure new or updated sites are protected without manual list maintenance.\n• Reduce administrative overhead by removing the need to maintain static site lists.\n• Maintain consistent DLP policy coverage as your SharePoint environment grows and changes.\n\nAdditional notes:\n• There is no impact to user workflows.\n• The feature is not enabled by default; admins must create and assign adaptive scopes.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nTo prepare for this update, you can:\n• Verify licensing and permissions.\n• Ensure your tenant has Microsoft 365 E5 or E5 Compliance licensing and that you hold the required Purview roles.\n• Learn more: Configure adaptive scopes - Adaptive Scopes | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n• Navigate to Adaptive scopes.\n• Go to Microsoft Purview compliance portal → Settings → Roles & scopes → Adaptive scopes (screenshot 1):\n\n• Create an adaptive scope.\n• Select + Create scope.\n• Provide a name and description.\n• Choose SharePoint sites as the scope type (screenshot 2):\n\n• Define the scope criteria.\n• Use the query builder to set rules based on SharePoint site attributes such as:• Site URL\n• Site name\n• Custom metadata\n\n• Review and create the scope.\n• Confirm your criteria and create the scope. The system evaluates and updates scope membership automatically.\n• Verify scope membership.\n• Review included sites using the Adaptive scopes details pane (screenshot 3):\n\n• Apply the scope to a DLP policy.\n• When creating or editing a SharePoint DLP policy, select your adaptive scope (screenshots 4 and 5):\n\n.\n\n• Allow time for periodic evaluation.\n• Changes to adaptive scopes may take time to reflect across applied policies.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1234571","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1307512","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: AI-powered notes for in-person meetings with Facilitator in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"Updated August 27, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo support more effective in-person collaboration, Microsoft Teams is expanding AI-powered meeting notes with the Facilitator agent to Teams Rooms on Windows. This enhancement allows teams meeting in a physical room to capture real-time notes, decisions, and action items—without requiring a scheduled or hybrid meeting. The experience is designed to ensure notes are securely stored in your tenant while no data remains on the room device after the meeting ends.\nThis feature is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560318.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability\n• Worldwide and GCC: We will begin rolling out in late October 2026 (previously early September) and expect to complete by mid-November 2026 (previously late September).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizations using Teams Rooms on Windows\n• Rooms licensed with Teams Rooms Pro\n\nWhat will happen\n• During an in-person meeting, users can start AI-powered notes by selecting the Take notes button on the Teams Rooms console.\n\n• Notes appear on the front-of-room display or touch board during the meeting:\n\n• Notes are stored in tenant-owned SharePoint embedded storage.\n\n• Access to notes requires adding your work account using the Access notes button on the Teams Rooms console:\n\n• After the meeting, notes can be viewed and edited by participants with access via the meeting recap in the meeting chat on the Teams desktop client.:\n• If no participant was added during the note-taking session via Access notes, notes are deleted automatically.\n\nDefault state:\n• The feature is available automatically once licensing and prerequisite configurations are met.\n• No additional admin enablement is required beyond existing settings.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo immediate action is required if your organization already meets the prerequisites.\nTo prepare:\n• Confirm Teams Rooms Pro licenses are assigned to applicable rooms.\n• Ensure Facilitator is enabled in your tenant.\n\n• Verify Loop components are enabled:• IsLoopEnabled\n• IsCollabMeetingNotesFluidEnabled\n\n• Ensure meeting transcription is enabled in Teams meeting policies.\n• Consider notifying helpdesk staff and users about:• How to start notes in an in-person meeting\n• Where notes are stored and accessed after the meeting\n\nLearn more:\n• Allow Facilitator in the Teams admin center - Set up Facilitator in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n• Meetings - Admins- Manage transcription and captions for Teams meetings | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n• Settings management for Loop functionality in Teams - Admin policies for Loop components and Loop workspaces | Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change store new customer data, and if so, where, and is the data cached or permanently stored?Yes. Meeting notes generated by Facilitator are stored in tenant‑owned SharePoint Embedded storage. No meeting data is stored or cached on the Teams Rooms device after the meeting ends.\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed (for example, documents, emails, or chats)?Yes. Meeting audio and transcription data are processed to generate AI‑powered meeting notes, including summaries, decisions, and action items. Access to the notes occurs through the meeting recap in the meeting chat on Teams desktop client.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. The Facilitator agent uses AI to generate real‑time meeting notes, summaries, decisions, and action items based on in‑person meeting content.\nDoes the change provide users a new way of interacting with generative AI, and if so, how?Yes. Users can initiate AI‑generated meeting notes during an in‑person meeting by selecting “Take notes” on the Teams Rooms console.\nDoes the change include an admin control, and can it be controlled through tenant configuration?Yes. Availability of the feature depends on existing tenant settings, including Teams Rooms Pro licensing, Facilitator enablement, Loop component settings, and meeting transcription policies.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1307512","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-560540","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Now smarter with visuals: Copilot Chat leverages embedded images for richer, more accurate answers.","desc":"Copilot has been enhanced to interpret and ground responses using images embedded in files such as Word documents (.docx), PowerPoint presentations (.pptx), and PDFs. This capability allows Copilot to extract insights from visual elements like charts, diagrams, and screenshots, ensuring that answers are not only text-based but also informed by graphical context. By combining textual and visual understanding, Copilot delivers more comprehensive and contextually accurate responses for complex queries","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-08-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560540","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-523209","title":"Microsoft Purview: Compliance Manager - AI Powered Regulatory Templates","desc":"This feature in Purview Compliance Manager shall enable customers to convert complex regulations from PDF documents to actionable controls and actions in multi cloud environment. Customers can use the converted regulatory templates to create assessments and identify compliance gaps, understand and implement controls to improve their compliance posture.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-06","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523209","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-569610","title":"Planner: Track task progress with the Completion (%) field","desc":"The new Completion (%) column in Microsoft Planner provides a more precise view of task progress. Users can view and update completion as a percentage, helping teams communicate incremental progress and quickly understand how far work has advanced.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-26","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569610","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"mc-MC1192260","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | Compliance Manager - AI Powered Regulatory Templates","desc":"Updated August 26, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nTo help organizations streamline compliance efforts across multi-cloud environments, Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager is introducing AI Powered Regulatory Templates. This feature enables customers to convert complex regulatory PDF documents into actionable controls, making it easier to create assessments, identify compliance gaps, and implement controls. This enhancement aligns with customer feedback requesting simplified regulatory mapping and automation.\n\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 523209.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: Rollout begins mid-November 2025; expected to complete by end of November 2025.\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins early October 2026 (previously early August); expected to complete by mid-October 2026 (previously late August).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\n• Who is affected:\n\n• Admins using Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager to manage regulatory compliance.\n\n• Organizations operating in multi-cloud environments seeking to automate compliance assessments.\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• A new option will be available to convert regulatory PDF documents into templates.\n\n• These templates can be used to create assessments within Compliance Manager.\n\n• There is no impact to existing workflows or data processing.\n\n• The feature is additive and does not require changes to current configurations.\n\n• The feature will be available by default once rolled out.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required to enable this feature.\n\n• Once available, you may:\n\n• Use the new template creation option to streamline assessment setup.\n\n• Review internal documentation if you maintain guidance on regulatory assessments.\n\n• Share this update with compliance teams to explore its benefits.\n\nLearn more: Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1192260","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-557681","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Intelligent Summaries in Copilot Dashboard","desc":"Use intelligent summaries in Copilot Dashboard to quickly surface what’s working and where targeted attention can accelerate Copilot adoption. Intelligent summaries highlight key adoption trends to focus on areas of success. Suggested prompts enable deeper exploration of underlying trends and drivers.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-16","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557681","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565863","title":"OneNote: Copilot Notebook in OneNote on Mac","desc":"Copilot Notebook, an AI-powered workspace for a project or topic built on reference materials, is coming to OneNote on Mac. Bring together your work context behind a project in one place.","products":["OneNote"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-12","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565863","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-488097","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Full Submissions experience in GCC","desc":"This is item is no longer accurate and we are removing it from the roadmap, we apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488097","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-415168","title":"Outlook: Automatically display auto-mapped calendars","desc":"Users will be able to automatically see their auto-mapped calendars when toggling from classic Outlook to the new. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-04","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=415168","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-551199","title":"Outlook: Print calendar events in new Outlook and Teams","desc":"Users will now have basic options for printing calendar events in #newoutlookforwindows and Teams calendar, including choosing whether to show all attendees or display a shortened list of up to 10 attendees via a checkbox.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-08-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551199","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-562994","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Reduce policy sync status SLA on the Purview UI from 2 hours to 30 mins","desc":"Policy updates in Microsoft Purview now sync faster, reducing wait times from up to 2 hours to just 30 minutes, so your protections stay up to date and take effect more quickly across your organization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-21","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562994","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-560535","title":"Outlook: 1-year and 2-year options for email sync window (Offline settings)","desc":"In the new Outlook for Windows, users can choose to save 1 year or 2 years of email on their device for offline access. This expands the existing offline settings and allows users to access more email when they are not connected to the internet. The new options are available under Settings > General > Offline > Days of email to save, giving users greater flexibility based on their storage and offline needs.\"","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-28","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560535","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569929","title":"Planner: Connected Plans","desc":"Connected Plans let teams link related plans together to organize work across projects and initiatives. Navigate between connected plans and make related work easier to find and manage.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-25","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569929","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-565220","title":"Microsoft Teams: Open message links in new window","desc":"Teams now enables links within chat and channel messages to open in a new window, so you can compare information side by side without losing the context of your ongoing conversation. Access this capability through the More options menu or by using Ctrl/Cmd + click.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-10","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565220","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-498491","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Tip Support in Outlook for Mac","desc":"DLP policy tips for Microsoft Outlook for Mac provide real-time notifications to users when their email contains sensitive information that violates organizational policies. Users can see policy tips directly in the mail tip UI and have the option to remove non-compliant recipients or override the policy if necessary. This feature ensures compliance by alerting users to potential data loss risks before sending emails.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-07","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498491","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-491016","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: DLP Policy Tip Support in Outlook Mobile","desc":"DLP policy tip support for Outlook Mobile enhances data loss prevention measures on mobile devices by providing real-time alerts to help users avoid accidentally sharing sensitive information, ensuring compliance with organizational policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-24","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491016","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-550514","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Newly created Declarative Agents now understand referenced scanned PDFs","desc":"Any newly created Declarative Agents can now reliably ground answers in scanned PDFs and image-based documents referenced from SharePoint, unlocking a major class of enterprise content that was previously hard to use in agent scenarios.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-22","modified":"2026-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=550514","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-569430","title":"Outlook: Manage Multiple Inbox Rules at Once","desc":"You will soon be able to manage multiple inbox rules at the same time. Select every rule or choose only the ones you want to update. You can then delete, enable, or disable the selected rules in one action. This makes it faster and easier to keep your rules organized. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-24","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569430","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569716","title":"Outlook: Purview Data Loss Prevention support for Calendar Events in Outlook mobile apps","desc":"Outlook for iOS and Android will support Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies for calendar events. Organizations can detect and help prevent the sharing of sensitive information in meeting subjects, descriptions, and invite content through policy tips, user remediation, and policy enforcement. This provides consistent compliance protection across email and calendar experiences on mobile devices.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-24","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569716","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569719","title":"Outlook: Purview DLP Wait-on-Send Support for Mac","desc":"Outlook for Mac will support Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) wait-on-send policies. Organizations can require a DLP evaluation before an email is sent and configure how long users must wait for policy evaluation to complete. This helps ensure sensitive information is inspected against organizational policies before messages leave the organization while providing administrators with flexible control over the user experience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-24","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569719","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569718","title":"Outlook: Purview DLP Wait-on-Send Support for Outlook mobile apps","desc":"Outlook for iOS and Android will support Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) wait-on-send policies. Organizations can require a DLP evaluation before an email is sent and configure how long users must wait for policy evaluation to complete. This helps ensure sensitive information is inspected against organizational policies before messages leave the organization while providing administrators with flexible control over the user experience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-24","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569718","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1258000","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – analyze files tied to endpoint DLP alerts","desc":"Updated August 24, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing endpoint Data Loss Prevention (DLP) events as a queryable data source in Data Security Investigations (DSI) in Microsoft Purview. With this update, administrators can build endpoint DLP queries directly in DSI using filters such as date range, and DSI will automatically pull files associated with those events into the investigation for analysis. This integration helps security teams examine endpoint DLP activity at scale, reducing time and effort spent triaging individual alerts and improving the ability to identify patterns and potential data exfiltration scenarios.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558547.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: Rollout begins in early June 2026 (previously late April) and completes in late June 2026 (previously early June).\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in late September 2026 (previously late August) and completes in late September 2026 (previously late August).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\nWho is affected\nAdmins and security investigators using Data Security Investigations (DSI) and endpoint Data Loss Prevention (DLP) in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal.\nWhat will happen\n• A new Endpoint DLP tab will appear in the DSI search experience, alongside the existing Query Builder and Audit tabs.\n• Admins and investigators can query endpoint DLP events using date range filters (additional filters coming soon).\n• Files associated with matching endpoint DLP events will be automatically added to the investigation scope for analysis using DSI’s AI‑powered tools.\n• This feature will appear automatically for eligible tenants when rollout completes. No admin action is required to enable it.\n• There is no user impact.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required. Optionally, you may:\n• Review how endpoint DLP query capabilities work within DSI.\n• Update internal documentation for alert triage and investigation workflows, if applicable.\n• Inform security teams and endpoint DLP administrators about this new capability.\n\nLearn more:\n• Learn about Data Security Investigations | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n• Learn about Endpoint data loss prevention | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestion Answer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Yes. Endpoint DLP event data becomes queryable in DSI, and associated files are automatically collected into investigations for analysis.\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML capabilities that interact with customer data?Yes. DSI’s existing AI‑assisted investigation tools will now analyze files gathered through endpoint DLP queries.\nDoes the change modify how admins can monitor, report on, or demonstrate compliance activities?Yes. Admins gain new ways to surface, query, and analyze endpoint DLP signals within DSI.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-21","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1258000","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565905","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): People Skills- removal and deletion admin control","desc":"A new admin control in the People Skills settings lets administrators permanently remove their organization's People Skills data from the tenant. With this new control, organizations can delete their entire skills library along with all users confirmed, inferred, and imported skills data—giving them full control to offboard from People Skills in support of data governance and compliance needs. Once deletion is initiated, skills will no longer appear on user profile cards or be used across Microsoft 365 skills-based experiences such as Copilot and Viva. The control is admin-only with no automatic changes.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565905","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-512431","title":"Planner: Custom Templates","desc":"Custom templates let you create reusable, pre-designed layouts tailored to your organization’s needs, ensuring consistency and saving time. They provide flexibility to standardize content while allowing easy customization for specific scenarios.","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=512431","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-503564","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Organizational Messages now supports Hybrid-joined Devices","desc":"Organizational Messages now supports Hybrid-joined Devices.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-08-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503564","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-569733","title":"Planner: Capacity view","desc":"Capacity view shows a timeline of who's working on what, so you can see how work is distributed across your team and spot overload or open capacity at a glance.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-21","modified":"2026-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569733","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569612","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management – Retention for Copilot Memory","desc":"Configure retention for Microsoft 365 Copilot memory to help preserve historical versions of memory items for security, compliance, and investigation scenarios. Copilot memory includes saved memories and details inferred from chat history that enable more personalized and context-aware Copilot experiences. Copilot memory items are stored in a hidden folder in the user’s Exchange mailbox. This capability will enable retention and versioning support for inactive memory items so that administrators can maintain visibility into memory changes while active memory continues to be managed by the Copilot experience.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-21","modified":"2026-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569612","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567120","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 admin center – New Microsoft 365 Copilot usage report for GCC High & DoD","desc":"We will be introducing a new Usage report covering Microsoft 365 Copilot. This report will include total enabled and active users, Copilot usage with a breakout per Microsoft 365 app, and user-level activity insights (anonymized by default). #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-06","modified":"2026-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567120","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-559021","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work IQ APIs – Unified REST Endpoint for Agents and Workflows","desc":"Introduces a new REST endpoint for Work IQ that serves as a unified entry point for invoking agents and workflows, providing a consistent, scalable alternative to legacy Copilot Chat endpoints.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559021","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555888","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation","desc":"You can now reference an email with Work IQ when using Edit with Copilot in PowerPoint to create a presentation.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555888","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-506743","title":"Microsoft 365: PAYGO consumption-based meter for your extra SharePoint storage needs","desc":"Use the new PAYGO consumption-based meter to pay for your extra SharePoint storage needs. This reduces the operational overhead associated with purchasing extra storage packs and more seamlessly integrates with Microsoft 365 Archive.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-26","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506743","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568365","title":"Microsoft Edge: Import Google account data anytime from Settings","desc":"Microsoft Edge now lets users import their Google account data - including passwords, bookmarks, history, and autofill data - directly from Edge Settings, at any time after setup. Previously, users had no way to import this data from a Google account outside the first-run experience. With this update, the import flow is unified into a single, streamlined entry point in Settings that combines import from Google Chrome import and Google account.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-29","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568365","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-569428","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365) Writing Blocks in M365 Copilot","desc":"M365 Copilot now supports Writing blocks. Edit drafts, memos, emails, and more inline while using Chat for easy editing and iteration.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569428","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568788","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Self-serve sync connectors","desc":"Self-serve sync connectors enable users to securely connect their own external data sources, such as Jira and Confluence Cloud, to Microsoft 365 Copilot. Using their own credentials and permissions, users can synchronize content they already have access to, making it discoverable in Copilot Chat and Microsoft Search. Administrators maintain oversight through tenant-level controls, including staged rollout, visibility management, and connector disablement.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568788","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569606","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint – Enhanced multiple-choice questions with up to 500 options","desc":"Viva Glint administrators will be able to create multiple-choice questions with up to 500 options and upload options using a CSV file. For questions containing more than 50 options, survey takers can search and filter the available responses, making longer lists faster and easier to navigate. Reporting will support the expanded option set.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569606","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569435","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint – In-product access to feature announcements","desc":"Viva Glint service administrators will see a new announcement icon in the product header that links directly to the Viva Glint Tech Community blog. This makes it easier to discover product news, feature announcements, and best practices.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569435","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569717","title":"Outlook: Purview Data Loss Prevention support for Calendar Events in Outlook for Mac","desc":"Outlook for Mac will support Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies for calendar events. Organizations can detect and help prevent the sharing of sensitive information in meeting subjects, descriptions, and invite content through policy tips, user remediation, and policy enforcement. This provides consistent compliance protection across email and calendar experiences on Mac devices.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569717","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-562665","title":"Microsoft Teams: Interpreter agent support in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"The Interpreter agent acts as a translator in Microsoft Teams meetings, allowing participants to listen to the meeting in their chosen language with real-time translation so speaking different languages isn’t a barrier to effective understanding and collaboration. It's now available in Teams Rooms on Android licensed for Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-20","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562665","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567468","title":"Microsoft Teams: Modernized Gallery view in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"The updated Gallery view in Teams Rooms on Android prioritizes video on the meeting stage, arranges participants in consistent aspect ratios, and minimizes movement of participant tiles on stage. Users can hide the room self-preview video and choose to see audio and video participants equally on stage, instead of prioritizing video participants. Admins can choose the default behavior using local device settings and the Pro Management portal.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-10","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567468","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565870","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Data Loss Prevention to safeguard sensitive information from external web search in Microsoft 356 Copilot and Copilot Chat","desc":"We are expanding Microsoft Purview DLP for Microsoft 365 Copilot to safeguard web searches containing sensitive data. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data leakage and oversharing risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat from using sensitive data for external web search.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-26","modified":"2026-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565870","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561034","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management – Hard delete capability for OneDrive and SharePoint through secure priority cleanup workflows","desc":"Data Lifecycle Management allows compliance admins to retain, review and delete content in M365 workloads. Deletion of content to adhere to compliance requirements, admins can set up Retention policies or labels. To help prevent inadvertent data loss, M365 retention labels policies and M365 retention policies do not hard delete content immediately and keeps the data in Recycle Bins for 93 days for ODSP. Hard delete itself is a very costly process as it opens Microsoft to heavy legal implications in case of any data loss incident that may occur due to a misconfigured policy or regression. Priority Cleanup feature allows users to bypass retention, and eDiscovery holds to help customers comply to changing legal/compliance requirements or manage data spillage scenarios. This feature requires the ability to hard delete specific files from the scoped locations. Ability to select hard delete configuration for a Priority cleanup policy for OneDrive and SharePoint content and skip recycle bins.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561034","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-560597","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Triage Agent in Data Loss Prevention - Reasoning Trace and Confidence Score for agent-triaged alerts","desc":"This feature introduces confidence scoring and reasoning trace explainability into the Data Security Triage Agent in DLP, addressing a critical trust gap reported across multiple customers. Today, without transparency into why the agent makes a decision or how confident it is, analysts are forced to fall back to manual review — completely negating the automation value. The feature will surface a reasoning trace alongside each agent decision and a confidence score, giving analysts a clear signal of how reliable the agent's output is. This provides SOC teams with an auditable, explainable output they can validate rather than blindly trust, enabling them to progressively increase reliance on automation over time.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560597","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566314","title":"Planner: Save AI-generated filters in Planner Agent chat","desc":"Save AI-filters generated by the Planner Agent for future use on your plans.","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-30","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566314","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569429","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Code Blocks in M365 Copilot","desc":"M365 Copilot now supports code blocks, which lets you preview code, charts, diagrams, and more directly inline while using Chat. Previously, users could preview code side-by-side in a code canvas.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-19","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569429","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569607","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Improvements to agent evaluations experience","desc":"Microsoft Copilot Studio is enhancing the Evaluations experience to help makers better understand agent quality and behavior. New capabilities include richer evaluation explanations, agent reasoning traces, cited knowledge sources, evaluation run comparison, support for larger datasets, customizable test generation, and dataset generation from knowledge sources. These improvements help makers identify quality issues more quickly, understand why evaluations succeed or fail, compare results across runs, and create higher quality evaluation datasets with less manual effort. Additional validation and guidance will help makers resolve configuration issues before running evaluations.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-19","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569607","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-558343","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management– Hard delete capability for OneDrive and SharePoint through secure priority cleanup workflows","desc":"Data Lifecycle Management allows compliance admins to retain, review and delete content in M365 workloads. Deletion of content to adhere to compliance requirements, admins can set up Retention policies or labels. To help prevent inadvertent data loss, M365 retention labels policies and M365 retention policies do not hard delete content immediately and keeps the data in Recycle Bins for 93 days for ODSP. Hard delete itself is a very costly process as it opens Microsoft to heavy legal implications in case of any data loss incident that may occur due to a misconfigured policy or regression. Priority Cleanup feature allows users to bypass retention, and eDiscovery holds to help customers comply to changing legal/compliance requirements or manage data spillage scenarios. This feature requires the ability to hard delete specific files from the scoped locations. Ability to select hard delete configuration for a Priority cleanup policy for OneDrive and SharePoint content and skip recycle bins.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-09","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558343","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-565370","title":"Microsoft Teams: Emoji shortcuts with autocomplete on mobile","desc":"Teams brings desktop-style emoji shortcuts to mobile (iOS and Android), allowing you to insert emojis by typing colon-based commands like :smile:. Real-time autocomplete suggestions help you quickly find the right emoji as you type, while support for custom emojis enables more personalized and expressive communication on the go.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-10","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565370","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-513278","title":"Planner: Available in Outlook","desc":"Planner in Outlook brings all your tasks, plans, and the new Planner Agent directly into your inbox, so you can manage work where you already work.","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513278","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-555882","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Attach and reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","desc":"You can now reference an image when creating a presentation with Copilot using Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555882","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-484854","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - DLP Policy Tip Support in Outlook for Mac","desc":"DLP policy tips for Microsoft Outlook for Mac provide real-time notifications to users when their email contains sensitive information that violates organizational policies. Users can see policy tips directly in the mail tip UI and have the option to remove non-compliant recipients or override the policy if necessary. This feature ensures compliance by alerting users to potential data loss risks before sending emails.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-13","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484854","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-547829","title":"Microsoft 365: Enhancements to the room booking experience in the Places app","desc":"We’re enhancing the room booking experience in the Places App to align with the desk booking flow and visuals. This unifies the booking experience across rooms and desks.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547829","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559019","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work IQ APIs - Endpoints: Declarative Agent Access","desc":"Enables programmatic access to first‑party and tenant‑defined declarative agents via the Work IQ endpoint, allowing applications to trigger specialized agents for domain‑specific tasks within broader workflows.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559019","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560815","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improved visibility and control for downloads","desc":"Download manager updates in Microsoft Teams make it easier to track file progress with improved visibility, control, and accessibility. You can now open the manager from the title bar or by using a keyboard shortcut, and view downloads without blocking key chat and channel actions.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560815","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-533043","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updated UI for Copilot Chat entry point in Word, Excel and PowerPoint apps","desc":"We are updating the entry point user interface for Copilot Chat. The Copilot Chat entry point button will move out of the app ribbon to the app canvas to help with discoverability and use within the context of the file. This update will apply to Microsoft 365 users of Word, Excel and PowerPoint who are eligible for Copilot Chat across web, mobile and desktop.","products":["Excel","PowerPoint","Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-21","modified":"2026-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=533043","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501201","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced Copilot chat summary","desc":"Missed many messages? Copilot will automatically generate a summary of the new messages in a chat conversation, so you can catch up quickly without reading every message.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2026-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501201","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-569212","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Federated Copilot Connectors in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"Federated Copilot connectors enable users to securely connect Microsoft Copilot to their favorite third party sources, retrieving data in real-time using the Model Context Protocol (MCP). Federated Copilot connectors do not store or index customer data in Microsoft - access happens in real time using the user’s own identity, while administrators retain full governance and control through the Microsoft 365 Admin Center. With GA, federated Copilot connectors will be supported across Researcher agent and Microsoft 365 Chat, allowing users to bring data into their workflows.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-18","modified":"2026-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569212","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-481834","title":"Microsoft 365: Long-term retention period for M365 Backup","desc":"This creates the ability to set longer term retention periods to restore beyond one year.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564608","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Support for MCP Agents with Interactive UI Widgets in Government Clouds","desc":"Feature description: Model Context Protocol (MCP) based agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat will now be able to surface rich, interactive UI widgets directly within chat. This enhancement enables developers to deliver more engaging and structured agent interactions. Users will experience these widgets when interacting with agents that implement them, and admins will continue to manage these agents through the Microsoft 365 Admin Center.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564608","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565221","title":"Microsoft Teams: Assistant field visibility in Organization view","desc":"Teams now displays assistant information in the Organization view on the profile card and in the Org Explorer, making it easier to identify a key support contact for executive coordination and scheduling. This designation is informational only and does not grant permissions, change roles, or affect organizational hierarchy.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565221","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-558860","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Data Security Triage Agent summaries and categorizations for DLP alerts will be made available in DLP Alerts in Microsoft Defender XDR","desc":"Data Security Triage Agent summaries and categorizations for DLP alerts will be made available in DLP Alerts in Microsoft Defender XDR.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-17","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558860","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2027","gaSort":202708,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-93269","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: eDiscovery (Premium) – Hold reports (U.S. Government clouds)","desc":"<div>Out-of-the-box reports that contain information about all legal holds associated with eDiscovery cases in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal. Sort and filter your view based on various criteria and download the aggregated information for further analysis. </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2022-06-02","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=93269","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702},{"id":"rm-93268","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: eDiscovery (Premium) – Hold reports","desc":"Out-of-the-box reports that contain information about all legal holds associated with eDiscovery cases in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal. Sort and filter your view based on various criteria and download the aggregated information for further analysis. Note: The status and release month has been updated to reflect the current state. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2022-06-02","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=93268","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2023"},{"id":"rm-565373","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - CMK (Customer managed key) for eDiscovery direct export","desc":"This release of eDiscovery features the implementation of customer-managed key (CMK) options, allowing users to manage their own encryption keys for the data included in the direct export workflow in eDiscovery, adding to the Microsoft-managed encryption already in place.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565373","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-557684","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery- CMK (Customer managed key) for eDiscovery direct export","desc":"This release of eDiscovery features the implementation of customer-managed key (CMK) options, allowing users to manage their own encryption keys for the data included in the direct export workflow in eDiscovery, adding to the Microsoft-managed encryption already in place.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557684","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569215","title":"OneDrive: Improved capabilities for files with Copilot in OneDrive Web","desc":"With improved Copilot file skills in OneDrive, you can go from files to finished work directly from chat. Copilot helps you find the right content, analyze files and data, create polished outputs like summaries, dashboards, and presentations, and collaborate by saving or sharing the results from OneDrive.","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569215","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569364","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery- Select user-owned SharePoint embedded container as a data source","desc":"eDiscovery users will be able to view and select SharePoint Embedded content containers owned or created by a selected person. These containers store content from apps such as Microsoft Loop, Copilot Pages, and Copilot Notebooks.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569431","title":"Outlook: Change the organizer of a meeting","desc":"Transfer ownership of a meeting or recurring meeting series to another person in your organization. The new organizer must accept the transfer before it is completed. This helps maintain continuity for long-running meetings while preserving the existing event for attendees. Available in Outlook for Windows and web and Teams calendar.","products":["Microsoft 365","Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569431","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569426","title":"Planner: Private tasks now stored in your private plan","desc":"Private tasks created in Planner and Planner-powered experiences are stored in the user’s private plan, providing a single place for tasks visible only to that user. Private tasks cannot be shared or assigned to others, and existing tasks continue to work and appear alongside them.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-17","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569426","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1255406","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | Data Security Triage Agent Summaries for DLP Alerts in Microsoft Defender XDR","desc":"Updated August 17, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe’re introducing Data Security Triage Agent summaries and categorizations for Data Loss Prevention (DLP) alerts directly within the Microsoft Defender XDR portal. This update helps security analysts triage DLP alerts more efficiently by surfacing AI-generated summaries and categorizations created by the Microsoft Purview Data Security Triage Agent.\nScreenshot 1: Data Security Triage Agent outputs and summaries now available in DLP alerts in Microsoft Defender XDR\n\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 558860.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out early April 2026 and expect to complete by mid-April 2026.\n•\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out August 2027 (previously August 2026).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n\n• Security analysts and admins triaging DLP alerts in Microsoft Defender XDR\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft Purview Data Security Triage Agent\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• DLP alerts in Defender XDR will display AI-generated summaries and categorizations when the Agent is deployed.\nScreenshot 2: Security Analysts and Admins triaging DLP alerts in Defenders will be able to deploy the Data Security Triage Agent from the Microsoft Defender XDR portal\n\n• If the Agent is not deployed, eligible analysts can deploy it from the DLP alert page in Defender XDR.\n\n• Agent management (instructions, pause/deactivate, usage monitoring) remains in Microsoft Purview.\n\n• Existing DLP policies and enforcement are not changed.\n\n• There is no impact to users.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Deploy the Data Security Triage Agent in Microsoft Purview to enable summaries in Defender XDR.\n• Review role assignments to ensure analysts who triage DLP alerts have the appropriate permissions.\n• Update internal security operations documentation to reflect the new triage experience.\n• Familiarize security teams with where Agent deployment can occur (Defender XDR) and where ongoing management is performed (Purview).\n\nLearn more: Before rollout, we will update this post with new documentation.\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nExplanation\n\nAI/ML or agent capabilities interacting with customer data\nThis change introduces AI-generated summaries and categorizations for DLP alerts using the Microsoft Purview Data Security Triage Agent, which processes existing DLP alert data to assist analysts during triage.\n\nAdmin controls\nAdmins can deploy the Data Security Triage Agent from the Microsoft Defender XDR portal. Ongoing agent management, including custom instructions, pausing or deactivating the agent, and monitoring usage, remains available in the Microsoft Purview portal.\n\nAdmin monitoring and compliance reporting\nThe update enhances DLP alert investigations by adding AI-generated context, improving how admins monitor and assess data security incidents without changing underlying DLP policy enforcement or audit logging.","products":["Microsoft Defender XDR","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-18","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1255406","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-562662","title":"Microsoft 365 app: New Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot App","desc":"The new Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app now lets users organize related chats, output creations, and references into a persistent AI workspace. Copilot uses the Notebook's accumulated context to ground responses, so work continues across sessions instead of starting over each time. While this is the quicker, light-weight Notebooks experience, you can still find the fuller, workspace-forward experience in OneNote.","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562662","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567305","title":"Microsoft Teams: Specify who has control of production tools in Teams meetings and events","desc":"A new meeting option for Teams meetings with presenters and events that enables organizers to designate 'Who has control of production tools' during the event. Users defined here will have access to the controls in 'Manage What Attendees See' and the ‘Green Room'.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567305","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-564805","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Organizational Data – Granular access policy controls for custom attributes","desc":"We are introducing enhanced access policy management for Organizational Data in Microsoft 365. This update enables admins to release custom attributes to specific users or groups, rather than broadly to all employees or all managers. This provides a more conservative default approach for managing sensitive organizational data, while also supporting staged rollout of new attributes. Additionally, admins can configure whether leaders and managers are permitted to share non-public data with Workforce Insights delegates. This enhancement improves governance, flexibility, and control over organizational data access.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564805","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-394279","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Decoupling of Policy tips and Email notifications while configuring rules on Data Loss Prevention for Sharepoint and Onedrive","desc":"As of today, whenever the user wants to enable email notifications the policy tips also need to be enabled and vice versa, but with this decoupling the admin can configure the following: 1) None of policy tips or email notification 2) Only policy tips 3) Only Email Notifications 4) Both Email Notifications and Policy tips","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-04-22","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=394279","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557190","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – File Quarantine Action in DLP for SharePoint/OneDrive","desc":"File Quarantine action in Microsoft Purview DLP for SharePoint and OneDrive, enables stronger, immediate protection for sensitive data. When a DLP policy is triggered, the File Quarantine action automatically moves the file to a restricted, admin‑controlled & defined quarantine location—instantly removing access for all users while preserving the file for review and investigation. This capability helps organizations contain data‑exposure risks, prevents further sharing or misuse, and delivers a powerful new layer of enforcement.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557190","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561321","title":"Microsoft Teams: SharePoint thumbnail previews","desc":"Microsoft Teams on desktop now shows rich link previews when you share SharePoint pages. Links automatically expand into a visually appealing card with a thumbnail image and page description, making it easier to understand and engage with shared SharePoint content directly in Teams.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-08-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561321","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-484086","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: eDiscovery - Advanced Review Set Explorer","desc":"The Advanced Review Set Explorer empowers reviewers to harness the power of real-time big data analytics on their review set data leveraging. This tool enhances data analysis by offering insights such as identifying top item types, spotting patterns, and trends within the review set. Reviewers can utilize powerful Kusto query constructs like complex filtering, pattern-based text extraction, and data format parsing to analyze and find key information specific to their case or organization. The results can then be visualized using various flexible charting solutions, providing a comprehensive understanding of the data's story.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-07","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484086","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-565372","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - Advanced Review Set Explorer","desc":"The Advanced Review Set Explorer empowers reviewers to harness the power of real-time big data analytics on their review set data. This tool enhances data analysis by offering insights such as identifying top item types, spotting patterns, and trends within the review set. Reviewers can utilize powerful Kusto query constructs like complex filtering, pattern-based text extraction, and data format parsing to analyze and find key information specific to their case or organization. The results can then be visualized using various flexible charting solutions, providing a comprehensive understanding of the data's story.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565372","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"mc-MC1240699","title":"(Updated) Introducing the new SharePoint experience","desc":"Updated August 14, 2026: We have updated this post as a reminder. We’re ready to begin the General Availability (GA) rollout of the new SharePoint experience on June 15, with deployment continuing over the subsequent months. Based on feedback from users in the preview program, we are simplifying item-keeping experiences across SharePoint and aligning on a single Favorites gesture that is consistent with the rest of Microsoft 365.\nAs part of this change:\n• Followed Sites will become Favorite Sites.\n• Saved for Later for pages and news posts will become Favorites.\n\nThis is a naming and experience update that will be reflected across all SharePoint surfaces where these experiences appear, providing a more consistent and streamlined experience for users across Microsoft 365. Existing followed sites and saved content will be preserved and automatically transition to the Favorites experience.\nAdditionally, as previously communicated, we are retiring Featured Links and encouraging customers to use modern alternatives such as Global Navigation, which can be configured to surface important organizational resources and destinations.\nPrevious update: We began the Targeted Release (TR) rollout on May 5, with an expected ramp to 100% TR by the end of the week. All customers and users in the TR program will automatically receive the new SharePoint experience, with no option to opt out at either the tenant or user level.\n• We recommend that customers explore the experience ahead of TR to ensure readiness.\n• For users and tenants already opted in via EAP or Public Preview, we will preserve their current state, their experience as of Monday will remain unchanged.\n\n[Introduction]\nWe are introducing a new SharePoint experience that includes a redesigned SharePoint app bar, a refreshed SharePoint start page for finding sites, content, and news, and support for AI-assisted creation, management, and discovery features. The new experience applies to all SharePoint users. Some capabilities in this experience use AI. Access to those capabilities requires a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 547732.\nBefore the new experience rolls out broadly, it will be available as a public preview. During the preview period, administrators can enable the experience for their tenant to evaluate the changes and prepare users. When enabled during preview, the experience applies to all users in the tenant. Users may opt out of the new experience during the preview period.\nWhen the public preview ends, Targeted Release rollout will begin, followed by General Availability (GA). Starting with Targeted Release, the new SharePoint experience will automatically apply to all tenants and users. Any tenant-level preview settings or individual user opt-outs from the preview period will be overridden, and no controls will remain. We recommend customers try the experience ahead of TR to be better prepared.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: Rolling out in early March 2026; expected completion by late April 2026.\n• Targeted Release: Rolling out in early May 2026 (previously late April); expected completion by mid-May 2026 (previously June).\n• General Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCC High, DoD): Rolling out in mid-June 2026 (previously early May); expected completion by mid to late September 2026 (previously mid-July).\n\nNote - the late September timeline pertains primarily to GCC, GCC High and DoD tenants.\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• All SharePoint users\n• Users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license will have access to AI capabilities included in this experience.\n\nWhat will happen\nWhen the new experience is enabled—either during preview or as part of the Targeted Release and General Availability (GA) rollout—users will see an updated SharePoint app bar that introduces entry points for discovering content, publishing communications, and building SharePoint solutions.\nThe updated app bar includes:\nDiscover\nA refreshed start experience to find relevant sites, content, and news.\n\nPublish\nA unified publishing hub that brings together pages, news, and campaign-style communications powered by Amplify.\n\nBuild\nA centralized place where makers can create and manage SharePoint sites, lists, libraries, and AI-powered agents from a single surface.\n\nThe app bar will also include:\n• OneDrive – Provides quick access to files.\n• Home – Appears when a Home site with global navigation is configured in the tenant.\n\nAdditional updates include:\n\n• Updated page, news, library, and list experiences with improved content visibility\n• Neutral theming applied across SharePoint product surfaces (site-level branding remains unchanged)\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• Review documentation: Enable the new SharePoint experience (preview) | SharePoint in Microsoft 365 | SharePoint | Microsoft Learn\n• Review changes to the SharePoint navigation experience, including the new app bar: SharePoint App Bar\n• Communicate expected UI changes to helpdesk teams and users.\n• Update internal documentation that references SharePoint navigation or app bar elements.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1240699","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1221453","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | eDiscovery – Advanced review set explorer","desc":"Updated August 14, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing the Advanced Review Set Explorer (public preview) for review sets in Microsoft Purview eDiscovery (Premium).\neDiscovery has long supported Keyword Query Language (KeyQL) because it provides a familiar, approachable, and powerful way to search and filter content—while working consistently across both search and review experiences. For many users and workflows, KeyQL remains the recommended and most efficient way to build queries.\nAt the same time, we understand that power users and advanced reviewers often need greater flexibility to slice, aggregate, and analyze review set data in more sophisticated ways. To meet this need, we’re adding a Kusto Query Language (KQL)–based experience to review sets through the Advanced Review Set Explorer.\nWith this update, reviewers will have two query options:\n• KeyQL, for familiar, streamlined search and filtering experiences\n• KQL, for advanced data exploration, aggregation, transformation, and visualization within a review set\n\nThe new Advanced review set explorer's key capabilities include:\n• Run advanced review set explorer using Kusto Query Language (KQL)\n• Apply complex filters, aggregations, and transformations\n• Visualize results with bar, column, and pie charts\n• Query across more than 100 metadata properties\n• Identify trends, detect patterns, and analyze data distribution\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 484086.\n\n[When this will happen]\n\n• Public Preview (Worldwide, excluding government clouds): We will start rolling out in February 2026 and expect to complete in February 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCCH, and DoD): We will start rolling out in late December 2026 (previously late August) and expect to complete in late December 2026 (previously late August).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\n\nWho is affected:\nOrganizations using Microsoft Purview eDiscovery (Premium).\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• A new Advanced Review Set Explorer will be available in review sets.\n\n• The feature is enabled by default.\n\n• Users with eDiscovery review permissions can run KQL queries.\n• Users can continue using existing KeyQL‑based searching within review set without change.\n\n• No existing queries or workflows are modified.\n\n• Existing admin policies and permissions are unchanged.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n\n• Inform eDiscovery teams that both KeyQL and KQL are supported, and users can choose the option that best fits their needs.\n• Consider providing KQL training or reference materials.\n\n• Update internal documentation or workflows as needed.\n\n• Inform eDiscovery teams about this new capability.\n\n• Review Microsoft Learn content on eDiscovery solutions.\n\nLearn more:\n• Kusto Query Language overview | Microsoft Learn\n• Learn about eDiscovery | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1221453","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1289726","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - CMK (Customer managed key) for eDiscovery direct export","desc":"Updated August 14, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nTo strengthen customer control over sensitive investigation data, Microsoft is extending Customer-managed key (CMK) protection to Microsoft Purview eDiscovery Direct Export. For tenants that have configured Data Encryption Policies (DEPs) using the Microsoft 365 Data-at-Rest Encryption Platform (MDEP), eDiscovery export packages will now be automatically encrypted using your organization’s CMK. This helps ensure exported investigation data remains protected under customer-controlled encryption policies throughout the export lifecycle, without changing the existing eDiscovery user experience.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557684.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out early May 2026 and expect to complete by early June 2026.\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out late December 2026 (previously early September) and expect to complete by early January 2027 (previously end of September).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Microsoft 365 tenants with Customer-managed keys enabled through Data Encryption Policies (DEPs), and request that Microsoft Support enable this feature for Purview eDiscovery Direct Export in their tenant\n\n• Admins and investigators using Microsoft Purview eDiscovery Direct Export\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• eDiscovery Direct Export packages for CMK‑enabled tenants will be encrypted at rest using tenant‑owned keys.\n• Encryption is applied automatically based on existing DEP configuration.\n\n• CMK configuration is dynamically validated through MDEP at export time.\n\n• No change to the eDiscovery user experience.\n\n• Only enabled for specific tenants by request to Microsoft Support\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\nTo use CMK encryption for eDiscovery Direct Export, your organization must complete the following steps:\n• Configure Customer Key (self-service) Your Microsoft 365 administrator must have Customer Key enabled through the Microsoft 365 Data-at-Rest Encryption Platform (MDEP) with a DEP in PolicyAssigned status.\n• This requires:• Two Azure subscriptions dedicated to Customer Key\n• Azure Key Vault(s) with RSA keys provisioned\n• A DEP created and assigned to your tenant\n• Follow the setup guidance here: Create two new Azure subscriptions | Microsoft Learn\n\n• Request feature enablement (contact Microsoft Support) • After Customer Key is configured, your organization must contact Microsoft Support to request that CMK for eDiscovery Direct Export be enabled for your tenant. This feature requires Microsoft-side service configuration that is not automatically applied. Work with your Microsoft Support contact or Customer Success Account Manager (CSAM) to complete enablement.\n\nImportant:\n• If your tenant does not have CMK properly configured through MDEP at export time, direct export jobs will proceed without CMK encryption.\n• No changes to the eDiscovery user experience are required — CMK encryption is applied transparently to export packages.\n• Encryption scopes, storage accounts, and containers are managed automatically by the service; no additional storage configuration is needed.\n• Exported data retention remains 14 days, unchanged by CMK.\n\nLearn more: Export search results in eDiscovery | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nImpact\n\nEncryption methods or key management\neDiscovery Direct Export packages are encrypted at rest using tenant‑owned customer‑managed keys defined in Data Encryption Policies through MDEP.\n\neDiscovery or Content Search\nDirect Export behavior is enhanced to automatically apply tenant‑specific encryption scopes to exported investigation data.\n\nHow customer data is processed or stored\nExported investigation data is stored in eDiscovery storage accounts encrypted with customer‑managed keys rather than Microsoft‑managed keys.\n\nAdmin controlsBehavior is governed by existing Data Encryption Policies; no new toggle is introduced, but encryption is controlled through CMK configuration.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1289726","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567467","title":"Microsoft Teams: Expand presenter visibility in 'Manage what attendees see' for Teams events","desc":"Users will now be able to resize and expand the presenter panel in 'Manage what attendees see' options for Teams events. This feature helps make it easier to view, manage, and switch between presenters during events.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567467","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-527831","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Actionable Email Notifications for Enhanced Incident Remediation","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention end-user email notification is getting advanced incident remediation capabilities: actionable email notifications. This new feature allows end users to take remediation actions directly from their mailbox, streamlining the remediation process. The end users will be able take remediation actions on files on OneDrive and SharePoint that caused a policy match. Key actions now available in our email notifications include - stop sharing file, delete file, apply label, override the policy, report false positive and unable to take action.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-13","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527831","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-464996","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Actionable Email Notifications for Enhanced Incident Remediation","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention end-user email notification is getting advanced incident remediation capabilities: actionable email notifications. This new feature allows end users to take remediation actions directly from their mailbox, streamlining the remediation process. The end users will be able take remediation actions on files on OneDrive and SharePoint that caused a policy match. Key actions now available in our email notifications include - stop sharing file, delete file, apply label, override the policy, report false positive and unable to take action. Currently this feature is only available for OneDrive and SharePoint workloads.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-11-06","modified":"2026-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=464996","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"December CY2024"},{"id":"rm-561916","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Granular classification error controls (Exchange online)","desc":"Granular Protections for Exchange Online is available in public preview. This release gives administrators fine-grained control to create DLP policies based on specific classification or text extraction failure types — such as timeout, throttling and other scan errors — rather than one blanket policy for all failure conditions.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-08-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561916","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-569217","title":"Microsoft Edge: Vertical Tabs update","desc":"Microsoft Edge is updating its vertical tab implementation and architecture. Edge is reimplementing capabilities across pane, layout, controls, tab behavior, visual treatments, & embedder customizations. No admin action is required.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-12","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569217","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-558682","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Reduce policy sync status SLA on the Purview UI from 2 hours to 30 mins","desc":"Admin should be able to see the Endpoint DLP policy sync status on the Purview portal within 30 mins.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-24","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558682","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-565374","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Policy Sync & Device Health AI-Powered Investigation","desc":"AI-powered visibility into DLP policy deployment across devices, helping admins track sync progress and understand enforcement coverage. They proactively identify impacted devices, explain root causes of sync failures, and guide admins with recommended actions to quickly diagnose and resolve issues.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565374","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-567462","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced live captions settings and right-side panel view","desc":"We are improving the live captions experience in Microsoft Teams with new viewing layouts and streamlined configuration options. Users can now view live captions in a new right-side panel, in addition to the existing options of viewing them at the top or bottom of the screen, or popping them out into a separate window. We are also making it easier to manage caption settings directly within the meeting. By clicking the existing gear icon in the live captions pane, users will see a consolidated menu to quickly configure spoken language, caption styles, and profanity filters without navigating to separate settings panels. Additionally, this menu includes a new toggle to turn on live captions by default for all meetings, as well as a new thumbs-up/thumbs-down feedback mechanism to easily share input on the captioning experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567462","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567458","title":"Microsoft Teams: Multilingual recap available with translation button","desc":"After meeting recap is automatically generated in the translation language chosen during the meeting, users can continue to change the language of the meeting recap after its generated.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567458","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-559801","title":"Outlook: Jump to Any Folder Instantly with Go to Folder","desc":"You can now quickly search for and navigate to any folder in your mailbox using the new Go to Folder feature. Instead of scrolling through long folder lists, just press Ctrl+Y or access it from your accounts context menu to instantly find what you need. Type a few letters of the folder name and jump straight there. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-28","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559801","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-548652","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ad-hoc room reservation from Teams Rooms on Android console","desc":"With Teams Rooms on Android consoles, you can quickly book a meeting room for immediate use, helping to avoid scheduling conflicts and ensure uninterrupted spontaneous meetings. Available in Teams Rooms Pro-licensed rooms.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-22","modified":"2026-08-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548652","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-561919","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Reusable Global List for Exchange Online","desc":"Reusable Lists centralize management of keywords, domains, and email addresses, eliminating duplication across rules and reducing the effort required to maintain large policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561919","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562342","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Count of Labelled Documents Condition","desc":"This release introduces a new condition for Exchange Online policies: “Count of labeled documents is greater than.” This condition evaluates the number of attachments in an email message that carry a matching sensitivity label. When the count exceeds a defined threshold, the DLP rule is triggered, and configured actions are applied. This capability enables detection of high-volume data exfiltration scenarios, where multiple sensitive files—individually low-risk—collectively represent a significant compliance or security risk. Existing conditions evaluate file content, but do not provide controls based on the volume of labeled attachments.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562342","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"November CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568076","title":"Microsoft Entra: Windows Hello for Business and macOS Platform Single Sign-on can now be used as a second factor for MFA","desc":"Windows Hello for Business (WHfB) and macOS Platform SSO (macOS PSSO) can now satisfy multifactor authentication as a standalone second factor. Previously, these methods only counted as MFA during primary sign-in, and users needed a separate passkey to complete step-up prompts, Authentication Strength policies, and sign-in frequency checks. With this change, WHfB and macOS PSSO work on their own for those scenarios, so more of your users can rely on strong, phishing-resistant sign-in without registering an extra method. What you need to know: Users who have only WHfB or macOS PSSO are now treated as MFA-capable and will no longer be automatically prompted to register another method. Because WHfB and macOS PSSO are tied to a specific device, we recommend having users register a portable method, such as a passkey or Microsoft Authenticator, during onboarding so they can complete MFA from any device.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568076","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569208","title":"SharePoint: HTML pages","desc":"Create HTML with Copilot in SharePoint or upload your own HTML from another source. Once stored in the pages library, you can render HTML as a page in SharePoint, make additional edits, and share with your audience. HTML gives you new ways to present your content beautifully alongside our existing ASPX pages.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569208","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569213","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Add Agents and Skills from the Plus menu","desc":"Users will be able to insert Agents and Skills in prompts for specialized tasks. They can add them from the Agents and Skills tab after selecting 'Add work content' from the plus (+) menu. Users can also access Agents and Skills by typing / and @ in their prompt.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569213","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569203","title":"OneNote: New Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app (DoD, GCC, GCC High)","desc":"The new Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app for DoD, GCC, and GCC High clouds now lets users organize related chats, output creations, and references into a persistent AI workspace. Copilot uses the Notebook's accumulated context to ground responses, so work continues across sessions instead of starting over each time. While this is the quicker, light-weight Notebooks experience, you can still find the workspace-forward experience in OneNote.","products":["OneNote"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-11","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569203","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567465","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams shared display mode and peripheral detection available for DoD environments","desc":"Shared display mode in Teams is now available in government DOD environments, enabling more seamless and private meeting hosting from your PC. Additionally, peripheral detection for bring-your-own-device spaces is available for inventory management and reporting through the Pro Management portal.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-07-15","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567465","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-497999","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Agents usage report","desc":"A new agents usage report will be available in the Microsoft 365 admin center. The report will be scoped to include agents in M365 Copilot and Copilot Chat with usage by both M365 Copilot licensed and unlicensed users. The report will include total active agent users, total active agents, active users segmentation by licensed and unlicensed users, and active users and active agents segmentation by publisher type (i.e. user-created agents, agents built by your org, agents built by Microsoft, agents built by Microsoft partners). The report will also include usage details per user, agent, and user-agent pair. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-02","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497999","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-565218","title":"Microsoft Teams: Queues app for Microsoft Teams in GCC High and DoD","desc":"We’re excited to announce that the Queues app is now available in the GCC High and DoD clouds. This Teams-native app helps organizations manage customer engagements more efficiently by bringing advanced call queue and auto attendant capabilities directly into Teams. Queues app is a Teams Premium feature. For more information about Queues app, including licensing information, please see Manage Queues app for Microsoft Teams in your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-09","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565218","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560706","title":"Teams Meetings in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Meetings as References in Copilot Notebooks bring Teams meeting content into the notebook experience, enabling users to ground Copilot on the discussions, decisions, and context that drive their work. By adding meetings as knowledge sources, users can connect transcripts, notes, chats, and shared content directly to their projects, enriching notebooks beyond files alone and improving downstream outputs like presentations and briefs. Available in Copilot Notebooks across Microsoft 365.","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-30","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560706","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560055","title":"Microsoft Teams: Efficiency Mode","desc":"Teams efficiency mode improves performance and responsiveness on hardware constrained devices by applying a reduced resource configuration by default, helping maintain meeting quality and responsiveness during collaboration.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-20","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560055","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-508521","title":"Microsoft Teams: Room health signals and notifications in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"When critical issues impact room functionality, users see a banner notification on both the front-of-room display and console in Teams Rooms on Windows. Room health signals help get issues resolved quickly and ensure productive meetings. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-02","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508521","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560074","title":"Microsoft Teams: Test your microphone before you join","desc":"Before joining a meeting on your pre-join screen, you can test your microphone and speaker to make sure others will hear you clearly. Select Test mic and speaker to record a short audio clip and play it back. This helps you confirm that the right devices are selected and that you’ll be heard—and hear others—once the meeting starts.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-10","modified":"2026-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560074","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-568929","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Dataverse integration on Copilot Studio","desc":"We are enabling Microsoft Dataverse as a native knowledge source in Copilot Studio, expanding the platform’s ability to ground AI agents in structured enterprise data. This enhancement allows organizations to leverage business-critical information stored in Dataverse—including records, customer data, operational data, and business application content—as a trusted knowledge source for agent experiences.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-10","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568929","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1059679","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | Insider Risk Management: Policy tuning analysis for priority content only policies","desc":"Updated August 10, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nIn Microsoft Purview | Insider Risk Management (IRM), policy tuning analysis provides admins with a real-time prediction of the number of users in a tenant that could potentially match a given set of policy conditions. After this rollout, policy tuning analysis will support insider risk policies that are scoped for priority content.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 378409.\nThis message is associated with MC786326 (about the preview for this feature that started in May 2024).\n[When this will happen:]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out late June 2025 (previously mid-June) and expect to complete by late August 2025 (previously late July).\nGeneral Availability (GCC, GCCHigh, DoD): We will begin rolling out mid-December 2026 and expect to complete by end of December 2026.\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nAfter this rollout, admins can use real-time analytics for policies scoped for priority content to help predict the number of users that could potentially match a given set of policy conditions. This feature enables admins to quickly adjust the selection of indicators and thresholds of activity occurrence so they can efficiently translate their insider risk strategies into pragmatic controls and keep from having too few or too many alerts.\n1. In IRM, Navigate to Settings > Insider Risk Management > Analytics, turn on Analytics, and then select Save.\n\n2. Create/edit a policy scoped to all users in the organization.\n\n3. When you get to Content to prioritize in the policy wizard, select the priority content types you want to prioritize:\n\n4. Select the items for each priority content type as applicable.\n5. On the scoring page, select Get alerts only for activity that includes priority content:\n\n6. Configure the rest of the policy as applicable and save it.\n7. 1-2 days after the policy is saved, edit the policy again and navigate to the indicator thresholds page where insights on user activity containing the scoped priority content for each indicator will be visible under Choose your own thresholds:\n\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nThis rollout will happen automatically by the specified date with no admin action required before the rollout. Review your current configuration to determine the impact for your organization. You may want to notify your users about this change and update any relevant documentation.\nThis change will be available by default for admins to configure. To use this feature, admins will need to enable Analytics in Insider risk management > Settings. After Analytics is enabled and insights are populated, admins will be able to see real-time predictions in policies scoped to all users/groups and scored only for priority content.\nMicrosoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.\n\nYou can access the Insider Risk Management solution in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal.\nLearn more: Configure policy indicators in insider risk management | Microsoft Learn","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-21","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1059679","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-564910","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Outlook Emails in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Outlook Emails as References in Copilot Notebooks bring email content into the notebook experience, enabling users to ground Copilot in the conversations, decisions, and context that drive their work. By adding emails as knowledge sources, users can connect context from their emails directly to their projects, enriching notebooks beyond files alone and improving downstream outputs like presentations and briefs. Available in Copilot Notebooks across Microsoft 365.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564910","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557191","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Block External Domain/User action in DLP for SharePoint/OneDrive","desc":"Block External Domain/User action in Microsoft Purview DLP for SharePoint and OneDrive, gives organizations stronger control over who can access sensitive files. With this enhancement, admins can configure DLP policies that block file access for specific external domains or individual users. This capability helps prevent unintended exposure by external users and supports enterprise compliance requirements.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-02","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557191","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562033","title":"Microsoft Purview: Role groups UI enhancements","desc":"The Role groups page in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal now allows admins to look up permissions by roles and memberships.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562033","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560821","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Export Heat Map report in Viva Glint to editable PowerPoint slides","desc":"Managers will be able to export the default sections from the Heat Map report in Viva Glint directly to editable PowerPoint slides. This enhancement allows for easier and quicker consumption of this report outside Viva Glint, compared to the previous export method which included static screenshots.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560821","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-565028","title":"OneDrive: New Shortcuts folder option when adding shortcuts","desc":"OneDrive makes it easy to add shortcuts to the files and folders you use most. Now you can choose to keep those shortcuts neatly together in one place instead of mixed in with everything else. When you add a shortcut, you can send it to a dedicated \"Shortcuts\" folder rather than your OneDrive root. The folder is created automatically the first time you use it and is easy to spot, with a distinct color and building icon. The Shortcuts folder behaves like any other folder—move it, rename it, share it, or remove it whenever you like.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-03","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565028","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-558250","title":"Microsoft 365 Apps: Cloud Update - Simplified Channel Management","desc":"Use device selection criteria in Cloud Update to assign profiles using Microsoft Entra ID groups and streamline the onboarding process. Admins can combine channel and profile assignment in a single step, making it easier to move devices between update channels and maintain consistent update management across the organization.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558250","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561037","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Vision in Microsoft 365 Copilot can analyze content shared on desktop screen and through mobile camera","desc":"Vision in Microsoft 365 Copilot helps you make faster, more informed decisions by understanding context from what you share on screen or camera. Copilot can analyze visual inputs from shared desktop screens and provide detailed insights about the content. You can also use vision on mobile during a real-time voice session to share your device camera, front or back, and ask questions about what is in front of you. Copilot analyzes the live camera feed or desktop screen in real time and provides spoken, context-aware answers grounded in work and web data.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561037","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561892","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention for Microsoft 365 Copilot to safeguard prompts for government clouds","desc":"We are expanding Microsoft Purview DLP for Microsoft 365 Copilot to safeguard prompts containing sensitive data. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data leakage and oversharing risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat from returning a response when prompts contain sensitive data or using that sensitive data for grounding in Microsoft 365 or the web.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-11","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561892","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-542790","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Posture Management-Data Security Posture Agent in DSPM","desc":"The Data Security Posture Agent is designed to expand the capacity of data security admins as they proactively work to stay on top of a dynamic data and risk landscape within their organization. Its primary job is to help discover sensitive data across your data estate. This agent is designed to analyze and search documents, emails, and messages that match the natural-language discovery intent requested by the user and assess associated risks. By moving beyond traditional keyword and information-type analysis and harnessing the power of LLMs, this agent enables organizations to identify risks based on the actual purpose and context of the content and take appropriate action.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-17","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542790","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-560551","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Configure data retention policy for Viva Glint","desc":"This feature will introduce the capability for Glint service administrators to configure a data retention policy for their Glint instances based on the organizational policies. Any past survey cycles including engagement surveys, always-on surveys, lifecycle surveys and 360s will be retained/deleted based on this data retention configuration period.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-08-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560551","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-566871","title":"Microsoft Edge: Enhanced Security Mode Plus","desc":"Enhanced Security Mode Plus adds optional, admin-configurable protections on top of Enhanced Security Mode to further reduce browser attack surface. Admins can configure preset or custom modes to restrict selected network protocols and compression behavior, hardware-access web APIs, WebGL, and external protocol launches when Enhanced Security Mode is enabled.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566871","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-569020","title":"OneDrive: Anchored comments in the PDF viewer","desc":"Microsoft is adding anchored comments to the PDF viewer in OneDrive and SharePoint on the web. Users can attach a comment to a specific spot on a page, to selected text, and collaborate through replies and @mentions — bringing PDF review to parity with commenting in Office documents. This feature will be on by default and requires no admin action.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569020","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-569023","title":"Outlook: Language support for Summarize in Classic Outlook","desc":"When the content language and the Outlook language do not match, you will be able to select a different language to view summarize Copilot responses.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569023","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568930","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: SQL server Support in Microsoft Copilot Studio","desc":"The Azure SQL Knowledge Source capability extends the range of enterprise data sources that makers can leverage when building agents in Copilot Studio. This enables organizations to bring business-critical information stored in Azure SQL into their agent experiences using the same knowledge-centric approach that customers already use across other supported knowledge sources. Azure SQL knowledge support represents another step toward a unified knowledge platform strategy, where customers can connect enterprise data sources through a common knowledge framework and leverage those sources consistently across agent experiences. It also strengthens the story for organizations seeking to build grounded, enterprise-ready AI solutions using existing Microsoft data assets.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568930","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-568934","title":"OneDrive: Uninstall OneDrive Photos without affecting file sync","desc":"OneDrive is giving people more control over their Windows experience by allowing them to uninstall the OneDrive Photos experience independently. Removing the Photos experience does not uninstall the OneDrive app, interrupt file sync, or delete photos and files. This provides a clear removal option for people who prefer to manage their photos with another app.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568934","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569022","title":"Outlook: Microsoft Purview Label Inheritance from Email Attachments","desc":"When composing an email in Outlook for Mac, Microsoft Purview sensitivity labels can be automatically applied or recommended based on the sensitivity labels of attached files. This helps users consistently protect sensitive information, reduces manual labeling effort, and supports organizational compliance requirements by aligning email protection with the sensitivity of attached content.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569022","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-569021","title":"Outlook: Purview Label Inheritance from Email Attachment for iOS and Android","desc":"Outlook for iOS and Android will support Microsoft Purview sensitivity label inheritance from attachments. When users attach files with sensitivity labels, Outlook can automatically apply or recommend an email sensitivity label based on organizational policy settings. This helps organizations maintain consistent data classification and protection while reducing manual labeling effort.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=569021","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-568931","title":"OneDrive: Manage access to the OneDrive Photos Desktop experience","desc":"OneDrive is adding administrative controls for the Photos experience on Windows. Organizations can manage whether users sign in with personal Microsoft accounts. These controls help IT teams align OneDrive Photos with their access, data governance, and device-management requirements.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-07","modified":"2026-08-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568931","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-497998","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Microsoft Places Support to GCCH and DoD","desc":"\"Microsoft Places is an AI-powered workplace app for flexible work. Places helps organizations reimagine flexible work with AI, enables employees to connect more easily in person so that they can make the most of in-office days.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-15","modified":"2026-08-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497998","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-568789","title":"Outlook: Enhanced user interface updates for iPhone and iPad","desc":"People using Outlook for iOS on iPhone and iPad will see refreshed interface elements aligned with the latest Liquid Glass iOS visual experience, including modernized app chrome, navigation, and use of screen space. It will be enabled by default with no administrator action required.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-06","modified":"2026-08-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568789","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-405754","title":"Outlook: Import support for data files in Outlook","desc":"This feature adds support for importing PST files into Outlook for Mac.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-07-03","modified":"2026-08-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=405754","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558853","title":"Microsoft Teams: Entra passwordless resource account support for Teams Rooms on Windows and Android devices","desc":"Teams rooms on Windows and Android, Panels and Teams Phones now supports Entra Resource Accounts for secure, passwordless sign-in that separates device and user identities. IT admins can migrate to Entra accounts easily with the migration wizard, and track progress using a dashboard in the Pro Management portal.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-08","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558853","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567298","title":"Microsoft Teams: External presenters can access production controls for Teams events","desc":"Organizations can allow external presenters to manage Teams events by granting them access to production controls. Federated (B2B) and guest users can be specified in the \"Who has control of production tools\" setting, enabling trusted external presenters to run events and manage what attendees see. This feature supports organizations that work with third-party event producers and vendors.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567298","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-568761","title":"OneDrive: Improved OneDrive experience in iOS Files app","desc":"OneDrive is updating its integration with the iOS Files app to use Apple's Replicated File Provider API. This update provides end-user improvements such as better upload progress. As part of the change, read-only Shared and Libraries locations will no longer appear in the Files app integration. Users can use Add to OneDrive for shared content and libraries they need to access, including write access where permitted.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-05","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568761","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-562035","title":"Microsoft Teams: Interpreter - Simultaneous mode enhancements","desc":"We’re raising the bar on clarity and control with Interpreter. Admins can fully disable voice simulation via PowerShell when needed. Each speaker is automatically assigned a distinct voice, making multi-speaker conversations easier to follow. We’re reducing distractions by showing shimmer effects only to Interpreter users. We’ve added audio notifications to confirm activation, and we’ve introduced in-product feedback mechanisms so users can easily share their input.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562035","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-555880","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an attached PowerPoint deck’s style when creating a new presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"When creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode, you can reference an existing PowerPoint file, so Copilot applies its theme and styles to the new deck, keeping the design consistent. Updated June 5, 2026: This feature is still in development and will begin rolling out mid-June 2026. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555880","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-555879","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an attached PowerPoint deck’s style when creating a new presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"When creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode, you can reference an existing PowerPoint file, so Copilot applies its theme and styles to the new deck, keeping formatting consistent. Updated June 5, 2026: This feature is still in development and will begin rolling out mid-June 2026. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555879","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-555878","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference an attached PowerPoint deck’s style when creating a new presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"When creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode, you can reference an existing PowerPoint file, so Copilot applies its theme and styles to the new deck, keeping formatting consistent. Updated June 5, 2026: This feature is still in development and will begin rolling out mid-June 2026. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555878","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-562413","title":"Microsoft Teams: Searchable keyboard shortcuts from the dialog in Teams","desc":"Easily find keyboard shortcuts with a new searchable experience in Microsoft Teams. Search by shortcut name or enter part of a key combination directly in the dialog.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562413","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559386","title":"Microsoft Teams: Queues app on Teams mobile","desc":"Manage call queues and engage with customers wherever work takes you. The Queues app on Teams mobile enables on the go workers to stay connected and responsive when handling customer calls. Calling representatives and supervisor leads can view assigned queues, opt in or out of a queue's call routing, and review their call history—all from their mobile device. Supervisor leads can also bulk manage queue participation for their teams. With seamless mobile access, the Queues app helps teams respond faster, handle calls more smoothly, and deliver a better customer experience anytime, anywhere.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559386","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-553223","title":"Microsoft Teams: Voice tethering","desc":"The voice tethering feature builds on the recent introduction of Sign Language Mode. It ensures that when an interpreter voices for a D/HH signer, captions and transcripts attribute the spoken content to the signer rather than the interpreter. This provides accurate representation in meetings and makes it clear who is contributing to the conversation. It also improves downstream meeting intelligence such as Copilot so that notes, summaries, action items, and insights are attributed to the correct participant.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553223","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-523205","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use voice for Q&A during Read Aloud in Word","desc":"Interact in real time with read aloud in Word with Copilot. While your document is being read aloud, you can ask questions with your voice—such as “What does this mean?” or “Summarize this section”—and get answers instantly. No need to pause and search manually. This keeps you in context, reduces interruptions, and helps you understand and act faster.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523205","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-502524","title":"Microsoft Teams: New SlimCore-based optimization for Microsoft Teams in VDI - support for MacOS on Citrix and Azure Virtual Desktops/Windows 365","desc":"This feature allows MAC endpoints to optimize Microsoft Teams in VDI environments with the new SlimCore-based media engine, providing an expanded feature set and multiple improvements in quality, reliability and performance.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-03","modified":"2026-08-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502524","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-558538","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Critique in Researcher","desc":"Responses are generated by GPT and Claude working together, with GPT drafting an initial response and Claude reviewing for increased response accuracy, completeness, and citation integrity.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558538","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-553213","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Researcher Council","desc":"Council in Researcher runs multiple leading AI models from different providers in parallel in one place, so you can quickly compare outputs and see consensus vs. conflict) to make high-stakes decisions with greater confidence—without switching tools.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553213","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562996","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot memory in Researcher","desc":"Copilot memory within Researcher brings forward relevant context from your past interactions—helping ground insights, personalize outputs, and reduce repetitive setup as you explore complex topics.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562996","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-568785","title":"Microsoft Purview: Adaptive Scope evaluation control with recipient and site owner lifecycle status","desc":"Microsoft Purview Adaptive Scopes will provide administrators with explicit control over lifecycle-state evaluation for recipients and site owners, helping ensure policy targeting and scope membership remain aligned with organizational requirements.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568785","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1269211","title":"(Updated) Clearer RSVP selection in Outlook Mobile","desc":"Updated August 4, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe’re improving the RSVP experience in Outlook Mobile by visually highlighting the response a user has selected (Yes, Maybe, or No). This makes it easier for users to quickly see how they’ve responded to a meeting invitation.\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCC High): Rollout begins mid-September 2026 (previously August) and is expected to complete by mid-October 2026 (previously end of August).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• All users who access Outlook Mobile on iOS or Android\n\n• Applies to Worldwide, GCC, and GCC High tenants\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• The selected RSVP option (Yes, Maybe, or No) will be visually highlighted\n\n• Users can quickly confirm how they responded to a meeting invitation and edit as needed\n\n• The feature is enabled by default\n\n• No changes to existing meeting workflows or policies\n\n• No impact to Outlook on the web or Outlook desktop clients\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No admin action is required; the update will roll out automatically\n\n• Consider notifying helpdesk staff of the visual change\n\n• Update internal documentation if needed\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-03","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1269211","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1293479","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview | Data Loss Prevention: New guided diagnostics experience for DLP","desc":"Updated August 4, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft is introducing a new guided diagnostics experience in Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) to help administrators diagnose and resolve DLP policy issues more efficiently. This experience provides clearer visibility into how DLP policies are evaluated, which conditions are matched, and what actions are taken. For eligible tenants, Security Copilot‑powered insights offer recommendations to support troubleshooting and policy optimization.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 561032.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public Preview: Early September 2026\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We expect to begin rolling out October 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Microsoft 365 administrators who manage Microsoft Purview DLP policies\n• Commercial tenants\n• Security Copilot‑powered insights are available only to customers with eligible Microsoft 365 E5 and Copilot licensing\n\nWhat will happen\n• A new guided diagnostics experience will be available in the Microsoft Purview portal to help troubleshoot DLP policy behavior.\n• The diagnostics will be available to all users who have permission to view DLP policies.\n• Admins will see a new guided diagnostics experience in the Microsoft Purview portal for troubleshooting DLP issues.\n• Diagnostics provide visibility into:• DLP policy evaluation order\n• Conditions that were matched\n• Actions taken (allow, block, audit)\n\n• Eligible tenants will receive Copilot‑powered insights and recommendations to assist with:• Identifying potential policy misconfigurations\n• Troubleshooting DLP behavior\n• Policy optimization\n\n• Existing DLP policies and enforcement behavior are not changed.\n• There is no impact to user workflows.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required.\nOptionally:\n• Review internal DLP troubleshooting documentation and update it to reference the new diagnostics experience.\n• Ensure security and compliance teams are aware of the new diagnostics flow in the Microsoft Purview portal.\n• Review Copilot licensing to understand availability of Security Copilot‑powered insights.\n\n(Documentation links will be provided once public preview documentation is available.)\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Yes. The guided diagnostics experience includes Security Copilot-powered insights and recommendations for eligible tenants. These insights analyze existing DLP configuration data and diagnostic metadata to help administrators understand policy behavior, troubleshoot issues, and identify opportunities for policy optimization. No new customer content sources are introduced, and Copilot does not change DLP enforcement decisions.\nDoes the change alter how admins can monitor, report on, or demonstrate compliance activities (for example, in Microsoft Purview reporting or diagnostics)?Yes. The new guided diagnostics experience enhances how administrators can monitor and understand DLP policy evaluation, including visibility into evaluation order, matched conditions, and resulting actions. This improves troubleshooting and compliance validation workflows without changing audit logs or enforcement behavior.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1293479","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-568079","title":"Outlook: Insert Signature Image from OneDrive","desc":"Users can now insert images into their email signature directly from OneDrive, in addition to the device photo library.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-08-04","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568079","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561652","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.151 - Passkey Sync for Enterprise Users","desc":"Microsoft Edge is introducing support for passkey synchronization for enterprise users, enabling secure, passwordless authentication across devices. Passkeys created in Edge can now be synced seamlessly, improving sign-in experience while maintaining strong security standards.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-07","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561652","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-559989","title":"Outlook: Copilot now provides concise summaries with Outlook search results","desc":"Get answers to queries quickly with Copilot's concise AI summaries at the top of Outlook search results. Users can dig deeper by opening Copilot chat directly from the Copilot summary card.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559989","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561488","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Simplified design for the Microsoft 365 Copilot app","desc":"A refreshed design for the Microsoft 365 Copilot web and desktop app simplifies the user experience to drive engagement with Copilot. This includes updates to the chat home screen, chat response layout, and navigation pane.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-04","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561488","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557558","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Localized Default Mark and Notify Email Template","desc":"Enabling localization for the default Mark and Notify email template used in admin review and automation flows for user reported messages. This ensures end users receive review outcome notifications in their preferred language, improving understanding, trust, and participation in email reporting within Microsoft Defender for Office 365.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557558","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-547834","title":"Microsoft Teams: Events in Meet app in Teams","desc":"Users can now use the Teams Meet app to discover events across their organization, track what important events are upcoming, and plan and organize their own professional events.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-567306","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced delegated calling with delegate call access restrictions and join notifications","desc":"Call delegation in Teams now includes new controls that give delegators greater privacy and control during active calls. Delegators can lock an ongoing call to prevent delegates from joining or resuming the call and can optionally enable warning tones that notify participants when a delegate joins or resumes a call.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-08-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567306","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-560813","title":"Microsoft Teams: Unblock users to send message while file is uploading in the background","desc":"Large file sharing in Teams today introduces blocking behavior, forcing users to wait for uploads to complete and disrupting real-time collaboration. To improve productivity and reduce perceived latency, we are introducing asynchronous file uploads. This allows users to continue sending messages while the file uploads in the background, enabling a more seamless and uninterrupted collaboration experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-08-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560813","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567457","title":"Microsoft Teams: View and manage auto attendant shared voicemails directly in the Queues app","desc":"Calls to an Auto Attendant that are routed to voicemail will now appear directly within Queues app. This enables organizations to manage shared Auto Attendant voicemails in a centralized experience, making it easier for teams to track, triage, and respond to customer messages.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-08-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567457","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-543425","title":"Outlook: Clear & Flag Actions in New Outlook","desc":"We’re introducing new rule actions in the new Outlook for Web and Windows to give users greater flexibility and control. This includes Clear Categories, Clear Flag, Complete Flag, and Flag Message, enabling more precise automation of message organization and follow‑up workflows. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-08","modified":"2026-07-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543425","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-503551","title":"Outlook: Expanded Conditions for Conditional Formatting in the New Outlook for Web and Windows","desc":"The new Outlook for web and Windows now offers expanded Conditional Formatting options, allowing you to highlight emails based on size, read/unread status, presence of attachments, flag settings, categories, or importance. These enhanced rules make it easier to identify critical messages at a glance and visually organize your folders. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-03","modified":"2026-07-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503551","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-567887","title":"SharePoint: Viva Connections multi-home site management moving to SharePoint admin center","desc":"Viva Connections multi-home site management is moving from the Microsoft 365 admin center (MAC) to the SharePoint Admin Center (SPAC). Administrators will be able to create and manage multiple Home sites, configure audience targeting, manage home site priority order, and remove Home sites directly from SPAC. Existing entry points in the Microsoft 365 admin center will direct administrators to the new SPAC experience. As part of this update, legacy Viva Connections (VC) instances and draft/enabled management concepts are being deprecated as Viva Connections administration is consolidated into SharePoint Home site management. Existing VC experiences will be upgraded to full Home sites.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-29","modified":"2026-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567887","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1117115","title":"(Updated) Updates to custom scripting in sites and Classic Publishing site creation","desc":"Updated January 29, 2026: We are updating this post as a reminder. Upcoming SharePoint Online changes may impact your organization. Please review the below.\nWe are implementing the following changes to custom scripting and classic publishing in SharePoint Online.\n1. Disablement of custom scripting\nCustom scripting will be disabled by default (setting DenyAddAndCustomizePages to 1 or $true) for sites created with the following templates:\n• BLANKINTERNETCONTAINER#0 = Classic Publishing Portal Site\n\n• CMSPUBLISHING#0 = Classic Publishing Site\n\n• BLANKINTERNET#0 = Classic Publishing Site Blank\n• CSPCONTAINER#0 = SharePoint Embedded Site\n\nNOTE:\n\n• Existing classic publishing sites created with the templates listed above will have custom scripting disabled by default.\n\n• Disabling custom scripting does not affect the execution of scripts that have already been added to a site or page.\n\nRefer to this documentation to learn more about the security considerations of ungoverned scripting.\n2. Ability to set site property bag valued without requiring custom scripting enablement.\nUsers no longer need to set DenyAddAndCustomizePages to $false or 0 (i.e. enable custom scripting) in a site to manage site property bag values. We have introduced a new AllowWebPropertyBagUpdateWhenDenyAddAndCustomizePagesIsEnabled setting at the site level and at the tenant level to allow adding/managing site property bag values. Please see documentation here for tenant level setting and here for the site level setting.\n3. Classic publishing sites creation and feature activation changes\nUsers will no longer be able to create new classic publishing related site collections or activate publishing features in existing site collections. This applies to both UX and API interactions.\nSites collections with the following templates cannot be created:\n• BLANKINTERNETCONTAINER#0 = Publishing Portal Site\n\n• CMSPUBLISHING#0 = Publishing Site\n\n• BLANKINTERNET#0 = Publishing Site Blank\n\n• ENTERWIKI#0 = Enterprise Wiki\n\n• SRCHCEN#0 = Enterprise Search Center\n\n• SPSSITES#0 = Site Directory\n\n• SPSNHOME#0 = News Home Site\n\n• PRODUCTCATALOG#0 = Product Catalog\n\n• SPSREPORTCENTER#0 = Report Center\n\n• SPSTOPIC#0 = Topic Area Template\n\nExisting classic publishing enabled site collections are unaffected and can continue regular usage, including creation of sub sites.\n[When this will happen]\nBoth changes, the extended custom scripting governance and the new classic publishing restrictions, will take effect starting September 15, 2025.\n[How this will affect your organization]\n\n• When custom scripting is disabled in classic publishing sites, users will no longer be able to use script editor web parts, create custom master pages or page layouts, and utilize several other features. More details on features affected when custom scripting is disabled can be viewed in this documentation.\n\n• With the change to stop the creation of new classic publishing site collections and publishing feature activation, SharePoint admins will no longer be able to create new classic publishing enabled site collections or enable publishing features at site collection level.\n\n[What you need to do to prepare]\nWe recommend taking the following actions to prepare for these upcoming changes.\n\n1. Inform owners of the classic publishing sites in your organization of these upcoming changes. Promote switching to use of Modern sites. Refer to this guide.\n2. The following tenant-level opt-out operation, used to allow custom scripting changes in classic publishing sites, will be retired starting March 15, 2026. Please ensure appropriate actions are taken ahead of this change.\nSet-SPOTenant -DelayDenyAddAndCustomizePagesEnforcementOnClassicPublishingSites $true\n3. Customers may still temporarily opt out of custom scripting enforcement for a specific site (any template) with tenant admin approval. This opt-out is effective for 24 hours and can be enabled using the following PowerShell command:\nSet-SPOSite <SiteURL>\n4. If you need to allow the creation of new classic publishing site collections or enable publishing feature activations, use the following PowerShell command set the flag to allow.\nSet-SPOTenant -AllowClassicPublishingSiteCreation $true\nNOTE:\n• You need to install the latest (16.0.26211.12010 or higher) SharePoint Online Management Shell in order to run the commands above.\n• The DelayDenyAddAndCustomizePagesEnforcementOnClassicPublishingSites command is scheduled to end starting on March 15, 2026, while all other commands are expected to remain functional beyond that date.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nThere is no impact or change to compliance.\n[Referenced content]\n\nSecurity considerations of allowing custom script - SharePoint in Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\nAllow or prevent custom script - SharePoint in Microsoft 365 | Microsoft Learn\nSharePoint modernization guidance | Microsoft Learn","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-18","modified":"2026-07-29","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1117115","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-562354","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updated Copilot Answers","desc":"Copilot Answers in Copilot Search (in the M365 Copilot App on web and desktop) will provide more concise responses and more prominently highlight the ability to continue in the conversation in Copilot chat on the right-hand sidebar.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-23","modified":"2026-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562354","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-410366","title":"Microsoft Teams: User uploaded custom background images for the new VDI solution for Microsoft Teams","desc":"With this new feature, users on the new VDI solution for Teams can blur their background, choose a Teams virtual background, or replace their background entirely with any image they want by uploading it through the \"Video effects and Settings\" option.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-08-06","modified":"2026-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=410366","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-497844","title":"Microsoft CoPilot (Microsoft 365): Makers can build DA's with Flexible layouts and rich UX components","desc":"Flexible layouts and rich UX components will enable makers to build highly expressive agents, ultimately driving increased user engagement and virality.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497844","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2027","gaSort":202705},{"id":"rm-560708","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection – AI-powered intent for classifiers","desc":"AI-powered intent for classifiers: Microsoft Purview Information Protection will generate a human-readable semantic intent for custom Sensitive Information Types (SITs), helping customers better understand what their classifiers detect and refine them for higher accuracy and fewer false positives.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560708","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567313","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Graph API Support for Archive Mailboxes","desc":"Access to Archive mailboxes (Main + Auxiliary) through Microsoft Graph. The goal is to give users a single, seamless Archive view, even though Archive data may physically reside across multiple auxiliary mailboxes with EWS Graph APIs getting deprecated by OCT 2026.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567313","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-559106","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - DLP Policy Change Insights with Security Copilot","desc":"Introduce an AI-powered capability leveraging Microsoft Security Copilot to automatically generate natural language explanations of changes made to DLP policies after each update within Microsoft Purview. This feature will analyze policy version deltas (pre-update vs. post-update) and produce a structured, human-readable summary that clearly explains: What changed Where the change occurred (rule, condition, action, location, etc.) The impact of the change The potential enforcement implications The goal is to eliminate manual policy diff analysis, reduce configuration ambiguity, and improve governance transparency for compliance and security administrators.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559106","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562341","title":"Microsoft Teams: Join Google Meet meetings in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"Organizations now have expanded meeting interoperability with two-way Direct Guest Join (DGJ) between Google Meet and Teams meetings. Teams Rooms on Windows devices can join Google Meet meetings, and Google Meet devices can join Teams meetings. Users can join with one click through the calendar or by meeting ID. This capability is now available for both Commercial (Feb 2026) and Government cloud environments.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-14","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562341","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-564766","title":"Microsoft Teams: Manage Built-in Teams agents in the Teams admin center","desc":"Admins will be able to manage Teams built-in agents across core Teams experiences, including chats, channels, and meetings, through a dedicated experience in the Teams admin center. From a centralized location, admins can control agents’ availability for users and groups. These agents will be enabled by default for licensed users and managed independently from org-wide Microsoft app settings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564766","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-562051","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Enriched Audit Data for Matched Rules","desc":"When DLP rules detect policy violations in Exchange Online, they generate audit records that administrators rely on for compliance monitoring, incident investigation, and policy tuning. Previously, these records only showed Sensitive Information Type matches. This feature aims to extend that to sender domain, subject keywords, attachment type, or recipient information. Now they will be visible in alerts and Activity Explorer providing data enrichment to the administrators.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562051","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557683","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management- Data Security Triage Agent in IRM Enhancements","desc":"The Data Security Triage Agent in Insider Risk Management is deploying enhancements such as improved user risk and activity explorer pattern summaries to support improved investigation accuracy, context, and decision quality. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-24","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557683","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-513274","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage Communities in Microsoft Teams","desc":"Your Viva Engage communities will now be available in Teams along side teams, chats and channels. Engage communities in Microsoft Teams make it simple to connect, share, and learn across your organization. This new experience brings discoverable, asynchronous conversations and leadership engagement into Teams—helping employees explore ideas and perspectives beyond project-based collaboration.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513274","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559996","title":"Microsoft Viva: New Overview experience in Agent Dashboard","desc":"Customers can now view and understand their agent landscape through the new Overview page that will be included as part of the Agent Dashboard in Microsoft Viva. This experience will provide customers with key at-a-glance insights on adoption in their organizations and visibility into who’s creating agents used in their organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-07","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559996","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557676","title":"Outlook: Delimiter setting admin policy","desc":"Admins will be able to define a tenant‑wide default value for the Mail Compose and Reply setting that controls whether commas are used to separate recipients. Updated June 2, 2026: We are in the process of correcting an issue with setting the policy. We expect to complete in mid-June. Thank you for your patience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-24","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557676","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561206","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: New dedicated License Requests page in Microsoft 365 Admin Center","desc":"We are introducing a new dedicated License Requests page in the Microsoft 365 Admin Center to help admins more easily discover, review, and manage Microsoft 365 Copilot license requests submitted by users.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-29","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561206","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-479965","title":"OneDrive: Upcoming change to shared folder experience in Microsoft OneDrive","desc":"With this feature update, when a user clicks a link to a shared folder from Teams chat, channels, email, or other places, they will navigate to the shared folder within the People view of their own OneDrive. This new view, organized by people, will show and allow access to all the files and folders that have been shared with the user.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-06","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=479965","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-555858","title":"Microsoft Teams: Admin setting for simpler meeting passcodes (numeric‑only)","desc":"Tenant admins can enable a meeting policy setting that generates 8 digit numeric-only passcodes for meetings organized by selected users/groups. Because numeric-only passcodes increase the risk of unauthorized access, enabling the setting displays a warning and requires explicit confirmation.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-380842","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Referenced sources are cited in drafted content","desc":"When drafting content using the inline canvas Copilot experience that's based on referenced sources, Copilot includes citations in the text it generates, indicating references to information in the content.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-12-06","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380842","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-494999","title":"Microsoft 365: M365 Archive Search","desc":"M365 Archive will introduce new search capabilities that allow end-users to easily identify archived content. This feature aims to improve productivity by making archived data searchable by end users so they can identify which site needs to be reactivated.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-24","modified":"2026-07-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494999","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"mc-MC1275312","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: AI meeting recap without transcript to meet compliance policies","desc":"Updated July 27, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nRecap without saving transcript provides an alternative now for Copilot users to generate a meeting summary using live meeting context, in case where saving a meeting transcript or recording is not preferred or allowed.\n\nThis capability is intended for scenarios where organizations want AI‑generated recaps but have policies that limit or prohibit the retention of transcripts or recordings. When disabled, no AI recap is generated. Existing Copilot licensing and tenant‑level AI controls continue to apply.\nThis feature will be available to users with an M365 Copilot (Premium) license across platforms, including desktop (Windows and Mac), web, and mobile.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558286.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out early October 2026 (previously mid-August) and expect to complete by mid-October 2026 (previously late August).\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out mid-October 2026 (previously late August) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late September).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Microsoft Teams meeting organizers and participants with an M365 Copilot (Premium) license\n\n• Microsoft 365 administrators managing Copilot and AI controls\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Teams admin center - Tenant admins will have control to opt in or out for AI features (e.g. Copilot, Intelligent Recap) for the meeting under the tenant. This feature is controlled by AI toggle/setting in the admin center. If AI is disabled at the tenant level, this experience is not available.\n• Meeting options (before meeting) - Meeting organizers with a Copilot license can enable or disable Recap without saving transcript in meeting options under Copilot and other AI before the meeting\n\n• In-Meeting controls (during meeting) – Meeting organizers with a Copilot license can enable or disable Recap without saving transcript anytime during the meeting via the AI toggle (appears at top-left). Participants can see whether AI is being turned on/off, while participants cannot change this setting.\n\n• Post-meeting AI summary - When enabled, Intelligent Recap will generate an AI summary even if recording and transcription are not turned on. Meeting attendees with Copilot license can view the AI summary after the meeting. No transcript or recording is saved as part of this experience.\n\n• Storage – When enabled, a doc will be stored in organizer’s OneDrive for default 120days, and it will be configurable in admin center for longer/shorter days as needed.\n\n• Deletion – For post-meeting AI summary, organizer can choose to delete the content from the Recap page, and it will result in the deletion of the doc in organizer’s OneDrive, and vice versa.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• Review your organization’s AI and Copilot governance policies to determine whether this experience aligns with your compliance posture.\n• If you want to opt out, disable the AI toggle in your tenant settings to prevent Recap without saving transcript from being used.\n• Update internal guidance and helpdesk documentation to reflect that meeting recaps may be generated without recordings or transcripts.\n• Communicate this change to meeting organizers, especially in regulated environments.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nExplanation\n\nAI/ML interaction with customer data\nCopilot generates AI-based meeting recaps using live meeting context even when recording and transcription are not enabled. No meeting transcript or recording is saved.\n\nNew way for users to interact with generative AI\nUsers can receive AI-generated Intelligent Recap without starting or saving a meeting recording or transcript.\n\nAdmin controls availableThis capability is governed by the existing tenant-level AI toggle. Disabling AI prevents Recap without saving transcript from being used.\n\nUser enable/disable capability\nMeeting organizers can enable or disable the feature before the meeting, and organizers or participants with Copilot licenses can toggle it during the meeting.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-09","modified":"2026-07-27","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1275312","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-553219","title":"Microsoft 365: New profile cards for buildings, rooms and desks","desc":"Buildings, rooms and desks that are added to the Places directory will have new profile cards, accessible from Copilot Chat and across other Microsoft 365 entry points.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-07-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553219","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-568073","title":"Microsoft Viva: Campaigns in SharePoint","desc":"Campaigns in SharePoint (site campaigns) is a new capability that brings Viva Amplify’ s campaign management natively into SharePoint. Corporate communications teams now have a unified place to create, distribute, and measure their news without leaving the platform where their news content already lives. This feature applies only to Amplify users as of now. This is a complementary way to create lighter weight campaigns inside a SharePoint site as a way to organize your SharePoint news posts and benefit from campaign analytics directly from SharePoint.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-23","modified":"2026-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=568073","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566470","title":"Microsoft Viva: Insights for GitHub Copilot spend and usage","desc":"AI spend and usage insights for GitHub Copilot will be available on Viva Insights for managers with at least 5 direct reports (scoped access), Global analysts and Microsoft Global administrators. They can track spend and make data-driven decisions for AI spend and usage in GitHub Copilot. The dashboard is enabled by default to ensure immediate access.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-23","modified":"2026-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566470","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-503590","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Admins can now edit user mappings and query filters for ServiceNow Connector","desc":"Support connection edit of user mapping, query filter for ServiceNow","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503590","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1287370","title":"(Updated) Auto upgrade of shared calendars from legacy MAPI model to modern REST model","desc":"Updated July 20, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft is introducing an automatic upgrade for shared calendars in Outlook and Exchange Online, transitioning from the legacy MAPI-based model to the modern REST-based model. This server-side upgrade will improve calendar sync reliability, performance, and consistency for delegates and users who access shared calendars. The change is designed to be seamless and will not require any action from users or administrators.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide):\nTill WW it is enabled and available to all WW tenants. Now we are expanding it to higher rings:\nGCC High /DoD:\nRollout starting August 2026 (previously end of June) and completing by late September 2026 (previously late July)\nNote: Rollout will be progressive and timing may vary by tenant.\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Microsoft 365 tenants using Exchange Online\n• Users who have Editor or higher permissions on shared calendars in user or shared mailboxes\n• Delegates and users who access shared calendars in Outlook\n\nWhat will happen\n• Shared calendars will be automatically upgraded from the legacy MAPI-based model to the modern REST-based model.\n• A new calendar folder will be created in a hidden state and will only become visible to the user once the full sync is successfully completed and validated, ensuring a seamless rollover to the new model.\n• The transition is expected to appear seamless, with no interruption to normal user workflows.\n• Events older than one year will be excluded from the initial sync window. However, recurring events with instances falling within or after the one-year threshold will still be included in the sync.\n• Existing permissions and sharing relationships will be preserved; no re-sharing or permission reset will be required.\n• The upgrade process is fully automatic and requires no action from the user — no Outlook restart, profile recreation, or any other manual steps.\n• No data loss is expected as a result of this change.\n• The rollout will initially support auto-upgrade for up to four shared calendars per delegate or principal, scaling up to six over time. Those managing more than six shared calendars will be excluded from the auto-upgrade and will experience no change to their current setup.\n\nHow does it effect the Classic Outlook setting 'Turn on shared calendar improvements'?\n• After migration, Classic Outlook will continue to honour the existing setting. Although shared calendars are upgraded to the REST model at the service level, Classic Outlook will follow the setting and use MAPI-based model if the setting is turned off. This behaviour is limited to Classic Outlook; all other endpoints (Outlook Web, Mobile, Mac, New Outlook) will use REST.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required.\nWe recommend that administrators:\n• During migration, a hidden shared calendar folder may be visible to tenant admins and support teams via the Get-MailboxFolderStatistics cmdlet. This is expected and has no impact on end users.\n• Monitor for persistent issues, such as missing meetings after the migration window or duplicate calendar folders, and contact Microsoft support if observed.\n• If a manual rollback is required after the calendar becomes visible, open a support request through standard Microsoft support channels.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1287370","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560321","title":"Microsoft Teams: Meeting toolbar redesigned","desc":"You can now customize the meeting toolbar by pinning, unpinning, and reordering controls to match how you work. Raise Hand is grouped under Reactions to reduce mis-clicks, and Leave is clearly separated on the right. It may feel different at first, but it’s designed to be faster and easier to use.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560321","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-555855","title":"Microsoft Teams: Camera view switching in multi-camera Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"When in a meeting with another Teams Rooms on Windows that has multiple cameras, you can switch camera views in that room via the participant panel on the console, or video tile on a touch board, to optimize your views.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561550","title":"Microsoft Teams: Proximity join support for presenters in Teams events from Teams Rooms on Windows and Android","desc":"Presenters can take advantage of proximity join with Teams Rooms on Windows or Android for fast, effortless connection to nearby room systems during Teams events, such as town halls, webinars, and structured meetings. This feature enables seamless live presentations.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561550","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-541830","title":"Microsoft Teams: Branded Meeting Reactions","desc":"With new branded reactions, organizations can now extend their visual identity directly into meetings. IT admins simply upload custom reaction icons reflecting brand elements or event themes, and these instantly become available for meeting participants. A simple way to create more cohesive, on-brand meeting experiences.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-16","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=541830","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-537281","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Search] [Copilot Search] Copilot Chat available when using Copilot Search","desc":"Copilot Chat will be available for Microsoft 365 Copilot users from the side pane on the right-hand side when using Copilot Search in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app. This allows users to engage with Copilot while browsing universal search without switching pages or losing context.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537281","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-512429","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Seamless Search and Chat Integration","desc":"Microsoft 365 Chat brings the power of conversational AI directly into Microsoft 365 Copilot Search, enabling users to move effortlessly from finding information to acting on it. Search results become the foundation for contextual chat, allowing you to ask follow-up questions, synthesize insights, and generate content—all in one unified experience. This integration reduces workflow fragmentation, accelerates decision-making, and delivers a more intuitive way to interact with your organization’s knowledge.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-08","modified":"2026-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=512429","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567894","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Share Autonomous Agents to End Users (Run-Only)","desc":"Previously, autonomous agents could only be used and managed by makers, limiting their reach to the people who needed them. Run-only sharing enables makers to securely share autonomous agents with end users, allowing users to benefit from agent-driven automation without requiring edit permissions or ownership. This extends autonomous agent capabilities to a broader audience while maintaining governance and control.","products":["Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-20","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567894","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561552","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention to restrict processing external emails in Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat","desc":"We are expanding Microsoft Purview DLP for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat to safeguard risks from external emails. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot and Chat from processing emails from senders external to your organization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561552","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567889","title":"SharePoint: Flexible Section Authoring Improvements","desc":"We've enhanced Flexible Sections in SharePoint Pages to make page layout creation more intuitive and predictable. Authors can now use visual column layout guides that mirror familiar sections, keep gridlines and layout guides visible while editing, and convert existing sections into Flexible Sections with a single click while preserving content placement. These improvements help authors create richer page designs with greater confidence and consistency across desktop, mobile, and email experiences.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-20","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567889","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1221452","title":"(Update)Microsoft Entra ID: General Availability of passkey profiles and migration for existing Passkeys (FIDO2) tenants","desc":"Updated July 20, 2026: We have updated the content. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nStarting in March 2026, Microsoft Entra ID will introduce passkey profiles and synced passkeys to General Availability (GA). This update allows administrators to opt in to a new passkey profiles experience that supports group-based passkey configurations and introduces a new passkeyType property.\nImportant: Only tenants that already have Passkeys (FIDO2) enabled are affected by this update.\n\nThe passkeyType property enables admins to configure:\n• Device-bound passkeys\n• Synced passkeys\n• Both\n\nIf your tenant already has Passkeys (FIDO2) enabled and you do not opt in to passkey profiles during the initial rollout window, your tenant will be automatically migrated to the passkey profiles schema at the date range specified below. When this occurs:\n• Existing Passkey (FIDO2) authentication method configurations will be moved into a Default passkey profile.\n• The passkeyType value will be set based on the tenant’s current attestation settings. Synced passkeys will be enabled for tenants with attestation enforcement disabled.\n• No new authentication methods are enabled as part of this migration.\n• This migration also impacts Authentication methods registration campaign set to “Microsoft managed” state, which uses passkey configuration settings to determine which registration prompts are shown to users.\n\nAuthentication Methods Registration Campaign changes (Microsoft-Managed Only)\nTenants are impacted when all the following conditions are met:\n• The Passkeys (FIDO2) authentication method policy is Enabled\n• Authentication methods registration campaign is set to “Microsoft managed” state\n• Allow self-service setup is Enabled\n• Target specific AAGUIDs is not selected (no AAGUID restrictions configured)\n• The Authentication Methods Registration Campaign state is set to Microsoft-managed\n• The tenant has at least one user enabled for both synced passkeys and device‑bound passkeys\n• Only users who are enabled for both synced passkeys and device‑bound passkeys, with no passkey profile restrictions configured (i.e. attestation enforcement, AAGUID restrictions), will receive a passkey registration nudge during sign‑in.\n\nFor these tenants, Microsoft-managed registration campaign settings will be updated after passkey profile automatic migration is complete. We will roll out changes incrementally to in-scope tenants according to the timeline outlined below.\n[When this will happen]\nPasskey profile and Synced passkeys General Availability\n• Public cloud Worldwide, GCC: Rollout begins in early March 2026 and is expected to complete by late March 2026\n• GCC High, DoD clouds: Rollout begins in early May 2026 and is expected to complete by late May 2026\n• USNat, USSec: Rollout begins in early October 2026 (previously early July) and is expected to complete by late October 2026 (previously late July)\n\nAutomatic migration for existing passkeys (FIDO2) enabled tenants\n• Public cloud Worldwide, GCC: Rollout begins in early May 2026 and is expected to complete by late June 2026\n• GCC High, DoD clouds: Rollout begins in early October 2026 (previously early August) and is expected to complete by late October 2026 (previously late August)\n• USNat, USSec: Rollout begins in early October 2026 (previously early August) and is expected to complete by late October 2026 (previously late August)\n\nAuthentication Methods registration campaign changes in Microsoft-Managed state (for in-scope tenants):\n• Public cloud Worldwide, GCC: Rollout begins in early May 2026 and is expected to complete by late June 2026\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nAutomatic migration for existing passkeys (FIDO2) enabled tenants\nWhat will happen:\nIf you have not opted in to passkey profiles by your automatic enablement period, your tenant will be migrated to passkey profiles.\n• Your existing Passkey (FIDO2) configurations will be migrated into a Default passkey profile\n• New passkeyType property will be auto-populated\n• If enforce attestation is enabled, then device-bound allowed\n• If enforce attestation is disabled, then device-bound and synced allowed\n• Any existing key restrictions will remain intact\n• Any existing user targets will be assigned to the Default passkey profile\n\nAuthentication Methods registration campaign changes in Microsoft-Managed state (for in-scope tenants)\nWhat will happen:\nMicrosoft-managed registration campaign settings will be updated:\n• \"Targeted authentication method” will change from Microsoft Authenticator to “passkeys (FIDO2)”.\n• “Days allowed to snooze” setting will change from 3days to “1 day”. This setting will no longer be configurable.\n• “Limited number of snoozes” setting will change from Enabled to \"Disabled”. This setting will no longer be configurable.\n• The default user targeting will be updated from voice call or text message users to all multifactor authentication (MFA) capable users.\n\nWhat is the end user impact:\nOnce the above changes have taken effect, users targeted in the registration campaign will begin to receive passkey registration nudges during sign-in flows after they have completed multifactor authentication.\n•\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nIf you want a configuration different from the migration defaults, review the timeline above and opt in to passkey profiles before your tenant’s automatic enablement window begins. Then configure the Default passkey profile’s passkeyType to your preferred values.\nWe also recommend:\n• Review your registration campaign configuration, especially if its set to Microsoft-managed. If you do not want registration campaign to target passkeys, you can:\n• Switch the registration campaign state to Enabled and continue targeting Microsoft Authenticator, or\n• Set the registration campaign state to Disabled.\n• Update runbooks and help content so your help desk and end users understand any changes in passkey availability or behavior.\n\nLearn more:\n• Enable passkeys for your organization - Microsoft Entra ID | Microsoft Learn\n• How to Enable Passkey (FIDO2) Profiles in Microsoft Entra ID (preview) - Microsoft Entra ID | Microsoft Learn\n• How to Enable Synced Passkeys (FIDO2) in Microsoft Entra ID (preview) - Microsoft Entra ID | Microsoft Learn\n• Synced passkeys FAQ - Microsoft Entra ID | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1221452","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"mc-MC1282568","title":"(Updated) General Availability: Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows","desc":"Updated July 20, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nMicrosoft Entra passkeys on Windows will soon be Generally Available, enabling phishing‑resistant, passwordless sign‑in to Microsoft Entra‑protected resources from Windows devices.\nThe Public Preview of this capability was previously announced in MC1247893.\nUsers can create device‑bound passkeys stored in the Windows Hello container and authenticate using Windows Hello methods (face, fingerprint, or PIN). This expands passwordless authentication support to Windows devices that aren’t Microsoft Entra‑joined or registered, helping organizations strengthen security and reduce reliance on passwords across corporate‑managed, personal, and shared device scenarios.\n[When this will happen:]\n• General Availability (Worldwide, GCC): We will begin rolling out in late April 2026 and expect to complete by mid‑June 2026.\n• General Availability (GCC High, DoD): We will begin rolling out in early October 2026 (previously early September 2026) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late September).\n\nHow this affects your organization:\nWho is affected:\nOrganizations using Microsoft Entra ID with passkeys enabled in the Authentication Methods policy whose users sign in from Windows devices, including:\n• Corporate‑managed PCs\n• Personal devices\n• Shared devices\n\nWhat will happen:\nWith this General Availability release:\n• Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows will no longer require explicit opt‑in through Windows Hello AAGUID allow‑listing in a passkey (FIDO2) profile.\n• This represents a change from Public Preview behavior, where administrators were required to explicitly allow Windows Hello AAGUIDs in a passkey profile for Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows to function.\n• If your passkey profile allows device‑bound, non‑attested passkeys:\n• Users scoped to that profile will now be able to register and use Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows by default without additional administrator configuration.\n• As a result:\n• Users in scope of passkey profiles that allow device‑bound, non‑attested passkeys may begin registering and using passkeys on Windows devices.\n• If Conditional Access policies allow:\n• Passkeys can be created and used on Windows devices that are not Microsoft Entra‑joined or registered, including personal or shared PCs.\n• Each Windows device requires separate passkey registration per Entra account.\n• Windows Hello for Business remains recommended for managed, Microsoft Entra‑joined or registered devices.\n• Passkeys on Windows supplement unmanaged or shared device scenarios and do not support device sign‑in.\n• Attestation is not currently supported for Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows but is planned for a future update.\n•\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n•\n\nNo action is required for most organizations.\nIf you do not want users to register or use Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows:\n• Update the relevant passkey (FIDO2) profile to block Windows Hello AAGUIDs.\n• Review existing passkey profiles that allow device‑bound, non‑attested passkeys.\n• Add Windows Hello AAGUIDs to the block list in passkey profiles where passkey usage on Windows devices should not be permitted.\n•\n\nLearn more: Enable Microsoft Entra passkey on Windows | Microsoft Learn (will be updated before GA rollout)\n[Compliance considerations:]\nCompliance areaExplanation\nDoes the change modify, interrupt, or disable Conditional Access policies?Existing Conditional Access policies continue to govern whether passkeys can be created or used on unmanaged Windows devices.\nDoes the change include an admin control and can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Admins can control passkey availability through Authentication Methods policies and FIDO2 passkey profiles scoped to Microsoft Entra ID groups.\nDoes the change allow a user to enable and disable the feature themselves?Users may register Microsoft Entra passkeys on Windows devices if permitted by administrator policy configuration.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1282568","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-564606","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Declarative agents with Actions available in GCC High and DoD","desc":"Declarative Agents with Actions enable Microsoft 365 Copilot to take real-world actions by invoking APIs, plugins, and enterprise workflows directly within the chat experience. Using custom actions, declarative agents can call external systems, execute operations, and retrieve or update data, moving beyond Q&A to full task completion. These actions are powered through API plugins, MCP tools, and enterprise connectors, allowing seamless integration with line-of-business applications and services. The Copilot platform dynamically reasons over available actions and selects the appropriate tool to fulfill user intent, enabling multi-step workflows such as creating records, submitting requests, or triggering business processes within a single conversational flow","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564606","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558681","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Enrich Defender alerts Graph API with DLP event data","desc":"Enhance current API infrastructure to provide easy and simple way for customers to export data to integrate with SIEM tools, create automated workflows and generate customizable reports. Today alert data is present in Graph API and DLP rule match event details are present in Management API. This work enriches the graph API with DLP event data to make correlation and integration easy for customers.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-13","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558681","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561647","title":"Microsoft Teams: Room availability signal for Teams events","desc":"In the Events app in Teams, Teams events organizers will now be able to see if the chosen room or space they have selected for their event is available at the designated time or not. This feature is available for any Teams event organizer with a Teams Enterprise license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-08","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561647","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561915","title":"Microsoft Teams: Save your event as template to reuse event configurations","desc":"Organizers for Teams events instances will now be able to reuse their event configurations in the Events app in Teams. Organizers can save these configurations as a template in the Events app to use again for future Teams events.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561915","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561912","title":"Microsoft Teams: Shared & Delegate Mailbox Scheduling for Events","desc":"Empower Chiefs of Staff and delegated roles to efficiently organize events on behalf of leaders or teams using shared or delegated mailboxes. By sending trusted invites from the chosen mailbox, this capability ensures consistent identity, improved trust, and smoother event setup.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561912","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-553220","title":"SharePoint: Admin policy for expiring \"People in your organization\" links","desc":"Administrators can now set organization-wide policies to automatically expire \"People in your organization\" sharing links after a specified period. This helps organizations maintain tighter control over internal content sharing by ensuring links don't remain active indefinitely. Configure expiration timeframes that align with your organization's data governance requirements—whether that's 30 days, 90 days, or a custom period.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-07-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553220","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-567670","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Agent 365 agents within Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat and Declarative Agents","desc":"Agents that are published to Agents 365 are already managed in the Microsoft 365 Admin Center. If the agent implements the Agent2Agent protocol, it can be used as a connected agent for the agents that users build in Agent Builder or Copilot Studio.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-17","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567670","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567893","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Agent 365 dashboard for managers","desc":"Managers in organizations can now access their Agent 365 data through the Agent Dashboard in Copilot Analytics (Insights), enabling them to understand activity across all agents registered through Agent 365. Customers with Agent 365 and Copilot will now see the Agent 365 Dashboard with the ability to view historical data in Agent Dashboard.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-17","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567893","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-567888","title":"Outlook: All Day events to show up more clearly in the Mail module Calendar Preview","desc":"We're making it easier to tell when receiving meeting invites that conflict with scheduled Out of Office time or Busy All Day events, on Outlook Web and Outlook for Windows.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-17","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567888","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1301714","title":"Microsoft Purview | Data Loss Prevention- DLP to restrict processing external emails in M365 Copilot and Copilot Chat","desc":"Updated July 17, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are expanding Microsoft Purview DLP for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat to safeguard risks from external emails. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot and Chat from processing emails from senders external to your organization.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 561552.\n[When this will happen]\n• Public preview: We will begin rolling out in early June 2026 and expect to complete by late June 2026.\n• General availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in late January 2027 (previously late July) and expect to complete by late February 2027 (previously late August).\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Organizations using Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) or Copilot Chat\n• Admins managing AI governance, security, and data protection using Microsoft Purview\n\nWhat will happen\n• A new DLP policy control will be available for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat.\n• When enabled by an admin:\n• Emails sent from external or untrusted domains are excluded from being:\n• Referenced\n• Summarized\n• Used as grounding data by Copilot\n• Copilot continues to generate responses using trusted internal Microsoft 365 data sources (for example, SharePoint, OneDrive, and internal Exchange content), subject to existing licensing and policy.\n\nThis change does not:\n• Affect email delivery, retention, eDiscovery, or user access\n• Change existing Copilot interaction behavior unless the policy is explicitly configured\n\nDefault state:\n• Off by default.\n• There is no change unless an admin enables this control in Microsoft Purview.\n\nScreenshot 1. Select Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat as the DLP policy location:\n\nScreenshot 2. New DLP setting to restrict processing of external email content:\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required if you do not plan to use this capability.\nIf you want to enable the feature:\n• Create or update a DLP policy for Microsoft 365 Copilot in the Microsoft Purview portal.\n• Review existing DLP configurations to understand potential Copilot impact.\n• Ensure your admin account has the required DLP and Purview roles.\n• Inform IT, security, and helpdesk teams about the new control.\n• Update internal documentation related to AI governance and Copilot usage.\n\nLearn more:\n• Learn about data loss prevention | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n• Learn about using Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention to protect interactions with Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n• Permissions - Create and deploy data loss prevention policies | Microsoft Purview | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nQuestionAnswer\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed?Yes. External email content is excluded from Copilot grounding when the policy is enabled; underlying email storage, access, and retention are unchanged.\nDoes the change introduce or modify AI/ML capabilities interacting with customer data?Yes. Copilot grounding logic is updated to respect a new DLP exclusion for external email content.\nDoes the change modify Purview DLP enforcement?Yes. Adds a new DLP control scoped specifically to Copilot and Copilot Chat grounding behavior.\nDoes the change include an admin control?Yes. The feature is controlled via Microsoft Purview DLP policies and is admin-configurable.","products":["Microsoft Purview","Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1301714","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560320","title":"Microsoft Teams: Breakout rooms up to 1,000 Attendees in Teams meetings","desc":"Organizers can now use breakout rooms in Teams meetings with up to 1,000 attendees, enabling more interactive sessions, smaller group discussions, and improved audience engagement without compromising scale or performance.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-15","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560320","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-557255","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention to prevent Microsoft 365 Copilot processing content with sensitivity labels supports all storage locations","desc":"The Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention policy to restrict Microsoft 365 Copilot processing sensitive files in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint will now apply regardless of file storage location.","products":["Excel","Microsoft 365","PowerPoint","Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557255","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-566695","title":"OneDrive: Block screen capture for sensitivity-labeled PDFs in the OneDrive and SharePoint web viewer","desc":"The OneDrive and SharePoint web PDF viewer will block screen capture in Microsoft Edge when users open PDFs whose sensitivity (MIP) label without Copy (EXTRACT) permission.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-07-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566695","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-534607","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage: Detect moderated themes in images","desc":"Engages theme moderation feature is a powerful AI tool to monitor and moderate content. With this update, images can now match to themes, just like text.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-27","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534607","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706},{"id":"rm-564616","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - AI Powered Data Loss Prevention Policy Optimizer","desc":"DLP Policy Optimizer uses AI to analyze your organization’s DLP policies, rule structure, and activity signals to identify optimization opportunities that are difficult to detect manually. It highlights overlapping rules, redundant conditions, misconfigurations, and sources of excessive noise, and presents prioritized recommendations with supporting evidence and suggested actions. This enables you to reduce false positives and alert noise, improve policy precision, and simplify policy management with confidence.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-02","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564616","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-380721","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Trigger Power automate workflows as outcome of DLP rule match","desc":"This introduces a new DLP rule action to trigger custom Power automate workflows when a DLP rule is violated.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-01-31","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380721","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1248389","title":"(Updated) Retirement of -Credential parameter when connecting to Exchange Online PowerShell","desc":"Updated July 15, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nMicrosoft is retiring the -Credential parameter used when connecting to Exchange Online PowerShell. Starting with module versions released in December 2026 and later, the -Credential parameter will be removed from both Connect-ExchangeOnline and Connect-IppsSession cmdlets. Organizations using this parameter in automation scripts must migrate to a supported authentication method before that date. This change improves security by moving away from legacy authentication methods that do not support modern protections such as multifactor authentication (MFA).\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• The -Credential parameter will be removed from Connect-ExchangeOnline and Connect-IppsSession cmdlets in Exchange Online PowerShell module versions released beginning end of year 2026 (previously July).\n\n• A separate server-side retirement of the underlying authentication flow is planned for a later date and will be communicated in advance.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Microsoft 365 administrators using Exchange Online or Security & Compliance PowerShell\n\n• Organizations with automation scripts that use the -Credential parameter\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• If your organization uses the -Credential parameter in PowerShell scripts or automation workflows connecting to Exchange Online or Security & Compliance PowerShell, those scripts will break when you update to an Exchange Online PowerShell module version released beginning December 2026.\n\n• No impact if your organization does not use the -Credential parameter\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n• If you are using the -Credential parameter, begin migrating your scripts now. Do not wait until December 2026. Choose the appropriate alternative based on your scenario:\n\n• Interactive admin access: Switch to modern authentication with MFA. Learn more: Connect to Exchange Online PowerShell.\n• Automation outside Azure: Use app-only authentication (certificate-based). Learn more: App-only authentication for unattended scripts in Exchange Online PowerShell and Security & Compliance PowerShell.\n• Automation within Azure: Use managed identity authentication (no secrets required). Learn more: Use Azure managed identities to connect to Exchange Online PowerShell.\n\n• Review internal documentation and communicate changes to admins\n\n• If you are not using the -Credential parameter, no action is required.\n\nAdditional information\n\nThis change is currently client-side only and will not take effect automatically. Your existing scripts will continue to work if you continue using an Exchange Online PowerShell module version released before December 2026. The -Credential parameter will only be removed when you upgrade to a module version released in December 2026 and later.\n\nA separate server-side retirement of the Credential parameter authentication flow is planned for a later date. When that occurs, the -Credential parameter will stop functioning even on older module versions. Microsoft will communicate that timeline separately and provide advance notice before any service-side changes take effect.\n\nWe strongly recommend migrating proactively rather than waiting, to avoid disruption when either change occurs. If you have questions or concerns, contact Microsoft Support or leave a comment on the Exchange Team Blog post.\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nImpact\n\nConditional Access policies\nRetiring the -Credential parameter removes use of the ROPC authentication flow and enables enforcement of Conditional Access and multifactor authentication for Exchange Online PowerShell connections.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1248389","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-567667","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Agent 365 Dashboard in Insights","desc":"Customers can now access their Agent 365 data through the Agent Dashboard in Copilot Analytics (Insights), enabling leaders to understand activity across all agents registered through Agent 365. Customers with Agent 365 and Copilot will now see the Agent 365 Dashboard with the ability to view historical data in Agent Dashboard.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567667","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-477371","title":"SharePoint: Microsoft 365 Archive file-level archiving","desc":"This introduces archiving at the file level for Microsoft 365 Archive.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=477371","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559110","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Find meetings based on topics and keywords","desc":"Copilot will be able to find meetings based on topics or keywords from relevant data like meeting body, chat and transcription.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-10","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559110","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561920","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): SharePoint list support in Agent Builder","desc":"Agent Builder now supports using a SharePoint list as a knowledge source for agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot. Makers can ground an agent in structured list data so users can ask questions and get responses based on information stored in a selected SharePoint list. For this release, each agent can reference one SharePoint list with up to 20,000 items, alongside other knowledge source types. Support for list attachments and lookup columns is not yet available.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561920","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-563806","title":"Outlook: Emails marked with External to be supported as Rules conditions","desc":"The External tag on an email, set by the ExternalInOutlook feature, will now be usable as a condition in Outlook Inbox Rules. This change also makes available the ability to create or modify these Rules on the new Outlook for Windows, Outlook Web, and Outlook for Mac.","products":["Exchange","Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-21","modified":"2026-07-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=563806","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558859","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Power Automate integration with records management","desc":"Initiate a Power Automate workflow when the item reaches the end of its retention period. For example, execute a complex disposition approval process or move the file to an archive.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-567669","title":"SharePoint: Enterprise store plugins in Copilot in SharePoint","desc":"Copilot in SharePoint now supports plugins from your enterprise store. A plugin can bundle skills, MCP servers, and other capabilities that extend what Copilot can do. Any plugin made available to your organization, whether installed tenant-wide by an admin or added by you, works directly in Copilot in SharePoint, all governed by your M365 admin. For example, your organization can publish a company-wide accessibility plugin once and have it work consistently across all agentic products, including Copilot in SharePoint, so everyone gets the same accessible experience wherever they work.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567669","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567668","title":"SharePoint: Personal Skills in Copilot in SharePoint","desc":"Create your own personal skills in Copilot in SharePoint and use them anywhere you work. Personal skills travel with you across SharePoint sites and OneDrive—so a skill like document generation works everywhere without recreating it per site. You own your skills, saved as a markdown file in your OneDrive.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-14","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567668","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-523201","title":"Microsoft Purview: Purview Information Protection | Classifier Simulation Mode (Health Monitoring)","desc":"Microsoft Purview introduces the Classifier Simulation Mode, the first phase of the broader Classifier Health Monitoring Platform. This capability enables you to test, analyze, and optimize custom classifiers on production data before publishing them, hence offering a reliable means of verifying the effectiveness of classifiers before committing them to live environments. Custom classifiers are powerful tools but can sometimes include inefficient regex patterns or overly broad logic, leading to Noisy classifier due to high matches, False positives and High scanning latency Simulation Mode mitigates these risks by allowing you to validate classifier quality and performance before publishing, helping ensure healthy, performant, and more precise classification outcomes.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523201","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"October CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560595","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Copilot assisted commenting in Glint survey taking","desc":"Viva Glint survey takers will be able to use a streamlined version of Microsoft Copilot in the Glint survey taking experience to help them rewrite their comments, helping survey takers feel more confident about the feedback they’re providing. By increasing perceived security through reducing identifiable writing patterns and minimizing the effort required to refine feedback, this experience can encourage greater participation, longer responses, and more candid comments, which can drive higher engagement and richer insights from surveys.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560595","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-560057","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention: Add control to include or exclude Default file paths exclusions for Windows","desc":"Previously customers would have system files either included or excluded manually configured. With this feature there is now a capability to provide this by default and have the option of including or excluding those paths. This list is managed by Microsoft to ensure accuracy and ease of management.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-29","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560057","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1185445","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Purview Information Protection | Classifier Simulation Mode (Health Monitoring)","desc":"Updated July 14, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nMicrosoft Purview is introducing Classifier Simulation Mode, the first phase of the broader Classifier Health Monitoring Platform. This new capability allows admins to test and validate custom classifiers on production data before publishing. Simulation Mode enables admins to optimize classifier logic before deployment, helping in reducing false positives, scanning latency, and noisy matches. Admins will access simulation controls and classifier health insights directly in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal, making it easier to monitor and improve classifier performance in one centralized location.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 523201.\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: Rollout begins mid-October 2026 (previously late June), completes by early November 2026 (previously end of July).\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins late November 2026 (previously end of July), completes late November 2026 (previously end of August).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\n• Who is affected: Admins managing Microsoft Purview Information Protection and custom sensitive information types (SITs).\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• By default, the feature will be available to all tenants.\n• Admins will see a new option to simulate a custom classifier before publishing.\n• Simulation is optional — admins can choose to simulate or publish directly.\n• Classifiers published without simulation will still be monitored for performance and flagged if unhealthy.\n\n• Classifier health insights will be available in the Microsoft Purview compliance portal, helping admins identify and remediate inefficient classifiers.\n• Inefficient classifiers may be automatically disabled to maintain system performance.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Admins can begin using Simulation Mode once available; no onboarding or training is required.\n• Once the feature is available:• Review classifier health insights in the compliance portal.\n• Monitor any SITs flagged as unhealthy and adjust logic as needed.\n• Consider simulating classifiers before publishing to reduce risk of false positives or performance issues.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nQuestionExplanation\n\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?Classifiers will be simulated on production data, but not published, allowing analysis without altering data classification outcomes.\n\nDoes the change introduce or significantly modify AI/ML or agent capabilities that interact with or provide access to customer data?Introduces classifier health monitoring logic that evaluates classifier performance and flags inefficiencies.\n\nDoes the change modify how admins can monitor, report on, or demonstrate compliance activities?Adds new health insights and monitoring capabilities for custom classifiers in the compliance portal.\n\nDoes the change include an admin control and, can it be controlled through Entra ID group membership?Simulation and publishing options are available to admins; access can be managed via role-based permissions.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1185445","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561489","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing OCR support","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data Security Investigations (DSI) is extending our investigations by adding optical character recognition (OCR), extracting text from images and incorporating it into investigation data. This enables AI-powered deep content analysis to uncover data security risks that are often hidden within visual content.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-04","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561489","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560547","title":"Microsoft Teams: Report external users for security concerns in Teams","desc":"Users can now report suspicious external users directly within Teams, alongside existing block actions. Reports are surfaced in the Teams admin center, giving admins visibility into potentially risky interactions and enabling them to investigate and take appropriate actions. This enhancement helps organizations respond faster to phishing, impersonation, and other external threats while leveraging end-user signals as an additional layer of protection.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560547","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560398","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Add support of hyperlinks in warn & block toast messages for Edge browser","desc":"With this feature, data officers can now complete their coverage story by now embedding hyperlinks within toast messages for the Edge browser. When this rule is triggered, the end user will see a toast with a customized title and message with a hyperlink. This feature is useful when organizations need to direct users to a specific resource or a repository for more specific instruction (e.g. internal policy SharePoint site).","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560398","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558935","title":"Microsoft Viva: New Post Creation Experience in Viva Enage","desc":"In Viva Engage, we've simplified how to create posts. The new post creation experience makes it easier and faster to share in Viva Engage with a cleaner, more intuitive publishing experience. It brings clearer layout, better accessibility, and smarter organization of tools—so you can focus on creating great posts without extra clicks or clutter.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558935","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-553218","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Content Explorer – Enhanced Tag (SIT, Labels) Filter at UI Layer","desc":"Introduces enhanced controls in Content Explorer’s UI, enabling scoped visibility and filtering of SIT and label data. This will help with content discoverability and governance.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-07-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553218","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-526796","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection- New Summary Metrics in Content Explorer for Unscanned Files and Classification History Details","desc":"Enhance Content Explorer by introducing new summary metrics that provide better visibility into scanning and classification activities. This update will include: 1. Unscanned Files Summary Displays the count and percentage of files that have not been scanned for classification, helping admins identify gaps and take corrective action. 2. Classification History Insights Shows trends and details of classification changes over time, helping admins to discover the stale data in their organization","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526796","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-545063","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management- Insider risk management for agents","desc":"As AI agents become deeply embedded in enterprise ecosystems, they are evolving beyond simple tools or workflows into a digital workforce. These agents can interpret intent, access and manipulate enterprise data, execute actions and even make real-time decisions. In many ways, they operate like human insiders only with machine-speed data processing capabilities. To govern and protect these agents effectively, Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management is being expanded to agents, with specific indicators and insider risk score built for agents based on agentic activities. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545063","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-512428","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot connectors are available for U.S. Department of Defense environment","desc":"Copilot connectors enable organizations to integrate content from other external data sources into Microsoft Graph, improving Copilot’s intelligence, contextual responses, and content discoverability","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=512428","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-381750","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention for endpoints - Optical character recognition (OCR) support for embedded images in endpoint","desc":"This release will extend OCR support from standalone images (JPEG, JPG, PNG, BMP, TIFF, and PDF) to images embedded inside the following files and file types: Office files (XLSX, DOCX, PPTX), container files (zip, rar, 7z, and more), and PDF files. Image-only PDF files are already supported, and this this release will support hybrid PDF files containing images and searchable text. Updated May 20, 2026: We have paused rollout and will resume soon. Thank you for your patience.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-02-28","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=381750","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560325","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – notification and improved search capabilities","desc":"We're introducing notification capabilities and search improvements to Microsoft Purview Data Security Investigations. Investigators will receive notifications when key investigation events occur, such as when AI jobs complete or when new data is added to scope. Search improvements include enhanced query building to more easily identify potentially impacted data","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560325","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561492","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery – Enhancement of Loop and Copilot Pages in Review and Export","desc":"Improves eDiscovery workflows for Loop and Copilot pages by enabling full indexing of page content for keyword search within review sets and adding HTML format support for export from search.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561492","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-516032","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-Insider risk management for agents","desc":"As AI agents become deeply embedded in enterprise ecosystems, they are evolving beyond simple tools or workflows into a digital workforce. These agents can interpret intent, access and manipulate enterprise data, execute actions and even make real-time decisions. In many ways, they operate like human insiders only with machine-speed data processing capabilities. To govern and protect these agents effectively, Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management is being expanded to agents, with specific indicators and insider risk score built for agents based on agentic activities. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. Updated January 30: This feature is still in development with a planned release of April 2026. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516032","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-566302","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Insights in Cowork and WorkIQ spend and usage","desc":"Insights into AI spend (Copilot credit usage) at a group or team level will be available in Viva Insights as a dashboard and in Advanced insights. The services in scope of this release are Cowork and Work IQ API. The dashboard experience is available to managers with at least 5 direct reports (scoped access), the Insights analysts, and Global administrators and is enabled by default to ensure immediate access to usage-based cost insights. For users to be able to use Cowork or WorkIQ API, your tenant must have usage-based billing setup via Cost Management in the Microsoft 365 admin center. Leader access to tenant-wide data is out of scope for this release. The same insights will be available for Insights Analysts and Global Administrators in Advanced Insights.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-06-19","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566302","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-545013","title":"SharePoint: Microsoft 365 Archive in GCC-L","desc":"Microsoft 365 Archive is designed to help organizations manage their inactive data efficiently. It allows you to move inactive SharePoint sites into a cold storage tier, which reduces storage costs while maintaining the same searchability, security, and compliance standards as active data. This feature is already available in Production and is now being released to GCC-L cloud.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-22","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545013","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-503563","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Organizational Messages now supports Action Segments","desc":"Action Segments empowers IT Admins to target Organizational Messages using dynamic, pre-defined usage segments. This behavior-based targeting approach goes beyond existing static group definitions, ensuring messages reach the most relevant users.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503563","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-515144","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Engage private content in M365 Copilot","desc":"Engage content from private communities and events will be used as grounding source for M365 Copilot. When a user queries in M365 Copilot, they will only be able to see content they are privileged to access.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515144","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-553136","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Surveys Agent and Copilot Chat in Microsoft Forms","desc":"Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat is now integrated in Microsoft Forms, including enabling the Surveys Agent from within Forms. Surveys Agent provides specialized capabilities to help with your form - from recommending and applying improvements to your form or quiz, to helping draft and send invitations, to analyzing your results. Surveys Agent is available to users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, and can be accessed by clicking the \"Copilot\" icon in Forms.","products":["Forms","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553136","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-503587","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Admins can manage access more precisely with support for nested permissions in Jira, Confluence, and ServiceNow","desc":"Support for hierarchical ACLs for SNOW, Confluence, Jira connectors.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503587","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557983","title":"SharePoint: Updates to SharePoint home sites","desc":"SharePoint home sites are getting the following new updates - A resources web part, a new UX to customize the SharePoint app (Viva Connections) experience for Teams desktop and mobile and ability to set up a new home site in the SharePoint admin center. Additionally, the Announcements web part and a new layout for News web part will be available in all sites.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557983","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-496371","title":"Outlook: add attachments while offline in the new Outlook for Windows","desc":"We are adding more functionality to offline mode in the new Outlook for Windows. You will now be able to add attachments while drafting your email without an internet connection. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-07-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496371","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-566999","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Enable express mode for flows invoked by an agent or app","desc":"Express mode ensures agents and apps receive timely and reliable responses by dramatically accelerating flow run times. This reduces flow failures, improves user experience, and eliminates costly interruptions caused by timeout issues. Organizations benefit from more dependable automations, higher adoption, and smoother operational workflows.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-10","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566999","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-494809","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Frontier and Microsoft agent user request approval flow in Microsoft 365 admin center","desc":"For Admins, agents in the Frontier program can be managed through the Microsoft 365 Admin Center. They are listed under the agents & connectors tab in Copilot Control System, where you can view all agent inventory for your organization. Agents built by Microsoft and available in the Frontier program will be displayed in the Agent Store. This feature will support users to request these agents if blocked by organizational policies. Admins will have the opportunity to further approve and reject these user request. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-05","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494809","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-486840","title":"Outlook: Import calendars and contacts from PST file to mailbox in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to import calendars and contacts from .pst file to mailbox. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486840","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-486839","title":"Outlook: Import calendars and contacts from PST file to mailbox in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to import calendars and contacts from .pst file to mailbox. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-25","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-485740","title":"Outlook: Import emails from PST file to mailbox in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to import emails from .pst file to mailbox. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-18","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485740","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-485756","title":"Outlook: Read-only access to contacts within a PST file in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to browse and read contacts within a .pst file. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-18","modified":"2026-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485756","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-567472","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - DS Triage Agent for IRM available in Defender","desc":"We’re introducing support for Insider Risk Management (IRM) alert agent summaries within Microsoft Defender, enabling investigators to access key triage insights directly in the Defender alert queue. When the IRM Triage Agent is active, IRM alerts surfaced in Microsoft Defender will now include the agent summary—such as agent categorization, investigation summary, identified risk patterns, and relevant user details—helping analysts quickly assess alert severity without leaving their existing Defender workflows. For deeper analysis, investigators can access the full IRM investigation experience within the Microsoft Purview portal. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567472","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567009","title":"SharePoint: Create new workflows with Copilot in SharePoint","desc":"Describe a workflow intent such as \"when files are set to status = Complete, post a message in my Teams chat\" and Copilot in SharePoint will assemble the necessary triggers, conditions, and actions to setup your workflow. You can come back to Copilot in SharePoint at any time to make changes or click \"Workflows\" from the command bar to see your live workflow.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567009","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-505441","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Improved content freshness using Copilot connectors with webhooks-led notifications","desc":"Copilot connectors will offer improved content freshness with more frequent sync of updates using webhook event notifications. The following connectors are in scope - Azure DevOps, Jira cloud, Confluence cloud, Trello, Asana, Bitbucket, GitHub and Gitlab.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505441","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-566704","title":"Microsoft 365 app: New Copilot Notebooks design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot App (Android)","desc":"Copilot Notebooks in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app (Android) now lets users organize related chats, output creations, and references into a persistent AI workspace. Copilot uses the Notebook's accumulated context to ground responses, so work continues across sessions instead of starting over each time.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566704","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-566696","title":"Thumbnail view for PDFs is available in OneDrive and SharePoint on the web","desc":"We are improving PDF navigation in OneDrive and SharePoint on the web by adding a thumbnail view in the PDF viewer. Users will be able to open a thumbnail panel to visually browse pages in a PDF and jump directly to a selected page. This update helps users navigate long PDFs more quickly, especially when they need to find a visual section, page layout, chart, image, or form page without scrolling page by page.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-09","modified":"2026-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566696","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-499895","title":"Viva Engage: My Team audiences and flexible targeting for leader communications","desc":"We’re introducing more flexible and precise targeting capabilities in Viva Engage, starting with Storyline Announcements. This new feature allows leaders and their delegates to define a custom audience at the time of posting, without relying on pre-configured Leader Audiences. Audiences can be built, and saved for reuse, using organizational attributes such as department, job title, or country, existing groups like M365 Groups, distribution lists, or security groups, and even individual users by name. This flexibility enables more relevant communication, helping leaders reach the right people with the right message. Notifications and delivery channels, including Teams and email, will continue to follow existing Storyline Announcement behavior, ensuring a seamless experience for recipients. This feature is designed to help leaders tailor communications to specific departments, locations, or groups, enhancing engagement and relevance across the organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499895","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-464990","title":"Microsoft 365: Create full-workload backup policies for Microsoft 365 Backup","desc":"Automatically backup all Exchange or OneDrive users and/or SharePoint sites in the tenant and have the tool automatically add new users/sites to the backup policy.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-29","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=464990","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567004","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Link meetings to CRM records automatically with AI","desc":"This feature saves you time by automatically connecting your meetings to the correct CRM records. You have the right deal insights at your fingertips when preparing for customer conversations, so you can focus less on updating records and more on selling with confidence and context.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567004","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567001","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Engage customers across multiple channels (web, voice, SMS & email)","desc":"A multi‑channel outreach capability, spanning web chat, voice, SMS, and email, is critical for meeting customers in the channel they naturally prefer and increasing the likelihood of timely engagement. By activating the agent across multiple surfaces, we ensure continuity of conversations, reduce drop‑off when a single channel fails, and support the FY27 goal of always‑on, end‑to‑end engagement from initial intent to close. This creates higher response rates, faster qualification, and a more seamless handoff to sales motions.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-08","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567001","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1183013","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Viva Engage: Flexible targeting of Storyline Announcements","desc":"Updated July 8, 2026: We have updated the content and timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nWe’re introducing My Team audiences and expanded targeting capabilities in Viva Engage to help leaders communicate with the employees in their organization and tailor messages to relevant teams, departments, locations, or groups. My Team provides a ready-to-use, automatically maintained audience based on the organizational hierarchy, so leaders can reach the employees who report up to them, including both direct and indirect reports. This audience helps unlock and improve leadership experiences across Viva Engage, making Storyline Announcements, audience analytics, Leadership Corner, and feed and digest distribution more relevant with less setup.\nLeaders and delegates can use My Team as-is, review its membership, or further customize and save it as a reusable audience across leader communication experiences. For Storyline Announcements, they can also define recipients at the time of publish, choosing My Team, a saved audience, or a custom audience built using organizational attributes such as department, job title, or country; existing groups like M365 Groups, distribution lists, or security groups; and individual users by name. Together, My Team and flexible targeting make leader communications more relevant, scalable, and easier to manage - with a dynamic default audience and precise targeting for relevant employee groups.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 499895.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview (Worldwide): Begins mid-November 2025 and completes by mid-March 2026 (previously early February).\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Begins early November 2026 (previously late-July) and completes by late November 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected: Leaders and delegates using Viva Engage Storyline Announcements in tenants enrolled in public preview.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• This capability is being introduced as part of the public preview for Viva Engage. During this phase, leaders and their delegates can actively experiment with flexible audience targeting for Storyline Announcements—defining a custom audience at the time of posting, rather than relying solely on pre‑configured Leader Audiences.\n• Audiences can include organizational attributes (such as reporting structure, country, department, job title), existing groups (Microsoft 365 Groups, DLs, SGs), or individual users.\n• Notifications and delivery channels (Teams, email, Viva Engage Inbox) remain unchanged for recipients.\n• No dependency on IT or advance audience setup—leaders can act immediately when communication needs arise.\n• Available only in public preview; functionality and targeting options may evolve before general availability.\n• Admins should ensure organizational attributes in Entra ID or Organizational Data in Microsoft are accurate to support successful targeting.\n• Available platforms: Desktop and web.\n• Licensing requirements: This feature requires a premium license available through Viva or Communications and Communities (C&C). Availability may vary depending on your organization's Microsoft 365 licensing agreement.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\nNo admin action is required for rollout. To prepare, you may want to:\n\n• Validate organizational attributes (reporting structure, country, department, role, job title) in Microsoft Entra ID or Organizational Data in Microsoft.\n\n• Confirm leader and delegate assignments to ensure the right people can use Storyline Announcements and the new targeting control.\n\nLearn more:\n• Use your organizational data in Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Viva | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1183013","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-503780","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention-Endpoint DLP support classification of Azure RMS protected Office documents","desc":"Endpoint DLP can now classify Office files stored in Windows devices that have Azure RMS protection applied. Classification will be triggered when file is used in applications or when just-in-time classification is enabled.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-22","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503780","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-499428","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Agent Mode in Word for Enhanced document editing","desc":"Copilot supports document editing in Word through chat-based interactions with Agent Mode. Users can initiate edits, share clarifying directions, and review a summary of changes within the document.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-01","modified":"2026-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499428","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-566859","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Use SharePoint lists as a knowledge source","desc":"Unlock the full value of your structured data by bringing SharePoint lists directly into your Microsoft Copilot Studio agents. With native support, customers can ground AI responses in up-to-date, business-critical data—such as tasks, inventory, customers, or operations—without manual data movement or complex integrations. This enables more accurate, context-aware copilots that reflect how your business runs, helping teams make faster decisions, reduce errors, and automate workflows with confidence.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-567318","title":"Outlook: Reply with a Template in Rules","desc":"You can now create a rule that automatically replies to incoming messages with a template you've set up. Set the conditions you care about and pick the template, and Outlook handles the response for you. It's a simple way to send consistent replies without typing the same thing over and over. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-07","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567318","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"mc-MC1293480","title":"(Updated) Exchange Online: Retirement of legacy TLS versions for POP and IMAP connections","desc":"Updated July 7, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are retiring support for legacy Transport Layer Security (TLS) versions for POP3 and IMAP4 connections to Exchange Online. This change improves security and aligns with current industry standards. TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1 are no longer considered secure. Most modern email clients already use TLS 1.2 or later.\n[When this will happen]\n• Rollout start: August 1, 2026\n• Rollout end: December 31, 2026\n\nThe rollout will occur gradually worldwide.\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\n• Microsoft 365 tenants using POP3 or IMAP4 with Exchange Online\n• Admins managing email clients, applications, or devices that use POP or IMAP\n\nWhat will happen\n• POP3 and IMAP4 connections will require TLS 1.2 or later.\n• Connections using TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1 will fail.\n• Modern email clients are not expected to be affected.\n• Legacy applications or devices may stop connecting.\n• Custom or embedded systems may require updates.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n• If you use POP or IMAP with Exchange Online, ensure email clients, applications, and libraries support TLS 1.2 or later and do not use legacy TLS endpoints.\n• Review all POP and IMAP clients in your organization.\n• Confirm support for TLS 1.2 or later.\n• Update or replace clients that rely on legacy TLS.\n• Validate TLS support with third‑party vendors.\n• Inform helpdesk and operations teams.\n\nNo action is required if all connections already use TLS 1.2 or later.\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1293480","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-561551","title":"Microsoft Edge: Intune MAM Protected Downloads","desc":"The protected downloads feature for Intune MAM will now save downloaded files to the Documents > Microsoft Edge > Downloads folder in OneDrive.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561551","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"mc-MC1217640","title":"Microsoft Purview | Information Protection - Content Explorer: Unscanned data and Classification History summary metrics","desc":"Updated July 7, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe’re enhancing Microsoft Purview Content Explorer with new summary metrics to improve visibility into scanning and classification activities. These updates will help admins identify unscanned files and monitor classification trends, enabling better data governance and informed decisions.\nThis message is associated with Roadmap ID 526796.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out late July 2026 (previously mid-July) and expect to complete by early October 2026 (previously early August).\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out early November 2026 (previously mid-August) and expect to complete by late November 2026 (previously late August).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\n• Who is affected: Admins managing Microsoft Purview Information Protection and using Content Explorer.\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• A new Unscanned Files Summary will display the count and percentage of files not scanned for classification.\n\n• Classification History Insights will show trends and details of classification changes over time.\n\n• These metrics will appear in Content Explorer alongside existing Sensitive Information Types (SITs) and labels.\n• Admins can explore the new metrics to identify gaps and use on-demand classification capabilities to retrigger scans if needed.\n\n• No changes to existing policies or configurations; the feature is enabled by default.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required.\n• These metrics will automatically appear in Content Explorer.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nQuestion\nExplanation\n\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed (e.g., documents, emails, chats, etc.)?\nThe feature accesses existing classification metadata to display trends and scanning status in Content Explorer.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-14","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1217640","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560399","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Microsoft Fabric, Cloud storage, cloud service activities as triggers","desc":"With this update, the indicators belonging to cloud storage apps (Box, Dropbox, Google Drive), cloud services (Azure, Amazon Web Services) and Microsoft Fabric (Power BI, Lakehouse) will be supported as triggers in Data leaks policy. With triggers, customers can define the conditions for bringing the user into the scope of a policy while the respective indicators are used to determine risk score. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-15","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560399","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-486695","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Prompt Gallery - Company-wide prompt publishing","desc":"Organizations can build their own collections of prompts that are tailored to their business needs and workflows and distribute these to all users within the tenant.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneNote","PowerPoint","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-24","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486695","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558686","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Sensitivity label inheritance for Teams meeting artifacts","desc":"Teams meeting artifacts, including recordings, transcripts, and Loop notes, can now be configured to automatically inherit the sensitivity label from the meeting. This ensures content generated during meetings is consistently protected without requiring manual labeling, reducing risk and simplifying protection at scale.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-16","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558686","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558685","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Exclude modern groups / include dynamic security groups support for sensitivity label policies","desc":"To provide more flexibility, admins can now exclude modern Microsoft 365 groups and scope sensitivity label policies to dynamic and non-mail enabled security groups—expanding policy targeting beyond individual users and mail enabled groups.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-16","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558685","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558684","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Sensitivity label support in Engage","desc":"Organizations can now manually apply Purview Information Protection sensitivity labels in Engage. Allowing admins to create labels and configure label publishing policies to determine which users and groups can manually label content in Engage communities. End users in Engage will be able to then manually apply labels to communities and in turn classify and protect their sensitive data via privacy and external user access controls.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-18","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558684","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558108","title":"Microsoft Teams: Catch up on conversations in Microsoft Teams mobile","desc":"Catch up in Teams mobile provides a unified view of all directed and followed conversations across chats, meeting chats, channels and threads. The mobile-optimized card view supports swipe actions, helping you quickly review and triage lists of important items.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558108","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558687","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Policy sync status for M365 Label publishing policies","desc":"Admins can now see the sync status of sensitivity label publishing policies directly in the Purview portal. This provides clear confirmation that label policy changes have been fully applied across Microsoft 365 workloads, reducing guesswork, speeding troubleshooting, and increasing confidence during large scale label deployments.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-16","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558687","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557975","title":"Microsoft Teams: One-time email passcodes for external presenters in Teams events","desc":"One-time email passcodes provide an easy way for tenant administrators and event organizers to verify anonymous, external presenters invited to their events. Anonymous external presenters will be shown with a \"Verified\" tag once completing the process. Based on admin settings, the event organizer will also have a set of options available to them that applies to all external presenters, providing the ability to control who is admitted to the meeting or allowing uninvited users with the link to be admitted from the lobby.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-07-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557975","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-566617","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Endpoint DLP now detects sensitivity labels on files inside archives","desc":"Endpoint Data Loss Prevention (DLP) is changing the way archive files, such as .zip and similar container formats, are classified and enforced. This update improves detection accuracy and gives administrators finer control over how content within archives is protected.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-25","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566617","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-502532","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] [Search UX] Enable customization of icon & name for data sources in Search (& chat)","desc":"Enable customization of icon & name for data sources in Search (& chat).","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-22","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502532","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-567316","title":"Outlook: Notification when not responding to most recent message of email thread","desc":"When replying to an email conversation and the message being replied to is not the latest in the conversation, Outlook for Windows and web will now display a notification indicating this. With this change, users can now be more confident that they are responding to the right message in an email conversation. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-06","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567316","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"mc-MC1218713","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Organization evaluation score for apps and agents","desc":"Updated July 6, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nToday, admins must manually review trust and compliance information for Teams apps and agents to determine whether they meet their organization’s security, privacy, and compliance requirements. To make this process more scalable and consistent, Teams will introduce a centralized evaluation experience. Admins will define their organization’s trust requirements once, and the system will generate a score and detailed evaluation report for each app and agent based on those requirements. This will help organizations make faster, more consistent approval decisions.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 532720.\n\n[When this will happen]\n\nTargeted release/Preview: We will begin rollout in late February 2026 and expect to complete by the end of March 2026.\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide and GCC): We will begin rollout in late September 2026 (previously early July) and expect to complete by early October 2026 (previously end of July).\n\n[How this will affect your organization]\n\nWho is affected: Admins who manage apps and agents in the Teams admin center.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• A new evaluation score settings tab will appear in Teams admin center > Teams apps.\n\n• Admins will be able to configure approval requirements—such as GDPR compliance, SOC 2 certification, and data residency—one time for their organization.\n\n• The system will automatically calculate an evaluation score for each app and agent based on how many requirements are met.\n\n• A new evaluation score column will appear in Teams admin center > Teams apps > Manage apps, with options to sort and filter by score.\n\n• A detailed evaluation report will be available on the App details page, providing requirement-by-requirement detail.\n\n• This feature will not change app enablement or blocking behavior and will not modify any underlying metadata.\n• The feature will be enabled by default and will not require admin action to activate.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n\nNo action is required. This feature will be available automatically in the Teams admin center.\nAdmins may choose to review their approval workflows once the feature becomes available.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1218713","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-564610","title":"Outlook: Variable number of message preview lines","desc":"Outlook for Windows and Outlook for Web will now allow users to modify how the preview text for emails show in the message list. The preview text can now take up 2 lines, 1 whole line, or 0 additional lines.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564610","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-557184","title":"Microsoft Teams: Context preservation in Teams","desc":"When you return to a conversation within a short duration of time, your selected tab, opened side panel, and layout are restored automatically, so you can keep working without resetting your workspace. In addition, returning to a Quick View within a short duration will restore your previously selected message.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557184","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557982","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Custom confidentiality statements","desc":"This feature enables Company Admins to customize the default Microsoft Viva Glint confidentiality statement. Admins can choose to turn off the default statement and instead define confidentiality messaging tailored to their specific program settings, such as whether responses are configured to be confidential.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557982","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-518287","title":"Outlook: LDAP directory support for S/MIME in New Outlook","desc":"The new Outlook now supports LDAP (Lightweight Directory Access Protocol) directories for sending S/MIME encrypted emails. This allows users to add an LDAP directory in the new Outlook and use it to fetch recipients’ certificates from the configured directory when sending S/MIME encrypted messages. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-27","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-518288","title":"Outlook: Support for Storing S/MIME Certificates in Contacts in New Outlook","desc":"The new Outlook will now allow users to store S/MIME encryption certificates within their Contacts. This enables users to save certificates directly in contact entries and use them to send S/MIME encrypted emails to the contacts. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518288","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-421612","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Microsoft Loop - Departed user content workflows for user-owned Loop workspaces","desc":"Manage retention and deletion workflows for user-owned Loop workspaces like Copilot Pages when users leave the organization. Notify and provide temporary access to other employees or administrators to save important data before deletion policies take effect.","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-10-30","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=421612","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-536571","title":"Microsoft Teams: User reported security signals in Teams admin center","desc":"This update brings end user security reporting into Teams Admin Center. Admins can now view and download signals from messages users report as a security concern or not a security concern within TAC Protection reports, helping them identify trends and fine tune policies and responses.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-17","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536571","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-548640","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Survey Designer Role","desc":"To empower organizations to run additional employee listening programs, like AI transformation or change management cases, we are creating a dedicated Survey Designer role. This role grants a user just enough permissions to run a Viva Glint survey without full access to platform settings and sensitive data, thus creating a more democratized platform.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548640","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-547837","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - New Permissions","desc":"Adding new, more granular permissions for Viva Glint administration. These areas include Advanced Configuration, Nudges, General Settings, and Viva Integrations. Updating the name of the highest privileged role in Viva Glint to “Viva Glint Service Admin”, and for increased security, restricting the ability to assign new Viva Glint Service Admins to the MAC only.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-14","modified":"2026-07-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547837","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-567006","title":"Outlook: Improvements to Save Contacts on iPhone and iPad","desc":"Outlook contacts become available system-wide (caller ID, Phone, Messages, Siri) using Apple's Contact Provider framework — without full address-book access or copying contacts onto your device.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-02","modified":"2026-07-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=567006","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-566997","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Block the use of maker-provided credentials for authentication","desc":"By blocking the use of maker's credentials by AI agents, admins can increase the security and compliance of agents in their organizations: - Prevent unauthorized access to sensitive systems or data that the maker's credentials might have access to. - Help organizations comply with data protection regulations (such as GDPR or HIPAA) by ensuring only authorized identities are used for data access. - Enable IT and security teams to enforce organizational policies around identity and access management. - Increase trust among stakeholders and IT departments, making it easier to adopt AI agents at scale.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-02","modified":"2026-07-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566997","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-502529","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] [AdminX] Pre-setup guides, editability, actionable errors & alerting support available for Connector admins","desc":"Pre-setup guides, editability, actionable errors & alerting support available for Connector admins.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-07-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502529","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560598","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing new custom examination","desc":"Data Security Investigations (DSI) is introducing the ability to create custom examination focus areas. This feature will empower admins to tailor examination to their specific needs depending on the type of investigation being performed and the information they are most concerned with. This addition works alongside DSI’s AI-powered content analysis features, such as categorization, AI search, and examination for risk, which help surface data security risks buried in data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-07-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560598","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-508518","title":"Microsoft Viva: Organizational Data in Microsoft 365 is now available in GCC-Moderate","desc":"We’re excited to announce that Organizational Data in Microsoft 365 is now available in the GCC-Moderate (GCC-M) environment! Organizational Data in Microsoft 365 provides a secure, compliant, and scalable platform for ingesting organizational data into Microsoft 365. With this release, government cloud customers can now leverage the same powerful data ingestion capabilities previously available only in commercial environments.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-07-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508518","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-566867","title":"Planner: Local Custom Fields/Columns","desc":"Custom Fields let you tailor your plans to match the way your team works. Add Text, Number, Date, Yes/No, and Choice fields to capture the information that matters most. View and update custom fields across Board, Grid, and Task details, with support for sorting, filtering, grouping, and bulk editing to keep your work organized and easy to manage.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566867","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-566873","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Enforce safe sharing by detecting credential oversharing","desc":"This feature helps organizations reduce security risk by preventing agents and flows from being shared when they rely on unsafe identities, such as maker credentials. By detecting identity oversharing early and enforcing safe‑sharing policies at publish and share time, customers can avoid identity leakage, privilege escalation, and unintended access - while still allowing makers to build and iterate safely within approved guardrails.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566873","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566998","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Invoke agents as workflow steps with the agent node","desc":"The agent node lets you embed reasoning directly into your workflow. This means fewer manual handoffs, faster processing times, and workflows that can handle nuanced decisions without additional development effort, helping teams automate more of their end-to-end processes and reduce operational overhead.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566998","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-505442","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Improved content freshness using Copilot connectors with webhooks-led notifications","desc":"Copilot connectors will offer improved content freshness with more frequent sync of updates using webhook event notifications. The following connectors are in scope - Azure DevOps, Jira cloud, Confluence cloud, Trello, Asana, Bitbucket, GitHub and Gitlab.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505442","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566869","title":"Microsoft Entra: Upcoming changes to federatedTokenValidationPolicy default settings","desc":"The federatedTokenValidationPolicy is a resource type in Microsoft Graph (beta) that governs the validation of federated authentication tokens and allows customers to configure a rule to block logins where internalDomainFederation does not match UPN domain. The feature by default requires manual configuration in the tenant to prohibit cross-domain logins. To strengthen security with cross-domain sign-in we will change the default rule for federatedTokenValidationPolicy to block logins where internalDomainFederation does not match UPN domain. This internalDomainFederation object is typically created automatically during federation setup with AD federation server or other IdPs.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-07-01","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566869","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565424","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improved request flows for apps and agents blocked by admins","desc":"We are improving how users request access to apps and agents blocked by admins in Teams by introducing a clear, guided, and end-to-end request experience. This work reduces end-user friction by driving clarity into the request process and notifying users when there's been an update to their request. In addition to enhancements in Teams, we've also improved the admin experience in Teams Admin Center, to simplify the process for admins to review requests and take action. Additionally, we're introducing a new capability to increase admin awareness of new requests, ensuring that user requests don't get stalled.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-06-10","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565424","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-554927","title":"Microsoft Teams: Recently used emojis sync across devices","desc":"Recently used emojis and reactions sync across Teams on desktop and mobile, making it easier to express yourself wherever you work.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554927","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-559387","title":"Microsoft Teams: Add Breakout Room Participants in Bulk Using CSV","desc":"Support for bulk breakout room participant assignment using a CSV file, helping organizers save time when setting up breakout rooms.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-07-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559387","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-561921","title":"Universal Print: Badge API","desc":"Admins can map employee badge credentials (card or NFC) to user identities in Universal Print, enabling users to release secure print jobs at compatible printers with a simple tap—no app, PIN, or sign-in required at the device. This enhances existing badge-based release with a standardized, cloud-based identity mapping model integrated with Microsoft 365.","products":["Universal Print"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-06-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561921","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"March CY2027"},{"id":"rm-554931","title":"Microsoft Teams: Microsoft Teams: Secure Reliable Transport (SRT) Support for Teams town halls","desc":"Microsoft Teams will soon support Secure Reliable Transport (SRT) streaming in Teams town halls. SRT is a network protocol designed to deliver high-quality, low-latency video across the public internet.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554931","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-516040","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Web Link as a Reference in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Add web links as references in your Copilot Notebooks.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-15","modified":"2026-06-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516040","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"mc-MC1219793","title":"(Updated) Brand impersonation protection for Teams Calling","desc":"Updated May 5, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nBrand Impersonation Protection for Teams Calling adds proactive safeguards against fraudulent or deceptive external callers who attempt to appear as trusted organizations. This helps reduce social-engineering risks and improves tenant security when users receive first-contact external calls. This update aligns with Microsoft’s ongoing investments in caller identity protection and secure collaboration.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 543239.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nTargeted Release: Rollout will begin mid-May 2026 (previously early May) and is expected to complete by late May (previously late April).\n\nGeneral Availability: Timelines will be communicated in a future message.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• All organizations using Microsoft Teams Calling that receive inbound VoIP calls from first-contact external callers.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Teams will evaluate inbound calls for signs of brand impersonation.\n\n• Users will see high-risk call warnings before answering suspicious calls.\n\n• Warnings may continue during the call if risk signals persist.\n\n• Users can accept, block, or end the call.\n\n• The feature will be enabled by default.\n\n• Existing Teams Calling policies remain unchanged.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\nNo admin action is required at this time.\n\n• Inform helpdesk staff that users may begin seeing high-risk call warnings.\n\n• Update internal training materials if applicable.\n\n• Review Microsoft documentation on caller ID security when available.\n\nBefore rollout, we will update this post with new documentation.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-21","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1219793","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-516576","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Planner Agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"Planner agent in Microsoft 365 will help you plan, organize, and manage work more efficiently. We’re starting with core task and plan management features to simplify project tracking and will introduce additional advanced project management capabilities over time. Updated May 21, 2026: We previously launched in Preview and GA is expected in June. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516576","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559020","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work IQ APIs – Remote MCP Server Support","desc":"Supports connecting to remote MCP servers through the Work IQ endpoint, enabling agents to securely invoke external tools and services beyond the local runtime for richer, distributed agent orchestration.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559020","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-562015","title":"Microsoft Teams: Scoped Search for SharePoint app in Teams (Viva Connections)","desc":"With this feature, users accessing search through the Teams search icon while within the SharePoint app in Teams (Viva Connections) will be able to receive search result scoped to SharePoint global search. Hitting enter on the search query will then open the SharePoint search page.","products":["Microsoft Teams","SharePoint"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-12","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562015","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560532","title":"Planner: Planner Agent chat","desc":"Introducing built-in Planner Agent chat with natural language Q&A, smart task discovery, and in-plan task management.","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560532","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555234","title":"Microsoft Teams: Live transcription in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"View and control live transcription during a meeting from a Teams Rooms on Android device. The real-time transcript includes speaker names and timestamps. You can adjust settings such as spoken language, translated language, and whether both original and translated transcripts are displayed side by side on the front of room display. This feature is available in Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555234","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC High"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-523214","title":"Microsoft Teams: Restart your Town hall event","desc":"Teams town hall producers can now restart a live event while the event is active in order to address technical issues that might arise during the execution of an instance. Whether technical, network, or other issue, this feature enables those managing the event to quickly resolve problems for attendees. This feature is designed to prevent the need for scheduling entirely new events.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-06-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523214","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-566698","title":"SharePoint: Neutral-themed SharePoint UI in Page Editing and Property Panes","desc":"Coming soon for SharePoint: Neutral-themed SharePoint UI will be expanded to page editing and property pane experiences. This update is part of the SharePoint visual refresh and applies our new design language across the SharePoint page editing surfaces, helping create a more consistent, accessible, and modern editing experience.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-26","modified":"2026-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566698","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-559995","title":"Microsoft Viva: Unlocking Deeper Copilot Insights with Enhanced Power BI Filtering","desc":"Enable Global and Insights admins to turn on additional attributes as filters in Power BI reports, including reserved attributes and your organization’s custom attributes. Users who have access to Power BI reports can then use these newly enabled filters to tailor reports to their business needs.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-07","modified":"2026-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559995","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-537271","title":"Microsoft Purview: Azure AI Foundry integration with Microsoft Purview for AI","desc":"Purview enablement in AI Foundry, allows Foundry admins to activate Microsoft Purview on their subscription. Once enabled, AI interaction data from all apps and agents flows into Purview for centralized compliance, governance, and posture management of AI data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537271","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-559991","title":"Outlook: Account Selector in Outlook Copilot Side Pane","desc":"When users have more than one Copilot-enabled account added to new Outlook, the Copilot side pane in Calendar will include an account dropdown that makes it clear which Copilot-enabled account you’re using and lets you switch accounts without relying on Outlook UI’s account context.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559991","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557556","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – AI analysis enhancements","desc":"Data Security Investigations (DSI) now further enhances its AI analysis tools, including the ability to choose between a standard categorization for potential time and/or cost savings or a more advanced categorization to include AI-generated topics. Additionally, we are making the DSI workflow faster by automatically preparing data for AI analysis as it is being added to the investigation, saving critical investigation time.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557556","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-68688","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Ability to set a retention period for a policy","desc":"<div>Introducing the ability to define how long content captured by a Communication Compliance policy is retained. Microsoft Purview Communication Compliance provides the tools to help organizations detect regulatory compliance violations (e.g. SEC or FINRA), such as sensitive or confidential information, harassing or threatening language, and sharing of adult content. Built with privacy by design, usernames are pseudonymized by default, role-based access controls are built in, investigators are opted in by an admin, and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2020-09-14","modified":"2026-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=68688","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"December CY2026","more":"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/compliance/communication-compliance?view=o365-worldwide"},{"id":"rm-534610","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Azure AI Search honors Purview labels and policies","desc":"Azure AI Search now ingests Microsoft Purview sensitivity labels and enforces corresponding protection policies through built-in indexers (SharePoint, OneLake, Azure Blob, ADLS Gen2). This enables secure, policy-aligned search over enterprise data, enabling agentic RAG scenarios where only authorized documents are returned or sent to LLMs, preventing data oversharing and aligning with enterprise data protection standards.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-25","modified":"2026-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534610","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-420335","title":"Microsoft Edge: Rewrite by Copilot in Edge is being upgraded to include enterprise data protection compliance standards","desc":"Rewrite by Copilot in Edge, which lets users edit typed text for tone, format, and length within an open page in Microsoft Edge, is being updated to include enterprise data protection for commercial customers. Once Rewrite is available, users signed in with a Microsoft Entra ID will have enterprise data protection when using the feature in Microsoft Edge. Updated March 20, 2026: We have paused release of this feature temporarily and will announce new release timelines soon. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-03","modified":"2026-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=420335","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/edge"},{"id":"rm-488800","title":"Microsoft Teams: Workplace check-in via Wi-Fi allows easy coordination in the office","desc":"Workplace Check-in via Wi-Fi acts as an extension of existing capabilities to check in to a building or a reserved desk, providing more flexibility and ease of use to help coordinate with co-workers. When users connect to their organization's Wi-Fi, Teams will soon be able to update their work location to reflect the building they're working from. This feature will be off by default. Tenant admins will decide whether to enable it or not and end-users always have the choice to opt-in or opt-out of sharing this information.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-09","modified":"2026-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-492618","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Copilot Prompt Gallery in Data Security Posture Management","desc":"The Data Security Posture Management (DSPM) Copilot Prompt Gallery is a curated collection of prompts and promptbooks created to help users engage more effectively with the Security Copilot experience in DSPM. It acts as a centralized hub where users can explore, search, and leverage prompts that streamline workflows and improve productivity. Designed to support a range of roles and use cases within Data Security, the Prompt Gallery is a powerful resource that enables users to quickly access relevant prompts, accelerate task completion, and unlock the full potential of the Copilot experience.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-09","modified":"2026-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492618","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-499154","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Unattended Remote Help for Windows - Remote Sign-in","desc":"Remotely access devices over the cloud without requiring end user involvement by signing in with credentials.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-28","modified":"2026-06-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499154","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-558934","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create Word documents from Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Copilot Notebooks allows users to generate Word documents using the content and references gathered in a notebook. Copilot drafts a structured document grounded in the notebook’s context, which can be opened and edited in Word, helping users move from ideas and source material to a ready‑to‑use document with fewer manual steps.","products":["Microsoft 365","OneNote","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-06-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558934","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-518215","title":"Microsoft Teams: Apps in Private Channels for Microsoft Teams","desc":"Bring the apps your team relies on—tabs, bots, and message extensions—directly into Private Channels in Microsoft Teams. This update lets channel owners add apps to a specific private channel, so everyone collaborating there (including invited collaborators from other teams or organizations, subject to admin policy) can work in one place without switching contexts.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-06-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518215","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-566531","title":"OneDrive: Find your group sites faster with the new My Sites tab in OneDrive for iOS","desc":"The new My Sites tab in the OneDrive iOS app gives you one place to find every group-connected SharePoint site you own or belong to. Instead of relying on recent files or search, you can browse a complete list of your sites and jump straight to their default document libraries — right from your iPhone or iPad. It's especially handy when you don't remember a site's name, haven't opened it recently, or were just added as a member of a new site, so you spend less time hunting and more time working with your team's content.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-23","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566531","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-478926","title":"Access: Design Access forms and reports without 22-inch size constraints","desc":"With the removal of the 22-inch limit, your apps can now take full advantage of today’s larger monitors. You can display more data, create flexible layouts, and deliver a better experience on wide and high-resolution screens.","products":["Access"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-03","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=478926","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-547824","title":"Microsoft Teams: Attend Microsoft webinars and structured meetings from Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"You can join a Microsoft webinar and structured meeting from a Teams Room on Android and interact seamlessly during the event. Available for Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-03","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547824","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-553591","title":"Microsoft Teams: Building level insights on the Pro Management portal recommended actions page","desc":"IT gets new building level insights on the recommended actions page in the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal. This feature intelligently identifies buildings with high Teams Rooms utilization to help IT prioritize upgrades of bring your own device (BYOD) meeting spaces and ensure consistent, high-quality user experiences throughout their office buildings. Available with a Teams Rooms Pro or Shared Space license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-24","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553591","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559602","title":"Microsoft Teams: Front-of-Room view control for Webinars & Structured Meetings in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"When a Teams Rooms on Android is invited as a meeting presenter, the front-of-room display defaults to the attendee view. Presenters always have full control from the console, including green room and off-stage management, and can switch the front-of-room display to presenter view without impacting attendees.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559602","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561549","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams room builder in the Pro Management portal","desc":"The Teams room builder is a user-friendly, visually engaging tool to help IT managers design and configure Teams Rooms traditional, signature, and flex meeting spaces. This feature, available in the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal, enables faster design, standards creation, and rollout. With a variety of equipment options and helpful criteria filters, device and license selection and purchase is simplified. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-05","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561549","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-172024","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Adaptive policy scope","desc":"Adaptive policy scopes enable your organization to create scopes that automatically updates which users to include in your policy based on geography, group, or another user attribute. The policy will automatically update to match the criteria defined in the scope instead of you constantly needing to update the static list of users in your policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-09-11","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=172024","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-172016","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Policy insights","desc":"The Communication Compliance homepage will provide two columns that offer a quick overview of policy performance: the first column shows the number of scanned parent items in real time, giving visibility into scanning progress; the second column keeps you informed about parent items that meet policy conditions, ensuring you stay updated on potential issues requiring attention and maintaining control over communication compliance. This item is no longer accurate and is being removed from the roadmap. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-10-25","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=172016","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-98186","title":"Microsoft Purview | Communication Compliance: Support for adaptive policy scopes","desc":"Adaptive policy scopes enable your organization to define user scopes for policies based on criteria such as geography, group, or other Azure Active Directory attributes. With adaptive policy scopes, policies are automatically updated to include users that match defined risk criteria rather than requiring admins to repeatedly update static lists of users to include in the policy scope. Microsoft Purview Communication Compliance provides the tools to help organizations detect regulatory compliance violations (e.g. SEC and FINRA obligations), such as inappropriate sharing of sensitive or confidential information, harassing or threatening language and sharing of adult content. Communication Compliance enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, usernames are pseudonymized by default, role-based access controls are built in, investigators are opted in by an admin, and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2022-09-16","modified":"2026-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=98186","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504,"preview":"January CY2023"},{"id":"rm-551195","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Enhanced M365 Copilot Memory - Copilot is now personalized with work data","desc":"Copilot now uses M365 activity to provide more relevant, contextual responses. Updated settings make it easier to view and manage what Copilot remembers and your personalization preferences.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-27","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551195","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-557256","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Explain slide selection during PowerPoint Live","desc":"This feature enhances the PowerPoint Live meeting experience by using Copilot to let attendees select slide text and get explanations for the content.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-21","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557256","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-552597","title":"Microsoft Edge: Extensions monitoring in the Edge management service","desc":"The Microsoft Edge management service now allows admins to gain visibility into extensions installed across their managed users. From the extensions monitoring page, admins can see which extensions have been installed as well as manage user requests for blocked extensions.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552597","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557185","title":"Microsoft Edge: Validate Edge builds early with enterprise preview","desc":"Enterprise preview provides a simpler way for admins to flight pre-release Edge builds to their users. To reduce friction and bolster usage, users will receive pre-release builds directly inside of their Stable Edge application. Admins can allow users to easily opt-out of the preview experience, using built-in rollback to switch between their pre-release and stable channels with ease. Microsoft 365 admin center users can configure the feature, view their flighting population, and receive personalized recommendations all in one place.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557185","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559992","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-AI app selection for Generative AI apps indicators","desc":"Customers can precisely choose which AI app they should use to detect any of the Generative AI apps indicators. This is applicable to the following indicators: \"Entering risky prompts in Copilot\", \"Receiving sensitive responses from Copilot\", \"Entering risky prompts in enterprise AI apps\", and \"Receiving sensitive responses from enterprise AI apps\". Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559992","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562535","title":"Microsoft Teams: Assign Open Shifts","desc":"Auto Assign Open Shifts is a Microsoft Teams Shifts feature that automatically fills unassigned (open) shifts for you. It lets managers automatically assign open shifts to available employees instead of doing it manually. The system considers factors like employee availability, approved time off, past scheduling patterns, and scheduling rules (e.g., max hours, rest time); and generates a draft schedule that you can review and adjust before publishing.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-19","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562535","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-468888","title":"Microsoft Purview: Apply sensitivity labels with user-defined permissions in Office for the web in Microsoft 365","desc":"Office for the web in Microsoft 365 supports the application of sensitivity labels with user-defined permissions.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Purview","PowerPoint","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-11-19","modified":"2026-06-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=468888","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557981","title":"Microsoft Viva: Insights - New Copilot Metrics Available","desc":"We are bringing a set of new Copilot metrics including actions taken in Microsoft 365 Copilot app, Edge and OneNote, and more key use cases across Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint including suggested reply, translate, coach, clean data and more. This will empower customers to more deeply understand the key Copilot adoption cases in Copilot Dashboard and Advanced Analysis in Viva Insights.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-02","modified":"2026-06-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557981","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559480","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create Excel spreadsheets from Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Copilot Notebooks allows users to generate Excel spreadsheets using the content and references gathered in a notebook. Copilot drafts a structured spreadsheet grounded in the notebook’s context, which can be opened and edited in Excel, helping users move from ideas and source material to a ready‑to‑use spreadsheet with fewer manual steps.","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-06-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559480","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560697","title":"Outlook: Bulk Opening/Closing calendar groups in the left nav","desc":"Users can now bulk select/deselect all calendars within a group on left rail in calendar in #newoutlookforwindows, similar to classic Outlook.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-06-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560697","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560534","title":"Outlook: ICS Preview experience","desc":"Users can now seamlessly import calendar events from ICS files & preview them before importing in three cases: when dragging ICS files directly into the calendar surface, uploading an ICS file ('Add calendar' flow) ICS file via email #newoutlookforwindows.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-06-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560534","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558857","title":"Outlook: Multiselect in the New Outlook and Teams calendars","desc":"You can now select multiple appointments and meetings in the new Outlook for Windows and Teams calendars. Use Ctrl+click to select individual items, or Shift+click to quickly select a range events. Once selected, you can take common actions across all selected items. Click anywhere outside the selection to clear it. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-06-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-473493","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Introduction of secure workflow to bypass legal holds and retention policies in Exchange","desc":"The first release of Priority cleanup enables admins to create a recurring exception to delete items under a broader retention policy and/or legal hold on Exchange workload. Creating a Priority cleanup will require a separate security role, multiple approvers, and will have a complete audit trail","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-08","modified":"2026-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473493","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-566204","title":"OneDrive: Find document libraries in OneDrive search results","desc":"We’re making it easier for users to find document libraries directly from OneDrive search results. When users search in OneDrive, relevant SharePoint document libraries may appear alongside files and folders, helping users quickly get back to shared team content without needing to navigate across multiple sites.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-18","modified":"2026-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566204","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-561028","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Phone Call Transfer Improvements","desc":"Microsoft Teams is improving the call transfer experience on desktop (Windows and Mac) with a streamlined workflow that makes transferring calls faster and more intuitive. These changes reduce the number of steps to initiate a transfer and introduce transfer suggestions to help users find the right transfer target more quickly.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561028","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558938","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create PowerPoint presentations from Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Copilot Notebooks enables users to generate PowerPoint presentations directly from the content and references collected in a notebook. Using the notebook’s curated context, Copilot creates a structured, editable slide deck that users can open and refine in PowerPoint, helping turn research, notes, and insights into shareable presentations more quickly.","products":["Microsoft 365","OneNote","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558938","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559418","title":"Outlook: Copilot provides coaching feedback in chat as you draft, edit and format emails","desc":"Copilot now provides coaching feedback on email drafts via chat and can apply suggestions directly to your message in Outlook. Users have the option to choose which suggestions are applied, and Copilot updates your email in place.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559418","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558565","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Inline DLP for Prompts for Microsoft Foundry apps and agents","desc":"With Purview enabled in Microsoft Foundry, Purview admins can setup inline DLP policies to prompts on Foundry built apps and agents to ensure data loss prevention of sensitive data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-02","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558565","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-566202","title":"SharePoint: Inline comments and notifications for Markdown files","desc":"We’re adding inline commenting support for Markdown files in OneDrive and SharePoint, making it easier for teams to review, discuss, and collaborate on Markdown content directly in Microsoft 365. Users will be able to leave comments on specific parts of a Markdown file and receive notifications when they are mentioned or when there is activity that needs their attention.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-17","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566202","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-565862","title":"Outlook: Block External Images Settings Update","desc":"Outlook on the web and the new Outlook for Windows now support will support new settings for loading external images. New settings will allow customers to block all external content, or to load all content by default if the customer admin allows. Existing default behavior will not be changed (load external content only for safe senders).","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-17","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565862","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"mc-MC1304291","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Purview: Data loss prevention inline controls for prompts in Microsoft Foundry apps and agents","desc":"Updated June 17, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nIntroduction\n\nWith Microsoft Purview enabled in Microsoft Foundry, Purview admins can apply inline data loss prevention (DLP) policies to prompts used in Foundry-built apps and agents. This helps prevent sensitive data from being shared through prompts and supports stronger data protection and compliance for AI-driven workflows.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558565.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview: We will begin rolling out in mid-May 2026 and expect to complete by early June 2026.\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout will begin in October 2026 (previously mid-June) and is expected to complete by end of October 2026 (previously late June).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Admins managing Microsoft Purview and Microsoft Foundry\n\n• Organizations building or using apps and agents in Microsoft Foundry\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• When your organization builds AI apps and agents on Microsoft Foundry, Foundry admins can enable Microsoft Purview by configuring the Purview toggle in Foundry, allowing Purview to manage how these apps and agents interact with data.\n• Security admins can ensure the data security and compliance posture of how these apps and agents interact with data by setting up DLP policies for prompts in Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP).\n• Admins can configure Microsoft Purview DLP policies to evaluate prompts submitted to Foundry apps and agents.\n\n• Policies can detect and help prevent the sharing of sensitive information in prompts to large language models (LLMs)..\n\n• DLP enforcement occurs inline as prompts are submitted.\n\n• This feature supports existing Microsoft Purview DLP capabilities and integrates with current compliance workflows.\n\n• No change occurs unless admins create or enable DLP policies for this scenario (admin configuration required).\n• Foundry-based DLP capabilities follow a pay-as-you-go model. Microsoft Purview must be enabled with a pay-as-you-go subscription for this feature to work.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Review your current Microsoft Purview DLP policies and identify scenarios that should apply to AI prompts.\n\n• Create and use DLP policy simulation mode to understand what data is being exchanged with AI apps and agents before enforcing policies.\n• Plan internal guidance for admins and compliance teams on managing prompt-level DLP.\n\n• Update internal documentation to include this capability if you use Microsoft Foundry apps and agents.\n\nLearn more:\n• Manage compliance and security in Microsoft Foundry - Microsoft Foundry | Microsoft Learn\n• Use Microsoft Purview to manage data security & compliance for Microsoft Foundry | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nArea\nExplanation\n\nAlters how existing customer data is processed\nPrompts submitted to Microsoft Foundry apps and agents are evaluated inline against Purview DLP policies to detect sensitive information.\n\nAI/ML interaction with customer data\nIntroduces DLP policy evaluation for prompts within AI apps and agents, adding governance to how AI systems process user-provided data.\n\nEnd-user interaction with generative AI\nUsers continue interacting with Foundry apps and agents, but prompts may now be evaluated or blocked based on DLP policies.\n\nModifies Purview DLP policies or enforcement\nExtends existing Purview DLP enforcement to include inline scanning and enforcement of prompts in Foundry apps and agents.\n\nAlters admin monitoring or reporting\nAdmins may use existing Purview reporting and auditing capabilities to monitor DLP activity for prompts, but no new reporting functionality is specified.\n\nIncludes admin control\nSecurity admins configure and manage DLP policies in Microsoft Purview DLP for this capability.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-08","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1304291","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559800","title":"SharePoint: Extending AI in SharePoint using custom skills","desc":"Skills allow extensibility of the SharePoint AI Agent, enabling customizable solutions that adapt to unique business needs. They address gaps in out-of-the-box functionality for unique business processes and enable reusable multi-step workflows.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-01","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558544","title":"Microsoft Teams: Create workflows with slash commands","desc":"Now you can create workflows quickly and easily using slash commands directly from the Teams compose box.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-11","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558544","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-546245","title":"Windows 365: Windows 365 Link - Customization of the login screen","desc":"IT can set a custom wallpaper, company logo and name on the Windows 365 Link login screen","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-02","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=546245","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-543421","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): PowerPoint Agent","desc":"PowerPoint Agent helps you build polished presentations with strong storytelling and visual structure. It streamlines research, formatting, and layout so you can stay focused on your message. Use multi‑turn chat to refine content or open the deck in PowerPoint for full editing and collaboration. Ideal for executive presentations, strategic updates, and market overviews. Available to Microsoft 365 users with or without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543421","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-554936","title":"Outlook: Copilot Chat available in shared and delegate mailboxes","desc":"Shared mailbox users and delegates with Read and manage (full access), and/or mail folder-level permission will now be able to access Copilot Chat directly from their shared and delegate mailboxes in new Outlook.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-06-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554936","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-475859","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Microsoft Fabric risk indicators in Insider Risk Management","desc":"With this update, Insider Risk Management extends its risk detection capabilities to Microsoft Fabric products by offering ready-to-use risk indicators based on activities that may lead to a data security incident in Power BI. Organizations can use these new indicators in data theft and data leaks policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-17","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=475859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610},{"id":"rm-566203","title":"Outlook: Export support for data files in Mac Outlook","desc":"This feature adds support for exporting PST files into Outlook for Mac.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-16","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=566203","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560599","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Viewing AI interaction messages for anonymized users in IRM","desc":"Customers can now access and review the underlying risky prompt and response interactions generated by users during AI usage, even when user anonymization is enabled within Insider Risk Management investigations. This capability ensures that anonymized investigation workflows do not limit visibility into the contextual AI activity associated with potential risk. This enables analysts to effectively investigate detailed AI interactions across the organization. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560599","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555857","title":"Microsoft Teams: Sensitivity label inheritance for Loop meeting notes","desc":"Loop meeting notes now automatically inherit your meeting’s sensitivity label. When admins enable label inheritance in the sensitivity label policy, any labeled meeting applies the same label to its Loop meeting notes, ensuring protections like encryption, access controls, and data handling rules carry forward consistently. This also ensures that Copilot and agent responses based on Loop meeting notes accurately reflect the meeting’s sensitivity, keeping confidential content protected end to end.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557178","title":"Microsoft Teams: Sensitivity label inheritance for meeting recordings","desc":"Meeting recordings now automatically inherit the meeting’s sensitivity label. When label inheritance is enabled in sensitivity label policies, a labeled meeting applies the same label to its MP4 recording, ensuring access controls, data handling rules, and Copilot or agent responses based on transcripts consistently respect the meeting’s sensitivity end to end.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557178","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559612","title":"Microsoft Teams: Badging updates help find messages that count in the chat list","desc":"Microsoft Teams displays a badge on the app bar that reflects activity across chats and channels. Now, it’s easier to find and clear the messages behind that badge. Unmuted chats show a purple indicator when they affect the badge, while mentions, followed threads, and tag mentions display a purple number indicating how many items within are unread and part of the count.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-31","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559612","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-537282","title":"Outlook: New and Improved People Hub on Web","desc":"In Outlook Web, the new and updated People Hub delivers a modern, multi-column contacts experience, with fast search and a streamlined interface. It provides a unified view of each person, automatically links duplicate entries, and enriches contacts with organizational profile information where available.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537282","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558434","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhancements to Interpreter quality and support for Traditional Chinese","desc":"Interpreter now delivers more accurate real-time interpretation, with improved recognition of people’s names and common industry terms. It also supports your organization’s Custom Dictionary from the Microsoft 365 admin center, so tenant-specific terms can be translated more consistently across meetings. Traditional Chinese is also now supported.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558434","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-499424","title":"Microsoft Edge: Ground Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in Edge for Business in your open YouTube videos","desc":"Get relevant answers and insights about your open YouTube videos in Copilot Chat in Edge.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-01","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499424","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-496364","title":"Microsoft Edge: Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat access to page content will soon extend to work across multiple open tabs","desc":"Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in Edge will soon be able to answer contextual questions about a user's open window. This extends the existing capability which can only access the open page. All existing user settings and policies and DLP considerations will continue to be respected.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-562648","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Identifiable Export metrics in the Copilot Dashboard","desc":"This enables users to export Identifiable row-level Copilot metrics from the Copilot Dashboard for reporting and deeper analysis. This capability can be tuned On by Admins in a tenant.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562648","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-560531","title":"Excel: Summarize text columns with Copilot","desc":"Copilot can analyze columns of text to generate related categories or tags. For example, Copilot will find the main themes in survey responses from open-ended questions.","products":["Excel"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560531","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-565861","title":"Outlook: S/MIME support for Shared Mailboxes and Delegate Mailboxes in New Outlook for Windows","desc":"New Outlook for Windows will extend S/MIME support to shared mailboxes and delegate mailboxes associated with a user's primary account. Users will be able to sign, encrypt, decrypt, and reply to S/MIME-protected messages while working from shared and delegated mailboxes. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-15","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565861","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560326","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Investigation templates for common data security scenarios","desc":"We're adding pre-built search templates to Microsoft Purview Data Security Investigations. Templates provide pre-configured search queries for common data security scenarios, allowing investigators to scope an investigation in just a few clicks instead of manually building queries. Users select a template, provide minimal inputs (such as a user or site), and the search is configured and ready to run.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560326","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558249","title":"Microsoft 365 Apps: Cloud Update - Update Health","desc":"Use enhanced error reporting in Cloud Update for Microsoft 365 Apps updates to access clear, descriptive error messages that help you easily identify why an update did not complete successfully. Admins can review comprehensive insights across all Cloud Update-managed devices and drill down into individual devices for detailed information. This improved feature expands on the existing upgrade progress insights by grouping issues according to error codes and providing straightforward descriptions. These advancements enable admins to diagnose problems more efficiently, reduce support escalations, and take decisive corrective actions to boost monthly compliance rates.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558249","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-536572","title":"Microsoft Teams: External Domains Anomalies Report","desc":"This new report helps admins proactively spot unusual or risky interactions with external organizations. By analyzing communication trends and detecting sudden spikes, new domains, or abnormal engagement patterns, it provides early visibility into potential data-sharing or security risks. As external collaboration grows, this report delivers actionable insights to safeguard your tenant while supporting productive cross-organization work.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536572","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557974","title":"Microsoft Teams: Honor Windows Do not disturb setting","desc":"Microsoft Teams integrates with the Do not disturb setting in Windows to help reduce interruptions. Teams notifications are paused when Do not disturb is turned on, and resume after it is turned off.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-13","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557974","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-89975","title":"Microsoft Teams: Meeting participants can request collaborative annotation sessions","desc":"In Microsoft Teams meetings, participants who are not sharing their screen can request to start a collaborative annotation session while a screen or window is being shared. The active sharer (presenter) must approve the request before annotations start for everyone in the meeting. Organizers and co-organizers can control who can start annotations via a new Meeting Options setting under Participation (Everyone (default) or Active sharer).","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-05-24","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=89975","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release (Entire Organization)"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-559266","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint and Viva Insights Integration - Exclusion List for data sharing","desc":"Viva Glint admins will be able to manage an exclusion list in Viva Feature Access Management that prevents selected people and groups from being included in Viva Insights data shared with Viva Glint. This simplifies configuration and helps organizations apply consistent, privacy-conscious controls for the integration.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-02","modified":"2026-06-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559266","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-565906","title":"OneDrive: Collaborate on Markdown files with co-authoring and autosave","desc":"We’re bringing co-authoring and autosave to Markdown files in OneDrive and SharePoint, making it easier for teams to collaborate on Markdown content directly in Microsoft 365. Multiple users will be able to edit the same Markdown file together in the web experience, with changes saved automatically, reducing the risk of lost work and removing the need to manually manage versions.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-12","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565906","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-548671","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Data Loss Prevention to safeguard sensitive web search in Microsoft 356 Copilot and Copilot Chat","desc":"We are expanding Microsoft Purview DLP for Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat to safeguard web searches containing sensitive data. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data leakage and oversharing risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot and agents from using sensitive data for external web search. This capability currently extends to Microsoft 365 Copilot and agents built in Copilot Studio that are published to Microsoft 365 Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548671","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559029","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Mind Maps in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Mind Maps in Copilot Notebooks are interactive visual artifacts that help users understand notebook content through a grounded map of key topics, themes, and relationships. Users can explore the Mind Map, view summaries for individual nodes, and use Notebook chat to get more detail about a node. Available across OneNote and Microsoft 365 Copilot App.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneNote"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-24","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559029","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559475","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics: \"All\"- licensed user page Copilot dashboard","desc":"The Copilot Dashboard adoption landing page will be updated to show a unified view of Copilot adoption across the organization. Instead of the default page showing only on Microsoft 365 Copilot (licensed) usage, the page will include all Copilot user adoption, covering both M365 Copilot and Copilot Chat usage that does not require a license. A License filter will allow users to switch between All, M365 Copilot (licensed), and Copilot Chat (unlicensed) views.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559475","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557549","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Introducing a new URL click alert in Teams via Microsoft Defender for Office 365","desc":"We are introducing a new URL click alert that proactively notifies security teams when a user clicks on a malicious link in Teams, helping organizations quickly identify risk and respond before further impact occurs.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557549","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-497546","title":"Outlook: Account Manager","desc":"Users can use the new Account Manager feature to learn more about their Microsoft account, display their profile picture, and add new accounts (if permitted by their organization).","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-09","modified":"2026-06-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497546","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-557978","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Remove bulk users from closed survey","desc":"This feature enhancement will enable Viva Glint Admins to remove survey participants from closed surveys in bulk.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-06-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557978","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-554940","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Ability to create cases without content in IRM","desc":"Insider Risk Management is providing the ability to create a case without content. With this, we will introduce a new active case limit (2000). This new functionality will allow customers to create more cases particularly when content download is unnecessary. If a case is created without content download, content download can be initiated anytime the case is active pending available content download limits. There is no change to the active content download limit (100). Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-06-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554940","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-485724","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Quickly launch the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on your iOS device","desc":"Press the Action button or ask Siri to launch Copilot on your iOS device.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-17","modified":"2026-06-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485724","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-564615","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Triage Agent - Sensitive Data Remediation through Microsoft Teams","desc":"The Data Security Triage Agent in Data Loss Prevention now offers a new sensitive data remediation function, which empowers organizations to proactively identify and remediate sensitive information—such as Social Security Numbers, passwords, and credit card data—across thousands of files stored in SharePoint or OneDrive locations, dramatically increasing the percentage of remediated files with sensitive information, resulting in reduced compliance risk. Seamlessly integrated with Microsoft Purview, this new agent function automatically detects file(s) with a Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policy match “Needs Attention” alerts and pushes a remediation notification to the end user who last modified the file guiding them to remove sensitive data through targeted Microsoft Teams messages. Its’ closed-loop workflow ensures that remediation progress is tracked and confirmed, giving admins real-time visibility and control via the Data Security Posture Management dashboard. By streamlining sensitive data cleanup and automating user engagement, this agent helps organizations achieve their remediation goals at scale. Let the Data Security Triage Agent handle the heavy lifting of pushing remediation requests directly to the end user, so Purview admins don't have to!","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-10","modified":"2026-06-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564615","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560337","title":"SharePoint: Create Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files with AI","desc":"You can ask AI in SharePoint to create a Word, Excel or PowerPoint file based on the information you've gathered within SharePoint","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560337","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561329","title":"Microsoft Edge: Enterprise WebView2 runtime downgrade via Downgrade Version policy","desc":"Administrators can temporarily roll back specific applications to a previous WebView2 Evergreen Runtime version (N-1 or N-2) using the new Downgrade Version policy in msedgewebview2.admx. This policy allows enterprises to mitigate critical regressions by specifying per-application exe-to-version mappings. The Edge Updater installs the target version side-by-side, and the WebView2 Loader redirects targeted apps accordingly. Downgrades auto-expire with each new WebView2 release: apps pinned to N-1 remain on the same version (now N-2) and auto-update in the next release, while apps pinned to N-2 revert to the current Evergreen version. The policy applies only to enterprise-managed devices (domain-joined or MDM-enrolled).","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-06","modified":"2026-06-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561329","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-553595","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copy Tables in Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat","desc":"Users can now copy tables created in Copilot. Leverage Copilot to make your content better and use it anywhere you need to.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-03","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553595","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-490154","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Learning Agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"The Learning agent helps employees build skills through personalized microlearning and structured learning experiences.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-29","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490154","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-541832","title":"Microsoft Edge: v. 149 - Clarify choices surrounding third-party cookie settings","desc":"Language under Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies will be clarified to better describe the choices users have in managing third-party cookies.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-12","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=541832","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561041","title":"Microsoft Edge: v. 149 - Unifying Copilot Chat policy controls","desc":"The Microsoft365CopilotChatIconEnabled policy is becoming the standard for configuring Copilot Chat. Extension and sidebar policies will no longer affect the appearance or functionality of Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-29","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561041","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559993","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.149 - Modern, unified, and updated Look and Feel","desc":"Microsoft Edge will update the Look and Feel to give customers a unified experience across all of Microsoft AI surfaces including Copilot and Bing. This will change multiple elements of the UX such as spacing, corners, fonts, default colors, etc.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559993","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560327","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Proactive AI insight powered by Data Security Posture Management","desc":"Data Security Investigations now delivers proactive AI insights within the Data Security Posture Management (DSPM) experience. When DSPM identifies potential data exfiltration, DSI automatically analyzes the flagged content against risk dimensions like intellectual property, financial data, and credentials. Results are surfaced directly in DSPM, helping security teams identify sensitive data at risk before an incident occurs — and take action in DSI when deeper investigation is needed.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560327","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-493319","title":"Microsoft Teams: BYOD space peripheral health signals and reports in the Pro Management portal","desc":"Admins can proactively manage peripherals in bring your own device (BYOD) rooms and desks with reports in the Pro Management portal that now flag if devices are faulty, undetectable by a PC, missing, or moved. Reports in the Pro Management portal require a Teams Shared Devices license for the room, and reports for desks are in public preview.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-29","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493319","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-561493","title":"Microsoft Teams: Upload custom backgrounds for Teams events","desc":"Organizers and presenters who have access to production tools can now upload custom backgrounds in the \"Manage what attendees see\" experience for Teams events. This enhancement allows organizations to display their brand identity by replacing the default backgrounds with their own images, such as company logos, event-specific artwork, or themed visuals. Custom backgrounds appear behind presenters and content, giving attendees a polished viewing experience. This feature is available for Teams events organizers with a Teams Premium license. This feature is available on Teams for Windows desktop and Mac desktop.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-05-07","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561493","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559267","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Device Health Reporting Dashboard","desc":"This dashboard will allow admins to view the device health across all their devices to ensure the system is healthy and ready to receive policy updates and quickly identify devices that are not ready.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559267","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-511801","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Onboarding emails for Leaders","desc":"This feature introduces automated, role-targeted onboarding emails for Leaders to drive discovery of the Copilot Dashboard in Viva insights.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511801","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560340","title":"Outlook: Copilot in File Previewer for iOS","desc":"Access Copilot directly when previewing files in Outlook. Tap the Copilot button to get smart suggestions, summaries, and answers about your documents without leaving the previewer. Get quick help understanding attachments and files right when you need it.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560340","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-516039","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot uses enterprise assets hosted on Adobe Experience Manager when creating presentations","desc":"Once you connect your asset library hosted on Adobe Experience Manager to Microsoft365 and Copilot, Copilot will create presentations using your organization's images.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516039","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-516038","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot uses enterprise assets hosted on Adobe Experience Manager when creating presentations","desc":"Once you connect your asset library hosted on Adobe Experience Manager to Microsoft365 and Copilot, Copilot will create presentations using your organization's images.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516038","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-516037","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot uses enterprise assets hosted on Adobe Experience Manager when creating presentations","desc":"Once you connect your asset library hosted on Adobe Experience Manager to Microsoft365 and Copilot, Copilot will create presentations using your organization's images.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516037","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-548641","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Open Word, Excel, and PowerPoint Files in Copilot Chat","desc":"Currently, clicking on cited content in Copilot opens files outside of Copilot. With this new feature, content can be opened directly in Copilot Chat to make viewing documents more streamlined alongside chat. This change is not available on the Microsfot 365 Copilot mobile app or when using Copilot in Edge, Copilot in Excel, Copilot in Word, and Copilot PowerPoint.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548641","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-546246","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Researcher Output Formats","desc":"The Researcher Agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot empowers users to create rich, detailed reports on any topic they choose whether from work or web content. We are introducing new output formats in the Researcher Agent that will allow users to export and consume generated reports in their preferred formats. Users will be able to export their Researcher reports to PowerPoint, PDF, Infographic or an Audio Overview. We are also updating the UX for previously existing output formats- Word and Pages.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-13","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=546246","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557254","title":"Outlook: Add support for Recommended Labels in Outlook mobile","desc":"When composing an email on your mobile device, Outlook can recommend or automatically apply an appropriate sensitivity label if your organization’s automatic or recommended labeling policies are enabled by admins and the message contains sensitive information. For recommended labels, you’ll see a prompt to review and apply the suggested label, and automatic labels will be applied without needing any action from you.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557254","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557253","title":"Outlook: Add support for Recommended Labels in Outlook mobile","desc":"When composing an email on your mobile device, Outlook can recommend or automatically apply an appropriate sensitivity label if your organization’s automatic or recommended labeling policies are enabled by admins and the message contains sensitive information. For recommended labels, you’ll see a prompt to review and apply the suggested label, and automatic labels will be applied without needing any action from you.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557253","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-559023","title":"Outlook: Shareable links now show as the document name in meeting descriptions","desc":"In Outlook for Android, shareable links now automatically show as the document name in meeting descriptions. Additionally, users can manage the link permissions on the shareable links directly from the meeting description, ensuring a more secure file sharing process.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559023","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557350","title":"Outlook: Improved results when filtering your message list","desc":"When you apply a filter in the message list, Outlook for iOS now helps you search for all matching messages—even older ones that aren’t currently synced. If more results may be available, you can tap to run a search with the filter already applied.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557350","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555233","title":"Outlook: Reply Options for EML Attachments","desc":"Now, when opening a .eml attachment, users will see reply, reply all and forward options.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555233","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555232","title":"Outlook: Reply Options for EML Attachments","desc":"Now, when opening a .eml attachment, users will see reply, reply all and forward options.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555232","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-541834","title":"Outlook: Font Search in Outlook for Android","desc":"Users can now search for the name of font they want to use when composing an email on Outlook for Android.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-10","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=541834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-541833","title":"Outlook: Font Search in Outlook for iOS","desc":"Users can now search for the name of font they want to use when composing an email on Outlook for iOS.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-10","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=541833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-500633","title":"Microsoft 365 Copilot: Initiate Copilot Chat by sharing files to the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPhone and iPad","desc":"When users on iPhone and iPad choose the action to share a Word, Excel, or PowerPoint file from a third party app (including Files) and choose Microsoft 365 Copilot as the target app, the file will be uploaded to chat. Users will then have the option to open a preview of the file or continue their conversation with Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-15","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500633","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-500631","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Preview and chat with Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPhone","desc":"When opening a Microsoft Word, Excel, or PowerPoint file in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPhone, users will get a preview experience where they can use Copilot Chat to command and ask questions about the files directly in the preview. This enables immediate access to Copilot Chat in a user's file.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-15","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500631","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-493946","title":"OneDrive: Transfer ownership of departing employees’ files with ease","desc":"We’ve made it easier to manage files when employees leave—account cleanup emails are now more prominent, new filters help managers quickly locate key files, and the enhanced “Move and keep sharing” feature supports bulk transfers with consolidated notifications, making the process more efficient. Security and compliance in ownership transfer ensures sensitive data remains protected, access is properly reassigned, and regulatory obligations are met during employee offboarding.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-16","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493946","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-500632","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat-centered experience for creating new documents in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPhone and iPad","desc":"In the Create experience in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPhone and iPad, users will see a chat-centered experience to create documents, enabling them to describe the document they want to create in a prompt.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2026-06-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500632","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-561323","title":"SharePoint: Authoritative Sites","desc":"Authoritative Sites feature empowers administrators to designate specific SharePoint sites as official, trusted sources of information. By classifying these sites as authoritative these high-quality, credible content, such as company news, policies, and updates, are prioritized across Copilot Chat and Copilot Search experiences","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-30","modified":"2026-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560550","title":"Exchange: Dynamic distribution groups now populate membership faster on creation and modification","desc":"We're updating dynamic distribution groups (DDGs) in Exchange Online to make group membership available sooner after creation or a filter change. For DDGs with 5,000 members or fewer, membership is now populated as part of the creation or modification operation — no more waiting up to 2 hours.","products":["Exchange"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560550","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-511820","title":"Planner: Planner Agent in group-based basic plans","desc":"Planner Agent will now be available for M365 Copilot licensed users in all group-based Planner plans, including basic plans.","products":["Planner","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511820","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"March CY2025"},{"id":"rm-564971","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Notifications for organizational data processing status","desc":"With this feature, organizational data source admins receive email notifications when data processing through one of their configured connectors completes successfully or requires attention. Notifications are enabled by default with the option to unsubscribe.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-04","modified":"2026-06-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564971","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-565027","title":"SharePoint: Agent Access Insights heatmap for SharePoint and OneDrive sites","desc":"Provides a visual heatmap of agent activity to help admins quickly detect patterns, hotspots, and unusual access behavior.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-04","modified":"2026-06-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=565027","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-559095","title":"OneNote: Multimodal capture in Copilot Notebooks (iPhone)","desc":"Multimodal capture enables users to transcribe audio, take images, and type notes in a single session. Copilot then creates a structured Copilot Page with insights and user-captured content, saved to a user-selected Copilot Notebook. Designed for capturing offline work moments—including in-person conversations, whiteboard sessions, and personal notes. Other endpoints coming soon.","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-24","modified":"2026-06-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559095","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557557","title":"Microsoft Purview: DSPM data risk assessments: item-level investigation & remediation","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data risk assessments now support item-level investigation and remediation of SharePoint data. New insights like sensitivity label and sharing link information help users identify items at risk of oversharing. Users are empowered to remediate overshared items by resolving, notifying, applying a sensitivity label, or removing sharing links for selected item(s). This helps organizations proactively reduce data exposure, strengthen compliance posture, and ensure sensitive data are only accessible to the right people.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-09","modified":"2026-06-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557557","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-386900","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Sensitivity label grouping modernization","desc":"To help improve label usability and configuration, the sensitivity labeling scheme will be simplified to only consist of labels and label groupings. These new label groupings allow admins to better organize and categorize their labels (previously done via parent labels).","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-03-14","modified":"2026-06-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=386900","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-560814","title":"Microsoft Teams: Search in quick sharing experience","desc":"Microsoft Teams makes it easier to find and attach files by enabling search directly within the quick sharing experience. You can now locate cloud based files while attaching content, reducing friction when sharing files across chats and channels.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560814","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559310","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updated chat-first design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot mobile app","desc":"We are introducing a refreshed chat-first design in the Microsoft 365 Copilot mobile app, bringing a cleaner, more intuitive interface to users. This update includes a modernized design language, streamlined navigation, and other improvements that make it easier and faster for users to start, continue, and manage chats on the mobile app.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-24","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559310","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560397","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Enforce DLP protection upon new content before its saved","desc":"Monitor or protect file with unsaved sensitive content from being printed or being moved to USB or network share.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560397","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-555898","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference webpages when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference webpages when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555898","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-555896","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference webpages when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference webpages when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555896","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-555893","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference webpages when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference webpages when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555893","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-518218","title":"Microsoft Teams: Consult and merge a PSTN caller through DTMF","desc":"Users have always been able to dial a phone number and add someone to a meeting. Now, meeting organizers can seamlessly consult and merge PSTN callers to active Teams meetings even if they are behind auto-attendants that require Dual-Tone Multi-Frequency, or DTMF, navigation. For example, you can connect with and consult a subject matter expert through an audio conference dial-in before adding them to the group discussion.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518218","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-555885","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555885","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555892","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555892","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555889","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint using Agent Mode.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555889","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555887","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference the content of a PowerPoint file when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555887","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-508529","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Find Exactly What You Need, Faster","desc":"Now you can filter your search as you type. Use person and source filters right in the Search box to refine results instantly. Get smart suggestions and see only what matters, all without leaving the box. 1. When “person” or “source” is typed, a list of relevant filter suggestions appears. This helps auto-complete the filter expression and enables effective pre-scoping. 2. Once filters are applied in the Search box, all subsequent suggestions are refined based on those filters.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508529","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-527830","title":"Microsoft Teams: App centric management in Teams Admin Center to manage the Apps access for tenants, end-users, and groups in GCC","desc":"App centric management introduces new admin settings to control who in the tenant can install Teams apps. First, admins can set a default value for new apps that are published to Teams app store. Second, admins can edit the availability of an app to 'All users can install', 'Specific users and groups can install', or 'No user can install'. This feature evolves the existing app permission policies and provides admins with the ability to manage access to the app individually. The app permission policies for existing customers are migrated to maintain existing app availability in the tenant.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-13","modified":"2026-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527830","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"mc-MC1289725","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Delete meeting generated content in recap","desc":"Updated June 2, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nMeeting organizers in Microsoft Teams can now delete meeting‑generated content—including recordings, transcripts, AI summaries, and notes—directly from the meeting recap. This capability helps organizers manage meeting artifacts after the meeting. Shared files from the meeting are not deleted.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557170.\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out in early May 2026 and expect to complete by early May 2026.\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in late May 2026 and expect to complete by early June 2026.\n• General Availability (GCC): We will begin rolling out in mid-June 2026 and expect to complete by mid-June 2026.\n• General Availability (GCCH): We will begin rolling out in early September 2026 (previously late June) and expect to complete by late September 2026 (previously late June).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Microsoft Teams meeting organizers\n\n• Tenants using meeting recap features\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• A new Delete recap content option will appear in the More (…) menu on the meeting recap page.\nScreenshot 1: Delete recap content option found under the More (...) menu:\n>\nScreenshot 2: Delete recap content confirmation:\n\n• Meeting organizers can permanently delete:• Recordings\n• Transcripts\n• AI summary\n• Notes\n\n• Shared files are not deleted and remain accessible in their original storage locations.\n• Custom summary and Audio recap will not be deleted with Delete recap content in this release.\n• Deleted meeting content cannot be restored.\n• The feature is enabled by default and does not require admin configuration.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Inform users about this new capability.\n\n• Update internal documentation and helpdesk guidance.\n\n• Review meeting governance and retention guidance.\n\n• Monitor usage through Teams and SharePoint analytics.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nMeeting organizers can now permanently delete meeting-generated content, impacting how users manage and delete their data. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1289725","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-560816","title":"Microsoft Teams: Quick Share for Images","desc":"Microsoft Teams extends Quick Share to images, making it fast and easy to share visual content across chats and channels. With access from hover, right click, overflow menus, and shared tabs, you can quickly copy links or share images while preserving existing permissions.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-24","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560816","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-558440","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Choose Anthropic models when editing with Copilot in Word","desc":"You can choose to select Anthropic models, in addition to OpenAI models, when editing a Word document using Copilot.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-10","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558440","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-559611","title":"Microsoft Teams: Annotations on Teams Single Window Sharing on macOS","desc":"Presenters can now share a single application window and enable participants to annotate directly on top of that content, without exposing their entire desktop. This means cleaner presentations, protected privacy, and more engaging discussions across training sessions, workshops, and client meetings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-02","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559611","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-422308","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Lists in Context IQ","desc":"Users will be able to search for and select SharePoint Lists through the Context IQ menu to help ground their prompts when using Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-02","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422308","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555884","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555884","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555883","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"You can now reference a Teams meeting or chat when creating a presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555883","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-558105","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Take Screenshot in Copilot","desc":"Give users a fast, built‑in way to capture screenshots and include them in Copilot prompts, helping them communicate visual context more easily and receive more accurate, actionable assistance.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558105","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-502523","title":"Microsoft Teams: Screen & Window Sharing on Mac via macOS native experience","desc":"Microsoft Teams is introducing a new feature that enables Mac users to share their screen or specific windows using the built-in native macOS sharing experience. This is Mac only, user opt-in experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-08","modified":"2026-06-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502523","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-564804","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Multiple Voice Styles in M365 Copilot voice chats","desc":"Users can select from multiple voice style options for their voice experience in M365 Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-06-01","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564804","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-559476","title":"Microsoft Entra: Account Discovery for Application Access Governance.","desc":"Account discovery provides visibility into who has access to connected applications by discovering local and orphaned accounts and identifying accounts that can be matched to Microsoft Entra ID users. Account discovery will help administrators identify access that exists outside of Microsoft Entra ID Governance and bring that access under governance—simplifying application onboarding while improving visibility and control over application access.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559476","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560694","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint directly from the PowerPoint Home","desc":"You can now create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint straight from the PowerPoint Home in file menu.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560694","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560536","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint directly from the PowerPoint Home","desc":"You can now create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint straight from the PowerPoint Home in file menu.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-20","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560536","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560537","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint directly from the PowerPoint Web App","desc":"You can now create a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint just as you open the PowerPoint web app.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560537","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-559028","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Logged-in user details on the Purview device onboarding page","desc":"This update introduces logged-in user details (user email) on the device onboarding page for Windows devices bringing it in line with the experience for MacOS devices. ​Admins can now see which user is currently signed in on a device, making It faster to confirm ownership and troubleshoot issues. ​","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559028","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-532728","title":"Microsoft Purview: New Microsoft Purview Data Security Posture Management Experience","desc":"At Ignite, Microsoft is introducing a major evolution of Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM) to help organizations strengthen data security and confidently embrace AI. The new DSPM experience unifies visibility and control across traditional data and AI-driven environments, delivering outcome-based guided workflows that turn insights into actionable steps—so teams can prioritize risks and remediate faster. It brings AI observability, enhanced posture reporting, and intelligent Security Copilot agents to automate tasks like triage and policy management. Plus, Purview now extends coverage beyond Microsoft data with third-party signals from partners like BigID, Cyera, OneTrust, and Varonis, giving security teams a single, streamlined view of sensitive data across clouds and platforms. Together, these innovations make DSPM the central hub for managing data security posture in the era of AI. We are also extending Data Risk Assessments to Fabric and to item-level analysis with new remediation actions like bulk disabling of overshared SharePoint links.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-25","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532728","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-560052","title":"Microsoft Teams: Multi-stream IntelliFrame support for GCC-H and DoD in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"GCC-H and DoD customers can now experience multi-stream IntelliFrame in Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows, which sends separate video feeds of each in-room participant to improve hybrid meeting visibility and inclusivity. Requires a compatible intelligent camera. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-09","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560052","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/devices/multistream-intelliframe"},{"id":"rm-560049","title":"Microsoft Teams: Multi‑camera view support for GCC-H and DoD in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"GCC-H and DoD cloud customers can now experience multi-camera views in Microsoft Teams Rooms on Windows, allowing remote participants to switch between multiple in-room camera feeds for improved visibility and engagement in larger spaces. Find camera requirements here. Available with Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-09","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560049","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/rooms/multicamera-view"},{"id":"rm-518221","title":"Microsoft Entra: Cross-tenant security group synchronization","desc":"We’re introducing cross-tenant group synchronization, a new capability that enables organizations to synchronize security groups across Microsoft Entra tenants. This feature simplifies collaboration scenarios by allowing shared access to resources across tenants while maintaining centralized group management. It also streamlines administration of multiple tenants by centralizing group membership control, reducing duplication and manual overhead.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518221","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-500895","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Endpoint DLP support classification of Azure RMS protected Office documents","desc":"Endpoint DLP can now classify Office files stored in Windows devices that have Azure RMS protection applied. Classification will be triggered when file is used in applications or when just-in-time classification is enabled","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-21","modified":"2026-06-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500895","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-423047","title":"Outlook: Mail Merge (Advanced) on Outlook on the Web and new Outlook for Windows","desc":"Mail Merge (Basic) will be improved upon to allow fields to be replaced by values per email address. When Mail Merge (Advanced) is launched, not only will every recipient receive their own email with only their email address in the recipients list, but the emails can further be personalized to include content such as their name. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-17","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=423047","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564909","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot suggested rename","desc":"Copilot Suggested Rename is an AI-powered OneDrive feature that automatically recommends clear, descriptive file names based on a file’s content—helping users organize and find their files more easily with minimal effort. What the feature does: - Analyzes the content of a file to generate context-aware filename suggestions - Presents 3 recommended names directly within the rename dialog - Allows users to pick a suggestion with a single click Where it shows up: - Within the rename dialog for supported files - Within the post-upload toast notification when a single supported file is uploaded Supported file types: - Microsoft Office documents Word (DOCX) PowerPoint (PPTX) Excel (XLSX) - Other document formats PDF Markdown (MD) - Images","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-29","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564909","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-564803","title":"Outlook: Sort improvements to the message list","desc":"When sorting on Outlook for Web or Outlook for Windows, if the Sort By field is not one of From, Subject, or Date Received, we will now show an additional column for the Sort By value (e.g., Size). We will also support sorting by Flag Due Date.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-29","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564803","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557173","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Submit agent to Agent Store from Agent Builder","desc":"Customers can submit their custom Copilot agents built in Agent Builder to the Agent Store under the \"Built by your org\" section, after admin review and approval in M365 Admin Center. This governed flow enables admins to review, approve, and publish submitted agents so that they can be discovered and used by others in the Agent Store. This helps organizations share validated agents at scale while maintaining quality and governance.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557173","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558256","title":"Microsoft Edge: Copilot New Tab Page","desc":"Search, chat, and explore the web from one search box with Copilot-suggested actions and curated work content to help your users get things done faster on the new, refreshed Copilot New Tab Page. Users can also view personalized news and activities.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558256","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-523206","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Real-time voice interactions in a podcast in Word","desc":"Interact in real time with podcasts created by Copilot in Word. Today, audio summaries help you absorb content on the go, but they’re one-way—listeners can’t clarify or explore without stopping. With this feature, you can ask questions with your voice while listening and get answers instantly, staying in the audio experience and understanding content faster.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523206","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-548670","title":"Microsoft 365: Drawn electronic signatures with eSignature for Microsoft 365","desc":"Signers will be able to add their electronic signature to PDFs using a stylus, touch, or mouse, in addition to the existing typed signature option.","products":["Microsoft 365","SharePoint","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548670","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-501540","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Customize AI-generated notes in meeting recap","desc":"Users can now customize the AI-generated notes in meeting recap, instantly transforming meeting notes into the format that works best for each person. Choose from built-in options like Speaker Summary or Executive Summary to quickly surface the details that matter most. Users can even create and save their own custom templates with a simple prompt, so meeting notes always match the way each user prefers to work.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501540","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-564621","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Unified alert queue","desc":"We’re introducing a new unified alert triage experience in Insider Risk Management that brings agent‑driven insights directly into the standard Alerts queue. With this update, analysts can view agent categorizations alongside traditional alert filters and columns in a single, consolidated workflow. The updated alert details panel, enables faster investigation and action from the alerts list page by embedding agent insights directly into the alert experience. To support customer transition, the existing alert and agent triage experience will remain available for 60 days and can be accessed via the Alerts tabs under Users in the left navigation. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564621","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"July CY2026"},{"id":"rm-564609","title":"Outlook: All Accounts view (Unified Inbox) brings your email into a single inbox view","desc":"The All-Accounts view, also known as Unified Inbox, lets you see emails from multiple accounts in a single inbox view in the new Outlook for Windows, without merging your mailboxes. Each account's inbox stays separate; the view brings them together so you can triage in one place. Users can read, delete, move, archive, and mark messages across accounts without switching between mailboxes. The experience integrates with Copilot for AI-assisted email workflows and supports Immersive Search for finding messages across your primary account. Advanced scenarios such as cross-account search and shared mailbox support will follow in later releases.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564609","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-529858","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Shortcuts for Pages on Mobile","desc":"Mobile users can utilize Copilot Shortcuts with suggested prompts to edit a Page.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-02","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-564607","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): MCP-Based Agent Enablement for U.S. Government Clouds","desc":"We’re introducing support for Model Context Protocol (MCP)-based agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot . This update enables developers to build Copilot agents using MCP servers and allows users to interact with these agents using familiar experiences. This change supports extensibility and improves agent capabilities for organizations.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-27","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=564607","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557179","title":"Microsoft Teams: Minimized meeting window enhancements","desc":"We're improving the experience when the active meeting window is minimized. Users can now raise their hand and send reactions without restoring the full meeting window. They can also choose between two minimized views: an expanded view that shows up to 4 participant videos, or a compact view that does not display other participants' video.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557179","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560695","title":"Outlook: Teammates Calendars in Left Nav in calendar","desc":"Users can now see colleagues’ and direct reports’ calendars in the left navigation by default—without manual setup. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560695","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"mc-MC1310378","title":"Power Platform admin center - Discover what's driving engagement with the Usage page","desc":"Update: Release of this feature has been updated.\n\nWe are announcing the ability to discover what's driving engagement with the Usage page in Power Platform admin center. This feature will reach general availability on August 17, 2026.\n\nHow does this affect me?\nThis feature helps you identify the top resources in your organization that are driving success and spot adoption trends, such as usage spikes for apps, flows, and agents. At the top of the page, you will find a summary view showcasing the adoption trends over time, as well as the resources that are driving the most value. You'll be able to see metrics that include: • The top apps by user activity\n• The top flows by run volume\n• The top agents by session count\n\nBelow the summary view, detailed tables provide sortable views of all apps, flows, and agents that are in use in your organization. Sort by users for apps, runs for flows, and sessions for agents to quickly identify trends and top performers.\n\nWhat action do I need to take?\nThis message is for awareness, and no action is required.\n\nIf you would like more information on this feature, please visit Discover what's driving engagement with the Usage page.","products":["Power Platform"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-14","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1310378","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-510100","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Add Search results as references to your Copilot Notebooks in the M365 Copilot app","desc":"Users can quickly add a Search result as a reference to a Copilot Notebook within the M365 Copilot app.","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-03","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=510100","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-515160","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with 15Five to surface team priorities and recognition with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with 15Five to surface team priorities and recognition with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515160","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-558340","title":"Microsoft Teams: Account Switching for Native Mac Controls via Dock and Menu Bar","desc":"Users will now find controls for switching between the accounts and tenants that they are signed into making it easier to navigate on Mac.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558340","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-553590","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Phone Device user multi-line","desc":"Teams Phone user multi‑line gives callers more flexibility and control by allowing administrators to assign up to 10 phone numbers to a single user. With full support on Teams Phone Android devices, users can seamlessly make and receive calls from multiple numbers without switching accounts or hardware. This makes it easy to manage different roles, departments, or regional identities—all from one unified Teams experience. The result is a familiar, localized calling experience for users who work across diverse markets or with global customers.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553590","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-531758","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Now smarter with visuals: Declarative Agents leverage embedded images for richer, more accurate answers","desc":"Declarative Agents have been enhanced to interpret and ground responses using images embedded in files such as Word documents (.docx), PowerPoint presentations (.pptx), and PDFs. This capability allows the agent to extract insights from visual elements like charts, diagrams, and screenshots, ensuring that answers are not only text-based but also informed by graphical context. By combining textual and visual understanding, Declarative Agents deliver more comprehensive and contextually accurate responses for complex queries.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-21","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=531758","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-557169","title":"Microsoft Teams: Simplified Teams app bar to create a cleaner and more focused experience.","desc":"We’ve simplified the app bar to help you focus on what matters. Apps are easier to scan in a cleaner View more apps list, the overflow menu is less cluttered, and you can choose to show or hide the app bar to create more space for your work.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557169","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-488091","title":"Microsoft Teams: Unified attachment flow on Teams Mobile","desc":"Introducing a new content picker for Teams Mobile! Attach any type of content, whether files or media, from the paperclip icon in the compose overflow menu. Our unified attach flow makes it easy and intuitive to attach content from any source location.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-05","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488091","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-506744","title":"Microsoft 365: Department Billing for Microsoft 365 Backup","desc":"Department Billing for Microsoft 365 Backup enables administrators to configure backups by granular scopes—such as departments, geographic locations, or member firms—and manage pay-as-you-go charges across multiple Azure subscriptions. With Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), department-specific backup administrators can be assigned, ensuring management control, and tailored backup management aligned to organizational boundaries.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-26","modified":"2026-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506744","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"rm-410249","title":"Outlook: Calendar support in Online Archive","desc":"Add calendar support in Online Archive.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-08-01","modified":"2026-05-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=410249","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"May CY2027"},{"id":"rm-509109","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Start writing, coding, and creating with Copilot in Pages","desc":"Use the tools menu in Copilot Chat to co-create content or code with Copilot in a Page and share with others when ready.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-03","modified":"2026-05-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=509109","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-559606","title":"Microsoft Teams: Sharing recap access","desc":"Recording and transcript owners can now grant recording and transcript access to specified people when copying or sharing recap link, and the specified people can access the recap without having to request access.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-04-03","modified":"2026-05-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559606","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557553","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Export DLP and Label Policy Configurations","desc":"A new export functionality will be introduced in two locations: the Data Loss Prevention > Policies page and the Information Protection > Label publishing policies page. This feature will allow users to export their existing DLP configurations and label policies, including schema, as a downloadable ZIP file. The exported file can be attached to support tickets to accelerate troubleshooting.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-05-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557553","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-563810","title":"Outlook: Navigate Your Favorite Folders Without Expanding the Folder Pane","desc":"You can now quickly switch between your favorite folders without opening the full folder pane. When the pane is collapsed, your favorite folders appear as a vertical list, giving you one-click access to the folders you use most. Each folder shows unread or total counts so you always know what needs attention. Right-click any favorite for the same options you're used to, and your selections stay put across sessions. It's a familiar experience for anyone who loved favorites in classic Outlook, now built right into the new Outlook. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-21","modified":"2026-05-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=563810","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"August CY2026"},{"id":"rm-481825","title":"SharePoint: Chat one-on-one with SharePoint agents in Teams","desc":"Users can chat one-on-one with a SharePoint agent directly within Teams chat.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","SharePoint"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-05-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-529849","title":"Outlook: Calendar Conditional Formatting in New Outlook","desc":"Users can now apply basic conditional formatting rules to the calendar in new Outlook, allowing events and appointments to be color-coded based on sender, location, attendees, and more. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-05-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529849","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-557168","title":"Microsoft Teams: Book future meetings directly from Teams panels","desc":"You can now make an upcoming meeting reservation from a Teams panel by browsing the calendar on the device and choosing any open time slot through midnight the next day. Add a guest during booking streamlining ad-hoc scheduling and coordination. Available with Teams Rooms Pro and Shared Device licenses.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-05-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557168","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-497909","title":"Microsoft CoPilot (Microsoft 365): List email attachments in M365 Copilot","desc":"Users will be able to list the file attachments that they received or sent over email in M365 Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-02","modified":"2026-05-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497909","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Developer","iOS","Linux","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558107","title":"Microsoft Teams: Identify bots joining your Teams meetings","desc":"During Teams meetings, if there is an external 3P bot trying to join the meeting, organizers will be able to see a clear representation of the bots while they wait in the lobby. Organizers will be required to explicitly and separately admit these bots into the meeting, if really required. This approach will ensure that no one inadvertently accepts the external bots into the meeting ensuring that the organizers have full control over the presence of these bots.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-05-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557678","title":"Outlook: Instantly Find Rules, Quick Steps, and More by Name","desc":"Managing your email automation in Outlook is now effortless with name search built into your key productivity tools. You can search within Rules, Conditional Formatting, Quick Steps, and Search Folders, filtering the list by name so you jump straight to the item you need. Whether you have dozens of rules or a growing library of quick steps, just type a few characters to narrow down results instantly. No more scrolling through long lists to find the right one, search puts you in control. Stay organized and make changes faster, right where you need them. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-05-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557678","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559018","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work IQ APIs: Researcher Agent Access","desc":"Allows developers to invoke the Researcher agent through the Work IQ endpoint to perform multi‑step analysis, deep reasoning, and synthesis across enterprise content as part of agentic workflows.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-18","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559018","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-502562","title":"Outlook: Calendar mini-month non-consecutive date selection updates","desc":"You can now use Shift+Click or CTRL+Click to select non-consecutive dates in the calendar mini-month. This will allow you to easily view and take action on the dates you care about. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-17","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502562","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"mc-MC1183611","title":"(Updated) Consult and merge into a meeting or group call via Dual-Tone Multi-Frequency (DTMF)","desc":"Updated May 18, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nTo improve collaboration and streamline meeting workflows, Microsoft Teams is introducing the ability to consult and merge Public Switched Telephone Network (PSTN) callers into active meetings—even when those callers are behind auto-attendants or Interactive Voice Response (IVR) systems that require Dual-Tone Multi-Frequency (DTMF) navigation. This enhancement allows users to reach subject matter experts via dial-in and seamlessly bring them into the broader conversation.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 518218.\n[When this will happen:]\n• Targeted Release: Rolling out early April 2026 (previously early March), expected to complete by mid-April 2026 (previously mid-March).\n\n• General Availability: Rolling out mid-April 2026 (previously late March), expected to complete by mid-June 2026 (previously late April).\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\n• Who is affected: All Microsoft Teams users who initiate or manage meetings with PSTN participants. Administrators overseeing Teams meeting policies and call configurations.\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• Users can consult with PSTN or Voice over Internet Protocol (VoIP) participants via the Participants panel.\n\n• A new interface will allow users to access a dialpad to navigate IVR systems and auto-attendants using DTMF tones.\n\n• Once the external party is reached, users can merge them into the ongoing meeting.\n\n• No changes to existing administrator policies; feature is enabled by default.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No administrator action is required for this rollout.\n\n• If your organization uses custom training or helpdesk documentation, consider updating it to reflect this new capability.\n• Before rollout, we will update this post with new documentation.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1183611","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202605},{"id":"mc-MC1314979","title":"Microsoft Dataverse - Solution-aware tables and metadata in Dataverse now classified as file storage","desc":"In April 2026, we updated how storage is reported in Dataverse, moving solution-aware components and metadata from the database tier to the file tier. This change has no impact on apps, flows, solutions, or integrations.\n\nHow does this affect me?\nWithin the Power Platform admin center, under Resources and then Capacity:• Database storage is lower by the amount previously attributed to this content.\n• File storage is proportionally higher.\n• Total tenant storage is unchanged. Content moved tiers; it did not grow.\n\nDatabase and file capacity are entitled and priced separately:• If you were near your database limit, you likely have more headroom.\n• If you were near your file limit, confirm you have sufficient file capacity; additional capacity is available via add-on.\n\nWhat do I need to do to prepare?\nThis message is for awareness and no action required.\n\nWe recommend admins sign in to the Power Platform admin center and navigate to Resources and then Capacity to review Database, File, and Log usage at the tenant and environment level, especially if trending near the file entitlement.\n\nIf you have questions about this change or your capacity position, please contact Microsoft Support.\n\nAdditional information• Dataverse capacity-based storage overview\n• Dataverse capacity-based storage details\n• Add more Microsoft Dataverse capacity to your tenant\n• Power Platform Licensing Guide","products":["Microsoft Dataverse"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-18","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1314979","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557167","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhanced issue detection in Teams Rooms on Windows and auto-remediation with Teams Rooms Pro Management.","desc":"Teams Rooms on Windows proactively monitors room audio, video, and display signals to detect issues in meeting spaces. Teams Rooms Pro Management automatically remediates common issues that can be resolved through software, configuration changes, or device resets during nightly maintenance. This ensures users have reliable, ready-to-use meeting rooms, while IT admins benefit from reduced manual troubleshooting and increased uptime. Available for Teams Rooms Pro-licensed rooms.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557167","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558442","title":"Outlook: Improved handling of disallowed and failed email reactions","desc":"Emails with reactions disallowed will now see the Reactions button grayed out correctly. Additionally, when any attempt to react fails, the local update will no longer remain onscreen and be properly undone.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558442","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365-apps/outlook/manage/manage-outlook-reactions?view=o365-worldwide"},{"id":"rm-559388","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing new personal data examination","desc":"Data Security Investigations (DSI) is introducing a new examination focus area concentrated on identifying personal data. The personal data examination will identify and extract various types of personal data from the selected items including but not limited to, names, addresses, bank account numbers, and more. This addition works alongside DSI’s AI-powered content analysis features, such as categorization, AI search, and examination for risk, which help surface data security risks buried in data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559388","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-548647","title":"Microsoft Teams: Digital signage in Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"As with Teams Rooms on Windows, IT Admins can now set up Teams Rooms on Android to show dynamic signage content on the front-of-room display when the device is not in use for meetings or presentation. Configuration is available for tenant-wide and room-specific settings via the Teams Rooms Pro Management portal. The feature supports select third-party digital signage partners like Appspace and XOGO, and is included with Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548647","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-554925","title":"Microsoft Teams: Resizable Gallery in Teams Meetings","desc":"Resize the top video gallery in Teams meetings to see more people when content is being shared.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554925","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558540","title":"Microsoft Teams: Video recap in Teams","desc":"Intelligent meeting recap will now include video-based recaps. Video recap creates narrated video highlights from recorded meetings, featuring key takeaways and short clips that showcase important moments.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558540","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-537280","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage Event Broadcast, Meetings and custom events with moderated feed, annoynmous posting on web & mobile","desc":"Enhancing the Engage Events experience with additional capabilities such as Broadcast for large scale produced events, Meetings based Events. Organizers will have additional support for moderating the posted questions and conversations, and attendees can post questions anonymously. An Events Landing page allows for attendees and organizers to have one place for the contiguous events experience of \"Before\", \"During\" and \"After\"","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537280","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-500696","title":"Microsoft Teams: New Organization chart in the Profile Card for Web and Desktop","desc":"With the new org chart users will not only be able to contextaulize a person, they will also be able to scroll through visited profiles, see a manager's reports counts, and more.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-21","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500696","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-542794","title":"Microsoft Teams: Create custom templates for immersive events in Microsoft Teams","desc":"This release brings the next evolution in immersive collaboration in Teams. Designed for creators and event organizers, these new capabilities empower users to create, manage, and use immersive templates for immersive events in Teams and save those templates to collections to use in future events—directly within the Teams Meet app. Users can save customized immersive events as reusable templates to an immersive collection, and share them with others by adding co-owners and members to collections.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-09","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-542789","title":"Microsoft Teams: Easily find unsent drafts","desc":"Use the Drafts quick view to easily find, edit, and send draft messages.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542789","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-518222","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): App Navigation Pane Update","desc":"The Microsoft 365 Copilot app now has a simpler, cleaner navigation. Key updates include an expanded chat history, quick actions to create new Notebooks and Agents, and intuitive feature grouping so users can find what they need faster and unlock more AI value.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518222","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-489231","title":"Microsoft Edge: Built-in PDF reader powered by Adobe engine","desc":"Microsoft Edge will launch the new version of the built-in PDF reader that's powered by Adobe’s PDF rendering engine. The new PDF reader ensures that there's no loss of functionality and delivers an enhanced PDF experience. This experience includes richer rendering, improved performance, strong security for PDF handling, and greater accessibility.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2026-05-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489231","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-562220","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Supercharge your workflows with computer use","desc":"Add resilient, AI-powered UI automation directly into your workflows with computer use tools. Makers can build reusable, goal-oriented automations that adapt dynamically to website or app changes, while admins maintain governance through access controls, hosted browser management, and environment-level permissions.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562220","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-561326","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot People Connectors introduces people data ingestions with differentiated access control","desc":"Copilot People Connector now supports importing people data with access controls into Microsoft 365. This release enables organizations to bring people data from external systems into Microsoft 365 along with associated access control lists (ACLs), ensuring Copilot respects existing permissions defined in source systems. The imported data can be scoped to specific individuals and groups, allowing Copilot to reason over people data while honoring access restrictions.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561326","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-562221","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Use MCP-compliant tools in agent workflows","desc":"Integrate proprietary systems, dynamic knowledge sources, and custom actions into your agentic workflows with MCP support, accelerating extensibility while preserving workflow reliability. This integration improves reuse across agents and workflows, reduces duplication of integrations, and embraces an emerging open and extensible agent ecosystem.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562221","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1311973","title":"PowerPoint for Mac: Create a presentation with Copilot directly from PowerPoint Home","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nWe’re improving how users get started with Copilot in PowerPoint for Windows by enabling presentation creation powered by Copilot directly from PowerPoint Home in the File menu. This update reduces friction at the start of the workflow, helping users move from idea to first draft faster without needing to open a new file.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560536.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in late May 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Users on PowerPoint for Mac\n\n• Users who are assigned a Microsoft Copilot license\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Users will find a new option on PowerPoint Home (File menu) to create a presentation using Copilot.\n\n• The experience is available immediately when PowerPoint is opened.\n\n• The feature is enabled by default for eligible users.\n\n• Existing Microsoft 365 and Copilot policies are respected; no admin configuration changes are required.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required.\n\n• Consider informing users about this new Copilot capability.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1311973","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202605},{"id":"mc-MC1311974","title":"PowerPoint for Windows: Create a presentation with Copilot directly from PowerPoint Home","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nWe’re improving how users get started with Copilot in PowerPoint for Windows by enabling presentation creation powered by Copilot directly from PowerPoint Home in the File menu. This update reduces friction at the start of the workflow, helping users move from idea to first draft faster without needing to open a new file.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 560694.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in late May 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Users on PowerPoint for Windows\n\n• Users who are assigned a Microsoft Copilot license\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Users will find a new option on PowerPoint Home (File menu) to create a presentation using Copilot.\n\n• The experience is available immediately when PowerPoint is opened.\n\n• The feature is enabled by default for eligible users.\n\n• Existing Microsoft 365 and Copilot policies are respected; no admin configuration changes are required.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No action is required.\n\n• Consider informing users about this new Copilot capability.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-05-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1311974","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-502519","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention: Expand protection to Copilot + PC devices for Recall snapshots through custom policies","desc":"Microsoft Purview Endpoint data loss prevention is expanding coverage to Copilot + PCs initially to support Recall snapshots and determining whether policies exist to prevent capture of windows containing restricted sensitivity labels and Sensitive information types (SITs). Purview admins will author Endpoint DLP custom policies to integrate with Windows Copilot + PC Recall setup by Intune admins for Copilot + PC devices exclusively.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502519","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-508527","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Search Matches on People's Department","desc":"Copilot Search can now match on a person's department, and you can find/lookup all people in a given department when searching the people source directly.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508527","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-547833","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Additional Diagnostics for Data Loss Prevention and Information Protection","desc":"The below diagnostics will help users understand which sensitive information exist in their document and what labels applied and what policies have been triggered: DLP SharePoint Diagnostics DLP EXO Diagnostics Auto labeling diagnostics for SPO/ODB","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-15","modified":"2026-05-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-562222","title":"Microsoft Copilot Studio: Invoke agents as workflow steps with the agent node","desc":"Add an agent node to your workflow to reason over data, call tools, and return a response, all within a single step. The agent node lets you embed reasoning directly into your workflow. This means fewer manual handoffs, faster processing times, and workflows that can handle nuanced decisions without additional development effort, helping teams automate more of their end-to-end processes and reduce operational overhead.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Copilot Studio"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-14","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=562222","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557552","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Enhancements to Data Security Triage Agent","desc":"Adding below enhancements to Data Security Triage Agent in MS Purview - Metadata supported Custom Instructions (DLP only) : Earlier the agent only supported custom instructions which are related to content (E.g. Focus on alerts related to financial information). Now we also support instructions related to metadata. (E.g. Focus on alerts related to financial information for user Adam in last 20 days) - Consolidated Agent settings : Earlier we had seperate controls for deployment configuration and triggers. We are now merging them into a single view as the settings can be altered anytime and it becomes easier for admins and analysts to change them from single view. - Support for alerts with Non content contains condition (DLP only) : Till now we were showing alerts generated from non-content contains conditions as unsupported. (E.g. Condition = RecipientDomainIs matches and triggers alert, alert is unsupported). Now we are bringing the alerts into triage capability and determining categorization for them also - Agent Identity : Now the Triage agent can be deployed with Agent's own identity generated in Microsoft Entra. There won't be a need to have the agent run using the user's identity who was setting up the agent. This provides cleaner audit capabilities.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557552","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-515945","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention for Microsoft 365 Copilot to safeguard prompts","desc":"We are expanding Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention for Microsoft 365 Copilot to safeguard prompts containing sensitive data. This real-time control helps organizations mitigate data leakage and oversharing risks by preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot, including pre-built agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot, from returning a response when prompts contain sensitive data or using that sensitive data for grounding in Microsoft 365 or the web.","products":["Microsoft Purview","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515945","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-398711","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Priva Privacy Management – Multicloud environments","desc":"Microsoft Priva Privacy Risk Management extends its overexposure policies into data contained in Azure SQL, Azure Data Lake Storage, and Amazon S3. Organizations can create privacy policies that specify which data sources, databases, or storage buckets are in scope and Priva will automatically notify data asset owners when matches are detected.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-05-30","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=398711","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"June CY2024"},{"id":"rm-511798","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Enhancements to variant limits and detection groups","desc":"Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management variant limit is being increased from 3 to 10 per indicator and an overall limit of 100 across all indicators. Along with this, the number of items in one detection group is being increased from 200 to 500.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-07","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511798","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-542187","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Triage agent in DLP is generally available worldwide","desc":"The Data Security Triage Agent creates an agent-managed alert queue that identifies and prioritizes the DLP and IRM alerts that pose the greatest risk to your organization. It delivers a summary and clear explanation for why each alert was prioritized, helping analysts focus on what matters most. For this GA release, we’re introducing expanded coverage (which also includes Endpoint DLP alerts as well as alerts that leverage Custom SITs (Sensitive Information Types)) and support for Entra Agent ID.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-05-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542187","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-561855","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Dynamic Tool Discovery for Declarative Agents and Federated Copilot Connectors","desc":"We're introducing dynamic tool discovery for declarative agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot. Developers can now add, update, or retire tools on their MCP servers without republishing the agent - so end users get the latest agent capabilities immediately, with no deployment cycle in between. Support for federated Copilot connectors will be a fast follow to declarative agents at a later stage. Dynamic tool discovery is backed by Microsoft's enterprise RAI and security protections, and customers retain full control over agent deployment and availability to users and groups.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-13","modified":"2026-05-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mobile","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-479755","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Self service for historical imports","desc":"This feature will introduce an alternative solution to the existing Advanced Configurations feature that allows an Admin to perform historical imports into the Viva Glint platform. This alternate reduces the number of needed files and offers a simplified user experience to bring historical data into Viva Glint.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-20","modified":"2026-05-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=479755","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-481518","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Admins will be able to define rules to automate agent lifecycle management.","desc":"Admins will have the ability to set up rules for various scenarios, such as - 1. Auto block risky agents. 2. Auto delete inactive agents. 3. Auto reassign ownerless agents to manager. . #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-28","modified":"2026-05-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481518","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-543239","title":"Microsoft Teams: Brand Impersonation Protection for Teams Calling","desc":"Identify if an external user is impersonating a brand commonly targeted by phishing attacks, during their initial contact with an enterprise user via Teams calling.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-01-08","modified":"2026-05-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543239","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558288","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Pay-as-you-go model for Other Generative AI apps indicators","desc":"Other AI apps will move to pay-as-you-go model. Microsoft Copilot experiences indicators can still be used for free even without subscription. To continue using Other AI apps indicators, please link an Azure subscription to Microsoft Purview to enable billing. Insider Risk Management indicators transitioning to a pay-as-you-go pricing model: “Entering risky prompt in Other AI apps”. This indicator is present in Policy indicators-> Generative AI apps -> Other AI apps Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. ​","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558288","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2027","gaSort":202703},{"id":"rm-503562","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Organizational Messages now supports Email messages","desc":"Organizational Messages now includes Email as a delivery channel, expanding beyond existing surfaces such as the Windows Taskbar, Windows Notifications, Windows Spotlight, and Teams Popovers.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503562","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-553214","title":"Microsoft 365: Modernized Access Denied Web Experience","desc":"We’re introducing a visual refresh of the Access Denied web experience across Microsoft 365, where users can request access to files, sites, and meeting recordings. This update features a modern Fluent design with new illustrations, animations, and clearer messaging to help users quickly gain confidence and seamlessly continue their collaboration.","products":["Microsoft 365","OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553214","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-537283","title":"Microsoft Edge: Microsoft Edge can now send work related browsing history to Copilot for more relevant work results when searching on M365 Copilot search","desc":"Microsoft Edge can now send IT admin selected work related browsing history to Copilot to improve search relevance. When a user searches for something on Copilot search, Copilot will also show results from browser history when relevant.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537283","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-537277","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.148 - Password affiliation service","desc":"Password autofill suggestions in Edge are currently based on top-level domain matching, which means the same credentials can be suggested on sites like account.microsoft.com and office.microsoft.com. With this feature, Edge groups related domains together across various desktop and mobile properties called affiliations. When a customer visits a URL, the Edge client will query the affiliations backend to obtain “affiliated groups” for that URL. The process involves sending a hash of the visited URLs to the service, which then returns a list of affiliated URLs and ensures that the relevant credentials will be displayed in the autofill suggestions across affiliated domains. Admins can control access to this feature using the PasswordManagerEnabled policy.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-18","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-560341","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.148 - Shadow AI","desc":"Currently admins can set Purview DLP policies to protect sensitive data from being sent to any Generative AI apps, users get blocked from sending their prompts to LLM when this is triggered and stops their workflow. This new add-on to the feature shows a new UI that will give users the option to be redirected to M365 Copilot which will open and navigate to this M365 Copilot tab and allow them to send the same prompt there.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560341","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-554933","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improved keyboard navigation and default line numbers in code blocks","desc":"Navigate code blocks more easily with improved keyboard controls and default line numbers. Set code language quickly and reference specific lines for improved collaboration and workflow.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554933","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-506748","title":"Microsoft Teams: Miracast support for Teams Rooms on Windows devices","desc":"In addition to Teams Cast and HDMI ingest; you are able to share wirelessly using Miracast with Teams Rooms on Windows devices including touch boards. Available in Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-07","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506748","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558688","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Add support of hyperlinks in warn & block toast messages for Edge browser","desc":"With this feature, data officers can now complete their coverage story by now embedding hyperlinks within toast messages for the Edge browser. When this rule is triggered, the end user will see a toast with a customized title and message with a hyperlink. This feature is useful when organizations need to direct users to a specific resource or a repository for more specific instruction (e.g. internal policy SharePoint site).","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-13","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558688","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557554","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – File Testing Against Sensitive Information Classifiers","desc":"A new feature will be introduced on the main Classification page, allowing users to test files against all available classifiers to identify the presence of sensitive information. Users will have the option to select a single classifier or run tests across all classifiers. This capability is designed to help users identify sensitive content within files and troubleshoot classification issues more efficiently.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557554","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-554926","title":"Microsoft Teams: Audio recap language expansion","desc":"Audio recap in Teams will begin supporting 8 new languages. These are (in alphabetical order) Chinese, variations across English, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Portuguese, and Spanish.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554926","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-516569","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot voice support in Word & PowerPoint.","desc":"Chat in Work and PowerPoint now supports voice. Users can talk and interact with Copilot to brainstorm ideas, create content, and analyze information. Same as text, voice understand documents, work and web context.","products":["PowerPoint","Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-05-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516569","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-561651","title":"Outlook: Export to PDF (preserving sensitivity labels)","desc":"Ability to create PDFs from email messages and preserve Sensitivity labels. This feature is accessible from File -> Open & Export -> Create PDF.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-05-08","modified":"2026-05-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561651","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"more":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/print-to-pdf-is-blocked-if-mandatory-labeling-is-enabled-328c575c-9db9-4879-953b-a5e176f61e78"},{"id":"rm-502875","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft Graph APIs for App & Agent Inventory and Details.","desc":"Microsoft 365 will introduce new Graph API endpoints designed to empower IT administrators and developers with robust programmatic access to app and agent management across Copilot, Teams, Outlook, and other MetaOS hosts. Key Features: • Inventory API: Retrieve a comprehensive inventory of all apps and agents within your tenant, with advanced filtering by type (1P, 3P, LOB, Shared), host (Copilot, Outlook, Teams, Office), last updated date, and more. This enables bulk management, compliance checks, and streamlined governance for large organizations. • Details API: Access detailed metadata for any specific app or agent, including availability, deployment status, supported hosts, creator information, version, sensitivity, categories, and capabilities (such as Graph connectors, knowledge sources, and plugin actions). This supports auditing, lifecycle management, and integration into existing IT workflows. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2026-05-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502875","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559261","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - DLM Retention support Microsoft Teams call logs","desc":"Microsoft Teams stores call logs in several persistent locations, such as CDR logs. Currently, these logs are retained indefinitely. However, regulatory requirements in various countries specify maximum retention periods for calling-related logs. This discrepancy creates a compliance gap, as the existing retention practices may not meet regulatory obligations. Additionally, tenant administrators may prefer to retain data for longer periods to improve the user experience. Therefore, this solution would help organizations ensure that Microsoft Teams remains compliant with regulatory mandates while also supporting evolving product features and business needs.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-05-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559261","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558438","title":"Microsoft Viva: Feature conversations to all network members","desc":"The featured conversation feature in public Viva Engage communities will include the option to feature a conversation to all network members or only to community members.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-11","modified":"2026-05-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558438","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-519572","title":"Universal Print: Scan with Universal Print","desc":"I can scan documents using my regular scanning capable multi-functional-printer and will get an email notification that my scan is ready to download.","products":["Universal Print"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-05-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=519572","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2027","gaSort":202706,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-552595","title":"Outlook: Draft, edit and format emails conversationally with Copilot in Outlook","desc":"In Outlook, Copilot now works side by side with users to draft, refine, and format emails conversationally, powered by the same agentic capabilities available in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-09","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552595","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559478","title":"PowerPoint: Create and Edit images with the model of your choice","desc":"You can now choose your preferred image model including OpenAI’s GPT Image, Black Forest Lab’s Flux and Microsoft’s MAI-Image and more, for smart, dynamic selection when creating or editing images with Copilot in PowerPoint, or when generating a new presentation or page.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-10","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559478","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-422725","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Microsoft Loop – Require Existing Microsoft 365 Group for New Loop workspaces","desc":"Ensure via optional IT admin policy that new shared Loop workspaces are connected to and managed by an existing Teams enabled Microsoft 365 Group.","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-10-29","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422725","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-559027","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Endpoint DLP Device Status API","desc":"Provides access to the same device health details currently available through the export function on the device onboarding page. ​With the new device status API, customers can pull device-level information directly into their own BI tools, dashboards, and workflows, eliminating manual exports and making it easier to automate reporting at scale.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559027","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-482198","title":"Microsoft SharePoint: New web part for FAQs","desc":"After further review, we mistakenly marked the roadmap as \"launched.\" The correct status is In Development. We apologize the inconvenience. SharePoint FAQ web part help assist content owners keep their content fresh and relevant. Powered by Microsoft 365 Copilot, this new web part can help content owner easily curate FAQ by working with agents and connected grounding data. With a Human-in-the-Loop approach, it ensures high-quality, trustworthy FAQs—without the hassle. The result? A living FAQ that evolves with your organization's needs. Updated February 24, 2026: We previously marked this item as launched when it is still in Preview. We expect to move to GA later this year. We apologize for this inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-08","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482198","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-476487","title":"Microsoft Teams: CVI support for Townhall and Webinar presenters","desc":"Organizations that do not currently use Microsoft Teams can now seamlessly join and present within Teams Town halls using their own video conferencing devices (VTC). By integrating Cloud Video Interoperability (CVI) capabilities into the event form, organizers and presenters receive join codes for their tenant. CVI presenters who join the call will automatically join and interact with other users in the green room prior to the event starting. This capability ensures all participants can see each other (and see the meeting video) without any limitations, providing a seamless and inclusive experience for everyone involved.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-23","modified":"2026-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=476487","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-536573","title":"Microsoft Teams: Report a Suspicious Call in Microsoft Teams","desc":"Microsoft Teams now includes a capability that lets users flag calls they believe are unusual or suspicious. When a call is reported, the signal helps Microsoft strengthen security measures and reduce future unwanted or malicious call activity. This feature empowers users to actively contribute to real-time threat detection, enhancing organizational safety.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-05-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536573","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-494830","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Access Copilot Chat in your Microsoft 365 apps","desc":"Easily access Copilot Chat from the side pane in your Microsoft 365 apps with a commercial Microsoft 365 license or a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Excel","Word","PowerPoint","Outlook","OneNote"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-16","modified":"2026-05-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494830","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-558548","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – analyze files tied to audit log activities","desc":"Speed up analysis of exfiltrated content by launching Data Security Investigations (DSI) from Unified Audit Log activity. In DSI, build your audit log query by specifying criteria such as time range, activities, users, and keywords. DSI then automatically pulls the associated files into the investigation (for example, UserA downloaded a file on 3/1/2026).","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558548","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-496146","title":"Outlook: Data Loss Prevention (DLP) Policy Tips & Override for Outlook Mobile","desc":"Outlook Mobile now supports Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policy tips, helping users avoid accidental data leaks. When sensitive content is detected, users are alerted with inline tips or pop-ups, based on admin-configured rules. This update aligns DLP behavior across all Outlook clients for consistent compliance enforcement.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496146","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-511791","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Data Loss Prevention-Enforce DLP protection upon new content before its saved","desc":"Monitor or protect file with unsaved sensitive content from being printed or being moved to USB or network share.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557192","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention – Enable DLP Diagnostics for All Roles with Purview DLP Policy Access","desc":"We’re updating permissions to ensure that all roles with access to view DLP policies in Microsoft Purview can also run diagnostics on those policies. This change enhances visibility and empowers authorized users to troubleshoot and validate policy behavior more effectively. The following roles will now have diagnostic access: Organization Configuration View-Only Configuration Compliance Admin Security Admin Security Reader DLP Compliance Management View-Only DLP Compliance Management Insider Risk Management Admin Information Protection Admin Information Protection Analyst Information Protection Investigator Data Security AI Admin","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557192","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558546","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – role-based access simplification","desc":"We are simplifying Data Security Investigations (DSI) roles following customer feedback and the continued integration with Data Security Posture Management (DSPM), Insider Risk Management (IRM), and Defender XDR. We added the Data Security Investigation Admin role to the Compliance Administrator role group. We added the Data Security Investigation Contributor role to the: Organization Management role group; Data Security Management role group; Insider Risk management role group.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558546","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557590","title":"Microsoft Purview: File Creation/Modification conditions in DLP for Sharepoint/OneDrive and AutoLabelling","desc":"File Creation and File Modification conditions in Microsoft Purview DLP for SharePoint and OneDrive and AutoLabelling will give organizations more precise control over DLP policy definition. These conditions allow admins to configure policies based on when the files were created or last modified, enabling policies that target newly created documents, recently edited files, or older content that may require stricter governance. With these new date-based predicates, Purview DLP delivers stronger lifecycle-aware protection, improved policy accuracy, and greater flexibility in securing data across SPOD.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557590","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559481","title":"OneDrive: Discover Copilot actions in File Preview","desc":"See what Copilot can do the moment you preview a file in OneDrive or SharePoint. Ready-to-use prompts appear alongside the Copilot button, helping you summarize documents, generate FAQs, and more — all without writing a single prompt.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-26","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559481","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-551197","title":"Microsoft Viva: Enhanced AI governance for Glint Copilot","desc":"Copilot in Viva Glint will align with Microsoft's enterprise AI governance platform: enabling your IT and compliance teams to use centralized governance tools for access management and unified monitoring and reporting across all AI deployments in your tenant. This reduces governance complexity and audit burden by providing a single control plane for managing AI features across Microsoft 365. This change removes the existing Copilot toggles in the Viva Glint admin UI, making Viva Feature Access Management (VFAM) the single control plane for Copilot enablement.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551197","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-496150","title":"Microsoft Teams: Noise Suppression for Dial-In Participants in Teams Audio Conferences","desc":"Microsoft Teams will soon support noise suppression for dial-in participants. This feature automatically filters out background noise (e.g., traffic, typing) for users who join meetings via phone (PSTN). It enhances clarity and reduces distractions for all meeting participants. The feature will be rolled out gradually. However, if you'd like to enable it yourself, you will be able to do so via the Teams Admin Center: 1. Go to Meeting policy 2. Navigate to the Audio & video section 3. Set Noise suppression for dial-in participants to Enabled or programmatically with MicrosoftTeamsPowerShell by setting NoiseSuppressionForDialInParticipants setting inside of CsTeamsMeetingPolicy to \"Enabled\".","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-17","modified":"2026-05-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496150","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Developer","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-560322","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - review set limit increase","desc":"Review set limit per case is increased from 20 per case to 100 per case.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560322","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557180","title":"Microsoft Teams: Consecutive interpretation in Interpreter","desc":"Consecutive interpretation enables turn-based interpretation for everyone in the meeting. Interpretation happens after each speaker finishes talking, creating a turn-based flow that supports interactive discussions across two languages.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557180","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558858","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - review set limit increase","desc":"Review set limit per case is increased from 20 per case to 100 per case.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-17","modified":"2026-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557977","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Security Store now available within Purview DLP to browse, purchase, and enable partner integrations","desc":"Microsoft Security Store is now integrated into the Microsoft Purview DLP experience, giving admins an in‑product way to discover a curated set of integrations that extend Purview capabilities, including data security capabilities for the network. Purchasing and management are completed through Security Store, simplifying how organizations procure partner integrations.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557977","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-493757","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management- Multi selectable DLP policies as an IRM triggering event","desc":"Insider Risk Management is releasing the ability to select multiple Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies as triggering events in a policy. Previously, admins could only select one DLP policy as a triggering event within Insider Risk Management policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2026-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493757","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-551196","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Copilot configuration insights in the Copilot Dashboard Readiness page","desc":"The Copilot Dashboard’s updated Readiness page provides IT leaders with tailored Copilot configuration recommendations. Th suggested settings are meant to streamline deployment, enhance user experience, and help users get most out of Microsoft 365 Copilot, Copilot Chat and agents. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-28","modified":"2026-04-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551196","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-561025","title":"SharePoint: Power Automate trigger and action for forms in SharePoint","desc":"We are introducing new Power Automate integration capabilities for forms in SharePoint, enabling customers to create automated workflows based on responses collected using list forms, file upload forms, and document generation forms. With this update, a new trigger and action are now available in Power Automate: Trigger: When a form is submitted This operation triggers a flow when a list form, document generation form, or file upload form is submitted. Customers can use this trigger to initiate automated workflows such as approvals, notifications, or routing based on form submission events. Action: Get form metadata This action retrieves the metadata of a form, which includes the form ID, title, link, form type, output format, and the form questions used to collect information. This enables Power Automate flows to dynamically read form schema before executing downstream automation logic. Disclaimer: Document generation forms are part of AI in SharePoint Public Preview. Access to DocGen Forms capabilities may be limited to customers enrolled in the preview program. List forms and file upload forms are not part of the AI in SharePoint preview.","products":["Microsoft 365","Power Automate","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-29","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561025","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557277","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Available to Copilot Chat users (without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license).","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557276","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Available to Copilot Chat users (without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license).","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557276","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558443","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit with the model of your choice in PowerPoint","desc":"When create or edit a presentation with Copilot in PowerPoint, you can now select which model to use, including both Open AI and Anthropic models. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot–licensed users.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-09","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558443","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-511794","title":"OneNote: Copilot Notebook in OneNote iPhone and iPad","desc":"Users will be able to use Copilot Notebooks in OneNote on iPhone and iPad.","products":["OneNote"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-08","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-516575","title":"Outlook: Triage your inbox on-the-go with Copilot voice for Outlook mobile","desc":"Stay on top of your inbox with the new Copilot voice experience in the Outlook mobile app. Ask Copilot to summarize your recent unread emails and then take action like flagging, pinning, archiving, or marking as read – all without the hassle of navigating your inbox by hand. You can interrupt or redirect Copilot at any point in the conversation.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516575","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-548646","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Available to Copilot Chat users (without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license).","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548646","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-168843","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Recommended policy scope","desc":"Leverage policy scope insights to understand the aggregated volume of policy violations that are missed from users that are not currently scoped into the policy. Communication Compliance provides the tools to help organizations detect code of conduct and regulatory compliance violations, such as harassing or threatening language, sharing of adult content, and inappropriate sharing of sensitive information. Built with privacy by design, usernames are pseudonymized by default, role-based access controls are built in, investigators are opted in by an admin, and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-09-08","modified":"2026-04-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=168843","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-559111","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Additional meeting results in Copilot responses","desc":"Today, Copilot can show up to 25 meeting results, which can limit visibility in larger calendars. We’re expanding this limit so you can see more relevant meetings at once making it easier to find, review, and act on the full context you need.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-28","modified":"2026-04-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559111","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","Developer","iOS","Linux","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557976","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- New policy configuration options available for inline network and Edge for Business policies","desc":"Admins can now scope Purview collection policies for unmanaged cloud apps based on the presence of sensitivity labels, enabling more precise discovery of sensitive activity across inline network traffic and the Edge for Business browser. Purview DLP policies also support \"URL contains text\" as a condition and exception, providing finer control over unmanaged cloud app usage across the network and Edge for Business, along with configurable email notifications to alert end users when activities are blocked.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-04-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557976","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-516578","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery - Add Sample to Review Set","desc":"This feature allows users to add only a sampled subset of search results to a review set, rather than adding the entire query output. Users can configure sampling parameters—such as confidence level and sample size—to ensure the subset meets their review objectives while reducing unnecessary data ingestion.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-04-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516578","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-542792","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention-Endpoint DLP Device Status API","desc":"Provides access to the same device health details currently available through the export function on the device onboarding page. ​With the new device status API, customers can pull device-level information directly into their own BI tools, dashboards, and workflows, eliminating manual exports and making it easier to automate reporting at scale.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-16","modified":"2026-04-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542792","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-547831","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Enable watermarks for AI-generated content for M365 Copilot","desc":"Add watermarks for AI-generated video, audio, and image gen content.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-21","modified":"2026-04-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547831","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-561039","title":"SharePoint: Admin Center - Data Access Governance - Permission report for a given group","desc":"A single group with broad membership or a special group for vendors etc. - can expose sensitive content to unintended recipients. With this new report, SharePoint admins can now see every site a group can access and the extent of that access.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-27","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=561039","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-557371","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] IT Admins will be able to enable Anthropic models by specific users and groups in the tenant","desc":"This feature introduces admin controls for managing Anthropic as a model provider for specific users and groups in the tenant.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-18","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557371","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557187","title":"Microsoft Edge: Cross Tenant Support using Intune MAM","desc":"Edge for Business extends its capability to deliver Intune App Protection Policies via Intune MAM. Organizations are enabled to apply data loss prevention controls to Edge for Business profiles even on devices managed by another tenant. This capability enforces Intune MAM policies—such as clipboard boundaries, watermarking, and protected downloads—within the Edge work profile, ensuring sensitive data remains governed by your tenant. When enabled, downloads initiated in Edge are redirected to OneDrive for Business instead of local storage, and leak controls for screenshots and DevTools activate when data protection settings are applied. This approach secures cross-tenant scenarios like contractors or mergers without requiring additional apps or disrupting the end user experience.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557187","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-500381","title":"Microsoft Teams: Private channels increased limits and transition to group compliance","desc":"We are updating private channels to use a shared mailbox, similar to shared channels, instead of messages being stored in each user's mailbox. With this change, compliance policies set for the team's Microsoft 365 group will apply to private channels messages going forward. In addition, teams will support more than 30 private channels, up to the 1000 total channel limit for the team. Private channel member limits will increase from 250 to 5000. You will also be able to schedule meetings in private channels.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500381","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557716","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Phone user multi-line","desc":"Teams Phone user multi‑line gives callers more flexibility and control by allowing administrators to assign up to 10 phone numbers to a single user. With full support across Teams desktop, Teams mobile, and Teams devices, users can seamlessly make and receive calls from multiple numbers without switching accounts or hardware. This makes it easy to manage different roles, departments, or regional identities - all from one unified Teams experience. The result is a familiar, localized calling experience for users who work across diverse markets or with global customers.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557716","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-506751","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot chats conversations","desc":"Copilot Conversations as Search Results: Users can now retrieve historical Copilot interaction, including chats from notebooks, agents, and the main Copilot chat interface, directly in the search results (SERP). Dedicated Data Source in Right Rail: A new entry labeled “Copilot Chats” appears in the right rail, allowing users to scope their search specifically to Copilot-generated content. Scoped Query Formulation (QF) Suggestions: When users select “Copilot Chats” as the active data source, the search box dynamically offers scoped QF suggestions tailored to that source. These suggestions help differentiate between session recall and prompt execution, aligning with user intent.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506751","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-501452","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Video recap in Copilot Chat","desc":"Video recaps in Copilot Chat makes it easy to catch up on recorded meetings directly in Copilot Chat. It identifies and extracts key topics from transcripts, provides AI generated narration to summarize discussions, and pairs these with 20–40 second video snippets highlighting impactful moments of your meeting.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-10","modified":"2026-04-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501452","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-558257","title":"Microsoft Viva: Expanded published report recipients","desc":"This enables analysts to publish Viva Insights Power BI reports to anyone in their organization. Today, analysts can publish them only to people with Copilot Dashboard access.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-05","modified":"2026-04-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558257","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-497848","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Say \"Hey Copilot\" to activate voice conversations with the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on Windows","desc":"With the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on Windows, say “Hey Copilot” to activate real-time voice conversations with Copilot. The wake word keeps you in flow, helping you draft content, analyze data, and get critical insights without having to navigate to a separate app or window. Built for enterprise, it respects your organization’s compliance and privacy settings, activating only when called.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-08","modified":"2026-04-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497848","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-531910","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat in Outlook expands to reason over inbox, calendar, and enterprise data","desc":"Copilot Chat in Outlook expanding to support reasoning over a user's entire inbox, calendar and other enterprise data for Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat users (without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license).","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-04-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=531910","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-502854","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and OneNote for GCC-M","desc":"Easily access Copilot Chat from a side pane in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and OneNote. This is available for Copilot Chat users with a Microsoft 365 license and for Microsoft 365 Copilot licensed users.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-05","modified":"2026-04-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502854","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-559615","title":"Microsoft Agent 365: Registry sync","desc":"Connect to external AI platforms to discover agents created outside Microsoft and automatically sync them into the Agent 365 registry for more complete agent visibility and governance.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Agent 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-04-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559615","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560796","title":"SharePoint: File Actions in SharePoint","desc":"With AI in SharePoint, you can find, analyze, and organize files all from chat. SharePoint understands complex requests like \"rename these files by date\" or \"move old reports to an archive folder.\" It analyzes your library, suggests a plan, and executes it with your approval, saving you time and effort.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-23","modified":"2026-04-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560796","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557348","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Infinite Scroll Chat History","desc":"Infinite scroll enables users to continuously browse older chat sessions by automatically loading additional conversations as they scroll. This creates a smoother, more modern chat history experience","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-04-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557348","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-512432","title":"Planner: Task chat and mentions in basic plans","desc":"Task chat lets team members collaborate directly on tasks using rich text, formatting, and mentions - making it easier to discuss work and notify teammates on what needs attention. Updated April 23, 2026: We are still rolling out this feature. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Planner"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-04-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=512432","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-560549","title":"OneDrive: Sync Support for up to 1 million items on Windows","desc":"OneDrive Sync supports syncing up to 1 million items on Windows devices, helping teams manage large document libraries and shared content at scale without compromising access across devices. This preview requires the Insiders ring and that devices meet minimum hardware and configuration requirements. Devices that don't meet these requirements continue to sync at the existing 300,000-item supported limit with no disruption.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560549","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-560698","title":"Outlook: Multiselect events on calendar surface","desc":"Users can now multi-select events on calendar surface and perform bulk operations like open, copy -paste, delete & categorize in #newoutlookforwindows, similar to classic Outlook.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-22","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560698","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-554932","title":"Microsoft Teams: Backup RTMP Support for Teams town halls","desc":"Teams town halls will soon provide support for a backup RTMP stream to keep a live broadcast running in the event of an interruption with the main stream.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554932","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558111","title":"Microsoft Viva: Glint: AI-generated survey insights with Copilot Highlights","desc":"Copilot in Viva Glint now generates AI-powered summaries of employee survey results directly within Team Summary and Executive Summary reports, helping leaders quickly understand strengths, opportunities, and trends across their teams. Copilot Highlights surfaces key insights - such as notable score changes, benchmark comparisons, and response rate confidence - so leaders can move from data to action faster. With general availability, Copilot Highlights expands to support multilingual summaries, enabling global organizations to deliver AI-generated survey insights in their preferred language.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558111","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-552596","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Unified Plus menu (+)","desc":"We're simplifying the Input Box in Copilot Chat by bringing together various user actions under the Plus menu (+). The unified Plus menu (+) will continue to allow users to add content to prompts, while also letting them access tools/agents and manage data sources used to ground Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-03","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552596","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-503316","title":"Outlook: Summarize email with Copilot chat in Outlook","desc":"Easily summarize your email and attachments with Copilot chat. This will be available to Android and iOS users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license who have pinning enabled. Updated April 21, 2026: We have cancelled rollout of this feature to Desktop, Mac, Web and both Classic and New Outlook for Windows at this time. We apologize for the inconvenience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-12","modified":"2026-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503316","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-560596","title":"SharePoint: AI in SharePoint can generate code to translate your intent into reliable workflows","desc":"AI in SharePoint can now generate code which allows it to take what you ask and build the behind-the-scenes instructions or \"helper programs\" needed to actually do the work, like generating reports.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-21","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560596","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-485712","title":"Microsoft Teams: Streamlined Microsoft 365 Certified App Management in Teams Admin Center","desc":"This feature allows Microsoft 365 administrators to enable Microsoft 365 certified SaaS applications within their tenant through org-wide settings for third-party apps. Admins can choose to allow a subset of applications that have already been verified against industry security and compliance standards. This ensures organizations can confidently adopt apps while maintaining governance and reducing approval overhead.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-21","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485712","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-555873","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): ): Create presentations with Work IQ using Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"Now with Agent Mode in PowerPoint, you can create presentations based on your Work IQ. Build rich presentations without the heavy lift of finding all the right files, meetings, and emails to compose relevant slides.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555873","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555876","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create executive summary slides with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"Generate an Executive Summary slide for your presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint. Copilot delivers a polished draft that highlights your key points and provides a clear, executive ready summary.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555876","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555877","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create executive summary slides with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"Generate an Executive Summary slide for your presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint. Copilot delivers a polished draft that highlights your key points and provides a clear, executive ready summary.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555877","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555875","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create executive summary slides with Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"Generate an Executive Summary slide for your presentation with Agent Mode in PowerPoint. Copilot delivers a polished draft that highlights your key points and provides a clear, executive ready summary.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555875","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555874","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create presentations with Work IQ using Agent Mode in Copilot in PowerPoint","desc":"Now with Agent Mode in Copilot in PowerPoint, you can create presentations based on your Work IQ. Build rich presentations without the heavy lift of finding all the right files, meetings, and emails to compose relevant slides.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555874","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555872","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create presentations with Work IQ using Agent Mode in PowerPoint","desc":"Now with Agent Mode in PowerPoint, you can create presentations based on your Work IQ. Build rich presentations without the heavy lift of finding all the right files, meetings, and emails to compose relevant slides.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-11","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555872","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-555239","title":"Microsoft Teams: Annotations on Teams Single Window Sharing on Windows OS","desc":"Presenters can now share a single application window and enable participants to annotate directly on top of that content, without exposing their entire desktop. This means cleaner presentations, protected privacy, and more engaging discussions across training sessions, workshops, and client meetings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555239","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-506750","title":"Microsoft Teams: Voice and Face Enrollment Dashboard for Admins","desc":"Admins now have visibility and insight for voice and facial profile enrollments through a dashboard in the Teams Admin Center (TAC). Voice and face profiles are critical for supporting AI-enhanced meeting experiences for users across the organization. The dashboard provides metrics on enrollments over time.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506750","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-528930","title":"Microsoft Teams: Resizable Gallery in Teams Meetings","desc":"Resize the video gallery in Teams meetings to see more people when content is being shared","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=528930","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-382633","title":"Exchange: High Volume Email for Microsoft 365","desc":"High Volume Email is a new service for line of business applications and other high-volume SMTP scenarios that enables you to send internal messages beyond the current limits of Exchange Online.","products":["Exchange"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-02-15","modified":"2026-04-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=382633","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"April CY2024"},{"id":"rm-560533","title":"Outlook: Save calendar events as .ics","desc":"Users can now save calendar events as .ics in #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-17","modified":"2026-04-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560533","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-553217","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Posture Management for AI: Fabric integration in Data Risk Assessment","desc":"Within Purview's Data Security Posture Management (preview), Data Risk Assessment now supports scanning all Fabric workspaces for potentially overshared Fabric data (dashboards, reports, etc.). The new Fabric tab in Data Risk Assessment allows users to view default assessment results, create custom assessments for scoped Fabric workspaces, and take proactive actions to secure your Fabric data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-04-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553217","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-560329","title":"OneDrive: Improved finding and browsing document libraries on iPhone and iPad","desc":"OneDrive now makes it easier to find and access your SharePoint document libraries on your iPhone and iPad. Search for libraries by name, browse an updated Libraries view with recent and alphabetical sorting, and navigate directly to the site's default document library for ease of access. Whether you're on the go or working remotely, you can quickly locate and open organizational content that matters to you.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-04-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560329","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"mc-MC1282571","title":"Copilot entry point changes in Excel","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nWe’re updating how users access Copilot in Excel to provide a clearer, more consistent, and more intuitive experience across Microsoft 365 apps. These changes consolidate multiple Copilot entry points into a single, predictable location and establish Excel Edit Mode in the right-side chat pane as the primary Copilot interface. This update improves discoverability, simplifies user workflows, and aligns the Excel Copilot experience with other Microsoft 365 applications.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): Rollout begins in late April 2026 and is expected to complete by early June 2026.\n\n• General Availability (GCC, GCC High, and DoD): Rollout begins in early October 2026 and is expected to complete by late October 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• All users of Microsoft 365 apps for Excel on Windows, macOS, and the web with Copilot enabled.\n• A Microsoft 365 Copilot (Premium) license is required to use this feature.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Some Copilot entry points that appear when selecting a cell or opening the right-click menu will be removed.\n\n• A single, consolidated Copilot entry point will appear in a consistent corner location within Excel.\nScreenshot: Updated Excel entry point:\n\n• The Excel Agent in the right-side chat pane becomes the primary interface for Copilot prompts and responses.\n\n• Copilot availability, licensing, and existing admin policies remain unchanged.\n\n• The feature is on by default for users who already have Copilot access.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\nNo action is required.\nYou may optionally:\n\n• Inform users about the updated Copilot entry points and chat-based experience in Excel.\n\n• Update internal documentation or training materials if you reference specific Copilot buttons or menus.\n\n• Notify helpdesk teams to prepare for user questions during rollout.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nCompliance area\nExplanation\n\nDoes the change provide end users a new way of interacting with generative AI?\nUsers will primarily interact with Copilot through the right-side chat pane instead of multiple in-context entry points within Excel.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps","Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-04-16","modified":"2026-04-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1282571","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202604},{"id":"mc-MC1225192","title":"Microsoft Entra ID Governance: Azure subscription required to continue using guest governance features","desc":"Introduction\n\nBeginning January 30, 2026, Microsoft Entra ID Governance will require all tenants to have a linked Azure subscription to continue using Identity Governance features for guest users. This change ensures accurate billing for governance actions performed by guests and supports continued access to advanced governance capabilities.\n\nWhen this will happen:\n\nGeneral availability and enforcement begin on January 30, 2026.\n\nHow this will affect your organization:\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft Entra ID Governance features for guest users (userType = Guest).\n\n• Admins managing lifecycle workflows or Entra ID Governance features in entitlement management for external or guest identities. Access reviews will be included by March 31, 2026.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• If your tenant does not have a linked Azure subscription, creation or updates of policies scoped to guest users using premium Entra ID Governance capabilities will be blocked.\n• The following actions will be unavailable:\n\n• Creating access reviews scoped to guest users (inactive user reviews, user-to-group affiliation helper)\n\n• Creating or updating entitlement management policies involving guests, sponsor approvers, custom extensions, Verified ID, or auto-assignment rules\n\n• Marking a guest as governed in entitlement management\n\n• Directly assigning a guest user to an access package in entitlement management\n\n• Creating or updating lifecycle workflows scoped to guest users.\n\n• Existing policies will continue to run, but no new guest-governance actions can be authored without billing enabled.\n• Once a subscription is linked, normal guest governance usage and billing will begin under the Monthly Active User (MAU) model.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n\n• Before January 30, 2026, link a valid Azure subscription to your tenant:\n\n• Navigate to Entra ID → ID Governance → Dashboard\n• In the Guest Access Governance panel, select Get Started\n• Choose a subscription and resource group, then select Turn on\n\n• Confirm your account has at least the Contributor role to enable subscription linking.\n• Review any guest-scoped workflows, reviews, or entitlement policies that may require updates after subscription linking.\n• Communicate this change to support teams or internal governance admins.\n• Update internal documentation regarding:\n\n• Guest governance prerequisites\n• Subscription dependency\n• Billing behavior for governance actions\n\nLearn more: Microsoft Entra ID Governance licensing for guest users | Microsoft Learn\n\nCompliance considerations:\n\nQuestion\nExplanation\n\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed, stored, or accessed?\nGuest-governance actions require a linked Azure subscription; creating or updating guest-scoped governance actions is blocked without subscription linkage.\n\nDoes the change modify admin controls?\nAdmins must link an Azure subscription to enable guest governance billing and can turn guest governance on or off in the Entra ID Governance dashboard.\n\nDoes the change allow a user or admin to enable or disable the feature?\nGuest governance features can be enabled or disabled through the Guest Governance panel in the Entra ID Governance dashboard.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-04-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1225192","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-115482","title":"Microsoft 365: Information Barriers (IB) upgrading from IB v1 to IB v2 with new capabilities","desc":"Information Barriers (IB) V2 brings new capabilities including larger segment scale support, multi-segment support, and flexible people discoverability etc. Existing IB v1 tenants require an upgrade to IB v2 to take advantage of these new capabilities. This roadmap item is intended only for all IB v1 customers. All other customers will get IB v2 capabilities when they enable IB in their tenants. IB v2 upgrade will be opt-in.","products":["Exchange","Microsoft Teams","OneDrive","SharePoint","Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-01-31","modified":"2026-04-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=115482","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-560330","title":"OneDrive: Improved Shared file experience on iPhone and iPad","desc":"The OneDrive Shared view on iPhone and iPad now features a streamlined two-tab layout. The \"With you\" tab shows files others have shared with you, while the \"By you\" tab displays files you've shared. Quickly find shared content with new sorting options and file type filters, plus see recent sharing and editing activity at a glance.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-04-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560330","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-501581","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Dashboard - Broader access to M365 Copilot Chat insights","desc":"Microsoft Viva is expanding access to M365 Copilot Chat Insights in Microsoft Copilot Dashboard by enabling tenants with 1-49 M365 Copilot licenses- allowing more tenants, including those with fewer licenses, to track adoption trends. Insights will include usage over time, group level adoption, retention, app-level breakdowns, retention, and more. Users can filter by organizational attributes to uncover usage patterns.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2026-04-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501581","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-542186","title":"Outlook: Prepare for meetings with Copilot in classic Outlook for Windows","desc":"With so many of us in back-to-back meetings, it can be a real struggle to stay on top of pre-reads, action items, and even what each meeting is about. Copilot quickly prepares you for meetings within minutes by bringing real-time insights and summarizing relevant context, tasks, documents, and other resources. You can also chat directly with Copilot to prepare more deeply, to ensure you're ready to go. This feature is already available in the new Outlook for Windows, Web, Mac, and Mobile and is now being adding to classic Outlook for Windows. It is only available for users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-16","modified":"2026-04-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542186","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-542185","title":"Outlook: Scheduling with Copilot chat in classic Outlook for Windows","desc":"Users can now schedule meetings directly from chat or by clicking \"Schedule with Copilot\" in the UI. Simply ask Copilot to schedule a meeting with colleagues, and it will find available times, book rooms, draft agendas, and send invites—all within the chat experience. This feature is available to users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-04-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542185","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559108","title":"Microsoft Viva: [Engage] More for you feed when opening posts","desc":"When viewing Engage notifications from the Teams Activity app, users will also see other trending posts in their organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-14","modified":"2026-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559108","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-558342","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection– Override manually applied labels and Remove labels with Auto-labeling","desc":"New enhancements for SharePoint and OneDrive enable organizations to automatically override manually applied sensitivity labels and remove labels at scale on Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and PDF files. These capabilities help ensure data remains correctly classified as policies, labels, and business requirements evolve—reducing reliance on manual user updates and improving consistency for data at rest across Microsoft 365.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-06","modified":"2026-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558342","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557680","title":"Outlook: One-step folder sharing","desc":"Today, sharing a folder requires manually sharing each parent folder in the hierarchy. Outlook will simplify this by allowing users to share a folder in a single step, automatically applying the required permissions to its parent folders. Before sharing, users will clearly see which folders (including parent folders) will be shared. This removes manual effort while keeping users informed and in control.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557680","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557349","title":"Outlook: Improved results when filtering your message list","desc":"When you apply a filter in the message list, Outlook for iOS now helps you search for all matching messages—even older ones that aren’t currently synced. If more results may be available, you can tap to run a search with the filter already applied.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557349","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-489826","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): See a summary from Copilot of the latest changes and comments in the Word, Excel, and PowerPoint backstage view.","desc":"Use Copilot in the backstage view, accessible from the tile tab or start menu, to see a summary of the latest changes and comments made to your Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files before opening them.","products":["Excel","Word","PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489826","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-500865","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Rich Bing web answer cards on M365 Copilot","desc":"M365 Copilot will be showing the rich and interactive Bing web answer cards like Weather, Stocks etc. to relevant queries to enrich the responses.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-25","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500865","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"mc-MC1278920","title":"Support for Office LTSC 2021, and additional apps will end on October 13, 2026","desc":"As previously communicated, support for Office LTSC 2021 will end on October 13, 2026. After that date, no further updates, security fixes, or technical support will be available for this version of Office. While the applications may continue to function, using unsupported software could lead to potential security risks, compliance risks, system incompatibilities, and other issues.\nSupport for Visio LTSC 2021 and Microsoft Project LTSC 2021 and several other products will also end on October 13, 2026. Organizations using these products should upgrade as soon as possible to maintain security, compliance, and performance.\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nAfter end of support, Office LTSC 2021 suites and standalones will no longer receive security updates or other fixes, and no technical assistance will be available for devices still running them. Continuing to use unsupported software can expose your organization to security and compliance risks and may impact service reliability and performance.\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\n\nTo mitigate these risks while maintaining access to desktop Office apps, we recommend upgrading devices to a Microsoft 365 or Office 365 suite that includes Microsoft 365 Apps (for enterprise or for business). Microsoft 365 Apps provides always-up-to-date versions of familiar apps like Word, Excel, and PowerPoint for desktop, mobile, and web with continuous support under the Modern Lifecycle Policy and is eligible for use with the Microsoft 365 Copilot add-on.\n• Enterprises should look to Microsoft 365 E3, Office 365 E3, or Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise.\n• Organizations with fewer than 300 users should look to Microsoft 365 Business Premium, Microsoft 365 Business Standard, or Microsoft 365 Apps for business.\n\nFor scenarios that require a fully disconnected solution, we recommend upgrading to Office LTSC 2024. Office LTSC 2024 includes a subset of the value in Microsoft 365 Apps and will be supported until October 2029 under the Fixed Lifecycle Policy.\nTake steps to prepare for this transition with the following resources:\n\n• Read the upgrade guidance for an overview of how to move from Office LTSC 2021 to Microsoft 365 Apps.\n\n• Consider engaging Microsoft FastTrack, a Microsoft support service, for moving to Microsoft 365.\n\nPlan ahead to avoid potential disruptions and keep your organization’s software environment secure and up to date.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-13","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1278920","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-498548","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Generative-AI skills for Create in Microsoft 365 Copilot app for Government Clouds","desc":"Design and edit images, posters, banners, infographics, text drafts, and forms with Copilot—align them to your brand using kits built by you or your team.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-26","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498548","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-554928","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Researcher Agent for GCC","desc":"Researcher will be available for Microsoft 365 business and enterprise users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot add-on license. Researcher is an advanced deep reasoning agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot designed to tackle complex, multi-step tasks by acting as a deep research assistant.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554928","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-520388","title":"Microsoft Purviewl: Data Lifecycle Management – Separate Retention policies for Copilots and AI Apps","desc":"Enable admins to configure retention policies for various Copilots and AI Apps.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=520388","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-557674","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics: Copilot adoption PBI version update including Power user insights.","desc":"The updated Copilot adoption Power BI report will come with a streamlined UX and new Power user insights.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557674","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-498323","title":"Microsoft Viva: Unread News Notifications in Connections","desc":"After further review, this has been delayed to a later date. We apologize for any inconvenience. Users will receive a weekly notification in the Connections apps in Microsoft Teams on mobile and desktop linking them to relevant SharePoint news that they might have missed in the preceding week. This unread news will be available in the \"News\" tab in the Connections app under the \"unread\" pill.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-10","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498323","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-490052","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Intelligent meeting recap can summarize content shared on screen","desc":"Intelligent meeting recap can incorporate content shared on screen in the AI-based summary provided after the meeting, providing a richer and more comprehensive recap of the meeting. It captures details that are shown when a participant shares their screen, ensuring those unspoken insights become part of the meeting recap.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-06","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490052","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-516042","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updated Copilot Notebooks UX","desc":"Users will find an updated, streamlined UX flow within Copilot Notebooks.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516042","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-552591","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Upload Local Files now Support .eml and .msg file types","desc":"Users will now be able to upload .eml and .msg files and share it as context with Copilot Chat and M365 Copilot App.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-28","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552591","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-406948","title":"Outlook: Replace quick compose pop-up with inline appointment creation in new Outlook for Windows and web","desc":"Following further review, this feature continues in development. We apologize for any inconvenience. When single clicking on an empty time slot on the calendar surface, the quick compose pop-up will no longer be shown - instead, you will be able to create an appointment by typing directly in the time slot on the calendar grid, just as you can in classic Outlook for Windows. There will be no change to double click behavior, the full compose form will still open as it does today. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-07-16","modified":"2026-04-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=406948","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-559479","title":"PowerPoint: Create and Edit images with the model of your choice","desc":"You can now choose your preferred image model including OpenAI’s GPT Image, Flux, or Auto for smart, dynamic selection when creating or editing images with Copilot in PowerPoint, or when generating a new presentation or page.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-10","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559479","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-532722","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage community membership management in Teams for iOS & Android","desc":"Community admins will be able to add and remove members from their communities.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532722","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-511812","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage Event Analytics","desc":"New analytics experiences available that complement the new Viva Engage Events.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-10","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511812","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-537270","title":"Microsoft Viva: Experts & verified answers in communities in Engage and Teams for iOS & Android","desc":"In the Engage app for Android and Engage app in Teams for iOS and Android, we are introducing the Community Expert. Experts will be able to endorse accurate and credible answers and be recognized as community experts with a special label next to their name. As well, experts & community admins will be able to mark answers to questions as verified answers to signal a credible and accurate answer. Verified answers will receive its own special label.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537270","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557947","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Share agents to Teams","desc":"With this feature, users will be able to share their agent with a Microsoft Teams team. Users can search for and find teams in the agent sharing dialog box. Users can also send a notification to the main channel of that team to make members aware of an agent being shared with them, and as an easy way to install and start using the agent.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557947","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-554939","title":"Outlook: Expand to Full Event Details on iPad","desc":"When viewing your calendar on iPad, you can now expand an event to a full‑screen view, giving you more space to review information and make edits.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554939","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-503104","title":"Microsoft Teams: Camera view switching in multi-camera Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"When in a meeting with another Teams Rooms on Windows that has multiple cameras, you can switch camera views in that room via the participant panel on the console, or video tile on a touch board, to optimize your views.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-17","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503104","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-500395","title":"Outlook: See progress when running rules manually in the new Outlook for Windows and Web","desc":"When you choose “Run Rule Now” in Outlook, you’ll now see a visual progress indicator in both the message list and the rules page, showing that the rule is actively being applied. This helps confirm the action is in progress especially for large mailboxes, so you’re not left wondering if anything is happening. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500395","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-497418","title":"Outlook: Expand and collapse folders when moving emails","desc":"Users can now expand and collapse folder trees in the move/copy email dialog. This makes it easier to navigate large folder structures and find the right destination faster, improving efficiency and control during email triage. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-25","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497418","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-493949","title":"Microsoft Viva: Organizers reply privately to individuals","desc":"Allows Engage event organizers to answer questions from specific attendees without displaying the reply to the other participants. This capability can be helpful for sensitive questions, personal inquiries, or follow-up discussions that are not intended to be broadcast to the entire audience.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-14","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493949","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-492983","title":"Microsoft Viva: Allow/disable reactions in Engage events","desc":"Organizers can now disable reactions in Engage events. When this setting is turned off, attendees won’t see or be able to use reactions on questions, discussions or comments. Organizers can manage this option under additional settings in the event creation/edit page.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492983","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-492626","title":"Microsoft Viva: Anonymous comments in Engage events","desc":"Organizers & attendees can now post comments anonymously during Engage events—just like anonymous questions. When enabled by the organizer, these comments are fully anonymous in the UI and compliance systems, helping foster open, honest conversations. Look for the “Comment anonymously” toggle when posting to protect your identity and encourage authentic engagement.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-08","modified":"2026-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492626","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-117569","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: eDiscovery (Premium) - CMK (Customer Managed Keys) encryption support for data at-rest in Review sets","desc":"This release of eDiscovery features the implementation of customer-managed key (CMK) options, allowing users to manage their own encryption keys for the data stored in eDiscovery review sets in addition to the default, strong Microsoft-managed encryption already in place.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-03-15","modified":"2026-04-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=117569","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2027","gaSort":202702,"preview":"December CY2026"},{"id":"rm-554935","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Catalog – Advanced resource sets","desc":"Logical grouping of files with same schema and are under the same folder into a single file known as resource set. Using advanced resource set capability, customers can define pattern rules that will help group files based on custom patterns.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-04-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554935","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557548","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Pay-as-you-go model for Other Generative AI apps indicators","desc":"Other AI apps will move to pay-as-you-go model. Microsoft Copilot experiences indicators can still be used for free even without subscription. To continue using Other AI apps indicators, please link an Azure subscription to Microsoft Purview to enable billing. Insider Risk Management indicators transitioning to a pay-as-you-go pricing model: “Entering risky prompt in Other AI apps”. This indicator is present in Policy indicators-> Generative AI apps -> Other AI apps Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. ​","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-04-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557548","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558253","title":"Windows 365: Windows 365 Link - Market Expansion","desc":"Windows 365 Link will be available for sale in Norway","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558253","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-560056","title":"Outlook: Upgraded Video and Audio Player for iOS","desc":"Preview videos and audio files with an improved player directly in the Outlook iOS mobile app. The enhanced player provides updated controls and a smoother playback experience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-04-08","modified":"2026-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=560056","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-557188","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Hard delete capability for OneDrive and SharePoint through secure priority cleanup workflows","desc":"Admins will be able to select hard delete configuration while setting up a priority cleanup policy for OneDrive and SharePoint content and skip recycle bins.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557188","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-486826","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Enhancements to global exclusions in IRM settings","desc":"In this update, we are making the below enhancements to IRM exclusions to reduce alert noise. 1. Keyword logic update for email - An email will be excluded from scoring only when all the attachments match the keyword exclusions or email subject matches the keyword exclusions. This will be helpful to reduce the email signature noise which commonly contains keyword \"image\". 2. Keyword exclusions on both target and source file paths - For signals like file copied to removable media, keyword exclusions apply on both target and source file paths. 3. File path exclusions for removable media - We will start supporting file path exclusions for removable media. 4. Exclusion support for browser - Domain exclusions are now supported for browsing indicators. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-31","modified":"2026-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486826","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-495468","title":"Outlook: Show teammates' calendars in the left navigation pane","desc":"Users can now see their teammates' calendars (including peers, direct reports, and managers) automatically displayed in the left navigation pane of the new outlook. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-04","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495468","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558109","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing new soft purge mitigation action","desc":"A new Data Security Investigations (DSI) mitigation action, soft purge, is now available to help admins quickly and efficiently soft-delete sensitive or overshared content during investigations. Content deleted using soft purge is retained until the deleted item retention period expires, allowing admins to have further control of their data. This addition works alongside DSI’s AI-powered content analysis features, such as categorization, AI search, and examination for risk, which help surface data security risks buried in data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-04","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558109","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-558856","title":"Microsoft Teams: Attendee capacity packs for Teams events","desc":"Attendee capacity packs provide increased capacity limits for Teams events. Organizers can scale event attendance beyond base limits while maintaining a consistent Teams events experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-20","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557177","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot connects to your brand kit so you can apply branded templates, insert brand‑approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot–licensed users.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557177","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-499655","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot connects to your brand kit so you can apply branded templates, insert brand‑approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot–licensed users.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499655","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-552588","title":"Microsoft Teams: People Skills on the profile card expanding to Teams","desc":"Access to People Skills on the Microsoft 365 profile card is expanding to Microsoft Teams. With this update, employees will be able to view skills directly on the profile card in Teams—making it easier to learn about colleagues, build meaningful connections, and manage their own skills profile right from within their everyday flow of work.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552588","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-526794","title":"SharePoint: Site Branding Governance via PowerShell","desc":"Empower tenant admins to centrally manage SharePoint site branding using PowerShell scripts. This feature enables organizations to enforce consistent branding, apply enterprise themes to individual sites, disable custom branding on specific sites, and audit branding changes - ensuring branding compliance and a unified brand experience across all SharePoint sites.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-13","modified":"2026-04-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526794","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-410247","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention - Optical Character Recognition (OCR) on Mac Endpoints","desc":"Purview policies like Data loss prevention (DLP) auto labelling can scan for sensitive content in most of the textual files, but images are not supported for content scanning today on Mac endpoint devices. We are adding OCR support on Mac endpoints to detect sensitive content in images and apply policies to protect these images.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-08-13","modified":"2026-04-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=410247","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2027","gaSort":202701},{"id":"rm-558543","title":"Microsoft Teams: Spoken language detection is now automatic","desc":"Spoken language detection is now fully automatic. Teams will automatically detect each speaker’s spoken language and update it in real time as the conversation evolves. Manual spoken language selection will no longer be available. This applies to both live captions and transcripts when Interpreter is enabled or when multilingual speech recognition is turned on in meeting options, helping deliver more accurate language recognition and a more consistent multilingual meeting experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-04-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558543","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-495467","title":"Outlook: Insert Graphic","desc":"When composing a message in the new Outlook for Windows and Outlook on the web, there will be a new Graphics button under the Insert ribbon tab. This opens a panel that will allow users to search and pick from a large selection of emoji, stock photos, and stickers, which are inserted into the message when selected. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-29","modified":"2026-04-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495467","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-532733","title":"Outlook: Draft emails using saved email snippets with Quick Parts for Outlook for Windows and web","desc":"Drafting emails is faster and easier with Quick Parts, now available for Outlook for Windows and web. Quick Parts are saved email snippets that can be reused when composing new messages, making it easy to assemble messages with reusable parts. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-04-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532733","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-552593","title":"SharePoint: Dark mode support in SharePoint Admin Center","desc":"Dark mode will now be supported in SharePoint Admin Center.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-04-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552593","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-392456","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Bulk replacement or removal of a retention label","desc":"Admins can perform a bulk replacement or removal of a retention label using the Purview compliance portal. They can perform the action across the entire tenant or targeted to specific content using KQL and static or adaptive scopes.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-04-12","modified":"2026-04-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=392456","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-541831","title":"Microsoft Teams: Meeting Notes now available for instant meetings","desc":"Teams meeting Notes, powered by Loop, are now available for instant meetings that started via ‘Meet now’ from the calendar. Notes are Loop components in Teams meetings and chats that allow end users to co-create and collaborate on their meeting agenda, notes, and action items that can be co-authored and edited by everyone. Since Notes are Loop components, they stay in sync across all the places they have been shared. Once added, meeting notes can also be shared and edited in the Loop app in your web browser.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-16","modified":"2026-04-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=541831","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-512430","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Overview Page in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Users will find Copilot-powered Notebook summaries and insights as a landing page within their Copilot Notebook.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-08","modified":"2026-04-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=512430","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-516568","title":"Outlook: Prepare for your meeting with Copilot chat in Outlook mobile","desc":"Outlook mobile users can now prepare for their meetings using Copilot chat in a single tap. This feature requires a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-20","modified":"2026-04-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516568","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-519570","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Files found via Chat search can be now analyzed by code interpreter","desc":"Code interpreter runs on files you upload in your agent or that the user explicitly attaches in the interaction. Files that Copilot Chat finds via enterprise search can be now analyzed by code interpreter without the need to explicitly link or upload them.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-04-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=519570","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-501448","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Discover graph connector prompts in the Prompt Gallery when using Copilot Chat","desc":"Popular graph connector prompts will now be available in the Prompt Gallery for use in Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-04-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501448","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Linux","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-501585","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Admins can create and deploy custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) connectors across Microsoft 365.","desc":"Admins can create custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) connectors in the Microsoft 365 Admin Centre and deploy them across Microsoft 365. This will allow admins to surface their organization's custom data in Microsoft 365 Copilot via these MCP-based connectors.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-19","modified":"2026-04-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501585","source":"roadmap","phases":["Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-551147","title":"Microsoft Purview: Role Group changes in Purview","desc":"We are introducing a new Microsoft Purview RBAC role—Purview Agent Deployment—and adding it to various existing built in role groups used by analysts and admins across Purview. This change enables users who use built-in role analyst groups to deploy Security Copilot Agents in Purview without needing any additional roles. If your organization prefers to limit agent deployment permissions, you can create a custom role group that does not include the Purview Agent Deployment role and assign that custom role group to analysts who should not be able to deploy agents. This update does not change default data access or expand visibility into customer content. All other permissions within each role group remain unchanged. Analysts who are assigned to custom role groups will not be able to deploy agents unless the Purview Agent Deployment role is explicitly added to those custom groups. We recommend reviewing and updating your organization’s RBAC documentation, internal processes, or onboarding guides to reflect these change We recommend reviewing and updating your organization’s RBAC documentation, internal processes, or onboarding guides to reflect these changes.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-04","modified":"2026-04-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551147","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-481138","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Voice chat in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"Voice in Microsoft 365 Copilot brings a natural, hands-free conversational experience to your desktop and mobile devices – enabling you to talk to Copilot like a colleague, unlocking a faster, more intuitive way to work. Speak directly to M365 Copilot to search for information, catch up between meetings, brainstorm out loud, and do it all in multiple languages.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-06","modified":"2026-04-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481138","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"mc-MC1226444","title":"Power Platform admin center – Environments page updates","desc":"The Manage option in the Updates card and the label for release wave in the Updates card will be removed on February 3, 2026.\n\nHow does this affect me?\nThe Environments page in the Power Platform admin center will be updated, removing the Manage option and the label for release wave in the Updates card. When this change takes effect, a new link in the Updates card titled, \"Release Wave opt-in has moved!\" will be added. Your environment behavior is now dependent on the Release Channel settings.\n\nWhat action do I need to take?\nTo Opt in to early access updates, use the monthly release channel, as explained in Use a release channel.\n\nLearn more:• For more information about Release channels, please see the Release channel overview learn article.• For more information about how to determine dates and build numbers for April and October waves, please see the General availability deployment learn article.","products":["Power Platform"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-03","modified":"2026-04-01","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1226444","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-559022","title":"SharePoint: Lists as a knowledge source for agents in SharePoint and OneDrive","desc":"We’re introducing support for Microsoft Lists as a knowledge source for custom agents in SharePoint and OneDrive. These custom agents can now ground responses in a list stored on a SharePoint site or your OneDrive.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-04-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559022","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-537285","title":"SharePoint: OneNote usage inclusion in SharePoint site analytics","desc":"With this release, usage from OneNote files (.one) in SharePoint will be included in SharePoint site analytics metrices \"Unique viewers\" and \"Site visits\". You will also see OneNote files appear in the popular content section if a OneNote file is heavily used in the last 7 days. Refer to the more information link to learn more about the list of excluded file types.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-04-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537285","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"more":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/view-usage-data-for-your-sharepoint-site-2fa8ddc2-c4b3-4268-8d26-a772dc55779e"},{"id":"rm-558595","title":"Microsoft 365: Companion apps - Copilot prompts in the Files app now available for Copilot Chat users","desc":"The Files companion app, part of the Microsoft 365 companion apps suite on the Windows taskbar, now surfaces AI-powered Copilot file prompts for Copilot Chat users. Previously available only to Microsoft 365 Copilot licensees, this update extends contextual file prompts to Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat users, enabling them to discover and interact with relevant files through intelligent suggestions. Users can find their most relevant files faster and take action on them directly from the Files app.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-03-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558595","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-558289","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention– Enhanced content extraction and file type coverage for DLP on Mac devices","desc":"With this release, the file type coverage to scan, classify and protect sensitive content on Mac devices with Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention policies will increase from current ~40 file types to 100+ file types. This release will make the coverage of file types on endpoint consistent with other locations such as Exchange, SharePoint and OneDrive. This will also include other enhancements like detecting label from pfile, detecting sensitive content in metadata, and detecting sensitive content in PDF forms.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-03-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558289","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-548520","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document in PowerPoint","desc":"Copilot in PowerPoint lets you create, edit, and refine presentations through natural conversation, directly in your presentation. You can start a new presentation or build on an existing one, asking Copilot to generate slides, update content, improve layouts, and polish design—while preserving formatting, structure, and branding. Copilot connects to your brand kit so you can apply branded templates, insert brand‑approved images, and check for brand compliance. Available to Microsoft 365 Copilot–licensed users.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-15","modified":"2026-03-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548520","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-499654","title":"SharePoint: Updates to News page in SharePoint sites","desc":"The News page renders news items in a given site. It is typically accessed via the \"see all\" experience of a news web part. We are updating the user experience of this page and bringing in Copilot capabilities to licensed users. Updated February 9, 2026: GA rollout for this item is starting in late February. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-31","modified":"2026-03-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499654","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-394274","title":"Microsoft Teams: App centric management for app deployment in Teams Admin Center","desc":"App centric management for app deployment will introduce a new admin setting to control who in the tenant has specific Teams apps preinstalled. Similar to app assignments, admins will be able to select from three options: 'Deployed to all users', 'Deployed to specific users and groups', or 'Deployed to no users'. This feature replaces the existing Installed apps section of app setup policies and provides admins with the ability to manage app deployment individually. The Installed apps section of app setup policies for existing customers will be migrated to maintain existing admin settings in the tenant.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-04-24","modified":"2026-03-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=394274","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2024","gaSort":202407},{"id":"rm-558252","title":"Outlook: Multiple Intune Accounts for Outlook on iOS","desc":"Multiple MAM (Mobile Application Management) Intune Accounts will now be supported in Outlook for iOS. Only one MDM (mobile device management) account will be supported at a time per device.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-30","modified":"2026-03-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558252","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/dlp-exchange-conditions-and-actions#recipients"},{"id":"rm-485739","title":"Outlook: Import emails from PST file to mailbox in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to import emails from .pst file to mailbox. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-18","modified":"2026-03-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485739","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-492615","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Access audio overviews from the top of your Word document","desc":"Ask Copilot to generate an audio overview of your document from the Summary tab in the document snapshot. We have updated the status to accurately reflect the current state of the feature.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-07","modified":"2026-03-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492615","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-489822","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - Contextual nudges on address bar offering help summarizing webpages.","desc":"Microsoft Edge for Business plans to introduce an easy way for users to get summaries of their open page from the address bar using Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat. This feature seeks to help users more easily understand relevant content and save time.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2026-03-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489822","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"September CY2026"},{"id":"rm-559477","title":"PowerPoint: Create and Edit images with the model of your choice","desc":"You can now choose your preferred image model including OpenAI’s GPT Image, Flux, or Auto for smart, dynamic selection when creating or editing images with Copilot in PowerPoint, or when generating a new presentation or page.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-27","modified":"2026-03-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559477","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"mc-MC1240704","title":"(Updated) Copilot entry point changes in Word and handoff to Agent in chat","desc":"Updated March 27, 2026: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are updating the entry points for Copilot in Word to provide a clearer, more consistent, and more intuitive experience. These changes unify how users access Copilot and introduce Word Agent in the chat pane as the primary Copilot interface. This update improves discoverability, simplifies the user workflow, and creates consistency with other Microsoft 365 apps.\n[When this will happen]\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in early April 2026 (previously late March) and expect to complete by June 2026 (previously late April).\nGeneral Availability (GCC, GCCH and DoD): We will begin rolling out in October 2026 (previously late March) and expect to complete by late October 2026 (previously late April).\n[How this affects your organization]\nWho is affected\nAll users of Microsoft 365 apps for Word on Windows, macOS, and Web.\nWhat will happen\n• The existing Copilot entry point in the left margin will be replaced by a consolidated entry point positioned in a consistent corner location.\n• Users will see contextual Copilot entry points when selecting content:• Windows and Web: inside the selection floatie\n• Mac: in the right‑click context menu\n\n• Word Agent in the right-side chat pane becomes the primary Copilot experience for prompts and responses.\n• All Copilot entry points—consolidated and contextual—will connect to Word Agent to ensure a unified experience.\n• There is no change to admin configuration, policy behavior, or Copilot availability settings.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo action is required.\nYou may optionally:\n• Inform your users about the new Copilot access points and updated experience in Word.\n• Update internal help content or training materials if you document Copilot entry points.\n\n[Compliance considerations]\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-27","modified":"2026-03-27","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1240704","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-496655","title":"Microsoft Viva: Satisfaction Rate Metric for Microsoft 365 Copilot in Copilot Dashboard","desc":"Track user sentiment of Microsoft 365 Copilot. Understand how users perceive Copilot value by analyzing the breakdown of thumbs up and thumbs down ratings after Copilot interactions. See trends over time and breakdowns by group.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-02","modified":"2026-03-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496655","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-492625","title":"Microsoft Teams: share file in chat with external users","desc":"Collaborating with users outside your organization has become more streamlined. You can now share files and Loop components with external users in 1:1, group, and meeting chats. When sending a file or Loop component, it will be automatically provisioned to users in the chat, or you can change its permissions.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-09","modified":"2026-03-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492625","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-422501","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention – Restrict access action support for sematic models and lakehouses in Fabric","desc":"Your organization can now control who can access your data depending on the sensitive information detected in Fabric semantic models and lakehouses. DLP restrict access action allows you to block access to guest users or all users depending on what labels or sensitive information types matches your semantic models or lakehouses. This is in addition to the ability already supported by DLP policies to audit and notify users via Policy Tips based on sensitive content within Fabric semantic models and lakehouses.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-19","modified":"2026-03-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422501","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2024"},{"id":"rm-559389","title":"Outlook: View, edit & share Copilot Pages with Outlook for Android","desc":"Users can now view, edit and share Copilot Pages with Outlook for Android, making it easier to continue working with Copilot and colleagues while on the go.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-26","modified":"2026-03-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=559389","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-498916","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Information Protection - Admin unit scoping in Content Explorer and Data Explorer","desc":"This feature introduces Admin Unit scoping to both Content Explorer and Data Explorer, enabling more granular visibility and control over M365 data. It ensures that data exploration respects organizational boundaries defined by Admin Units, enhancing compliance and governance.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-23","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498916","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-464991","title":"Microsoft 365: Perform granular file-level restore using Microsoft 365 Backup","desc":"Perform file-level browse/search and then restore using Microsoft 365 Backup. With this enhancement you will be able to browse for files across in a site from available daily restore points and apply filters to narrow results, restore at the original location by overwriting existing content or to a new place by creating a copy of the content.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-10-29","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=464991","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557682","title":"SharePoint: Entra B2B integration for external sharing in OneDrive & SharePoint","desc":"OneDrive and SharePoint will use Microsoft Entra B2B as the invitation and authentication method for external users, replacing the legacy SharePoint One Time Passcode (SPO OTP) experience. External sharing will automatically create B2B guest accounts in your directory, delivering consistent external collaboration across Microsoft 365, stronger guest identity management, and modern security aligned with Microsoft Entra standards.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-25","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557682","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"May CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1181209","title":"(Updated) [Reminder] Microsoft Teams Premium Self-Service Trials (Originally announced in MC670435)","desc":"Updated March 25, 2026: We have updated the content. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\nWe are resurfacing MC670435, published September 2023 to remind admins of the Microsoft Teams Premium self-service trial capability. This message serves as a reminder as we begin a broader rollout of the feature announced in 2023. As we expand rollout and introduce additional entry points for this feature, we want to ensure continued awareness and readiness.\n\n[When this will happen:]\nOngoing rollout.\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nWhen rolled out, users within your organization will be able to directly initiate a Teams Premium trial. These self-service trial licenses will be a part of your Microsoft organizational tenant, and you will be able to manage these licenses like other Microsoft subscriptions. You will be able to cancel these trial licenses at any time.\nIf you choose to disable the self-serve trials, please refer to self-service trial controls. After disabling the policy, it may take between 24-72 hours for the trial entry point to be removed from Teams. We also recommend fully restarting the app (quit and relaunch) to ensure the change is reflected.\nYou will also be able to fully control whether trials are converted to paid subscriptions. Users will not need to input payment information when signing up. If a user would like to convert to a paid license, they must work with you directly to do so as there is no auto-renew functionality for these trials. If a user isn’t upgraded to a paid subscription, all services included in their Microsoft Teams Premium will end, and the user may lose read only access to data generated by Teams Premium, stored in Microsoft Teams, OneDrive, and SharePoint.\n\nUsers in tenants where self-service trials are disabled may still see the “Get Premium” prompt when accessing features that require a premium license. This is expected behavior and helps signal user interest to admins. It can also help identify which users in your organization may need a Teams Premium license, allowing you to better manage and allocate your available licenses. To reduce confusion and prevent users from submitting license requests, admins can customize the license request flow. Instead of showing the default request form, they can configure a custom message explaining that license requests are not supported in their organization. For setup instructions, see Use your own request process – Microsoft Learn.\nMicrosoft Teams Premium helps make your Teams meetings more intelligent, protected, and engaging. Unlike other meeting and collaboration tools, Teams Premium brings advanced capabilities for meetings, virtual appointments, and webinars together for one low cost. You can learn more about Teams Premium here.\nThe customer data for all services associated with the Microsoft Teams Premium trial will be handled in accordance with the Microsoft Online Subscription Agreement and the Product Terms.\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nGlobal or billing admins can use the same self-service purchase controls to disable self-service trials while making use of subscription management capabilities to oversee and manage trial licenses on the Your Products page in the Billing section of Microsoft 365 admin center.\nNote: This is a new Teams Premium trial and is enabled or disabled independently of past trial offerings.\nReview our updated self-service purchase and trial documentation here. We’ve added important information about the way trials work, the data that is collected, and the terms that apply.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-29","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1181209","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-526793","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Copilot settings – Optimize view","desc":"The new Copilot settings landing experience in the Microsoft 365 admin center centralizes visibility into key configuration status and helps admins optimize settings for Copilot success using Microsoft‑recommended policies, actions, and guidance—enabling secure and confident Copilot deployment.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-20","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526793","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-523202","title":"Microsoft Purview: DSPM data risk assessments: item-level investigation & remediation","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data risk assessments now support item-level investigation and remediation of SharePoint data. Item-level insights like sensitivity label and sharing links created help users identify potentially overshared items. Users are empowered to remediate overshared items by resolving, notifying, applying a sensitivity label, or removing sharing links for selected item(s). This helps organizations proactively reduce data exposure, strengthen compliance posture, and ensure sensitive data are only accessible to the right people.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523202","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-557555","title":"Microsoft Teams: Channel Agent Updates","desc":"Updates include dynamic, channel‑aware welcome messages, greater flexibility in channel creation (with or without an agent), expanded agent permissions for member management, scheduling enhancements, and overall quality improvements.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-24","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557555","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-551187","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Quickly edit an image in PowerPoint","desc":"Edit your images directly in PowerPoint with Copilot, no need to switch apps or interrupt your flow. Whether you're refining visuals for a pitch deck, enhancing marketing assets, or simply making your slides pop, the image editor makes it fast and seamless. You can make edits like improving the resolution, removing the background, and more.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-27","modified":"2026-03-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551187","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-481821","title":"Outlook: Copilot Pages – View, edit & share in Outlook Mobile","desc":"Continue working with Copilot and colleagues while on the go, with the ability to view, edit and share Pages on mobile.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481821","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-501107","title":"Microsoft Teams: Copilot Chat for Teams Chats, Channels, Calling and Meetings","desc":"Copilot Chat will soon be available for Teams chats, channels, calling and meetings.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-513283","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Egnyte to collaborate on secure file storage with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Egnyte to collaborate on secure file storage with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-13","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513283","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-169212","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Advanced trainable classifiers to detect workplace safety scenarios","desc":"New detections are being added to Communication Compliance that enables you to build safer online environments by detecting potential hate and violence then assigning severity scores to unsafe text across languages. These classifiers are built using large language models. Microsoft Purview Communication Compliance provides the tools to help organizations detect business conduct and regulatory compliance violations (e.g. SEC or FINRA), such as sensitive or confidential information, harassing or threatening language, and sharing of adult content. Built with privacy by design, usernames are pseudonymized by default, role-based access controls are built in, investigators are opted in by an admin, and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-09-06","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=169212","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-387500","title":"SharePoint: Pages - Heading levels for web parts","desc":"When authoring pages, this will create the ability to choose heading level for webparts to help define the hierarchy of information on a page.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-03-19","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=387500","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2024","gaSort":202404},{"id":"rm-184359","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Catch Up Improvements on Web","desc":"Catch Up allows you to stay in sync with your collaborators in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint by showing you the latest comment activity that is directed at you and a summary of recent changes. Based on your feedback, we made improvements to the Catch Up feature. The comment activity directed at you will now persist in Catch Up between sessions for up to 28 days. New items will be indicated with a blue dot for clarity. You can also dismiss items individually if you do not wish to keep them in Catch Up.","products":["Excel","PowerPoint","Word","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-10-27","modified":"2026-03-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=184359","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2024","gaSort":202401,"preview":"November CY2023"},{"id":"rm-490738","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: Usage reports - Message consumption for Pay-as-you-go experiences in Copilot Chat.","desc":"A new report to help IT admins manage costs for billed messages that are Pay-as-you-go enabled for Copilot Chat. Reporting includes drill down of billed messages per user, per billing policy, per agent-level and agent-user level pair. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2026-03-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490738","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609,"preview":"May CY2025"},{"id":"rm-558940","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create interactive visuals in Copilot Pages","desc":"Create an interactive report, visualization, or dashboard using Copilot Pages. Copilot uses web data and the latest LLM models and can also ground responses in your Work data.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-23","modified":"2026-03-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558940","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-508530","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Quickly edit an image in PowerPoint","desc":"Edit your images directly in PowerPoint with Copilot, no need to switch apps or interrupt your flow. Whether you're refining visuals for a pitch deck, enhancing marketing assets, or simply making your slides pop, the image editor makes it fast and seamless. You can make edits like improving the resolution, removing the background, and more.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-03-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508530","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501453","title":"Outlook: Multi-select capability for calendar categories","desc":"In #newoutlookforwindows, users can now apply more than one category to their calendar events from the event right-click context menu. Selected categories will be indicated with a check mark within this menu. This specific update is for applying multiple categories to an event.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-04","modified":"2026-03-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501453","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-485797","title":"SharePoint: Content Security Policy Control in Tenant Administration","desc":"SharePoint Online Tenant Administrators can now allow script sources for modern pages in SharePoint sites. This is particularly useful in scenarios where modern pages have custom code that load scripts (e.g. TypeScript code) from external sources like CDN. SharePoint will now report to administrators where are loaded from sources that have not been allowed giving administrators a way to identify those sources and take actions. Tenant Administrators can also enforce browsers to only load scripts from allowed sources. This behavior can be enabled using SharePoint Online Management Shell.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-10","modified":"2026-03-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485797","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"mc-MC1257999","title":"Microsoft Purview DLP: Unmanaged cloud app discovery and protection with Microsoft Purview and Palo Alto Prisma Access","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nMicrosoft Purview network data security now integrates with Palo Alto Prisma Access, extending discovery and protection to network traffic. With this integration, new and existing Palo Alto Prisma Access customers can configure Microsoft Purview collection and data loss prevention policies to discover and protect sensitive data shared with unmanaged cloud apps via HTTP/HTTPS, using the same classifiers, sensitive information types, and sensitivity labels used in other Purview policies. This integration also further enriches Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM), Insider Risk Management (IRM), enables data security & compliance for AI interactions, and more.\n\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 558939.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public preview: We will begin rolling out in mid-April 2026 and expect to complete by mid-May 2026.\n\n• General availability: We will begin rolling out in late October 2026 and expect to complete by late November 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft Purview.\n\n• Customers using or planning to use Palo Alto Prisma Access.\n\n• Microsoft 365 administrators managing Purview collection and DLP policies.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• The Palo Alto Prisma Access integration will automatically appear in the Purview DLP Security Store as the feature rolls out.\n\n• The integration is not enabled by default. Administrators must explicitly enable it before it can be used in policies.\n\n• Once enabled, administrators can use existing or new Purview collection and DLP policies to inspect and protect data detected through Palo Alto Prisma Access network traffic.\n\n• Existing network data security collection and DLP policies will automatically apply after the integration is enabled.\n\n• There is no impact to users unless administrators enable the integration and configure network data security policies in Microsoft Purview.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Confirm that Purview pay-as-you-go is enabled and configured for your tenant, as it is required to use this integration. Learn more: Enable Microsoft Purview pay-as-you-go features for new customers.\n\n• Review your existing Purview collection and DLP policies to identify where network-based data inspection may be appropriate.\n\n• Inform other data security and compliance administrators in your organization about this upcoming capability.\n\n• After rollout, enable the Palo Alto Prisma Access integration from the Purview DLP Security Store when you are ready to use it.\n\nLearn about Microsoft Purview Network Data Security\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nArea\n\nExplanation\n\nDoes the change alter how existing customer data is processed?\n\nNetwork traffic inspected by Palo Alto Prisma Access can be evaluated by Microsoft Purview DLP policies once the integration is enabled by an administrator.\n\nDoes the change modify Purview DLP policies or enforcement?\n\nExisting Purview DLP and network data security policies can be applied to network-based data flows through Palo Alto Prisma Access.\n\nDoes the change alter how admins can monitor or report on compliance activities?\n\nAdmins can monitor network-based data inspection and policy enforcement through existing Purview reporting and dashboards.\n\nDoes the change add an integration with third-party software?\n\nThis feature integrates Microsoft Purview with Palo Alto Prisma Access.\n\nDoes the change include an admin control?\n\nThe integration is disabled by default and must be explicitly enabled by administrators in the Purview DLP Security Store.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-21","modified":"2026-03-21","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1257999","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-558939","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Unmanaged cloud app discovery and protection with Microsoft Purview and Palo Alto Prisma Access","desc":"Microsoft Purview network data security now integrates with Palo Alto Prisma Access, extending discovery and protection to network traffic. With this integration, new and existing Palo Alto Prisma Access customers can configure Microsoft Purview collection and data loss prevention policies to discover and protect sensitive data shared with unmanaged cloud apps via HTTP/HTTPS, using the same classifiers, sensitive information types, and sensitivity labels used in other Purview policies. This integration further enriches Purview Data Security Posture Management (DSPM), Insider Risk Management (IRM), enables data security & compliance for AI interactions, and more.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-03-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558939","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2026","gaSort":202610,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-558936","title":"Outlook: Font Improvements in Outlook for Android","desc":"Now when composing emails, users can change the font color and add highlight color to their text. Additionally, users will now have easy access to recently used fonts in the font list.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-19","modified":"2026-03-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558936","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-551194","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Image Upload in Copilot Chat for Government Cloud","desc":"The image upload feature in Microsoft 365 Copilot allows users to upload images and seek insights from Copilot based on those images. We are bringing this capability to Government Cloud environments, delivering parity with existing Copilot experiences while ensuring the functionality operates within applicable Government Cloud boundaries.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-29","modified":"2026-03-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551194","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-537288","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Scatter image effect in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"Use scatter image effect directly in Copilot Chat and the create experience to further customize your visual artifacts generated with Copilot.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-03-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537288","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-557562","title":"OneDrive: Set a custom name for the OneDrive sync folder","desc":"IT admins can now customize the local OneDrive sync root folder name on users' Windows computers. By default, the folder is named \"OneDrive - {organization name},\" which can consume valuable path length for deeply nested files and folders. With this new policy, admins can set a shorter, organization-specific folder name — reducing path length issues and giving users a cleaner file system experience.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-03-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557562","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-534490","title":"Microsoft Teams: Activity in other accounts and organizations","desc":"Users can view and respond to activity across multiple tenants without switching accounts. You can triage notifications, reply to chats, and pin tenants to the left rail for quick access.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-03","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534490","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-414513","title":"Microsoft Teams: Network Strength icon to understand strength of your network","desc":"Quickly understand strength of your network along with suggestions to conserve bandwidth if you are experiencing networking issues.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-10","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=414513","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-523211","title":"Microsoft Teams: Simplified controls to manage external collaboration","desc":"Admins have access to a new overview page in the Teams Admin Center under the external collaboration section. This page allows admins to review and modify their organization's external collaboration settings. To make changes, admins can use a guided flow and select either the open or controlled preset modes, or choose to customize the settings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523211","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-516571","title":"Microsoft Teams: Interpreter agent support in Teams rooms on Windows","desc":"The Interpreter agent acts as a translator in Microsoft Teams meetings, allowing participants to listen to the meeting in their chosen language with real-time translation so speaking different languages isn’t a barrier to effective understanding and collaboration. It's now available in Teams Rooms on Windows licensed for Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516571","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526788","title":"SharePoint: Microsoft designed dark themes for SharePoint Sites","desc":"Introduce two official Microsoft-designed dark themes for SharePoint sites, delivering a modern, elegant look with improved visual comfort and accessibility. These themes provide consistent branding options and enhance user experience in low-light environments while maintaining compliance with Microsoft design standards.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526788","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-516567","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Copilot to get a detailed and contextual explanation","desc":"Users will be able to click on \"Explain this' on an acronym, text box, an image, or even a complete slide, and get a detailed contextual explanation of the selected object.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516567","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-516566","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Copilot to get a detailed and contextual explanation","desc":"Users will be able to click on \"Explain this' on an acronym, text box, an image, or even a complete slide, and get a detailed contextual explanation of the selected object.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516566","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-516565","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Copilot to get a detailed and contextual explanation","desc":"Users will be able to click on \"Explain this' on an acronym, text box, an image, or even a complete slide, and get a detailed contextual explanation of the selected object.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=516565","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-502521","title":"Microsoft Teams: Improvements in call transfer experience on Teams Phone devices","desc":"New call controls and streamlined transitions enable simple and seamless transfers for Teams Phone users on Android devices.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502521","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-500379","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI Workflows in Workflows app","desc":"With AI Workflows in the Workflows app, you will have access to custom AI-powered templates to automate complex tasks and streamline daily operations. AI Workflows enhance productivity by simplifying task execution and helping users stay organized throughout the day. Admins can enable this feature to equip users with intelligent automation tools that make managing work more efficient and intuitive.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-20","modified":"2026-03-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500379","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-492743","title":"Exchange: Exchange Online Moderation approval requests via Actionable Messages","desc":"The Exchange Online Moderation feature gives message moderators the ability to Approve or Reject sending a moderated message to its intended recipients via a special email message form that includes Approve and Reject buttons in the Outlook Desktop or Outlook on the web toolbar. However, the ability to approve or reject a moderated message currently isn't supported on Outlook for iOS, Outlook for Android, or Outlook for Mac. With this update to use Actionable Messages for moderation approval messages, moderators with mailboxes hosted in Exchange Online will now be able to approve or reject moderated messages via all the Microsoft email clients: from Outlook for Windows, Outlook for Mac, Outlook for iOS and Outlook for Android.","products":["Exchange"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-06","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492743","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-508519","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.146 - Desktop Visual Search","desc":"Quickly send images to Bing Visual Search from the Edge Desktop Search Bar to identify images, people, animals, and shows; extract, copy, and translate text while keeping its format. Solve questions quickly in various subjects and get trusted information to boost your knowledge. Discover products, fashion, recipes, identify a location and more. Available on Windows devices. Admins can control availability to this feature using the VisualSearchEnabled policy.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508519","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-499431","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention -- Always-on diagnostics for Windows Endpoints (Phase 2)","desc":"Admins can retrieve diagnostic 'Always-on diagnostic' traces directly from Windows endpoints and selectively upload them to Microsoft through the Purview Portal at the time of an investigation request such as submitting a support ticket, without disrupting end users or impacting their productivity. This eliminates the need for user coordination while maintaining seamless troubleshooting capabilities","products":["Microsoft Information Protection","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-31","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499431","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"mc-MC1253752","title":"Microsoft Teams: Manage multiple phone numbers within one Teams account","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nTeams Phone user multi-line provides greater flexibility for organizations whose users manage multiple business numbers. This capability allows administrators to assign up to 10 telephone numbers to a single Teams Phone user, all within one Teams account. Users can make and receive calls from multiple numbers across Teams desktop, Teams mobile, and Teams devices without switching accounts or hardware. This enhancement supports a familiar and localized calling experience for users who work across regions, roles, or business lines.\n\nThis capability supports scenarios such as:\n\n• Establishing local presence across multiple regions\n\n• Supporting users with multiple roles or responsibilities\n\n• Allowing executives, assistants, or support teams to manage multiple business lines within one Teams account\n\nThis message applies to Teams for Windows desktop, Teams for Mac desktop, and Teams for the web. It is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 557716.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Targeted Release: We will begin rolling out in early April 2026 and expect to complete by late April 2026.\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out in late April 2026 and expect to complete by mid-May 2026.\n\n[How this will affect your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft Teams Phone\n\n• Teams administrators who manage phone number assignments\n\n• Users assigned more than one business telephone number\n• A Teams Phone license is required to use this feature\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Admins can assign up to 10 telephone numbers to a single Teams Phone user.\n\n• Assigned numbers appear as separate lines in the Calls app in Microsoft Teams.\n\n• Additional numbers automatically appear for users after assignment; no user configuration is required.\n• This feature is Off by default. Admin must configure for it to be available to users.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\nNo action is required before this feature rolls out.\n\nAfter the feature becomes available, administrators can:\n\n• Review which users may benefit from having multiple phone numbers.\n\n• Assign and manage additional telephone numbers in the Microsoft Teams admin center.\n\n• Confirm that each telephone number has a valid emergency address configured.\n\n• Ensure assigned numbers comply with regional telecommunications regulations and existing Teams Phone requirements.\n\nManaging multi-line number assignments requires the Teams Administrator role (or equivalent permissions).\nBefore rollout, we will update this post with new documentation.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-16","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1253752","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-534606","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): SharePoint list agent","desc":"Enables effortless list creation for Copilot users through prompts, with intelligent schema generation and setup. This agent helps teams to quickly transform structured information and Copilot responses to Microsoft Lists.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534606","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-511816","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management – Introduction of pay-as-you-go feature usage report","desc":"Introducing a Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management pay-as-you-go feature usage report designed to provide transparency to the customers, enabling more accurate budget planning and policy tuning. This report provides granular breakdowns of billed processing unit usage across different data source categories and activity indicators over time, empowering IRM admins to identify cost-saving opportunities and tune their policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-08","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511816","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-542791","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-Alert Classification Property for DLP Alerts on Purview Portal","desc":"This feature introduces the ability to classify DLP alerts directly in the Purview portal. In addition to assigning a status, customers can now categorize alerts as True Positive, False Positive, or Benign Positive. This capability helps security teams better organize, track, and manage alerts, enabling more accurate reporting and efficient incident handling.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-18","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-537276","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-User based alert aggregation","desc":"User-Based Aggregation consolidates DLP alerts by user identity i.e. a DLP rule violations, in a specified aggregation time window, of the same rule and single user will be aggregated into a single alert enabling quicker triage and remediation. Instead of reviewing alerts containing rule match events of multiple users, DLP admin can now analyze grouped DLP rule match events per user, gaining insights into repeated policy violations and anomalous behavior.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-10","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537276","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-551164","title":"Microsoft Purview: eDiscovery-Tenant level process report","desc":"The tenant‑level process report provides eDiscovery administrators and managers with a centralized view of eDiscovery processes running across cases in the tenant—or across the cases they have access to. It surfaces key details such as process type, status, duration, timestamps, and who initiated each process, enabling better operational oversight, faster issue triage, and clearer end‑to‑end visibility into eDiscovery activity.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551164","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-543243","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-New Microsoft Fabric lakehouse risk indicators","desc":"With this update, Insider Risk Management extends its risk-detection capabilities to Microsoft Fabric lakehouses (in addition to Power BI which is supported today) by offering ready-to-use risk indicators based on user activities in Fabric lakehouses. Organizations can use these new indicators in data theft and data leaks policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543243","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-498921","title":"Outlook: Customizable Oversharing dialog for DLP in New Outlook","desc":"New Outlook for Windows will now support ability to show customizable oversharing dialog for Data Loss Prevention. The support will be to configure custom title, body, business justifications, and dynamic variables/tokens for matched recipients, attachment names, and labels. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-23","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498921","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-545895","title":"Outlook: Save an Event as a Draft on iOS","desc":"We're introducing the ability to save meeting invites as drafts on mobile. This feature allows users to begin composing a meeting and return to it later without sending the invite immediately—helping them stay organized and flexible when scheduling. Updated February 13, 2026: This item is still rolling and has not completed yet. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-13","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545895","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-498226","title":"Microsoft Teams: Deploy Teams frontline worker pilot in Teams Admin Center","desc":"Deploy a frontline worker (FLW) pilot in Teams Admin Center","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-11","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498226","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-492616","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: M365 Copilot - Billing and usage - Usage insights","desc":"As you enable M365 Copilot Chat pay-as-you-go billing, AI administrators can view usage insights to inform agent management decisions. This feature displays the cost and number of messages in total and per agent. Cost and usage details can be filtered by billing policy and date range.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-28","modified":"2026-03-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492616","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-554924","title":"Microsoft Teams: Image viewer improvements enable scrolling and jumping to original message","desc":"Lightbox enhancements let users scroll through all previously shared images in a conversation, provide a clearer visual focus on the image being viewed, and add a header option that jumps directly to the original message where the image was posted.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-03-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=554924","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-495263","title":"Windows 365: Frontline in Shared mode availability for Switzerland North, Switzerland West, Norway East, Norway East, Norway West, UAE central, UAE north","desc":"Windows 365 Frontline in Shared mode availability for Switzerland West, Norway West, UAE central","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-03-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495263","source":"roadmap","phases":["Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-503106","title":"Microsoft Teams: Call history Admin control","desc":"Teams admins can now control whether Teams meetings and calls appear in users’ iPhone call logs.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2026-03-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503106","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-497298","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat Tools Control","desc":"Tools acts as a lightweight entry point into high-value, task-specific Copilot features and capabilities directly from the prompt box. By selecting Tools, users get a menu where they can easily discover and trigger the right Copilot feature or capability for their current task, while also providing consistent interactions across tools.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-04","modified":"2026-03-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497298","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-495262","title":"Windows 365: Frontline in Shared mode availability for Germany West Central, Korea Central, Korea South","desc":"Windows 365 Frontline in Shared Mode is expanding to Korea Central, helping frontline workers in these regions to securely share Cloud PCs across shifts.","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-27","modified":"2026-03-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495262","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-558441","title":"SharePoint: Plan and Create Pages with AI","desc":"This feature allows you to edit new and existing pages with an AI chat pane. Now, with just prompts, you can add webparts, grounding documents, and refine the visuals and text on your page.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-03-12","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=558441","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-515165","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Query Coda Docs and Wikis with Copilot Connectors","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Coda with Copilot connectors to query collaborative documents and wikis.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515165","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-502534","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] [Search UX] Custom filter support for data sources on Copilot Search","desc":"1. Allow IT admins to customize filters at a data source level. 2. IT admins can add/delete a filter at data source level.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502534","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513285","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Amazon S3 to access structured document repositories with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Amazon S3 to access structured document repositories with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-13","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513285","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515175","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Asana to manage projects and tasks with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Asana to manage projects and tasks with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515175","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515158","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with GitLab Issues (Cloud and Server) to track engineering tasks and bugs with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with GitLab Issues (Cloud and Server) to track engineering tasks and bugs with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515158","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515177","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Monday.com to track work and team progress with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Monday.com to track work and team progress with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515177","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513279","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Zendesk Help Center to retrieve support articles and FAQs with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Zendesk Help Center to retrieve support articles and FAQs with Copilot Connector","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-13","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513279","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513281","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Guru for Internal Knowledge and Insights","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Guru with Copilot connectors to retrieve internal knowledge and team insights.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513281","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501112","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] No-Code Publishing for Azure AI Foundry Agents to Microsoft 365 Copilot Agent Store","desc":"Developers can now publish Azure AI Foundry Agents directly to the Microsoft 365 Copilot Agent Store with a simplified, no-code experience.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501112","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-502878","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Agent metadata in inventory export","desc":"Agent metadata export in Microsoft 365 admin center includes expanded metadata fields, covering Capabilities, Data Sources, Actions, Created In, and Created By. Enables enhanced visibility for auditing, governance, and lifecycle tracking. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502878","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-499422","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Copilot Studio agent report in Insights enhanced with autonomous agents.","desc":"Enhancement to Copilot studio agents report (Viva Insights) - 1. Inclusion of agents with \"generative\" orchestration 2. Autonomous agent adoption and impact (maker led time and cost saving).","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-04","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499422","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-497913","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Easier access to Researcher in Microsoft Word","desc":"The Researcher agent now has easier entry points on the Word canvas —making it faster to go from idea to polished research report without breaking your flow.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-10","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497913","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-474448","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot extensibility – Embedded Knowledge capability support for declarative agents.","desc":"Developers and makers can embed knowledge (pdf, doc/docx, ppt) into their declarative agents built with Teams Toolkit for additional grounding capabilities.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-28","modified":"2026-03-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=474448","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-413718","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Calendar search for email delegates","desc":"Delegates with existing calendar access of other users, can now search for meetings using Copilot Chat, helping to save time and streamline processes.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-03-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=413718","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-498233","title":"Microsoft Viva: News AI audio briefing in Connections Mobile","desc":"This feature provides an AI generated audio overview of top 10 news items in the Viva Connections news reader experience. It plays the 10 audio clips sequentially to help users catch up on top news in a hands-free manner. This experience will be available in the Viva Connections App in Teams mobile on iOS and android.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-10","modified":"2026-03-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498233","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-497944","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Service health dashboard","desc":"As a Microsoft Purview user, you'll be able to view outages, service issues, and advisories that might impact your services. This new dashboard will combine the services and solutions health of Purview, Microsoft 365 services, and Azure Cloud Services in one central place in the Purview portal, eliminating the need to go to several places to find this information.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-07","modified":"2026-03-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497944","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2026","gaSort":202609},{"id":"rm-529848","title":"Outlook: Filter Out Declined Meetings in Outlook Mobile","desc":"You can now declutter your calendar by hiding declined meetings. If you’ve enabled “Show declined meetings” in New Outlook or Outlook for the Web, you’ll see a setting in Outlook Mobile to hide them for a simpler view.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-03-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529848","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526795","title":"Outlook: Hide Declined Meetings in Outlook Mobile","desc":"If you have enabled Show declined events in New Outlook, you can choose to hide declined events in your Outlook iOS or Android app. Go to Settings > Calendar > Hide Declined Events. This will filter out declined events from your mobile calendar, while keeping those events visible in New Outlook.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-03-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526795","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-502844","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Image effects in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"We’re adding a new set of image effects to Microsoft 365 Copilot that make it easy to enhance your visuals. Whether you're using AI-generated images or uploading your own, you can apply these effects in the Create experience or directly in Copilot Chat to make your content stand out.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-08","modified":"2026-03-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502844","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-547832","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention- Show customized message or hyperlink for multiple file toast","desc":"With this feature when multiple files are involved in a DLP enforcement action, the policy tip will now show multiple files and their respective status.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-27","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547832","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-543244","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-New quick policies to detect data theft from Microsoft Fabric & non-Microsoft 365 data sources","desc":"We are adding to Insider Risk Management a pre-configured quick policy template to detect data theft from Microsoft Fabric and non-Microsoft 365 data sources like Box, Dropbox, Google Drive, Azure and Amazon Web Services (AWS). This will enable admins to create scenario-specific policies, with little configurations needed, to get started faster. All scenario based quick policies can be found in the Policies page > Create Policies. Additional tuning post deployment to meet individual alert volume needs can be expected. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543244","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-535423","title":"Microsoft Viva: AI audio overview support for pages and additional languages","desc":"This feature provides additional languages support for AI generated audio overview of top 10 news items in the Viva Connections news reader experience. Additionally, if the SharePoint Knowledge Agent is available in a site, site pages and news posts will now have the AI audio summary experience.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=535423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-531912","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit Scheduled prompts","desc":"Enable customers to edit the scheduled prompt schedule","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=531912","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-510107","title":"Outlook: Enhanced Search Experience in Win32","desc":"After executing a search in classic Outlook, users will have the option to easily opt into seeing an AI generated summary of their search results in their Copilot side pane. They can ask further questions in their chat, navigate to cited files and emails, or go back to their email experience easily.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-06","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=510107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-480728","title":"OneDrive: OneDrive files as knowledge sources for agents","desc":"Allow files from OneDrive to be added as a grounding source in the Sources tab when creating a custom agent. This would apply to agents created from both OneDrive and SharePoint.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-24","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480728","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-369345","title":"Microsoft Teams: ‘Add emoji’ updated keyboard shortcut","desc":"Insert emojis directly from your keyboard without any distractions. Use colons (e.g. :smile:) in the compose box to add any emoji, even your custom ones, making it quicker to express yourself.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-23","modified":"2026-03-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=369345","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-531760","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: User Report capabilities to Defender for Office Plan 1","desc":"Security admins with Defender for Office 365 Plan 1 can avail the benefits of end user reporting of Teams Messages","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=531760","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-491632","title":"Microsoft Teams: New Workflows app experience in Teams and SharePoint","desc":"The new Workflows app is to provide an experience that is both simpler and faster to enable everyday Teams and SharePoint users to create automations in three steps or less. Fully launched in Teams and coming to SharePoint lists and libraries soon.","products":["Microsoft Teams","SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-04","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491632","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-513276","title":"Microsoft Viva: Hide a user's messages in Viva Engage","desc":"The hide user messages feature is a user-level moderation control. It allows users to see fewer messages from other users, helping to reduce interactions that may be unwanted or inappropriate. Users cannot hide designated leaders, corporate communicators, or network/verified/Engage admins. The hide user feature is default on; admins can turn it off for their network in the Engage admin center.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-10","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513276","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-500020","title":"OneNote: Microsoft Purview Sensitivity Labels in OneNote","desc":"Microsoft Purview Sensitivity Labels in OneNote will allow users to classify and protect OneNote Sections with the same compliance standards available across Microsoft 365 apps. Users will be able to apply labels directly within OneNote, ensuring sensitive content is encrypted, access-controlled, and compliant with the organization's policies.","products":["OneNote"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-07","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500020","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-543423","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Chat History Landing page: Filtering UI Refresh","desc":"To help you quickly find the conversations that matter, we’re updating the Chat History filtering experience. This refresh makes the interface simpler and makes it easier to clear filters whenever you need to.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-23","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-527840","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Copilot to Share with Summary for OneDrive files in Windows","desc":"We’re bringing the power of Microsoft 365 Copilot directly into your daily file experience in Windows. With this feature, users can summarize files and send the summary within the share dialog. This feature will be available in File Explorer and OneDrive Activity Center.","products":["OneNote","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-25","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527840","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-513421","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Floating Copilot button in OneDrive","desc":"The floating Copilot button is a quick-access button that appears prominently in your OneDrive web interface. It’s your gateway to Copilot-powered actions —right where you need them. Instant Copilot Access: Ask questions about your files, summarize documents, or compare content—all without leaving OneDrive. Contextual Recommendations: The button will suggest helpful actions based on your file selection—like generating a status report from a file you've selected or generating a summary of a new file shared with you. Streamlined Navigation: No more hunting through menus; the Copilot floating button brings the most relevant tools to your fingertips.","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-28","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513421","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-413720","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Meetings search using categories added in Outlook","desc":"This unblocks customers from searching for meetings specifying the categories they have added in Outlook.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=413720","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-500870","title":"SharePoint: Updated Document Library User Experience","desc":"We're updating the SharePoint document library experience to more closely align with the user experience in OneDrive - while making it easier than ever before to access the valuable functionality unique to document libraries. When you’re working in a document library, we’ve brought custom views and filters front and center – just like in OneDrive. We’ve also redesigned the command bar to help you take action, faster. All your view customization tools are now grouped under one simplified menu, making it easy to apply conditional formatting or organize items by metadata in seconds.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-20","modified":"2026-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500870","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-555856","title":"Microsoft Teams: New controls for quick views in the chat list","desc":"Positioned at the top of the chat and channels list, quick views give users fast access to mentions, followed threads, and more. Users can choose when and how quick views are displayed – selecting “always show,” “always hide,” or “show only when unread” – and can collapse the section at any time.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-03-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-537279","title":"Microsoft Teams: Choose Your Enter Key Behavior in Teams Chat","desc":"Microsoft Teams now gives you control over how the Enter key works when composing messages. You can choose whether pressing Enter sends your message or starts a new line—making it easier to write longer messages without accidental sends.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-03-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537279","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-529816","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Zero-hour auto-purge (ZAP) Teams protection capabilities to Defender for Office Plan 1","desc":"Security admins with Defender for Office 365 Plan 1 can utilize Zero-hour auto purge (ZAP) and admin quarantine for zapped Teams messages.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-03-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529816","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-513432","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Floating Copilot icon in File Previewer for OneDrive","desc":"A new Copilot icon button provides a quick, visible entry point to Copilot directly within the file previewer in OneDrive. Positioned at the bottom-right corner (instead of the command bar), this button surfaces contextual prompts tailored to the file type and offers seamless access to Copilot chat, making it easier to get insights and take action without leaving the preview experience.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-28","modified":"2026-03-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513432","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-392457","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Lifecycle Management - Bulk replacement or removal of a retention label","desc":"Admins can perform a bulk replacement or removal of a retention label using the Purview compliance portal. They can perform the action across the entire tenant or targeted to specific content using KQL and static or adaptive scopes.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-04-18","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=392457","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-548642","title":"Outlook: Open and Send Outlook File Templates","desc":"We're introducing the ability to open and send OFT files (Outlook File Templates) on mobile. This feature allows users to view and open OFT files as a draft message, so users can easily resue their Outlook email templates.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548642","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-486856","title":"Microsoft 365: Microsoft 365 companion apps- a suite of apps designed to enhance productivity","desc":"Microsoft 365 companions is a suite of apps, including People, File Search, and Calendar, designed to enhance productivity through quick access to key tools directly from the Windows 11 taskbar. These lightweight apps integrate seamlessly with Microsoft 365, allowing users to efficiently look up contacts and navigate organization charts, locate files, view calendars and streamline workflows without distractions.","products":["Microsoft 365","Windows"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-11","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-496988","title":"OneDrive: Sync admin reports - GCC-H and DoD","desc":"We are adding support for the OneDrive Sync admin reports for the GCC-H and DoD environments.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-20","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496988","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-490064","title":"OneDrive: Prompt for permitted users to sign in to OneDrive app with personal Microsoft account","desc":"Users have long been able to use personal Microsoft accounts with the OneDrive app on corporate Windows devices—unless restricted by admin policy. This new feature introduces a prompt only when a personal account is already signed in on the device, encouraging users to also sign in to the OneDrive app with that account. Administrators who have already restricted personal accounts on corporate devices can continue to manage this as before. Organizations that have already disabled personal OneDrive accounts on corporate devices with the DisablePersonalSync policy will not see this prompt. Administrators can also suppress it using the DisableNewAccountDetection policy. More information on configuring policies can be found here:","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-25","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490064","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sharepoint/use-group-policy#manage-onedrive-using-group-policy"},{"id":"rm-381953","title":"Microsoft Teams: Short meeting URL","desc":"We are making meeting URL shorter and removing unnecessary symbols/info from there to make it more convenient for sharing","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-02-06","modified":"2026-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=381953","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-542930","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations-Introducing new purge mitigation action","desc":"A new Data Security Investigations (DSI) mitigation action, purge, is now available to help admins quickly and efficiently delete sensitive or overshared content during investigations, within the product UX. This addition works alongside DSI’s AI-powered content analysis features, such as categorization, AI search, and examination for risk, which help surface data security risks buried in data.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-18","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542930","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"mc-MC1242781","title":"Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android: License-based management updates for DM-synced devices","desc":"Introduction\n\nWe are introducing license-based management updates for Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android (MTRA) and other Android-based Teams devices that are synced to the Teams Rooms Pro Management Portal through Device Management (DM) services.\n\nThis update aligns management portal capabilities with existing Teams Rooms license entitlements (Basic, Standard, and Pro). By enforcing license boundaries in the portal, this change provides clearer expectations for inventory visibility versus advanced monitoring and management features, while maintaining the current in-room meeting experience.\n\nThese changes apply only to Android devices currently synced from DM services. Internet of Things (IoT)–based Android management convergence is still in progress and is not yet Generally Available.\n\nWhen this will happen\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide, GCC, GCC High, DoD): Rollout will begin in early March 2026 and is expected to complete by late March 2026.\n\nHow this affects your organization\n\nWho is affected\n\n• Admins managing Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android or other Android-based Teams devices\n\n• Devices synced to the Teams Rooms Pro Management Portal via DM services\n\n• Tenants using Teams Rooms Basic, Standard, or Pro licenses for Android devices\n\nWhat will happen\n\n• There is no change to the in-room Teams meeting experience.\n• The update affects only the admin experience in the Teams Rooms Pro Management Portal.\n• Portal features will reflect the license assigned to each Android device:\n\n• Teams Rooms Pro (Android)\n\n• Full advanced monitoring and management capabilities remain available.\n\n• Teams Rooms Standard (Android)• Device inventory metadata (such as firmware and app versions) remains visible.\n• Advanced management and diagnostic features are restricted and may display upgrade prompts where applicable.\n\n• Teams Rooms Basic (Android)• Devices remain visible in Rooms and Inventory views\n• Advanced monitoring and configuration features are not available\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\n\n• Review license assignments for Android-based Teams Rooms devices\n\n• Ensure devices requiring advanced management are licensed with Teams Rooms Pro\n\n• No action is required unless you plan to upgrade licenses\n\nCompliance considerations\n\nNo compliance considerations identified; review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-03-03","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1242781","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-513272","title":"Microsoft Teams: Live meetings indicator for channels","desc":"Introducing a new indicator in channels to help users find meetings occurring live within the channel and join them.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-21","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513272","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-532724","title":"Microsoft Teams: Automatic installation and update of Network Device Interface (NDI) in Teams (MAC)","desc":"This update now enables users to install and update the Network Device Interface (NDI) automatically in Microsoft Teams on MAC devices without any manual process. This allows organizations to broadcast audio and video streams from Teams instances to a user's local network.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532724","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515152","title":"Microsoft 365: Cloud Update - Rollback All Devices","desc":"Use rollback all devices to quickly revert updates for all device managed by cloud update and on the latest N-0 release of Monthly Enterprise Channel. This feature helps recover devices to a previous version of Microsoft 365 Apps in the event an issue occurs following an update. Updates can then be resumed from the portal or with the next release of Monthly Enterprise Channel. It works for organizations of any size and delivers a quick and efficient recovery method.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-15","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515152","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-515151","title":"Microsoft 365: Cloud Update - Rollback by Group","desc":"Use rollback by group to selectively revert updates for specific device or user groups managed by cloud update. This feature helps recover devices to a previous version of Microsoft 365 Apps in the event an issue occurs following an update. Updates can then be resumed from the portal or with the next release of Monthly Enterprise Channel. It works for organizations of any size and delivers a quick and efficient recovery method.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-20","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515151","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-490051","title":"Microsoft Teams: Copilot in Teams can generate an audio overview of your meetings","desc":"Copilot can generate an audio overview of your transcribed meetings, transforming one or multiple meetings into an engaging listening experience. Users can choose how they want to listen: select one or two speakers, adjust the tone from concise to playful, and tailor the length. This capability is only available in English currently.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2026-03-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490051","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-531761","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Admins can hunt on calls in Microsoft Teams","desc":"Security admins with Defender for Office 365 Plan 2 can hunt on calls and meetings made inside Microsoft Teams for their organization","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=531761","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-549287","title":"Outlook: New search folder types","desc":"Search folders are being moved to the Settings experience in the new Outlook for Windows and web, improving discoverability and alignment with modern organization workflows. In addition, we are expanding supported search folder types, including mail with attachments, old mail, and large mail and more. Users will also gain the ability to filter search folders by specific folders, providing more precise control over how email is organized and surfaced. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-28","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=549287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-422503","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Administrative units support","desc":"Administrative units allow admins with appropriate permissions to subdivide the organization into smaller units, and then assign specific admins or role groups that can manage only the members of those units. For example, German administrators can only create/manage policies for only German users, and German investigators can only investigate alerts and activities from only German users. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-10-21","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422503","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-518286","title":"Microsoft Teams: New SlimCore-based optimization for Microsoft Teams in VDI - support for Windows endpoints on Omnissa environments","desc":"This feature allows Windows endpoints to optimize Microsoft Teams in VDI environments with the new SlimCore-based media engine, providing an expanded feature set and multiple improvements in quality, reliability and performance.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-21","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518286","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-542194","title":"Minecraft Education: Update v1.21.13","desc":"The \"Copper, Collaborate & Compete\" update for Minecraft Education, bringing the version to 1.21.13.","products":["Minecraft Education"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-12","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542194","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-549286","title":"Outlook: New search folder types","desc":"Search Folders are being moved to the Settings experience in the new Outlook for Web and Windows, improving discoverability and alignment with modern organization workflows. In addition, we are expanding supported Search Folder types, including Mail with attachments, Old mail, and Large mail and more. Users will also gain the ability to filter Search Folders by specific folders, providing more precise control over how email is organized and surfaced. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-21","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=549286","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-497836","title":"Outlook: Play a Sound Rule","desc":"Users can set up Outlook rules to play a sound or show a desktop alert whenever an email that matches your chosen conditions arrives, whether it’s from a specific person, includes certain words, or meets any other rule criteria you define. These features help you stay alerted to the emails that matter most. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-02","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497836","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-496141","title":"Outlook: Rule to display desktop alert","desc":"Create rules that trigger a desktop alert when specific emails arrive. This makes it easier to stay on top of important messages without missing a beat. Look for the new \"Display a Desktop Alert\" action when setting up or editing your rules. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496141","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-523215","title":"Outlook: Run rule over a specific folder","desc":"Run Rule on Specific Folder enables users to manually apply an existing rule to a chosen folder instead of running it only on incoming mail in Inbox. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523215","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-473447","title":"Microsoft 365 (Microsoft Copilot): Copilot Chat - Loop Notebooks in ContextIQ","desc":"When grounding your prompts in Copilot Chat, you will be able to use ContextIQ to scope to your Loop Notebooks content in the Files tab.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-12-17","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473447","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-498159","title":"Microsoft Teams: Chat Notes","desc":"A new collaborative space is now available directly from your Teams chat, enabling real-time collaboration, organization of key information, and streamlined communications. Chat notes is available in 1:1 and group chat, and is accessible only to the chat members. Add images, format text, share Loop components, and mention chat members when you require their attention.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-05","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498159","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-473439","title":"Outlook: Online archive for shared mailboxes in the new Outlook for Windows","desc":"Online archive mailboxes will appear in the folder pane alongside other accounts, making it easier to access archived content for shared mailboxes. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-12-18","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473439","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-409965","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management- Adaptive scopes","desc":"Ability to target IRM policies using global Adaptive Scopes. Adaptive scopes within IRM policies allow admins to use existing adaptive scopes created on the Microsoft Purview compliance portal within IRM policies, Adaptive scopes can be created using queries to define user groups dynamically. This feature provides more powerful targeting for policies, allowing different settings to be assigned to users based on attributes from Entra ID without the administrative burden of creating and maintaining groups. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-16","modified":"2026-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=409965","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504,"preview":"August CY2024"},{"id":"rm-557980","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Pulse - Capture targeted Copilot sentiment from power and novice users","desc":"Enable change leaders to quickly identify and auto-populate Microsoft 365 Copilot power users and novice users based on organizational attributes and aggregated Copilot usage data. Automatic audience targeting in Viva Pulse will empower change leaders to capture sentiment on Copilot use cases, verbatims, and learnings with insights into whether specific audiences need more training or whether certain pockets of the organization would benefit from receiving upgraded Copilot licenses.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-02-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557980","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"June CY2026"},{"id":"rm-557979","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Pulse - Measure Copilot sentiment to change manage and scale Copilot adoption","desc":"Add new Viva Pulse survey templates for Copilot readiness, adoption, and business value, with built-in entry points and reporting surfaced directly in the Copilot Dashboard. All Copilot templates are fully customizable in Pulse, with the ability to add or edit questions using Copilot authoring and the question library. Organizations can also easily upload pilot group users into Pulse via CSV to target surveys at the right audiences from day one.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-26","modified":"2026-02-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557979","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-490565","title":"SharePoint: Modern SharePoint Page Templates","desc":"The Modern SharePoint Page Templates feature introduces a new Template Gallery, providing users with a centralized hub to discover, preview, and select from over 50 modern out-of-the-box (OOB) templates and custom templates. This feature empowers users to create high-quality, on-brand pages effortlessly, enhancing productivity while ensuring consistency and visual appeal across SharePoint sites. Key highlights: Template Gallery: Centralized hub to access both Saved on this site (custom templates) and From Microsoft (OOB templates). 50+ new OOB templates: A collection of aesthetically pleasing, professional, and easy-to-use templates that empower users to quickly create visually engaging and consistent content for common use cases like status updates, event announcements, and team introductions.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-22","modified":"2026-02-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490565","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-543969","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Email attachment Preview in Activity Explorer","desc":"We're enhancing Activity Explorer to provide greater visibility into sensitive data flagged in Exchange Online. Previously, only the message body was viewable, which limited insight into flagged content. With this update, admins will be able to preview email attachments directly within Activity Explorer—without needing to download the email.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-31","modified":"2026-02-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543969","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-523204","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Voice chats can reference Memory","desc":"While users are in M365 Copilot voice chat, Copilot can respond using existing memories already stored in user personalization settings. Users cannot modify/edit their memories from voice chats yet due to privacy considerations. All memories that can be used for Copilot responses in voice chat are visible and manageable by users in their Personalization settings.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-02-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523204","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-557673","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can edit your document by default in Word","desc":"The default chat experience with Copilot in Word now allows Copilot to directly edit your document. All changes made by Copilot are fully reviewable and reversible, and users can turn this experience off if needed.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-25","modified":"2026-02-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557673","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-536574","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft M365): Review PDFs using Copilot context menu and AI actions","desc":"Copilot makes PDF reviews faster and easier. It explains selected text in plain language and lets you customize the prompt for tailored results—so you spend less time switching between apps.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-02-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536574","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-542189","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Admins can block external users in Microsoft Teams from Defender Portal","desc":"Security admins with Defender for Office 365 Plan 1 and above can block external users from sending messages, calls, meetings invitation over Microsoft Teams via the Tenant Allow Block List in Microsoft Defender portal. Updated January 28, 2026: We are pausing rollout at this time as we address an ongoing issue. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-12","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542189","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-505444","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: eDiscovery - Generate keyword query language from natural language prompt in eDiscovery with Copilot for Security","desc":"Copilot for Security is embedded in eDiscovery to enable users to provide a search prompt in natural language and will translate into keyword query language to help expedite the start of an eDiscovery search.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505444","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-529854","title":"Microsoft Teams: Network Device Interface (NDI) bandwidth increase","desc":"Microsoft Teams will soon increase the bandwidth when Network Device Interface (NDI) is used with Teams meetings, webinars, or town halls. When an NDI feed is subscribed within the meeting, the bandwidth will automatically increase without the need to pin or spotlight select users for prioritization. Customers can experience up to 8 distinct 1080p NDI streams based on network conditions.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529854","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-481559","title":"Outlook: Agents for Microsoft 365 Copilot available in Copilot Chat in classic Outlook for Windows","desc":"We will be adding declarative agents support for agents in Copilot Chat in Outlook. This roadmap item tracks availability in classic Outlook for Windows.","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481559","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-502528","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Auto-Remediation of Malicious Similarity Clusters in AIR","desc":"We are expanding the auto-remediation capabilities in Automated Investigations and Response (AIR) to fully automate the remediation of malicious similarity clusters. Earlier this year, we introduced auto-remediation for malicious URL and file clusters. Building on that foundation, this enhancement enables AIR to automatically approve all pending remediation actions it generates—eliminating the need for manual intervention and streamlining the response process for SOC teams. This advancement significantly reduces response time and operational overhead, allowing security teams to focus on higher-priority threats.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-03","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502528","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-503112","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Agentic AI Phish Submission Analysis & Response","desc":"We are introducing Advanced Agentic AI grading system integrated into the native MDO submission analysis and response workflow. This integration allows for prompt, detailed verdicts with natural language explanations when customers report phishing messages to Microsoft.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503112","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-503108","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Automated Investigation & Response (AIR) Platform Modernization – User Submission Playbook","desc":"We are modernizing the AIR platform for increased scalability and speed of AIR investigations to deliver the user submission playbook faster including quicker verdicts and faster resolutions.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-11","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503108","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-505791","title":"Microsoft Teams: Apps in Shared Channels for Microsoft Teams","desc":"Bring the apps your team relies on—tabs, bots, and message extensions—directly into Shared Channels in Microsoft Teams. This update lets channel owners add apps to a specific shared channel, so everyone collaborating there (including invited collaborators from other teams or organizations, subject to admin policy) can work in one place without switching contexts.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505791","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-422817","title":"Outlook: Insert signature into calendar events","desc":"Users can manually insert a signature into a calendar event like they can in the classic outlook. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-17","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=422817","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-557564","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Local file support for Agent Mode in Excel","desc":"Extending support for modern Excel workbooks stored on your device to Agent Mode in Excel, giving users the flexibility to use multi-step editing capabilities with Copilot in Excel no matter whether files are stored locally or in the cloud.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-20","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557564","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-543420","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Word Agent","desc":"Word Agent helps you handle research, structure, and formatting so you can stay focused on your ideas. Use multi‑turn chat to refine your draft or open it in Word for full editing and collaboration. It’s designed for long‑form, information‑dense work—like strategic plans, policy documents, and technical papers—making it easier to turn complex material into clear, well‑written content. Available to Microsoft 365 users with or without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543420","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-526798","title":"Microsoft Edge: Announcement page on update experience","desc":"Edge for Business will introduce a \"What's New\" enhancements page to the Edge update experience. This page will help your users understand how to best utilize the browser's newest features for maximum productivity.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526798","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-542183","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.145 - Introducing a new policy that can enable/disable web app installation from the browser","desc":"Admins can control whether users can install web apps through the browser using the WebAppInstallByUserEnabled policy.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-12","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542183","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-525366","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.145 - Securely enable AI generated applications","desc":"Leverage the latest AI advancements to build prototypes, learning applications or interactive reports using your favorite tools in Edge without worrying about your data. This extension enables apps to leverage some new security improvements for safely executing AI generated code.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-06","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=525366","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-545894","title":"Microsoft Entra: App Deactivation","desc":"Admins or app owners can now safely pause an app’s access to Entra protected resources without deleting it or disrupting configuration. When deactivated, the app and its service principals globally (across tenants) can’t request new tokens and user sign ins are blocked, while existing tokens simply expire on their normal schedule. This makes it easy for admins to temporarily freeze suspicious or unused apps during investigations, bulk cleanup, or tenant hygiene work. This capability is now available in the Entra admin center (App registrations, Enterprise apps) and Microsoft Graph API.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-01-13","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545894","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/enterprise-apps/deactivate-application-portal"},{"id":"rm-534487","title":"Microsoft Teams: Autocorrect in Teams compose","desc":"Users will now have commonly misspelled words automatically corrected in compose.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-03","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534487","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-493320","title":"Microsoft Teams: Line key configuration on Teams Phone devices from Teams Admin Center (TAC)","desc":"This feature allows admins to configure line keys for various scenarios on Teams phone devices, including personal and common area phones (CAP). Scenarios supported include speed dial, shared line, collaborative call delegation, and call transfers. This item's rollout was paused and will begin in 2026. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493320","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-498920","title":"Outlook: Wait on Send for oversharing dialog in New Outlook","desc":"New Outlook for Windows will now support Wait on Send for Oversharing. This feature allows admins to block sending of emails in case DLP policy evaluation is not completed for labeled or sensitive content. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-23","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498920","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-470597","title":"Microsoft Teams: Shared tab in channel","desc":"The Files tab in channels is now \"Shared\". In addition to files that are currently shown from document library, new experience will also show all the files and links shared in the channel conversations. This makes it easier to find content all in one place.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-12-10","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470597","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-498355","title":"Microsoft Teams: New VDI solution for Teams optimization in Amazon WorkSpaces","desc":"New VDI solution for Teams introduces multimedia offloading and optimization solution for Microsoft Teams when running in Amazon WorkSpaces (Personal and Pools). Users of the WorkSpaces Client for Windows can enjoy a high-definition experience in virtual desktops, where audio/video/screensharing are offloaded to the user's device and processed by the SlimCore media engine. This entry applies to WorkSpaces only (AppStream is not supported).","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-16","modified":"2026-02-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498355","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-417063","title":"Outlook: Grant mail delegate sharing permissions from the new Outlook","desc":"Delegate access for mailbox and folders can be granted from the new Outlook app. Users will be able to view the permissions granted for a mailboxes and folders. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-09-24","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=417063","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607},{"id":"rm-557175","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Copilot - Billing and usage - Standalone consumption of prepaid capacity pack credits","desc":"Use a prepaid capacity pack as the sole billing method for supported Copilot experiences. Admins can configure billing policies with prepaid capacity such that usage for users in the policy is deducted exclusively from prepaid capacity credits, with no pay as you go charges.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-19","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557175","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"mc-MC1193421","title":"(Updated) Retirement of several Microsoft Planner features in early 2026 as part of a Planner update","desc":"Updated February 19, 2026: Performance may be slower on some browsers for large basic plans with more than 300 tasks. For best results, please use the latest versions of Edge (144 or higher) or Chrome (144 or higher). Meanwhile, we're also working on an update that we expect to improve performance.\n[Introduction]\n\nIn early 2026, a major update of Planner will begin rolling out. This update will introduce several new capabilities. In addition, several features will be retired from Microsoft Planner. These changes will begin rolling out between mid-January 2026 and mid-February 2026.\n[When this will happen:]\nRefer to the sections below for details on timing.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected: All users of Microsoft Planner in your organization, including those using Planner components in Loop, integrations with Viva Goals, and premium Planner plans.\nWhat will happen:\n\nIn early 2026, we will begin rolling out a new major update of the Planner app in Teams desktop and web as well as Planner on the web. This update will come with several new enhancements, and we will also be retiring several features at this time. See each section below for more detail on the timing.\nNew features in the upcoming Planner update:\n• These changes will be available with the new update, which we expect to begin rolling in mid-February 2026.\n\n• Tasks chats in basic plans will allow team members to collaborate directly on tasks using rich text formatting and @mentions, making it easier to discuss work and notify teammates about what needs attention.\n• Goals in basic plans for users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license or a Planner premium license. Goals will allow teams to set clear, well-defined objectives to help prioritize work. By connecting tasks to shared goals, teams achieve greater alignment, gain clarity on priorities, and track progress and outcomes—driving the plan forward together.\n\nNew features coming in subsequent Planner updates:\n• Project manager agent will be available in all plans for M365 Copilot licensed users, including basic plans. The Project Manager agent can help teams get work done faster by executing on tasks and can help drive alignment by writing comprehensive status reports based on plan updates.\n• Custom templates will allow you to create reusable, pre-designed plan layouts tailored to your organization’s needs, ensuring consistency and saving time. They provide the ability to standardize content while allowing easy customization for specific scenarios.\n\nFeatures in Planner that will be retired:\n\n• We expect this rollout to begin between mid-January 2026 and mid-February 2026.\n• The following changes will take effect as this build rolls out to your organization:\n• A new Task chat experience will replace the prior comments experience for basic plan tasks: • As noted above, the previous task comments experience will be replaced by a new task chat feature that supports messages about the task that can include @mentions and rich text formatting, in response to a longstanding top customer request. Due to customer feedback on our notifications experience, the new chat feature only sends an email/Teams notification to a colleague that’s been @mentioned in the message.\n• The task chat experience will be available on Planner in Teams web/desktop and the Planner web experience, and the old experience for viewing comments will no longer be directly visible on a task. Instead, the task details pane will show a link to open a page in Outlook where task comments can be seen.\n• Users can continue to use and see the previous task comments experience in the iOS Planner app, Android Planner app, and Planner in Teams mobile. New task chat messages will not be visible in the mobile experience at this time.\n• There are no changes to email notifications for the existing task comments experience, meaning that an email notification will be sent to all group members associated with the plan when a task comment is added.\n• There is no change to the premium plan conversations feature at this time.\n\n• The whiteboard tab for premium plans will be retired. • This feature automatically created a whiteboard for premium plans in Planner and allowed users to create tasks in Planner from that whiteboard's sticky notes.\n• The whiteboard tab will be unavailable on the premium plan after retirement of this feature.\n• Users will be unable to create tasks from a whiteboard as a result.\n• Any existing whiteboard content will remain available via the Whiteboard app.\n• There is no replacement for this feature at this time.\n\nFeatures in Planner that will be temporarily unavailable:\n• We expect this rollout to begin between mid-January 2026 and mid-February 2026.\n• Convert a basic plan to a premium plan will be temporarily unavailable.\n• The ability to convert an existing basic plan to a premium plan will be unavailable.\n• We plan to make similar functionality available again in the future.\n• In the meantime, users will need to create a new premium plan and manually copy the tasks into the new plan.\n\nFeatures that will be retired as we pursue a long‑term plan to bring equivalent capabilities:\n• Planner component in Loop pages.• This control, which could previously be inserted by typing /planner in a Loop workspace or pasting the link to a Plan, was one of the available options. This control will be retired between mid-January 2026 and mid-February 2026.\n• Loop pages support various options for capturing task information. We recommend the Task List Control in Loop to capture tasks.\n• After the retirement of this control, which is expected to begin in January 2026 and will roll out independent of the Planner update rollout, it will no longer be possible to add a new component of this type in a Loop workspace.\n• Workspaces where these components were already present will display the Planner plan URL where the component was previously located.\n• Tasks previously entered in these components will remain available in Planner.\n\nWhile the Planner component in Loop is being retired currently, we recognize the user need around a component like this for their planning needs. We have a longer-term goal to bring a similar Planner component across our M365 suite, including Loop. Considering these discussions are still in an early stage, we do not have an ETA to share currently.\nFeatures outside of Planner that will be retired without replacement:\n• Planner integration in Viva Goals.• Viva Goals will be retired on December 31, 2025, as previously announced. Refer to Viva Goals retirement for more information.\n• When Viva Goals is retired, the entry point in Viva Goals for use with Planner will no longer be available.\n\n• iCalendar feed integration retirement.• This feature will be retired between mid-January 2026 and mid-February 2026.\n• This feature allowed users to subscribe to their Planner tasks as an iCalendar feed that could be viewed in iCalendar-compatible applications like Outlook.\n• After this feature is retired, users will not be able to create new iCalendar feeds for their tasks or plans, and they will stop seeing their tasks in the iCalendar feeds they previous created.\n• There is no replacement for this feature at this time.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n• These changes will happen automatically by the specified dates.\n• No admin action is required.\n• Notify users about this change.• Update relevant documentation as appropriate.\n• Share the recommended alternate options where appropriate, as described above.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-09","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1193421","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-497135","title":"Microsoft Edge: Summarization, Translation, and Citation will soon be supported by Microsoft Copilot and Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat in our menus","desc":"Menus in Edge where the user has highlighted content in the browser will soon support a summarization, translation, and citation with Microsoft Copilot and Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-23","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497135","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-498641","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.145 - Add “Summarize” and “Explain” Copilot actions in PDF reader","desc":"Microsoft Edge will expand its existing “Ask Copilot” integration in the built-in PDF reader by introducing two new actions — “Summarize” and “Explain.” These options will allow users to generate a concise overview or simplify complex content within a PDF or selected portion. The new actions build on the existing “Ask Copilot” integration and follow the same enterprise controls and policies.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498641","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-503593","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.145 - Adding protection against malicious sideloaded extensions","desc":"Microsoft Edge will detect and revoke malicious sideloaded extensions.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-25","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503593","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-551198","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.145 - Navigation management for Progress Web Apps","desc":"Microsoft Edge has improved how a Progressive Web App (PWA) handles user navigation. When a user clicks a link, the browser will determine whether it should launch the installed PWA or open a new browser tab to give users a more seamless experience.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-28","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=551198","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-547825","title":"Microsoft Teams: Queues app historical reporting supports 45 days of data","desc":"Historical reporting within Queues app will now support 45 days of historical data. The report will default a 7-day range with ability to customize the reporting range with up to 45 days of history.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-15","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-495466","title":"Outlook: Editor (Proofing and Spellcheck)","desc":"Automatic spelling and grammar checking when composing an email message. Corrections are underlined on the draft, and clicking on them reveals suggested corrections.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-29","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495466","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-498897","title":"Outlook: Global Address List Redesign","desc":"The Global Address List, or Address Book, is getting a major visual redesign to make it easier to navigate, show more contact information in the search results list, improve its accessibility, and improve its appearance overall. This window is accessible via the To/Cc/Bcc buttons in the email compose form. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-22","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498897","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-483488","title":"Outlook: External tag in contact suggestions","desc":"An \"External\" tag will be added to contact suggestions that appear in the dropdown when entering contacts in the email compose form in the new Outlook for Windows. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-28","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483488","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-483487","title":"Outlook: New Outlook for Windows - Reply To header","desc":"Users will be able to toggle a \"Reply to\" field in the email compose form, which will allow them to add one or multiple addresses which will be used as the recipients for any replies to that message. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-11","modified":"2026-02-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483487","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-484851","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Pulse - Authoring with M365 Copilot","desc":"Viva Pulse authors can now work with M365 Copilot to add a question, rewrite a question, and create a survey from scratch to quickly create and send their surveys to their teams to collect feedback. M365 Copilot can seamlessly capture the author's needs to recommend survey questions that fit their unique scenario. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-11","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484851","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-495833","title":"Microsoft Edge: A Refreshed Profile Flyout Experience for Better Clarity and Actionability","desc":"We’re updating the Microsoft Edge profile flyout to deliver a cleaner, more intuitive experience. The refreshed design makes it easier to distinguish between work and personal profiles, manage credentials, and quickly access key settings—all within a polished interface that supports modern browsing needs. With streamlined sign-in, clearer profile types, and organization branding preserved, this update enables a more efficient and trustworthy experience for customers.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-04","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-526786","title":"Excel: Python in Excel","desc":"Python in Excel allows you to bring the capabilities of Python directly into the Excel grid. As a part of this feature, users will be able to add Python formulas directly into their workbooks without any installation required. These Python formulas will be run by Excel in a secure container on the Microsoft Cloud with enterprise-level security as a compliant Microsoft 365 connected experience.","products":["Excel"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526786","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-537275","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention-UX improvements to the DLP Alerts in Purview Portal","desc":"We’re excited to announce UX improvements to the DLP Alerts Portal in Purview to help you triage incidents faster and more efficiently. What’s New: 1. Unified View: Events related to each alert are now available directly on the alerts page — no need to switch to new tab or drill down. 2. Faster Access: Access event details (e.g. Impacted assets) with just 1 click on the main alerts page itself, compared to 4 clicks earlier, reducing triage time significantly. 3. Enhanced Context: We've added 4 new columns - Location, DLP Rule name, DLP Policy name, Rule Action to display key alert and event attributes upfront — giving you more visibility at a glance. 4. Performance Boost: Cache improvements to ensure faster load times and a smoother experience. These updates are designed to streamline your workflow, reduce response times, and give you the context you need — all in a single, efficient view.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-10","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537275","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-530579","title":"Microsoft Teams: Shared call history in Queues app","desc":"Queues app now supports shared history for all missed, incoming, and outgoing calls in a queue. This new feature provides greater visibility and collaboration by allowing users to view a complete call history across the team. Shared history can be enabled by your Teams admin, who can choose to grant access to either: All members of the queue, or Only authorized users","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=530579","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-503111","title":"Outlook: New third-party enriched properties available for customizing profile cards","desc":"Customers can now customize their M365 profile cards by adding new properties such as Cost Center, Role, Employee Type, Employee ID and Division. These properties will show in the Contact Information section and can be ingested from external sources like HR systems, so that users' profiles are enriched with relevant information.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503111","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-490059","title":"Outlook: Offline Support for Calendar - Create, Edit and Delete Event support","desc":"We are adding more offline functionality in the new Outlook for Windows. You will now be able to create, edit, and delete events in your calendar when not connected to the internet. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-07","modified":"2026-02-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490059","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-557176","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Copilot - Billing & usage: High-usage users","desc":"See a list of users with high Copilot pay-as-you-go usage (i.e., greater than 2000 credits). You can buy and assign Copilot licenses to the high-usage users directly on this page.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-13","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557176","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-542182","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Agent Mode in Excel for desktop apps","desc":"Agent Mode is releasing to Copilot in Excel on Windows and Mac enabling users to build and edit workbooks with Copilot using multi-step workflows. Eligible licenses can now select which model to use, including both Open AI and Anthropic models.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-17","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542182","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-493287","title":"Microsoft Edge: Ask Copilot from the address bar","desc":"When users type a search query in the Edge address bar, they will have the option to send their search query directly to Copilot for a synthesized, more targeted answer pulling from across the web (and their work content, for premium users).","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"May CY2025"},{"id":"rm-529847","title":"Outlook: Book a Workspace when Creating an Event","desc":"When creating an event, you can now book a workspace directly from the location field by searching or tapping Browse Workspaces. This feature is only available if you have workspace bookings enabled in settings and by your IT admin.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529847","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-527835","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Agent Mode in Excel","desc":"Agent Mode lets you build and edit workbooks side by side with Copilot. When you're updating budgets, creating financial models, or analyzing data, Agent Mode uses Excel's most powerful tools like tables, charts, PivotTables, and formulas to help you get the job done.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527835","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-532735","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Scheduling with Copilot","desc":"Scheduling with Copilot: Users can now schedule meetings directly from chat. Simply ask Copilot to schedule a meeting with colleagues, and it will find available times, book rooms, draft agendas, and send invites—all within the chat experience. This feature will roll out in phases and is expected to be generally available in Copilot chat across all endpoints for users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license in the coming months.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-21","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532735","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-537204","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-New cmdlet to remove retention from inactive mailboxes","desc":"Today, there is not a way to remove retention policies or labels (called a hold in Exchange) from items in inactive mailboxes in bulk. Now we are introducing a PowerShell cmdlet that enables retention policies or labels to be removed in bulk from these items. This removal will not affect legal holds.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=537204","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-525364","title":"Outlook: Updated Compose Actions in Outlook Mobile","desc":"We are updating the toolbar when composing an email so you can customize the order and placement of the actions to suit your needs.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=525364","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-525365","title":"Outlook: Updated Multi-Select Actions in Outlook Mobile","desc":"We are updating the toolbar when selecting multiple emails so you can customize the order and placement of the actions to suit your needs.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=525365","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-468293","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Advanced editing from camera","desc":"This aligns the capture experience in camera and editor by enabling a seamless switch to the Clipchamp editor to make videos more appealing and impactful using advanced edit capabilities.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-11-14","modified":"2026-02-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=468293","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-536578","title":"Microsoft Entra: Microsoft Security Copilot App Lifecycle Management Agent in Microsoft Entra","desc":"Application Lifecycle Management Agent: This agent unifies the entire application lifecycle into one intelligent workflow—replacing multiple disconnected admin tasks with a single, guided experience. It automatically discovers unmanaged private apps using Global Secure Access telemetry, recommends onboarding them to Microsoft Entra, and handles setup with automated naming, tagging, and least-privilege scoping. After onboarding, the agent continuously monitors app usage and permissions, flags unused high privileged apps and proactively notifies owners with clear next steps via Teams or email. Using the data the agent has gathered, it suggests a phased disablement plan that admins can customize to their risk prioritization preferences.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536578","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-557174","title":"OneDrive: Microsoft 365 Copilot in OneDrive","desc":"We're excited to bring M365 Copilot in OneDrive, a new unified Copilot chat experience designed to make working with your files simpler, smarter, and more seamless across Microsoft 365.","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=557174","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-511797","title":"OneNote: Copilot Notebooks available in OneNote on Web","desc":"Users will now have access to their Copilot Notebooks on the web version of OneNote.","products":["OneNote"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511797","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-395793","title":"Outlook: Support for Auto-Expanding Archives","desc":"Auto-Expanding Archives are a component that provides customers the ability to grow their mailbox archives over the normal 100 GB quota limit.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-05-02","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=395793","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC High"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-555240","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Search Helps You Discover People","desc":"Now Copilot Search can return matching people for your broader people search queries. Allowing you to discover, disambiguate, and explore known and new people to contact. Discover Whether you're looking for people with a specific skill like \"Project leadership\" or \"Artificial Intelligence\" Copilot Search can help you explore potential contacts through the People data source. Disambiguate When there are multiple people matching in exact name, email, or alias Copilot Search will help you disambiguate through a new carousel on the main results page alongside other relevant results.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=555240","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-548643","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): People Skills - Expanded AI inferencing for E3/E5 users","desc":"People Skills is expanding AI powered skill inferencing to include Microsoft 365 E3 and E5 licensed users. Previously, AI powered skill inferencing was available only to Microsoft 365 Copilot and Microsoft Viva licensed users. With this update, admins will have the option to turn on AI powered skill inferencing for Microsoft 365 E3 / E5 licensed users directly in the Microsoft 365 admin center. AI powered skill inferencing uses AI to automatically identify and update skills on users’ Microsoft 365 profiles based on their work activity from the Microsoft Graph. This control will be available to tenants with Copilot licenses.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548643","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"mc-MC1231437","title":"Update PowerPoint to maintain Captions","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nTo maintain a high-quality and reliable experience for live Captions & Subtitles in the Microsoft 365 PowerPoint app, Microsoft is upgrading the backend service that supports this capability. As part of this improvement, older Office client versions will no longer be supported. Updating to the minimum required PowerPoint version ensures continued accessibility, performance, and reliability.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nUpgrade by the end of September 2026\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using Microsoft 365 PowerPoint app (Win32 or Mac)\n\n• Users running PowerPoint versions earlier than:\n\n• Windows (Win32): 16.0.19426.20218\n\n• macOS: 16.103.1207.4\n\n[What will happen:]\n\n• Users on unsupported versions will lose access to Captions & Subtitles after the listed dates.\n\n• There is no change for users on supported versions.\n\n• No changes to default settings or admin configuration are required.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Review PowerPoint client versions across your organization (Windows and Mac).\n• Update Office clients to:• Windows (Win32): 16.0.19426.20218 or later\n• macOS: 16.103.1207.4 or later\n\n• Plan upgrades ahead of September 2026, especially for environments on managed or restricted update cadences.\n\n• Notify helpdesk and accessibility stakeholders.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-12","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1231437","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-543242","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Chat] Agent Mode in Excel","desc":"Available for Microsoft 365 subscribers without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license. Agent Mode is releasing to Copilot in Excel for the web, Windows and Mac, enabling users to build and edit workbooks with Copilot using multi-step workflows. When you're updating budgets, creating financial models, or analyzing data, Agent Mode uses Excel's most powerful tools like tables, charts, PivotTables, and formulas to help you get the job done.","products":["Excel","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543242","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-505438","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit capability for selecting permission reading option for existing ServiceNow Knowledge & Catalog Connections","desc":"Earlier admins had to create new connections to adopt to the hierarchical permissions for ServiceNow Knowledge & Catalog Copilot Connectors as the edit capability was missing. Now, admins can easily edit their existing connections to switch between the permission handling option i.e. Simple vs Advanced to quickly adopt to the hierarchical permission feature.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505438","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-429645","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Teams Channels in Context IQ","desc":"Users will be able to search for and select Teams Channels in the Context IQ menu to help ground their prompts when using Copilot Chat.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-02","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=429645","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-416091","title":"Outlook: Sort by Flag option","desc":"We are adding support for sort by flag status, flag due date and flag start date.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-12","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=416091","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-506847","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): New Create module with Word, Excel and PPT templates","desc":"New Create module within M365 Copilot App to access Word, Excel and PPT templates.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-02","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506847","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-497161","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Increased efficiency with auto-generated Copilot Pages","desc":"Copilot Chat can automatically create and open a Page side-by-side when it detects a relevant scenario, enabling instant editing, steering, and sharing.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-24","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497161","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-488100","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Camera Update","desc":"Camera in our editor will be updated to a newer version with improved recording controls and command bar options.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-02","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488100","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-488099","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Windows Widget","desc":"With Microsoft Clipchamp Windows widget, Windows 11 users will have a quick way to launch screen recording, camera recording and create video projects.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-02","modified":"2026-02-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488099","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-515169","title":"Microsoft Teams: Update user labels to show familiarity with external users","desc":"Trust Indicators are visual badges next to external users in Microsoft Teams that show a person’s trust level. They help you quickly see if someone is internal, external, a guest, or anonymous. This lets you collaborate confidently with users from external organizations and avoid sharing sensitive information with the wrong audience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-21","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515169","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-547836","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Navigation improvements in Reporting","desc":"Viva Glint Reporting users like managers and leaders will be able to retrace their navigation flow i.e. drill down and drill up in reports rather than lose their navigation flow within reports. Navigation improvements will replace \"Go Back\" to Reporting home page with an alternative clickable UX to enable users to go back to the last page of reporting they were in. In other words, this feature will cater to Back navigation improvements in Reporting.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547836","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-515163","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Query Bitbucket Pull Requests with Copilot Connectors","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Bitbucket with Copilot connectors to query knowledge base content and pull requests.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-25","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515163","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515162","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Query GitLab Merge Requests and Content with Copilot","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to GitLab with Copilot connectors to query knowledge base content and merge requests","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515162","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515166","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Query Miro Visuals with Microsoft 365 Copilot Connectors","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Miro with Copilot connectors to query visual boards and diagrams.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515166","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526777","title":"Microsoft Teams: Interpreter in Microsoft Teams calls","desc":"We’re expanding the Interpreter agent in Microsoft Teams to include real-time speech-to-speech interpretation for Teams calls. This brings the same functionality previously available in meetings to calls, enabling users to speak and listen in up to nine supported languages. Interpreter helps eliminate language barriers and fosters seamless collaboration across global teams. For a more inclusive experience, users can also opt to have Interpreter simulate their personal voice.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526777","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526781","title":"Microsoft Teams: VDI optimization monitoring in Best practice configurations dashboard","desc":"Administrator can monitor which locations and users across their organization are facing meeting quality issues due to unoptimized VDI.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526781","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-513277","title":"Microsoft Viva: Block posts with theme moderation","desc":"Theme moderation in Engage will soon offer an option to block message creation if content aligns with a theme. This change expands on the previous release to monitor and mute content based on themes. When a theme is blocked, users will see a message explaining why their message can't be published. Users can edit or discard the message. Admins and corporate communicators can control where blocks happen across storylines and communities. Leaders, corporate communicators, and network/verified/Engage admins cannot be blocked regardless of theme.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515159","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Aha! to manage product features and customer ideas with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Aha! to manage product features and customer ideas with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515159","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515178","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Shortcut to manage agile development workflows with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Shortcut to manage agile development workflows with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515178","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-527839","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Use Copilot with OneDrive files in Finder","desc":"We’re bringing the power of Microsoft 365 Copilot directly into your daily file management experience in macOS. With this update, users can interact with Copilot in Finder to ask questions about their OneDrive files.","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-478924","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage - Multi-language posts","desc":"Authors of Viva Engage posts will be able to add multiple manually written translations to a single post.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-14","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=478924","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-505443","title":"Microsoft Teams: Search for images","desc":"Search for images by message content, people, or where they were shared. See results as you type, filter to show only images, or explore them in the dedicated Images tab — all from the search bar.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505443","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-498320","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Summarize email with Copilot chat in Outlook","desc":"Users without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license can now easily summarize emails in a single click, using Copilot chat. Users must have access to Copilot chat and pinning enabled to utilize. This change is coming to both Classic and New Outlook for Windows #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-16","modified":"2026-02-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498320","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-500894","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Expanding access to Diagnostics to Compliance Administrator, Security Administrator and Organization Management","desc":"We are expanding the access to Diagnostics beyond Global Admin to: Compliance Administrator, Security Administrator and Organization Management.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-19","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500894","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-505437","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Ticket Status updates more frequently in ServiceNow Tickets Copilot Connector","desc":"ServiceNow Tickets Copilot connector did not use to correctly update the ticket status because of not ingesting inactive tickets. But now, the connector updates the change in ticket status more frequently. Additionally, users can now edit the data query filter to include inactive tickets even for existing connections. By default, copilot connectors now ingest both active & inactive tickets to ensure better quality responses in Copilot connectors.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505437","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-522536","title":"Microsoft Edge: Cross-platform policies in the Edge management service","desc":"Admins can now configure policies for Edge for Business across macOS, iOS, and Android devices on top of their existing Windows configurations in the Edge management service.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-29","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=522536","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-523212","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Purview in Microsoft Admin Center","desc":"AI and IT admins in Microsoft Admin Center can 1) gain visibility around oversharing risks and drive remediations 2) Understand how much of sensitive copilot interactions are protected and turn on Purview DLP for M365 Copilot right from there. Enables secure adoption of Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523212","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-518642","title":"Microsoft Purview: Inline data security controls (DLP) for file uploads to unmanaged GenAI apps in Edge for Business","desc":"Inline protections for file upload protection are directly integrated into for Edge for Business to help prevent data leakage when users upload files to consumer GenAI apps in the browser. In addition to existing text upload controls in Purview collection and DLP policies, Admins can now detect and enforce inline protections on file uploads. Policies can target file-specific conditions such as file size, file type, and sensitive information types, enabling organizations to audit or block activities for users in Edge on Intune-managed Windows devices.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-28","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518642","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-518643","title":"Microsoft Purview: Inline data security controls (DLP) for more unmanaged GenAI apps in Edge for Business","desc":"Inline protections for text and file uploads, directly integrated into for Edge for Business, can be applied to more unmanaged consumer GenAI apps. Admins can now apply Purview collection policies and Purview DLP policies to detect and protect inline against sensitive data sharing in the Edge browser by users on Intune-managed Windows devices to a selection of new unmanaged app locations.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-28","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518643","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-503315","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Graph API support for Working Hours and Location","desc":"We're adding support in Microsoft Graph to read and write users' Working Hours and Location #MicrosoftPlaces","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503315","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-526792","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention- Mac device and device group-based policy scoping support for Endpoint DLP","desc":"Currently you can create Purview Endpoint DLP policy and assign to specific users or user groups. This feature will allow you to create and assign policy based on both users and machines. You can use this feature to achieve different policies for same user on different Mac devices.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-02-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526792","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-508526","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 Copilot Search Supports SharePoint Online Custom Properties Search","desc":"Discover and find people through Microsoft 365 Copilot Search based on your company's custom profile properties from SharePoint Online.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=508526","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-470026","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Custom user mapping for SuccessFactors integration","desc":"Admins can now specify the user mapping attributes in the LMS setup form.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-24","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470026","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-501584","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Admins can govern and manage federated copilot connectors in Microsoft 365 admin center","desc":"Admins can govern and manage federated copilot connectors in Microsoft 365 admin center. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-06","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501584","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-475058","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - User analytics","desc":"With this feature, insights will be generated for potentially risky behaviors at a user level and will be surfaced across the following experiences: 1) Insider risk management context in DLP alert investigation 2) Insider risk management context in Communication compliance alert investigation 3) Insider risk management context in Microsoft Defender XDR user entity page 4) Advanced hunting in Microsoft Defender XDR User analytics will cover all eligible users in the tenant including users not in the scope of any Insider risk management policy. Customers can enable/disable user analytics in their tenant from Insider Risk Management settings. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-23","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=475058","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"March CY2025"},{"id":"rm-518290","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Preview and chat with Word, Excel, and PowerPoint files in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on Android","desc":"When opening a Microsoft Word, Excel, or PowerPoint file in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on Android, users will see a preview experience where they can use M365 Copilot Chat to command and ask questions about the file. If users wish to edit the document, they will transition to the standalone Word, Excel, or PowerPoint app. PDF scenarios are not affected. The feature will begin a phased rollout in December.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518290","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-495464","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Dashboard - Benchmarks","desc":"Compare Copilot active usage with benchmarks in Copilot Dashboard. External benchmarks will provide a reference for how usage compares to other companies. Internal benchmarks will enable users to compare similar groups, within your company. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-29","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495464","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-485755","title":"Outlook: Read-only access to contacts within a PST file in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"With this update of support for .pst files (a.k.a. Outlook Data File) in the new Outlook for Windows, users will be able to browse and read contacts within a .pst file. Future releases of new Outlook will expand the support for .pst file capabilities. #newoutlookforwindows #pstfilesupport.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-19","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485755","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-484081","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance center: Insider Risk Management - Policy scoping enhancements","desc":"After further review, we continue rolling this out. We apologize for any inconvenience. With this release, Insider Risk Management administrators can include or exclude specific users, groups, and adaptive scopes within policies. We are also adding support for non-mail enabled Security Groups within IRM policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-10","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484081","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"April CY2025"},{"id":"rm-412942","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - User exclusion","desc":"After further review, we continue rolling this out. We apologize for any inconvenience. This introduces the ability to exclude users and groups from IRM policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-05","modified":"2026-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=412942","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"mc-MC1227454","title":"Exchange Web Services (EWS) retirement update","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nWe're updating the timeline and process for the retirement of Exchange Web Services (EWS) in Exchange Online. As previously announced, EWS will be retired in favor of Microsoft Graph, which offers improved security, modern authentication, and broader capability support. A phased disablement begins October 1, 2026, with permanent shutdown starting April 1, 2027.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Phased EWS disablement begins: October 1, 2026\n\n• Full and permanent EWS retirement: April 1, 2027\n\n• EWS App AllowList feature availability: Coming soon (before retirement milestones)\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using custom or vendor applications that rely on EWS\n\n• Workflows involving mail, calendar, or integrations that use EWS\n\n• This change only impacts Exchange Online; Exchange Server (on-premises) is not affected\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Beginning October 1, 2026, EWS will be blocked unless the tenant configures an AppID AllowList and sets EWSEnabled=True.\n\n• Without admin action, Microsoft will set EWSEnabled=False and EWS apps will stop working. Tenant admins will be able to re-enable EWS if necessary.\n\n• Temporary “scream tests” may occur before October 2026 to help identify dependencies.\n\n• After April 1, 2027, EWS access will be permanently removed with no re-enablement.\n• No changes are being made to EWS in Exchange Server (on-premises).\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Review EWS usage in the Microsoft 365 admin center or using published scripts to identify dependent applications.\n\n• Begin migrating any remaining EWS-based workflows to Microsoft Graph, which provides near-complete API parity.\n\n• If EWS is required after October 2026, configure an AppID AllowList and set EWSEnabled=True before end of August 2026.\n\n• Communicate these changes internally and update documentation.\n\nLearn more:\n• Deprecation of Exchange Web Services in Exchange Online\n• EWS Retirement Process overview\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Exchange Online"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-05","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1227454","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-513282","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Dropbox to access and manage cloud files with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Dropbox to access and manage cloud files with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-13","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513282","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-495003","title":"Microsoft Teams: Open Teams' apps in new window","desc":"Organize your work environment to fit your needs. Users can open Teams' apps, like Chat, Calls, Activity and more in separate windows, allowing users to view and interact with these apps simultaneously.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-27","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495003","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-469503","title":"OneDrive: Agents in OneDrive","desc":"Find yourself referencing the same files using Copilot in OneDrive? We are bringing the power of agents to OneDrive, allowing you to build, use, and share your own agents using files and content stored in your OneDrive. This feature requires a Microsoft Copilot for Microsoft 365 license and will be available to customers on OneDrive Web.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-11-27","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=469503","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-365059","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Enhanced Classification Support for Thai Language in Endpoint","desc":"Thai Language sentences do not have spaces in between them. And for classification purpose, we relied on right keywords to be added while creating Sensitive Information Type for ensuring accurate match. However, with this feature, spaces will be added automatically in keywords which will ensure higher match accuracy in EndPoint.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-02-29","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=365059","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-366697","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Enhanced Classification Support for Thai language in Exchange Online, Microsoft Teams, SharePoint, and OneDrive","desc":"In our continued efforts to enhance classification capabilities, we have added a new feature, Word-Breaker, to our existing Thai Language support in Classification. Words in Thai language sentences do not have spaces between them. And for classification purpose, we relied on the right keywords to be added while creating Sensitive Information Type for ensuring accurate match. However, with this feature, spaces will be added automatically in keywords which will ensure higher match accuracy across all cloud locations (Exchange, Teams, One Drive, SharePoint).","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-01-20","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=366697","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-413717","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Customer Facing Reports via Insights Integration","desc":"Org level breakdown of Learning metrics in Viva Insights.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-10-04","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=413717","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-414523","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Sync provider data from a specific date range","desc":"We are introducing flexibility on provider setup form where admins can sync data from specific dates for a provider instead of full data sync.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-04","modified":"2026-02-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=414523","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-480730","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Risky AI usage","desc":"With this update, Insider Risk Management will help admins identify risky AI usage. We are adding new detections of intentional and unintentional insider risk activity on generative AI apps that can pose a risk to an organization. Activities will include risky prompts containing sensitive info or risky intent and sensitive responses containing sensitive info or is generated from sensitive files or sites. Coverage will span across Microsoft Copilots and 3P generative AI apps. These detections will also contribute to Adaptive Protection insider risk levels. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-11","modified":"2026-02-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480730","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-509110","title":"Microsoft Teams: Open channels in a new window","desc":"You can now open channels in a separate window to stay on top of multiple conversations at once.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-03","modified":"2026-02-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=509110","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513270","title":"Microsoft Teams: 1080P Resolution in Teams Town Halls","desc":"Teams town hall will soon bring 1080P resolution to Teams town hall. This enhancement brings a sharper appearance with more visual clarity to videos, images, and other visual assets within your online events. This feature is available for town halls created by organizers with a Teams Premium license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2026-02-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513270","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-500701","title":"Microsoft Teams: Facilitator can help manage tasks and create documents","desc":"Facilitator can help users manage tasks and create documents during meetings. In addition to the tasks that the agent is automatically capturing during the meeting, users can ask Facilitator directly through the meeting chat to create, edit, and assign tasks, which sync to Planner. For tasks related to document creation, users can assign to Facilitator and it will draft the document based on the meeting discussion. Users can also ask the agent to create a draft document on a topic discussed in the meeting.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2026-02-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500701","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-518228","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing new AI analysis capabilities","desc":"Data Security Investigations (DSI) now features advanced AI analysis tools, including options to add investigative context for higher-quality results, as well as improvements in vector search relevance and content categorization to better identify risky material. Additionally, we've launched a new AI-powered search function that lets investigators use natural language to locate specific files by searching through keywords, metadata, and embeddings.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518228","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-518225","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introduction of both in-product cost estimator and transparency report","desc":"Introducing a Data Security Investigations (DSI) lightweight cost estimator designed to help analysts model and forecast both storage and compute unit costs based on specific use cases, enabling more accurate budget planning. In addition to the estimator, a new report provides granular breakdowns of billed storage and compute unit usage, empowering DSI analysts to identify cost-saving opportunities and optimize resource allocation.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518225","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"mc-MC1226495","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Live Events is retiring","desc":"[Introduction]\nMicrosoft is retiring Teams Live Events and the Microsoft Graph APIs used to create them on June 30, 2026. Existing events scheduled before that date will continue to function through February 28, 2027. We encourage customers to migrate to Teams town halls, which offer an enhanced, end-to-end experience for large-scale events. This retirement supports Microsoft’s investment in Teams town halls, which provide an improved experience for digital and hybrid events and include comparable Graph APIs for programmatic creation, management, and integration.\n[When this will happen]\n• Teams Live Events and associated Microsoft Graph APIs will retire on June 30, 2026.\n• Existing Teams Live Events will continue to function through February 28, 2027.\n• Customers will no longer be able to schedule Teams Live Events past June 30, 2026, beginning February 3, 2026.\n• Customers scheduling through Dynamics 365 will not be able to schedule events past June 30, 2026, beginning February 3, 2026.\n• The isBroadcast property within the onlineMeetingGraph resource will remain available until June 30, 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization]\nYou are receiving this message because our reporting indicates your organization may be using or has access to Teams Live Events.\nWho is affected:\n• Organizations using Teams Live Events.\n• Organizations using Microsoft Graph APIs to create Teams Live Events.\n• Organizations scheduling Teams Live Events through Viva Engage or Microsoft Dynamics 365.\n\nWhat will happen:\n• Teams Live Events and the associated Microsoft Graph APIs will no longer be available after retirement.\n• Teams town hall is now the recommended option for large scale events.\n• New scheduling of Teams Live Events will become limited as the retirement date approaches.\n• Existing scheduled events will remain supported through the end of the service window.\n• Workflows or applications that depend on the isBroadcast property will need to transition.\n• Teams town halls and Teams meeting Graph APIs will serve as replacements for large-scale broadcast scenarios.\n• Customers should migrate to Teams town halls or Teams meeting Graph APIs.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\nNo admin configuration changes are required. We recommend the following:\n• Assess dependencies\n• Identify where your organization uses Teams Live Events, including events scheduled through Viva Engage, Dynamics 365, or custom Graph-based solutions.\n• Plan your transition\n• Move large-scale broadcast and virtual event scenarios to Teams town halls or Teams meetings.\n• Update or replace workflows that rely on the retiring Graph API functionality.\n• Prepare users\n• Inform event organizers and producers about the retirement and their transition path.\n• Update internal training, documentation, and support materials.\n\nUse these resources\n• Plan for Teams town halls | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn\n• Get started with town hall in Microsoft Teams | Meetings | Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Support\n• Retiring Teams live events: The next chapter for events at scale in Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Teams Blog\n\n• Virtual events town hall API use cases | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\n• Customer Hub events readiness sessions - recommended for Teams Live Events users transitioning to Teams town halls:\n• What’s new in Microsoft Teams town halls and webinars\n• Migrating from Teams Live Events to town halls\n• Tips, tricks, and traps for town halls and webinars in Microsoft Teams\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-02-03","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1226495","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-494517","title":"Microsoft 365: Microsoft 365 Backup capabilities available in GCC","desc":"We are bringing Microsoft 365 Backup Service capabilities to GCC. Microsoft 365 Backup is a product offering spanning across the OneDrive, SharePoint, and Exchange Online services that provides customers with a consistent, cross product solution, to recover their M365 data from cataclysmic events such as: at scale ransomware attacks, or malicious/accidental data deletion/corruption by end users.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-02","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494517","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-523819","title":"Planner: Support for Microsoft Information Protection (MIP) content sensitivity labels","desc":"Microsoft Information Protection (MIP) content sensitivity label support in Planner will enable encryption, restrict unauthorised actions such as copying, printing, or exporting plan contents, and add visual markings like watermarks for clear sensitivity awareness. By enforcing content-level protections, Planner will help organisations prevent data leaks, maintain compliance, and enable secure collaboration without affecting productivity.","products":["Planner"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523819","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-496370","title":"Excel: Formula completion with Copilot in Excel","desc":"This feature leverages AI to autocomplete the user's formula upon typing the '=' sign. It provides context-based suggestions, streamlining the formula creation process by offering intelligent and relevant completions.","products":["Excel"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-28","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496370","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-313800","title":"Microsoft Teams: Apply partial settings for Android devices using configuration profiles in the Teams admin center","desc":"In the Teams admin center, admins can now modify, review, and apply configuration settings to Android devices without overriding other settings ensuring only the desired changes are made.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-04","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=313800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-477822","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Detailed error description for SuccessFactors sync failures","desc":"Sync failure details pop-up will now have detailed error description and next steps.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-13","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=477822","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-477817","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Ingestion logs in Viva Learning for SAP SuccessFactors","desc":"This creates LMS ingestion logs for sync summary, user sync, and LRS data. Logs will help admins debug any ingestion-related issues.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-05","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=477817","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-485780","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Ability to view inferred skills and course recommendations","desc":"Learners would be able to select skills for learning, view inferred skills and courses recommendations based on inferred skills. Inferred skills are generated by taking users activity in M365 ecosystem into account.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-25","modified":"2026-02-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485780","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-396562","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft365): Graph API - Copilot for Microsoft 365 usage","desc":"Copilot for Microsoft 365 usage will be added to the Microsoft Graph API, allowing for the creation of customized reporting and analytics. Metrics included in the Graph API will match those available in the Copilot for Microsoft 365 usage report in the Microsoft 365 admin center, including tenant-level count of enabled users and active users, as well as last activity date per user (all up and per Microsoft 365 app). #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-05-15","modified":"2026-02-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=396562","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"September CY2024"},{"id":"rm-553225","title":"Microsoft 365: New map-based room booking experience in Places Finder","desc":"We are enhancing the room booking experience in the new calendar experience across Outlook for Windows, Outlook for the web, and Teams by introducing a map view within Places Finder. This update replaces the existing side panel with a full screen, easier to use interface that helps people quickly find and book the right space.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553225","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2026","gaSort":202608},{"id":"rm-552589","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Customize M365 Copilot for your organization with Copilot Tuning","desc":"Microsoft 365 Copilot Tuning is introducing new templates in Agent Builder, designed for tasks such as drafting complex documents, validating documents against guidelines, and editing to match a distinct writing style. Users with Copilot Tuning enabled can further customize the template-based agents by tuning the context, tools, and underlying models with their organization’s proprietary data, processes, and standards. This empowers your teams with customized agents aligned to how your organization works.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=552589","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-553222","title":"Microsoft Intune: macOS Custom Compliance","desc":"This feature will enable users to use discovery script and json file to define compliance policy to specific organziational needs. The experience mirrors Windows and Linux custom compliance experience.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-30","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=553222","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-542795","title":"Microsoft Teams: Automatic removal of EXIF data from shared images","desc":"Teams will automatically remove hidden metadata (EXIF) from images shared in conversations. This privacy protection helps prevent sensitive information such as photo location and device details from being shared without your knowledge.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542795","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-543714","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint DLP - Enhanced content extraction and file type coverage for DLP on Mac devices","desc":"With this release, the file type coverage to scan, classify and protect sensitive content on Mac devices with Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention policies will increase from current ~40 file types to 100+ file types. This release will make the coverage of file types on endpoint consistent with other locations such as Exchange, SharePoint and OneDrive.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-29","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543714","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-536570","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ability for IT admins to customize the user notification strings for recording and transcription","desc":"IT admins can customize the message and privacy link used to notify implicitly or gain explicit consent from meeting participants for the use of recording, transcription during the meeting.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536570","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526784","title":"Microsoft Teams: Troubleshoot meetings and calls with automatic issue identification and recommendations","desc":"Administrators can troubleshoot Teams meetings and calls in Teams admin center with ease with a streamlined flow, meeting quality issues, and detailed telemetry.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526784","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-503300","title":"Microsoft Teams: Emojis in Section Names","desc":"Choose an emoji to accompany section names in your chats and channels list.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503300","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-496368","title":"Microsoft Teams: Front-of-room view control for Town Hall and Webinar in Teams Rooms on Windows","desc":"When a Teams Rooms on Windows is invited as a meeting presenter, the front-of-room display defaults to the attendee view. Presenters always have full control from the console, including green room and off-stage management, and can switch the front-of-room display to presenter view without impacting attendees. Available in Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-13","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496368","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-478610","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams client health dashboards in Teams Admin Center","desc":"IT Administrators can view and monitor the health of Teams desktop clients on both Windows and Mac platforms. This feature offers comprehensive admin actionable insights into client health metrics, including client crashes and launch failures. Administrators are equipped with detailed information on issues, insights, and mitigation tools to promptly and effectively address any potential client health problems.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-28","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=478610","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-483882","title":"PowerPoint: Designer is now part of Copilot, enhanced with new template and slide Suggestions.","desc":"Designer is now part of Copilot. Copilot Suggestions now brings you familiar Designer slide layout and presentation template suggestions in a vertical gallery, along with new capabilities.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","PowerPoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-04","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483882","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-470436","title":"Excel: Post-migration Excel remediation","desc":"Enable the remediation of incompatible formulas and file links in formulas in Excel files after migration from other cloud platforms to Microsoft 365.","products":["Excel"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-12-02","modified":"2026-01-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470436","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-511813","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Highlights on Copilot adoption from Viva Engage","desc":"Explore how Copilot is making a difference in your organization through Viva Engage posts that users have shared. The Copilot Dashboard showcases real-world success stories, user-shared excitement about new Copilot features, and vibrant community discussions. These examples offer a qualitative view into how Copilot is driving productivity and engagement across your tenant, directly in the Copilot Dashboard. #CopilotControlSystem","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-01-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511813","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-515172","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Auto-Archive for Exchange Online","desc":"A new capability called Auto-Archiving for Exchange Online will enter public preview in November 2025 (currently under private preview for selected customers). When a user's mailbox utilization exceeds 95% of its quota and archive mailbox is present, this feature automatically moves the oldest items excluding those tagged with “Never Move to Archive” from the primary mailbox to the archive mailbox to prevent mail flow disruptions by keeping usage below the safe threshold of 95% of mailbox quota.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-01-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515172","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-527838","title":"Outlook: Updated Copilot Button for Android","desc":"We are updating the UI for Copilot Chat so that the button is separate from the mail and event compose buttons. This feature will be available for users with a Copilot license.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-01-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527838","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-478647","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): In Copilot Pages, the Chat can now be used to modify the Page","desc":"When a Chat and a Page are open side by side, prompts within the Chat can now be used to modify or add to the contents of the Page.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-10","modified":"2026-01-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=478647","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"mc-MC1220762","title":"(Updated) Retirement notice: MDE and XDR Advanced Hunting APIs retiring; migrate to Microsoft Graph Security API","desc":"Updated January 26, 2026: We have updated the content. Thank you for your patience.\n[Introduction]\n\nWe’re retiring the Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (MDE) Advanced Hunting API and Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting API and transitioning customers to the Microsoft Graph Security API. This update aligns our security integrations with a unified interface and schema across Microsoft Defender products. The Microsoft Graph Security API provides broader data coverage, improved consistency, and better scalability for automation and security workflows.\n\n[When this will happen]\n• Retirement start: February 6, 2026\n• Full retirement: February 1, 2027\n\n• After February 1, 2027, the MDE and XDR APIs will no longer function.\n\n[How this affects your organization]\n\nWho is affected:\n• Organizations using the MDE or XDR Advanced Hunting API for automation, integration, or custom workflows.\n• You are receiving this message because our reporting indicates your organization may be using these APIs.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• The MDE and XDR Advanced Hunting APIs will stop functioning after February 1, 2027.\n\n• Existing scripts, automations, and workflows that rely on these APIs will fail if not updated.\n\n• The Microsoft Graph Security API will be the supported API for accessing Microsoft security data.\n\n• No automatic migration will occur; manual updates will be required.\n\n[What you can do to prepare]\n\n• Migrate all existing API workflows to the Microsoft Graph Security API by January 31, 2027.\n\n• Update internal documentation, automation scripts, and integration endpoints to use the Microsoft Graph Security API.\n\n• Communicate these changes to your security operations, engineering, and development teams.\n\n• Review Microsoft documentation to plan your migration: Use the Microsoft Graph security API.\n\n• If your organization uses custom solutions, validate that new queries and response schemas work as expected before the retirement date.\n\nLearn more:\n• Advanced hunting - Use the Microsoft Graph security API | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\n• Migrate from the older APIs - Use the Microsoft Graph security API | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\n• (to be retired) Advanced Hunting API - Microsoft Defender for Endpoint | Microsoft Learn\n• (to be retired) Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting API - Microsoft Defender XDR | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified. Review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Defender XDR"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-22","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1220762","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-522537","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - Improved Autofill experience in Microsoft Edge","desc":"When users fill in an Address on a form, they will be prompted to choose whether to save it for future Autofill suggestions. This enhancement ensures Autofill data is saved intentionally by users and reduces unwanted entries as part of their Autofill suggestion.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-29","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=522537","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-527833","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - New WebGL software backend","desc":"Microsoft Edge, on Windows systems without a physical GPU, will use the Windows Advanced Rasterization Platform (WARP) rasterizer for WebGL workloads. Prior versions use SwiftShader. This scenario is most common associated with headless environments and virtual machines. On non-Windows platforms, a physical GPU will be required for WebGL moving forward.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-14","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"more":"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flearn.microsoft.com%2Fen-us%2Fwindows%2Fwin32%2Fdirect3darticles%2Fdirectx-warp&data=05%7C02%7Cv-zbeg%40microsoft.com%7Cf203f7982a30414cb90a08de1e5e8d5d%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C638981588692598882%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=bK82pFEbE%2BVGvJO%2FbPYUuc8OmyOrOLCY2bhdmks936Q%3D&reserved=0"},{"id":"rm-536580","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - Tenant Restrictions v2 (TRv2)","desc":"New enforcement to block access from unauthorized Microsoft 365 tenants directly in Microsoft Edge for Business, helping organizations maintain strict compliance and prevent data leakage across tenant boundaries.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-03","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536580","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-498915","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Information Protection - Admin unit scoping in Content Explorer and Data Explorer","desc":"This feature introduces Admin Unit scoping to both Content Explorer and Data Explorer, enabling more granular visibility and control over M365 data. It ensures that data exploration respects organizational boundaries defined by Admin Units, enhancing compliance and governance.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-23","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498915","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-518224","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Content Explorer – Enhanced Tag (SIT, Labels) Filter at UI Layer","desc":"Introduces enhanced controls in Content Explorer’s UI, enabling scoped visibility and filtering of SIT and label data. This will help with content discoverability and governance.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518224","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-527834","title":"Microsoft Purview: Information Protection-Email attachment Preview in Activity Explorer","desc":"We're enhancing Activity Explorer to provide greater visibility into sensitive data flagged in Exchange Online. Previously, only the message body was viewable, which limited insight into flagged content. With this update, admins will be able to preview email attachments directly within Activity Explorer—without needing to download the email.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-25","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-485709","title":"Microsoft Teams: Migration Tool for Teams","desc":"Customers will now be able to migrate content seamlessly from Slack public and private channels to Teams shared, public, and private channels. A new first-party migration tool in the Microsoft Admin Center (MAC) will allow admins to review which Slack channels they wish to migrate, then perform content migration to Teams.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-21","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485709","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-498922","title":"Microsoft Viva: Focus Area simplification and enhancements","desc":"Beginning with this feature release, Focus Areas will be associated with survey cycles and goal periods will be retired. Users will be able to select the same Focus Area across multiple cycles. The Focus Area Overview report will be filterable to groups of interest (e.g. managers only). Draft/deleted Focus Areas will no longer be included in Focus Area calculations.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-24","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498922","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-518223","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management-Introduction of secure workflow to bypass retention holds and delete Teams transcripts and/or Teams recordings","desc":"Introducing a capability to Purview compliance admins via a Data Lifecycle Management to bypass retention hold or legal holds to delete content on OneDrive or SharePoint Online such as Teams meeting transcripts and/or recordings earlier than the hold durations to comply with emerging compliance requirements. Leveraging Simulation, authoring approvals, Audit and disposition reviews to set-up and enforce defensible policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518223","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-526783","title":"Microsoft Viva: Update storyline cover photos in Teams for iOS.","desc":"Users will be able to update their storyline cover photo from Teams for iOS. This is already currently supported on Teams for Android or Windows, Mac, on the web.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-08","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526783","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-492621","title":"SharePoint: Permissions report for a given user - SharePoint admin center","desc":"This report, under Data access governance within SharePoint admin center, provides SharePoint admin with a list of sites where the given user has direct and indirect permissions at a site/lib/folder/file level","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492621","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-520386","title":"Outlook: Outlook for Android supports PDF attachment preview","desc":"Users can now preview PDFs directly in the Outlook for Android app.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=520386","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-413114","title":"Outlook: People Hub improvements in new Outlook for Windows","desc":"In new Outlook for Windows, the People Hub offers a streamlined contacts interface with a single view of each person, automatically linking duplicates and enriching them with organizational profiles. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-30","modified":"2026-01-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=413114","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-547835","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention- Source context based file protection for Endpoint","desc":"Protect file based on the website the file is downloaded or the app the file is created.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-27","modified":"2026-01-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547835","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-493749","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Custom permissions UI enhancements in Microsoft Purview Information Protection File Labeler","desc":"This feature borrows the familiar custom permissions menu in Office and replaces the existing custom permissions UI in the Microsoft Purview Information Protection File Labeler. The new menu enables viewer, restricted editor, editor and owner permissions to be assigned to multiple groups at the same time.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-15","modified":"2026-01-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493749","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2026","gaSort":202607,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-548669","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention- Logged-in user details on the Purview device onboarding page","desc":"This update introduces logged-in user details (user email) on the device onboarding page for Windows devices bringing it in line with the experience for MacOS devices. ​Admins can now see which user is currently signed in on a device, making It faster to confirm ownership and troubleshoot issues.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-23","modified":"2026-01-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=548669","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-499661","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Export Executive Summary report in Viva Glint to editable PowerPoint slides","desc":"Managers will be able to export the default sections from the Executive Summary report in Viva Glint directly to editable PowerPoint slides. This enhancement allows for easier and quicker consumption of this report outside Viva Glint, compared to the previous export method which included static screenshots.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-12","modified":"2026-01-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499661","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-487848","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot can now answer questions about opened Copilot Pages in chat","desc":"When using Copilot Pages side-by-side in Copilot Chat, you can now ask questions in chat about your open page, and Copilot will provide answers based on the contents of that page.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-21","modified":"2026-01-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487848","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-503571","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Support for refining query filters for Confluence Copilot connectors","desc":"This feature enhances and standardizes query filtering across both Confluence Cloud and Confluence On-premises connectors. For Confluence Cloud connector, it introduces simplified options to filter pages by page id, creation date/time and last update date/time, helping improve productivity and reduce human errors. For Confluence On-premises connector, it adds support for advanced CQL-based filtering, enabling more complex and flexible filtering scenarios.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-11","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503571","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-496363","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: Agent-Level Controls for Pay-as-you-go","desc":"This feature introduces admin controls for managing AI agents on a consumption basis within Microsoft 365 Copilot. Administrators can specify which users can access particular agents through pay-as-you-go, control which agents are available for metered consumption, and establish billing policy for each agent. Initially focusing on declarative agents in M365 Copilot Chat and SharePoint, this enhancement enables organizations to effectively manage AI consumption costs and scale intelligent capabilities according to business needs. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496363","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604,"preview":"April CY2026"},{"id":"rm-518291","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management – Enhancements to variant limits and detection groups","desc":"Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management variant limit is being increased from 3 to 10 per indicator and an overall limit of 100 across all indicators. Along with this, the number of items in one detection group is being increased from 200 to 500. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518291","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-506752","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Data source specific filters","desc":"We are introducing a dynamic filtering experience in Microsoft 365 Copilot search that empowers users to refine their results more precisely by leveraging data source-specific filters in the right rail. When a user selects a data source from the right rail, such as Outlook, SharePoint, Jira, or Copilot Chats, the interface dynamically presents a tailored set of filters specific to that source. These refiners allow users to narrow down results based on attributes unique to the selected data source, such as item type, status, or semantic labels.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft 365"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506752","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-513422","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Steer your presentation length, tone, style, and images when creating with Copilot.","desc":"You can now adjust the length of your presentation, the tone of your narrative, the style of your slides, and leverage AI-generated images when creating with Copilot.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513422","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513431","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Steer your presentation length, tone, style, and images when creating with Copilot.","desc":"You can now adjust the length of your presentation, the tone of your narrative, the style of your slides, and leverage AI-generated images when creating with Copilot.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513431","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513430","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Steer your presentation length, tone, style, and images when creating with Copilot.","desc":"You can now adjust the length of your presentation, the tone of your narrative, the style of your slides, and leverage AI-generated images when creating with Copilot.","products":["PowerPoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513430","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-520772","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention - Data Loss Prevention to restrict Microsoft 365 Copilot processing on content with sensitivity labels","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention is extended to Microsoft 365 Copilot. This feature will allow DLP policies to provide detection of sensitivity labels in enterprise grounding data and restrict access of the content in Microsoft 365 Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Purview","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=520772","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-522095","title":"Microsoft Purview: Inline protection, alerting, and incident management for sensitive data shared over the network through non-Microsoft SASE integrations","desc":"Extend Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies and Insider Risk Management indicators to the network by integrating with your existing non-Microsoft Secure Access Service Edge (SASE) solution. This integration enables organizations to intercept and inspect traffic inline at the network layer and enforce actions based on DLP policy conditions. It helps prevent sensitive data from being shared with untrusted cloud applications through browsers, apps, APIs, add-ins, and more - including generative AI platforms, cloud storage, and content-sharing services - while managing alerts and incidents through Purview and Microsoft Defender. If configured, these signals also inform user risk indicators in Insider Risk Management","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=522095","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-488297","title":"SharePoint: Copilot actions in SharePoint document libraries","desc":"When you select an item in OneDrive on the Web, the Copilot button appears, offering a range of actions you can perform on that item. The same feature and actions are coming to document library views in SharePoint and Teams.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-18","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488297","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-483519","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Catch up on a summary of document comments in the top of your document","desc":"Copilot will have a Discussion tab in the top of your document to summarize open comments, helping you quickly understand what people have said in comments.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2026-01-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483519","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-529856","title":"Microsoft Entra: ID Account Recovery","desc":"Microsoft Entra ID Account Recovery is an advanced authentication recovery mechanism that enables users to regain access to their organizational accounts when they've lost access to all registered authentication methods. Unlike traditional password reset capabilities, account recovery focuses on identity verification and trust re-establishment prior to replacement of authentication methods rather than simple credential recovery.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-21","modified":"2026-01-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529856","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-484084","title":"Microsoft Purview: Discovery of sensitive data sharing to any cloud application or website (inc. GenAI) via network layer","desc":"With this update, IRM will support the discovery of sensitive files and text shared to any cloud application or website (inc. GenAI) via network layer. This capability is based on integration with 3rd party network partners (with data being captured via network layer). Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-10","modified":"2026-01-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484084","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-486827","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management - Data Security Investigation integration","desc":"Launch a pre-scoped Data Security Investigation (DSI) from an IRM case. When a data security admin identifies a risky user who needs deeper investigation, they can launch a pre-scoped investigation directly from an IRM case, allowing them to view content analysis related to that user and better assess post-incident data impact.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2026-01-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486827","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-547828","title":"Microsoft Edge: Protected Clipboard","desc":"Admins shouldn’t have to choose between locking down copy/paste and risking data leaks. Protected Clipboard offers a smarter way for keeping sensitive data safe without disrupting user workflows. Leveraging Purview DLP policies to define trusted boundaries across managed cloud apps. Data inside those admin defined boundaries can stay protected while external data can enter if needed. Granular control for admins. Seamless productivity for users.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-17","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=547828","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612,"more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-management-protected-clipboard"},{"id":"rm-536579","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - Copilot icon visibility","desc":"Users can now manage the Copilot icon in their toolbar. To hide the icon, right-click the Copilot icon and select “Hide Copilot”. This will open Settings to toggle the icon’s visibility. Admins can control whether the Copilot icon shows in the toolbar using the Microsoft365CopilotChatIconEnabled policy.","products":["Microsoft Edge","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536579","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-534608","title":"Microsoft Edge: v.144 - Performance settings update and feature name changes","desc":"Efficiency mode feature name will change to energy saver and efficiency mode for PC gaming name will be renamed PC gaming boost to better describe the feature benefits. The new names will be in browser performance settings after the update.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-26","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=534608","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-526797","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention- Admin units support for SharePoint Online","desc":"Delegate management and remediation authority for different people in different regions or organization units with role-based access control (RBAC). For example, German investigators should be able to investigate alerts and audit events for only German users. This update extends support to SharePoint for Microsoft 365.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-20","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526797","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-502864","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Generate icons for your agents using AI in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"A picture is worth a thousand words. Before, Microsoft 365 Copilot agent builders would need to use the default icon or manually upload their own image. This process meant browsing the web for an image, asking different teams for icons, or manually drawing one. Users can now use AI to describe how the icon should look like, thus helping inform end users of the agent's function more easily, with more expression. Users can now generate icons using AI in Agent Builder. Users can enter custom prompts or use the description of the agent to generate the icon. Alternatively, users can manually upload their own icon or select from a set of pre-created icons. Icons are capped at 1 MB (192px).","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-17","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502864","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-499024","title":"SharePoint: eSignature - Free Text Field Support","desc":"SharePoint eSignature users would be able to add custom free text fields to their request documents. This new eSignature field can be used to request information (such as address, full name, etc.) from signers.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499024","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-501591","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Data Loss Prevention: DLP to restrict Microsoft 365 Copilot processing on emails with sensitivity labels","desc":"Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention (DLP) is extended to preventing Microsoft 365 Copilot from processing emails with sensitivity labels. This feature will allow DLP policies to provide detection of sensitivity labels in emails as enterprise grounding data and restrict access of the labeled emails in Microsoft 365 Copilot chat experiences.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-02","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501591","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-482189","title":"Microsoft Teams: Local PTZ camera controls for Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"If the camera is not currently auto-framing the room, in-room users can now control the Pan-Tilt-Zoom (PTZ) of the active camera to keep the focus where they want it.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-27","modified":"2026-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482189","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"mc-MC1218421","title":"Retirement of Power BI Q&A","desc":"Introduction\n\nWe are announcing the retirement of Q&A, Power BI’s legacy natural language tool. Starting December 2026, Q&A experiences will be retired. Moving forward, users can leverage Power BI Copilot, which offers a more advanced and integrated solution for querying data using generative AI. This change reduces feature overlap, accelerates innovation, and provides a consistent experience across Power BI.\n\nWhen this will happen:\nQ&A experiences and Q&A Setup will be fully retired by the end of December 2026.\nHow this affects your organization:\n\nWho is affected: All organizations using Q&A experiences in Power BI reports, dashboards, mobile, or embedded analytics.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Creation of new Q&A visuals or experiences will no longer be permitted after December 2026.\n\n• Existing Q&A visuals in reports, dashboards, mobile, and embedded scenarios will stop working and will be removed.\n\n• Q&A Setup tools (synonyms, linguistic relationships, teach Q&A, etc.) will be retired.\n\n• Users should transition to Power BI Copilot for natural language queries and insights.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n\n• Review reports and dashboards for Q&A visuals and plan to replace them with Copilot experiences. Learn more: Microsoft Power BI Updates Blog: Deprecating Power BI Q&A.\n• Familiarize yourself with Power BI Copilot and Prep Data for AI as alternatives to Q&A and Q&A Setup.\n\n• Update internal documentation and helpdesk guidance to reflect this change.\n\nCompliance considerations:\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Power BI"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-16","modified":"2026-01-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1218421","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-500873","title":"Microsoft 365: eSignature Smart Tagging for Electronically Signed Documents","desc":"Documents that have been electronically signed will now be automatically recognized and tagged as “Signed” upon upload to SharePoint. This enhancement also applies retroactively as existing e-signed files will be updated with the appropriate tags. To give users more visibility and control, we’re introducing two optional metadata columns for document libraries: Electronically Signed – Indicates whether a document has been eSigned. Signature Provider – Displays the service used for the eSignature. This feature is available exclusively to tenants with eSignature enabled, helping streamline compliance tracking and document management.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-19","modified":"2026-01-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500873","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-494515","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Catchup on important emails in Copilot Chat","desc":"Copilot Chat helps you stay on top of your inbox by highlighting important and actionable emails such as messages from your manager, leadership, top collaborators, or emails containing tasks when you use prompts like “What’s hot in my inbox?” or “What were the important emails from last week?”","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-04","modified":"2026-01-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494515","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-483355","title":"Microsoft Teams: Share apps from app bar via right click","desc":"Allow users to right-click and share apps directly from the app icon on hover, while using the app.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-02-27","modified":"2026-01-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483355","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-65632","title":"Excel: Refresh queries from Authenticated Data Sources in Excel for the Web","desc":"<div>You can now refresh Power Query data from data sources that require authentication in Excel for the Web. </div>","products":["Excel"],"status":"Launched","created":"2023-08-22","modified":"2026-01-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=65632","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release (Entire Organization)"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-503295","title":"Microsoft Teams: New Policy Setting to Require Explicit Consent for Recording and Transcription in Teams 1:1 Calls","desc":"We're expanding the capability to require explicit consent for recording and transcription to include 1:1 calls in Microsoft Teams. A new setting in the Teams Calling policy allows admins to enforce this requirement before recording or transcription can begin. When a user with the policy initiates recording, transcription, or both in a 1:1 call, the other participant is automatically muted, with their camera and content sharing turned off. The participant will see a prompt asking whether they consent to be included in the recording and transcription.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-23","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503295","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-505436","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Knowledge templates support for ServiceNow Knowledge Connector","desc":"Earlier ServiceNow Knowledge connector did not support ingestion of content for articles created using templates in ServiceNow. But now ServiceNow Knowledge connector supports ingestion of knowledge articles based on out-of-the-box templates like FAQ, How to, What is, etc. & even custom templates used by the customers in their organization.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=505436","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-523207","title":"Outlook: Collapsible Automatic Replies on Outlook for Android","desc":"Now when users receive multiple automatic replies at once, they appear collapsed in the reading pane by default. Users can then expand to see all the automatic replies if desired.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523207","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-523208","title":"Outlook: Collapsible Automatic Replies on Outlook for iOS","desc":"Now when users receive multiple automatic replies at once, they appear collapsed in the reading pane by default. Users can then expand to see all the automatic replies if desired.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523208","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-499421","title":"Microsoft Viva: Enhancement to Copilot studio agents report","desc":"Following further review, this feature continues in development. We apologize for any inconvenience. Enhancement to Copilot studio agents report (Preview) 1. Addition of Weekly active user count 2. Report aggregation changed to weekly to main consistency with other reports","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-30","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499421","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-410245","title":"Microsoft 365: Multi-Geo In-Region Routing","desc":"Multi-Geo In-Region Routing (IRR) enables customers to control the routing of inbound emails. Using IRR, customers can set the geo-region that inbound mail should be routed to for specific Accepted Domains.","products":["Microsoft 365","Exchange"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-08-06","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=410245","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"October CY2025"},{"id":"rm-485733","title":"Microsoft Purview Information Protection: Doc library default labeling for SharePoint Online and Copilot","desc":"This new capability further integrates SharePoint Online with Purview sensitivity labeling. SharePoint Online document library owners can set a new type of default label on the library, which automatically applies that label to all unprotected Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and PDF files within the library. This simplifies labeling in bulk across document libraries in an organization, enriches DLP and Copilot with signal to allow admins to monitor and restrict access to this content, and enables inheritance of sensitivity labels to output artifacts in Copilot. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485733","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-490055","title":"Microsoft Teams: Silent test call","desc":"Silent Test enables IT administrators to proactively run synthetic Teams call simulations to specific subnets, helping assess network readiness and detect potential issues before they impact users, ensuring a seamless communication experience.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-28","modified":"2026-01-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490055","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-545012","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): When using Agent Mode in Word, you will be able to manually select which model to use","desc":"Agent Mode in Word lets you choose from multiple models, giving you flexibility to select the right model for your task.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-13","modified":"2026-01-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=545012","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-526789","title":"Microsoft Purview: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention- Show customized message or hyperlink for multiple file toast","desc":"With this feature when multiple files are involved in a DLP enforcement action, the policy tip will now show multiple files and their respective status.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526789","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-536997","title":"Microsoft Teams: Select multiple messages to forward","desc":"You can now select up to five messages from a chat or channel and forward them together in one message—preserving both context and order.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536997","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-493756","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management- Multi selectable DLP policies as an IRM triggering event","desc":"Insider Risk Management is releasing the ability to select multiple Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies as triggering events in a policy. Previously, admins could only select one DLP policy as a triggering event within Insider Risk Management policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-20","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493756","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-503764","title":"Microsoft Purview: Insider Risk Management-Data Security Alert Triage Agent in Insider Risk Management","desc":"Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management (IRM) introduces the Security Copilot Alert Triage Agent in IRM that analyzes and prioritizes IRM alerts so analysts can understand and act on their most urgent alerts first. On top of prioritizing critical alerts for analysts to triage first, alert triage agent will provide a summary of findings to help users understand what are the riskiest activities that make this alert critical to review. IRM correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. IRM enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-22","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503764","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-496654","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Analytics - Copilot Employee Experience Outcomes Report with Viva Glint","desc":"A new Power BI report in Viva Insights highlights the relationships and impact of M365 Copilot usage on employee experience sentiment outcomes in Viva Glint. This report enables robust analysis by allowing users to slice and dice data based on Copilot usage segments, different sentiment outcomes and organizational attributes. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-13","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496654","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-489229","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint and Viva Insights Integration - Workplace Patterns Report in Viva Glint","desc":"An intuitive report that highlights the relationships between employee sentiment items and the workplace patterns and drivers that shape engagement. This feature eliminates the need for custom analysis, enabling users to share out of the box actionable insights with leaders—accelerating decision-making to drive meaningful actions across the organization","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-30","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489229","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-502867","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Agent Ownership Reassignment","desc":"Admins can reassign ownership of shared agents created within the organization through tools such as Copilot Studio or the Microsoft 365 Agents Toolkit. Once reassigned, the new owner will gain full edit and delete permissions, along with access to any files uploaded by the previous owner. The former owner will lose all access, including read rights. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502867","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-491633","title":"Microsoft Teams: Customize the screen in Teams Town hall through \"Manage what attendees see\"","desc":"Organizers will be able to effortlessly enhance their Teams Town hall presentations. In “Manage what attendees see” users will be able to customize their screen using select layouts, backgrounds, and name tags, resulting in a polished, high-quality, and engaging event. This feature is available with a Teams Premium License.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-09","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491633","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-501427","title":"SharePoint: Content Management Assessment (CMA)","desc":"The Content Management Assessment (CMA) helps tenant admins quickly evaluate site health, permissions, and lifecycle readiness—all in a single, actionable dashboard. It brings together multiple SAM reports, including Site Lifecycle Management (SLM) and Data Access Governance (DAG), and delivers clear, tailored recommendations to strengthen governance and prepare for Copilot onboarding. How it works: - CMA streamlines a process that was once manual and time-consuming: - CMA automatically runs backend APIs to generate reports such as SLM and DAG. - Results are presented in a clean, easy-to-read dashboard with actionable guidance. Preview highlights: - Clearer, more accessible UI - Refined tooltips and issue categories - Easier navigation across reports Getting started: 1. Open the SharePoint Admin Center. 2. Go to Advanced Management. 3. Select “Start a free content assessment.” 4. Review results and explore tailored recommendations. 5. Share your feedback to help shape future improvements.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-28","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501427","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-367423","title":"Excel: Enable \"View Side by Side\" on Mac","desc":"You can now quickly compare worksheets in the same workbook or in different workbooks by viewing them side by side with synchronous scrolling and reset window positioning on Mac.","products":["Excel"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-15","modified":"2026-01-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=367423","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"mc-MC1215070","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center multifactor authentication enforcement","desc":"If you have already set up multi-factor authentication, thank you. No further action is needed at this time. If you have not, please read on.\nAs part of our ongoing commitment to advancing cybersecurity across our company and products, last year, starting February 2025, Microsoft began requiring all users to use multi-factor authentication (MFA) when signing into the Microsoft 365 admin center. Starting February 9th 2026, Microsoft will continue to ramp up enforcement, and users will be unable to sign in to the Microsoft 365 admin center without successfully completing MFA.\n\nImplementing MFA in the Microsoft 365 admin center significantly reduces the risk of account compromise, prevents unauthorized access, and safeguards sensitive data. By adding an extra layer of protection beyond standard username and password authentication, MFA makes it harder for attackers to steal data and prevents unauthorized access from phishing, credential stuffing, brute force, or password reuse attacks.\nTake action now\nGlobal admins: To set up MFA in your organization now, visit the MFA setup guide at aka.ms/MFAWizard or refer to Set up multifactor authentication for Microsoft 365\n\nUsers accessing the Microsoft 365 admin center: Check your verification methods and add one if needed by going to aka.ms/mfasetup.\n\nHow this will affect your organization\n\nMFA will need to be enabled for your tenant to ensure admins are able to sign-in to the Microsoft 365 admin center. Note that the following Microsoft 365 admin center URLs are impacted by this change:\n\n• https://portal.office.com/adminportal/home\n\n• https://admin.cloud.microsoft\n\n• https://admin.microsoft.com\n\nWhat to do to prepare\n\n• If you have not already, set up MFA as soon as possible to avoid sign-in issues once mandatory MFA enforcement is rolled out to your organization.\n\n• If you have already set up MFA, no action is required. It is recommended that you verify that all users accessing the Microsoft 365 admin center have added a verification method to their account (such as a Microsoft Authenticator).\n\n• Global admins: To set up MFA in your organization now, visit the MFA setup guide at aka.ms/MFAWizard or refer to Set up multifactor authentication for Microsoft 365.\n\n• Users accessing the Microsoft 365 admin center: Check your verification methods and add one if needed by going to aka.ms/mfasetup.\n\nFor more information, refer to the FAQs in the blog post here.\nAdditional info URL (i.e., link to relevant support doc):\nhttps://aka.ms/mfasetup\n\nMultifactor authentication for Microsoft 365 - Microsoft 365 admin | Microsoft Learn\n\nSet up multifactor authentication for users - Microsoft 365 admin | Microsoft Learn","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-08","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1215070","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-536569","title":"Microsoft Viva: Update Engage community cover photos in Teams for iOS","desc":"Admins of communities in Viva Engage will be able to update their community cover photo from Teams for iOS. This is already currently supported on Teams for Android or Windows, Mac, on the web.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-04","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536569","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-526707","title":"Microsoft Viva: Search Engage conversations in Teams mobile","desc":"Users will be able to search for Viva Engage conversations directly in the Viva Engage app for Teams.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-20","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526707","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS","Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-499620","title":"Microsoft Teams: Customize captions on Mobile","desc":"Live captions are now available on mobile devices with enhanced customization options, making captions easier to read and follow during meetings. You can personalize your captions by adjusting the font color, caption background color, and caption height. These enhancements ensure captions remain accessible and comfortable, especially under varying lighting conditions or when you're on the go.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-08","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499620","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-490212","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Improved Python-powered answers in Copilot in Excel","desc":"Copilot in Excel now provides improved direct answers to your data analysis questions, using Python.","products":["Excel","Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-01","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490212","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-474126","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage - Community replies and reactions in Teams","desc":"Users with the Viva Engage app in Teams will now receive notifications when others reply or react to their posts.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-01-08","modified":"2026-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=474126","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-543208","title":"Outlook: Sort by flag","desc":"We are adding support for sort by flag status, flag due date and flag start date.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2026-01-06","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543208","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605},{"id":"rm-480726","title":"Microsoft Viva: SharePoint agent analytics on Viva Insights","desc":"Explore how your employees used key SharePoint agent features over a given time period and understand the ROI. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-14","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480726","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"February CY2026"},{"id":"rm-509108","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 Copilot - your AI assistant in the GCCH environment","desc":"Bringing Microsoft 365 Copilot your AI assistant for work in the GCC-H environment. It combines the power of Large Language Models with your work content and context, to help you draft and rewrite, summarize and organize, catch up on what you missed, and get answers to questions via open prompts. Copilot generates answers using the rich, people-centric data and insights available in the Microsoft Graph. Microsoft 365 Copilot is available in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app (web), Teams, Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OneNote, SharePoint, and Clipchamp.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-15","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=509108","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-509107","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat - General Availability for the GCC High environment","desc":"Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat will be generally available for the GCC High environment, and it will be delivered with web grounding OFF by default. This is required to help protect US government sensitive information which should not leave the GCC High compliance boundary.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-02","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=509107","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-497638","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Import Non-M365 data into review set for modern eDiscovery","desc":"Microsoft Purview modern eDiscovery experience now enables legal and compliance teams to import non-Microsoft 365 data directly into review set as part of the modern eDiscovery workflow. This feature allows organizations to consolidate all their data into a single secure review environment for streamlined review.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-06-26","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497638","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-520389","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhancements to Interpreter and multilingual meeting experience","desc":"First, spoken language is now automatically detected and updated across Interpreter, live captions, and live transcription when Interpreter is enabled, keeping all speech features consistent with the language being spoken - no manual setup required. When Interpreter is disabled, live captions and transcription will still work, but auto-update spoken language will not be available, which may result in gibberish or inaccurate content if participants switch languages during the meeting. Next, a new “preparing” status provides clear visual feedback while Interpreter initializes, helping users know when the system is ready -especially important for multilingual meetings. Lastly, Interpreter settings have also been improved with concise explanations for each configuration and field, making setup easier and minimizing confusion.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-12","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=520389","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-503148","title":"Microsoft Viva: User Schema Enhancements - Delete Attributes","desc":"This feature enables Viva Glint admins to delete custom user attributes directly in the platform. This empowers admins to easily update and maintain the structure of user data without requiring support.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-17","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503148","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-499425","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Generating PPT grounded on a Copilot Page","desc":"Generating PPT grounded on a Copilot Page","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-07-30","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499425","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-417481","title":"SharePoint: Enterprise Application Insights for SharePoint sites","desc":"Enterprise Application Insights is a powerful report which helps SharePoint Administrators to discover all the SharePoint sites that are allowed access by third-party applications registered in your tenant. The report also provides details on the application's permission and requests count to help admins take further action to strengthen the security of the site. It is part of SharePoint Advanced Management capabilities. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-09-19","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=417481","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"January CY2025"},{"id":"rm-399921","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Automatic summary of documents on file-open in Word","desc":"When you open a document, Copilot will generate a summary in the Word window. You can hide the summary or open the Copilot chat pane to ask specific questions about the document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Launched","created":"2024-06-12","modified":"2026-01-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=399921","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2024","gaSort":202408},{"id":"rm-493755","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Experience enhancements to IRM alert investigation workflow","desc":"Experience enhancements to IRM alert investigation workflow including updates to the alert's \"All risk factors\" page and activity explorer. These enhancements will give customers the ability to maximize the visual space for their investigation. We are adding to each component a minimize/ maximize button and hiding the horizontal banner on the Alerts pages by default. We are also enhancing the All Risk Factors page for better UX.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2026-01-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493755","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-532736","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Model Selector in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"The Model Selector in Microsoft 365 Copilot gives users more control over reasoning depth, enabling automatic reasoning for simple tasks and explicit control when desired. The three modes that are supported as part of GPT-5 are: Auto (default) - system decides how long to think, Quick response - answers right away, Think deeper - Thinks longer for better answers.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-21","modified":"2025-12-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=532736","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-500702","title":"Microsoft Teams: Join town halls and webinars as an attendee from Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android","desc":"Microsoft Teams Rooms on Android can now join Town Halls in Teams as attendees. You can attend directly from the invited Teams Room, with the same features that attendees have for Town Halls on the Teams desktop app. Available in Teams Rooms Pro.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-08-28","modified":"2025-12-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500702","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-523216","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Add a Partner to Viva Glint","desc":"This feature will simplify the process to onboard external resources (Partners) to your Viva Glint instance.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2025-12-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523216","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-506753","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] [1.02] Generate Word, Excel, and PowerPoint documents from agents built in Microsoft 365 Copilot","desc":"With Agent Builder inside Microsoft 365 Copilot, users can now use Office skills like generating PowerPoint decks, Excel spreadsheets, and Word documents by chatting with the agent. This helps users save time by completing commonly used tasks. These Office skills will come as a part of the \"Generate documents, charts, and code\" capability in Agent Builder (formerly known as Code Interpreter).","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-11-11","modified":"2025-12-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506753","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-529855","title":"Microsoft Entra: Conditional Access support for Entra ID Account Recovery","desc":"Microsoft Entra ID Account Recovery is an advanced authentication recovery mechanism that enables users to regain access to their organizational accounts when they've lost access to all registered authentication methods. This feature adds additional support for protecting the account recovery flow by enabling CA policies to be applied. Learn more","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-23","modified":"2025-12-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2026","gaSort":202605,"preview":"March CY2026"},{"id":"rm-542929","title":"Exchange: Message Trace - Custom Retention","desc":"We will be introducing customizable retention options for Message Trace logs. Organizations will be able to choose from a predefined set of retention periods.","products":["Exchange"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2025-12-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=542929","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2026","gaSort":202612},{"id":"rm-543241","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Chat] Agent mode in Word enables conversational support to create, edit and refine document content from chat","desc":"Available for M365 users without a M365 Copilot license. From Chat, you can use natural language to generate and direct edits to new and existing documents, when in an Edit mode. In this mode, Copilot will ask clarifying questions if needed, and after making changes will recap actions take and recommended next steps. Changes to the document are supported with controls in the document canvas to review changes made.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2025-12-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=543241","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-529842","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Recommended Notebooks in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Users can quickly create new Copilot Notebooks via Recommended Notebooks based on recent user work activity.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2025-12-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529842","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-529843","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Suggested References in Copilot Notebooks","desc":"Users can now quickly enrich their Copilot Notebook with relevant Suggested References based on recent user work activity.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-19","modified":"2025-12-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529843","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"mc-MC1127222","title":"(Updated) Please update Microsoft 365 Office apps to a version higher than 16.0.18827.20202","desc":"Updated December 12, 2025: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nTo ensure continued high-quality performance of the Read Aloud, Transcription, and Dictation features in Microsoft 365 Office apps, we’re upgrading the backend service that powers these capabilities. As a result, these features will no longer function on Office clients running versions earlier than 16.0.18827.20202 after September 2026.\nWe are extending the supporting period for customers to prepare and upgrade to the supported version. Here is the updated timeline:\n\n• General Availability (Worldwide): End of September 2026 (previously end of January)\n\n• General Availability (GCC, GCC High, DoD): End of November 2026 (previously end of March)\n\nHow this affects your organization\n\nIf your organization is using Microsoft 365 Office apps with version numbers lower than 16.0.18827.20202, users will lose access to Read Aloud, Transcription, and Dictation features after the dates listed above.\n\nThere is no change to the user experience for clients on supported versions.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\nTo avoid service disruption, ensure that all Office clients are updated to version 16.0.18827.20202 or later before the applicable deadline.\n\nYou can learn more about these features using the following resources:\n\n• Listen to your Word documents\n• Transcribe your recordings\n• Dictate your documents in Word\n\nCompliance considerations\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 apps"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-01","modified":"2025-12-12","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1127222","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202512},{"id":"mc-MC1192661","title":"Workspaces in Edge: Upcoming migration to improved architecture","desc":"[Introduction]\n\nWe’re improving the reliability and performance of Microsoft Edge Workspaces by migrating to a new architecture. Workspaces, introduced in 2022, lets users create durable sets of tabs that can be saved and shared. As part of this update, we will migrate saved Workspace data from OneDrive/SharePoint to the Edge Sync service and remove the collaboration/share functionality.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nGeneral Availability (Production, GCC, GCCH, DoD): Rollout begins mid-February 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\n\nWho is affected: All organizations using Microsoft Edge Workspaces.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Saved Workspace data will migrate from OneDrive/SharePoint to Edge Sync service.\n\n• Collaboration and sharing functionality will be removed.\n\n• Organizations that have disabled Workspaces via EdgeWorkspacesEnabled policy will not have data migrated.\n\n• If Sync is disabled through policy, existing Workspaces created under the current architecture will still migrate. However, new Workspaces created after migration will not sync across devices and will remain local to each device.\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• No admin action is required; migration will occur automatically during rollout.\n\n• If you wish to opt out, contact Microsoft CSS before rollout begins.\n\n• If your organization has significant Workspace usage, notify users and update internal documentation.\n\nLearn more: Workspaces in Microsoft Edge\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-06","modified":"2025-12-06","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1192661","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-529859","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit a Page using Copilot Chat on Mobile","desc":"Mobile users can now use Copilot Chat to edit Pages.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2025-12-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529859","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-536575","title":"Microsoft Intune: Assignment filters support for Apple declarative device management (DDM)","desc":"Admins can use assignment filters when targeting Apple DDM policies.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-05","modified":"2025-12-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=536575","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"mc-MC1191924","title":"Microsoft Entra ID: Enhance protection of the authentication experience by blocking external script injection","desc":"Introduction\n\nAs part of Microsoft’s Secure Future Initiative, we’re updating our Content Security Policy for the Microsoft Entra ID sign-in experience. This change adds an extra layer of protection by allowing only scripts from trusted Microsoft domains to run during authentication, blocking unauthorized or injected external code. This proactive measure helps safeguard users against threats like cross-site scripting (XSS), further strengthening security for your organization.\n\nWhen this will happen\n\nGeneral Availability (Production/Worldwide only):\n\n• Rollout begins mid-October 2026\n\n• Expected completion by late October 2026\n\nPeriodic communications will be sent closer to release.\n\nHow this affects your organization\n\nWho is affected:\n\n• Organizations using browser-based sign-in experiences on URLs starting with login.microsoftonline.com.\n\n• No impact to Microsoft Entra External ID tenants.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• A new Content Security Policy header will be added to Microsoft Entra sign-in pages.\n\n• Scripts will only be allowed from Microsoft trusted CDN domains.\n\n• Inline script execution will only be allowed from trusted Microsoft sources.\n\n• Browser extensions or tools that inject code into the sign-in page will stop working, though users can still sign in.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\n\n• If you do not use tools or extensions that inject code into the sign-in experience, no action is required.\n\n• If you do use such tools, switch to alternatives that don’t inject code.\n\n• Test your sign-in flows thoroughly before rollout to identify and resolve any issues early. Testing instructions can be found on our CSP Guide for Microsoft Entra ID.\n\nLearn more:\n• Content Security Policy Overview for Microsoft Entra ID\n• Microsoft Entra ID Content Security Policy Public Blog Post on Techcommunity\n• Microsoft Secure Future Initiative\n• The CSP nonce guide | Content Security Policy (CSP) quick reference guide\n• The CSP script-src directive guide | Content Security Policy (CSP) quick reference guide\n• Why XSS still matters: MSRC’s perspective on a 25-year-old threat | Microsoft Blog\n\nCompliance considerations\n\nNo compliance considerations identified; review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-12-03","modified":"2025-12-03","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1191924","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501457","title":"Microsoft Intune: Recovery Lock management for macOS","desc":"This feature adds the ability to manage the password used to access the macOS recovery partition. Configuring a recovery OS password prevents users from booting company-owned devices into recovery mode, reinstalling macOS, and bypassing remote management.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-09","modified":"2025-12-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501457","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-529852","title":"Microsoft Purview: Communication Compliance- Alert improvements","desc":"Communication Compliance is improving the capabilities and customization of policy alerts. Admins will be able to customize the alert frequency per policy as well as adjust the email alerts frequency and recipients within the policy creation wizard. Microsoft Purview Communication Compliance provides the tools to help organizations detect regulatory compliance violations (for example SEC or FINRA), such as sensitive or confidential information, harassing or threatening language, and sharing of adult content. Built with privacy by design, usernames are pseudonymized by default, role-based access controls are built in, investigators are opted in by an admin, and audit logs are in place to ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-12-02","modified":"2025-12-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-489454","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Loss Prevention OCR Cost Estimator Support for MAC Endpoints","desc":"OCR Cost Estimator allows you to estimate the potential cost for using Optical Character Recognition. This means that you will no longer be required to set up an Azure Subscription for billing first and can accurately estimate the cost you would have incurred while using OCR. This will help you to identify the optimal configuration settings for OCR as per your requirements. Cost Estimator can be used for 30 days and will not scan images for sensitive content.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2025-12-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489454","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-513273","title":"SharePoint: M365 Agent Access Insights for SharePoint and OneDrive sites","desc":"Rich insights on agents accessing content in SharePoint and OneDrive sites as part of SharePoint Advanced Management controls.","products":["OneDrive","SharePoint"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-30","modified":"2025-11-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513273","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-529857","title":"Microsoft Entra: ID Account Recovery","desc":"Self-Serv Account Recovery for tenants using Passkey.Account Recovery from Total Loss using Verified ID with Face Check","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-21","modified":"2025-11-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=529857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-528932","title":"Microsoft Forms: Enable Sensitivity Labels","desc":"Microsoft Forms will enable sensitivity labels, empowering organizations to control access and manage information protection directly within Forms. Authors and co-authors will be able to manually assign or edit sensitivity labels on forms, ensuring that only users with appropriate permissions can access form design and response pages. Sensitivity labels will also be inherited by Excel files generated from Forms, maintaining consistent data protection across exported content.","products":["Forms"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2025-11-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=528932","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-502855","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Chat in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneNote, and Outlook for DoD","desc":"Easily access Copilot Chat from a side pane in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneNote, and Outlook. This is available for Copilot Chat users with a Microsoft 365 license and for Microsoft 365 Copilot licensed users.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-05","modified":"2025-11-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-527829","title":"Microsoft Teams: Enhancements to channel agents","desc":"Each channel can have a dedicated agent that draws on the channel’s knowledge to act as a domain expert for the team. New enhancements enable the agent to use files from the channel’s SharePoint when responding to queries, create ad hoc status reports configured through natural language, and generate new workback plans that can be added to Planner. In addition, new controls in Teams Admin Center allow admins to disable automatic agent creation.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2025-11-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527829","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-518641","title":"SharePoint: Page Agent","desc":"The SharePoint Page Agent is a declarative agent that enables users to create and refine SharePoint pages directly within BizChat or other Copilot apps. It seamlessly integrates SharePoint authoring into everyday conversations, eliminating the need to switch apps or manually open SharePoint. With this feature, users can generate structured content such as meeting recaps, announcements, and project updates, create SharePoint pages instantly from chat.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2025-11-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518641","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-523222","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Your Command Center for AI Success","desc":"The refreshed Copilot landing page in Microsoft 365 admin center gives an at-a-glance view of your Copilot journey across Chat, Agents, and M365 Copilot. It includes success metrics for each pillar, new metrics like active chat users, assisted hours, and satisfaction rate, plus multi-signal, personalized and actionable insights to drive adoption. We’ve added a security pivot for Purview actions and centralized Copilot usage reports under a new usage pivot.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2025-11-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=523222","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"mc-MC1188230","title":"Microsoft Entra ID: Retirement of duplicative properties in passkey (FIDO2) authentication methods policy","desc":"Introduction\n\nStarting October 2027 and ending November 2027, we will retire the isAttestationEnforced and keyRestrictionsproperties from the existing fido2AuthenticationMethodConfiguration API schema. This change aligns with the latest update to the passkey policy API schema, which introduces support for granular group-based configurations with passkey profiles.\n\nDuring the retirement period, isAttestationEnforced and keyRestrictions will remain in sync with their counterparts attestationEnforcement and keyRestrictions within the Default passkey profile.\n\nWhen this will happen\nRetirement begins in mid-October 2027 and is expected to complete by early November 2027.\n\nHow this affects your organization:\nYou are receiving this message because our reporting indicates your organization may be using this feature.\n\nWho is affected: Admins managing FIDO2 authentication configurations and any custom automations or third-party integrations using these properties.\n\nWhat will happen\n\n• isAttestationEnforced and keyRestrictions properties will be retired.\n\n• New properties are available in the updated passkey policy API schema.\n\n• Existing properties will sync with new ones during the transition period.\n\n• Automations or integrations using retired properties will stop working after the change.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare\n\n• Review your current configuration.\n\n• Update any custom automations and third-party integrations to support the new schema.\n\n• Notify your admins and update internal documentation.\n\nScreenshot - The read arrows indicate the properties to be retired:\n\nLearn more: fido2AuthenticationMethodConfiguration resource type | Microsoft Graph | Microsoft Learn\nCompliance considerations:\n\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-19","modified":"2025-11-19","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1188230","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-518226","title":"Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations – Introducing integration with Data Security Posture Management and deepening integration with Defender XDR, Insider Risk Management","desc":"Data Security Investigations (DSI) insights are now being incorporated into Data Security Posture Management to support the prevention of sensitive content exfiltration. Additionally, DSI integrations with Defender XDR and Insider Risk Management are being enhanced, reflecting customer feedback received during the Public Preview phase.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2025-11-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=518226","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-527837","title":"SharePoint: Get relevant information from Lists in Knowledge Agent","desc":"Users will be able to find relevant information, matching items and get answers from Microsoft Lists using Knowledge Agent.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2025-11-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=527837","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-506848","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Simplified Agent Creation experience","desc":"Drastically simplified first run experience and guide users quickly from idea to success. Faster responses and improved performance for a smoother experience. Familiar, intuitive flow that mirrors Copilot’s simplicity.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-18","modified":"2025-11-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506848","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515466","title":"Microsoft Teams: Channel agent to 3P MCP tool orchestration in Teams channels","desc":"Agent-MCP Orchestration in Teams enables Channel agent to work with select third-party MCP servers, such as GitHub, Asana and Atlassian (JIRA). This setup allows collaborative workflows that mirror real human teamwork. When a user asks Channel Agent a question, the agent can collaborate with other tools to gather information or complete tasks, transparently showing each step of its reasoning along the way.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-10-17","modified":"2025-11-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515466","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-503105","title":"Microsoft Teams: Unified Agent and App Availability Management Across Microsoft 365 and Teams Admin Center","desc":"Administrators using the Microsoft 365 admin center and Teams admin center who manage agents and apps that work across Teams, Outlook and the Microsoft 365 copilot will be able to apply their changes consistently across all these surfaces. Before this update, changes made through the Integrated Apps section in the Microsoft 365 admin center would only affect these apps on Outlook and the Microsoft 365 copilot; similarly, changes made in the Teams admin center would exclusively affect Teams. With this change, app and agent availability will be unified across Teams, Outlook and Microsoft 365 copilot.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2025-11-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503105","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-481135","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Work context suggestions in Copilot Chat ContextIQ menu","desc":"Copilot Chat will suggest prompts and work context you have access to as you type in the prompt, helping you find relevant information for your conversations.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-31","modified":"2025-11-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481135","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-502530","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Streamlined Authentication process with OAuth for Connector Admins","desc":"Effortless authentication, unified through OAuth — empowering Connector Admins to connect in just a few clicks. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-08","modified":"2025-11-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502530","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-526787","title":"Microsoft 365: People Skills profile editing improvements","desc":"People Skills is releasing two updates to give you more control over how others see your skills profile and ease of access for skill profile management. With these updates, you can easily control the order in which the skills you confirm are displayed to others in your profile card. Additionally, you'll find a new deep link directly to skill profile editing from the Skills component on the profile card. These updates will begin rollout to customers in November and are expected to be available to all People Skills customers by December.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-07","modified":"2025-11-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=526787","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-497849","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Press and hold Win + C or Copilot key to activate voice on the Microsoft 365 Copilot app","desc":"Press and hold Win + C keys, or the dedicated Copilot key for applicable devices, and the Microsoft 365 Copilot app will activate voice. With voice, talk to Copilot like a personal assistant - interrupting and redirecting at any time to prepare for the workday, create documents, understand topics, and search for information. This shortcut to activate voice means you don't have to switch between screens to talk with Copilot. Enterprise-grade security and compliance are built in, so conversations stay private while productivity soars.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-21","modified":"2025-11-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497849","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-491022","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Insights - Skills landscape report for organizations","desc":"A Power BI report that provides an overview of the skills distribution in the organization and supports users in identifying skill gaps and making informed decisions on workforce planning, resource allocation, and skilling initiatives.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-15","modified":"2025-11-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491022","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"June CY2025"},{"id":"rm-489217","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot in Excel with Python for GCC High","desc":"Copilot in Excel gains powerful new insights and visualizations with Advanced Analysis. Explore your data in a natural, conversational way, while Copilot does the heavy lifting using Python, a rich programming language that supercharges what is possible in your spreadsheets.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2025-11-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489217","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-511814","title":"Microsoft Viva: Engage Frequent Contributor Analytics","desc":"Updating analytics related to frequent contributors to include more metrics and an enhanced design.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2025-11-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511814","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-506756","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Chat] Apply your brand kit and style to visual creations","desc":"Easily customize your visual content with built-in controls to select your preferred style, choose your visual format, whether it’s a poster, infographic, or image and with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, apply your brand kit.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2025-11-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506756","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-506755","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Chat] Apply your brand kit and style to visual creations","desc":"Easily customize your prompt output with built-in controls to select your preferred style and choose the format, whether it’s a poster, infographic, or image. With a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, apply your organization brand kit to create on-brand content without manually uploading assets and describing your style.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-05","modified":"2025-11-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=506755","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-513286","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Adobe Experience Manager Assets to retrieve marketing and creative assets with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Adobe Experience Manager Assets to retrieve marketing and creative assets with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2025-11-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513286","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-502546","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users can create agents scoped on Custom connector containers","desc":"1. Makers can now scope their data in their agent created on custom connector data at a particular container. 2. These containers will be defined during creation/updating of the custom connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2025-11-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502546","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"mc-MC1182696","title":"Microsoft Defender: Application Guard for Office is being removed","desc":"Microsoft Defender Application Guard for Office was retired in April 2024 and is now being removed from Office. This change aligns with the end of support for Windows 11 version 23H2 and helps streamline the security experience for users. Documents that previously opened in Application Guard will now open in Protected View, maintaining strong protection against threats.\n\nWhen this will happen:\nPhase 1: Removal begins with Office version 2602\n\n• Current Channel: early February 2026\n\n• Monthly Enterprise Channel: April 2026\n\n• Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel: July 2026\n\nPhase 2: Full removal with Office version 2612\n\n• Current Channel: early December 2026\n\n• Monthly Enterprise Channel: February 2027\n\n• Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel: July 2027\n\nHow this affects your organization:\n\nWho is affected: All Win32 users who previously used Microsoft Defender Application Guard for Office.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• Files that previously opened in Application Guard will now open in Protected View.\n\n• Application Guard for Office will be disabled in Phase 1; support exceptions may be available until Phase 2.\n\n• Application Guard for Office will be fully removed in Phase 2 with no workaround.\n\n• Admins are encouraged to enable Microsoft Defender for Endpoint Attack Surface Reduction (ASR) rules and Windows Defender Application Control (WDAC).\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\nNo admin action is required for the removal itself. However, to maintain strong protection, we recommend:\n\n• Enable Microsoft Defender for Endpoint ASR rules to block risky behaviors in Office files.\n\n• Enable Windows Defender Application Control (WDAC) to ensure only trusted, signed code runs on devices.\n\n• Review internal documentation and helpdesk guidance if your organization previously relied on Application Guard for Office.\n\nFor instructions on verifying if users are using Application Guard for Office, refer to Confirm that Application Guard for Office is enabled and working - Application Guard for Office for admins | Microsoft Learn.\n\nCompliance considerations:\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["Microsoft 365 suite"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-11-04","modified":"2025-11-04","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1182696","source":"mc","phases":["Plan for change"],"gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-509112","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot edits on a Page are highlighted by default","desc":"When using Copilot to edit a Page, those changes will be highlighted by default, making it easier to review and confirm your edits.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-31","modified":"2025-10-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=509112","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-396289","title":"Microsoft Edge: AI theme generator","desc":"Microsoft Edge will include an AI theme generator, that allows users to input a text prompt and generate a series of images to preview as browser themes. Applying the theme includes setting the generated image on the Edge new tab page, and applying the image's dominant color to the browser frame. Admins can restrict access to this feature using the AIGenThemesEnabled policy.","products":["Microsoft Edge"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-09","modified":"2025-10-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=396289","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-496142","title":"Outlook: Rule to display desktop alert","desc":"Create rules that trigger a desktop alert when specific emails arrive. This makes it easier to stay on top of important messages without missing a beat. Look for the new \"Display a Desktop Alert\" action when setting up or editing your rules. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-10","modified":"2025-10-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496142","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-503302","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Remove users from closed survey","desc":"This feature will enable Viva Glint Admins to remove survey participants from surveys. The selected survey must have a closed status, and this action will be irreversible.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-28","modified":"2025-10-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503302","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-500380","title":"Microsoft Teams: Private channels increased limits and transition to group compliance","desc":"We are updating private channels to align with compliance model for all channels. After this change, compliance policies applied to the team (M365 Group) will apply to all channels in the team - across standard, private, and shared. Private channels will no longer need user level targeting of policies different from other channels, and private channel compliance messages will no longer be copied to user mailboxes, relying on a dedicated, internal mailbox per channel like shared channels. In addition, limits for private channels will be increased so each team can have more than 30 private channels, up to the 1000 total channel limit per team. Private channel member limits will increase from 250 to 5000. You will also be able to schedule meetings in private channels.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-19","modified":"2025-10-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500380","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-401127","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Microsoft 365 Groups scoping in Teams DLP policy extend protection to 1:1/n chats","desc":"When scoping policies to Microsoft 365 Groups in Teams DLP policies, members of Teams standard and shared channel chats associated with the groups are currently protected by the policies. This change will automatically extend the protection to standard/shared channels chats in other Microsfot 365 Groups and 1:1/n (non-channel) chats. There is no longer a need to add users, security groups or other Microsoft 365 groups to protect these chats, except for customers that have enabled optical character recognition (OCR) in Teams chat.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-06-20","modified":"2025-10-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=401127","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2026","gaSort":202611},{"id":"rm-490060","title":"Outlook: Offline Support for Calendar - Create, Edit and Delete Event support for GCC-M","desc":"We are adding more offline functionality in the new Outlook for Windows. You will now be able to create, edit, and delete events in your calendar when not connected to the internet. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2025-10-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490060","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-502540","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] ​​[DevX] Compliance sensitivity labels for custom connectors","desc":"Compliance sensitivity labels for custom connectors.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-27","modified":"2025-10-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502540","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-502547","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] User can create agents scoped on specific item/ container using URL","desc":"1. Maker can create agents by providing 3p URL. 2. Maker can provide either an item URL or a container level, for e.g. ADO ticket/ ADO area path.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-27","modified":"2025-10-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502547","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-498914","title":"Outlook: New Scheduling and Event Creation Experience","desc":"The Outlook and Teams calendars will receive an update to the scheduling and event creation experience. Additionally, new capabilities will be available in this new experience to help streamline and enhance scheduling using Copilot. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Microsoft Teams","Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-04","modified":"2025-10-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498914","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-515168","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot Connector for DataStax Now Available","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to DataStax with Copilot connectors to query insights from distributed databases.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515168","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515164","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Microsoft 365 Copilot Integrates with Adobe Experience Manager","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to Adobe Experience Manager with Copilot connectors to query and summarize web content.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515164","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-515167","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Query Structured Data via Copilot Connectors for PostgreSQL","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to PostgreSQL with Copilot connectors to query structured data","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515167","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-513284","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Enable Microsoft 365 Copilot Integration with SharePoint Server","desc":"Customers can now connect Microsoft 365 Copilot to SharePoint Server with Copilot connectors to query and manage enterprise documents.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=513284","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501438","title":"Microsoft Intune: Windows Backup for organizations in Intune","desc":"Windows Backup for Organizations will be generally available in Intune with controls for backing up and restoring backups in OOBE. Backup and restore experience of user settings, especially for enterprises transitioning to Windows 11.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-24","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501438","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-501590","title":"Microsoft Viva: Updated Regional Benchmarks for employee feedback","desc":"Viva Glint will refresh its Country & Region external benchmark suites for 2025. These updated benchmarks provide organizations with more accurate and current comparative insights into employee feedback across geographies, enabling better-informed decisions and more relevant action planning.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-08","modified":"2025-10-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501590","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-515161","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with PagerDuty to access escalation policies and on-call schedules with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with PagerDuty to access escalation policies and on-call schedules with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2025-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515161","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515176","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Trello to organize boards and cards with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Trello to organize boards and cards with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2025-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515176","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-515157","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Zendesk Tickets to triage and resolve customer issues with Copilot Connector","desc":"Customers can connect M365 Copilot with Zendesk Tickets to triage and resolve customer issues with Copilot Connector.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-23","modified":"2025-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=515157","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501277","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updates to OneDrive file browsing experience in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app on iPad and iPhone","desc":"Users on the Microsoft 365 Copilot app for iPad and iPhone devices will be directed to the standalone OneDrive app for file browsing and management. While users can still access their most recent files and search for OneDrive content within the Microsoft 365 Copilot app, advanced actions like folder navigation, permission settings, downloads, and deletions must be done in the OneDrive app.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2025-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501277","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"mc-MC1155312","title":"(Updated) Introducing Knowledge Agent (preview): AI-powered content optimization for SharePoint and Copilot","desc":"Updated October 22, 2025: We have updated the content below. Thank you for your patience.\n\n[Introduction]\nWe’re introducing Knowledge Agent, a built-in SharePoint capability that helps organizations prepare content for AI at scale. It unifies fragmented AI features into a single, context-aware interface that adapts to user roles and surfaces intelligent actions directly in the flow of work. This enhancement supports high-quality, trustworthy responses from Microsoft 365 Copilot and custom agents.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\n• Public Preview (Worldwide): Begins mid-September 2025; completes by late February 2026.\n\n[How this affects your organization:]\nWho is affected:\n\n• Users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license on tenants opted into Knowledge Agent preview.\n\n• Admins managing SharePoint content and agents.\n\nWhat will happen:\n\n• A floating button will appear in the lower-right corner of SharePoint surfaces, launching a context-aware menu with intelligent actions.\n\n• Role-based capabilities include:\n\n• Content managers can structure, tag, and enrich content using smart metadata and AI recommendations.\n\n• Site owners can identify stale pages, broken links, and content gaps.\n\n• Content creators can generate pages and documents using natural language prompts.\n\n• Collaborators and viewers can surface grounded insights via natural language chat.\n\nImpact to SharePoint agents users:\n\n• Ready-made SharePoint site agents are now exclusively available to customers with Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses. These agents are no longer accessible through the Microsoft 365 Pay-As-You-Go (PAYG) billing model under the SharePoint agents meter.\n\n• PAYG customers can still create custom-built, no-code SharePoint agents using the same SharePoint agents meter, but they will not have access to the ready-made site agents unless they are Microsoft 365 Copilot licensed.\n\n• The SharePoint ribbon icon has changed from the Copilot logo to a hexagon to indicate Knowledge Agent-enabled sites.\n\n• Agent creation remains available via:\n\n• Site homepage\n\n• Agent chat pane\n\n• AI actions menu in the command bar of a document library\n\n• Content menu of selected file(s) in a document library\n\n[What you can do to prepare:]\n\n• Knowledge Agent Public Preview begins September 18, 2025 on a tenant opt-in basis to users with a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.\n\n• Learn more about opting into the preview: Get started with Knowledge Agent (preview). If you receive a command not recognized error running the commands , please review this article for additional troubleshooting.\n• For tenants who have opted in, it is possible to opt out for specific sites.The ability to opt-in for certain types is coming in mid-to-late November.\n\n• No setup is required for individual features.\n\n• Learn more via the Knowledge Agent blog.\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\n\nConsiderationExplanation\n\nIntroduces or modifies AI/ML capabilitiesKnowledge Agent introduces new AI-driven features that interact with customer content to provide intelligent actions and insights.\n\nProvides new user interaction with generative AIUsers can interact with SharePoint content using natural language prompts and chat.\n\nModifies access to existing featuresChanges availability of ready-made SharePoint agents based on licensing.\n\nIncludes admin controlAdmins can opt in/out of preview and manage site-level availability.","products":["SharePoint Online"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2025-10-22","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1155312","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-500637","title":"Microsoft Teams: App Deployment in Teams Admin Center","desc":"We're introducing a new admin setting that replaces the Installed apps section in app setup policies, enabling more streamlined per-app deployment control. With controls to pre-install the app for : all users, specific users and groups, or no users.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-20","modified":"2025-10-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500637","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-503299","title":"Microsoft Teams: Customize the screen in Teams Town halls through ‘Manage what attendees see’ [Teams Premium]","desc":"The enhanced “Manage what attendees see” experience enables organizers to take their Town hall presentations to the next level. Organizers and presenters can apply layouts, backgrounds, theme colors, and name tags to deliver events that are polished, professional, and highly engaging. This feature is available to organizers with a Teams Premium license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-23","modified":"2025-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503299","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-499889","title":"Microsoft Teams: Raise hands in Town Hall","desc":"Currently in a Teams Town hall, attendees cannot raise their hands and share their microphone and camera as they can in a meeting. With this new update, town halls organized by users with Teams Premium will allow attendees to raise their hand like they would in a standard Teams meeting. The ability to raise a hand can signal to organizers and presenters, who can then bring attendees on screen to allow them to share their camera and microphone.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-14","modified":"2025-10-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499889","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-502538","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] ​​[DevX] Schema enrichment & validation for custom connectors for better relevance & UX","desc":"Schema enrichment & validation for custom connectors for better relevance & UX (Property descriptions, content Category attributes and additional semantic labels)","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2025-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502538","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-503767","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users will be able to upload files stored locally or in one drive to custom engine agents","desc":"Users will be able to upload files stored locally or in one drive to custom engine agents.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2025-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=503767","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"mc-MC1173930","title":"Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive: General availability of tenant rename with no scale limitations","desc":"Organizations undergoing rebranding, mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, or tenant consolidations often need their SharePoint domain name in URLs to reflect their new identity. The SharePoint Online Tenant Rename feature enables this change. We are announcing general availability of advanced tenant rename with no site count limitation. With this update, the feature is now accessible to all customers, regardless of the total number of sites in the tenant.\n\nWhen this will happen:\nGeneral availability begins worldwide on October 16, 2025. Rollout started in early October and is expected to complete by mid-October 2025.\n\nHow this affects your organization:\n\n• Who is affected: Admins managing SharePoint Online and OneDrive for Business tenants globally.\n\n• What will happen:\n\n• Rename support is now available for all Microsoft 365 tenants, regardless of site count.\n\n• High reliability is maintained across rename operations.\n\n• Business-as-usual continuity is ensured during and after rename.\n\n• Compatible with Microsoft 365 partner scenarios including Microsoft Teams and PowerApps.\n\n• Not supported for vanity domains or Multi-Geo customers.\n\nWhat you can do to prepare:\n\n• Confirm total site count using the SharePoint admin center (SPAC) or PowerShell before scheduling.\n• Licensing requirement: Tenants with site count greater than 10,000 must have SAM licenses purchased for all users in the organization.\n\n• Review unsupported features or limitations (such as Hub site limitations, vanity domains, third-party integrations).\n\n• Communicate any impact to site owners using public documentation.\n\n• Validate custom scripts, PowerShell automations, and integrations that rely on the old domain name.\n\n• Learn more: Change your SharePoint domain name | Microsoft Learn\n\n[Compliance considerations:]\nNo compliance considerations identified, review as appropriate for your organization.","products":["SharePoint Online","Microsoft OneDrive"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-10-16","modified":"2025-10-16","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1173930","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-483489","title":"Outlook: Calendar support for copying, cutting, and pasting events and appointments","desc":"Customers can now copy, cut, and paste meetings and appointments on their calendar in the new Outlook using CTRL+C, CTRL+X, and CTRL+V keyboard shortcuts. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-31","modified":"2025-10-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483489","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-502543","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Users can explore third-party content in Copilot chat with deep citations and side-by-side previews","desc":"Drive Copilot chat engagement for 3P content via deep citations, inline citations, side by side preview experiences.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-15","modified":"2025-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502543","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-489834","title":"SharePoint: Document Libraries - A new forms experience for streamlined document collection","desc":"Introducing native forms within SharePoint Document Libraries to streamline document collection. Users can create custom forms directly in libraries for seamless file uploads and metadata submission. Forms can be shared as links within the organization, facilitating document collection without additional access. This integration enhances productivity by simplifying workflows and improving user experience.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-15","modified":"2025-10-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489834","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-399933","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Improved elevation detection","desc":"This improvement expands the types of elevation actions in Windows that EPM can detect and control elevation for.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-06-28","modified":"2025-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=399933","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"August CY2024"},{"id":"rm-399928","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Endpoint Privilege Management on single session Azure Virtual Desktop","desc":"With this release, you can use Endpoint Privilege Management elevation rules and policy to more easily manage standard users on Azure Virtual Desktop.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-03","modified":"2025-10-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=399928","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-511800","title":"SharePoint: Optimizing Version History for lists and libraries","desc":"We're improving version history for SharePoint Lists and Document Libraries generated with grid view editing. This change improves reliability, reduces storage, and streamlines the user experience by consolidating multiple edits into one where possible. Automation rules and flows, if configured with item level edits, will also now trigger more efficiently.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-10","modified":"2025-10-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=511800","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-499901","title":"Outlook: Automatic Draft Minimize","desc":"When users close a draft in progress, it automatically minimizes instead of closing completely. The minimized draft can now be quickly accessed via a button that appears in the message list.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-20","modified":"2025-10-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499901","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498319","title":"Outlook: Immersive Search","desc":"After completing a search in Outlook, a user will see a Copilot entry point that will take them to an LLM generated summary of their search query (emails, Teams messages and documents) within their Copilot side pane. They will be able to interact further with Copilot to dig deeper into these results and take action items accordingly.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-10","modified":"2025-10-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498319","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-501450","title":"Microsoft Intune: Windows Quality Update management policies","desc":"Manage individual Windows quality updates including non-Security and out of band updates. Choose which update types to automatically approve and the rollout options for those approvals.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-03","modified":"2025-10-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501450","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-502537","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Graph API enhancements for better Relevance & UX","desc":"Graph API for custom connectors will provide the options to configure icons, visibility, connection metadata, property descriptions and more semantic labels for improved relevance and UX.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-10-01","modified":"2025-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502537","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-498899","title":"Microsoft Intune: Additional granular RBAC controls to manage Antivirus, Firewall, BitLocker, and Endpoint Detection and Response endpoint security workloads","desc":"Expanded granular RBAC controls to manage Endpoint Security workloads. The ‘Security baselines’ permission previously included all security policies and now all security workloads have their own permission set","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-18","modified":"2025-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498899","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-501456","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune settings available in Catalog and Account Protection template for Adminless feature","desc":"Adminless settings able to be configured in settings catalog and account protection template.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-26","modified":"2025-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501456","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-499156","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Support approvals can now be requested by non-primary users of a device.","desc":"We're updating Endpoint Privilege Management to allow users who are not assigned as the primary user of a device to initiate support approval requests. Previously, these requests would fail, but with this change, they will be processed successfully.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-10-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499156","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-495463","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Dashboard - Enhanced scope drilldown","desc":"Leaders and managers can drilldown and explore data in Copilot Dashboard by indirect groups, unlocking a new layer of visibility into Copilot adoption and impact. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-29","modified":"2025-09-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495463","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-479750","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Copilot Academy reports in Viva Insights","desc":"Usage reporting for Copilot Academy will be available in Viva Insights via the Analyst Workbench. Users can access these reports through Excel or a PowerBI dashboard.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-05","modified":"2025-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=479750","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606,"preview":"May CY2025"},{"id":"rm-487847","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: Control Settings for agents with actions in Teams Toolkit","desc":"To give admins control over whether agent makers can publish advanced agents (agents with actions) for their tenants, we are introducing a new control in the M365 admin center. This control specifically applies to advanced agents created from Teams Toolkit. #copilotcontrolsystem","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-01","modified":"2025-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487847","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"December CY2025"},{"id":"rm-502551","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Unique Counting of EDM Matches","desc":"Providing a new mode to count EDM Matches where each row is counted once in addition to the current behavior where each primary element is counted once","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-24","modified":"2025-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502551","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-502526","title":"Microsoft Teams: Channel Agent","desc":"Channel agent works alongside you and your team to help you manage projects. It can create status reports, send emails, schedule meetings, co-author documents, and answer questions. Channel agent understands context from meetings, chats, and files, and uses that knowledge to help you move work forward. It’s designed to save time, reduce manual effort, and make collaboration more intelligent.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2025-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502526","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-492742","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Notification Settings","desc":"Admins can now enable/disable all learning-related notifications from a centralized settings page.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-08","modified":"2025-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492742","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-336046","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Communication Compliance - Enhanced Policy Conditions","desc":"Three updates are coming to enhance policy conditions. First, our updated policy conditions enable the detection of messages sent and received both to and from external email addresses, allowing you to identify specific instances of information being shared with external contacts. Secondly, with the new OR condition capability, you can combine multiple conditions within the same policy, creating custom logic to suit your unique compliance requirements. Lastly, to make policy creation and updates a seamless process, we've introduced the ability to test conditions before implementing them. By using sample messages, you can evaluate how your conditions will perform and fine-tune them to align with your compliance goals.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-12-14","modified":"2025-09-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=336046","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-477373","title":"Outlook: Support for enhanced calendar-sharing architecture in the New Outlook for Windows and Web","desc":"This update improves the reliability of calendar sharing and ensures that the events seen by delegates are always up to date. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-24","modified":"2025-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=477373","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2026","gaSort":202604},{"id":"rm-500871","title":"Microsoft Teams: Preview changes before sending content live in 'Manage what attendees see'","desc":"An enhancement to the 'Manage what attendees see' feature allows organizers and presenters to preview changes to what is going to be displayed on or off the screen before sending the changes live to attendees. This capability is only available for Town hall.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-09-03","modified":"2025-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500871","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-500160","title":"Outlook: Chat for Outlook iOS and Android","desc":"On phone devices, users currently access Copilot Chat in Outlook Mobile via a tab at the bottom of their screen (or in Apps). Outlook is introducing a new Copilot Chat overlay experience, allowing users to chat with Copilot while continuing to interact with their email, calendar, and contacts. This overlay will be context-aware—understanding what the user is viewing—so users can ask Copilot about the content on their screen. Users with M365 Copilot licenses will also benefit from Copilot’s ability to draw on Microsoft 365 Graph to provide richer, more personalized responses.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-08-19","modified":"2025-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500160","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-486838","title":"Outlook: Grid keyboard navigation in calendar month view via arrow keys in new Outlook for Windows and Web","desc":"When focused on the calendar grid, you will be able to navigate the time slots on the calendar via left/right/up/down arrow keys in month view. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2025-09-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486838","source":"roadmap","phases":["Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-501124","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Admins can deploy and govern agents with MCP in the M365 admin center","desc":"Admins can deploy, monitor, and manage agents built with the Model Context Protocol (MCP) in the M365 admin center for secure enterprise use.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-19","modified":"2025-09-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501124","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-501785","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Edit your Copilot-generated PowerPoint presentation outline via Pages in Chat","desc":"You can now edit and collaborate on the presentation outline generated by Copilot in a Page before the PowerPoint deck is created.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-19","modified":"2025-09-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501785","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-499420","title":"Microsoft 365: AI workflows in Teams Workflows app & SharePoint document libraries","desc":"With AI workflows in the Workflows app for Teams & SharePoint document libraries, you can build custom AI-powered templates to automate complex tasks and streamline daily operations. Admins can enable this feature to equip users with intelligent automation tools that make managing work more efficient and intuitive.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-18","modified":"2025-09-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499420","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-502542","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Improve discovery of Champion connector prompts for Users","desc":"Improve discovery of Champion connector prompts - inline suggestive pre & post prompts, prompt library.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-12","modified":"2025-09-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502542","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-501437","title":"Microsoft Intune: Windows Backup for organizations in Intune","desc":"Windows Backup for Organizations will be generally available in Intune with controls for backing up and restoring backups in OOBE. Backup and restore experience of user settings, especially for enterprises transitioning to Windows 11.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-10","modified":"2025-09-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501437","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-389857","title":"Microsoft Intune: Managed device attestation for iOS/iPadOS and macOS device enrollment and ADE","desc":"Intune is bringing ACME and managed device attestation support for eligible Apple devices to GA. This includes device enrollment and ADE enrollments, including AC2. This applies to new enrollments with device enrollment (BYOD) and new enrollments with ADE or Apple Configurator tool.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-06","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=389857","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-378649","title":"Microsoft Intune: Windows enrollment attestation","desc":"Physical Windows devices will be attested at enrollment that enrollment credentials are stored in the hardware of the device. Administrators can view device attestations in the new Device attestation status report and manually force attestation from that report.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-01-19","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=378649","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"April CY2024"},{"id":"rm-468887","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Automated device enrollment without user affinity for visionOS and tvOS","desc":"Support for visionOS and tvOS through automated device enrollment for userless enrollment with Microsoft Intune Suite including Intune Plan 2","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-16","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=468887","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602},{"id":"rm-406907","title":"Microsoft Intune: Enrollment time grouping for iOS/iPadOS automated device enrollment","desc":"Enrollment time grouping for iOS/iPadOS automated device enrollment (ADE) ensures targeted apps and policies can get to devices faster and reduce latency of device setup. ETG will only be part of new iOS/iPadOS enrollment policies. Admins can add a static Entra ID group into the enrollment policy, so devices will be part of that group upon enrollment, reducing latency of targeted policies and apps.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-12","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=406907","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-469032","title":"Microsoft Intune: New enrollment policies experience for iOS/iPadOS ADE","desc":"These enrollment policies for iOS/iPadOS contains enrollment time grouping, improved UI, and removes automatic deployment of the Company Portal app and deprecated settings.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-15","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=469032","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-499155","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Endpoint Privilege Management Virtual Account Support","desc":"EPM will introduce a per-rule option to run elevated apps with the original user's identity context, preserving app data, save locations, and preferences. This offers a more personalized app runtime experience compared to the default virtual account.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499155","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-491027","title":"Microsoft Intune: Intune Suite - Operational dashboard to gain insight on EPM status and elevations.","desc":"The dashboard focuses EPM insights on rollout status as well as elevations in the environment and suggestions for new rules to create.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-28","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491027","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-498229","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Updated Clipchamp video start page","desc":"The Clipchamp start page new unified hub is a revamped video hub start page experience of a single video destination for creation, discovery & consumption.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-17","modified":"2025-09-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498229","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-501539","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Discovery of sensitive data sharing to any cloud application or website (inc. GenAI) via network layer","desc":"With this update, Insider Risk Management will support the discovery of sensitive files and text shared to any cloud application or website (inc. GenAI) via network layer. This capability is based on integration with 3rd party network partners (with data being captured via network layer). Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2025-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501539","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-501538","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Generative AI apps activities as triggers in IRM","desc":"With this update, the generative AI apps indicators will be supported as triggers in Risky AI usage policy. With triggers, customers can define the conditions for bringing the user into the scope of a policy while the generative AI apps indicators are used to determine risk score. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-27","modified":"2025-09-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501538","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-501559","title":"Microsoft Intune: Autopilot device preparation for Windows 365 Frontline shared general availability","desc":"Admins can use Windows Autopilot device preparation to provision their Windows 365 Frontline shared devices.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-04","modified":"2025-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501559","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-501455","title":"SharePoint: New Microsoft 365 Copilot Skills for SharePoint Administration","desc":"We’re excited to announce two new Copilot skills in the SharePoint Admin Center: 1. Step-by-Step Task Guidance Copilot can now walk you through the exact steps required to complete common admin tasks. Example: “How can I find sites that are potentially over-permissioned?” What to expect: Copilot will recommend clear, sequential instructions to guide you from start to finish. 2. Multi-Criteria Site Search Copilot can help you find sites using multiple conditions at once. Example: “Find sites that have been inactive for more than 60 days and are shared externally.” What to expect: Copilot will generate a filtered list of sites that meet your criteria and suggest recommended actions.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-04","modified":"2025-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501455","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-419811","title":"Microsoft Teams: Decorate your background for GCC and GCC High environments (Premium)","desc":"Decorate your background is now available to customers in the GCC and GCC High environments. Decorate your background is a generative background effect in Teams that makes meetings more fun and personal by using AI to spruce up your meeting background. Blend your physical and digital spaces, enabling you to revamp what’s seen of your physical meeting space for each call. This technology allows for effortless room clean-ups, adding virtual plants, or festive decorations for special events. Decorate your background requires a Teams Premium license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-10-07","modified":"2025-09-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=419811","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-502527","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: OCR Audit logs","desc":"This feature is designed to provide Audit logs for each OCR transaction; this feature is only available in Exchange and teams workload for public preview.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-09-03","modified":"2025-09-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=502527","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"mc-MC1058259","title":"(Updated) Microsoft Teams: Preview changes before making them visible to attendees with \"Manage what attendees see\"","desc":"Updated September 3, 2025: We have updated the timeline. Thank you for your patience.\nComing soon for Microsoft Teams: A new Manage what attendees see feature will help organizers and presenters deliver polished town hall events by simplifying the attendee view and keeping the focus on participants brought on screen. The new feature allows assigned organizers and presenters to preview changes before applying them all at once.\nThis message applies to Teams for Windows desktop, Teams for Mac desktop, and Teams for the web.\nThis message is associated with Microsoft 365 Roadmap ID 487431.\n\n[When this will happen:]\n\nTargeted Release: We will begin rolling out mid-July 2025 and expect to complete by late July 2025.\n\nGeneral Availability (Worldwide): We will begin rolling out late July 2025 and expect to complete by late September 2025.\n[How this will affect your organization:]\nBefore this rollout, when an organizer or presenter brings a participant or shared content on or off screen, the change is immediately reflected in the attendees' view.\nAfter this rollout, organizers and presenters will have the option to preview their changes before applying them. This allows for smoother, more polished transitions in the attendee's view, without showing every adjustment made by the organizer or presenter managing the screen. Organizers can go to the town hall Meeting options to locate the Manage what attendees see feature.\n\nWe will change the Manage what attendees see option from a toggle to radio buttons. Manage what attendees see will have three options:\n• Off: All participants will appear onscreen.\n\n• On: Organizers and presenters can share content and bring attendees on screen to view the content.\n\n• On with preview: Organizers and presenters can share content, preview the content, and then bring attendees on screen to view the content.\n\nTo use the new On with preview option, the organizer must select it before the event begins. By default, Manage what attendees see is set to Off when scheduling a meeting or webinar, and On when scheduling a town hall. The On with preview option is only available for town halls and does not require a Teams Premium license.\nLimitations\n• The On with preview option is not available in meetings or webinars. For these events, the organizer will only have the option to select Off or On for Manage what attendees see.\n• Only assigned users joining through Teams for Windows desktop or Teams for the web will have the option to preview and apply changes. Any assigned users joining through mobile or Microsoft Teams Room will not have the ability to bring participants or shared content on or off screen.\n• Users joining through older Teams versions will continue to see the existing behavior, where users don't have the option to preview changes in Manage what attendees see.\n\nAny new meetings or events created after mid-June 2025 will receive the new updates by default to the Manage what attendees see feature.\nThis feature will be available by default for meeting organizers to configure.\nSelect the presenter or content you’d like to preview before sending live to your event:\n\nSelect Send live to seamlessly send the content from the Preview window to the attendee view:\n\n[What you need to do to prepare:]\nThis rollout will happen automatically by the specified dates with no admin action required before the rollout. You may want to notify your users about this change and update any relevant documentation.\nWe recommend you review Manage what attendees see in Teams meetings (will be updated before rollout) for a comprehensive overview of the feature and conduct a test session with the feature turned on to get acquainted with the new controls.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Launched","created":"2025-04-18","modified":"2025-09-03","link":"https://admin.microsoft.com/Adminportal/Home#/MessageCenter/:/messages/MC1058259","source":"mc","phases":["Stay informed"],"gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-477363","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Recommended thresholds","desc":"With this update, admins with the appropriate permissions can get tailored recommended thresholds for all the built-in indicators within the policy wizard. This feature enables organizations to fine tune their insider risk policies and get an optimal number of alerts. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-06","modified":"2025-09-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=477363","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-501449","title":"Microsoft Intune: Windows Quality Update management policies","desc":"Manage individual Windows quality updates including non-Security and out of band updates. Choose which update types to automatically approve and the rollout options for those approvals.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-28","modified":"2025-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=501449","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2026","gaSort":202602,"preview":"January CY2026"},{"id":"rm-488102","title":"Microsoft 365 app: Microsoft Places - Onboard to the Places Directory with AI","desc":"Seamlessly onboard to the Places Directory by using a new and improved AI-powered Initialize-Places PowerShell script. #MicrosoftPlaces","products":["Microsoft 365 app"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-11","modified":"2025-08-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488102","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-496595","title":"Outlook: Save an Event as a Draft on Android","desc":"You can save a meeting as a draft on your calendar if you aren't ready to send the meeting invites. When composing an event with at least one attendee added, select dismiss and then select Save as a Draft. The draft event will show on your calendar as [Draft] along with the title of the event.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-18","modified":"2025-08-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496595","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-176155","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Exact Data Match adding support for role-based access control (RBAC) for EDM upload authorization","desc":"Customers will be able to choose to leverage RBAC to authorize users for uploading data to the Exact Data Match (EDM) service instead of leveraging the EDM_DataUploaders security group for authorization.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-09-27","modified":"2025-08-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=176155","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-122278","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal : Insider Risk Management – Bring your own detections","desc":"<div><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DengXian;color:black;\">Allow customers to bring their own user activity indicators from homegrown, SIEM/UEBA platforms, or other line-of-business applications, and leverage them in existing Insider Risk Management playbooks. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</span> </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-03-10","modified":"2025-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=122278","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"June CY2023","more":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/compliance/insider-risk-management?view=o365-worldwide"},{"id":"rm-485713","title":"Microsoft Teams: Select camera in pre-join and during meeting","desc":"Users can select an internal or external camera, or keep it turned off, before joining or during Teams meetings.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-28","modified":"2025-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485713","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-498639","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Pulse - New Pulse customization options","desc":"Authors will have new options when starting surveys, including choosing to send without pre-defining an audience, and feedback can instead be gathered by sharing a link that people can access the survey and respond through, sending a survey without a specified end date, allowing for longer-term data collection and multiple responses from recipients over time, and collecting identified responses, where answers are attributed to the person who submitted them.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-17","modified":"2025-08-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498639","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-498898","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] View Index browser, schema and errors for Custom Connectors on MAC","desc":"View index browser, schema, and the errors for custom connectors from the M365 Admin center for better troubleshooting.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-18","modified":"2025-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498898","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-413712","title":"Microsoft Teams: Support for PowerPoint live within Cloud Video Interop (CVI)","desc":"This new functionality will provide CVI Partners with the ability to display still images when PowerPoint live content is being presented within a Microsoft Teams meeting. The PowerPoint presentation will then be displayed as video content, this will not include animations or embedded videos.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-08-26","modified":"2025-08-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=413712","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-380841","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Referenced sources are cited in drafted content","desc":"When drafting content that's based on referenced sources, Copilot includes citations in the text it generates, indicating references to information in the content.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-12-06","modified":"2025-08-15","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380841","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-500639","title":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Portal: Collection policies support in IRM","desc":"With this update, IRM will start supporting collection policies. Collection policies allow customers to scope classification (SITs - Sensitive Information Types) and activities for scoped users. For device indicators based IRM policy, required collection policies will be automatically created in the background. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies to manage security and compliance. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-14","modified":"2025-08-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=500639","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-496590","title":"Microsoft Teams: SQL-like commands in the search bar","desc":"Efficiently narrow down your search results by using SQL-like commands in the search bar. Users can quickly filter messages, files, or conversations with precise queries such as from:username, with:username or in:channel.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-07-01","modified":"2025-08-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496590","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-497939","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Update document sections from new sources","desc":"Easily refresh parts of your document using content from other files—without copying and pasting. Copilot keeps your formatting intact while pulling in the latest updates from new sources.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-08-04","modified":"2025-08-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497939","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-499432","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Endpoint Data Loss Prevention -- Always-on diagnostics for macOS endpoints (Phase 1)","desc":"This feature release ‘Always-on diagnostics’, captures critical diagnostic data from onboarded endpoint devices running on macOS for EDLP issue reporting. Comprehensive trace logs will be automatically recorded and stored locally on onboarded Mac devices, eliminating the need to reproduce issues when submitting investigation requests to Microsoft. It allows for the collection of detailed traces over extended periods (up to 90 days). While raising tickets to submit investigation requests to Microsoft regarding Microsoft Endpoint DLP, customers can share enhanced diagnostic information with Microsoft without needing to reproduce the exact scenario.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-31","modified":"2025-07-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=499432","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2025","gaSort":202511},{"id":"rm-167331","title":"Microsoft Purview | Compliance Manager: Microsoft Defender for Cloud (MDC) integration","desc":"<div style=\"margin:0px 0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;\">Compliance Manager now integrates with Microsoft Defender for Cloud, allowing customers to assess their compliance posture across Microsoft 365, Azure, Google Cloud Platform, and Amazon Web Services with resource-level testing and cloud-specific guidance. </div><div style=\"margin:0px 0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;\"> </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-09-21","modified":"2025-07-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=167331","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-480729","title":"SharePoint: SharePoint agent usage statistics across all SharePoint sites","desc":"SharePoint agents' usage statistics would be aggregated across all SharePoint sites and available for the tenant admin persona.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-03","modified":"2025-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480729","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-493753","title":"Outlook: Contact Improvements on Outlook Mobile","desc":"On Outlook mobile we are improving the \"Contacts\" experience by showing additional profile information for your contacts, where applicable. Secondly, this improvement hides identical duplicate contacts.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-23","modified":"2025-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=493753","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-494154","title":"Outlook: Create a meeting from an email thread with Copilot","desc":"Copilot makes it fast and easy to schedule a meeting from an email thread. When you use the Schedule with Copilot option, Copilot analyzes the email and creates a meeting invitation for you, filling in a meeting title and agenda, and adding the email thread as an attachment. The people on the email thread are included as meeting attendees, and you can quickly review the invitation, add or change info, and then send it out.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-21","modified":"2025-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494154","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-498918","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Connector Metadata Enrichment for Custom Copilot Connectors","desc":"We’re introducing new options that allow admins and developers to enrich their custom Copilot connectors and its schema properties with descriptive metadata. With this update, you can now: * Provide richer context about the connection and its schema properties to Copilot’s LLM, enabling more accurate and relevant responses. Add alternate names, data source categories, common actions to your connector and description for schema properties. * Improve search and chat quality by helping Copilot better understand the semantics and purpose of your data.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498918","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498909","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Customize icons and display names for custom Copilot connectors","desc":"1. Add or Customize icons for Custom Copilot connectors using the Graph API or from the M365 Admin Center. 2. Add or Customize display names for Custom Copilot connectors using the Graph API or from the M365 Admin Center.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498909","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498919","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Delete Schema Properties via Copilot Connector APIs","desc":"We’re adding support for property deletion in custom Copilot connectors, giving admins and developers more control over schema evolution. With this feature, you can: * Use Copilot connector APIs to delete or drop individual schema properties that are no longer needed. * Keep your connector schema clean and up-to-date without requiring full re-ingestion. * Reduce developer overhead and simplify maintenance workflows as your data models evolve.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498919","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498910","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Full refresh of custom connectors datasource","desc":"Admins and developers can do a full refresh or sync of their datasource for Custom Connectors using Graph APIs. This also ensures that any items deleted in the source are automatically deleted during this full sync and admins do not have to use separate delete APIs to do this.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498910","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498911","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Schema Recommendations for Custom Connectors in M365 Admin Center","desc":"Accelerate your custom connector development with intelligent schema guidance directly in the Microsoft 365 Admin Center. This feature provides: * Proposed schema suggestions tailored to the connector you’re building. * Real-time recommendations to identify gaps or errors in your schema design to help improve search and chat results in Copilot. Whether you're starting from scratch or refining an existing connector, this enhancement ensures your schema is optimized for Copilot extensibility and performance.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498911","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-498912","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): [Copilot Extensibility] Simplified People Resolution for Custom Copilot Connectors","desc":"This feature enables connectors to resolve external identities—such as email addresses or user IDs from third-party data sources—to their corresponding Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) identities. By allowing flexible identity mapping, developers can: * Simplify integration workflows without needing complex Graph API lookups. * Reduce setup friction by avoiding strict dependency on object IDs. * Improve search and chat relevance in Copilot by ensuring accurate people attribution across connected systems.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-25","modified":"2025-07-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498912","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-380848","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Referenced sources are cited in drafted content","desc":"When drafting content that's based on referenced sources, Copilot includes citations in the text it generates, indicating references to information in the content.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-12-13","modified":"2025-07-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380848","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-109560","title":"Microsoft Intune: iOS app multiple managed accounts","desc":"Allows people to use a single device with multiple managed accounts to access company information through Teams iOS app, with Outlook to follow.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-02-10","modified":"2025-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=109560","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603,"preview":"November CY2025"},{"id":"rm-497544","title":"Word: 3rd party citation add-in in reference tab","desc":"This integrates popular third-party citation providers under the Word Reference tab, helping users efficiently complete their reference lists.","products":["Microsoft 365 app","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-23","modified":"2025-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497544","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-482601","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Access SharePoint agents in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app","desc":"Use SharePoint agents seamlessly without navigating to the SharePoint site. With this new feature, you can quickly return to your most recently used SharePoint agents directly in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-17","modified":"2025-07-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482601","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-497941","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Recent activity is part of Copilot's dynamic document snapshot in Word","desc":"Select the Activity tab within the Copilot summary at the top of a document for a summary of recent comments and changes. Choose a time window of 3 days, 1 week, or 2 weeks.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-21","modified":"2025-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497941","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-473461","title":"Word: Draft on a selection and retain your existing formatting","desc":"Draft on a selection and retain your existing formatting so that your content is seamless and fits with your document.","products":["Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-18","modified":"2025-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473461","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-497937","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Auto-update document sections from new sources","desc":"Easily refresh parts of your document using content from other files—without copying and pasting. Copilot keeps your formatting intact while pulling in the latest updates from new sources.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-21","modified":"2025-07-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497937","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-497833","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Researcher is in Microsoft Word","desc":"The Researcher agent now has easier entry points on the Word canvas —making it faster to go from idea to polished research report without breaking your flow.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-01","modified":"2025-07-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497833","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-487855","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot surfaces key statistics in the top of a document","desc":"Copilot includes a summary at the top of key statistics from your Word document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2025-07-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487855","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-475858","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Support for multicloud environments","desc":"Insider Risk Management extends its detection into multicloud environments by offering ready-to-use risk indicators in Azure, AWS, and SaaS apps including Box, Dropbox, Google Drive, and GitHub. Organizations can use these new indicators in data theft and data leaks policies. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-17","modified":"2025-07-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=475858","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2026","gaSort":202606},{"id":"rm-497914","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Easier access to Researcher in Microsoft Word","desc":"The Researcher agent now has easier entry points on the Word canvas —making it faster to go from idea to polished research report without breaking your flow.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-10","modified":"2025-07-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497914","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-498158","title":"Microsoft Entra: Improved Backup and Restore Experience for the Authenticator App on iOS","desc":"Users of the Microsoft Authenticator app on iOS will be able to back up account names—including Microsoft work or school accounts, Microsoft personal accounts, and third-party accounts like Amazon or Google—using iCloud and iCloud Keychain. This enables secure, end-to-end encrypted backup of account names and TOTP credentials. When setting up a new iOS device, account names will automatically appear in the app, and users can sign in to complete setup.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-09","modified":"2025-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=498158","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508,"preview":"September CY2025"},{"id":"rm-495454","title":"Microsoft Teams: Usability and privacy improvements for live captions and live transcript in meetings","desc":"Introducing enhancements to live captions and live transcripts in Microsoft Teams to make meetings more intuitive, accessible, and privacy-focused. Live captions are now scrollable, allowing users to review past conversation with more flexibility and over a larger surface area. Next, copying captions is disabled by default to protect sensitive information and support compliance. Additionally, the live transcript panel won’t open automatically with features that trigger transcription—like recording, giving users greater control over their layout. Lastly, If transcription is enabled, users who attempt to open the live transcript panel will see a banner suggesting they switch to live captions for real-time comprehension. These updates streamline the experience while supporting accessibility and privacy.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-06-05","modified":"2025-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495454","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-497132","title":"SharePoint: Text Editor Copilot 'Refine' update","desc":"SharePoint is updating the capabilities of its text editor Copilot. Now, you can not only use copilot to rewrite your existing text but also use it to keep writing or add a grounding document. By answering the question \"what do you want copilot to change\", you can perform any number of refinements to your existing content.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-09","modified":"2025-07-09","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497132","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-497940","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Recent activity is part of Copilot's dynamic document snapshot in Word","desc":"Select the Activity tab within the Copilot summary at the top of a document for a summary of recent comments and changes. Choose a time window of 3 days, 1 week, or 2 weeks.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-08","modified":"2025-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497940","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-497936","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Recent activity is part of Copilot's dynamic document snapshot in Word","desc":"Select the Activity tab within the Copilot summary at the top of a document for a summary of recent comments and changes. Choose a time window of 3 days, 1 week, or 2 weeks.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-08","modified":"2025-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497936","source":"roadmap","phases":["Current Channel","General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-378409","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Policy tuning analysis for priority content-only policies","desc":"Policy tuning analysis provides admins with a real-time prediction of the number of users in a tenant that could potentially match a given set of policy conditions. With this update, policy tuning analysis will support insider risk policies that are scoped for priority content. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-01-12","modified":"2025-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=378409","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"May CY2024"},{"id":"rm-491019","title":"Outlook: Add custom sounds for Mail Notifications, Reactions, and Calendar Reminders","desc":"In your Notification settings, you'll be able to add a custom sound for your mail notifications, mail reactions, and calendar notifications (aka reminders). #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2025-07-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491019","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-497912","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Optical character recognition (OCR) - Support for embedded images in files including Office files in SharePoint and OneDrive","desc":"Optical character recognition (OCR) scanning enables Microsoft Purview to scan images for sensitive information. With Embedded support, OCR will scan content in DOCX, PPTX, XLSX and PDFs (scanned and hybrid containing searchable text and images). This will be in addition to support for standalone images","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-07-03","modified":"2025-07-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497912","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-497297","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Document snapshot in Word personalizes output","desc":"The document snapshot helps the user focus faster by surfacing the most important information for them based on their personal context.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-30","modified":"2025-06-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497297","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509},{"id":"rm-495828","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Content suggestions in Word","desc":"Select the Suggestions tab within the Copilot summary at the top of a Word document for suggestions on improving the content of the document.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-30","modified":"2025-06-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=495828","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-394282","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Sensitivity labels protection policy support for Azure Storage","desc":"Label-based protection support is now possible for Azure Data Lake Gen 2 and Azure Blob storage, all within Microsoft Purview information Protection. You may already know how to protect Microsoft 365 data like documents or emails with sensitivity labels, and you will now be able to apply these labels and the related protections to these additional sources. In addition, you will have a consistent framework for your sensitive information by allowing your existing label scheme and extending it to apply within these sources.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-06","modified":"2025-06-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=394282","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-497548","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Overview dashboard","desc":"We are introducing a new Overview dashboard to help customers understand how our product effectively protects their organization environment and digital assets. The overview dashboard focuses on showcasing the effectiveness of our tools, how customers can further amplify this effectiveness and our product’s leading position in comparison to the other non-Microsoft security solutions out there.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-26","modified":"2025-06-26","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497548","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-476489","title":"Microsoft Teams: Presenter joins Townhalls via dial-in","desc":"Now, with a Public Switched Telephone Network (PSTN) code provided in the town hall share event dialog, organizers can share these codes with presenters. With these codes, presenters will join as an attendee and promoted to a presenter to join either the green room or the live session.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-01-23","modified":"2025-06-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=476489","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-497243","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage supports 14 more languages","desc":"Viva Engage now supports 14 additional languages (listed below), making the platform more accessible to global users. This update allows employees to engage in their preferred language, helping improve communication across multilingual teams. Users can navigate to their settings in Viva Engage and choose their preferred language in the drop down under 'Language' settings. The new languages are - 1. Arabic 2. Vietnamese 3. Serbian (Latin) 4. Slovak 5. Croatian 6. Hebrew 7. Slovenian 8. Lithuanian 9. Estonian 10. Bulgarian 11. Latvian12. English (United Kingdom) 13. Spanish (Mexico) 14. French (Canada)","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-24","modified":"2025-06-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=497243","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-494159","title":"SharePoint: Site attestation","desc":"Site attestation policy is the newest addition to the site lifecycle management suite. It is a one-stop solution to ensure your sites are secure and compliant by reducing the risk of unmanaged sites. This involves regular reviews by site owners or admins to check and confirm the accuracy of site information, including the site's necessity, its owners, members, permissions, and sharing settings. You can also choose to automate actions on sites that remain unattested for more than 3 months to prevent risks of content over exposure.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-23","modified":"2025-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494159","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-494688","title":"Microsoft Viva: Customize visuals and pages in embedded PowerBI reports","desc":"Analysts can now use embedded PowerBI edit tools to customize their reports to add visuals, pages and change themes, text and more, and then publish it to their organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-23","modified":"2025-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=494688","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-489821","title":"Microsoft Teams: AI assistant for admins in the Pro Management portal","desc":"IT admins can optimize their time and resources by utilizing the Pro Management Portal AI assistant. It offers comprehensive answers to questions about Teams meeting spaces and management solutions and delivers data and insights specific to inventory in the organization’s environment. This feature is available with Teams Rooms Pro and does not require a Microsoft 365 Copilot license.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2025-06-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489821","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-490048","title":"Microsoft Teams: Configurable Keyboard Shortcuts","desc":"Set your own keyboard shortcuts to match your work preferences. Customize the keyboard shortcut for an action you frequently use by clicking on the ellipsis and selecting Keyboard shortcuts from the menu.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-23","modified":"2025-06-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490048","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-171185","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management- OCR support in Insider Risk Management","desc":"<div>With this update, Insider Risk Management will support the scanning technique of Optical Character Recognition (OCR) to detect potentially risky activities that may lead to data security incidents related to images in SharePoint, Teams messages, and endpoints. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy. </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-09-25","modified":"2025-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=171185","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-496374","title":"SharePoint: Support for click through rate metric in page analytics","desc":"This release will enhance SharePoint page analytics by adding click through rate metric. A new card will show the percentage of unique viewers who clicked on a link from the news post, providing insights into user engagement with the post.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-16","modified":"2025-06-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496374","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-491438","title":"Microsoft Teams: Set New Ringtones in Teams Mobile","desc":"This feature allows you to customize and select different sounds for various types of calls, helping you better manage your alerts and distinguish between different incoming communications. For users with Microsoft Teams Phone, this also includes calls for forwarded and delegated calls.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-30","modified":"2025-06-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=491438","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-124890","title":"Microsoft Intune: On demand remediations - single device","desc":"Remediations are script packages that can detect and fix common support issues on a user's device before they even realize there's a problem. These remediations can help reduce support calls. On demand remediations enables admins to execute a remediation on demand and as soon as possible on a single device.","products":["Microsoft Intune"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-08-04","modified":"2025-06-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=124890","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"June CY2023"},{"id":"rm-402516","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Barriers v2 support for all new onboarding customers","desc":"Microsoft Purview Information Barriers v2 (IB v2) is now available for all new onboarding customers. IB v2 has enhanced architecture which enables the following new features: Large-scale segment support: The segment limit in organizations has increased to 5,000. Multi-segment support: Users can be assigned to up to 10 segments. Flexible user discoverability: Organizations can now choose to allow IB-protected users to discover each other while adhering to IB communication and collaboration policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-06-26","modified":"2025-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=402516","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2026","gaSort":202603},{"id":"rm-484123","title":"Microsoft Teams: Copilot summary for transferred calls","desc":"When a call is forwarded/transferred to another colleague, users can prompt Copilot to automatically summarize the context, open questions, etc. for the call as a briefing for the receiving colleague. This feature ensures that the recipient is well-informed about the previous conversations related to the transferred call, enhancing their understanding and preparedness.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-07","modified":"2025-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484123","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-496147","title":"Microsoft Viva: Manage GDPR requests in Engage admin center","desc":"You can now manage GDPR deletion requests directly within the Engage admin center, streamlining the process and reducing reliance on the legacy Yammer admin center. This update centralizes compliance actions in one modern interface.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-06-05","modified":"2025-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=496147","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-489831","title":"Outlook: Create, Delete, Rename, and Move Folders","desc":"You will now be able to more easily create, delete, rename, and move folders on mobile. From your inbox, tap the Edit icon in the sidebar. Tap on any folder to create a subfolder, or rename, move, and delete that folder. You can also rearrange and nest your folders by dragging and dropping them.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-15","modified":"2025-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489831","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-478645","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Support for summarization of very long documents","desc":"Copilot in Word can summarize documents up to about 1,500,000 words or 3,000 pages. This summary will be available on top of the document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-25","modified":"2025-06-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=478645","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-490566","title":"Microsoft Teams: External group chat policy enforcements for max two orgs","desc":"Facilitate creation and maintenance of external group chats with bilateral policy enforcement where members in the chat can belong to a maximum of two tenants. Allow tenant admins to control bilateral chat policy and apply it to users and groups.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-28","modified":"2025-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490566","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-486706","title":"Microsoft Teams: Town hall usage reports in TAC will have all the relevant usage data related to town hall events in the tenant.","desc":"When Town hall was released, there were some columns/data related to each Town hall event that were missing in the TAC usage reports for IT Admins. Now all the relevant usage related data are added to the town hall usage reports available in the TAC portal for Admins.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2025-06-03","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486706","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-483954","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Fix all spelling and grammar issues with Copilot","desc":"One-click solution to fix spelling and grammar errors in the document","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-04-15","modified":"2025-05-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483954","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-483356","title":"Microsoft Teams: Users can view app ratings before installing apps or agents","desc":"We have improved user options for sharing a link for a Teams app or a Microsoft 365 Copilot agent in a chat. Links to apps and agents will have a new preview card with user ratings for users to consider before installing apps or agents in Teams and clear actions like Add (which installs the app or agent) and View detail. A Microsoft 365 Copilot license is not required to share Copilot agent links but may be required to install and use the agent.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-27","modified":"2025-05-28","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483356","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-357562","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Learning - Private thumbnail using SharePoint links for courses","desc":"Private thumbnail using SharePoint links for courses hosted at SuccessFactors can be displayed at Viva Learning.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-03","modified":"2025-05-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=357562","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507,"preview":"July CY2025"},{"id":"rm-483254","title":"Microsoft Teams: App ratings will be available in the unfurled links","desc":"App ratings will appear on the unfurled links for shared apps and agents to allow users who rely on ratings to evaluate apps prior to installing.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-27","modified":"2025-05-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483254","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-325948","title":"Microsoft Teams: Ability to Stop Copilot while it is generating a response","desc":"Copilot in Teams will now have a 'stop' button after sending a prompt. This will allow the user to stop Copilot's response either before the response has started to generate, or even after the response is generating. The user may then start a new prompt if they wish.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-06","modified":"2025-05-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=325948","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-467445","title":"Microsoft Teams: Presenter Chat while screensharing","desc":"Enable presenters to more easily access the meeting chat while screensharing by adding an entry point in the presenter toolbar.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-11-15","modified":"2025-05-16","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=467445","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-492617","title":"Microsoft 365 Admin Center: Admin Copilot available in GCC","desc":"Microsoft Copilot in the Microsoft 365 admin center will soon be available in government clouds (GCC). Tenants that have at least one Microsoft 365 Copilot license will be able to access Copilot in the Microsoft 365 admin center via the Copilot button on the top right corner of the screen.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-13","modified":"2025-05-13","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492617","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-482747","title":"Microsoft Teams: Opening Calls in a small window in Teams","desc":"Allowing users to open calls in a small window to reduce disruptions in Teams.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-26","modified":"2025-05-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482747","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-492984","title":"SharePoint: New File Format Support for Document Translation","desc":"We're expanding file format support for Content AI Document Translation in SharePoint Online. Newly added extensions include: xlf, tsv, tab, mdown, mdtext, mdtxt, mdwn, mht, mhtml, mkd, mkdn, odt, rmd. This update brings us in alignment with Azure Document Translation capabilities and unlocks new scenarios, such as .xlf support, which enables seamless translation of eLearning and localization content exported from many industry tools.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-05-07","modified":"2025-05-07","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=492984","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-464205","title":"Outlook: Additional features on the profile card in Outlook Mobile","desc":"Reachability panel, hybrid location, and pronouns (read only) will be available on the Outlook profile card in iOS and Android. Events panel will be replaced with the calendar in Outlook mobile.","products":["Outlook"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-10-30","modified":"2025-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=464205","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"January CY2025"},{"id":"rm-471000","title":"Microsoft Teams: Open file links preference to extend across M365 apps","desc":"When it comes to how links to cloud-hosted Word, Excel, or PowerPoint files should open, you may prefer they open in a browser, desktop apps, or directly in Teams. Now, your Teams file open preference will extend to across Microsoft 365 apps starting with classic Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint. This makes the open file experience consistent on your Windows PC/device. If you prefer, you will still be able to choose your Teams file open preference separately.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-12-04","modified":"2025-05-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=471000","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-485714","title":"Microsoft Teams: Teams Button Support on Multiple Connected Peripheral Devices","desc":"You can now use the Teams button across peripheral devices without having to manually select a specific device in the Teams devices settings. This ensures a more seamless experience navigating across multiple certified for Microsoft Teams personal peripheral USB devices (with a wire or a dongle) connected to the same host device (such as your laptop). For example, you can use the Teams button on headset A to bring up the meeting pre-join screen, then use the Teams button on headset B to join the meeting, and then use the Teams button on your connected speakerphone to raise hand in the meeting, etc.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-03-26","modified":"2025-05-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485714","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-485727","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot Dashboard Trendline Additions","desc":"Copilot Dashboard users can now visualize trends in additional key adoption and impact metrics over time to more quickly identify patterns and opportunities in employee adoption for better licensing decisions. Users will be able to now view Adoption metrics on either a monthly or weekly timeframe for specific groups of interest, as well as deep dive into Impact metrics like Copilot Assisted Hours, Actions Taken, and feature-specific dimensions.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-19","modified":"2025-05-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485727","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-481352","title":"Microsoft Teams: Copilot in Teams meetings responses can be exported to Word and Excel","desc":"Now, certain responses from Copilot in Teams meetings will have an option to ‘edit in’ Word or Excel. The ‘edit in’ option for Word will be available for Copilot responses that are long (more than 1300 characters) and will automatically open a Word document with the response written. The ‘edit in’ option for Excel will be available for Copilot responses that are formatted in a table, and will automatically open an Excel file with the formatted response added. Copilot responses can only be exported if the meeting policy for the meeting is set to allow copying or forwarding of meeting chat, live captions, transcript, and Copilot responses. The export capability will also inherit the sensitivity label of the meeting (sensitivity labels are available to Teams Premium users).","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-26","modified":"2025-05-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481352","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-380839","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Current web content included when drafting with Copilot in Word","desc":"Draft with Copilot will include information from Bing search, resulting in content that's as current as what you would find when searching with Bing on the web.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-09","modified":"2025-04-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380839","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512},{"id":"rm-486825","title":"Word: Email Notification Context Previews for Files Protected with Microsoft Purview","desc":"This is being removed as a duplicate of 486820","products":["Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-02","modified":"2025-04-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=486825","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-481283","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Catchup Skill (Copilot in Engage)","desc":"Catch up effortlessly on Home Feed or Community conversations since you last checked- this card will provide a personalized update to what you missed since you last logged into the Viva Engage homepage or since you last clicked into the Feed for a specific Community you follow","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-09","modified":"2025-04-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481283","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-489220","title":"Microsoft Viva: Search Skill (Copilot in Engage)","desc":"Engage Copilot now uses search skills to find and summarize relevant posts, with citations and direct links.","products":["Microsoft Viva","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2025-04-25","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=489220","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-490567","title":"Planner: New Microsoft Planner App for Teams for customers in GCC-H","desc":"The new Microsoft Planner app in Teams is a single, unified work management experience. It brings together the simplicity of To Do, the collaboration of Planner and the power of Project into a single and simple solution that offers individual task management, collaborative work management as well as enterprise work management.","products":["Microsoft Project","Microsoft To Do","Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-22","modified":"2025-04-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=490567","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["GCC High"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-411302","title":"Outlook: Prioritize my inbox by Copilot","desc":"Prioritize my inbox by Copilot marks high priority mails in your inbox and provides a short summary of the mail's importance in the message list and the reading pane. Mails can be sorted and filtered by Copilot's priority. In Web and New Outlook for Windows, you can also choose to have Copilot mark low priority mails. #newoutlookforwindows","products":["Outlook","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-09-16","modified":"2025-04-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=411302","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Android","Desktop","iOS","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-380678","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - Ability to rename the policy and rule names in DLP","desc":"This feature gives the ability for the DLP admin to rename the existing policy/rule without having to create the entire the rule or policy again.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-01-26","modified":"2025-04-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380678","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"October CY2025","gaSort":202510},{"id":"rm-483949","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Drafting on a selection includes being able to reference files, emails, and meetings","desc":"Just like when you're using Copilot to draft content on a blank line in your document, you can reference resources that provide context in addition to the content you've selected in your document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-18","modified":"2025-04-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=483949","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-485183","title":"Microsoft 365: Copilot Prompt Gallery - Share a prompt to a Microsoft Teams team","desc":"Share custom prompts with members of a Microsoft Teams team from the Copilot Prompt Gallery App, allowing team members to easily discover and utilize these prompts in Copilot Prompt Gallery App.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-31","modified":"2025-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485183","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-485720","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create Copilot Pages on your mobile phone","desc":"Create Copilot Pages from Copilot Chat on your mobile phone to continue working on the go.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-14","modified":"2025-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485720","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-420946","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage - Leaders updated via group sync","desc":"Currently, leaders are managed in Viva Engage manually. If you wish to add or remove leaders, you need to go to Engage to do so. This feature will allow you to define a group that includes users who should be designated as leaders. As you add or remove people from that group, they will gain or lose privileges accordingly. The manual method will continue to be available.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-09","modified":"2025-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=420946","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-179883","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Insider Risk Management - Progressive alert scoring","desc":"<div><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;\">With this new feature, user activities that could potentially result in data security incidents will be assessed more frequently within a 24-hour period compared with the current practice of once every 24 hours. Alert insights will now be updated every few hours with this increased frequency, providing designated analysts with timely alerts and continuously evolving insights. Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management correlates various signals to identify potential malicious or inadvertent insider risks, such as IP theft, data leakage, and security violations. Insider Risk Management enables customers to create policies based on their own internal policies, governance, and organizational requirements. Built with privacy by design, users are pseudonymized by default, and role-based access controls and audit logs are in place to help ensure user-level privacy.</span> </div>","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2023-10-10","modified":"2025-04-14","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=179883","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501,"preview":"August CY2024"},{"id":"rm-488095","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: Additional actions include submit, allow/block, and trigger AIR from Advanced Hunting.","desc":"SoC will be able to do submissions and tenant level block and trigger investigation actions from Advanced Hunting","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-10","modified":"2025-04-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=488095","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-487851","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Catch up on a summary of document comments in the top of your document","desc":"Copilot will have a Discussion tab in the top of your document to summarize open comments, helping you quickly understand what people have said in comments.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-08","modified":"2025-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487851","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-487849","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Catch up on a summary of document comments in the top of your document","desc":"Copilot will have a Discussion tab in the top of your document to summarize open comments, helping you quickly understand what people have said in comments.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-08","modified":"2025-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487849","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-487850","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot surfaces key statistics in the top of a document","desc":"Copilot includes a summary at the top of key statistics from your Word document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-08","modified":"2025-04-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=487850","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-485730","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Drafting on a selection includes being able to reference files, people, emails, and meetings","desc":"Just like when you're using Copilot to draft content on a blank line in your document, you can reference resources that provide context in addition to the content you've selected in your document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-05","modified":"2025-04-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485730","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"August CY2025","gaSort":202508},{"id":"rm-485729","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Drafting on a selection includes being able to reference files, people, emails, and meetings","desc":"Just like when you're using Copilot to draft content on a blank line in your document, you can reference resources that provide context in addition to the content you've selected in your document.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-05","modified":"2025-04-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485729","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-485722","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Reference People from your enterprise in Copilot in Word","desc":"Users can now reference People from your enterprise while generating content in Word.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-04-05","modified":"2025-04-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=485722","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-470427","title":"Microsoft Teams: Together Mode New Flow","desc":"After further review, this feature continues rolling out. We apologize for any inconvenience. Together mode will get a new simplified flow which will take the user from the beginning to the end through the steps of setting up the scene, assigning the seats and applying for everyone in the call in a transparent and easy-to-understand way. The function itself does not change but there will be more transparency thanks to the icons on the meeting toolbar for an easy access for each next step in the familiar Together mode flow.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-12-06","modified":"2025-04-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470427","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-480720","title":"Microsoft Teams: Customize the location of Teams notifications on web","desc":"You can now customize where your Teams notification appear on your screen when using Teams on web. Options include bottom right, top right, bottom left, and top left, allowing you to choose the most convenient and least intrusive location for a better experience and productivity.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2025-02-07","modified":"2025-04-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=480720","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-481823","title":"SharePoint: SharePoint agents in Teams Mobile","desc":"Use SharePoint agents in Teams Mobile group chats and meetings.","products":["SharePoint","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-14","modified":"2025-04-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481823","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"September CY2025","gaSort":202509,"preview":"August CY2025"},{"id":"rm-482411","title":"SharePoint: Design ideas for quick links webpart","desc":"Design Ideas now provides formatting suggestions for the quick links webpart. This includes suggesting icons and images for a given link, as well as showing how the webpart would look with different card sizes, for single quick link webparts in a section.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-10","modified":"2025-03-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=482411","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-484054","title":"SharePoint: Design Ideas for Blank Flexible Sections","desc":"When you add a blank flexible section to your page, you will now be able to open up the Design Ideas panel to get blank section suggestions just as you can for standard sections.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-06","modified":"2025-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484054","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"rm-484053","title":"SharePoint: Design Ideas Suggests Images from Org Assets","desc":"SharePoint Design ideas can now pull from your Org Asset images to use within design ideas. If available when performing image suggestion, the first 3 ideas will show suggestions with images from org assets, whereas the rest of the ideas will use stock images.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-06","modified":"2025-03-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=484053","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"rm-481157","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Amplify - Animated GIFs in email","desc":"We are bringing animated GIFs to email crafted by Viva Amplify. GIFs of limited size will appear as animations in Outlook clients.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-03-05","modified":"2025-03-05","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481157","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-470986","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Create the perfect banner for your document with Copilot and Designer","desc":"Chat with Copilot in Word, and let Designer help your document stand out by producing eye-catching visuals that fill the width of the page.","products":["Word","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-05","modified":"2025-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470986","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-405753","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot takes emails and meetings into account while drafting content in Word","desc":"You will no longer need to reference certain types of organizational data for Copilot to generate contextually relevant content. People and chats will still need to be referenced explicitly.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-09","modified":"2025-03-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=405753","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"rm-481517","title":"OneDrive: Annotate with Apple Pencil Experience on OneDrive for iOS","desc":"Annotating with hand-drawn content in the OneDrive apps for iOS and iPadOS is now easier than ever. Enjoy various types of annotation tools and expressive strokes that match your pressure.","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-19","modified":"2025-02-27","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481517","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"July CY2025","gaSort":202507},{"id":"rm-481149","title":"Windows 365: Available from New Zealand North","desc":"Windows 365 will be available in New Zealand North.","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-24","modified":"2025-02-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=481149","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-469506","title":"Microsoft Teams: Forward messages with app cards","desc":"Messages containing app cards in chats and channels can now be forwarded. To use, navigate to the more actions menu of any message containing an app card, and select \"Forward\".","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-11-22","modified":"2025-02-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=469506","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-476496","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Developers building agents in Azure AI Foundry can ground their agent in files stored in SharePoint","desc":"Tenant Graph grounding provides grounding for agents with relevant information from Microsoft Graph, including files stored in SharePoint. This capability is now available to developers building agents in Azure AI Foundry.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-02-06","modified":"2025-02-06","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=476496","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"March CY2025"},{"id":"rm-421188","title":"Microsoft Teams: Inline preview of files shared","desc":"Now you can review a file shared in chat and channels in your flow of work. Select ‘preview’ and scroll through the file’s content without leaving the chat or channel.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-10-22","modified":"2025-02-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=421188","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-410396","title":"Microsoft Viva: Import HRIS data in Viva Glint from Microsoft Admin Center","desc":"Customers will be able to use various connectors to HRIS tools to import HRIS data into Viva Glint from Microsoft Admin Center.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-08-06","modified":"2025-01-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=410396","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2026","gaSort":202601},{"id":"rm-479408","title":"Microsoft Viva: Advanced moderation access control for corporate communicators","desc":"Network admins can choose to enable advanced moderation access for corporate communicators to manage AI themes + keywords detected within organization.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-31","modified":"2025-01-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=479408","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-401125","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Data Loss Prevention - New ChatGPT Enterprise connector to discover and bring prompts and responses into the scope of Purview features","desc":"Using the unified Purview portal, organizations will be able to establish a connection to their ChatGPT Enterprise workspaces to discover, collect, and store contents of interactions of users with ChatGPT Enterprise into the scope of Purview capabilities and policies.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-18","modified":"2025-01-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=401125","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"December CY2025","gaSort":202512,"preview":"December CY2024"},{"id":"rm-476490","title":"Microsoft Clipchamp: Editor simplification and introduction of light mode","desc":"This change will simplify the Clipchamp editing experience and increase the space you have on the stage to make great videos. We're also introducing light mode as a new option for people to choose whether they view the Clipchamp editor in a Light or Dark scheme.","products":["Microsoft Clipchamp"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-24","modified":"2025-01-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=476490","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-475059","title":"Planner: Smart backgrounds for basic plans","desc":"Get ready to customize your plans like never before! With smart backgrounds, you’ll be able to quickly spot the right plans. This feature was part of our legacy Planner experience, and we’re now enabling it for basic plans in the new Planner.","products":["Planner"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-17","modified":"2025-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=475059","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-117394","title":"Whiteboard: Existing Azure Board Migration","desc":"This feature will migrate boards that exist in your tenant's Azure storage to OneDrive for Business storage. More information will follow as we near release.","products":["Whiteboard"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2023-02-09","modified":"2025-01-17","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=117394","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-474445","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Copilot extensibility – Developers can build custom engine agents with the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK","desc":"Developers can use the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK to create custom engine agents. These agents, built on their own AI stack, can be deployed to various platforms, including Microsoft 365 Copilot, Microsoft Teams, and other non-Microsoft channels.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-10","modified":"2025-01-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=474445","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Developer"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-471004","title":"Microsoft 365: Updated settings for the Microsoft 365 app on Windows","desc":"The Microsoft 365 app on Windows added settings to pin the app to the taskbar.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-13","modified":"2025-01-10","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=471004","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502},{"id":"rm-473454","title":"Windows 365: Concurrency assignment for Windows 365 Frontline in dedicated mode","desc":"Concurrency assignment in Windows 365 Frontline in dedicated mode refers to the number of active Cloud PCs that can be used simultaneously within the total number of licensed Cloud PC usage for Frontline. This allocation ensures that resources are optimized based on the specific needs of the organization and its users.","products":["Windows 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-08","modified":"2025-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473454","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"February CY2025"},{"id":"rm-470140","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: New Feature access management UI in Admin Center","desc":"Through the new Feature Access management user interface, admins will be able to manage feature access settings directly in Microsoft 365 admin center. Feature access management allows admins to use access policies to manage which users can access specific features in Viva apps, so you can tailor your deployments to meet your local regulatory or business requirements. Previously, these policies could only be managed with Microsoft PowerShell cmdlets. After this rollout, admins can choose to use either Microsoft 365 admin center or PowerShell to manage feature access. Existing policies set for an organization will persist and can be managed in both places.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-08","modified":"2025-01-08","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470140","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-472920","title":"SharePoint: Modifications in the Embedded container type creation cmdlets in PowerShell","desc":"We’re introducing modifications in the container type creation cmdlets. The New-SPOContainerType cmdlet will only create a new container type. We are introducing the Add-SPOContainerTypeBilling cmdlet to add billing profile to the new container type.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2025-01-04","modified":"2025-01-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=472920","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-472919","title":"SharePoint: Additional support on SPAC to identify different types of Embedded containers and their principal owner","desc":"The update enables SharePoint Embedded Administrators (SPE Admins) to identify the different kind of containers (user, tenant, and group) and the principal owner associated with the container.","products":["SharePoint"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-31","modified":"2024-12-31","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=472919","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-471003","title":"Microsoft 365: Updates to the Microsoft 365 app","desc":"The Microsoft 365 app name, icon, and UI will evolve to support future AI-first experiences. Key UI changes include reducing the top header and consolidating app-level tools and settings into the App toolbar on the left.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-20","modified":"2024-12-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=471003","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-473444","title":"Word: Draft on a selection and retain your existing formatting","desc":"Draft on a selection and retain your existing formatting so that your content is seamless and fits with your document.","products":["Word"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-18","modified":"2024-12-18","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=473444","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-408537","title":"Microsoft Viva: List-based Forms card for Viva Connections Dashboard","desc":"This feature will allow operators to add a card for any form/survey created for data collection on the Viva Connections Dashboard for attention and quick action.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-08-01","modified":"2024-12-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=408537","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"May CY2025","gaSort":202505},{"id":"rm-471447","title":"Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): Updated welcome screen for the Microsoft 365 app on Windows","desc":"The Microsoft 365 app welcome screen on Windows will be updated to display a welcome message and progress bar while the Microsoft 365 app loads.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-12-11","modified":"2024-12-11","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=471447","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501},{"id":"rm-470139","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Unified Google Workspace Migration","desc":"Offer Microsoft 365 customers a seamless experience for migrating Google Workspace workloads to M365. Through a unified portal page, you can initiate and monitor migration tasks for both Gmail and Google Drive. Additionally, if your Google Workspace tenant has fewer than 1,000 users, you'll benefit from the newly revamped Gmail migration flow, which simplifies the process and guides you through each step.","products":["Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-22","modified":"2024-11-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470139","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503},{"id":"rm-470024","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Google Groups to M365 Modern Groups Migration Service","desc":"Google Groups to M365 Modern Groups Migration Service is a 1st party service for migrating Google groups with the M365 Admin center as a new feature, so that Google compete customers moving to M365 would have the ability to automatically create the groups, its members, member conversations and all permissions to M365 Groups without the need to recreate the groups which is the only solution for customers moving from Google.","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-22","modified":"2024-11-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470024","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"February CY2025","gaSort":202502,"preview":"January CY2025"},{"id":"rm-470023","title":"Microsoft 365 admin center: Google to Entra Identity Sync service","desc":"Google to Entra Identity Sync service is a cloud-2-cloud user Identity onboarding and one way synchronization tool from Google workspace to Entra ID. This will be available as part of the M365 Admin center for Google compete customers moving into M365 to create the identities in M365 farm and move Drive and Mail content into Onedrive and Exchange online","products":["Microsoft 365","Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-22","modified":"2024-11-22","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=470023","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501,"preview":"December CY2024"},{"id":"rm-469502","title":"OneDrive: Convert Copilot response into a Word file","desc":"Like a summary or FAQ that Copilot generated for you? Now, with one click, you can convert any Copilot response into a Word document. This feature requires a Microsoft Copilot for Microsoft 365 license and will be available to commercial customers on OneDrive Web.","products":["Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)","OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-20","modified":"2024-11-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=469502","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-469501","title":"OneDrive: Create a presentation from a Word file","desc":"With Copilot, you can create the first draft of your presentation using a Word file in just a single click. This feature requires a Microsoft Copilot for Microsoft 365 license and will be available to commercial customers on OneDrive Web.","products":["OneDrive","Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365)"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-11-20","modified":"2024-11-20","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=469501","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504},{"id":"rm-402185","title":"Microsoft Teams: EDU tenant type selection in policy wizard","desc":"Admins can now select tenant type for their institution from the policy wizard. This setting can be changed anytime from the wizard.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-07-03","modified":"2024-11-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=402185","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac","Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"November CY2024","gaSort":202411},{"id":"rm-464992","title":"Microsoft 365: Dedicated Backup Administrator Role for Microsoft 365 Backup","desc":"Use a dedicated Backup Administrator role to manage your M365 Backup administration tasks.","products":["Microsoft 365"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-29","modified":"2024-10-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=464992","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503,"preview":"January CY2025"},{"id":"rm-375287","title":"Microsoft Stream: Video reactions","desc":"This feature will allow users to add or remove reactions to specific points of a recorded video via Stream Web App and Embed. Viewers will be able to see how their colleagues feel about a video and show their support towards the video owner. These reactions will be present in the timeline to highlight the most important parts of the video and can be used for navigation. Also, owners of the video can see detailed analytics about when viewers are reacting to videos and have ability to disable the feature. This feature was incorrectly updated to a status of rolling out upon preview availability. We apologize for any inconvenience.","products":["Microsoft Stream"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-01-12","modified":"2024-10-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=375287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"January CY2025","gaSort":202501,"preview":"June CY2024"},{"id":"rm-406910","title":"Microsoft Stream: Seek bar thumbnails for Teams meeting recordings","desc":"This feature adds seek bar (preview) thumbnails to Microsoft Stream's video player. The thumbnails provide a preview of the video content when hovering over the player's seek bar at a certain timestamp. Currently, it will only be made available for Teams meeting recordings.","products":["Microsoft Stream"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-23","modified":"2024-10-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=406910","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Targeted Release"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-420331","title":"Microsoft Purview compliance portal: Information Protection - Sensitivity labels protection policy support for Microsoft Fabric","desc":"Your organization can now apply sensitivity labels in Microsoft Purview Information Protection to Microsoft Fabric workspaces. This new functionality will allow users to manually label Fabric items with their sensitivity level and then apply access control protections based upon the protection policies set by administrators.","products":["Microsoft Purview"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-10-04","modified":"2024-10-04","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=420331","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506,"preview":"October CY2024"},{"id":"rm-395940","title":"Microsoft Viva: Viva Engage - Topic Subscription notification","desc":"This feature allows users to subscribe to notifications for Viva Engage topics they follow. Users will receive a Viva Engage bell notification when a new post is tagged with a topic they are subscribed to or when the topic is added to an existing post.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-05-06","modified":"2024-09-24","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=395940","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Teams and Surface Devices","Web"],"clouds":["GCC"],"ga":"September CY2024","gaSort":202409},{"id":"rm-329253","title":"Microsoft Teams: Latest meeting experiences with performance improvements on web for Safari and Firefox (for anonymous join only)","desc":"The latest Teams meeting experiences will be available for Teams on the web in Safari and Firefox browsers - including performance improvements, refreshed pre-join, updated meeting stage, and the updated meeting toolbar. (for anonymous join only)","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2023-12-15","modified":"2024-09-12","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=329253","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"September CY2024","gaSort":202409},{"id":"rm-409529","title":"Microsoft Entra: Passkey authentication in brokered Microsoft apps on Android","desc":"Microsoft Entra ID users can now use a passkey to sign into Microsoft apps on Android devices where an authentication broker like Microsoft Authenticator or Microsoft Intune Company Portal is installed.","products":["Microsoft Entra"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-07-26","modified":"2024-08-21","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=409529","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"March CY2025","gaSort":202503,"preview":"August CY2024"},{"id":"rm-178292","title":"OneDrive: Admins can configure a group policy to block specific folders from OneDrive Sync","desc":"<div><span style=\"\">In addition to being able to configure a group policy to exclude specific files or file extensions from Syncing with OneDrive, admins can now exclude folders as well. End-users will be able to see the excluded folders in the Sync configuration applied to them via their OneDrive Advanced Settings.</span> </div>","products":["OneDrive"],"status":"In development","created":"2023-10-04","modified":"2024-08-01","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=178292","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop","Mac"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"June CY2025","gaSort":202506},{"id":"rm-184915","title":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365: False positive email release from Quarantine through threat explorer, email summary panel, advanced hunting, and custom detection email entity page take action","desc":"SecOps can now mange False positives and take move to inbox (i.e. release) quarantined messages from Threat explorer, advanced hunting, custom detection and Email entity page without the need to tab out to the Quarantine portal to take the action.","products":["Microsoft Defender for Office 365"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2023-11-10","modified":"2024-07-30","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=184915","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2024","gaSort":202407,"preview":"November CY2023","more":"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-defender-for-office/announcing-quarantine-release-integration-in-microsoft-defender/ba-p/4198601"},{"id":"rm-396287","title":"Microsoft Viva: Copilot assisted goal authoring with Context IQ grounding","desc":"When generating goals, users will be able to add more than one file from context IQ suggestions as references in their prompts to Copilot.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"In development","created":"2024-05-08","modified":"2024-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=396287","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability","Preview"],"platforms":["Web"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2025","gaSort":202504,"preview":"January CY2025"},{"id":"rm-398447","title":"Microsoft Teams: School Connection – Providing access to parents via their phone number","desc":"The School Connection app in Microsoft Teams (mobile) empowers parents and guardians to engage, support, and monitor their student's learning at school. This release enables a parent/guardian to get access to their child’s profile in School Connection if they login to Teams (mobile) with their phone number and the school has registered that phone number as a parent/guardian contact. Additionally, a parent/guardian will easily get access to their child’s profile if the phone number or email address that is registered by the school is saved as a login information in their Microsoft account. Learn more about School Connection at the link below.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-06-04","modified":"2024-07-29","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=398447","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2024","gaSort":202407,"more":"https://parent.microsoft.com/"},{"id":"rm-393931","title":"Microsoft Teams: Microsoft 365 admin centers – Manage Teams apps that work on Outlook and Microsoft 365 App","desc":"Administrators using the Microsoft 365 admin center and Teams admin center who manage Teams apps that work on Outlook and the Microsoft 365 App will be able to apply their changes across all three clients (Teams, Outlook and Microsoft 365 App). Before this update, changes made through the Integrated Apps section in the Microsoft 365 admin center would only affect these apps on Outlook and the Microsoft 365 App; similarly, changes made in the Teams admin center would exclusively affect Teams. With this change, management of these apps will be unified across Teams, Outlook and Microsoft 365 App.","products":["Microsoft Teams","Microsoft 365 admin center"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-04-18","modified":"2024-07-23","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=393931","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Desktop"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"July CY2024","gaSort":202407},{"id":"rm-380852","title":"Microsoft Teams: Change background while recording on phone","desc":"You can record a video clip with your phone camera and switch your background to any picture you want or make it blurry. With this feature, you can record yourself anywhere and share it with coworkers in your Teams chat or channel.","products":["Microsoft Teams"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-02-06","modified":"2024-05-02","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=380852","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide","GCC","GCC High","DoD"],"ga":"May CY2024","gaSort":202405},{"id":"rm-382643","title":"Microsoft Viva: Search in Viva Connections on iOS and Android tablet","desc":"This adds a search entry point and a new tailored experience for Viva Connection users on iOS and Android tablets.","products":["Microsoft Viva"],"status":"Rolling out","created":"2024-02-14","modified":"2024-04-19","link":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?searchterms=382643","source":"roadmap","phases":["General Availability"],"platforms":["Android","iOS"],"clouds":["Worldwide"],"ga":"April CY2024","gaSort":202404}];
